        StaticBook("A Letter to Len", "SpaceOfAids", "*The writing is a bit childish, crude. But legible.*\n\nDear Len\n\nI love you. Hurts to be apart from you, honey. Me and your mother are getting better, being good. She is researching into becoming a Cleric, which is someone\nwho heals and helps. Ask someone about them. I left some gifts in the mailbox, for you birthday-- Happy birthday, my little princess. You are what keeps us happy, know that-- Love you, love you.\n\nLove, Maln", ""),
        StaticBook("a special elf", "Toe", "once upon time\n\nthere was man name adeon\n\nhe hav wite hair and very tall\n\ngood bones and strong muscals\n\ncharm smile\nhe com from band brigade\n\nbrigman say to him \"frend you ned good woman\"\n\n\"no\" adeon say \"iam not for love\"\n\n\"why not??\" frend ask\n\n\"love is for good man\" adoen say \"iam bad...\"\none day adeon meet jarsy stunton\n\na nice prety lady of oran\n\nshe hav blone hair and nice figure\n\nwide hips and tight wast\n\ngood teeth and nice hand\n\"mmMMmm\" say adoen \"helo\"\n\nnice lady blush\n\n\"excus me sir\" she say to him \"i just passin thru\"\n\n\"mmm\" he say \"lets talk\"\n\n\"ok\" say she\nshe falow him and they talk\n\nthe two hava many love nights\n\nBUT one day king of human jon horan say to him\n\n\"go kill monstars i order it\"\n\"but mlord\" say adon \"mwife is pregntn and i love her\"\n\n\"are u married?\" ask jon king horan\n\n\"no...\" adeon reply\n\n\"then go kill\" king say\n \nking is MAD\n\n!!!\non last nite befor hunting seson\n\njarzy water brake\n\n\"oh no!!\" she say \"i dont fel so good...\"\n\n\"he is coming\" adon say\n\n\"iam scared\" she say to him\n\"dont wory\" adeon say \"i believe\"\n\njarsy hold his hand\n \n\"puuuuuush!\" he say to her\n\n\"iiiii ammm!!!\" she say \"is paaainfuuull!\"\n\n\"ok\" adeon say \"breath harder\"\nafter mny hours of intense moment\n\ntwo finlly have cute babby\n\nadeon smile wit jary who is very sweaty\n\nadon kiss jarz forhead\n\n\"good job\" he say\nhapi couple very proud\n\nbut somthing is wrong...\n\n\"baby is welf!\" say jarzy \"how??\"\n\nshe is rely shock\n\n\"is ok is miracle\" adeon say \"is miracle baby we ned to take care\"\n\"he gona do gret things somday\" adon say agen\n\n\"how??\" jarz ask\n\n\"i just know ok??\" adeon say to her \"dont question\"\nmyn years later\n\ncute baby grow up witout father\n\nhe sufer many long nights alone and hunry\n\nnights cold and dark and scary somtimes\n\nbut is ok becaus he hav mny gud frends\nthey lik brothers to him\n\nvery close\n \nthey do many things togeter\n\nlik skip ropes jumpin jacks and throw rocks into water\n\nthey laugh an hav fun\n\nbut one day...\nthey all die\n\n!!!\n\nand toe is alone agen...\nhe cry few nights\n\nbut he move on\n\nhe know is what his frend would want\n\nhe look at thick clouds and smile\n\n\"i not foget frends\" toe say\ntoe go on to do adventurs\n\nhe fite mny hideos beast\n\nhe get manny money\n\nmny lady lik him\n\nbut he not hapi...\n\nhe miss mom and dad\none day he see his father face in the cloud\n\nis adeon\n\n!!!\n\"father\" toe say \"why you leave me??\"\n\n\"i did not want to\" adeon say \"but i had importrent busness...\"\n\n\"i spend mny night alone and afraid!\" toe say \"i had frends but they dead!!\"\n\"i know\" adoen say \"is hard life you hav i know this\"\n\ntoe cry abit\n\n\"dont cry\" adeon say \"is toough but you ben brave\"\ntoe cry more\n\n\"braver than any man i know\" adoen say \"i knew you specail\"\n\n\"how??\" toe say\n\ntoe sob\n\n\"i just know ok?\" adeon say\n\nadoen smile\n\"stay father\" toe say\n\n\"i wish\" adeon say \"but i mus go...\"\n\n\"go far my son\" adeon say\n\nadeon disaper\n\ntoe stop cry and smile\n\n\"i will dad\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Thesis", "Father Cedrik", "A Thesis on Charitable Evangelization, penned by Cedrik Engel, eternal servant of the Holy Father.\n\nIn nomine Patris.\n\nA man fed by another is beholden to him that provides food. Such is hardly deniable, even in the sense that a man who tends fields that\nbelong to another is beholden to him who owns the land; for land brings forth food with the labor of the tenant, and thus the tenant is fed by the landlord. This is the manner in which our world is governed. This feudal government over which our ever\nmerciful and most blessed GOD presides provides for a system that encourages loyalty and promotes a mutual understanding of responsibility. For without such a system the Holy Orenian Empire would utterly crumble upon its weak foundation, and the Church of\nthe Most High Father would be left stranded upon the harsh landscapes of this Plane. Thus, the importance of the general necessity of sustenance is realized.\n\nUpon this revelation, the Church may begin to develop a plan in which the scattered\nmasses of the Pagan world shall be brought forth into the eternal light of our Father, blessed by His Divine Providence. For from the ashes of this broken world of dismal heathens and faltering believers, the Church may yet arise anew, bearing the holy\nmight of GOD upon the mob of the proletariat, and elevate them to a higher standing, one of communion with His Divine Mercy.\n\nTherefore I beg the Church, I beseech it, to take up its Holy Standard and, in addition to the multitude of righteous\npractices it currently exercises, wield the mighty weapon of Charity, and spread His Love to all corners of this Earth, and perhaps the Pagan may begin to realize the falsity of his idolatrous gods, and turn to the liberating light of the Holy Father.\nThus I pray unto Him, that He may guide the Church with His Mighty Hand and evangelize this crippled land and the whole world may cry \"Glory!\" unto the Heavens.\n\nIn nomine Patris, Amen.\n\nDeus Magnus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeran", "Ashton", "\"Dear Aeran,\n\nToday, I sat on your bench. I layed on your bedroll. I'm writing right now on your table. \n\nThe grove feels so empty without you. The bench is empty. No one goes there anymore.\"\n\"I don't remember the last time I saw people sit there and talk. \n\nMy worst fear did come true. \n\nThat empty bench...it taunts me. I look at it every day. I hate it, but I love it.\"\n\"I love looking at it and remembering all the times we shared there. \n\nSometimes, I look at it and think...maybe you're just sleeping inside.\"\n\"When I think of that, I feel like you're closer to me. I feel as if you're not gone. \n\nI miss you.\"\n\"I tried to sit on your side of the bench just now. \n\nIt felt so wrong.\n\nThat spot was yours. It could never be anyone else's.\"\n\"I wish you could come home.\"\n\"Your family misses you.\"\n\"I love you.\"\n\"I'm sorry.\n\n\n-Ashton\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeran to Len 1", "SpaceOfAids", "Dear Len\n\nI'm sorry we didn't get to visit today. We got trapped halfway across the island from you. Again, I'm sorry. It hurts me beyond anything to be away from you. But we're still working, we're still getting better. Your mother is very\ndedicated to this Cleric thing, which is good-- She's a great woman, and this will allow her to help others. \n\nI just want to keep this one short. Or else I'll be here all night writing-- I'd prefer to tell you everything to your face. Love you.\nLove,\nMaln.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Laws", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: The Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange\n-------------------\nRe-Written by: Sarrion di' Pascali\n\nFrom:\nThe Tales of a Traveling Alchemist\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always here of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced\na sarcastic, yet thought provoking, question. This question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “ ‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff outta nothin’?”\nNow as shameful as his speech may be, the question remains the same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping the spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of, seemingly, nothing?\nThe answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the Principle of Equivalent Exchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing.\nAs the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion. This fundamental rule applies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what\nI call “Modern” alchemy. Although I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for example a bottle of alchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell\ncasted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing. Know that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants, objects, and other representations of what they wish to make.\nFor example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an oil base, a mixture of Drake’s Tail, blaze powder, and a dash of coal dust. Why would one need these items?\nThe oil base provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the oil the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter. The Drake’s Tail, a crimson, thorned\nplant that grows most often in deserts, is often warm to the touch and often associated with rage and flame. This provides an superb symbol for the element of fire. The Blaze Powder, another powerful symbol of fire,\nmixes well with the crushed Drake’s Tail to produce something truly strong. The coal dust, an optional portion, is another symbol of flame,\nalbeit both weaker than blaze powder or Drake’s Tail for both a Blaze and Drake’s fire burns far greater than coal.\nNow then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply toss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always. One must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much.\nAnd giving too much will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results. Why is this you might ask? When balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchanged, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell\nof your desire, than all is well. But when you disrupt this balance and push on the world, taking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required,\nfor one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty. This is a common misconception for not providing enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos. This can be easily\nassociated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will produce similar results. Of course it could also produce blander results,\nand in that case a potion may not be spoiled but it will simply be weak. This is preferable to exploding, of course. \n===================End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Mixtures", "Ahernin the Adventurer", "-=Mending Potion=-\nHeals minor cuts and wounds; Stops bleeding.\n-Base: Distilled Water\n-Serpant's Stalk\n-Tippen's Root\n-=Smoke Whisper=-\nWhen shattered, produces smoke that clouds sight.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Blood Lotus\n-Drake's Tail\n-Crouching Feather\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-=Frozen Blood=-\nFreezes when in contact with blood. Acts like a 'liquid bandage'.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Frost Vine\n-Athin\n-Crouching Feather\n-Tippen's Root\n-=Greater Chillblain Potion=-\nFire Resistance\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Frost Vine\n-Athin\n-=Potion of Celerity=-\nPotion of speed (Even with armor)\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Dwarf's Pumkin\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-Crouching Feather\n-Elf's Hair Vine\n\n((Glitched))\n-=Greating Healing=-\nHeals wounds, stops bleedings, repares fractures; Can stop internal bleeding if digested.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Frost Vine\n-Athin\n-Crouching Feather\n-Tippen's Root\n-Alabster Leaf\n-=Great Accuity=-\nIncreases sences, speed, and mobility (jump).\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Elf's Hair Vine\n-Crouching Feather\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-Halfling's Grass\n-=Alchemist's Fire=-\nFire in a bottle\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Serpant's Stalk\n-Mandagora\n-Drake's Tail\n-Crimson Vase\n-Dwarf's Pumkin\n-Flametongue Root\n-Crouching Feather\n-=Fast Healing=-\nQuickly heals wounds\n-Base: Distilled Water\n-Elf's Hair Vine\n-Tippen's Root\n-=Greater Blood Soup=- \nSubstance that can provide all nutitional\nneeds with one bottle.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Blood Lotus\n-=Nether's Wrath=-\nCan melt glass on touch\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Serpant's Stalk\n-Madagora\n-Flametounge Root\n-Dwarf's Pumkin\n-Crimson Vase\n-Drake's Tail\n-=Freezing Salve=-\nMakes traveling through hot climates easier.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Athin\n-Serpant Stalk\n-=Beauty Sleep=-\nAIDS drinker in falling asleep.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Halfling Grass\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-Elf's Hair Vine\n-=Potion of Incence=-\nProduces a pleasent smell\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Drake's Tail\n-Blood Lotus\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-=Soothing Ointment=-\nReleaves burns and itches.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Mandagora\n-Serpant's Stalk\n-Crimson Vase\n-=Stoneskin Potion=-\nTurns skin into stone. Can cause paralysis and death if you too much.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-\n\n!Still to be found!\n-=Soft Relaxtant=-\nRelaxes Consumer\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Halfling's Grass\n-Larihei's Fingers\n-=Potion of Beauty=-\nEnhances phyiscal features.\n-Base: Aqua Vitae\n-Halfling Grass\n-Crouching Feather\n-Larihei's Fingers", ""),
        StaticBook("ALetterToElswyen", "Anthron", "Over the pain of the days\nThe loss of many, some close, some not\nOver joyful days\nTo blessed and fought for nights\nSome moments so small\nCan be what matters most\nFrom changes\nTo familarities\nFriendships created\nAnd hearts broken\nAll in life is of nature's whim\nWhether it be good\nOr whether it be bad\nWe can not predict the outcome\nFor we can not see the future\nAnd with this note I leave\nInto the ashen night\n~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~To Elswyen\nAlthough I had not said it, but I loved you. I am sorry that I was not brave enough to tell you this. But do not mourn my leaving, because I will be back someday, whether you look for me or not, I will still respect you and\nlove you, no matter which you choose.\n\nFrom Anthron\n\n~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~", ""),
        StaticBook("Alphabet By Barb", "Andrik Barbanov", "a\nb\nc\nd\ne\nf\ng\nh\ni\nj\nk\nl\nm\nn\no\np\nq\nr\ns\nt\nu\nv\nw\nx\ny\nz", ""),
        StaticBook("Amoss The Wizard", "Arthur Caulfield", "Amoss the wizard spoke of death to the prince. \n  Yakov, the target, had not been seen since.\n  Hold up in a castle full of armed guards. \n  Amoss' mind was smashed into shards. \n  Believing he could take on all of the men.\n  Amoss the wizard\nrushed into Oren.\n  Then rushing back out, chased by an angry mob.\n  Amoss the wizard looked quite the knob.\n  Surrounded by metal, which could deliver such pain.\n  Amoss the wizard gave up and put in chain.\nGrigor, the lead man in a mob of patriotic Orenians. \n  A determined mind that put him above millions. \n  Organised the mob into a killing machine. \n  Each section took the orders ever so keen.\n  To shed blood, for the emperor who runs this place.\nAnd oh how they moved, at such a high pace it would seem to be a race to rip off the enemies face.\n  Eraborn. No one saw him, sneak on the rooftop. \n  Only when his eyes fell on to Grigor did he stop.\n  Withdrew a bow, and an arrow made from\nthe finest of steel. \n  To make sure that where the head struck, the wound would not heal.\n  I kid you not, it struck his head, but he shrugged it away. \n  Many may tell you different, but I was there on that day.\nA day when the guards seized the man on the roof.\n  But using his magic, he escaped their clutches with a poof. \n  While that man is being hunted Amoss is on trial.\n  The treachorous things he shouted were ever so vile.\n\"Off\" shouted the crowd, \"Off with his head!\"\n  And after the trial, I am sure Amoss will be dead.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Apple", "Shawn Telvin", "\"Roses are red\nApples are, too\nWithin nature\nBoth things grew\n\nTo see their beauty\nYou must know\nBoth are special\nBoth can show\nThe power of nature\nAnd how it flows.\"\n\"I would like to think that poem would be enough for my assignment, but it doesn't seem good enough to me.\n\nSo, instead, I am submitting this statuette of an apple I made.\"\n*The statuette is of an apple, a piece missing. The core can be seen, some seeds seated inside. The bottom is flat, making it easier to place on a table.*\n\"I chose an apple, because to me, it represents all of life and nature.\n\nI sat under an apple tree, near a rose bush, and I began to think about how people praise and cherish roses.\nApples are seen as just being a necessity. They are food. You eat them, and you forget them. Yet, if someone gives you roses, you remember them.\n\nWhy?\"\n\"It shouldn't be this way. Apples represent life so well. They are so much more than nourishment. \n\nThey are beautiful. Within their core, they hold life. They fall from their origins and go on their own journey.\"\n\"They live. They serve a purpose. They die. From them grows a new life, a new tree -- to continue on the legacy. Living, creating, dying.\"\n\"The apples inspired me. So often, we forget the things that give us continued life. We forget how precious each living thing is. People take for granted the importance of each and every thing in this world.\"\n\"Something as simple as an apple, which you may hold, yet forget about tomorrow -- is just as precious and amazing as the most beautiful rose.\"\n*Upon closer inspection of the statuette, one might notice a very fine, small inscription on the bottom of the apple.*\n\n\"Beauty in nature,\nBeauty in life.\nBeauty in all things.\nEven in strife.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Aren'iril", "JMACKLES", "Aren'iril\nYou were there\n'Neath Delfyr's Sanctuary\n\nYou were there\nAs I came to be.\n\nYou learned by my side as I trained in my arts, taking a totem that was not for me.\n\nTogether we created much, spread\nverdure long.  The Mother of Elandriel and Swamp of Song I do not claim my power that you gave.  It is of the Aspect's will you endured, becoming more than a staff, becoming my closest, longest friend.\n\nLost to the void, I would leap in to find you.\nAnd I did.\n\nYou were there when the land began to fall, and Ethanriel's call grew weak, you TOOK her into you, kept her for me, till time was right to plant the seed.\n\nTogether we searched the lands for the Sacred Three.\nYou tried to stop me from dying, but I was so tired.  So very, very tired.....though you could not know the Wolf's plan.....\n\nAnd when forward came the SonofNone, for the second time you resisted him, and let my brothers know of his existence.\nYou were there through every moment, and I was not there for your last.\n\nI could not be there to stop your demise, but I promise you this....\nI will find who did this and bring justice to them.  There will be no mercy for such a pure life destroyed.\nOr I will die trying.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  ~Song", ""),
        StaticBook("Ashton & Connor", "elliot5", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=To the person I love,\nthe person I live for,\n         Ashton.\n=-=-=-   <3  -=-=-=-\n\nWritten by Connor,\n   Written for Ashton,\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n                            Date of creation,\n   1568\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nAshton, if I were to ever die or lose you,\nknow I'll always be by your side, protecting and watching over you and the future that will come to you, will be secured by me.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nAshton, know that love is dynamic not static, and loving others is fine, even if it does cause me pain, I understand the pain it causes you. I just wish for you to stay happy.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=    <3   =-=-=-\n\nIf you ever need a cuddle, hug or kiss. If you are ever feeling down, if you are ever hurt, or if your heart is ever broken, I'll be here for you holding you, by your side.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nIf you ever forget me maybe memory loss, here is my documentation so our\nmemories are written in words.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n          --->\n[!] This page's corner\nis folded.\n===================\n   Your biggest fan\n===================\n\nName: Connor Tenun\nRace: Human\nGender: Male\nAge: 24 (As of 1568)\nEyes: Blue\nHair: Dark Brown\nLoves: Ashton\n\n===================\n===================      How we met\n===================\n\nOne summer day, Connor walked up to a beautiful women called Ashton. On this day he handed her a pumpkin pie, and from there it began.\n\n===================\n===================      How we met\n===================\n\nThe sun set as we talked through the night, about family, relationships and having laughs. We hugged eachother in friendship.\n\n===================\n===================\n     How we met\n===================\n\nWe went to your fathers place, and talked in your room for hours, until we kissed. We admitted our love was growing stronger...\n\n===================\n===================\n     How we met\n===================\n\nWe talked for hours, before making a magic kiss that started all of this, as we admitted our love together, we wanted to live together.\n\n===================\n===================      How we met\n===================\n\nBut before we knew it, disaster striked, the drudic community found out, and where enraged at Connor, but this was only the start...\n\n===================\n===================\n     How we met\n===================\n\nYou knew how you felt about me, but also your father. This caused drama and pain for both of us, as your feelings clashed in confusion.\n\n===================\n===================        Conclusion\n===================\n\nLife is hard, and I learned that I do love you with all my heart, so no matter who you love, it doesn't effect me, I love you and only you.\n\n===================\n===================     The pain I feel\n=v=v=v=v=v=v=v=v=v=\n\nThis has caused many sleepless nights of crying, and much pain, but one thing makes me smile, thinking about you smiling and that's all I need.\n\n===================\n=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=\n\n            [!]\n   A heart is drawn\n With Ashton under it.\n\n          \n           <3\n\n=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=\"My heart is always in this book, keep safe, my loved one.\"\n=*=*=*==*=*=*=*=*=*=\n(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)\n       Feel happy\n(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)\n\n\"When I hug you I never want to let go.\"\n\n\"When you talk you always bring me a smile.\"\n\n\n\n- <3 --------------\n(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)\n       Feel happy\n(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)(-)\n\n\"I never knew you could kiss a angel.\" \n\n\"I never knew someone could make me laugh even in the worst situations.\"\n\n\n- <3 --------------\n-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-\n   Time to draw you\n-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-\n\n[!] A note is pinned onto this page.\n\n\"Please forgive my drawing skills, but this did take me a few hours of dedication.\"\n\n-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-\n-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-\n   Time to draw you\n-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-^-\n\n[!] A drawing of you has been shaded, you are on a cliff picking a flower and smiling looking towards Connor.\n\n\n-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-v-\n-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-\n\n     Ashton you are,\n  Magical to me,\n       And should be,\n To everyone,\n          At all times,\n  Every day,\n       Every year,\n          All year,\n    Ashton I love you.\n\n-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-\n===================          How to;\n Make an amazing pie.\n===================\n\nAshton, don't we all love pie, maybe pumpkin pie? If you ever miss me, make pie just how I make it and hopefully it'll remind you of me.\n\n= <3 ==============\n===================          How to;\n Make an amazing pie.\n===================\n\n1) Two eggs.\n2) Three cups of flower.\n3) A spoon full of ginger and nutmeg.\n4) One cup of milk.\n\n= <3 ==============\n===================          How to;\n Make an amazing pie.\n===================\n\n5) Half a spoon of salt.\n6) A cup of sugar.\n7) Three spoon fulls of cold water.\n\n\n= <3 ==============\n===================          How to;\n Make an amazing pie.\n===================\n\n1) Prepare pie crust in a bowl with flour and salt, add cold water. Mix until formed. Shape the dough into a ball, roll it into a bowl\n\n= <3 ==============\n===================          How to;\n Make an amazing pie.\n===================\n\n2) Beat the eggs, pumpkin, sugar, cinnamon and ginger/nutmeg in a bowl, pour into crust. And cook slowly.\n\n= <3 ==============\n=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]\nI love you so much.\nMore then anyone\nMore then anything.\nTime passes by,\nfaster then I want.\n[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=[]=\n\n[!] A note is attached.\n\"Hey, someone just gave me colored pencils.\"\n\n<3\n===================         Kiss me\n===================\n\nWhen we kiss I feel like I'm in a whole new world, and all my problems dissapear. It makes me smile no matter how sad I am. Thank you Ashton.\n\n==================\n-- <3 ------------\n===================         Hug me\n===================\n\nWhen we hug I feel like I'm in a warm pool of water, safe and secure, I hope you feel the same. Because when I hug you I never want to let go.\n\n==================\n-- <3 ------------\n===================\n     My life goals\n===================\n\nMy life goals, are to move in, marry, have a child, explore the world together, master cooking, and become a poet, aswell as lots more. Ashton.  <3\n\n===================\n===================        Perfection\n===================\n\nAshton, you are perfect to me. All your flaws only make you stronger. § Never forget this for me, never forget me for me. Thank you.\n\n===================\n===================  Family are important\n===================\n\nI agree with the title of this page. I understand if you ever need to go with family Ashton. I'll always be there waiting for you.\n\n===================\n===================   Top ten reasons;\n I love you, Ashton.\n===================\n\n1) We understand eachother.\n\n2) I feel an aura coming from you at all times.\n\n§§===================\n===================   Top ten reasons;\n I love you, Ashton.\n===================\n\n3) You're beautiful.\n\n4) You're an angel.\n\n5) Your smile makes my day in an instant.\n\n===================\n===================\n  Top ten reasons;\n I love you, Ashton.\n===================\n\n6) You're always there when I need you.\n\n7) You're the most trust worthy person I currently know.\n\n§====================\n===================   Top ten reasons;\n I love you, Ashton.\n===================\n\n8) I respect your hardships.\n\n9) You are who you are, thank you Ashton, I love you.\n\n===================\n===================   Top ten reasons;\n I love you, Ashton.\n===================\n\n10) I see you in my dreams, you save me in my nightmares. I feel strong with you, and weak without you. That is me, that is us.\n\n===================\n===================   Death do us apart,\n===================\n\nI have decided to make sure you are safe and happy until I die. I vow to this in words, here right now. And I will stick to this promise. \n\n===================-- <3 -------------\n===================     A poem for you.\n===================\n\nMay the waters flow,\nhow could this be so?\nI stop without someone like you by my side.\nI guess this isn't just a ride. Life passes by. Without a wave or goodbye. \n\n==================\n===================\n    A poem for you.\n===================\n\nBut at this time,\nI cannot rhyme.\nAs I'm bad at poem writing.\n\nI love you Ashton.\nJust keep on fighting.\n<3\n\n==================\n===================\n    Don't worry, \n      I'm never mad.\n===================\n\nI can be sad, or disappointed in you. But I'll never be mad at someone like you Ashton, know this.\n\n===================-- <3 -------------\n===================       I'm Connor.\n===================\n\nFavourite Animal;\n  Fox.\nFavourite Color:\n  Red\nFavoruite Person:\n  Ashton\nFavoruite Food:\n  Pumpkin Pie\n\n==================\n=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*= §    Another drawing.\n=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=\n\n  [!]\n The same drawing as the one on page 19 has been drawn, but this time in color.\n                 \n=*=                   =*=\n   =*=*=*=*=*=*=*=\n           <3\n===================    Not smiling yet?\n===================\n\n[!] A note is attatched; \"I'm so sorry for this.\"\n\nHow can you tell the ocean is friendly?\nIt waves.\n\n===================\n===================    Not smiling yet?\n===================\n\nWhen is the moon at it's heaviest?\nWhen it's full\n\nWhat washes up on very small beaches?\nMicrowaves.\n\n===================\n===================\n\n        I love,\nEllie\nBeth\n       Ashton\nMia\nBella\nAmelia\nSophia\n\n===================-- <3 -------------\n===================\n  A bit embarrassing\n===================\n\nI'm happy I was your first, and I'm happy you were my first, no matter what you do, it does hurt me. But I still feel like you're pure to me.\n\n===================\n===================   What others think?\n===================\n\nI don't care what others think, about us. Aslong as it doesn't effect our happiness or safety. I only care what you think. \n         <3\n\n===================\n===================   I'll always be here.\n===================\n\n[!] A note is stuck next to a spot of blood on the page. \"I was a bit scared, but now I'll always be apart of this book.\" \n       (*)\n\n===================\n===================    You're nearing,\n the end of this book.\n===================\n\nI want this to go on forever, I could talk about love, you and me forever. But you must learn, everything has a end eventually.\n\n===================\n===================   Ashton I love you.\n===================\n\nIt's true. I love you. Please, please, please. Before you do anything, flick through this book. Think of me Ashton, stay happy for me. Okay? Goodnight  <3\n\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Essay", "Riley Powell", "The assignment presented to me was to give examples on how the Aspects help to preserve the balance.\nThey do this in many ways but the main way is through Druids.\nDruids are directed to preserve and protect the balance of nature.\nThey can do this through many ways. One of the main examples that I remember is when we first were coming to Vailor.\n I was a little kid then, but I remember the Mother Grove becoming overrun with rabbits.\nThere were so many rabbits you could hardly walk for stepping on one. My big sister Gwen even started naming them all and tried to create a family tree for them all.\nBut the rabbits were suffering. There wasn’t enough food there for all the rabbits,\neven with people feeding them, and there definitely wasn’t enough room for them and us.\nSo a few Druids relocated a bunch of the rabbits to another area in Vailor, so the population could spread out there.\nAnother example of this can be through the Aspects using nature itself to preserve the balance. Areas in the world are sometimes too overgrown with trees and plants, or overpopulated with animals.\nOne way that this can be solved through nature would be natural events, like a forest fire, or hurricane.\nIn an area with too many trees, a strong wind of a hurricane would blow down trees with weaker root systems and make room for the other trees to\nexpand their roots. Fire can also help with this. When the trees and plants burn, their ashes make the soil rich, so that new life and bloom forth with time.\nThe other way could be through an event, like a natural sickness and the changing of the seasons. Sometimes a natural sickness, like rabies, will become rampant in an area.\nThose that get infected die off and leave more room for those that survived to\nthrive.\nThe same goes for harsh summers and winters. Weaker animals succumb to the elements, while the stronger ones survive. \nThose that die, their bodies go on to join the natural cycle and provide nourishment for the other animals and plants.\nSo there are many ways that the Aspects can preserve the balance of nature. Through Druids, weather, natural events, and nature itself, the balance will continue to be preserved and the natural cycle maintained.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aurum Study", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "I'm writing this book now for proper study of aurum in the use of transmutation. Not only that, but this may prove useful for enchantment studies in the future. \n   In order to use this in transmutation, I will be going over how the material -\n-reacts to each of the five senses, how it's made, its average weight, breaking point, shape, and melting point. Alongside various other things, such as gaining the magical understanding of aurum.\nSight:\n   Gold takes on quite a deep yellow coloring. The specific coloring is actually called gold. Whether the color was named after the metal or vice versa, I'm unsure. Regardless, gold has quite the sheen to it. Pure aurum is rather shiny in the -\npresence of light. This is important to note because it is the distinguishing factor between aurum and magegold. More on this later.\nHearing:\n   The sound of aurum isn't particularly different than most metals. Offering the sounds of pings and scraping upon certain forms of contact.\nSmell:\n   Gold itself doesn't have much of a scent to it other than perhaps a very dim metallic type of smell.\nTouch:\n   Gold is a rather brittle metal in comparison to something like iron. Due to its weak breaking point (More on that next), it isn't terribly effective in combat unless specifically necessary. Magegold is especially not useful here.\nTaste:\n   I won't waste too much time here. There isn't any particular taste that pure aurum has.\nBreaking Point:\n   In comparison to iron, gold is an extremely soft, brittle metal. Most swords or weapons made of this material will not be expected to endure past a single battle. This is especially true in magegold, which has a glass-like composition.\nMelting Point:\n   Gold requires a relatively higher melting point than the glass which I've studied previously. Gold should melt at about 1000 degrees celsius. Slightly higher than that, actually at 1064 degrees.\nAverage Weight and Shape:\n   Interestingly, the shape of aurum is mostly dependent on the way it was cooled. Meaning that it can take on a plethora of shapes. As for its average weight, your typical aurum bar will weigh about 12.4 kg or 438.9 ounces.\nHow It's Made:\n   Normally gold is made by taking its impure ore form and conditioning it repeatedly through a forge until all imperfections are removed. After being repeatedly heated and cooled, the aurum takes on its pure form.\nMagical Understanding:\n   This understanding is not easily put into words nor explained. In order to fully understand gold and how to interact with it, a mage must spend countless hours getting acquainted to it on a spiritual and subconscious level.\nThis allows for one to understand how to exactly envelope the entity in your mana anchor.\n   As for the magical properties of gold. There are quite a few. Your regular aurum is often used in a way to cleave and damage spectral entities. Why this is the\ncase isn't always fully explained. I believe it is due to aurum's ability to easily absorb magical energies. Perhaps it is capable of absorbing whatever mana or energies that make up a spectral entity.\n   The ability to absorb large amounts of magical\nenergy is especially true for magegold. Although due to its extreme weakness, it is never used in combat. This does seem useful to the many enchanters out there as it works marvelously as a magical amplificare. No one truly seems to know how or why this-\n- is the case. \n   The only two ways that one might tell the difference between gold and magegold is magegold's noticablely weaker shine. Also magegold's greater brittleness.\nCultural Emphasis:\n   The word for aurum in elven is 'acaln'. This is a strange one, as the word is often regarded as ominous, as it has a dual meaning with 'curse'. Why this is the case seems to have been lost to the ages, or simply not known to the-\nmasses. \n   Orcs have been known to refer to gold as 'shinies', although this is a more general term for anything that may appear valuable. Which is quite right, gold is relatively rare compared to other resources.\n*Upon flipping to the next page you're greeted with a complicated work of diagrams, illustrations, graphs, charts, and equations. For pages onwards you see more of this, the author attempting display what was already mentioned in a mathematical sense or -\notherwise. This goes on for quite a long while as the book goes into greater depth. Eventually, you're met with the last page.*\nThat has been all I've studied regarding aurum and its workings thus far. Hopefully this will allow me to use it properly in transmutation in the future as well as give a base of understanding for enchanting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Avayla to Oliver", "Avayla", "Dear Oliver,\n\nI will be gone for a little while, though I'm not sure for how long. No matter what Aeran might thing or say, I will be fine. \n\nMake sure to tell Len every day how much I love her. I'm sorry to do this to you, but I feel I must.\nI will be fine. I will come back after all this has passed. I need to get away.\n\nAeran is an idiot. \n\nKeep Len safe and happy for me.\n\n-Avayla", ""),
        StaticBook("Barn Invest.", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "Upon hearing rumor of some barn outside of the Library of Dragur, which was involved with some sort of magical anomaly, I set out to investigate it. Before that however, let me explain a bit further.\n   Without boring anyone with the minute details, I-\n-shall proceed. The barn is a little ways to the west of the library. As the story goes, Orithur and a few others went to this barn to open a tome of 'unknown power'. Soon afterwards, a large crackle of energy was sensed surging desperately from the barn.\nReturning to the barn, Orithur was reportedly seen 'radiating' with magical energy as he stormed away. Once getting to the scene, it's reported there was a 'magical washboard' that whisked a female away. What this means, I am unsure. The only other -\n-person left in the barn informed the newcomers that this was the scene of a summoning. The summoning of a Voidal Horror known as the 'Outvoker'. This being was spoken to have already perished during some unknown previous event, according to the paper.\nThat is all that is known of this story.\n   Eventually I found myself to this said barn, and I must say, there are quite a few strange details about it. I first noticed that there is a strange portion of the land just in front of the entrance which is -\n- accursed by some blight which is unknown to me. Following what may or may not be blood, I entered the barn. \n   The second thing I noticed was that the barn was left with only a single story remaining, the rest of the barn inexplicably vanished without-\n-a roof.\n   Next and thirdly, I realized there are many pits, holes, and divots within the barn's floor. There are also reportedly less foliage, but that may just be because this is a barn and wouldn't have much anyway.\n   Upon further inspection, it-\n-appears that several trees near the barn have also inexplicably been severed from the midsection up. No traces of the trees' upper half. \n   A peculiar note, I realized that this barn is quite in the middle of nowhere. What purpose does a barn serve if -\nthere is no farmland nearby, nor cattle. Why was this even here in the first place? Was this barn even always here?\n   It appears that there are certainly anomalies about this barn, and a void node, Voidal Horror, or a tome of 'unknown power' may be -\n-responsible for this. I shall continue my investigation and research in the future. Until then, that is all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blue Orchid A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "To inform the reader, this book is mainly existent for the purpose of containing diagrams of the anatomy of a blue orchid. Ultimately, this is for the use in conjuration.\n*All over this page there is an exquisitely detailed depiction and labelled analysis of a blue orchid. It involves things such as the roots, stem, pedals, and etcetera.*\nThe roots of the flower exist for several purposes. These include keeping it properly rooted into the ground as well as for gaining nutrients/water from the surrounding soil.\nNext, the stem of the blue orchid. The stem exists for the purpose of transporting nutrients throughout the flower for sustenance. This would include various materials for use in photosynthesis and water.\nThen there are the pedals and leaves of the plant. Much of the photosynthesis is done within these parts of the plant. By collecting sunlight, the orchid is capable of processing it into a form of sugar.\nWithin the flowers include reproductive organs as well, including things such as the ovules.\nAs for habitat, I have found that the blue orchid mainly grows in humid regions, such as swamplands and islands.\n*Finally, there are several closer depictions of the several different portions of the flower's form. They seem zoomed in closer than the initial picture from before and show slightly more detail.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Bear A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "This book has been written for documenting the various systems within the common brown bear species for use in conjuration.\n   The systems being covered in this book include: cardiovascular, respiratory, nervous, skin, musculoskeletal, digestive, and-\n-urinary systems.\n*Flipping to this page, you find a rather detailed sketching of a brown bear's cardiovascular system. It includes the heart, veins, and arteries being spread throughout the entire body.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   This system is composed of the heart, veins, and arteries throughout the entire body.\n   The purpose of this system is to carry blood throughout the body and provide it with proper nutrients.\n   The brown bear's cardiovascular-\n-system is rather large, as it has a large body to provide with blood.\n*The next sketch is riddled with similar detail as before, but instead of a heart and veins, you are greeted with a sketching of lungs connected through the bear's throat.*\nRespiratory System:\n   This system is composed of the mouth connected via the throat into the bear's lungs.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide the blood stream with nutrients via oxygen and breathing.\n   The bear's respiratory system isn't -\n- particularly unique besides it being some what larger than a human's or otherwise.\n*The next sketching is displaying what appears to be the brain, connected and sprawling throughout the rest of the bear's body. Nerves branch out from the spinal cord.*\nNervous System:\n   This system includes the brain, the spinal cord, and all the nerves within the body.\n   The purpose of this system is to direct intentional actions, and enable thinking and emotions.\n   The brown bear isn't particularly self aware, -\n- much like other animals, but it is intelligent to a certain extent and with a plethora of instincts.\n*This sketch is a bit different than the others, as it displays three different figures. The first displays a shaved bear, the second shows the various layers within the skin, and the third shows a bear with its fur.*\nSkin:\n   This system is actually just one organ, but the organ is so expansive that it warrants itself as its own system.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide a barrier to the external environment and protect the inner workings of the body.\nThe brown bear has a rather dark brown hair covering its skin. Otherwise, the skin is rather similar in function to other animals.\n*A rather complicated sketch appears on this next page, showing two sketchings of a bear. The first is of the various muscles within, and the other shows the bear's skeleton.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   This system includes all the muscles, ligaments and tendons within the bear, as well as the entire skeleton.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide motion of the body and structure.\n   The brown bear is a huge, behemoth of-\n- a creature. Its body is rather massive, with large muscles and thick bones, allowing it to be a powerful hunter. Its claws and teeth are also rather sharp to add onto its dangerous nature.\n*This sketch shows the bear's mouth being connected through the throat into its stomach, then into the large/small intestines, then finally out through the back. It's quite noticably the digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   This system also includes the mouth connected through the throat into the stomach, the intestines, then finally excreting out the behind. It also includes the pancreas, gallbladder, and the liver. \n   The purpose of this system is to-\n- extract nutrients from food, then to excrete wastes.\n   The bear is rather similar to other animals in its digestive system.\n*The final sketching seems rather lacking compared to the others, with only displaying the kidneys, and bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   For conjuration purposes, you only need to worry about the kidney and bladder within this system.\n   The purpose of this system is to filter wastes out from the blood stream.\n   For the brown bear, nothing is particularly unique.\nSide Notes:\n-Very defensive of their young, a mother brown bear is a force to be reckoned with.\n-They aren't immune to fire.\n-Sorry.\nList of Systems:\n-Cardiovascular\n-Respiratory\n-Nervous\n-Skin\n-Musculoskeletal\n-Digestive\n-Urinary\n*The final pages of this book are a compilation of miniature versions of all the sketches previously shown in the book. They are relatively close together for comparison.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Recluse", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "The purpose of this book is in detailing the various systems and structures within a brown recluse spider.    The few systems within the brown recluse spider include its two sections. These are its abdomen and its cephalothorax.\n*The next page shows the intricately detailed sketching of a spider's back end. The abdomen. Within it shows the various workings within.*\nAbdomen:\n   The various parts within the abdomen include the heart gut, digestive gland, malpighian tubule, spinnerets, silk glands, and book rung.\n   The purpose of this system is in digesting nutrients, producing webbings, and reproduction.\n*The next sketching is equally detailed as it shows the various structures within the first segment of a spider. Showing its various inner workings, it is the cephalothorax.*\nCephalothorax:\n   The various structures within the cephalothorax are the legs, the brain, the main stomach, simple eyes, pedipalp, poison gland, chelicera, and mouth.\n   The purpose of this system is commanding any remote thought, digesting, -\ncatching pray, locomotion, and providing structure alongside the abdomen.\nSide Notes:\n-A single brown recluse's bite can kill you in about two days. The poison works in a conjuration, but only remains for as long as the conjuration does.\n-Damn this was scary to study.\n-Still not sorry.\nList of Systems:\n-Abdomen\n-Cephalothorax\n*You're met with the two previous sketchings shown within the book, with just as much detail as they are combined to show comparison and the sum of their parts.*", ""),
        StaticBook("C&A: Compliments", "elliot5", "===================   My daily compliment\n===================\n \nEveryday please read one compliment in this book, if you reach the end, just ask for a part two. \n\n===================-- <3 -------------\n===================        Days 1-3\n===================\n\n1) You smell like roses and cinnamon.\n\n2) You're generally just the most funny and outgoing person I've met..\n\n3) Perfection, you are, perfect.\n===================        Days 4-6\n===================\n\n4) Your smile always makes my day.\n\n5) Your laugh always ends up with me laughing.\n\n6) Your grin makes me want to squeese you.\n===================        Days 7-9\n===================\n\n7) My love is endless for someone like you.\n\n8) You are perfect the way you are, changes are optional.\n\n9) When you're hurt, I'm even more hurt.\n===================        Days 10-12\n===================\n\n10) Without you, I am nothing, with you, you are my everything.\n\n11) You smell like roses and cinnamon.\n\n12) I love everything and every part of you.\n===================        Days 13-15\n===================\n\n13) I'm open to anything, no matter how crazy, or weird. \n\n14) I feel safe when I'm with you.\n\n15) Your eyes are a work of beauty.\n===================        Days 16-18\n===================\n\n16) All my problems just go, when you're around me.\n\n17) I dream about you all day, and at night I want to sleep with you.\n\n18) You're an angel.\n===================        Days 19-21\n===================\n\n19) No one or nothing could describe you.\n\n20) Lots and lots of people love you, know this.\n\n21) You're special to me, and many people.\n===================        Days 21-23\n===================\n\n21) Your cuddles are medicine. \n\n22) Whenever you're cold I'm here to warm you up.\n\n23) You're a reliable person.\n===================        Days 24-27\n===================\n\n24) All your flaws only add to why I love you.\n\n25) You're always so happy and kind to people.\n\n26) The time I spend with you, is the best time of my life.\n===================        Days 27-29\n===================\n\n27) My world stops when I see you.\n\n28) Your confidence makes you shine\n\n29) Never, never. Let someone put you down.\n===================        Days 30-32\n===================\n\n30) You can make me laugh and cry with tears of happiness at will.\n\n31) I love you, yes that's it.\n\n32) I'll never forget you.\n===================        Days 33-35\n===================\n\n33) Even when there is discord you handle it.\n\n34) Your voice brings harmony to the lands.\n\n35) You are skilled in the art of being perfect.\n===================        Days 36-38\n===================\n\n36) You remind me of a goddess.\n\n37) You're better at making compliments then me.\n\n38) I have great respect for you.\n===================        Thank you.\n===================\n\nThank you for all you have done, thank you for being with me in need. Thank you for what you are, and what I hope you will become.\n\n<3     I love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("C.S. Bar Tax", "Serelia T.A.", "Welcome to your new establishment, designated Center Square Bar/Grill for tax purposes. Your current tax level is 250 mina per year. To pay, please deposit\n(2) 100 mina tax receipts and\n(1) 50 mina tax receipt each year. ((To be done by Sundays))\nPlease do not remove this document from the chest.\n\nIf there are any concerns, please contact the current Lord/Lady Steward.\n\nOFFICIAL DOCUMENT OF THE CITY OF VELARIS", ""),
        StaticBook("City Secrets", "Ciri'lla", "~City Secrets~\n     Author: ----\n\n\"Nations all have weaknessess. . . just how you utilize them is the matter if downfall will be there only option\"-C\n\n*A twisted picture of a dagger, stained in crimson is below, with a piece of lavender*\n-Index-\nLaureh'lin\n-Preface: 3-4\n-Entryways: 5-8\n-Strengths: 9-11\n-Weaknesses: 12-14\n-Extra Info: 15-17\nHaelun'or\n-Preface: 18-19\n-Entryways: 20-25\n-Strengths: 26-29\n-Weaknesses: 30-35\n-E.I.: 36-37\n-Laureh'lin-\nThe city of wood elves, Mali'ame as more of you know, and other abandoned and lost souls holds some of the most pure and holy sources of power with a continuing connection and grip upon the Grove, filled with Druids, and houses\nquite a few Paladins and Clerics as well. Their constant and blooming community holds strong bonds with one another. . . until everything starts falling apart. . .\n-Entry Ways-\nFront Gate is held together with one layer of iron bars and a wooden gate behind it. One iron door to the left allows guards quick entry and the visitor passage to the right with a small gate allows for quick entry after being identified\nCoord.: X: 2394, Z:-2024\n\nA mine resides in the back side of the settlement, only approved workers may enter as well.\nCoord.: X: 2505, Z:-2030\n\nThe other main entry is in the back, next to the mine almost with\none iron gate in the front, which is damaged as of now, and a wooden one behind it. Entry through this route would be most likely easier than the front since there is an empty are once entering here which is usually vacant while the front has a large\nstairway where many tend to hang about.\nCoord.: X:2534, Z:-2044\n\n*All coordinates marked seem to be depicted as a small image, as if drawing the image of the central area*\n\nAlso, the back gate's lever is vulnerable.\n-Strengths-\n*The amount of paladins and archdruids at a snap of a fingers pose a threat to any dark magic users.\n*Various healers, whether magical or surgical, reside in the town with a clinic near the back gate\n*Their tall defenses, being their walls, are built with wood and reinforced by stone in order to resist damaging blows\n*A large force of soldiers, the Sirame, are generally around quite a lot \n*The community knows one another very well so they are able to\npick out those who do not fit their usual social groups. By this, it is meant to not be too creepy or wear ominous objects.\n\n*A few drawings of hoods, robes, colored hairs, and a ghost like creature are here as examples*\n-Weaknesses-\n*The whole place is generally made of wood! A torch, bomb, fire evocation. . . just light it so it may turn to ash!\n*Their gate in the back has a vulnerable lever in which someone could open to let others in.\n*There are so many houses and alleyways that it is easy for someone to sneak around, prey upon others. \n*Some egg sacks of spiders I believe reside in some of the tall tree tops\n*Many of them rely on their emotions rather than knowledge, easy to\nbreak them apart just by killing one of their family.\n*Generally slow at building and do not have many minas. . .\n*A civil war can be easily broken out with druids against Oren. . . one dead may result in all out warfare\n*Artimec Camoryn. . .\n-Extra Info-\n*This city does not allow magic without payment, which may be their minas resource. Not following such will result in fines and punishment. Fire and conjuration seem to be their biggest fears by this decree\n*Right next to the grove,\ntheir farms spread amongst the outside of the defenses. This may be utilized for poisoning, corrupting, or cursing to ruin their food, animal, and water resources. \n*Two large mechanical bow like weapons are located one in front side and one in back.\nFront Coord.: X:2486, Z:-2147\nBack Coord.: X:2554\nZ:-2045\n\n*A large crossbow like machine is depicted here, with wheels to push it*\n-Haelun'or-\nAwe, the city of the 'pure' high elves, Mali'aheral. This city of stone and elegant glass is home to many Mali'aheral who seek to have a similar community and be protected of their highly regarded principles. A lot of knowledge is held\nin this city whether it be in the magical arts or in the many books the Eternal Library holds. . . those who may seem purest to may not be, seeing a lot of dark magic is actually in the city as you read. . . it is just who will be revealed first?\n-Entry-\nThis city seems to be one of the most well guarded due to their principles of prestigious purity. The first obstacle is the large bridge connecting to a small island up north which is very beautiful and contructed from stone. The first\ngate appears on the bridge which is generally left open. It is also before the the fountain in front of the main entryway.\nCoord.: X:80, Z:-416\n\nThe next main entry is right behind the bridge gate, which is the hardest way to enter into this\nfortification. It is a series of iron barred gates, three to be almost exact, which are reinforced with a quartz structure and even more stone. This provides for a towering and great defense. However, a large stained glass symbol of the Mali'aheral sits\nabove such which may be broke into easily if having accessibility to anything that may crash through it or anything to pull you through it such as ropes.\nCoord.: X:80, Z:-371\n\nThe back gate, being the better way to get inside, is just a single iron gate\nwhich is smaller than the ones in front. It is next to the stable of horses in the back too.\n\nCoord.: X:55, Z:-291\n\nLastly, all the sides of the island are fortified with stone and quartz boundaries which cuts off access from\nthe sea. However, you may swim or sail all the way to island that connects the main one by a land bridge to get onto the island securely. It may be some steep slopes but its an easy way to get in.\nBack Island Coord.: X:185, Z:-207\n-Strengths-\n*The defense for this city is amazing with quartz and stone walls lining the base to defend from sea entry and rock pillars to support the walls.\n*Even though the guards of the Mali'ame are around more, the Evarir, guards here, are\nmuch more organized and take their roles very seriously compared to those of Laureh'lin. It is usually black and white with them, meaning no exceptions.\n*Generally good about who they allow in, being it must be of pure characteristics and have a clean\nstatus.\n*Punishment such as liquidating in acid, banishment, or execution is very severe here with no mercy shown usually.\n*Haelun'or exemplifies in collection of resources with various land claims and usage of lumber south of the area\n*A profound amount of knowledge is here being in the many texts of the Eternal Library, the people and their abilities, and rare artifacts well protected. \n*The set of rules, following Maehr'sae hiylun, is pretty specific, which governs the people\n-Weaknesses-\n*The guard force, Evarir, are not around the area as often like the Sirame are\n*Ignorance is a big issue among them, being if you have redeeming qualities and show a bit of knowledge on their culture, you will be allowed in\n*The entryway through the back side is much weaker than in the front. Also, the land bridge seemingly ruins the point of the sea barriers since people may cross over that way\n*Rumors and anger is spread quickly which may easily get someone outcasted from\nthe establishment by their fellow peers\n*Many there are not really pure so uncovering one may lead to a lot of chaos politically, with new laws, or physically, with warfare\n*Their large resource of water is all around them which may be easily\nvulnerable to cursing or corrupting\n*Some of the farming, being sugarcane and lumber, lies outside the defenses as well which may be burnt down or destroyed\n*A lot of the structuring is made to be stable but is also made to look elaborate, meaning\ndelicate like the glass art or some of the weak stone structures\n*No paladins or druids reside here, since most of that magic tends to be frowned upon, so healing or direct danger against dark magic isnt a threat\n*Expansive research may hold dangerous\nand deadly chemicals or ores, such as Thanhium, which could destroy them from the inside out.\n-Extra Info-\n*A lot of dark magic users reside here. . . watch your back if not of their kind\n*Thanhium seems to have already wrecked them, multiple Thanhium bombs having already been set off\n*Devoid of a lot of emotion, many of them rely on their\nmorals and intelligence\n*Many tend to learn the magical arts so combat is harder for them meaning smaller muscles and stability\n*Recording of your name and personal info is done when entering, so they may track who resides there\n-Conclusion-\nA pleasure it has been to record down all these useful tips, information, and mapping of these noble cities in the case of information used later on. Each holds their own values and properties and to use against themselves\nto eleminate them. The people of these elvish establishments are generally kind hearted, or just extremely stuck in their ways, so they do not accept dark magic. As a warning, be prepared to develop strategy. . . it is the only way.~\n*Crude images of Laureh'lin on the top half and Haelun'or on the bottom half are shown, as if an ending note to this fabulous book*\n\n\n~May the odds forever be in your favor~-C", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Len", "morrisaye", "\"Dear Len,\n\nMy name is Ashton. I'm not sure if you'll know me when you're older, but I am your cousin -- more or less. \n\nMy dad and your dad have been best friends for many years. We might as well be sisters, really.\"\n\"Your dad has my greatest friend since I met him when I was seven years old. \n\nI want to tell you about how wonderful, kind, and amazing he is.\"\n\"I know that he can sometimes get loud, mean, scary, over protective, odd, and all the other traits that dads have. \n\nYou need to know, though, that he is the best man I've ever met in my entire life.\"\n\"When I was a small girl, I was afraid of your father. \n\nHe was very smart, and he ran the library. \n\nI felt like he thought I was a stupid little girl.\"\n\"In fact, the first time I met him, he accused me of being a thief. Tried to tell me to leave the grove, even! \nI was so angry at him for accusing me of that. Now, I look back on it and laugh.\"\n\"I remember a time when I went to Felsen -- I doubt it will exist by the time you're older enough to read this letter. That place is worse than the nether. -- I couldn't have been more than 8 or 9 years old.\"\n\"I went to a church ceremony there. For some king who died, I don't know. \n\nAfter the ceremony ended, an Orc came up and tried to kidnap me! \nDo you know who rescued me? \n\nIt was your dad.\"\n\"From that moment on, I felt so safe around him. \n\nI was a very shy kid. I never spoke to anyone except for your father and my father.\n\nYour dad was my safe haven. I went to him every day.\"\n\"He told me stories and sung me songs. I'm sure he'll do those things for you, too. \n\nHe took care of me. He made me smile no matter how sad I was. He made me feel special and loved. He made me feel like I had a family.\"\n\"Any problems I had, I could go to him. Remember that. Remember that, no matter what, he'll be there for you. He will listen and help you. \n\nHe doesn't always have the right answers or know what to say, but he will do the best he can.\"\n\"I spent every day with him growing up.\n\nHe was always very brave. \n\nAny time a scream would ring through the grove, he'd run to it. I never saw him run away.\"\n\"He protected the children in the grove.\n\nHe's a very noble man, no matter what he says about himself.\"\n\"That's another thing you should understand.\n\nHe'll always talk poorly of himself. Make himself out to be a monster. \n\nIndeed, sometimes he'll do monsterous things.\"\n\"At the end of the day, though, he is the kindest, gentlest, most loving person I'll ever know. \n\nI love him with all of my heart. \n\nHe loves you and your mother with all of his heart. Never forget that.\"\n\"I love you as well, Len. I will try my hardest to be there for you as much as I can. You are family to me, and any time you need someone, just send me a bird. I'll come as fast as I can. \nYour dad will, too. Always.\"\n\"I hope you have the best life you can, Len. \n\nYou are beautiful, just like your mother. Yet, you have your dad's eyes. \n\nI always thought he had the most fantastic eyes I had ever seen.\"\n\"Be happy. Be healthy. Be proud of who you are and where you come from. \n\nLove you. \n\n\n-Ashton Gallic\nThe Swan Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Decisions.", "Dirk Novokain", "[!] On the backside of the notebook's cover would be written:\n\"Taking time to write down your thoughts, can be a blessing and a curse.\"\nThrough times we have all made decisions, every single descendant and non-descendant has made decisions. I dare even say decisions are what shape the world around us. It's all based around the decisions that we, our ancestors, the aenguls, the daemons,\nanything and anyone has made. That is why everything is why it is.\nThough, I perceive that some people's decisions matter more than others. The decisions of the Emperor matter more, than the decisions of a peasant. But then again, all decisions ever made have mattered to shape our world.\nOf course, I myself have made decisions to change the world around me. I have made good and bad decisions, many of which I regret. Many people hope, even pray, for a chance to go back and amend their decisions, and some see leaving their life behind as\na way to amend their decisions. And I have to admit, I have considered many times, to just up and leave, to start over again.\n\n[!] In much smaller writing, it would say:\n\"And even as of late, the thought has been reappearing frequently.\"\n[!] And in almost tiny writing, on the last page of the notebook, which had been ripped in half, it would say:\n\"But I can't, and I won't leave.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "Tristanm1", "The Dedicant's Vow\nScribed by Salmon Druid Petyr\nI will walk the forest with my new kin, I will swim the river of truth, wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need, I will help preserve the balance, even as dusk approaches.\nI vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary", "Raziel", "23rd of The Grand Harvest, 1554:\n\nAs I look out of the opening of Jue's tent, all I see is this floating structure. The lands is heavily scorched around it, but it has some kind of overworldly, heavenly spark to it.\nPillars of what looks to be quartz are streching out from the ground, lava and burned grass everywhere.\nThis floating structure of some sort, looks like it has a library on the top of it.\n[!] A quick sketch of the scene would be drawn here ((contact Dracofire for picture))\n\nFrom my tent I can feel the warmth, Jude is currently taking his own notes to this chaotic scene. I don't know what this is, I will provide more information once\ngathered.\n\n2nd of Sun's Smile:\n\nA man met us at out camp, we don't know if he has evil intentions or not, Jude and man nearly ended up in a fight. Man walked off to get his tent.\nMan is called Dagr.\n3rd of Sun's Smile:\nWe climbed the one of the platforms which was around the main island using a makeshift grappelinghook. We then climbed up to the library from the smaller platform which appeared to be trying to find balance.\nWhen we were ontop of the library, we found some books containing historical information about some holy warrior, and the ascendeds war between the undead.\nWe were however unable to take the books, since they were burning with immense heat, it didn't\nlook like normal flames though, looked more holy, almost heavnly. Jude got filled with greed and attempted to take one of the books, his hand then burned and I myself had to cut it off.\nWe then went to the second floor, Marvick, and me examined the\narea on the upperfloor, it looked as if something was missing.\n\nAs I looked at a few of the books on the bookshelves, I could tell that they contained information about the Ascendeds war between the undead, and a rather weird book\nwhich from what I could see was about some holy warrior, fighting an everlasting combat in a city within the skies.\n\nI at this moment don't know how to put out the holy fire which is around the books, but I will attempt at my best to search for the\ninformation I need.\n6th of Sun's Smile 1554:\nI returned to the island, a strange man was standing there, releasing my makeshift grapplinghook still hanging down from the island, he refuses to give information about who I am, he keeps calling me descendant?\nHe says the thing crashed down alongside the other meteors, and that it's a place for the ascended.\nIs waiting for the ascended to come and claim the island. He says he is ascended of Aeriel. The island supposly floats because of the books.\nSays he wont harm descdantes unless I climb up\nCalled Garsto over, who apparently has a shot at becoming ascendant.\n3rd of Amber Cold 1554:\nCame to get back Jude's hand, looks like something exploded up there.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary Entry #567", "Doc", "Dear Diary,\n\nStill too tired to build Doc's Dock... How am I supposed to build it everytime we move villages? I've done it about 8 times now!\n\nI can't put it off, though, might as well start of the work... I still need to return these books, though...", ""),
        StaticBook("Document #1", "Owynn Iron-Forge", "Owynn Iron-Forge, hereby referred to as the signee, on signing this legal document, promises a lump sum of 4000 mina to be paid out in the month of Sun's Smile, 1542, and promises another lump sum of 1600 mina to be paid out later within the Elvish Month.\nIf the signee does not comply within the legal span of time, or if Lexa and Nemir, referred to as the owners, choose to alleviate the deal, all rights of the tavern, as well as any brought in income, shall return to the owners. In the event that the\nowners decide to refuse the agreed upon amount, the signee will be refunded the amount of money that they have paid. In the event that the signee decides to renig the deal, none of the money that was originally paid to the owners will be refunded.\nSection for Wealth Distribution\nThe original lump sum of 4000 mina provided to the owners will be distributed equally into their respective banks, as well as the 1600 mina secondary payment. If either party attempts economic subterfuge, all assets given\nvia this contract will be returned to the other respective owner. Notorized, John the Friendly, Financial and Legal Advisor to Blackwood Industries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragons", "Archrim Elmoran", "Dragons\n\nDragons are now days know by most everyone, much like our less dangerous chicken, the dragon egg goes into a one month incubation period in which the mother warms the eggs under her belly\nThe mother dragon increases her body temperature to that of a large and very hot fire for more than hours at a time, for about a month, then the eggs hatches and the dragon progresses to the stage of a hatchling\nThe young dragon is not yet able to fly but it does have wings none the less and they wont be able to fly untill much later,\nDragon hatchlings are normaly the size of a male wolf but are usually pretty tame and are much like a big puppy\nonly within its second week of life the young hatchling is left on its own and goes to hunt and live for itself, not long after this time the dragon reaches its ability to summon fire, not in the ammount to be deadly by it is noted that smoke can be seen\nrising from the nostrills and mouth about this time. After about a year the hatchling is no longer a baby but is to be considerd a drake\n\nAt this age the dragon cannot yet summon the full power of fire but are actually quite deadly hunters and\nare known to be quite grumpy. they are also seen wondering farther from their nest at this age to help satisfy their curiosity, for this reason they are the most commonly seen dragon since they tend to wonder close to cities and towns\nbut out in the wild they are know to attack and kill any who come near them\n\nYears later the dragon now becomes a full adult and is now able to do 3 things\n1- summon fire\n2- fly\n3- mate\nAdult dragons are mainly unaggresive since they do not care much about what the other races do but still it is not recommended to approch or sneak up on a dragon for it could mean the end for you, But there are time in which a dragon tends to be aggresive\none of which is during their mating season, if a town is within a certian distance of a chosen nesting spot they will destroy it\nIt should also be noted that the well known myth of dragons having a affinity for gold and or gems has never been proven or\ndisproven and should be kept in mind while exploring caves, also it is known that dragons enjoy riddles I have no idea if its true but this should be remembered if you come face to face with a dragon within its nest, it might just save your life.\nEventually if the dragon survives adulthood it becomes a wyrm, which is a very old dragon and very few of them have ever been said to exist\nThey should be feared and never sought out but I would say judging by how dragons attitudes are they are mostly\nnonagressive and would see us as if we were no bigger than a fly, and could care less about what we do, and I would imagin that they are extreamly wise at the same time, but none the less do not try to find a wyrm because death is still possible", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur Books", "Aeran", "Books the Dragur Library does not have:\n\n-Filtration mask\n-Close but far\n-De Shroom Guide\n-Letter Of Marrow\n-Mana Gem Research\n-Boogie Man Letter\n-Tend'el's Journal\n-Elephant Inn\n-A Time Before\n-An Orphan\n-Wise Sayings\n-Zei Grei\n-Malinor's Fall\n-A Dangerous Art\n-Opinion On Truth\n-Gardening Guide\n-Mysterious Badge\n-Saren's Journal\n-On Pigmen\n-Seeds Of Laurelin\n-Notes On Inwe", ""),
        StaticBook("Earthen Rocks", "Gladuos", "In this book we will be exploring the traits of common earthen materials found in the lands of Vailor. As such, we'll describe how it basically reacts to the senses, how it's formed, average weight, shape, hardness, breaking point, and finally the -\n- magical understanding of them.\nCommon earthen materials can be divided into three categories. That being metamorphic, sedimentary, and igneous rocks. \n\n   Igneous rocks are formed from the cooling of lava or magma into a solid form.\nSedimentary rocks are formed by the corrosion and deposition of other types of rocks that eventually lead into being compacted into new materials.\n\nMetamorphic rocks are formed by the intense heating of either igneous or\nsedimentary rocks which lead into fundamental changes of the rock's structure.\nGenerally there is no singular appearance to what a rock may look like but normally they are rigid, dull-colored pieces of stone that may seem grainy to the senses. \n\n   Rocks are usually very dense, hard pieces of material, mostly thanks to\ntheir natural crystalized structures. Although they can be found in grains such as sand as well.\nThere is no clear cut way to describe how rocks were originally formed without first understanding how the world itself was created, but that is a subject for another time. Although the basic understanding can be surmised for each type of common rock.\nDue to their efficient compactibility, rocks are can easily take on very dense, heavy forms. This is evident in Mankind's prevalent usage of the earthen materials to form strong constructions.\nRocks can take on a plethora of different shapes depending on how they were eroded or compacted. This can be shown in the descendant's rigorous usage of sculpting to form the many different earthen materials into statues and statuettes.\nOnce again rocks are very dense, and heavy materials. So it comes as no surprise when it's revealed that they are incredibly hard to break as well. Evident in the creation of golems, swords would be no use against these types of constructs.\nRegardless, Mankind has taken the liking to creating smashing tools to deal with these tough materials.\nThere is no set melting point for any of these materials as rocks can take on a large variety of different types. However, one can usually bet that an earthen rock will reach its melting point at about 1200 degrees Celsius.\nAnd finally, one must understand the magical signature of these materials. Now, rocks are a fairly common material on this world of ours, and such they will only hold a mediocre value of magical energies as compared to the more precious minerals such\nas gemstones.\n*Upon reaching the next page you are greeted with a plethora of diagrams, sketchings, charts, illustrations, and equations that span onwards for many many pages. They are accompanied by several notes and lines of information. The following pages -\n- merely seem to attempt supporting the previous statements, as well as point out more nuanced, less relevant points of information.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ebon Darkness", "Itiireae", "Observations\n\nIt was unlike anything of which I had ever beheld. Ebon scales as dark as twilight clicking and grinding into form what it was only desribable as an appendage meant to look like that of a hand and forearm. The fear that gripped me at\nsuch an unnatural sight bright dread as real as air into my lungs and terror as sharp as ice into my throat. I know not of what this is. I know not of what he can do. I only know that fear builds and grows. Actions of which transpired compelling me into\nsubmission. I will observe. I will observe and record. For that is all I can muster.\n\nObservations II\n\n[!] The rest of the book seems to be badly damaged from water stains.\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nHi :^)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elephant Inn", "Ser Paul Ryan Jr.", "+ The Elephant Inn + -------------------\n\n       Foodstuffs:\n\nBread - 1 mina\nBaked Potatoe - 2 mina Steak - 5 mina\n\nVarious specials - ask\n+ The Elephant Inn + -------------------           Drinks \n\nAle - 2 Mina\nWine - 3 Mina\nSpecial - Ask\n+ The Elephant Inn +\n-------------------         Services \n\nRooms - 10 minas \nMassage - 5 minas \nEntertainment - varies \nSpecials - ask", ""),
        StaticBook("Elf A&P (L)", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "This book has been created for the purpose of documenting a few various systems involved within the elven anatomy.\n   A few of these systems involve: Nervous system, Respiratory system, skin, Cardiovascular system, Musculoskeletal system, Digestive-\n-system, and Urinary system.\n*Upon flipping to the next page you are greeted by an incredibly detailed and full scale sketching of what appears to be the nervous system. The brain appears connected with a large system of nerves throughout the body via the spinal cord.*\nNervous System:\n   The nervous system is primarily composed of the brain, nerves, and the spinal cord which connected the two throughout the body.\n   The purpose of the nervous system is to provide consciousness to the creature and allow its -\n- bodily functions to automate. The nerves and spinal cord allow for context with the body around the brain, such as pain and feeling.\n   The primary functions of the nervous system are relatively the same within the elven anatomy with exception to its -\n-superior intellect.\n*You see yet another sketch similar to the previous one with a detailed showcase of what appears to be the respiratory system. It shows the mouth and nose connected through the throat towards the lungs.*\nRespiratory System:\n   This system includes various structures such as the nose and mouth connected via the passages through the throat towards the lungs.\n   The main purpose of the respiratory system is to provide oxygen to the bloodstream.\nAs for the average elven individual, this has no particular deviation.\n*Another sketching appears on this page. With closer examination you can see a heart connected via various veins and arteries spreading throughout an entire outline of an elven man's body.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   The main parts of this system include the heart, veins, blood vessels, and arteries.\n   The purpose of this system is to pump blood throughout the body and provide it with its various nutrients.\n   An average elven individual\nhas only one heart throughout its system.\n*The sketching on this page appears to show both a full body representation of its various muscles in extreme detail as well as a full skeleton. This appears to be the musculoskeletal system.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   Muscles, tendons and ligaments, and bones are various portions within this system.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide the body with motion and structure in its daily activities.\n   An elven individual is bipedal and\nsome what thinner compared to the other races.\n*As usual a sketching would appear on this next page. There appears to be the mouth again connected through a separate passage in the throat towards the stomach, then the large and small intestines, then finally out the bottom. The digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   Within this system is the mouth connected through a separate passage through the throat into the stomach, through the intestines and out the rectum. There also appears the gallblader, pancreas, and appendix.\n   The purpose of this\n-system is to extract nutrients from food, then to excrete wastes.\n   There is no particular anomaly with this system for the average elven individual.\n*There appears a sketch of an elven man with dark skin, then another sketch of skin from the side so you can see its various connective tissues. This system is of the skin.*\nSkin:\n   Although a single organ of its own right, the skin is so large and complex that it constitutes as its own system. This system also includes the various connective tissue within the skin but below the surface.\n   The purpose of skin is to provide-\n-a barrier from the outside environment for the rest of the body. It helps protect from various things that range from injury to disease.\n   As for elves, various shades of skin can exist, and as showcased on the prior sketch, it can be dark, but also-\n-can be rather light, depending on the pigmentation.\n*This next sketch appears a lot less complex as the previous ones, but just as detailed. Within the sketch you can see includes the kidneys and bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   This system includes the kidneys, bladder, and urethra.\n   Although a smaller system, the purpose of this system is rather important. It exists for extracting and excreting wastes out of the blood stream.\n   There are no-\n-anomalies existent within this system for the average elf.\nSide Notes:\n-Although relatively the same to other races, I've included details within the sketchings to provide visual reference for structural differences in the elven race.\nList of Systems:\n-Nervous\n-Respiratory\n-Skin\n-Cardiovascular\n-Musculoskeletal\n-Digestive\n-Urinary\n*Upon reaching the final pages, you can see miniature versions of the various sketches you've seen throughout this book.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 3", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 3\n\nOriginally By: \nKalenz Unradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\nTo conjugate verbs in elven, one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated: \n\n-e - 1st sing\n\n-a - 2nd sing\n\n-e - 3rd sing\n-ae - 1st pl\n\n-an - 2nd pl\n\n-eyae - 3rd pl\n\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simply in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day.\nFor these two tenses, the following four words are used:\n\nKarin'ento- Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante- Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento- Next sunset\nKer'ante- Last sunset\n\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are\nsimply added on the end of sentences to designate the tense. Ex. : Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech, these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno, and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ent Legend", "birdwhisperer", "Foreword\n\nThis book is originally from Asulon, and was found in the Druid’s Grove of Elandriel. Its author is unknown, and it was brought to Anthos and preserved by Elorna Avern.\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n The Legend of the\n           Ents\nThe Ents are mysterious creatures that were found within the forests of Aegis, and now in Asulon. Little is known about them, but they are often found near sacred groves or ancient trees, keeping them protected and free of disruption. But the tale of the\nfirst Ent is interesting in itself.\n\nIt is said that the Aspects granted ancient and wonderful power to a certain tree older than time itself. This tree, far wiser than the entire forest, yearned to protect his kind, but could not do much\nfrom within the confines of his roots. So, he waited for the stars to align, and produced a seed of gold, and let it fall to the foot of his gargantuan trunk to sprout.\n\nThrough the course of many moons, this seed grew until it became a\ntree half as large as its father. However, it found that its roots were not bound in the soil, and so it walked. It roamed the forest, finding purpose under the gentle guidance of the Eldertree. The Ent soon found humans attempting to fell an ancient oak,\nwhich cried out in agony. Letting out a roar, the great being assumed its role as guardian of the forest, and tore through the men with unforgiving vengeance. And such is the story of the first Ent.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ethros Goodbye", "Gray Kellian III", "My Dearest Elinor and Gray. I know I havent spoken to either of you in a long time.. \n\nBut I have some regrets on my mind I wish to expell, before my unavoidable death sometime in the future.\nFirstly, To My First, and only son Gray, I have so much I wanted to tell you, So much I wanted to do with you, Stuff a Father and son should have done together.\n\nBut with the death of your mother. Our lives were thrown into an unavoidable chaos.\nAnd that is where my first Regret Lies. As a man who as you know, lived with the rule of \"Live your life, without Regrets.\" This is hard to speak about.. but I know you will understand.\nI wish before you ran away, Before I couldent find you, Before I went mad.. I wish I could of been there for you. to help you through the pain in your heart, to help you ease the suffering of loseing a loved one,\nBut, I couldent. I failed as a father. In more ways than one *some tear marks can be seen present in the page* I always wanted to have a family, You and your sisters were the Greatest thing to happen to me. But I failed. and I am sorry.\nSecondly, I wanted to say just how proud I am of you. I know I do not have the right because I wasent there for you growing up. But I met some of your friends. Karyssmov is a good man, And I hope you continue your friendship tell the end of times.\n*more tear marks,* I also got to see You aswell one more Elinor. And to you, I have more regrets than anyone. I always wanted to see you grow up, to see you become the brilliant young woman you are now. *tears* I know your mother never told you who your\nreal father was. But I am able to tell you.\n\n*many scribbles can be seen as if he wrote something, before scratching it out, over, and over, and over again*\n*Blank page*\nIts me.\nI know it seems farfetched.. but it is true. After your mothers partner died, and After my wife died. We both were stricken with Greif, After I fled the city, your mother moved to Haria.. On one fateful night I went to meet her. And from that visit, You\nwere created. My Daughter. Your Mother was never able to remember, we both were highly intoxicated.. But when She found out she was having a baby, I knew it was mine. and this is my greatest Regret. I never told her nor you.\nBut I couldent.. I didn't have the courage, So I Just watched over you, poseing as your uncle, I came to see you everyday, I loved you.\n\nAnd thats when Your mother made Lilliana and Ed your godparents.\nI knew if anything ever happened you would go with them I fought with your mother to reconcider, to let you go with me instead of them. but after she died, Lilliana swept in and took you away before I had the chance to take you back, to be your father.\nAnd I was greif ridden, I lost yet another child. First Gray when he ran away. Then Leona the same way. And then you.. Taken away by people I trusted. taken by people who were not your blood. all because I didnt have the courage to speak up.\nAnd it drove my madness further. Until I broke, So please. Tell Archrim I am sorry for that day, And Tell Princess Lilyana I am sorry I betrayed her and left her side for madness. And most of all, I am sorry to you Elinor\nSo Please.. Forgive me,  *Tear marks*\n\nI am so sorry... I am a horrible father,  But I hope *Tear marks* If you can forgive me, you both can live on happily.. knowing you are close family than you thought\nLove,\n\n   Your Loving Father\n     Ethro Kellian II\n\n\n  Please remember me\nwithout hate. but with Love my children,\n\nThis is Goodbye", ""),
        StaticBook("Fiction Volume 1", "Brathal MacDuhn", "Greybeard Fiction\n\n\"My Precious\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Brathal MacDuhn\nRestless did it make his mind, frustrated due to absence, Her absence. The ‘Ker rolled to his right, seeking a means to rid himself of this lust. This.. desire, a desire for Her. He could not think, merely act. And thus the ‘Ker went out.\nHe had been watching her from a distance. Her visit to the Druids, her time with Aeran and his wife. No, he would not have it. He would not have Her, yet. When she emerged without his mark, he had grown enraged.\nAn arm extended to her direction, grabbing the air in vain. However, he had to bide his time. She wasn’t alone, he could not make her his yet. Her visit to a grave was when he would follow. The young high elven maiden knelt by the grave site of a toddler.\nHe watched her in silence as another came and consoled her a moment. He watched her speak then leave. The dark lips parting into a cheshire cat grin.\nHe followed her into Laureh’lin. Her innocence, her naivety. His lust for it, his hunger, brought him closer. His mind still restless, unclear, a tunnel. The ‘Ker now here, made his first mistake, for as he approached, he brought forth a dagger.\nThe shadows hid the mali’ker from view. Slowly he stepped behind her and covered her mouth. Producing the dagger had been a mistake. She struggled, cutting her hand, leaving blood on the door in her struggles.\nHe cursed, dropped the dagger and moved to hit her hard in the head, causing her to crumple into his arm. Breathing heavily he stood there, embracing Her.\n“Alast, my dear, we are together once more.” The Ker then spoke on a hushed tone.\nShe was his now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fiction Volume 2", "Brathal MacDuhn", "Greybeard Fiction\n\n\"The Guardian of the Woods\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Brathal MacDuhn\nA cool breeze finds its way through the dense forest. Twigs crack as they move along in the wind, leaves detaching from them. You peer around in the misty undergrowth as all of a sudden a chill finds its way up your spine.\nA certain disturbance boils up inside of you, as your eyes spot a form of movement in the corner of your eye. Slowly the grip around your axe tightens, your fingers firmly clasped around the wooden hilt.\nA certain thing approaches, footsteps are heard: Slow… Heavy… Slowly but surely it approaches. Yet, nothing seen but trees. “Who are you?” You mutter, as you carefully take a few steps back, your boots sticking in the muddy soil.\nThe footsteps no longer heard. A silence once more fills the forests, all silent but the breeze. The being must have stopped you think. Perhaps it was all just imagination.\nYour left hand detaches its self from your axe, as you proceed your way onto the marked tree, a few feet away from you. You inspect it, and deem it ready to be processed.\nYou grab the hilt and swing back, when all of a sudden an Ancient Roar fills your surroundings, the breeze changed to a wind flow onto you. Carrying countless leaves from the trees around you.\nUnable to see your surrounding you trip over exposed roots. The axe releasing its self from your hands as you fall into the muddy forest soil. The forest now dies once more, all sound, even the breeze had stopped.\nNo more footsteps, no more roaring. A dead silence had filled your surroundings as you look around you. Confused, Scared, Desperate even you look around you as you try and get back on your feet.\nWith shaking leggs you take a step towards the place where your axe fell. Upon the touching of its wooden hilt. Another Roar fills the forest. Closer, as if next to you.\nSurvival instincts and fear take over, forcing you to sprint off in the same direction as you came from. Slowly the being turns around. Cracking. Falling of leaves.\nUp until the moment the Ent reached the centre of the forest. The heavy footsteps stopped. As had the Cracking. Silence filling the forest as slowly the breeze, finds its way back into it. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("First Seed 1570", "Ashton", "*A few pages of Ashton's old journals are torn out and included with this letter.*\n\"I talked to Mister Aeran, and I do feel a bit better. Still, I feel like I'm not special to anyone. I just sort of exist. I feel so lonely.\n\nMister Aeran said I can talk to him whenver I feel lonely. I hope it helps.\"\n\"I care very deeply for him. I'm not sure in what way. He is the one person I can count on. He's always been there for me.\n\nI wish I could make him truly happy. I wish I could make him feel joy.\"\n\"I feel sad today. I don't know why. It's like a darkness pulling me down. I just feel so...I don't have a word for it.\"\n\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\n\"Aeran and I talked for the longest time. He made me feel so much happier.\"\n*After the three journal pages, the actual letter begins. \n\nThe markings are smudged and written with sloppy writing, but not bad enough that it can't be made out. It would seem to be emotionally written.*\nI don't know when I lost you. I don't know when it was that I stopped coming to you for help, advice, whenever I felt lonely. \nI think I forgot. I stopped reading my journals for a long time, and I forgot. I forgot that the theme was always the same.\nEvery single journal has one thing in common.\n\nYou. \n\nYou and me.\n\nYou and me against the world. \n\nWe were always together. Every day.\nWhen did it stop? \n\nWhy did stop? Is it my fault? Was it Avayla? Was it because of how things went with my aunt? \n\nWhatever happened, I know it's my fault. I let myself fade away, and I stopped talking to you as much. Now here we are.\nI feel like I've lost the greatest friend I ever had in my entire life, and it's all my fault. \n\nI just knew you'd always be there for me, no matter what, that I took you for granted.\nNow, you have an actual daughter. Not just some stupid, overemotional goddaughter.\nI'm sorry I stressed you out. I'll leave you and Len alone from now on. I didn't mean to cause you pain. I've never wanted to cause you pain. All I've ever wanted was to make you as happy as you used to make me. \n\nI'm sorry I'm so terrible.\nAeran...\n\nYou will always by my dad in my heart. You raised me. I know you'll do so great with Len, because I know how happy you made me. I know I'm not great, but look where I am now. I wouldn't be me without you having been in my life.\nI love you, Dad. \n\nI always will.\n\n- Ashton", ""),
        StaticBook("For Daniel", "Nemir", "Right.... Left.... Down...\nUp.\n\nNo matter where I am.  No matter where you stand.\n\nNorth... South... East... West.\n\nIt can be over a hill or beneath a tree.\nForward... Backwards... Inwards... Outwards.\n\nNo matter where.  I'll still love your warm eyes.\n\nThrough here... Through there... \n\nAnywhere.\nNo matter where.\n\nI'll still love hearing your wonderful laugh.\n\nI'll still love seeing your comforting smile.\n\nWherever.\n\nI'll still love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Nemir", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "You've given me drive to do better in this life. A purpose I am proud of every day. I'm so whole with you around, it's like a dream sometimes and I wonder if I'm going to wake up. \n\nYou tell me that I'm your sun and your torch, but you're my heart.\nYou are my core, my love. With you I am given structure, and strength. A reason once again. We can hold each other together; we'll make it through anything if we just hold on.\nThank you for being the only one that can look upon me at my lowest and still love me. Unconditionally...\n\n\nI love you, Nemir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Foul Play", "Hileia'elr", "-----Foul Play-----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nCan a simple man overcome his feelings for the most lovely creature he's ever met; Or will he have to express his true feelings?\nIt was a day like any other in the Caliphate. The sun was shining, there were few clouds to be seen, and there were plenty of travelers coming to Al- Wakhrah looking to make some coin, or buy some supplies.\nIn fact, for Larrion, it was the perfect day to run a shop. His store was flooded with customers, wanting to buy some goods from the man. Larrion would shout out, pleading with the sea of people in his tiny shop to make a single-file line.\nAfter about an hour of the alchemist selling to the large amount of travelers in his shop, a man in a red hat approached the counter. It was his friend, Keltran. \"Aye, Larrion, how you doing?\" Larrion simply groaned, wiping off the counter.\n\"What do you want?\" Larrion said with a neutral tone.\n\n\"Well...\" Beltran began, \"I felt somewhat sorry about what I did to you a while ago...\"\n\n\"Wait.\" Larrion started. \"What did you do now?\"\n\"Oh! S-So you don't know?!\" Keltran exclaimed.\n\n\"You fool... The hell did you do now?\"\n\n\"U-Uhm... Why don't you go for a nice walk while I watch your store?!?\" Keltran nervously stated.\nLarrion gave him a dead look. \"This isn't over... Here are the keys.\"\n\nAs Keltran watched the store, Larrion walked out of his shop, turning to the left to see the lines of small stores set up.\nHe walked pass the fountain, and made a sharp turn into his friend's store.\n\nAs he opened the doors to the small shop, he noticed a person behind the counter, sorting some books.\nIt was none other than Netiley the Vixen. She was sorting her collection of magic books, guides, and novels for sale.\n\n\"Ooh, hello, Larrion!\" she said. \"Have you come for your royalties today?\"\n\"Er, yes...\" Larrion replied. \"How many of my books have you sold?\"\n\nNetiley plopped a brown sack on the counter. \"See for yourself.\" she said.\nAs Larrion opened the pouch, about 85 minas shimmered with a sparkling flare. Larrion then dipped his nose inside the bag and took in a deep breath.\n\n\"Aah, minas...\"\n\"Thank you, Netily.\" Larrion said, as he placed the pouch into his bag. \"Yuuup! No problem.\" Netiley replied.\n\nAs Larrion was just about to leave, he noticed yet another figure over the counter...\nIt was a chicken. A small, white, chicken, sitting behind Netily on it's lap.\n\nLarrion stared for quite some time. \"Who is that?\"\n\nNetily pointed. \"Aye, that would be Hegory.\"\nLarrion stared at the bird for moments, when he finally asked, \"Can we go upstairs? I want to introduce myself to your friend.\"\n\nNetiley shrugged, and opened the door to the upstairs area for him and Hegory.\"\nAs Larrion and Hegory sat down at a table for two, they stared eachother in the center of their eyes for quite some time. It was only a minute or so, but to Larrion, it felt like hours.\n\nLarrion broke the iceberg.\n\"So... what is it you do in the shop?\"\n\nThe chicken made a clucking noise.\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nLarrion placed his elbows on the table, and rolled his eyes.\n\"Do you have any hobbies?\"\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nFamily?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nJob?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\nAt this point, Larrion decided to talk about himself.\n\n\"Well, I am especially interested in alchemy. Aside from that, I run a small store.\"\n\n\"Cluck. Cluck cluck, cluck-- Cluck cluck cluck, cluck CLUCK!\"\nAt this point, Larrion was blushing. Never before had anyone shown such compassion, such sympathy, and such care for what Larrion went through everyday. He finally found someone who would listen to him.\nLarrion removed the goggles that rested on his eyes, and held Hegory's left wing in between his own two. Larrion bent down to kiss the top of his love interest's wing, and smiled. Hegory couldn't smile, but instead looked to the ceiling.\nThe very next day, no one could seem to find Hegory or Larrion. Any sign of the two ever being there in the first place had vanished. As everyone searched for them, little did they know that the two were already at the docks, planning their new lives.\nThe two decided to live out at sea on a house boat. For the next 15 years, the two lovers would survive off of fish and fried eggs. They met few people during their time at sea, and that's just how they liked it...\n-The End", ""),
        StaticBook("From Arcus", "Aneirin Leorora", "Kate. I honestly hate you.\n\nYou ruined my life once, and i'm not going to let you do it again.\n\nIf you need me, I won't be remaining in Sutica for a while.\n\nIf you need me, I shall be in the desert. It's the large boat at the\nend of Cloud Temple's docks, orange sails, opposite side of the Dwarve's boat.\n\nFuck you,\nArcus", ""),
        StaticBook("G. Harvest 1569", "Calliope_", "Dearest Len,\n\nMommy and Maln here! We both love you very, very much. More than the entire world. \n\nWe're going to write you every day, okay? \n\nHow was your birthday, sweet pea? Was it good? I hope so.\nIt's hard to believe you're four years old already! Our little girl is getting so big.\n\nThings have been pretty good for your Maln and me. We're working on making ourselves better. Your Maln has been very good to Mommy.\nI'm working on becoming a Cleric. Do you know what a Cleric is? It's a person who heals people. Ask Oli about them. Clerics and Druids are good friends.\n\nYour Maln is meditating every day to help himself get better.\nI want you to know that we want you home more than anything, but we also want you to be safe. \n\nSo, even if it makes you sad, being with Oliver is the best thing for you right now until Maln and me are better, okay?\nYou're such a good girl. Continue to be good for Oli. He loves you just as much as we do, and he only wants you to be happy and safe, too. \n\nWe'll visit you as soon as we're well enough to, alright?\nYour Maln left a poem and necklace for your birthday. Did you like them? \n\nHappy Late Birthday from me, sweet pea. I'm sorry for missing it. Mommy has been very busy working on making herself better. I promise I won't miss your next birthday.\nWe both love you so much! Never forget that. Everything we're doing, we're doing to try to make things better for you. \n\nUntil our next letter, little love. \n\n-Sending you lots of hugs and kisses!\nAvayla and Aeran", ""),
        StaticBook("Gastropoda", "Itiireae", "Gastropoda\nCornu aspersum\n\nPreface\n\nThe Cornu aspersum (likewise known in common as the garden snail) is an interesting species to observe. Through many observations and by devoting much time to studying the\nbehaviours of such creatures, an outlined journal containing has been constructed to highlight the interesting mannerisms of the Cornu aspersum.\nObservations I\n\nThe shell (or mantle) of the garden snail is typically of dark brown, brownish golden, or chestnut with yellow stripes, flecks, or streaks (characteristically interrupted brown bands) when it comes to shade and color.\nThe aperture is large and generally oblique, it's margin in adults is white and reflected.\n\nIn adults, the thin shells are of calcareous make, with four or five whorls.\n\nThe body (or visceral mass) is a soft, slimy substane of\nbrownish-grey. When inactive or threatened, the creature will retract itself into the shelll.\n\nWhen injured or badly irritated, the animal will produce a defensive mucus that may repel some enemies from tje base of the snail (or the foot).\nObservations II\n\nWhile viewing the various methods of reproduction in the garden snail, it may be determined that they are capable of self-replication. After one such veiwing, a particular specimen proved incapable of finding a mate. Thus\nit resorted to self fertilization which proved effective and resulted in approximatly eighty pearly white eggs nested within the moist soil of it's home.\n\n[!] The book seems to have gathered dust, unfinished and untouched.", ""),
        StaticBook("Glass Study", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "The purpose for this writing is in detailing various bits of information pertaining to glass for effective use in transmutation studies.\n   There are a few things I'll try to illustrate and describe here, such as: how it reacts to each of the-\n- senses, what it's made of, how it's made, average weight, shape, its breaking point, and melting point.\nSight:\n   Glass is a mostly translucent material. It gives off a slight sheen in the presence of direct light and can be quite easily seen through. It tends to be some what wavey depending on how exactly it was formed.\nHearing:\n   The sound glass can give off depends on what is being done to it. A simple flick of the substance tends to give off a sharp pinging sound, while completely breaking it can create a shattering burst of noise.\nSmell: \n   Glass doesn't often have a very distinct smell compared to more pungent substances I've handled in the past. The smells associated with it are moreso from the materials that have rubbed off on it rather than the glass itself.\nTaste:\n   Again, this sense is rather dull in regards to glass. Such a thing does not accumulate much of a taste due to the nature of its composition.\nFeeling:\n   The feeling of glass is often smooth or wavey in texture. It has no obvious ridges unless it is broken. In this case, those parts of the object are rather sharp and can cause cuts.\nMelting and Breaking Point: \n   The amount of force necessary to break glass tends to be dependant on how it was applied. I've recognized that it takes about fifty pounds of force over around fifteen square inches to break it. \n   As for the melting-\n- point, glass tends to be fully liquified at around 1400 to 1600 degrees celsius, depending on the type of glass.\nWeight and Shape:\n   Glass is rather light, as I've found that a circular piece of average thickness glass at three inches of diameter is less than a quarter of a pound. \n   As for the shape, glass can take on various forms with a skilled -\n- craftsman, but it generally takes on either a flat or spherical shape.\nWhat It's Made of, How It's Made:\n   Glass is most primarily made from liquified and molded sand. \n   In order to make glass, one must take a good amount of sand, and put it through the process of melting at around the previously mentioned melting point-\n- before slowly molding the liquid into the desired shape. Once cooled off properly, the sand will have taken on a new clear shape and substance: glass.\n*Upon flipping to the next page, you're greeted with a plethora of diagrams, sketchings, charts, illustrations, and equations. For pages upon pages, you see these images and lines of information, proving in more elaborate detail the previously mentioned -\n- points within the book. Alongside that, you see notes written to the side of these, giving short explanations and further points not previously mentioned.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Gray Wolf A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "As this is one book of many, I shall keep the introductions short. This book was made for the purpose of understanding the gray wolf anatomy in conjuration.\n   The types of organ systems that will be covered in this book include: nervous system,\nrespiratory system, skin, cardiovascular system, musculoskeletal system, digestive system, and urinary system.\n*Here you see a very intricate and detailed sketching of a gray wolf's shape being filled in with various strings and cords connecting into a central spinal location until it finally connects with a brain. It appears to be the nervous system.*\nNervous System: \n   The nervous system is made up entirely out of the animal's nerves, spinal cord, as well as the brain. \n   This part of the animal's system is there for the purpose of directing the rest of the body in its daily functions. It includes\nthe animal's instincts, the creature's mind, and all of the feelings that go along with it: including pain.\n   As for the gray wolf, there isn't a lot different about it as far as structure of the nervous system and how it performs its tasks.\n*Upon flipping to the next page, you are greeted with yet another intricately detailed sketching of a gray wolf. Instead of a nervous system, you see the lungs connected through the throat to the mouth and nose. It's the respiratory system.*\nRespiratory System:\n   Organs within this system include the lungs connected with the rest of the body to support blood with oxygen, as well as all the ways it connects with the mouth and nose to breathe.\n   The purpose of the respiratory system is\nin breathing the air around the animal to then supply the body with oxygen so that it may live.\n   As for the gray wolf, it works like any land-based animal would.\n*On the next page there appears to be various sketches in the same intricate detail as before. They seem to show various different layers of skin and what they look like. It's the skin of a gray wolf.*\nSkin:\n   Skin itself is a large enough complex to be warranted as its own system. Things that are inside involve the outer layer that everyone knows, and the inner layers including connective tissues, fats, and blood vessels.\n   The purpose of skin\nis solely for protection of the inner parts of the body from the external environment.    A gray wolf's skin is covered in a thick gray-white coat that not only helps protect the animal, but also adds an abundance of warmth.\n*Following the pattern, another detailed sketching appears upon this page. It shows a vast network of veins and arteries connected with the heart of the gray wolf. It's the cardiovascular system.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   This system involves the expansive network of veins, arteries, and the heart.\n   Blood is pumped through the body as a result of this system, giving nutrients to the entire creature so that it may live.\n   Gray wolves are\nsimilar to many other animals in that they have only one heart and it functions just the same.\n*Once again, a sketch is shown. Upon it you can see various different layers in how the muscles and bones are positioned within the body of a gray wolf. It's the musculoskeletal system.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   Within this system is all of the bones and muscles that give the creature shape and structure. These include joints, ligaments, tendons, and otherwise.\n   The bones and muscles of the body serve the creature by giving it not\nonly structure and shape, but also movement and strength. Via the nervous system, the creature controls its muscles and how they move, allowing it daily function.\n   A gray wolf is quadripedal in structure, and has fairly powerful jaws for a creature of\nits size. Otherwise, this system works just as you'd imagine.\n*The fully realized and detailed image of a gray wolf's mouth, esophagus, stomach, and the like is shown. It appears to be a detailed sketch of the digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   There are quite a few parts to this system. These parts include: the mouth, the esophagus, the stomach, the large and small intestines, the rectum, the liver, the gallbladder, and the pancreas.\n   To put simply, this system is in\nplace for the purpose of extracting nutrients from food and excreting wastes from the body.\n   Gray wolves are entirely carnivorous, meaning that their bodies will only prefer meat based diets.\n*A bit less detailed from what was shown previously, but you can tell that there are a few organs sketched into the frame of the gray wolf. It includes what looks like kidneys, and the bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   Connected closely with the cardiovascular system, the urinary system includes kidneys, the bladder, the urethra, and all things inbetween.\n   Due to being so closely linked with the cardiovascular system, this system's job is in\nseparating wastes from the blood stream.\n   Otherwise, the gray wolf doesn't function very uniquely from other organisms in this regard.\nSide Notes:\n- Highly pack-oriented, gray wolves are vicious hunters, and should never be underestimated and always be admired.\n- Many gray wolves were harmed in the making of this book. Sorry again.\nList of Systems:\n- Nervous\n- Respiratory\n- Skin\n- Cardiovascular\n- Musculoskeletal\n- Digestive\n- Urinary\n*Upon getting to the end of the book, you see that all of the sketchings from all throughout the book have been downsized and placed next to each other for the last few pages, for quick reference.*t", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide", "Cecila Narn'wynn", "-=+=-\nAlchemic Ingredient\nLocations: \n\nCrimson Vase\nFound in Woodlands\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nDrake's Tail\nFound in Savana's\n((MC Block: Shrub))\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nFound in Swapms\n((MC Block: Grass, sometimes lily pads\n\nBlood Lotus\nFound in Woodlands, Plains, and Savana's\n((MC Block: Grass // Shrubs in Savana's))\nFlametongue Root\nFound in Woodlands, and Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\n~End of Fire Symboles~\nMandragora\nFound in Swamps\n((MC Block: Lily Pads))\n\nSerpent's Stalk\nFound in Woodlands\n((MC Block: Sugarcane))\n\nFrost Vine\nFound in Snowy Regions, Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\nBlissfoil\nFound in Woodlands, Plains\n((NO MC Block: Blue Orchard))\n\nAthin\nFound in Snowy Icelands\n((MC Block: Ice))\n\n~End of Water Symboles~\nTippen's Root\nFound in Woodlands, Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nAlbaster Leaf\nFound in Woodlands, Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nSaffvil\nFound in Swamps\n((MC Block: Grass))\nClutcher's Straw\nFound in Savana's\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nMetzli's Tangle\nFound in Jungles\n((MC Block: Grass or Vines))\n\n~End of Earth Symboles~\nLarihei's Fingers\nFound in Snowy Areas, Mountains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nElf's Hair Vine\nFound in Snowy Areas, Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\n\nCrouching Feather\nFound in Woodlands, Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\nHalfling's Grass\nFound in Woodlands, Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\n~End of Air Symboles~", ""),
        StaticBook("Happy Krugsmas", "Nemir", "Dear Daniel,\n\nYou are the sun to my world.  You are my torch in the night.  You are the color in my life.  With you, you bring a smile to my face, a warmth in my heart, and comfort and love to my soul.  You are my love.\nWith you, I feel as if we can overcome anything that is thrown at us.\n\nI love you and Happy Krugsmas.  I hope you enjoy your gifts, my beloved.\n\n- Nemir", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 2", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 2\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun\nMalin's Heart\nA white flower that grows in plains and forests.\nEffects: Chewing numbs the whole body for a few minutes.\nOverdose: Prolonged numbness.\nNotes: A bit harder to find than blissfoil.\nMandragora\nA parsnip shaped herb that grows in swamps and wetlands.\nEffects: Revitalization and regenerative properties make the plant valuable, but the spores it releases in season cause hallucinations.\nOverdose: Can cause growths. The hallucinogenic spores often cause choking and can be fatal.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol, often used in healing potions.\nNotes: Harvest 2 weeks after maturity to avoid spores.\nNight Sap\nA golden sap that drips from deformed oak trees.\nEffects: Causes a sense of calm, safety, and happiness, along with tiredness. It usually makes for about 5 hours of sleep. After waking, though, it brings splitting headaches\nand paralysis for as much time as the sleep.\nOverdose: Longer lasting effects.\nNotes: Highly addictive.\nSaffvil\nA sickly green grass that grows in swamps near dead things.\nEffects: Nausea and blood clotting\nOverdose: Death\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate fire symbol.\nSagedust\nPollen from the Alabaster plant.\nEffects: Increased metabolism and speed, along with heightened senses and a rapid heart rate.\nOverdose: Possible heart attack.\nNotes: Incredibly difficult to harvest.\nSerpent's Stalk\nA long, reed like emerald stalk that grows in forests near or in water.\nEffects: Cooling effect when applied with water, may cause rashes.\nOverdose: Mild hypothermia.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol. Typically used in antidotes, calming, and healing potions.\nNotes: Poisonous to bugs.\nShade Leaf\nA short, small plant with plain leaves, yellow flowers, and silvery veins that is commongly found anwhere there is grass and shade.\nEffects: Calming, stress releaving, bloodshot eyes, increased appetite.\nOverdose: Hallucinations\nNotes: Grows in large quantities, simmilar to normal weeds. Makes a popping noise when exposed to rain.\nSwamp Blossom\nA purple green flower with a short, thick stem, found in the branches of swamp trees.\nEffects: Nectar is like honey, and the flower is nutritious, though consuming raw can gum up the throat.\nOverdose: Smelly breath and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate air symbol, usually used in speed potions.\nTippen's Root\nPurple flowers with a dark yellow speckled root that grow near fallen trees in dense forests.\nEffects: Stops bleeding almost instantly, but stinks to the seven hells.\nOverdose: Blood clots, and the dangers of blood clots.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate earth symbol, commonly used in strength and healing potions.\nNotes: Really, seriously stinks. Really. Make sure you're prepared for the stink.\nYarrow\nA white to pink flowered plant that grows in grasslands and forests.\nEffects: Can reduce inflammation and blood pressure, as well as intensify the medicinal effects of other herbs.\nOverdose: Dizziness and fainting due to\nlow blood pressure.\nZawabate\nA plant with a tall stalk and yellow-green curled petals that grows in a desert oasis in water.\nEffects: Out of body experiences, hallucinations, pain numbing.\nOverdose: Can destroy a person's mind.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate water symbol, used in numbing and healing potions.\nNotes: Nectar is the medicinal part of the plant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Honey Bee A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "As an introduction, the book is written with the purpose of studying the anatomy of your average honey bee for use in conjuration.\n   In this book, I shall be covering the honey bee's anatomy in three sections: the head, thorax, and the abdomen.\n*Upon flipping onward, you're greeted by several incredibly detailed sketchings of the honey bee's head from various angles and even the structures there within.*\nThe Head:\n   This part of the honey bee consists of the vertex, gena, ocelli, antenna, compound eyes, feelers, and proboscis.\n   The purpose of the head is fairly self evident. Its purpose is to house the brain, allow for various functions such as -\n- feeding and sensing the environment.\n*The next page shows sketchings much like before, except they display the mid-section of the bee, its thorax. They show from various angles and the structures there within just as before.*\nThorax:\n   The various structures within this system are the six legs, its wings, and many of the bee's organs.\n   The purpose of it involves transportation via the wings or legs, which collect pollen. Otherwise, there are the organs within, -\n- which were detailed in the sketching.\n*This next page contains a similar set of sketchings as the previous two, demonstrating the various structures and organs within the abdomen of a honey bee.*\nAbdomen:\n   The abdomen is where the stinger and the sternum are. More interestingly for this study, where its venom lies.\n   The purpose of the abdomen in a honey bee is in excreting its wastes as well as using its stinger to kill threats.\nUnfortunately for the honey bee, its stinger is often lost when trying to sting a much larger target, resulting in its death shortly after.\nSide Notes:\n-Honey bees are generally less aggressive than their wasp friends, whom bite instead of sting.\n-Many bees died.\n-Sorry. Sort of.\n*All of the sketches previously seen throughout the book are miniature and set side by side throughout the last pages of the book, clearly in place for comparison purposes.*", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Druii", "Riv'su Des'Nox", "\"A druid is a child of the Aspects... We have a sworn duty to keep the balance and defend nature. With the Aspects as our 'parents' our fellow druii are our brothers and sisters... It is also not something that is chosen lightly... to be a druid is a life\nchoice and should be taken seriously.\"\n- Lynx Druid Tailesin one of the three archdruii of the Mother grove.\n\"What it means to be a druid depends on you and you alone. Here in Naelurir, druids are priests. Our mandate is to preserve wood elven teachings, and spread and maintain the worship of the Aspects in our nation so the wilds are protected by an entire race\nshould you go to another circle, their goal will be different but this is ours.\"\n\n- Artimec. The Archdruid of el'Naelurir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v3", "Bishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume III: The Second Age of Kings\nThe Second Age of Kings\n1422-1431\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nKings from the Houses of Horen, Carrion, Hightower, Elendil, Flay-Silverblade\nAlso known as: The Fractured Era, the Age of Five Kings, the Second Unrest, the First Dark Ages, the\nFirst Papal Intercession\n\nFollowing Salvus's betrayal and the disbanding of the empire, High Pontiff Goddard I claimed the dissolution of the empire had freed his territories from royal fealty, as they had been granted autonomy from direct\nrule when William took the throne. He claimed the Salvian-affiliated territory of Emperor's Forest (later formalized as the County of Kvaz in the second empire), and the Prince-Archbishopric of Savoie (composed of the County of Norfolk, Barony of\nAldersberg, Viscounty of Bar, and other minor territories) as independent of the Orenian crown. In a matter of months, the Dukes Charles Greymane of Corpathia and Siegmund Carrion of Raev also swore under the High Pontiff, who took the title Apostolic\nKing and subbed his realm the Holy Kingdom of Savoie. \n\nIn the east, the newly seceded Flay-Silverblade island Kingdom of Galahar was not as successful, and it dwindled in relevance as it faced government inefficiency, brutality, and mass emigration\nresulting from its disconnect with the Orenian mainland. It was soon forced to wild banditry in order to fund its expenditures. During this period, the Kings of Savoie, Adunia, and Oren took protectorate status under the Grand-King Thorin of the dwarven\nGrand Kingdom of Urguan in an effort to try and protect their borders from incursions by one another and the dwarven state. Despites this, Galahar continued its heavy raids until the Duke Siegmund Carrion brought the bandit-state under his command.\nThe Savoyard state was around this time then abdicated to Siegmund Carrion, who had been named heir apparent to the pontiff of Carrion blood, and the pontiff returned to matters of the faith.\n\nWhen the Grand-King of Urguan died, the human states were\nreleased from their protectorate status and were quickly at odds with one another. Renatus readied for war against Savoie's growing state, which had recently negotiated the absorption of Salvus and hte pagan nation of Adunia into its borders. The King of\nSavoie redubbed his state the Kingdom of Ruska, in reference to the culture of his people, the Raevirs.\n\nThreatened by the growth in land and power of Savoie, the King William III of Oren declared High Pontiff Goddard I excommunicated (citing the\ncaesareopapist reign of Horen V as legal precedent for state over church supremacy) in an effort to diminish the authority of the kingdom, and brought the nations of Ruska and Oren to the brink of war.\n\nThe Lord High Steward of Oren, Edward\nWinter II, met in secret with Goddard I, and the two negotirated terms contingent upon Edward's deposition of William and his gathering the support of other leading advisors and nobles. Goddard I and Edward II led a peaceful exchange of power from William\nIII to his cousin, Lord High Treasurer Silus I, who agreed to back the Ruskan-Winter agreement. Silus quickly assumed the throne and appointed countless Ruskan nobility in court positions. In thanks for his services, Edward was created King of Herendul,\nand given control of his former liege's, Duke Codrik Green of Hanseti, territories as his kingdom. Herendul, the Crownlands of Oren (now renamed Renatus), Ruska, and the weakened state of Salvus then combined into a loose confederacy governed by a\nconstitutional monarchy. King Silus then stepped down and abdicated to Otto Carrion, resulting in an imbalance of of the constitutional monarchy that ensured the election of Siegmund Carrion as Emperor of the Second Empire of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v4", "Bishop Cordal", "The History of Humanity from Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume IV: The Second Empire\nThe Second Empire\n1431-1447\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion\nAlso known as: The Time of Crows, the Imperium Secundus\n\nThe Carrions emerged from the Second Age of Kings in command of humanity, and did so\nwithout interruption for several years. Siegmund's rule began with the systematic execution and seizure of property by Otto and Tuv Carrion from all of the first empire nobles that remained loyal to House Horen, wiping the slate clean for a new\nRaevir-dominated nobility. His reign was a quiet one, and primarily foccused on rebuilding a unified state after the Second Age of Kings. There was a short rebellion by Empress-claimant Sophia Horen, who was backed by several disenfranchised nobles of the\nFirst Empire, but it fell into disorder after a year. \n\nAnother rebellion followed, led by descendants of Eze'kiel Tarus, the Teutonic Order, and dwarves who challenged the Carrion's right-to-throne in open rebellion.\nSeveral prominent families of the First Empire also joined Horen and Tarus. The House Stafyre was almost pushed into joining when then-High Pontiff, who styled himself High Ecclesiarch Radomir I, nearly flogged a Stafyr for defending a heretic. However,\nthe Stafyrs were persuaded to back the empire, and their castle was used to garrison Orenian troops bolstered by the Church's Order of Saint Lucien in a victorious defense against the rebel coalition.\n\nIt was not too many years later that the\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion died of age, and in his will dissolved the second empire into its constituent states of the Kingdom of Oren and the Kingdom of Herendul.", ""),
        StaticBook("Humble Petition", "Ceriwyn de Savoie", "The Humble Petition And Advice\n-------------------Written to his Lordship of Aldersburg_________\n___________________A Guide For The Re-Organization of The Fuedal Levies And Standing Sortie\n___________________The Art Of War\nIntroduction___________________________Standing armies are dangerous, evidence can be found in Petrus. Chivay would still be in power now if it used fuedal levies. Also, it is cheaper to mantain and we can have a more numerous army.\nThe Sergeants_____________________________The sergeants are a small group of professional, middle class spearmen. This will be very small in number, and these will be the few professional troops we have.\nMilitiamen______________________________Miltiamen are semi-professional troops that make up the garrisons of the county's forces. They are not full-time soldiers and train in their spare time. They act as full-time soldiers in times of desperation.\nMost of the guard will be changed to miltiamen. They are numerous but not too well-paid, equipped, or trained because they do it in their spare time. Miltiamen buy their own equipment and therefore rich, upper class mitliamen will be much better off.\nLevies_____________Levies are ordinary people hastily rallied in times of war. They are poorly trained, but will be very numerous and make up most of the army. They will be given basic equipment and are at their liberty to equip themselves better.\nMercinaries_________Mercinaries will be about as numerous as the sergeants. They come in many types.\n\nRaevir Soldaty-The flat terrian of the east produces excellent cavalry and spearmen (who counter the enemy's cavalry).\nPetrusian Crossbowmen________The city of Petrus produces excellent crossbowmen. These will help our cause.\n\nElven Longbowmen-As long as they are no heathens, we can accept longbowmen of the Elves.\nKnights and Squires____________Knights and squires act as the super heavy cavalry and heavy infantry. They can also act as junior officers and knights as senior ones. They are about as numerous as the sergeants.\nPercentages________50% Levies\n20% Militia\n10% Sergeants\n10% Mercinaries\n10% Knights and Squires.\nOrganization________ (( http://imgur.com/9afs2oZ ))\n\n*A diagram of the Organization is here*\nClass System And Troops_____________\n                              Marshal of Aldersburg-knight   or aristocrat\n\nSenior Knight-Knight\n\nSenior Squire-Gentry \n\nSquires-Gentry\nSergeants-Middle Class\n\nLevies-Peasants\n\nJunior Knights-Knights and upper gentry in times of war.\n\nMiltia Captain-Gentry\n\nMiltia Lieutenant-Middle Class\nMiltiamen-Lower and Middle Classes\n\nTactics_____________                             Formations\n\nInfantry____________\n                             Infantry must be firmly grouped together in dense formation in order\nto resist cavalry attacks. \n\nTherefore, in the case of a cavalry attack, the missle infantry are to be placed behind the main infantry formation. The men will form three ranks, with the sergeant spearmen in front\nThen the levied spearmen, with everyone else in the third rank. \n\n______Sergeants\n_________Levies\n______Everyone else\n_Officers\n\nIn the case of infantry attack, the missle infantry\nshould be grouped in front, in a single rank, in front of the infantry. (when the melee clash begins they withdraw in good order to the rear)\n\n_______Swordsman\n_________Levies\n____________Militia and Sergeants\nIn the event of attacking an enemy with a high proportion of missle troops, All haste must be given to ensure great speed in forming up. A metre's space should be given to each soldier and all should be formed in a single rank. They should advance with\ngreat haste.\n\nCavalry Tactics_____\n\nIn the event of attacking enemy infantry, there are two options. The first is to form loosely up, in a few loose ranks. THen to harass and skirmish at the infantry.\nThe second, and this is if they are hasty levies or have poor morale, or are at breaking point, is to charge. Form a wedge, four deep, and charge.\n\nIn the event of fighting a force largly made up of missle infantry, just charge and run the\nblackguards down.\n\nIn the case attacking another cavalry force, if it is missle or light type than it should be ambushed, or met with other skirmisher cavalry. \n\nIf it is a heavy cavalry force, it is usually best to\nuse your cavalry to lure them into your spearmen, and then charge with both horse and foot.\n\n              _\n            _   _\n         _    _    _\nThe wedge formation, officers in front.\nThe first basic rule of cavalry is not to attack disciplined, formed, ready infantry, but to attack them in the rear, or attack lightly armed infantry.\nStrategy____________Sieges____\nSwordsman are to be the folorn hope of a siege. They are to attack the breech first. Remember, however, it is always better to starve the enemy out than to charge.\nMissle troops can act as covering troops, advancing first and shooting men on the battlements. \n\nHow To adress Troops As an Officer\n\nTroops should adress you loyally, and adress you by rank, not by name.\nFurthermore, you must not spol them. It is good for troops to be treated well on first occassion, and then, whent hey have come to love their officers, discipline should shake in. You must be firm, no exceptions are to be given.\nIn turn, you must adress your men religously, firmly and you must be formal and look every inch the soldier.\n\nOn campaign___________Salted food is preffered. If mobility is key, then foraging from the enemy or\nfrom local villages is preferable. However, if this is not the case, and you are fighting a more defensive campaign, a heavy baggage train is preffered.", ""),
        StaticBook("I love you", "Avayla", "I don't know if you'll ever notice this little book amongst your odd collection of tomes. However, if you do, and you take the time to read it, then I thank you.\nToday is the fourth of The Amber Cold. I have just gotten my first home in this new land, and I have a beautiful ocean view. Sutica is a beautiful place. Very neat and clean. The people I've met so far are very kind. I think I will like it here.\nFor most people, today would be a great day, I think. For me, though, it's clouded by the fact that we are no longer together. \n\nI know in my mind that this is the right thing. You need your time and space. You need to sort things out.\nWhen we first got to know each other, you were broken. I said I would fix you. I'd like to think that's what I've done in some small way. That I've helped you come to be who you are now. \n\nEither way, I look at how strong you are, and I am proud of you.\nI've always been proud of you, though. I hope you know that.\n\nDo you remember the first time I told you I was proud of you?\n\nIt was when you were weaning off the fairy ring, and you were doing it all on your own.\nYou were afraid and in pain. You felt completely helpless. You had lost the most important thing in the world to you. Everyone you ever loved seemed to cast you aside. \n\nYet, you stood strong and pushed through it. I am still proud of you.\nEvery step of the way, through all the bad, I've been proud of you. I always will be. \n\nI love you.\n\nI miss you.\nI promised you long ago that I would never abandon you, regardless of any mistakes you might possibly make. I meant that. \n\nYou will always have my support.\nWhile it hurts to admit, I know that us splitting up isn't you abandonig me. We'll always have each other in some way. We're bound together for life through Len and through the memories we've made together.\nNo matter what, you'll always be the love of my life. \n\nYou have always been the perfect man for me, and no one else could ever compare to you. \n\nI never said these things enough when we were together.\nYou're a good person, Aeran. Even if you make mistakes sometimes, you're the best man I've ever known. \n\nYou've changed my entire life for the better.\nWhen we met, I was a scared little girl. Now, I'm a strong woman, and despite having the worst pain I've ever known in my heart, I know that I can stay strong and hold my head up proud, because I don't hate myself anymore thanks to you.\nYou've taught me what it means to live and love. You've shown me that I can stand up for myself. You given me so much good and joy and love and I can never thank you enough.\nI love you.\nThe only time I ever said my vow to you was when you were angry. So, I am going to write it down for you the best I can now.\n\nForgive me. It's been nine years. It may not be perfect, but I still hold it true, and I always will.\nYou are the one that brings music into my heart. Before you, there were no words. There was only a tune with no lyrics. No meaning. No real joy. Then, you came into my life.\nThe sun became warmth instead of only a light. \n\nThe moon was beautiful, and I saw the stars as more than just specks of nothingness for the first time.\nI can feel my heart beating out of my chest when I'm with you.\n\nYou are the love of my life, and I am your lute girl. \n\nForever your lute girl, I shall be.\nWhenever you need me, I will be there for you.\nShould you ever find yourself in need of a song, a laugh, a hug, a kiss, someone to yell at, even -- find me. \n\nI'm here for you. \n\nYou never have to be alone. I will never abandon you.\nI love you.\n\n\n\n- Lute Girl\n\n\n\n\n\n4th of The Amber Cold, 1571", ""),
        StaticBook("I Love You More", "Kira Winterleaf", "I love you more than cookies.\nThan fresh vanilla cake.\nAnd chocolate frosting,\nand running so far it's exhausting,\nand swimming in a lake.\nI love you more than the library,\nAnd eating ripe cherries.\nI love you more than writing\npoems.\nThan my future Druid totem. \nI love you more than drawing art.\nThen riding in bouncy carts.\nI love you more than butter on toast.\nAnd though I like pies of any size,\nI love you the most.", ""),
        StaticBook("Infomercial", "Dharok", "Lightning Evocation\nTeachers:\nIllion - Easy\nAlfred - Moderate\n(Find near Degenerates).\nOOC: Usernames are _suitandtie_ and Jentos\nScorching Flesh\nBase: AV\nSerpant's Stalk\nMandagora\nCrimson Vase\nFlametongue Root\n+ Drake's Tale for\nPyromaniac.\nPyromaniac = Weaker Alchemist's Fire, ignites on air contact\nAscended Notes:\n>Great Creator admist Nothignness of Reality\n>Used dust and cosmos to create Aenguls and Daemons\n>Realm of mortals was created\n>Creator vanished, archaengul and others angry\n>Arch Aengul stopped interfering with mortals\n>Mortals begin to die and go to soulstream, confuses aenguls\n>Aenguls not familiar with death\n>Soulstream: A realm in between the realm of the divine and mortals\n>Dead souls wandered aimlessly in the soulstream\n>AAerial, archaengul, made the sou\nlstream a good place, cities of gold. Place for souls to rest in peace.\n>Robed man taveled throughout the mortal realm gifting mortals, becoming their friend\n>Robed man was born in the heated metal of volcanoes\n>Krug doesn't accept robed man's gif\nts and assaults him to figure out his identity\n>Robed man erupts into flames during fight with krug, revealing himself as the arch daemon ibless.\n>Krug's messengers send word to the 3 other nations about iblees and they disagreed until seeing Krug's\ndisfigured body. They declared war against Ibless\n>Corpses and undead rose from the dead and fought in a war with mortals\n>Aeriel and her kin showed up to help the mortals when they nearly lost the war to help fight iblees and the undead.\n>Took all aenguls to defeat archdaemon and just before he was defeated, he placed a curse on Malin, Urguan, Krug, and the human guy that I forgot the name of, and all of their kin.\n>The four nations found aegis, a place to call home, Aeriel helped weaken\nthe curses on mortals, though she could not completely remove it.\nWraith:\nName: Aldred\nMagics: Lightning Evocation though he likely knows others.\nDescription: Very old Highlander with a small white beard dressed in black robes. The robes cover most of his head, leaving his face revealed. He has blue eyes and pale skin\nAscended Note\nSecond invasion\n>World at peace, people forget about war\n>Arcdaemon broke barrier between nether and mortal plane during time of peace and attacked\\\n>Aeriel notices this and mocks iblees by giving people ascended powers\n>Ascended and Aeriel vs Undead and iblees\n>Ascended grew in numbers\n>Created soulstream rift\n>All ascended gone, though some heald onto their faith led by aeriel\n>Ascended weakned, undead began to destroy civilization\n>Miasma - Trademark gas of undead territory\n>Undead open rifts leading to the nether\n>Charged through undead portal\n>Only those in nether klnow what happened\n>When they left, darkness faded\n>Descendants won the war and sealed iblees\n>Colonized on Asulon\nI don't understand, even after my years of contemplation, why I receive hostility from others after I show kindness and tranquillity towards them.\nAscended Lecture 3\n\n\n*most of this page, aside from the heading, is ripped out.\n*This page too*\n*And this one*\nStunt Potion\nBase: Aqua Vitae\nBlood Lotus\nFlametounge Root\nGoblin's Ivy\nClutcher's Straw", ""),
        StaticBook("Ingredients List", "Ketiley the Vixen", "Alchemical list of\nIngredients:\n\nMandragora\nSerpent's Stalk\nFrost Vine\nBlissfoil\nAthin\nCrimson Vase\nDrake's Tail\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nBlood Lotus\nFlametongue's Root\nLarihei's Fingers\nElf's Hair Vine\nCrouching Feather\nHalfling's Grass\nTippen's Roots\nAlabaster Leaf\nSaffvil\nClutcher's Straw\nMetzli's Tangle\nGoblin's Ivy", ""),
        StaticBook("Inspiration", "Aebek", "This is a banana,\nBanana is yellow,\nYellow is a happy color,\nI believe in you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Iron and Steel", "Gladuos", "In the following book we will be exploring the physical and magical traits of iron or steel, how it may react to the mundane senses, how it's made, weight, shape, hardness, melting point, and a magical understanding.\nIron or steel generally takes on a white-ish grey coloration that may give off a dim shine if smithed in the correct manner. \n   It will often give off clanging and dinging noises as it is used in whatever way it may. Sounds can occasionally\nreverberate throughout the material. \n   Iron, and especially steel, are incredibly tough materials. They are often used during combat or for specially tough constructions if necessary. Compared to stone or lesser materials, iron/steel\nis far more valuable and strong. Steel has a higher coal content compared to iron, and as thus is even more tough.\nMetallic iron or steel is usually created through treating the ore variant through intense blast furnacing and introducing coals to improve quality of the material. The heat of these furnaces usually take on a heat of about 2000 degrees Celsius.\nThe difference between iron and steel is that steel has a higher content of coal added during this process to give an even tougher finish. This is removed from the furnace and cooled in a slow, meticulous process of reheating, cooling, tempering and so-\n- on.\n\n   Steel or iron are metallic materials and thus are often fairly dense, heavy materials, even comparative to earthen minerals.\nThe average shape of steel or iron varies dramatically depending on how it was formed. In its ore variant, it is normally in the shape of any other rock. However, it can be formed into the metallic variant that takes on a shape depending on the -\n- smith's choice and skill.\n\n   Once again, steel or iron are generally very strong materials. This can be often shown when making fine weapons or armors, as making purely metallic constructions may simply be too costly.\nThe melting point of steel and iron is in the range between 1370 and 1550 degrees Celsius. The lower portions of this range are attributed to steel, while the higher is closer to iron's melting point.\nThe magical signature of iron and steel isn't too terrible. It may not be comparable to carbarum or mage gold in conductivity of magical forces, but it may be slightly less resistant than some of the lesser valuable materials in the mortal planes.\n*When reaching these final pages, the reader would be shown a large amount of diagrams, sketches, illustrations, charts, and equations about the various properties of iron and steel. For pages and pages, these continue, being accompanied by various lines-\n- of information attempting to support many of the previous statements of the book. There are also some nuanced details of the materials less relevant than the information already given.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ivlisar Trials", "Ivlisar Sagehand", "I aided Rowan Sagehand while they were drunk.\n\nI guided and protected Mal'rean while he was being attacked by ghouls. I dispatched the ghouls and took care of his wounds and I brought him to the nearest city.\nI helped Alenthir fell some trees to help him gain some money. I refused to take any money from him as I wasn't helping him for money.\n\nI helped Ardnea in her time of need as she was being attacked by bandits. I sprung into action and I managed to fi\noff the bandit.\n\nI helped Martyn Norringtan with his broken jaw. I made sure that he was fine before sending him away.", ""),
        StaticBook("jehan's poem", "Jehan", "rosus ar red\nvailetes ar blu\nmy nem iz jehan\nand i laik yu", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Aeran", "I think it's been 5 Elven weeks since I was kicked out of the Druids, for the last time. And I think I feel worse.\n\nI guess it's because I've consistently destroyed all relationships I've had with anyone, whether that be 'intentional' (Me driving people\naway when they try to help me) or accidental (me being a regular piece of shit). Because that, I have no support. If most other people went through a trouble like this, they would have friends and family and be able to accept the help that is offered.\nBut I'm not like that, I guess. I have a large family, I thought I had more than a few friends, but as each day passes and I sit alone, crying or angry, I am doubting that.\n\nBut, like I said, that's my fault, for how I act and react. So I suppose I can't\ncomplain.\n\nBut, because of that, I need somewhere to put my thoughts, and something to maybe break up the monotony of every single day. So I will keep a journal. So, I guess this is entry 1.\n16th of The Grand Harvest, 1517\n\nI guess that introduction was like an entry, but I'll say this is the first semi-standard one.\n\nIt seems silly to care so much about the order of a fucking diary, but I guess it's better than not\ncaring about anything.\n\nI don't know how much longer I can stand this. Just sitting, praying that someone will walk up to me and say 'Hey, Aeran, are you ok?' so I can maybe try to ellude to all the trouble I am actually going through.\nBecause I think that's something that's missing; I don't think anybody truly understands how I am feeling. I am being dramatic, I know, but I think I'm a bit justified. My life is over.\n\nWow, what a juvenile thing to say.\n\nWhat I mean by that is\nmy personality, my being, is a piece of shit. The way I think, the way I treat others, the things I believe in, are absolutely awful. But you can't really change that, can you? I can't. So, there is no solution.\n\nI guess one. But maybe a bit too dark for\nthis. But yeah, offing myself is on my mind often.\n\nThere was one incident I wanted to write about; I was at a Moot, a while ago. I shouldn't have been, I didn't belong, and it just made me more upset about everything, but I couldn't resist. I thought\nAeras would say something about me, because I had talked to him, but... After 4 people telling me that they were going to try to get me attuned, or try to make me a Dedicant again, I lost my hope for that. But that's my fault; I was always vague and quiet\nwhen anyone tried to help.\n\nI digress. I was at the Moot, and I saw my mother. I hadn't seen her for a long time, since way before we even left Athera, since just after she was kidnapped by Harbringers.\n\nAnd, I didn't make any\neffort to try to communicate with her. I didn't want to; I am just a dissapointment, and I need to dissociate myself from her.\n\nBut she never once even showed that she saw me, through the whole long Moot. And... I guess that upsets me, even though I think\nit's better if she has nothing to do with me.\n\nI guess I want to be the one to make that decision, not to just be... Not even ignored, I guess, just not acknowledged.\n\nThat makes me really sad.\n17 of Sun's Smile, 1517\n\nI still am hopeful, everytime I wake up, that today will be the day someone comes to me and says 'Aeran, I see you are going through a hard time, and I want you to know I am there for you.'\n\nBut I am starting to think that won't\nhappen. At this moment, I am certain it won't. But in an hour I'll be certain it will. Weird.\n\nI feel like I should talk to Raine. Lillith always wanted grand children, and she is Lillith's best chance for that.\n\nBut I guess the 'Lillith True Blood'\nbloodline is going to die for me.\n\nI'm sorry about that. It was never going to happen. I shouldn't have led her on with hope that it would. That's my fault.\n\nI find myself crying a lot more, recently. I know that sounds just... Silly, but I\ndon't think I cried for 100 years. And now I started. I can't help it. I don't want to feel like this.\n\nI feel like I should try for a cry for help, something. Go talk to someone. But I can't. I guess I'm not like that.\n\nOne last cry for help before\nit's over.\n\nBut that won't happen. \n\nSorry.\n3rd Entry\n\nI lost track of time long ago, and can't stand asking people for the date anymore.\n\nIt's weird. I used to be... Friendly. Or atleast, I could talk to people easily. I didn't feel nervous meeting a new person, or trying to impress a\ngirl.\n\nBut now? I can't even see someone without getting a sinking feeling in my stomach, a lump in my throat. Almost always I will just turn away and avoid anyone. Which is very counter- productive, because I think that the only thing that is going to\n'save' me is someone else hleping me.\n\nBut that's silly. I shouldn't rely on anyone else. That's not fair to anyone else. I have to deal with my own shit. Everyone else has issues they deal with, and they are all certainly more important than me.\nI also remembered something; Last conversation I probably will ever have with my mother was her telling me she had never been more disappointed in me.\n\nThat makes me sad.\n\nI wish there was a way out of this. I wish I could somehow snap\nmy fingers and it would all be good. But that's never going to happen. So I have no good solution. 1 solution I know is bad, but I will probably end up doing.\n\nI don't know.\n4th Entry I think\n\nI think it would be really easy to blame others for my problems. You said you would be there for me, you aren't. You convinced me it was worth troopin' through, but it's not.\n\nBut I don't think that's good. I don't think it's\nvery truthful, or very... I don't know the world, but something. I can't blame others. It's my fault, 100%. It's my burden to bare, nobody elses.\n\nI guess that's sorta a repeat of what I've said before.\n\nI'm thinking some very stupid things lately,\nand worry that I'm going to act on some of them. \n\nAlso, to add onto that first thing I said, it's sometimes hard to keep in mind that the world isn't based off me. If I'm feeling bad, the skies aren't going to rain for 10 days straight. Nothing is\nweeping for me, nothing is going to break because of my lack of presence. People have completely independent lifes from mine. Infact, everyone does. I am alone in this. \nAnd I guess, over the long term, that's better. Short term it fucking sucks, but I\ndon't want to cause strife to anyone.\n\nI guess I have a bit of a thing for martyrdom, or theatrics. I want to be selfless, making decisions based off of how they will effect those around me. But I think I am a very selfish guy, even with that. I guess\nyou just have to add that to the 'end it' list.\n\nAgain, sorry.\nThe Next Entry\n\nI fucked up. I said that I could use someone to help support me, and that opportunity arose.\n\nBut I fucked up. I just told them to forget about me. Due to my fucked up sense of heroism or something. Fuck.\nI can't bring myself to write more, I guess. I fucked up, and I think that's part of the last straw; I thought that I could get help, if someone offered, and then when someone did I denied it. So this is how I'm going to be for the rest of my life, then.\nThe Next Next Entry\n\nI had a lot of people talk to me, for some reason. A few new Dedicants just came and started talking to me. Then Taynuel came to talk to me.\n\nHe knows how I feel and was trying to help me. He said a lot, and some of it gave me hope\nfor my future. But, looking back, no, I don't think that's the right thing to do.\n\nThe talk ended with him telling me he was wrong in thinking I was deserving of becoming a Druid.\n\nAnd that's that. He said he would talk to people\nabout making me a Dedicant again, but then he said the part about him being wrong.\n\nSo we're back as a sad piece of shit.\n\nFuck.\n'Nother Entry\n\nI thought I felt better, until I woke up today. No. That's over. I feel basically the same as before I talked to anyone recently. I'm lonely and it hurts, but there is no solution.\n\nI guess now I am not angry at anyone for ignoring me, or\nnot going out of their way to try to make me happy. That's not their responsibility. They all have a life that is far more important than mine, and I just would make them feel bad if I talked to them.\n\nTaynuel said I should try to be socialable.\nBut, for the reason I put in the last paragraph, I can't. I am a nuisance. I should leave all these people alone, let them forget me. But it's so hard to let go. It's hard to care.\n\nStanding up takes a lot of effort. Eating takes a lot of effort. I know\nI smell bad, I know I'm filthy. But what does it matter, really? Do you think I'll be denied from the Seven Skies because people I smell like a farm? No.\n\nI wanted to ask someone who knew about the Seven Skies and all that. I know when I asked an Amyas\nmember he told me that non-humans could get to the Seven Skies if they lived a holy life and all that.\n\nBut I haven't, so, I guess that is bust.\n\nThe other place I know about is the Eternal Forest, or something like that. But that's reserved for really\ngood Druids, or something. And I'm not even a Druid, let alone one deserving of the special Aspect land.\n\nSo I don't know what's gonna happen. I guess I'll just rot, and that's that. I don't know.\n\nI don't want to ask though. Because then it will raise\nquestions I don't want to answer.\n\nI guess there's nothing else to say about it.\n\nOh, and, I was wondering what was gonna happen to this... Journal, after I'm gone. I thought I would just put it in a chest of my other things, and\nlet whoever cleans up after me find it. Or just not look in it and throw it in the trash.\n\nThen I thought I would just keep it with me. It served it's purpose; Giving me some sort of closure on some things. I can be done with everything, if atleast I know\nI expressed what I thought somewhere. Even if that never gets viewed.\n\nI don't want to burden anyone with guilt. So I think the best thing to do is just throw it away before I do anything.\n\nFuck.\nEntry 9?\n\nToday is a really bad day. I don't know how much more I can take. If this is the last entry, that's cause I did something about it all. \n\nThere's this island that the Druids were on briefly during the beginning of Vailor. I spent time on it,\ntried to make it a bit prettier and less fucked. I found a fairy circle on it.\n\nAnd I think that's the best way to do it. Step into it, and just not come out. I don't think I'd feel much, I'd just wear away over the days. I don't know how long you could\ngo, but it only has to be a few days. \n\nAnd, if I did that, I'd feel sort of what I wanted to feel; Attuned. I've been in lots of Fairy Circles before, so maybe I would be too used to it. I don't know what else to do.\n\nI don't want to do it\nalone. I don't want to be alone when I go. I want someone to be there holding my hand. I don't want anyone to do what I do, but I\n\nI don't want to be alone.\n\nFuck. Ignore this entry, I'm just emotional at the moment.\nEntry Something\n\nStill feel the same. I don't know what's holding me back from doing it now. It's never gonna get better. I'm never gonna fix this. Nobody is ever gonna be able to help me. \n\nI guess I don't know how to finish everything. There\nare so many things I want to do, so many people I want to talk to. I won't be able to do that if I'm gone.\n\nBut it's better to leave without doing all that, maybe. I'm just gonna make it harder for myself, for others maybe.\n§\nI set this aside for a long time. I am still here. Not for long. Gonna go soon. That's that. Sorry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Unknown", "-------------------\n\n\n\n\n\"The Devourer's Mercy\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\nEntry #1:\n-------------------I have recently been looking for leads on the beast which has coined the name, The Devourer. From the last voyage I have established that the sheer size of the beast is to unimaginable proportions. Though this means that the -\n-creature is indeed ancient. This beast is not new, or not the child of some other primal beast. It's face has apparently never been seen, as I have found various manuscripts from the past inhabitants of these isles... Translation will be tedious but it-\n-will be worth it. For what I find in these documents, I believe will help me establish a connection to the Devourer and its true purpose...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n[!]\nVarious sketches of strange elven symbols are scattered along the page, transcribing them would take time, as each symbol is distorted by the various quill strokes against the paper.\n[!]\nEntry #2\n-------------------These documents are quite interesting... They detail some sort of temple or place of worship. The words, \"The Drowned Children\" seem to repeat themselves through this document, with further outlining of these disgusting rituals\n-and practices which were performed by these children. Though my lead was right, these ancient people were indeed connected to the Devourer. They believed for the creature to be some sort of god which guarded them from the East. The document has further-\n-references to certain mural sites which are scattered along the Eastern Coastline. I am not sure if I wish to explore these, since the rituals depicted were performed at these sites... I am having trouble composing myself to write this entry. Though I-\n-must document this to ensure that this knowledge gets spread to the general Vailorian populace. I believe this creature is alot more than it currently appears, for the old seemed to worship it with an undying sense of loyalty... I'll update this when-\n-more leads are uncovered by these documents.\n-------------------\n[!] Distorted circles are placed upon a drawn landmass, scattered along its east. They appear to be different to the current continent of Vailor.\n[!]\nEntry #3\n-------------------I have found one of the mural sites! I pack and leave in the next day. Further investigation upon the documents have revealed that these rituals somehow powered a certain stone... A Prophet was believed to wield this stone-\n-control the very fabric of time and the world. Through the manipulation of the Devourer! These discoveries make my jaw drop, for if there is a stone which holds this power, that would mean it could be an object used to bargain between nations. Or -\n-glorious riches... Yes, imagine the small earth digger to have the riches of the Salvian Vaults, that would be grand... I shall write in a new book to record my further studies, for this one shall stay until I compile them all into a journal. That I will\n-release upon the discovery of this stone. I shall leave this disgusting shack and move to more glorious fronts, to the mural site I shall go.\"\n-------------------[!] A final scribble ends the journal, the rest of the pages blank.\n[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 1", "An Unknown Author", "The group was successful on their endeavor today. The blight seeping from the cave was held back and the immediate tree line restored. They celebrated with a festival, the grove becoming alive with laughter and song.\nIt’s nice to be with people again, it…..it helps me forget about the last group and how I abandoned them in their time of need.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 2", "An Unknown Author", "I feel it every time we get close to the blight. Something calling to me, something whispering in my ear…..no, my mind.\nMy eyes look to the others that fight against it as I stay in the back, they seem to be deaf to the words it speaks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 3", "An Unknown Author", "We lost one today….a sister. The blight became too strong for the group to hold back with so few. She didn’t turn away though like the others.\nShe didn’t run like I had. I watched on from the treeline, frozen in fear, as she put herself between the Blight and her kin. It washed over her as the exhausted Druids pulled back, watching her sacrifice.\nThey’re having a ceremony for her now in the grove, but I’m sitting in her room. I found a laurel of leaves she once wore, a crown that a hero would wear. Maybe, one day I can wear this like the hero she was.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 4", "An Unknown Author", "The blight is spreading faster. Overnight, it reached the treeline. The lively deep browns and reds of the tree trunks have become plastered with grotesque shadows, as if the bark itself was turning to ooze.\nThat is how the others describe it, ‘grotesque’. As I look upon the blight, I see a….interesting design within it.\nHow as it scars the landscape, it creates wondrous images. Perhaps this hilltop would look like a deer prancing from a predator or this tree would snap and look like a mortally wounded crane.\nIt makes me wonder if blight is not part of the natural cycle itself? Isn’t death part of it?\n\n*The handwriting would appear to become unstable.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 5", "An Unknown Author", "The circle is shrinking quickly. Many are being lost to the blight and the beasts that come from it. Others are disappearing.\nHistory repeats itself. Soon I will be on my own again, alone and afraid. But am I truly alone? These whispers in my mind keep me company, their words becoming slightly clearer with each passing eve. I\nfound a man in the trees earlier today. Old and hunched over, but for some reason the Blight seemed to pay him no mind. He asked me to meet with him again, promised to tell me more in the coming days.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry 6", "An Unknown Author", "The grove has been taken by the blight. I am the only one left. Brother and Sister lay at my feet, groaning in pain and sickness as the blight takes hold of them.\nNecessary sacrifices to the cause, that is what the old man said when he showed me how to blight my own grove. I have much to learn from my new guide, much to learn of this control over blight.\nThey were too deaf to hear the whispers of our Aspects. They were not enlightened like myself, like my new circle. Here, I shall prove to my new Brothers and Sisters that I am no coward….that I am more than a simple parasite.", ""),
        StaticBook("Leona Kellian", "Leona Nyx Kellian", "If this is found, I'm either showing this to you because I escaped. Or I died. If I'm dead,\nI'm sorry Gray.\nForgive me.\n-Leona Nyx Kellian\n\n\n*this book would be covered in dirt and blood*\nDay 1:\nIt's been 5 hours (I think? I was knocked out for a long while) since I fell. I was on my way to see my brother, Gray, in Sutica. But on my way, I fell through the ground and into a long maze of cave rooms and tunnels. I've been looking for a\nway out for a few hours now. No lucky yet. Wish me luck! Gray better appreciate what I do for him.\nDay 2: \nStill no luck. My eyes have ajusted to the dark, the only light is from the distance glow high above me, some cracks in the ground leak in light. It's far too high for me to climb out. Gray doesn't know I was going to see him. No one knows\nI'm gone. It's getting hard to think down here. And it's only been a lttle over a day...\nDay 5:\nNothing but rocks and dirt. I've been sleeping on my backpack these last few nights (I think they have been nights.) My neck is sore. I found water, thank god. I'm hungry.\nDay 12:\nI've been forced to eat the bugs and rodents that lurk in this cave. When will I get out of here?\nDay 23 or 24:\nIt's getting hard to keep track of the days. I don;t know what I'm going to do. I've looked everywhere fo a way out. I'm trapped.\nDay ???:\nI don't know what day it is anymore. I think winter is coming, it's getting cold.\nDay ???:\nI'm scared. I'm forgetting. I can't remember what the sun feels like, what does Gray's voice sound like? I'm scared, I don't want to forget.\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nI'm hurt. A small part of the cave feel in and a rock hit my head and I passed out. It hurts s much Ican hardly think.\nEver since my head was injured, I keep blacking out for periods of time. I don't remember then them but I must be awake or doing something... I've been painting images on the wall. It looks like a woman dancing and men watching her.\nThe blackouts are getting more frequent. I worry that I may stay like that permanently soon. This other me that seems to take over is very... odd. I drew a picture of what I think is a fish drowning the other morning. Or was it a week? Months? Years?\nMaybe I should just end it. What's the point anymore.\n*unreadable words would be scratched all over the page*\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*tear drops as well*\nDeath death death dark dark dark dark\nWhere is the light?\nH\n            E\n   L\n                          P\n\n\n\nM\n\n  E\n                        P\n                    LE\n               A\n                        SE\nI can't see, I can't hear, I can't feel. I'm floating forever in the darkness with no way out.\nGod forgive my sins.\n*the page would again be filled with unreadable words and tears. And sickening blood stain covers half the page too..*\nI m d ead. . . ?\n*blank page*\n*blank page*\n*blank page but with a few random sudges of dirt or maybe blood*\nEthan and I had a lovely dinner date today. After I finished working, he and I met up at his place for a meal. He was going on and on about how he saved this poor little fish from drowning. He's so noble. After our meal of black tar and necklace beads,\nhe took me outside and told me to look at the moon. And there in bright pink letter written on the moons surface was, \"MaRRy Me LeoNa!\" Of course I said maybe. We kissed and went back inside to skin the rabbits. Lovely day.\nI'm so happy. \n\n*a badly drawn photo of Leona and Ethan fills the page*\nEthan's dead, he died saving the poor fish again... You'd think that fish WANTED  to drown or something. It can't be helped I guess. I have to go back to work now. Dancing on tables should help me forget.\n*nothing but a bloody hand print with a smile scratched out on the palm*\nI\nheard\nsomething\nno\nsome?\none?\nI have o quit my job as an exotc dancer. These lovely men who claim to have 'resuced me' are telling me to go home and that I'm too old to dance anymore. Home? Where is home again? I should see if my niece or nephew know where home is.\n*The journal ends*\n(Okay so. Leona falls into a cave and is trapped for roughly 10years. She goes crazy and imagens this 'other life' where she's basically a stripper. ((I did that for the lolz)) She had a husband who died. After many years these men found her in the caves\nwhile digging for ores. They had no cluee she had been down there so long and just sent her off, thinking she was a crazy old women. So Leona stumbles and manages to find her way to Sutica and finds Eli. She thinks that her illusions are real. She has no\nclue she was trapped in a cave for 10 years.)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~FoxyPandaBear", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Ashton", "\"Dear Aeran,\n\nOnce again, I am writing a letter to you to better express my feelings. I have no ability to express them in person without exploding.\n\nI am sorry.\"\n\"I am sorry for my actions and my hurtful words. I am sorry for causing such strife and pain in your life. I have caused all of this.\"\n\"Perhaps it is best that we don't speak until I am more mature and capable of controlling my emotions.\n\nI am sorry.\"\n\"You are my only friend. You are the best thing that has ever happened to me. To lose you...it hurts. However, I have no ability to control myself when it comes to you. I am so sorry. \n\nPlease, forgive me.\n\n-Ashton\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter for Aeran", "Ashton", "\"Dearest Aeran,\n\nI am writing to you, because speaking about how I feel always goes wrong. I either stuff my feelings inside myself, denying everything that's wrong, or I blow up with anger, panic, and do drastic things.\"\n\"So, a letter. If I become overwhelmed with emotions, I can simply walk away and come back to it later.\n\nI hope I can keep this short and sweet. I'm sorry in advance if I can't.\"\n\"I feel replaced. It's the only word I can think of. It's the only word that fits. Even though I know that isn't the case, it's the only word that belongs there.\"\n\"Up until recently, I was the only person in my dad's immediate family. His mother lived far away. His sister was in hiding. He apparently has a brother that he can't stand. He doesn't identify himself as a Winterleaf to have those relations.\"\n\"It was just us. Me and him.\n\nThe same was true with you and me.\n\nSure, the kids in the grove came to you. As far as actually hanging out and being friends, you were all I had, though.\"\n\"For a time, I illusioned myself into believing the same was true for your end. That I was your only real friend. \n\nMy dad might be your best friend, but he doesn't come around often. He doesn't talk often. When he does, it's deep and meaningful, sure.\"\n\"However, he's often fleeting and after his meaningful words are spoken, he goes back into his meditative state, not really saying much of anything for days or weeks.\"\n\"I felt like we were all a team. You, me, my dad. I felt like we were outcasts here. Everyone sort of thinks differently and acts like a jerk towards you and my dad.\"\n\"Then, Riley came back.\"\n\"Suddenly, my dad is around more, and all he wants to do is spend time with his sister.\n\nI understand. I truly do. Their mother just died. That's his SISTER. I get it.\n\nBut I was alone.\"\n\"Suddenly, you were in love with her. Every conversation was about her. About how pretty she is. About how wonderful and kind she is. About how I'll like her. About how it doesn't have to upset me that she's here. Everything was about her.\"\n\"And again, I was alone.\"\n\"I feel alone. Like I did in Felsen. Before I came to the grove. Everything is about her now. \n\nI feel like all of this is happening for the wrong reasons, but perhaps it's just because I'm not really involved.\"\n\"What I see...is two people getting married for the wrong reasons.\n\nShe wants to live her life to the fullest. Great! She wants to make up for all the time she lost while in hiding. Great! She feels like she needs to do something drastic.\"\n\"To make sure she doesn't lose any more time. That's what I see in her. Immaturity. Restlessness. The need to do crazy things to feel alive again.\"\n\"And what I see in you?\n\nI see someone who wants to prove that he has a purpose here. Someone who was almost ousted from his home, from his family. \n\nThat's what you told me when I came here.\"\n\"We are ALL family. That's what you said when I told you how alone I felt.\n\nI can't imagine how it must feel to know they wanted to unattune you. To feel like your family wanted you gone. You've been shoved away by so many people.\"\n\"I'm afraid you're going to marry my aunt, because she makes you feel like you're not alone. Like she won't shove you away. \n\nI'm scared it's for all the wrong reasons.\"\n\"But I don't know. I don't know anything. I feel so in the dark.\n\nWhen I'm around, it's not about how things really are. It's just about how perfect she is. That's all it's ever about.\n\nWith you and with my dad.\"\n\"It's always the same. I can't even say hello and talk without it turning into, \"Have you seen your aunt today? She's great, right? You like her, right? Let me tell you more about her, so you'll like her more.\"\n\nI get it. You both want me to like her.\"\n\"But I feel so replaced.\"\n\"I feel so alone.\"\n\"I feel like I don't belong here anymore.\"\n\"Or maybe I replaced her for my dad.\n\nMaybe he missed his family, and I was just their replacement.\n\nNow, he has his sister back, and I just sort of exist here.\"\n\"Maybe with you, I was just a filler until someone you could love came along. Someone pretty and nice and wonderful and smart.\"\n\"I know that isn't true. I know that's not how it is, but damn, that's how it feels.\"\n\"I'm sorry to pour all this on you, my friend.\n\nThis is a time of happiness in your life, and that's all I've wanted for you since you became my friend. I've wanted to see you smile and be truly happy, and you seem to be now.\"\n\"I'm sorry.\"\n\n\n-Ashton", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to my Son", "Gray Kellian III", "To Gray Kellian III\n To my Eldest and Only son. \nI am Sorry.\nBut I relized I am not Well. So I am leaving for a while. I need time to reflect.\nI leave the house to you, Along with all my gear I kept precious to me. Do not allow anyone to use\nThem. They are yours, and only Yours.\nSecondly, I leave my Title to you. You can call yourself\nGray Kellian the Third, Keeper of the Kellian household and all her possessions.\nFarewell for now my son.\nI love you, Your father\n\n  -Ethro Kellian the Second, Retired Keeper of the Kellians", ""),
        StaticBook("Light&Dark", "Gray Kellian III", "Clerical Jornal\nEntry 1:\n\nThe Question was given to me to go and think about,\n\n\"What is light and dark to you\"\n\nAnd here is my answer after careful thought\nFirst of all What is light?\n\nLight according to Tahariae, is purity with white light being the purest.\n\nBut what could you relate purity to? Innocences. And who is innocent above everything? Youth.\nLight is the youth of the world, for no child can be born evil. And the youth are the protecters of tomorrow. And we must raise them to fight the evil of tomorrow until one day. there will be no evil.\nAnd Darkness\n\nAccording to Tahariae Darkness is the Evil, the undead the ghouls, and just the 'Spooks' As the decendents have dubbed them.\n\nBut it appears to not include decendents who do evil deeds, such as murders, and bandits\nBut to me? Darkness is all forms of evil, Someone who kills and pilliages for fun, I beleive to be in the darkness. The people whos only wish is to watch other people suffer, are in the darkness.\nBut that is where the line fades, and blends together.\n\nThe point where you need to make a choice.\n\nTahariae does not give us his power to fight off bandits, and murders, but the taint, and spooks\nSo sometimes we might have to make a decision when helping people of purity. \n\nDo we use what he can to stop a murder?\n\nWould that displease Tahariae because to him, The murderer is not a Killer?\nTherefore to make that decision is a huge one, with even greater potential risks.\n\nSo choose carefuly. \nBecause this is a test of your Morals.\nSigned\n\nGray Kellian the Third\n\nKeeper of the Kellian Family, Along will her assets.", ""),
        StaticBook("Llirame & The", "Nivndil Duskhollow", "(~+~)  Llirame  (~+~)\n                &\n          The Tree\n\n\nThere once was a Wood Elf named Llirame. He lived in a small cottage near Oakhearth. In the garden grew a young apple tree.\n\nAs a young Elf, Llirame played in the tree.\nWhen he was troubled or saddened, he spoke to the tree and he felt comforted.\n\nLlirame became dear friends with the tree, as they aged together.\n\nOver the years, the tree blossomed every Malin's Welcome and grew fruit every Grand Harvest.\nWhen Llirame reached three-hundred years old, he had a family of his own.\n\nYear after year, the tree provided fruit and shelter for Llirame and his family. His children climbed in its branches, just as he had before them.\nUntil one year, when the tree's leaves became a sickly yellow.\n\nLlirame came out to the tree and said, \"Old friend you look gravely ill, though I know not what to do. Should I cut you down?\"\n\nThe tree did not reply.\nAs the Seeds went on, the tree grew worse.\n\nThe bark of its branches came loose and its fruit became bitter and wilted.\n\nLlirame came out to the tree again. \"Old friend, you are gravely ill. I should cut you down to save you from pain.\"\nThe tree did not reply.\n\nBut the tree grew sicker still. It's branches grew heavy and some began to fall from the tree with rot.\n\nIt's bark began to peel from its boughs and its leaves folded inwards. Insects burrows into its trunk.\nOne day, a Druid came to Oakhearth. Llirame sought her out earnestly.\n\n\"Oh wise Druid, my best friend is gravely ill and I know not what to do,\" Llirame pleaded.\n\n\"Very well,\" she replied. \"Take me to your friend.\"\nLlirame brought the Druid to the tree.\n\n\"Llirame, your friend is gravely ill,\" she said examining the tree carefully.\n\n\"What should I do?\" he asked. \"Should I cut it down to save it from suffering?\"\n\"No,\" replied the Druid. \"Your friend tells me that it does not want to be cut down.\"\n\nLlirame looked upon the tree and sighed, \"Old friend I will not cut you down unless you wish it so.\" He promised.\nThe Druid produced a talisman, made from roots woven together. She tied it around a thick branch of the tree and said, \"The tree is able to use this talisman. If your friend wishes to be cut down, the talisman will fall and not before.\"\nLlirame thanked the Druid, who left Oakhearth and went on her way.\n\nDays went by, when Llirame would come out to the try and say, \"Old friend, you are gravely ill. Is today when you would have me cut you down?\nThe talisman had not moved.\n\nWeeks went by, when Llirame would come out to the tree.\n\n\"Is today when you would have me cut you down, old friend?\"\n\nThe talisman did not move.\nSeeds had passed, when Llirame came out to the tree.\n\n\"Old friend you are gravely ill. Is today when you would have me cut you down?\" he asked.\n\nBut the tree had died.\nIt's leaves had fallen and its twisted branches were bare.\n\nIt's bark was black and peeled and the flesh beneath was diseased and rotten.\n\nLlirame cried as he beheld the dead tree.\nHe did not eat for days, in mourning for his oldest friend.\n\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth, she visited Llirame in his home.\n\n\"Oh wise Druid, my oldest friend is dead and I know not what to do,\" he sobbed.\n\"You were good to respect the wishes of your friend,\" she replied.\n\n\"But my friend has died in pain and suffering,\" sobbed Llirame.\n\nSoon after, the Druid left Oakheart and went on her way.\nDays passed, before Llirame could bring himself to remove the remains of the tree.\n\nHe went to it and sobbed as he peeled away its blackened bark.\n\nHe wept as he went to get his sharpest axe.\nBefore Llirame could ready to swing however, he saw something green and new in the tree.\n\nIn a hole of its trunk, where bark and splinters and soil had gathered, there grew a small sprout.\n\nLlirame brought it water and compost.\nLlirame tended the sprout for days, just as the tree had cared for Llirame and his family.\n\nAs the weeks passed and the Seeds changed, the sprout grew stronger.\n\nThe old tree quickly fell apart and crumbled away.\nBut in its husk the new sprout was sheltered from the wind and the heavier rains.\n\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth a year later, she visited Llirame who presented her with the budding sappling.\nThe Druid smiled and touched Llirame on the shoulder.\n\n\"Just as there is death\nthere is also life. As there is decay so there is growth. As there is rot, so\nthere is blossom,\"\n\nShe said to him.\nIn the years to come, the new tree became a dear friend to Llirame's children.\n\nIt gave fruit and sheltered many small animals.\n\nLlirame never forgot his old friend, but as it had been there for him, so he was there for the new tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Student", "Astaroth Stormtaker", "I have heard about you and i wish to learn Electrical Evocation. I await your reply eagerly. (pm McKidderZ)", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana Gems", "Gladuos", "Introduction:\n   Within this book will be the research of various gems for usage in transfiguration practices.\n   Namely, the precious gems are known as ruby, sapphire, emerald, and diamond. Each with their own unique qualities.\nFirstly, each gem will be described in its physical sense, then we'll explore how they're made, average weight, shape, hardness, melting points, magical understandings and much more.\nSight:\n   The gems are usually hard, translucent objects created from minerals within the planet. The diamond is normally a clear substance akin to the visual appearance of glass with an air of shinyness. The other gems follow suit with\nfairly minor differences such as sapphire being blue, ruby being red, emerald being green.\nHow They Form:\n   Most gems are formed when rocks are solluted with water near the surface of the earth, which slowly evaporates and allows the rock to form into minerals. Otherwise gems are often formed by extreme pressure being put onto rocks until -\n- they completely change in makeup.\nThe shape and weight of gems tends to be a differing occurance. Generally gems are relatively dense materials that result in higher weight. They also form together in specialized crystalizations that often create shapes not often seen within nature -\n- such as cubes. \n\n   Gems are some of the hardest materials within the known natural world, with diamond being the hardest of the precious gems.\nThe melting point of gems tend to be at extremely high at over 3500 degrees celsius. They tend to be so resistent to melting that many forges within the known realm would be unable to melt them down. Of course, they are still fairly susceptible -\ntowards being cut and reshaped with chisels or other proper tools.\nThe precious gems have a strangely unique property with magical understandings. They are capable of holding tremendous amounts of mana compared to other materials, relative to valuability and size.\nIt's good to note that there are a plethora of other gems that tend to follow suit with the same characteristics with a few select differences. Otherwise, there are some fairly unique gems that do not follow the norm such as thanhium, focus crystals, -\nand demon stone. These would not be explained in great detail through this book, but may be in the future.\n*Upon flipping to the next page, you are greeted with a plethora of diagrams, charts, sketchings, illustrations, equations, and secondary notes that go on for pages upon pages. They appear to attempt supporting and bolstering previous statements within -\n- the book as well as making a few minor unspoken statements.*", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "Jistuma", ">|<Monk>|<\n-=~Resurrection~=-\nIt is the salvation of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall at the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some\nof these happenings, or so I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to be manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performing it\nis praying to the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but it has other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives at the sanctuary a bit hurt after travels. It appears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their\nsavior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course due to their magic, small flecks of light I have seen surrounding and healing the wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once\ndeceased fully mortal once more.\n\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death, in\nnear perfect condition. From those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present effect of being saved. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it.\nOther common effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met its end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most is that sometimes the ones saved change… I have talked to some before and after saving, and changes can\nbe quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why that happens, all of them without means of\nproving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\n\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had\nperished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover. Before that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact\nlocation of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through that exact area when returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument even\nhappened when the woman just wanted to go home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to go through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas he returned to normal about half a day\nlater. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviors such as people staying in the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after leaving with a friend. I simply believe once more, that\nthe experience was so horrible, that those saved gain a subconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body? \n\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the\nbody to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection. I have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is favorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated,\neaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits and drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never been found once more, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when\nI ask them. They do answer a few questions. I learned, for instance, that the monks are neutral, and never take side in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being\nsaved together with the children that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks before, many want others to remain dead.\n\nMost of the stories of the saved start simply with them explaining how they woke up in the monk’s care.\nSeems to always be the same as I stated. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful. As the monks mention,\nthey cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monks rooms an elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they don’t want to live anymore, then\nthey wouldn’t return to the land of the living.\n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals, they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\nWritten by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452", ""),
        StaticBook("Morning Nemir", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "Good morning my love. I hope you enjoy the food I made for you this morning! I know it's early but have a wonderfully bright day.\n\nI just want to say sorry for my... Proposal the other elven day. It was horribly timed and -\n- I made you feel awkward about it. I guess, for lack of better words... I've been missing you in that way. I hope you can forgive me for that.\n\nRegardless perhaps we can spend some time together in the coming -\n- few elven days? Have that date and that chat we spoke about?\n\nAnyway, I digress. I'll leave you to your breakfast, dear. Again, have a beautiful day my heart. I love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("motherland", "Orchaldir", "there was once a man\n\nwho hated ascended very much\n\nhe took his sisters soul for the opportunity to piss on their rug\n\nhe was the man from haelunor", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "Tristanm1", "Mundane Healing\nby Nienna Calm\n\nCopied by\nLeyun Taliamonn\n\n(( On 5/31/2013 ))\n--Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nNienna's Foreward: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the\nTreatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with\nnothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I've recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n-Minor Cut (Nienna)\nSimply apply a dose of deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it. The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n-Stomach Ache (Nienna)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n-Soreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n-Burns (Nienna)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about\nburns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check and clean the burn wound daily until the\nskin can finally reform.\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim's body cool using cold water. Give them hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nativitas", "Shady_Tales", "There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either,but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity. Truly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe seven skies. With his intent and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. THe rolling seas, the proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God. The World was\nnot created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what?Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how  hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and\ngood our actions be. The first mortal being to be created was a man.This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see.The Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created\nbefore the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.God then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell  and the Man lived. God then took the\nman and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman.These simple beings could not talk, nor talk, nor\ndid they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis. Malin was the first of\ntheir sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh\nmeadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for\neach Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken\nwith grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks\nand traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis. At this\ntime, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for\neach other and each others people.Urguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of\nAegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace.Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the void, kin spirits\nto the Aengul, defected.Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things\ndelicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's\nplan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content.\n Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy\nthe barren forests.To Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him. Horen, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased\nHe needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality. Krug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The\nbeast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror. In Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in\nflame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time.\nHe stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the strength of Krug as they fought\nthe beast.Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.For the thirty years the Descendants\nfought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw\nup their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast.Urguan grew greedy, he fought\nvalourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day. One\nday where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers. An army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty\nand beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\nIblees' soldiers\nburned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed\napparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark\nsoul would be forever trapped in torment. But..Before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time. “You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it\nshall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it. Malin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of\nyour own. Even you have done my work, if you realize it or not.Urguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in\nthe deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied. Horen, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and\ndie before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors. And you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your\nlust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.\"As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\nThe Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to\ncorrupt their souls, the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason. The robed figure stood before the four brothers. \"There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to\nbless you. Malin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived. Urguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind. Krug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist. And Horen, may your people\none day explore the Seven Skies. I can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.\" And with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into\nthin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's beauty", "the Chronicler", "[!] the sketch is that of a Kha woman, standing on the shore of an underground sea. it is highly stylized and shaded to bring the attention to the Kha instead of the surroundings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nothing", "The March Ash", "I have once again arrived in the Far Glade. The second time is more imposing than the first. Then, I had heard only stories. Now, I know what awaits me: nothing. Nothing but the shadows and green things.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations", "Sorceress_Haven", "I've decided writing is perhaps my best course of action, given I have no skill in painting or poetry or song. infact, Im a rather terrible bard, but this task will not go entirely waisted. The truth is I am far better at gathering my thoughts on paper, I\nhave some abbillity to draw. Now then, I am in some far corner of Lorraine, the likes of which I've never visited, and although the kingdom here isnt entirely complete, the scene before me is absolutely heavenly. There's a church fashioned to that of\nArchitecture quite common in the desert. Sandstone and brick, with a beautiful stone cross atop the highest spire, and before the church is a winding river, around it, life teems. Flowers, a forest, bunnies, and even a few wolves which have paid me no\nmore mind then I them. Where I stand is a large field of wheat, golden and gleeming in the setting sun. Truly beautiful, even if this scene was mostly brought about by man, rather than nature. The winds move over the wheat, causing them to glisten in a\nway similair to the waves of the ocean. Above me are the leaves of a beautiful oak, with richly colored bark, and the leaves... They form such a gentle song as the wind stirs them.\n\n    I suppose, I'll camp here, and continue...\nwhatever it is I am doing.. wandering I suppose, tomorrow.\n*Below is a simply sketch, in ink. A Spanish church, the river, and the wheat fields. At the top corner of the drawing, leaves and branches have been carefully etched*\nIt is very early in the morning. In fact, the sun as even yet risen. I had a nightmare, and I suppose those are common, but now I a awake and my mind wont let me rest. I suppose I will put my thoughts in order-\nI started this journey with the idea that I\nwould attempt to find this \"secret\" grove, as it is described in one of the book's in the library, but since then Ive come to realize, this task is about gaining new insight, the abbillity to see beauty in all things. Right? So what is the point in my\ntravelling to a grove that has been described as breath taking? I will not gain any insight into its true beauty as its true beauty is not hidden. So, I'm sticking to the roads, and viewing the landscape as anyone else would, only, Ill stop, and I'll\ntake time to carefully study land, to try and find the beauty in something so common.\n*a Valley is etched here, with a cobbel road before it. Grass has been carefully drawn about like spots of wheat, and in the distance, a forest begins.*\n*A pretty light pink tulip has been pressed between the pages, Next to a note.*\n\nWild flowers dont grow so commonly in the fields, but rather, closer to the spots of trees, and small forests. Never noticed that before, I wonder why?\n*A small tree is drawn here, jutting from the side of rather rocky hill, or perhaps small mountain? Its roots grip the sides of the rocks and span out in all directions, keeping the little tree virtually suspended in the air.*\nDay 3-\n\nIve never really realized how much I've missed of the world, until I stop to really look at it. Rolling hills of green, trees in all shapes and size, the castles in the distance, the sky and its rolling clouds that sometimes form familliar\nshapes. The little clovers that seem so soft to the eye, the spits of whites and violets of small field flowers, the castles looming in the diatance. Ive travelled some of these roads many times over, but never have I noticed such things.\nIt seems Ive found my way back to Felson, in truth, I can hardly remember where I began my journey. I cultivated some field clovers to plant when I return home, as I find I rather enjoy their mark on the landscape, and the life they attract.\nIve never truly noticed all the small, and even grander details that I so often pass when I take the roads. Mice, the little blue beetles that love nesting deep in the grass, the lady bugs that buzz around the wild flowers, and the birds that sit in\nwaiting to swoop down and devour them. I hope to take good care in notticing even the smallest things that add to the sights before me, each detail regardless of how small, is important for it adds character and beauty to all I lay mine eyes upon. -R\n*a four leaf clover and few small violet and white and yellow field flowers have been pressed here.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Nature", "Pine Druid Gi'Garun", "An Ode to Nature\n    by The Pine Druid\n\nWe walk upon her soil,\nWe gaze upon her trees.\n\nWe're surrounded by all kinds of things, \nThat sprouted from her seeds.\nWhen one steps out of one's front door,\nOne will see her work.\n\nHer prowess great and beautiful,\nNo dark or evil mirk.\n\nWhat is it that I speak about?\n\nWhat is it that I praise?\nThe lands we roam,\nThe streams that foam.\n\nThe trees so tall,\nThe rain that falls.\n\nAll of these are of her make, for they are her and her alone. The make of two of love and great.\n\nThat be Nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Void", "Thereon Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following is in no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\nOn the Void\n\nAs potential, waiting to be shaped and formed. Such is the role of an arcane mage.\n\nChapter II\n\nIn the previous chapter, everything that exists in our world exists as potential in the void.\nBut within the void, it is useless to us. Therefore, through trainning a mage can learn to connect to the void and harness its potential in various ways. One example, is evocation, the art of evoking a certain element. An evocanionist uses the void to\nForm their element out of the voids potential and then pull it into our physical world. They will have control over this evoked element (mind you the level of control depends of their skill) and it will be able to effect the physical plane (evoked flames\nwill burn, evoked winds will blow). make no mistake however, that which comes from the void does not belong in our physical plane. As such, as soon as a mage looses connention to the void, be it because he is too tired to continue, his concentration is\nbroken or he simply servers the connention, that which came from the void will return there. this applies to all arcane magic, not just evocation. You way be wondering, if the void is full of everything, why can't mages /make/ everything. The anser lies\nwith knowladge. You see, creating something from the void is no walk in the park. A mage requires absoloute knowlage of what they are attempting to create before they can create it. For this reason, arcane mages focus on one area of harnessing the void\n(or more for advanced mages). An evocationist will spend time learning and experiencing all they can about their element, a conjurer will disect creatures so as to understand how they work and an illusionist need to know how something feels before they\ncan make someone elsefeel it. So, how is it we can connect to the void?\n\nChapter III\n\nRelatively simple to learn but takes a lot of time to master. An arcane mage just starting out learning his craft (regardless of what that craft is)\nwill need to spend a lot of time meditating. Why do they meditate? To achieve the state  of nothingness needed to connect to the void. A connection to the void requires your mind to be empty. All thoughts, feelings amd emotions must be brushed aside. For\na mage just starting out, this will be quite rather difficult and requires a comfortable and secluded area in which they can meditate with extreme focus. To a mage just starting out meditating, it is best if you find somewhere quiet as when you hear a\nnoise your mind will subconsciously focus on it, which disrupts your focus. When meditation for the first time, to not expect to summon anything. When a mage has /truly/ gotten a grasp for this state nothingness they will feel a connecting to the void for\nthe very first time. Nothing will physically happen but you, the mage will most surely feel the power of the void. I can not say how exactly you will feel it. the result differs from person to person with some fainting, some feeling immense power surge\nthrough them and some having belling noses. But you /will/ feel it. After making your first connection it will slowly get easier from there as you progress now that you know what you need to achieve. You can now start experimenting with your art, assuming\nyou already have extensive knowledge on what you intend to create. Bare in mind that pulling something from the void, wether it be a feeling, an element or a creature, requires larger amounts of mana. Large and of longer sustained spells requre larger\namounts of mana to keep them from returning to the void. It is importaint that you recognise your limits, for mana has a physical strain on the body, leaving you fatigued. A mage that does not recognise his own limits may end up knocking himself out from\nhis own spell which is quite counter productive. As a new mage, Do not try anything large or long. You will not be able to sustain the provide the mana needed. Start small and work your way up. with lots of meditation and practice, there will come a day\nwhen you may connect with the void in an instant.\n\nThe way of a mage is lifelong. Mastery is simply staying the path. So stay the path.\n\nElers, Regent of the Arcane Delvers and Aeromancer 1st of suns smile 1445.", ""),
