        StaticBook("Dark Magic", "§bDaeren Rorel", "Dark Magic & You \n===============\nOriginally composed by Nienna Calm.\nRevised and translated by Daeren Rorel.\n\nContents:\n-What is a Dark Mage?\n-Necromancy\n-Shades\n-Soul Puppeteers\n  - Soul Contractors\n-Black Dragon Parasites.\n-General Warning Signs of a dark mage.\n\nWhat is a Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including pacts with dark gods, rituals set forth by Iblees,\n\nand other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\n\nNecromancy\n-------------------Necromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. Its age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\n\nthis world. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\n\nHow to Identify a Necromancer:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state.  Since necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life,\n\nor reports of people feeling drained after touching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\n\nShades\n-------------------Shades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, a second personality that desires for only chaos and destruction.\n\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, a second personality that desires for only chaos and destruction.\n\nHow to Identify Shades: \nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only only revealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air.\n\nTheir ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of being a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics,\n\nand these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a shade.\n\nSoul Puppeteers\n-------------------\n\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), they are able to bring sickness, pain and even death\n\nto a person from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify a Soul Puppeteer:\n\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer straight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies.\n\nIf you suspect someone of soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it’s the only way to confirm for sure.\n\nSoul Contractors are similar to soul puppeteers, in that they are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word.  This would be potentially useful,\n\nif not for the material they must fashion these documents on.  Soul contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken while they were still alive.  It is a brutal and horrifying process,\n\nthat speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\n-------------------\n\nA more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its host and causes\n\nthem to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how a parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you isolate a suspected carrier far from the uninfected.\n\n It is currently unknown if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they either be expelled from the city, or in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify a Black-Dragon Parasite:\n\nBlack-Dragon Parasites are easy to identify. All carriers for the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area.\n\nIf you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full body search immediately.\n\nGeneral Warning Signs of a Dark Mage\n-------------------\n\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general.\n\nThese are by no means deciding factors in a suspect’s ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nNext page for list.\n\nBe suspicious of any persons you see that:\nWear primarily black robes.\nAre hooded at all times.\nPossess bright red eyes.\nProject a magical aura that is black, gray or red in color.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fearful Thoughts", "§bReese Duchannes", "Fear is a fickle thing. As you spend more time within this world your fears change and adapt, the things you feared as a child are no longer frightening to you, while the things you fear as an adult likely wouldn't frighten you as a child. To pinpoint a\n\nfear is only to pinpoint a fear at your current moment in life. §0\n§0\n§0However, there are fears, ones born from traumatic moments that can carry throughout your life. To understand mine you must first understand my story. Something I have dreaded speaking\n\nabout, or acknowledging in the slightest. However if I wish to move on, I understand that I cannot be afraid of it any longer. §0\n§0\n§0My father, Lyrath Duchannes was a cold man. He was married at a young age, and taught to be the perfect Mali'thil.\n\nHe was pure in all the senses of a Mali'Aheral. Until he met my mother, a woman I never really knew, as I was conceived out of wedlock. My mother, from what I know was a captivating Mali'ame, with dark hair, and dark blue eyes. She carried me in secret\n\nuntil I was born. On that day my father returned and took me away from her, against her will. He took me to the silver state, where he told his wife, Kyri Duchannes, about me. She was distraught as anyone within this situation would be. However she loved\n\nmy father, and agreed to keep me a secret. I was confined to the basement as a child, my cries often times only heard by the bare walls of my room. When I was four my father brought books down into my room, he expected me to learn to read with\n\nno assistance. I tried my best but at such a young age I struggled. At the age of five, I had quite the nice collection of finished books. At this age my father and step mother allowed my presence upstairs, but only for a few hours and simply to preform\n\nhousework, and never near any windows. For most of my life I hadn't seen the sun. Years past like this, until my tenth birthday, when my father invited me upstairs, and onto the balcony of our family home. However little did I know, but he did it against\n\nmy step mothers wishes. She blew up that night, and locked me within the same bland room within the basement that had become all to familar. I could hear her shouting, I could hear the nasty things she said about me, and the things my father said in\n\nreturn, just as nasty. The next day, my father woke me up early, and told me he'd gotten a gift for me. We went upstairs and he brought me to the front door, he unlocked it and pushed me outside. The light was blinding, even in the early morning. My\n\nfather stepped out behind me, and prodded me along the streets. I moved along, glancing about as I took it all in, knowing this wouldn't last long, as everyone would awake soon. My father led me to a park. Maybe it was the shock from being outside, or\n\nperhaps just me being foolish, but when I turned around to look at my father he was gone. I was alone, even outside I felt like I was back in my room, just with a better view. As I said, taking everything in was foolish, I shouldn't have let my guard down\n\nIn my foolishness I didnt pay attention to how I got there, meaning I didnt know how to get home. I began to panic, before glancing about, though I dared not raise my voice to call out for him. Instead I sat down on a bench, trying to remain calm.\n\nThe sunrise was beautiful, I'd only read about it within my books, seeing it in person was something else. I sat there and watch it, until children began to appear within the park, their eyes filled with disgust as they saw me. I stood out like a sore\n\nthumb, with my dark hair. It only took a few moments before a guard showed up. I knew he was after me the moment I saw him. I got up and ran, he chased after me, soon more followed behind him. In an effort to flee I began to climb over a fence, I slipped\n\nnear the top, and sliced a long thin gash into my leg. I limped on still trying to flee the guardsmen. However with my leg I didnt make it very far, they caught me. The guards took me to a cell, they questioned me, but I couldnt tell them much.\n\nThey dragged me over into another room, one with a fireplace in it. Within the fireplace sat a hot brand, glowing with heat. Within an instant they grabbed it and pressed it into my neck, marking me as impure. After they took all I knew, and branded me\n\nthey threw me out of the city. §0\n§0\n§0So there you have it. Or at least what started it all. So my greatest fear, is betrayal of the ones I trust, and abandonment from the ones I love.", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "§bJohnathan Faroe", "What is purity? I truely believe that it's a gray area, so much so, that trying to define it strips it of any power or meaning. Purity is desgined to be subjective by nature. All clerics hold different ideals to different standards.\n\nIf I were to atempted to define what purity means to me, I would define it as the following:§0\n§0\n§0Purity is the accumulation of all actions commited by an individual of which they are judged apon.§0\n§0\n§0Though impure actions commited will never\n\ncease to exist, they can be out weighted in by actions done with goodness in mind.§0\n§0\n§0By this deffintion, it is possible for a bandit to attone for his actions, while also possible for a good man to fall. This is the chaotic, ever-shifting nature of purity.", ""),
        StaticBook("Control", "§bTheodore Faroe", "Cousin, while I write this I sit on the brink of execution by the paladins and walk away wounded from a brawl in the ocean, in which I was saved by Reese.§0\n§0\n§0I only mention this, because it highlights my true fear.. Being helpless, or being viewed as\n\nhelpless. My nightmares are plagued by the sensation of being bound, while my loved ones are slain before me. Of course, like everyone, I fear losing my loved ones.. But for me, the deeper sensation is the loss of control. I fear when things spiral out of\n\nmy hands, and I'm forced to sit and watch, shivering in my boots. Control is important to me, and my blade allows me to maintain some semblance of grasp on reality. Being stripped of it, put on my knees before a jury much like I will be when the paladin's\n\nseize me.. That matter truly rumbles the depths of my being and my courage.§0\n§0\n§0[!] Moisture drips along this page, ink blotted in one spot as if he left the quill pressed into the parchment. It shakily tapers off, as if dropped suddenly.§0\n§0\n§0A shaken signature\n\nrests at the bottom of the last page.§0\n§0\n§0- Theodore Faroe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diplomatic Writ", "§bOwyn Amador", "===================           Writ of §0\n§0        Diplomatic§0\n§0          Mission§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0*The Seal of House Amador is marked here is Blue Wax*§0\n§0\n§0Owyn Amador, Baron of Mondstadt.\n\nTo the Trade Princess of the Federation of Sutica, Lilyana, and her government of those aforementioned isles.§0\n§0\n§0Please accept unto your House and Halls one Aylwin Blaxton, to act as Diplomat and Envoy on behalf of House Amador.\n\nI, Owyn Amador, Baron of Mondstadt, have sent the said diplomat to your isles in order to improve our current diplomatic relations. Whilst in the lands of Sutica, I request that the said diplomat and envoy receives the following curtosies:\n\n* Diplomatic Immunity.§0\n§0  - Whilst in the Isles        of Sutica, the said       Diplomat will               Adhere to the laws      & Customs of§0\n§0     Sutica, to better         Relations. Please         Expel the Diplomat       if this is not§0\n§0     Upheld.\n\n* Residency.§0\n§0  - Please house the§0\n§0     said diplomat in §0\n§0     accomodation§0\n§0     close to the Trade      Princess' Court, §0\n§0     So relations may         be improved§0\n§0     between House §0\n§0     Amador & Sutica.\n\nI hope that this gesture of goodwill will be accepted in good faith. I hope that, in the future, a trade agreement between our two peoples can be concluded. Until then, please accept my sincerest wishes for good relations between us. §0\n§0* Baron Owyn Amador", ""),
        StaticBook("Citizen Passport", "§bFloris de Ruyter", "=-     PASSPORT    -=\n\nIssued by Floris de Ruyter of the Imperial Administration and given to Shynys, whom is a class C1 citizen, on the 6th of the First Seed, 1587.\n   This passport is legal tender until the 6th of the First Seed, 1597. If found\n\nplease return to the Imperial Administration in Johannesberg.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter.", "§bLaethesia", "[!] A letter sits within the donation chest, careless handwriting depicting a note. \n\n\"Dear Shynys Itesti, I'd first like to say that your library is nice, and it has a sufficient amount of books concerning magic. Good job.\n\n- I'd then like to ask of you a favour. In exchange for minas, I want to buy copies of some of your books.\n\nAs a fellow booklover, I think you will understand my need to own them and not travel across Axios each time I wish to read. -\n\nIf you accept my proposal of a generous amount of minas, please contact me.\"\n\n[!] The letter would be signed in a scribbled fashion by a 'Laethesia'. Besides her signature would sit a small drawing of a cat.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Purity", "§bQuinn", "§0\n§0\n§0        On Purity§0\n§0    An Opinion Piece§0\n§0\n§0 §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By: Quinn M. Faberry\n\nWhen asked what purity means to me, I really didn’t know. Those questions are still ringing in my ears. §0\n§0What is purity?§0\n§0\n§0Who decides what is pure in the world?§0\n§0\n\nWhat does it mean to protect that purity? §0\n§0\n§0There is so much to consider, and it’s all quite personal. §0\n§0\n§0In my personal opinion, purity is when things are as they should be.\n\nOkay, who decides that?§0\n§0\n§0If I were to wield the light of Tahariae, would it be in my right to use my best judgement to decide what is pure?§0\n§0\n\nPerhaps it’s Tahariae that decides what is pure, and I am to trust in my faith to guide me in enforcing his judgements.§0\n§0\n§0Thinking on it more, I believe the world decides. Everything was one way. It was created that way and should stay that way.\n\nThe evils of the world corrupt things and change them to something they shouldn’t be.§0\n§0\n§0Iblees is one of the most notable examples. He tainted the world, raised undead, and cursed all of the Descendants.\n\nHe corrupted what was once pure and twisted it to his suit evil desires. To this day, undead, monstrous abominations roam the world, leaving a horrid scar on what is natural and beautiful. §0\n\nI believe nature decides what is pure.§0\n§0\n§0That is further expanded upon by Tahariae’s words and tenants.§0\n§0\n\nTo protect that purity, we must fight against the ones who wish to taint it, and we must lead others towards the same goals as our own.§0\n§0\n§0Together, the Clerics stand against the darkness that wishes to take hold of all that is righteous in the world.\n\nThat is what I wish to do as well. §0\n§0\n§0I feel my place in all of this is to fight against the evils of the world, to heal others, and to protect the innocent people.\n\nI wish to provide them with sanctuary from the taint that would corrupt their souls while guiding them down the better path. §0", ""),
        StaticBook("A Valiant Soldie", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n\n\n    The Valiant Soldier\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Reich Ministry of\n    Enlightenment and\n    Truth\n\nYoung Billy played in his garden the day they came. A soaring Eagle upon their tabards, these were the Kaisereichs finest. \n\nHe watched them parade into the Caliphate, and watched a throng of curious people begin to cheer them into the city, eager to see\n\nthe fighting men and women of the Kaisereich. The clapping continued for hours as the troops poured in, banners held high, it was if it was a public show of solidarity with the common man. \n\nYoung runners ran beside the parade, handing out small\n\nflyers to those who would take them. The flyers listed places men and women alike could sign up for the Imperial Army, the fighting force of the Kaisereich. One such places was the Recruitment office in the Caliphate, near the main gate.\n\nAlongside the runners and the parade, men on horseback and wearing a thick leather coat and a snazzy black cap were the Ministry of Truth Officers. They were helping to distribute flyers to the runners. They handled the media, arts and news within the\n\nKaisereich. \n\nAnd last but not least, came the officers of the Kaisereichs Imperial Army. The mighty officers, and the Champion of Hallowvale, a Caliphate local! The black children in the crowd roared as they saw him. They shouted \"Praise the Champion!\"\n\nOne of the officers at the end of the parade brought forth a large rolling float - and people saw a portrait of the Kaiser. As the float came closer and closer, a figure emerged through the portrait - it was only the Kaiser himself! The crowd roared with\n\npraise and love, the parading soliders could barely contain the crowd for their show of unabashed dedication to the Kaiser. He waved to the crowd, and made a stirring speech about re-vitalization of the core aspects of the Caliphate, and how we as a\n\npeoples were going to make the Caliphate better for all. \n\n\n            PRAISE\n              THE\n            KAISER", ""),
        StaticBook("Inspiration", "§bRagnar de Autson VI", "JUST DO IT!!!\n\nDON'T LET YOUR DREAMS JUST BE DREAMS!!!\n\nJUST.....DO ITTTT!", ""),
        StaticBook("treasureclue w", "§bSer Drake Lancefeld", "\"It lit aflame as our mutual passion did, though bringing sorrow and not joy.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser's Love", "§bHigh Dictator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    The Kaisers Love\n\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Ministry of Truth\n\n\n\n==================\n\nThe people of Al'Wakhrah slept soundly in their beds when the Ghouls attacked. The three Ghouls stood firm at the entrance to the city, looking for easy targets to consume. Larry Kringle, an Elven officer within the Reich Ministry of Truth, sounded the\n\nalarm. The Kaisereich answered. The good denizens of the Hallowvale Company answered the call, headed by the Qalasheen Champion of the Hallowvale and the Kaiser himself. The company created a line of Elves and Humans alike at the gate.\n\nThe three Ghouls would be no match for the Kaisers finest! The elite troops pulled out their aurum blades and laid waste to the evil creatures where they stood. They never even reached the steps to Al'Wakhrah. The Champion and the Grand Conservitor worked\n\ntogether to take one of the ghouls head clean off! The Kaiser himself slashed with no mercy, finally impaling an aurum dagger int he eye socket of one of the animated corpses. The last was slow, behind the other two. This nightmarish creations of Iblees\n\norigin were hacked down by an unknown citizen of the Kaisereich. The unknown solider of Good. The Kaiser, under instruction from a wandering Cleric, ordered the building of a fire to burn the bodies of the fetid Ghouls. The group rallies, all lending a\n\nhand to rid the world of the monstrosities. \n\nThe Kaiser had few words for the valiant group that night, but offered his humbles thanks to all those who helped secure the safety of the children inside the walls of Al'Wakhrah. His humility\n\nwas unexpected, and took the group by surprise. It was then that they realized, we as an Empire, as Vanderlorians, are stronger together than we are apart. The Humans and Elves worked hand in hand, under the grace of God, and were victorious.\n\nThe Kaisers strongest words were the quietest spoken. \n\n\n     HEIL VANDALORIA\n     HEIL ROVINKIN\n     HEIL DECIMUS\n     HEIL TRUTH", ""),
        StaticBook("Treasure clue", "§bSer Drake Lancefeld", "\"My love, you are enchanting\nto me beyond all belief.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity.", "§bGabriel Maul", "**Many Ink Stains cover the pages of this book, the penmanship very fine and thick** §0\n§0“I am Gabriel Maul, A student of Lilyana’s, I was asked to write down my thoughts of ‘Purity’, So, Here it Goes.\n\nI believe if you ask a single man or woman from each race what their thoughts of Purity is, What it is, who has it, E.c.t, You’ll get a list of different replies, , I believe Purity is something gifted to us by the Lord,\n\nSomething each, and every breathing, living being has, From Krug, The Malin, to Lady Lilyana, to a simple Guardsman, like myself, If all people have ‘Purity’ inside them.§0\n§0what are the questions?\n\n Do they enhance it? Do they bring out the light in themselves,§0\n§0or do they hide it under a cloak of darkness? §0\n§0There is a Thick line between ‘Good’ And Purity.\n\nA man that walks along the streets of an Oren city, giving food to the poor, doesn’t make them pure,§0\n§0For Purity, is much much deeper,  I believe Purity, is mercy, forgiveness, and Faith.\n\nrather it be in a god, or in your self, I’ve once met an elven man, who says he has never shed a  drop of blood, but has been brought to his knees many times, un braking his faith in the Lord,\n\ndespite being so beaten, That, is purity, or maybe It’s §0not..Maybe§0 Purity is something more, A Gift from the Aenguls.. or simple thought in one man’s mind. But no matter how you see it,\n\nNo matter who’s tongue it comes §0from..no§0 one can truly tell you what Purity is. A Dear Friend of mine, told me what he thought Purity was Being free from immortality, for when you’re pure, you’ll have no darkness He said.\n\nA Rather vague reply, but I simply nodded, Now, let me tell you what /I/ Truly think it is...\"“My Father was a noble man, for the ten years I knew him, he prayed to the Lord, and thanked the Creator for his life,\n\nbut by night, he slept with many, and lead his vessel to ‘impurity’, So in short, praying, loving the lord, acting as if you have faith, is not purity. For purity, is something else, it is being unmarked,\n\nIt is being an Untouched Vessel. It’s being able to push thru the darkness, without being lead on by it’s promises No love for gold, or heart for women should stop you from being pure.\n\nYou should be able to jump into a pool full of lust, and greed, and even death. But bed no more than your wife, spend no more than your own, and slay no innocent man,\n\nIf one can truly do this, if one can truly live thru life without being blinded by the darkness, then, Aren’t they pure? Maybe not..” **Ink drops would cover the rest of that page, as if Maul was going to say more, but went to the next page.** §0\n§0\n\n“If You have two (or more) eyes, breath your own breath, and have flesh, rather it be Green, black, or White, You have purity within §0you..The§0 option to use this purity is your own. So long as your will, is your own,\n\nthen you can embrace your purity, and let it shine like a light that weakens the dark, and blinds the faithless For you, and only you, can lead yourself into purity, No High elf King, No Orcish Rex, and no Graven Spook can tell you you are impure..\n\n For the choice is yours, and only yours,” §0\n\n“‘I am §0lost..broken§0, and unfixable,’ Something the Darkness will poke at you, and make you think to bend your will, and brake your faith, but worry §0not..there§0 is §0hope..If§0 you hurt the lives of innocent,\n\nbe it man or woman, Orc or Elf, §0Elder..Or§0 §0Youth..Then§0 free yourself..I say that anyone who is §0impure..and§0 can §0pure..because§0 why? Because, I have faith,\n\nI have faith that not only did the Lord gift us all with purity, but, also with Free §0will..One§0 small change in your §0life..Could§0 make the change, of everyone around you\n\nShine bright, Love all your  enemies, be loyal to your wives, and nothing. Can stop you, from being Pure..”§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Respiren", "§bOliver", "Wayward Druid,\nRespiren Nox,\n\nThe Founder\n\nIt is said that in ancient times, Respiren was blown to the shores of Aegis like a seed upon the wind, and what blossomed forth from him was the sprout of what we now know as the Druidic Order.\n\nHe was a traveler from a distant land, who brought to us the gifts to hear nature's song.\n\nHe began his quest in a shack in Laurelin, and quickly nature-lovers from all over began to flock to learn from him. It was this holy spot that grew into the first great grove, and the Order was born.\n\nUnfortunately, his teachings were disorganized, and without true purpose beyond revering nature and bolstering its strength.\n\nThen came the light of the Dawn Druid, Maiavel.", ""),
        StaticBook("treasureclue r", "§bSer Drake Lancefeld", "\"As you look past this box, know that our lost one's memory will never be forgotten..\n\n\"Go back to the beginning, my love.\"\n*Drake's signature is signed with love*", ""),
        StaticBook("hanky panky", "§bBjark Warghearth", "Visit me in Fi'Ceru at the back of the town.\n\n§sso we can do hanky panky", ""),
        StaticBook("Maiavel", "§bOliver", "Dawn Druid,\nMaiavel,\n\nThe Reformer\n\n---\n\nAfter the founding of the Order, we were without purpose or direction in our service to nature.\n\nWe were growing, but had no structure to support ourselves on, and began to collapse into unruly mobs and Druids unable to cope with their gifts wandering into the wilds to never be seen again.\n\nWe had entered the first dark age of Druidism, and as the dawn which is her namesake, it was the Druid Maiavel who saved us from this.\n\nMaiavel rallied the Druids and held them together. She gave us our hierarchy, our lore, our tenets, and officially cemented us as an Order. Though it was still primordial, we still use much of the framework she laid out to this day.\n\nShe standardized teaching and gave us purpose, and no longer were we in danger of collapsing under chaos.\n\nDuring this time, the Salmon Druid, Petyr, brought knowledge and faith to our order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Callax", "§bOliver", "Sostice Druid,\nCallax,\n\nThe Preserver\n\n---\n\nAfter Respiren, Maiavel, and Petyr had finally left us and became immortalized in history, the Order began to dwindle along with them.\n\nOur numbers gradually decreased until a point that it seemed as though our time had finally come to an end, to live on only in old tales.\n\nThere came a time when only a single Druid remained in the Order: The Solstice Druid, Callax, who alone brought the Order from its knees into a thriving culture once more, and continued to do so for at least two more times throughout history.\n\nHe taught many students, brought many Druids back from the depths of the forests, and performed acts, diplomatic or otherwise, that would secure our roots firmly in place once again.\n\nUnfortunately, he has fallen to infamy in recent history, so I ask you kindly:\n\nPlease do not vandilize his statue. He's still a historical figure.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to get girls", "§bKalameet", "{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI.. . ..\ndon't know how to", ""),
        StaticBook("treasure clue g", "§bSer Drake Lancefeld", "\"My feelings for you bloom like a garden of verdant flowers and flow like a rushing stream.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Aengul&Daemon", "§bEques Erwin Gerold", "The Aenguls are great race, just like Daemons, they are an ancient race with great power. Aenguls are a type of AenguDaemons. Not many Aenguls are known, only a few people have direct connections with the mortals. Only those that have truly shown\n\nthemselves to the mortals with their powers are true known Aenguls, though there are legends of many more! §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0NEXT PAGE: DAEMON\n\nLike Aenguls, Daemons are an ancient race with GREAT power,but they normally do not use it. Daemons are part of Aengudaemons. Daemons RARELY walk in the mortal worlds, usually choosing to appear to a mortal. There are not many Daemons that have presented\n\nthemselves to mortals.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0NEXT PAGE: LIST OF AENGULS AND DAEMONS\n\nAeriel, Care Taker of Souls, and Aengul of peace and love, Patron of the Ascended. Tahariae Aengul of Purity, patron of clerics. Yeu Rthuly, Aengul of Contentment and Compassion. Xan, Aengul of Order and Guardship, Patron of the Brotherhood Golden Lion.\n\nList of Daemons.§0\n§0Dragur, the daemon of knowledge, and creator of Dragaars and dragons, powerful god-like beings that seek to collect wisdom and information. Iblees,the corrupted, Iblees was the Daemon that wished to conquer Aegis and was defeated. He now\n\nhas risen once again, due to the races own curiosity of an ancient ruin in which he was being impriosoned, and threatens the races life in Athere. Metztli, the Daemon of Moon, and creator of the Kharajyr. Apohet,the Daemon of faith and ambition,and\n\ncreator of the Spiritual Plane that eventually was divided into the §0Elemental.Ancestral§0, and Immortal planes. Tayl, the Daemon Of Companionship, who would take the lives of the wicked, the good and everything in between if it meant rallying mortals\n\ntogether.§0\n§0I believe the Aenguls serve the Light, as the Daemon would do the complete opposite....§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0    Written by Erwin", ""),
        StaticBook("Petyr", "§bOliver", "Salmon Druid,\nPetyr,\n\nThe Dreamer\n\n---\n\nDuring the Age of Reformation and Reconstruction, in which Maiavel gained her fame for giving order to the Druids, the Druid Petyr did the same for knowledge.\n\nPetyr brought us the attunement ceremony, our library, and our vows, but didn't become historically famous until he began recieving visions from nature.\n\nHe became known as the Dreamer because of one particularly keen vision, which shook our fate enough that, in the old books, it is considered an entirely new era of history.\n\nIt was Petyr that first spoke of the Aspects, having seen them in his vision. An explination for our feats, our gifts, the song we hear.\n\nHe and Respiren gathered the Druids and told them of this discovery, and soon they were adopted as our official deities.\n\nUnfortunately, this 'golden age' only lasted so long, and it seemed, eventually, that the Order had died. Next came the Solstice Druid, Callax.", ""),
        StaticBook("Librarium Report", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "A report on the Grand Library of Sutica, formerly the Lubba Atheneum.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Curator Gallidron Elindrow.\n\nI am pleased to announce, that despite the derelict conditions that the former curator left the library in, I have brought about order and organization.§0\n§0\n§0After combing through the many, MANY donations to the library that had been\n\nand left to gather dust, I found a good number of tomes and novels that could make a delightful contribution to our collection. As such I have more than doubled our inventory within the sections of the Beastiary§0\n§0Religious writings§0\n§0Human history\n\nand mundane healing.§0\n§0\n§0As well I have added a spattering of books in the other sections of the library.§0\n§0\n§0I have also undertaken to increase the security of our books, given the rash of disapearances of tomes of all kinds\n\nacross Axios. It is a more cumbersome system, but the books won't simply vanish off the shelves anymore.§0\n§0\n§0I am of course endevoring to find more books of every kind to strengthen our selection. To that end I have begun speaking with the Enchantry in hopes\n\nthat they may have some books to trade.§0\n§0\n§0This concludes my report.§0\n§0\n§0~Gallidron Elindrow§0\n§0\n§0Curator of the Grand Library of Sutica", ""),
        StaticBook("Rorry's Mistake", "§bGalahiern Haludorn", "Rorry Hammerfist was an interesting kind of dwarf. He was obedient, bravehearted and headstrong. All qualities you would want in a Dwarf. But Rorry was naive! Far too naive! Once a prisoner was captured and he asked to be let go. And Rorry set him\n\nfree. He was shamed by all his fellow soldiers, espcially Duren Hammerfist, his captain. But far greater dangers were created by this mistake then either realised. For the prisoner which Rorry had freed was Gollum. And he would change life of Vailor as\n\nanyone knew it. Soon all races found themselves against war with Dark Elves. Arrows flew, swords clashed and Thor hit the dark elves with his hammer. Soon only Rorry was left against the dark lord, Voldemort. Rorry picked his wand up and shouted\n\nEXPELLIARMUS, and Voldemort was defeated. Rorry was a hero amongst all the lands, but everyone else was dead, thanks to Rorry's Mistake.\nThe End", ""),
        StaticBook("The Edict", "§bKarim Vayle", "The Crimson Edict\nAnd reasons you should join:\n\n1. We believe in equality. It doesn't matter what your race is, you're a potential member. That also means we don't tolerate slavery, so you've gotta help deal with that if we find any.\n\n2. We know you don't like necromancers, and we don't either. That also applies for any dark magic that screws with or hurts other people.\n\n3. We're more than just mercenaries. We're a thriving community made up of all kinds of people, including those who don't do much fighting. A good example of this would be the handsome and charming Head Bard, Karim Vayle.\n\n4. Almost-free lodgings! You need to be active and a contributing member, but other than that you don't have to pay a mina to stay!\n\n5. Loyalty. We're not gonna sell you out, mostly because of a life oath. That means you don't fuck us over either, or we're gonna hunt you down.", ""),
        StaticBook("On The Drui.", "§bGabriel Maul", "*The words would look a little finer, and less thicker then they did in the last reflection.* On the Drui', I was told to Write about my Thoughts on the Druid, then To Reflect on what I gather. I believe this is a wonderful near ending task for a Student,\n\nSo, Let us begin, Tailesin Was the Lynx Druid who spoke with me on the infomation I gathered, The Druid Serve under the Aspects, the Mother, and Father of Nature, Cerridwen And Cernunnos, I then asked them what they stood for,\n\nWhat Their meaning was, To Defend Nature, and Balance, They go from Grove to Grove, City to city, Curing Blight/Taint, They stride as the Defenders of Nature, and Balance, Keeping all things natrual as should be.\n\nTheir goal being at that, To Defend The Wild, From unatrual, Such as the Darkend Taint. How dose Tahariae see this? And Does this Somehow mix with Tahariae's goal? Well, HEre are my thoughts.\n\nIf their goal is to, Defend nature, Rather it be from a Crazed Halfling with a Wooden ladle, Or A Necromancer with an army of Undead, They are still Defending, The Natural side of things, and if, Like the Light, Nature is natrual,\n\nAren't they defending a part of the light? If we, as clerics are defending the people of The realm from Darkness, and we are pushing for a darkness free, pure life, Then we might, have a similar if not the same goal, no?\n\nThe Creator, 'Created' The realms, Nature, In a way their task is as our task, maybe masked under a different goal. Lilyana, In her own words spoke of how, our goals are all a like, even if they sound diffrent, they all lead down the same road.\n\nThat road, Being purity. I was asked to reflect what I think of Them, What I think we should do with them, should we help the Defenders of Nature? Or do we turn them away? What would Tah Do Exactly.\n\nI believe they are as Lily said, going down the same road we are, but they don't go out, and fight Undead, they defend their home, they defend the wild, from the Unatrual, If that unatrual is The Darkness, then so be it.\n\nSo, If Us, As Clerics, andthem as Drui put our task side by side, and took a deep look into §0it..We§0 all are working for purity, and we all, togehter could bring Tahariae's goal within the road a-head of us.\n\nSo let it be, Let the Drui' The Paladins, The Clerics, and The Ascended Come together, and lets bind together as one, to bring purity to all.", ""),
        StaticBook("A thin letter", "§bEques Erwin Gerold", "Dear Trade Princess,§0\n§0\n§0I've come to write to you pertaining to earning your tutelage of being a cleric.§0\n§0\n§0I believe that the dark creatures must be purged. People must be healed, yes, but it's better to stop the problem from its source; the\n\ncreatures that hurt others. I understand that some may be trapped in their condition, and I do feel sympathy for them, and I would like to help liberate them.§0\n§0\n§0To care and protect my loved ones, I believe that the path of the cleric is the best option\n\nfor me. I'd like to make it a better place for them by healing and cleansing the realm, so please consider my case.§0\n§0\n§0                     Sincerly,§0\n§0              Erwin Gerold", ""),
        StaticBook("Reaper", "TheDarkIsEternal", "Reaper\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Azalya Fray\n\nHe waits just ouside the dying candlelight\nsmirking, waiting for darkness\n\nhe hisses when the light hits his eyes\nSnarling, waiting for darkness\n\nHe stalks when there are no stars in the sky\n\nslinking in darkness\n\nwhen the candlelight dies, he's there \nprobing the darkness.\n\nIt is there, in the darkness, that he swims \nthroughout the mind, staring.\n\nIt is there, that he resides\nAdding to the darkness, growing\n\nAnd when all the light is extinguished\nhe makes his move\nand swallows up the wax that had been once a being.", ""),
        StaticBook("Helpful Hand", "§bDaveed Batler", "§0\n§0Daveed Batler Assistive Journal§0\n\nPerson One: Gray Kellian §0\n§0\n§0Helped by giving him my personal book.\n\nPerson 2 : Dymase §0\n§0Gave him a bag of sugar§0 to make cookies for his grandmother\n\nPerson 3:§0\n§0Moohissa Gave him a bag of sugar to bake a cake for a friend\n\nPerson 4: Duke§0\n§0Swept,Waxed,andMopped the §0boat...tiring\n\nPerson 5 : Guards§0\n§0Helped guard with the removale of an intruder.", ""),
        StaticBook("Marden", "§bDavid FeatherHeart", "He is the shadow in the light. He stalks his prey with the power of men. He is only named by those who fear him yet serve him. This man , no, beast is named Marden. \n                He is not a man of no goals though. He is brocken and seeks power in the\n\nislands of Vailor. He wants to sit on the throne of his lies in peace with his army of men. \n        He was once a man. Or more like one and not the wraps of villany that he is today. He lived on the ancient island of Kathersa. He live in fear of the worl\n\nd as the world feared him as well. As you can tell, this man was not of the usual. He was of the Guild of Marden. They lived upon the great moutain of God's peak and studied the art of war.The art of death. The art of insanity. At that time he was not nam\n\ned Marden. Then he was only a name that was hidden and despised by all. He trained thier with the guild along myself. He would train each day and by each day only his humanity drained in the hole of his thoughts. \n              Soon after our graduation h\n\ne and I (along with my brother) took the mighty boat , God's mass, to the islands of vailor. As we arrived I saw him look upon the land. I saw the greed in his eyes. The power in his fists. He was going to rule. I then saw a miracle happen. He smiled. But\n\nnot of happiness, no, but of greed once more.\n         He now plans in the shadows for no one knows his true name but I. He now only goes by Marden to represent his guild. I only serve him now along my dearest brother. \n             He now looks for follo\n\nwers to use. If you are in any way interested visit the lands of count Roswell nearby Felsen and find me. Then and only then will You be able to join.\n          This is a warning to all kingdoms. No. All of Vailor. Beware the power of Marden.", ""),
        StaticBook("My D-Tool", "TheNander", "*The book seems to have been printed in large quantities for the Dwarven Legion.*\n\nThis is my D-Tool. There are many like it, but this one is mine. My D-Tool is my best friend. It is my life. I must master it as I must master my life.\n\nMy D-Tool, without me, is useless. Without my D-Tool, I am useless. I must use my D-Tool true. I must use it better than my enemy who is trying to kill me. I must cut him before he cuts me. I will...\n\nMy D-Tool and I know that what counts in this war is not the enemies we decapitate, the noise of our brothers, or the holes we dig. We know that it is the hits that count. We will hit...\n\nMy D-Tool is Dwarven, even as I, because it is my life. Thus, I will learn it as a brother. I will learn its weaknesses, its strength, its parts, its accessories, its blade and its handle. I will keep my D-Tool sharp and ready, even as I am sharp and\n\nready. We will become part of each other. We will... \n\nBefore Yemekar, I swear this creed. My D-Tool and I are the defenders of my Kingdom. We are the masters of our enemy. We are the saviors of my life.\n\nSo be it, until victory is The Kingdom of Urguan's and there is no enemy, but peace!\n\n- Nalro Grayhammer", ""),
        StaticBook("To Mylas", "§bOld Courier Woman", "To: Mylas\nFrom: The Old Courier\n\n\nHere I am. Another day, another delivery to your doorstep. Once again, I find myself bringing this rusted helmet to you. This time, though, I also had to drag a large carpet along as well.\n\nFor the helmet --\nThis was the first thing the sender would see you wear every time you visited her. It'd fall over your eyes as you shuffeled, and was the last thing they'd see as you left them.\n\nThey looked for that rusty shine every day to see your approach.\n\nFor the carpet --\n\nNo matter how troubled their mind was, you always reassured them that at the very least, their carpets were all accounted for.\n\nYour humor and wit made their day and your laugh is something they miss dearly. They sit by the water's edge, listening to the familiar waves, hoping your laugh will travel along them from the shores of Vailor to their new home.\n\nNow that's out of the way. \n\nShould you find yourself returning these things as you did the first time, keep in mind the poor old woman who has to drag them back the very next day, hmm?\n\nDrag them back yourself, at least. Feel the weight of the carpet rolled up on your shoulder as you carry it along from Johannesburg to Sutica. It will seem heavier with each step.\n\nFocus on that weight for the entire trip until it becomes too painful to carry any longer. \n\nSomething once light and silly will feel like a searing ache.\n\nThat is the feeling in the heart of the one that asked me to deliver these things to you. \n\nI know a sorrowful, broken heart when I see one.\n\nSo, kindly...If a broken heart does not move you even slightly, at least think of the old broken back that will keep carrying these things to you day after day. \n\nCarry them back yourself if you must. For me. Please.\nGood day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finally Sa'vi", "§b???", "Dear Reader,§0\n§0\n§0This may have to do with them... Eet may not. Well anyway Aife needs to find her own way in this world... Away from everyone... This is her Sa'vi....§0\n§0\n§0Aife isn't planning to return.§0\n§0\n§0Aife loves Lilyana,\n\nGray, Thain, Archrim (Even if he has ugly beard), and Tepah. Ever that Kary guy. §0\n§0\n§0Mul'ta for the love and care yaw show Aife... Ever after own race tried tuu kill her. And other people... Aife sorry for trouble cause... Aife need to find own way...\n\nThis is finally sa'vi.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task", "§bEques Erwin Gerold", "Goodfellow: I've made a leather hat for him!\nFlavius: Provided food for him!\nJon Snowell: I helped him find a magic teacher!\nTristan: Made a enchantment for him! (Mind i din't take any of his minas)\nEllavorn: Made a fishing rod for him!", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Notes", "§bDaveed Batler", "§0\n§0Clerical Notes\n\n4th, 3rd§0\n§0\n§0PRotect and guide the Grey to a path of purity\n\n\n§0Daveed Batler-§0\n§0- Page Number 206-§0\n§0-Journal Number:7 Clericalism -§0\n§0\n§0\n\nDaveed sits down on the main square bench in Sutica, opening his leather bound notebook. He examines the pages thoroughly making sure he does not damage a single page from turning too quickly.\n\n He then stops on the page referencing to “The different color Lights of Tahariae” . §0\n§0\n§0“Exactly what I needed, Absolutely wonderous.” He says sighing with slight relief, reading the notes he had previously written from a past lesson,\n\nHe pulls out a remaining charcoal fragment  he kept buried in his pockets and began to add to what he had written. §0\n§0\n§0“The clerical mission and how our blessing helps us.”\n\nhe mumbles under his breath as he examines the page, tracing his fingers along the bottom of the words  while reading  for more information he could add, he then stops and taps the paper with the charcoal and begins writing.\n\nWhen I had first begun my path of clericalism, I was not a man I had wished to be. I was forgetful,sloth-like, and unkind to those around me.\n\n However the man that inspired me to always achieve my goal, Grey Kellian the Third; had offered me a chance to walk the brighter path of life.\n\n A path that guided me to being a better person, and a much more respectable man. Tahariae not only gives us a better life to live by his word but to prove ourselves worthy of his blessings.\n\nWith his blessing he grants those who have undergone connection a powerful tool to help us defend our brothers, sister, and the meek .\n\n With this powerful blessing those are given a color of light to reflect their nature and each color a different meaning Blue “Light of the Warrior”, Gold “Light of the Knight”, White “ Light of the Pure” and lastly Silver “Light of the Servant”.\n\n-Blue Light User: Users of this light, according to past notes seems to be the Warrior group. Charging in first to defend those who need it immediately and healing those wounded at the start of a battle.\n\nThis more than likely means they undergo more physical and mental practices to adjust to being such a wonderful task of first responders to a similar situation\n\n-Gold Light User: Users of the notes seems to be more brave and carry themselves with the utmost courage and respectability. They are the “Knights of the Light” this shows in them protecting loved ones with their blessing gifted from Tahariae\n\nto bring a desirable lifestyle to those they surround themselves with. And this shows in the way their personality is given off.\n\n-White Light User: Users of this are the wisest most,and  admirable clerics. They are as noted “Light of the Pure.” I don’t have very many notes on these clerics…..However, they keep\n\never burning lights lit, and those without light they give  a new beginning with their gifts.\n\n-Silver Light Users: Users of the Silver lights are classified “Light of the Servant.” They are by far the second most admirable light users. Considering they have a major focus on purging the darkness in the world,\n\nthey also are devoted to healing the people of the realm. However as noted it says that they are the most ‘ambiguous’ out of the three other users, however they are still dedicated nonetheless.\n\nDaveed then drops the remaining piece of charcoal onto the ground then pulls another from his pocket and smiles slightly, flipping the page over as he continues his writing.\n\nThough each color may represent a different aspect in a cleric's life, our mission is still the same.\n\n “ Shelter and protect thy brethren. Cannot stray from thy faith. Shall guide the lost. Shall not kill, harm, or spill the blood of the innocent. Abuse of thine gift and punishment shall fall to you.”\n\n In my experience so far, Tahariae has given us so much more than any being could ever wish for. §0\n§0 §0\n§0Daveed then stands folding the corner of the page where he had last written and closes it gently.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Nature of", "§bAlem'shun Vanguard", "Let me preface this with the simple fact this is just the ponderings, thoughts and ideas of an Elf none of it is fact more of possible ideas. First in conventional clerical teaching and thinking the idea of Monochromatics is rather simple.\n\nThe idea that Light is perfection and therefore also good and that the dark or darkness is the absolute idea of imperfection or is of a completely unnatural origin. Then there is everything in between often labeled as\n\n“They Grey” or neutrally imperfective by others. This grey area is where most of everything falls. Humans, animals, plants all for the most part fall into the grey. The darkness is generally considered to be filled with creations\n\nof false life or daemonicly influenced beings. Clerics are often times considered to be rather towards the side of perfection on the monochromatic scales and while this could be true let another view possibly influence future teachings.\n\nClerics by definition are regular people which are neutrally imperfect and therefore fall into the vast grey. I believe due to the nature of a connected cleric being a person infused with aengul power it is by very definition less perfect\n\nthan it was before. This means clerics by my own observations are not beacons of perfection or purity but are even closer to their brethren that serve daemons.  The clerical patron Aengul themself hates aengul daemon influence into\n\nthe mortal world. It tampers with the ideals of perfection and while Clerics are tools of great influence in destroying imperfection and on a whole shifting the monochromatic spectrum. It can not be denied that clerics due to there own creation are rather\n\ncontradictory and are inherently even less perfect and even more dark than a regular person.§0\n§0\n§0Now while clerics may be more dark than an ordinary person of the grey it by no means strikes them as evil doers.\n\nThis is a popular misconception that dark means bad light means good etc etc. Good and Evil have very little to do with perfection which is what the monochromatic scale measures.\n\nMeaning even if a cleric is darker than a regular person a cleric can still be a person who strives for the betterment of all and indeed the ideals of perfection.§0\n§0For instance let us look to the library Dragthar\n\nan institution that any and all can obtain information from. A institution which many believe to be of a good cause. The patron of this library is a daemon but this does not mean the library is an unholy order of pure evil bend\n\non the destruction of the planet and conquest of all people. Like mentioned earlier dark does not mean evil neither does light mean good. I believe clerics and all people who use the monochromatic scales need to understand these\n\ndifferences and begin to realize their full mission for purity not necessarily be a do gooder.", ""),
        StaticBook("Helping PeopleV1", "§bGray Kellian III", "§0My first person I helped was a girl named Elise. She was blind and looking to return her sight. So I brought her to Lily and Andriel to give her the gift of a lifetime§0\n§0(ZoruaSama)\n\nThe second person I helped was Alem to give a law test to Thain, which she passed yay!§0\n§0\n§0(seventhCircle)\n\nThe Third person I helped was a strange man on a horse who was looking to buy carrots. so I gatherd my hoes and went to the farm with him to get him carrots,§0\n§0\n§0He then tried to recruit me for Oren army.§0\n§0(no clue, Dexxsomething)\n\nThe forth was when I was walking to Oren. there was a lad looking for food, and I gave him the rest of mine to help him. He thanked me and blessed me before eating his meal happily§0\n§0(Mcthornz)\n\nThe last was a man looking to reunite with old friends, I knew whom he was looking for and allowed him to use my parrot Blue to reconnect with his old friends§0\n§0(tidemanno)", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Get Girls", "§bAmras Yeager", "How to get a girl.\n\nStep 1: If you haven't talked to her before the ask if she is new. If she says no I'm not new or something along the lines of that then you say \"Hmm I don't know how I wouldn't notice such a pretty face.\n\nStep 1 B: If she says that she is new then say \"Good 'cause I don't know how I would've missed such a pretty face.\n\nStep 2: Figure out if she has any problems like if she is sad because of something. Then comfort her and tell her it's alright.\n\nStep 3: Figure out what she likes and dislikes. This step might be time consuming but if you really want that girl it's worth it. Usually offering them cake is good 'cause a lot of people like cake.\n\nStep 4: Ask her on a date, stand up straight or she might not think well of you and think that you are a wimp. If she does accept then remember the things that she stresses with and give her good solutions to her problems and treat her to the things she\n\nlikes. Then continue until you have been on a few dates with her then you can propose to her. Good Luck!\n\n\nAuthor - Amras Yeager\n\nElsiln Athri and Katar Aureon help create this book.\n\nWARNING: \n\nMay not always work some girls are different!", ""),
        StaticBook("Forbidden Tome", "§bDruid", "*A dusty, unlabeled tome. It bears more weight than most.*\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/jlh46vp\n\n(mirror, just in case)\n\nhttp://bit.ly/2fdrcv3", ""),
        StaticBook("Karlors' Card", "§bKarlor Ludecke", "===Heil Vandoria===\n\nThe business card of one Doctor Karlor Ludecke, Ph.d. \n\nReich Minister of Truth and Enlightenment in the name of the Kaiser and the Kaisereich. \n\nMember of the Covenent of Stahl\n==================", ""),
