        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*A quick, panic-scrawled message is wrote here, on repeat.*§0\n§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n\nRemember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone§0\n§0Remember them or they're gone\n\nRemember them or they're gone§0\n§0\n§0*The message continues to be repeated, over and over, seeming to hold only personal value.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Ring", "§bKyral Rilann", "The following is from myself, Kyral, and my time spent meditating in a fairy circle.\n\nThese are the three days of this task.\n\nDay one\n\nSitting  in the tree when the all familiar humming noises filled my senses, it felt overwhelming, but I tried and tried to stay in as long as I could, focusing on the humming for as long as I could. Was I incomfortable? or\n\nwas it just the noise getting to me? At least this was my first time in, I had plenty of time to get used to such noises.\n\nI figure it will be easier the more I go in, but I need to pace myself, I feel a woman could go a little crazy if left inside that\n\nFairy ring for far too long. Did I mention it was hard resisting the urge to dance? I never dance and I felt myself wanting to do it more and more.\n\nI don't like dancing.\n\nDay two\n\nI easily entered the circle, finding it much easier then the last to meditate with my eyes closed. It was more amazing to focus in the humming I heard with my other senses, a whole new experience that left me more amazed at\n\nthis mystical ring, I can't comprehend the things I heard, but I think its the forest.. doing something.\n\nAs for leaving the circle, I left with only slight issues, having to get back in for this book, but I looked around the whole grove for signs of\n\npeople, and I skipped around the fairy circle.\n\nIt was amazing I felt, relieved. I hated to dance but it was just skipping, and I felt so much better.\n\nDay three\n\nThis day was one of the more amazing, I meditated after having had a long talk with one of my former Scions, talking about what I did and redemption. Having been calmed by that chat, I walked back into the fairy ring.\n\nI was not ready and i did not expect to hear what I did. It was like the Pulse of the realm was guiding itself to me, I felt everything moving and coming towards me, Meditating was hard, but i managed to keep it going, remembering my times as a Cleric and\n\nMage to keep me going, to focus on one of those feelings, one of those pulses of life.\n\nI almost did it, but I felt my thoughts filling my mind with crazy reasoning, and I needed to get out. This wasn't a safe day to be inside the circle. I feel that I am\n\ngetting closer to understanding the way the realm works, but I might be wrong, this Fairy circle continues to bring new and new things to me to realize, that the realm is forever changing.\n\nI skipped around the circle again, and stopped it at that.\n\nThis would be my final day, but I expect to be asked to meditate here from time to time.\n\n*The following pages\nseem to be sketches slid into the book*\n\n*A large Rainbow tree seems to be cut by a figure in this one, the top half of this page\ndepicts this.\n\nWhile the lower half depicts the tree igniting, leaving scrambled markings on the ground /#&!(@/ *\n\n*Another sketch seems to be the apple, blue in color being picked from the still standing rainbow tree, a hand extending to it as if this was a panel by panel sketch. but it stops there.*", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol I", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 1\nby Kalenz Uradir\n\nIn elven grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one instead of placing an adjective before a noun it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\n\nKarin'ayla - Goodmorning\nKer'ayla - Goodnight\nVan'ayla - Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjective describing it. Noun and adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\n\nOther important words for the beginner in elven include race names:\n\nMali - Elf\nUruk - Orc\nValah - Human\nBortu - Dwarf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\nMali'aheral - High Elf\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures the suffix tali- may be used. This word most directly means 'part of'.\n\nTali'uruk - Goblin (Lit. Part Orc)\nTali'valah - Halfling (Lit. Part Human)\n\nOther basic phrases include exclamations including:\n\nAyla - Good\nSul'leyun - Brilliant (Lit. Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol II", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 2\n by Kalenz Uradir\n\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in elven are as follows: \n\nKae - Me \nLae - Him/He \nNae - You \nLye - We - Used to speak of elves, people or the world. \nHae - Her/She\n\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well). \n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning elven include basic affixes. These affixes may b\n\n added to create further detail or form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\n\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe. \n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness. \nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholars. For example: Ah'Lucion.\n\nfi- - New or anew.\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. For example: Cer'Silir.\n-ante (-nte) - Last \n-ento (-nto) - Next \n-onn - From or born. \nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive. \n-ir - Designates purpose of someone or something. \n-sae - The spreading, development or management. \n-ii - Diminutive form. For example: Malii, meaning little elf.\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Achient elves\n\nA long time ago, before written history, the world was inhabited by a single race known now as the achient elves and were the first ofthe Aegis, the build marvels in what is now niben bay\n\nThe achient elves built cities that are now considerd marvels and large statues of birds, lions, and also dragons, and it should be noted the elves learned how to befriend dragons aswell.\n\nthey knew the friendship between them was strong and so the dragons tought them the basics of what is know nowdays as magic, they also taught them on how to store energy within crystals and use them to power cities and give them light\n\nEventually a dragon by the name of Akron took power of the empire that had previously been formed by the elves and dragons. Akron hated the other newly formed races including the elves and so he started creating large crystals and using them for war\n\nbut there were dragons who did not agree with him and stood in the way of his plans, and so Akron called upon the forces of Iblees\nHe then used this power to slowly drain the life of the other dragons. and then the dragons seeing the inevitable end, us\n\ntheir remaining strength to close the gate to the nether that supplied Akrons Evil power. They died in the progress of closing the portal. The few dragons remaining turned them selves to stone waiting to one day be awoken\n\nWith the dragons out of the way Akron started the inslavement of the other races and with that came the great war witch lasted decades.\nFinnaly Akron was one day defeated and with that the humans took control of the crystals of power the dragon once ow\n\nThe human eventually became mad with power and started the genocide of the Anchient elves and burnt their cities to the ground, few managed to escape, and those few are now the ancestors of the current elven peoples\n\nAnd thus ended the Anchient elves", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\n\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\n\n       Lesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\n\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\n\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\n\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\n\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallnes\n\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\n\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treat\n\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\n\n        Lesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\n\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the c\n\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\n\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\n\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\n\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\n\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\n\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\n\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\n\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\n\n      Lesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\n\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\n\n      Lesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and\n\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\n\n you can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\n\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\n\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\n\n       Lesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers\n\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate\n\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and ma\n\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\n\ntaken with all seriousness.\n\n       Lesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\n\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\n\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\n\n     Lesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf\n\n this offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\n\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\n\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\n\n        Conclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\n\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\n\n         A Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfli\n\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shun", "§bTristanm1", "The Shun\nInscribed by Dawn Druid Maiavel\n\nThe Great Druid can impose a strong, nonviolent sanction upon those who have offended the circle. All must shun someone placed under the shun; no druid in the circle will aid, speak to, or associate with the target of the shun. When an entire town or\n\nvillage suffers the shun, no druid may enter that area or speak to or aid any resident. Some druidic allies volunteer to follow the custom of the shun as well.\nThe great druid has the right to pronounce a shun on any druid in the circle.  A shun also can\n\nnondruids, whole communities, or druids visiting from other domains (except the Grand Druid and personal servants), to demonstrate the circle's displeasure. \nTo pronounce the shun, the great druid stands up during a moot and  announces to the group the\n\nreasons to impose the shun. Then the subject of the shun--if present--answers the accusations before the assembly. Finally, the High Council of the Moot votes on the matter openly, usually at sunset. If a majority of the council votes in favor of the shun\n\n, it passes. If not, the great druid should start keeping an eye on the circle's archdruids--the opposition to the shun likely reflects an impending challenge. \nA shun punishes a druid for violating the tenets of the druidic order or reprimands a\n\ncharacter whose actions, while within the bounds of the druidic ethos, nevertheless were contrary to the Order's interests. A shun generally lasts 10 summers. However, the inner circle can vote to lift a shun early or (once the time is up) to extend it.\n\nThe shunning does not extend outside the domain, so shunned druids usually choose to go into exile--the result the great druid probably intended in the first place.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Achient elves\n\nA long time ago, before written history, the world was inhabited by a single race known now as the achient elves and were the first ofthe Aegis, the build marvels in what is now niben bay\n\nThe achient elves built cities that are now considerd marvels and large statues of birds, lions, and also dragons, and it should be noted the elves learned how to befriend dragons aswell.\n\nthey knew the friendship between them was strong and so the dragons tought them the basics of what is know nowdays as magic, they also taught them on how to store energy within crystals and use them to power cities and give them light\n\nEventually a dragon by the name of Akron took power of the empire that had previously been formed by the elves and dragons. Akron hated the other newly formed races including the elves and so he started creating large crystals and using them for war\n\nbut there were dragons who did not agree with him and stood in the way of his plans, and so Akron called upon the forces of Iblees\nHe then used this power to slowly drain the life of the other dragons. and then the dragons seeing the inevitable end, used\n\ntheir remaining strength to close the gate to the nether that supplied Akrons Evil power. They died in the progress of closing the portal. The few dragons remaining turned them selves to stone waiting to one day be awoken\n\nWith the dragons out of the way Akron started the inslavement of the other races and with that came the great war witch lasted decades.\nFinnaly Akron was one day defeated and with that the humans took control of the crystals of power the dragon once owned\n\nThe human eventually became mad with power and started the genocide of the Anchient elves and burnt their cities to the ground, few managed to escape, and those few are now the ancestors of the current elven peoples\n\nAnd thus ended the Anchient elves", ""),
        StaticBook("Laethisian Times", "§bOrias", "The Laethisian              Period\n----------------Penned by Orias\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    Now I shall be brief in my forenote, as I have much to account for in very little space, but know this. These accounts are taken from an active\n\nparticapant of this period, I shall hope to avoid any biases or discrepencies in recounting the tales, but with such complexity and vastness I may fall to some. If it has not been made self evident, this tome shall cover everything from the rise of\n\nLaethis to what may be considered modern day.\n----------------\n\n         Ch. 1\nThe Ascension     & The Betrayal\n\n--------------Note; This may be perhaps my most hazy recollection.\n\nTo begin..\n\nMany years following, the assassination of Vydra and Avern's rule under Martial Law, a perhaps unifying or restoring figure emerged as Sohaer.\n\nThis figure came to be known as Laethis Izalith. \n\nHis first years were a budding spring in terms of what a leader could hope for. Relations flourished, and the rebellious Kalenz\nUradir had been killed.\n\n  While it was a humble peace, it did not last, as most tend to do. Laethis morphed into a vile mongrel with his newfound power. \n\n  The Triumvirate established in this reign of terror proved just as sinister. Let it be known that both\n\nContinued..\n\nparties played an equal role in the slaughters and betrayal to our people.\n\nSoon after, Laethis was killed off by unknown conspirators. And perhaps much like\n\nvalah do, a new Izalith assumed himself as our leader.\n\nKalameet was his name, and while his rule is recorded as being a light one It is important to note his abolishment of the Triumvirate. This\n\nwould later set the stage for a coming imperialism in our ruling, one without democracy or representation.\n----------------\n    Chapter 2\n\nThe Weary and The Damned.\n\n--------------\n\nNote; I shall continue my concise and neat format, although if you wish for a more detailed account, I shall be scribed so soon.\n\n  In the wake of an era dominated by the Izaliths, a new\nfigurehead, not\n\nprompted by true or lawful authority. Iatrilemar Elervathar  rose to prominent power.\n\n Iat. or how I shall abbreviate his dully long name, sought to maintain unity coupled with reformation of ties burned in the past\n\nHe was not a true Sohaer no, but rather the Maheral whom reigned as a beacon of hope for some decades.\n\n  Though this was all well and good, a new and true leader had to emerge. Coming from an Anti-mage\n\nheritage, the mali known as Taeleh and his band of other conglomerates took the helm in our goverment.\n\n  Reformations to the law were made, tolerance was somewhat maintained despite\n\nTaeleh's past convictions. Iat still maintaned some prominence with his figure, but it was truly Taeleh that had governed the land.\n\nThe Silluminir (Guardsforce or Haelun'or) were albiet abolished\n\nand replaced by the mage hunters known as The Golden Owl. Who were essentially Taeleh's puppets to enforce his will.\n\nThe previous home of all Aheral in Vailor, The Citadel saw a similar fate as the Sillumir\n\nin being abandoned and replaced by a cihi Taeleh constructed, Fi'Ceru.\n----------------    Chapter 3\n\nThe Continuation of Purity (Perhaps.)\n\n--------------\n\n  Taeleh's reign did last perhaps a decade or more, but as most grand reformers see. Opposition came quick, and it came in multtide. The first election was won, but the second against Avern was lost.\n\n  Avern has still started quite recently, but that has not halted her in revision. The Sohaer has been brought back along with small law changes.\n\n  It is during the youth of her rule that a new appointment seen\n\ncontroversial decision. Iat, the long reigning Maheral had chosen...\n\nLaethis Izalith to succeed him. It has come to be the focal point of politics now, and is debated currently. Though to clarify\n\nyou may wonder, what happened to Laethis after his exile and killing?\nIt can be summarized like so, Laethis fled after his supposed killing and then founded a new cihi to rival Haelun'or. the Sanctuary.\n\nTo conclude...\n\nIt seems we are in the stiffening winter and conclusion of the Laethisian Period, however with a new Maheral and a new Sohaer.. The path of the Mali'Thill is unclear once more.\n\nThe End.\n\nBy \n\nOrias\n\nThe Dutifull scribe of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("Killing Yourself", "§bArchembalt", "Effective Ways of \nCommitting Suicide\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     Perhaps you have taken this tome because you are generally a curious individual, or maybe you've considered that life is not worth living. If the latter is your case, I am\n\n-terribly sorry that not everything has been too satisfactory throughout your period of existence. \n\n   Nonetheless, everyone reserves the right to end their lives. I am here now to convey effective methods with which one could swiftly end\n\n-their life.\n\n        Sections\n=+------<>-------+=\n\nI. The Natural Way\n\nII. Poisons and Potions\n\nIII. Death, Accompanied with Solace\n\n   The Natural Way\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Jumping off a cliff. Make sure that you are not falling into a sea. It is only more painful. Ensure that the surface is hard, or that there are stone crags at the bottom. Death will surely occur.\n\n2. Poisonous mushrooms. Eat an abundance. Fever, convulsing, vomiting, then succinct death. The more you take, the quicker you will reach the end. Find a mushroom with a white stalk, red head, and with white spots on its surface.\n\n3. Drowning. Tie a heavy rock to your feet and hop into a pool, river, ocean, et cetera. There is no escape. The struggle won't last too long. There will be a burning sensation, and shock will begin to take place. Not as swift, but effective enough.\n\n4. Have someone twist your head about and snap your neck. Ensure your friend/assailant is strong. Pay them some money to kill you. Tell them to make it quick. A quick severing of the spine should bring you to death in no time.\n\n5. Beheading. Get a trusted friend or hire someone with minas. Their blade should be sharpened, their grip confident, and they must be considerably strong. One swipe will separate your head from your body, if everything has been planned out well.\n\n6. Hanging. Slightly more painful, but depends on the height from which you jump. Tie a noose around your neck and then to a tree branch. Stand on the tree branch, and make sure that you are an apt height from the ground. Jump. The noose should constrict-\n\n-around your neck finely and perhaps crush your larynx in no time, cutting off your access to a considerable supply of air. In some cases, your spine will snap. This method is more well-known.\n\n7. Arbalest bolt to the temple. Acquire someone strong and able to properly load the heavy war bow known as an arbalest. The piercing power of this brutal weapon will easily end your life. Instruct them to point it at your temple (side of  your head) and-\n\n-stand around two meters away from you when firing. Almost as quick as beheading.\n\n8. Explosion. Perhaps a tad harder to set up. A stick of dynamite will do, maybe two. Strap it to your upper chest, preferably to the sternum. You may make the fuse as short as you wish. Execute this out in a field, or perhaps run into a room of -\n\n- individuals you absolutely despise, and light the fuse. A last 'hurrah' before you pass on. Death by explosion is nearly instant. Dynamite is also not too hard to get your hands on.\n\n9. Exsanguination. Slitting your forearm. Acquire a knife or something especially sharp. Draw the blade up the inside of your forearm all the way to your wristline. The cut does not have to be too deep. Ensure the severing of multiple veins. The result\n\n-will be extreme loss of blood. Your heart will slow and your mind will be deprived of necessary fluids. Death is soon to occur.\n\n10. Thanhium dust. Thanhium, surprisingly, is not too hard to get a hold of. In order to execute this suicide method properly, procure a decent-sized chunk of thanhium. Begin to break it down in order to release the toxic dust. Begin to inhale, and do -\n\n- not stop. You will begin to feel cold, and more than likely break into a sweat. The toxic dust will become overbearing and your mind will soon 'shut off'.\n\n  Poisons and Potions\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Overdose on sleeping potions. If one could request an abundance of sleeping potions, this method of suicide would be painless and peaceful. You would quickly fall into a deep sleep, -\n\n- but never to awake.\n\n2. Nether's Wrath. An incredibly harmful potion, scalding hot and incredibly bright. Pour into the eyes. Painful at first, but the concoction will sear through the flesh of your eyes and promptly penetrate to strike at your brain, frying it to a crisp, w-\n\n- ith this method only taking less than ten seconds once the potion is acquired.\n\n3. Greater Drake's Poison. Overdose on this, and you will overheat in no time. Your lips will become parched, your stomach aflame, and soon your mind will not be able to register much. Death is guaranteed with this.\n\n4. Blissfoil. Consume an abundance of this flower, or drink the potion. You will gradually lose the ability to properly move your arms or leg as you eat them, until your entire body is paralyzed. At this point, your brain cannot register\n\n-any pain or sensation, and once this point has been reached, you will die.\n\n5. Alchemist's Fire. It will melt the flesh off of your bone. Ask someone to throw it upon you and aim for the head or upper torso. More effective than regularly setting yourself on fire.\n\n6. Frost Oil. Primarily used as a coolant for clothing, it may also be applied to weapons. Drink it instead. Overdose will work in a similar way to blissfoil. Your body will be overcome with the cold, and your mind too will freeze. Death is guaranteed.\n\n7. Basilisk venom. When extracted and taken in large amounts, will cause swift death. Straightforward. This method can be applied with a wide array of venomous snakes and beasts.\n\nDeath, Accompanied by Solace\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     It is up to the one committing suicide to determine whether or not they wish to settle personal qualms with other individuals, or if they do not wish for their ending to be peaceful.\n\nTheir reasons are their own. \n\n    Take some time to truly reflect on your life, the decisions you have taken, and consider if everything has been truly settled. If reflecting back on your life has become too painful, then do not feel the need to such.\n\n    If one would prefer an even more peaceful ending, however, a prime way of committing suicide would be by enjoying whatever you can before you take your life. Have a drink, eat whatever food you'd like, or take a nice nap. Maybe poison your drink so -\n\n- the pain will be alleviated even further. \n\n    There are a multitude of ways in which one may kill themselves, and this tome only details a few of those. Thank you for reading, and I hope you find this information useful.\n\n-Written by Archibald Vallero (alias: Archembalt)\n\n           -1546", ""),
        StaticBook("Wizardry", "§bAugustus d'Amaury", "Petition for Botan to be court wizard\n\n-Alexander of Lorraine\n\n-Dima Malinov\n\n-Liriel Fisher\n\n-Nemir\n\n-Aebek\n\n-Selrik Lance\n\n-Vargen Vallberg\n\n-Lexa Green\n\n-Rozaliya Malinov\n\n-Hendrik Fisher\n\n-Nikolai J. Ruhnsted\n\n-Krug\n\n-Victor Duval\n\nI, Augustus d'Amaury, accept Botan the Shrewd to be the Court Wizard of the Lorraine, alongside Cerberus.", ""),
        StaticBook("!!Attention!!", "§bTarien Arvius", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon IV - A Warning\nTo the Spellcrafter Archon,\nI hope this message reaches you in time. We were deceived, the Seal was a false lead, the Radiant Man, or as he is truly called, the aengul Garzardiel, had\n\nhis own agenda all along, and Rivel faces imminent attack and possibly annihilation.\nMost of the Spellcrafters in the task force are fully under Garzardiel’s sway, mere puppets to his will. I have broken free of his influence and escaped but in\n\nturn have lost both my powers from him and my skill with the Arcane. I fear how many of my decisions in the past months have been acts based not on my own judgement but on his influence!\nWhen we opened the Hall we found it littered with\n\nskeletal corpses: the Forgotten Dwarves were wiped out by a civil war: the ruling caste trying in desperation to give the Seal enough fuel to defeat the Ravager, and the people fighting back. It seems too that the ruling caste won the war and the death\n\nsimply fueled the Seal further. The city was also filled with hundreds of war constructs designed for raiding the surface for harvesting more souls: I suppose when you’ve enacted a near total genocide on your own people in the name of\n\nsurvival the deaths of a few hundred surface dwellers aren’t going to bother you. It seems these constructs wiped out the surviving Forgotten Dwarves.\nAs for the Seal, the machine itself is complete, but damaged: we\n\nsuspect the damage allowed vengeful souls to leak out and possess the constructs, wiping out the surviving dwarves. Garzardiel revealed that the goal of the Forgotten Dwarves was impossible: the Seal could never hold enough souls to\n\ntrap the Ravager, which begs the question, whatever does he want it for?\nOnce he had access to the Seal Garzardiel took control of the constructs and ordered the elimination of all loose ends, all who knew about the Seal.\n\nThat means the Spellcrafters of our company that were not fully under his sway and Rivel itself. I attempted to conceal myself, but without my arcane powers it was most difficult. The last I saw of Garzardiel was him headed to the Seal Chamber\n\nitself, a writhing mongoose held by the neck in his grip. After that I was forced to flee the city, and as I left I realised the direness of our situation.\nThe majority of soul harvesting constructs left for Rivel hours ago: I know not how long\n\nyou have to formulate a defence against their oncoming assault on the walls.\nI will find the keys and reseal this Hall. My last act will be to return the keys to their hiding places. I don’t know what Garzardiel really wanted to trap in\n\nthat machine, but Urguan’s Hall must never again be found.\n- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("FSOE Pt. 1", "§bDavid Enrique", "=-----------------------------------=\n\n         Fifty Shades\n           \n             Of\n\n           Enrique\n\n\n=-----------------------------------=\n\nAny other day. That's what David expected it to be in the land of Athera, during the year 1500 as he set off on a stroll down the streets of Salvus. It was the old Salvus! Where people lived.. Relatively happily with the small, gradually growing -\n\n - population of Salvus. People never knew what the future of this republic would be, but ultimately in the present time, things don't seem too well. But change is always good! But this is not a propoganda book, or one on the history of Salvus! This.. -\n\n- tells a greater story. The story of David Enrique's erotic day in Salvus. Once again, he had no knowledge of what was to happen on that day, but it was definitely going to be an exciting, eventful one. He approached the tavern, where Linda was -\n\n- brewing and bartending peacefully and idly. But suddenly.. Her clothes. Her clothes? The light breeze from outside seemed to begin to pick up.. And h- They're off! Her clothes simply ripped off, right away! \"David! DAVID!\" A voice ringed -\n\n- repeatively in his head as he stared intently at Linda, her cheeks growing a rosy red colour. \"DAVID!\" Was screeched one more time, as he shook his head back and forth, and snapped back to reality. He was in fact still in the tavern, but Linda -\n\n- was fully clothed, and  they weren't alone. \"David!\" Linda growled out, with a hint of anger in her tone. \"You still owe me money, better get me it soon.\" David silently nodded, still taken aback. His imagination usually doesn't go crazy -\n\n- like that, so he was quite suprised by his own actions! He disregards it, swinging around to seat himself beside the legend.. Kolohe Finn. \".. Er. Kolohe. What are you doing here? I usually.. /Never/ see you just in the Salvus tavern.\" -\n\n- \"Oh.\" He responded, bobbing his head up and down idly. \"I simply was here to see Luxeanna, we've been growing quite close lately, have you heard?\" He says this with a sly smirk splaying across his face, indefinitely implying something. -\n\n- As Luxeanna swung the door open to the tavern, David's eyes just seemed.. instinctively glued to her exposed thighs. He knew this wasn't right, as he should take some time from relationships, as he just -\n\n- got out of a suicidal, depressed state from his last divorce. But there was something about Luxeanna. The exposed thighs.. The.. Exposed thighs? The exposed thighs.. and the.. exposed.. thighs. He just really had some -\n\n- weird ass fetish for thighs, it seems! Ah, David, you were always a strange one. As David silently had some.. even increasingly stranger thoughts go through his head, Kolohe and Luxeanna conversed until -\n\n- he was snapped out of it by non-other than Luxeanna herself. \"David! How have you been doing. We haven't talked much lately.\" A wry grin came across her face, as she leaned forward into the table, which made her dress, willingly or unwillingly, -\n\n- slip down her shoulder a tad, causing her to show off her cleavage a bit, whether if she was meaning to or not, David was also drawn to that. \"Uhm.. Good, good!\" Today was a special day, as Luxeanna cut right to the chase. -\n\n- \"Well.. I actually need a bit of help in the Bard's Guild.. Can you come with me?\" She gestures her hand towards herself, hopping up to her feet, and pacing out of the tavern. Kolohe jaw hangs wide open as he stares at David slither out of -\n\n- his chair and trail behind her, him simply watching in disbelief. Luxeanna delivered her promise, taking him inside the Bard's Guild building. \"So.. What did you need help wi- WHA!\" David exclaimed, as Luxeanna abruptly pinned him to the wall. -\n\n- \"I needed you..\" She whispered into his left ear, giving a dramatic pause before continuing with her sentence. \"For some.. experiments.\" She giggled at her own statement, poking her tongue through her closed lips, and beginning to trail it up and down -\n\n- the side of his head. David simply groans in anticipation in response to her, and in impatience, rolls around to switch their positions now pushing her up against the wall. He reaches behind her, firmly grasping a handful of her hair, and -\n\n- yanking it back to get better access to her lips, which he immediately locks and slips his tongue inside, passionately and thoroughly kissing. \"Mm.. Luxeanna..\" He groaned into her mouth. She snickered against his lips, and moaned -\n\n- back in response. \"Oh.. Davi-\" She cut off her own words, wriggling her head away from his grip, and drawing her head back. \"Times up! Thanks for the experiment, David.\" She immediately shoves him out of the building, -\n\n- leaving David distraught, and with a look of genuine confusion across his features. \"Wait, what!\" He yelled out, hopping up to his feet. But his yelling effort was to no avail, as she ignored him, and went deeper inside the building.\n-\n\n- David emits an expasperated sigh, now pivoting around on his back heel, and departing back down the road, striding down the stone bricks. But then.. Another female.. Is that.. Was it.. It was.. Oh.. My creator.. What a beauty.. -\n\n- Oh. It was simply Tyrell Blavier and Roopak, conversing like regular black folk. \"Oh, hello you two.\" David nods  towards them in a friendly manner, before continuing along the stone path that would set his destiny.. into a woman's pants. -\n\n- Well, not really... For now. He casually strolled into the town square, where he saw Arenai Garense. He took immediate interest in her, so he paced up to the unsuspecting woman, and nonchalantly locked their lips. -\n\n- she.. Suprisingly smiled? And took hold of his hand, leading her to her inn room. They had rough fucking sex, had a baby named Ryder, and were planned to get married. Instead, she broke up with him in 1517, and -\n\n- fucked Glacio, which David was furious about. Even more so, he killed her afterwards, leaving his child in his hands. He didn't mind the taking care of the child part, that would just make him a horrible person. So.. This is more like.. 'The fifteen -\n\n- Year Erotic Story'.. And.. That's the story. David also got married six times in that duration of time.. So it wasn't really.. You know.. One marriage. It was.. M- Okay. I don't know why I am continously rambling on about this. That's the story, so -\n\n- you fucking happy? Thank you. Also, David wanked furiously somewhere in that timeline.. So. That's erotic too.\n\n--------------------------------------\n\n\n           THE\n\n\n           END\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------\n\n*A rough, bolded sketch up Luxeanna completely nude is drawn on the back cover of the book, a suggesting a and wry smirk splaying on her face, both of her hands however, shielding her breasts and privates. You pervert.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Rasputin", "§bAbram Votyakov", "There lived a certain man, in Oren long ago.\n\nHe was big and strong, in his eyes a flaming glow.\n\nMost people looked at him, with terror and with fear.\n\nBut to Petrus chicks, he was such a lovely dear.\n\nHe could preach the canon like a preacher, full of ecstacy and fire.\n\nBut, he also was the kind of teacher\nWomen would desire\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's greatest love machine!\n\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\n\nHe ruled the Oren land, and never mind the king.\n\nBut the kasochok he danced really wunderbar.\n\nIn all affairs of state, he was the man to please.\n\nBut he was real great when he had a girl to squeeze.\n\nFor the queen, he was no wheeler dealer\n\nThough she'd heard the things he'd done\n\nShe believed he was a hole healer,\n\nWho would heal her son.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! Oren's greatest love machine.\n\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\n\nBut when his drinking, and lusting, and his hunger for power became known to more and more people, the demands to do something about this outrageous man became louder and louder.\n\n\"This man's just got to go!\"\nDeclared his enemies.\n\nBut the ladies begged,\n\"Don't you try to do it, please.\"\n\nNo doubt this Rasputin, had lots of hidden charms.\n\nThough he was a brute, they just fell into his arms.\n\nThen, one night some men of higher standing set a trap, they're not to blame.\n\n\"Come to visit us\" they kept demanding, and he really came.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey put some poison into his wine.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! \nOren's greatest love machine!\n\nHe drank it all and he said \"I feel fine!\"\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey didn't quit, they wanted his head.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's Greatest love machine!\n\nAnd so they shot him 'till he was dead!\n\nOh, those Oreners...", ""),
