        StaticBook("Human History v1", "§bBishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity, From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume I: Introduction and The First Age of Kings\n\nAuthor's Note: The states of the modern realm were formed in a time of civic unrest caused by militarized cultural differe\n\nwithin the Fourth Empire. However, while these nations differ in culture, they retain a simple heritage of governing states, so that the modern man may understand the liegestate to which he pays homage. While my cousin Cordal Winter sought to chronicle\n\nthe timeline of humanity and my fellow writer Procopius sought to color them with his heart, I seek to establish a coherent and continuous history connecting the modern nations to those of the past, and documenting the states through which humanity\n\nprogressed, to allow the modern man to draw parallels between this time and the times before.\n\n-Edward Winter II\n\nThe First Age of Kings\n600s-mid 1300s\nOn the Continent of Aegis and Asulon\nKings from the houses of Perea, Sheffield, Tarus, Horen, Marius, de Nurem\nAlso known as: Aegisian Ages, the First Unrest\n\nIn the first years of recorded histor\n\nformed by the conquering lords of the House Horen, who united many smaller sovereign feudatories into one nation. The last reigning king from the first regnal dynasty was King Daniel Horen, whose seneschal took the crown in a coup, and styled himself King\n\nPampo Perea. Upon his death, his own seneschal, King Edmund Sheffield, took power. King Edmund was then corrupted by the Undead and tried to eat the flesh of his wife and himself died. He was succeeded by his son, King Enor Sheffield.\n\nThe Sheffield\n\nDynasty was fraught with inaction and sloth, and in a coup known as the Phoenix Rebellion, Zibaen Vivayean and Eze'kiel Tarus split from the kingdom and formed their own, called Renatus, with Eze'kiel as king. King Enor Sheffield granted the remainder of\n\nOren to the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order, Gaius Marius, who named it Hanseti.\n\nHochmeister Gaius Marius died, and he was succeeded by Hochmeister Samuel Bealcrest. The King Eze'kiel Tarus, fearing the military threat of the Teutons,\n\ndemanded their disbandment. The resolution of the ensuing war occurred when King Eze'kiel met a sariant, a soldier of the Teutonic Order, in a duel and was defeated.\n\nThe Kingdom of Salvus was formed on a nearby island by the dethroned Enor\n\nSheffield, alongside his wife Dawn Perea. They lived apart from the warfare of the human realm for a short while. On the mainland, King Eze'kiel left his governance to his regent, Reynard Lycian.\n\nThe kingdoms' citizens moved to a new continent when\n\nundead plague threatened their survival on Aegis, and were joined by the newly founded Kingdom of Seventis. This new kingdom joined Renatus in defending against an assault by the Realm of Hanseti, the dwarven Kingdom of Urguan, the Kingdom of Salvus, the\n\nmulti-racial Kingdom of Alras, and the Orcish war-state.\n\nUrguan, Salvus, and Hanseti then aligned themselves against Renatus, Seventis, Alras, the Orcs, and a dissident faction within Salvus led by Lorethos Basileus called the Twilight Army. Salvus\n\ndefeated, and was absorbed into Renatus. The noble House of Hightower was given control of the Salvian realm. Seventis was shortly after stricken with plague and devastated, and its lands too were absorbed into Renatus. The then-Hochmeister Mirtok de\n\nNurem, following a conflict with Renatus and an internal dissident faction called the Wolverines, surrendered his lands too to Godfrey Horen, a politician who had been handed control of Renatus and later was crowned Emperor of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Crusade", "§bWalter Marshall", "The Tragedy Of The Childrens Crusade\n\nAn accurate account ofthe massacre at the Silver City gates.\n\nBy Walter Marshall\n\nUpon the frigid and barren peak of Mount Augustus, a small assemblage of noblemen, soldiers, and guardsmen sit in a circle. Their grimly-set visages dimly illuminated by the moonlight, the men mutter tersely amongst themselves.\n\n The first to rise and speak is the Prince Boris Carrion..\nBoris paces back and forth in thought, his downward gaze denoting pensiveness. At last he speaks, an alarming tone in his voice. “The crowned prince, my cousin Roy - where is he?\"\n\nSer Lothar Horen turns to Boris in response to his frantic query. “Our last report tells us he is encamped outside of Haelun’or, the Silver City. Your cousin has amassed an entourage of boy soldiers, and he has embarked on a children’s crusade.\n\nSer Baron Corbett VanCleef acts as his guard.” Boris stops in his steps, his eyes narrowing as he glances out towards the glimmering spires of the distant elven holding. “Corbett? A loyal man. But in times such as these, we do not know who we can trust.\n\nBring me my cousin Ser, bring me my nephew, and should the Baron attempt to stop you, put a dagger through his heart.” Boris then gives a quick glance to Dederick Varodyr, who stands expectantly as he leans on his greatsword. “And you, ser?\n\nTake my ward with you, it’s about time he met the son of Heinrik.” Ser Lothar gives a quick nod, striding away. Dederick scrambles suit, following after Horen in his brusque pace.\n\nFrom the edge of the forest, Dederick perches himself on the thick branch of an ancient tree, brushing the leaves to a side to peer down at the bustling camp below. His hawk-like gaze scours the large congregation of nomads,\n\nglancing down at the children as they dart in and out of the rows of tents. Many of the young boys and girls heft up swords much too big for themselves, as they move to converge on a single lad under the looming shadow of Haelun’or.\n\nA young boy within the camp, with a bejeweled crown upon his head, swings his oversized sword wildly as he roars loudly. “In the name of the King and holy Godan! Attack!” At the rallying call of their boy leader,\n\nthe droves of children rush towards the gates of the Silver City with unimposing cries, attempting to lift the gate to no avail.\nDederick, with a look of relief upon his face, clambers down from the tree, joining Lothar at the massive timber base.\n\n“It’s him! It’s the crown prince Roy!” With an air of mirth, Varodyr begins to jog towards the group of children, Ser Lothar following with an unimpressed grunt as they near the children’s militia.\n\nAs the mass of youths surround and swarm the steel gate, hanging from the bars and whooping indignantly, Roy Carrion turns to the distant thundering sound of hooves against the cobbled roads. Riding in hard from Vekaro,\n\nthe encroaching throng of horsemen heave up the crimson banners of the Decterum. Giving a boisterous chuckle at the sight of his father’s army, Roy lifts his sword with a triumphant cry as he bellows towards the gatehouse.\n\n“Your city is truly in peril now, elves, for Heinrik’s legion has arrived! Fear the men of the Decterum, for your days are suddenly numbered!” As the young prince continues to hurl imprecations at the unyielding gates of the elven city,\n\na new and alarming sound reaches his ears - the clash of swords accompanied by shrill cries of terror. As Roy shoulders his way past the mass of armored boys at the gates, his eyes widen in despair at the treacherous and cruel sight before him.\n\nThe soldiers of the Decterum advance on the children in the camp, cutting down the young crusaders mercilessly and callously setting fire to the tents as they go. The youthful and inexperienced boys stand no match for the hardened and pragmatic soldiers,\n\nand they carve a swath through Roy’s camp as they cleave their way towards the fearfully paralysed children at the gates.\n\nMeanwhile, the two sent to rescue the crown prince stand similarly frozen in shock at the appalling and insidious massacre. As they watch the sacking of the camp, and the men of the Decterum redden their blades with the blood of the youths,\n\na deep sense of dread ran over them. Had they failed their prince?\nThe remaining children, who stood at the gates, rapped frantically on the iron bars they were moments ago attempting to pull open. Corbett VanCleef, the steadfast servant of Roy,\n\nsparred with many members of the Decterum, but as they surged onwards and surrounded him, he was brought to his knees with a series of blows and shackled. Roy, spinning around confusedly amidst the massacre,\n\nwas hoisted from the ground by a passing uruk and evacuated before the men of the Decterum could kill him.\nMeanwhile, both Lothar and Dederick watch in disarray, at the events unfold before them. Dederick began to rush forth, unsheathing his sword,\n\nbut Lothar stopped him with gritted teeth - to run into the folly ahead was sure and certain suicide. As the men watched helplessly, the surviving rabble of child crusaders swatted fruitlessly at the gates, begging for mercy.\n\nBut no mercy did come that day, and at the hands of the Decterum the gates of the Silver City were awash in red.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Agustus Raid", "§bFinel Cole", "I am keeping track of what things I see, hear, feel, and touch. What I also eat, too. I will record what the people are like, what they think of the destination, their occupation. There is a long journey ahead of me, and I hope this is a success.\n\n So far I am in Oren. The people around me have this wierd accent. I will classify these things in my way. I will attempt to make my own language for it to spread around. I will call these people Orenians. The architecture around here is very complex.\n\n This job that I am doing right now is a Menel. A Menal is someone who records the information around them and makes new things. Now, there is something called Mountain Agustus. Who lives in there are fighters. Protecters of Oren.\n\n Dwarves are attacking. There will be a battle. Todays date is the 30th of The Grand harvest, 1456. This battle will be called The Battle of Oren. The humans are currently in a world war with everyone. I will call the world war, The War of All.\n\n The humans fought the dwarves over, but it isn't over yet.\nThe dwarves have taken over the fort. We have lost control. We are contesting over Fort Vekaro, which is the fort that we lost. The battle is not over yet. The dwarves are almost in.\n\n  I am not calling it a battle anymore. It is no longer The Battle of Oren. It is now The Agustus Raid. Orenians took back Fort Vekaro, no one has won the The Agustus Raid. The dwarves will come back.\n\n They have come back. We fought them back, but they WILL come back. It turns out they were a mix of races in the group. Elves, orcs, and dwarves. They went back to their city, Kal'Alras. Orenians are strong. But are they strong enough?", ""),
        StaticBook("11 Commandments", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Hail Valdoria===\n\n\n\n      The 11 Doctrines\n          of Conduct\n\n\n\n        Approved by\n    The Reich Ministry\n           of Truth\n\n-------------------In the heart of the Kaiser's men lies a singular hope, a dream, that is for the conception of propserity through the devotion of the Kaiser and so be his will. Our souls are ready, let us rise my brothers, let us conceive together the\n\nchild of nationalism and holy power. For now we shall instigate 11 doctrines of conduct, for all who live and shall be must conform, else grasp the warted shaft of Iblees. We, the pure race, shall now impose upon the realm a New Order.\n\nThus follows, thou shalt obey.\n\n1. The rivaling nations of the Vander shall reunite under the banner of purity and fraternity so the Kaiser wills it.\n\n2. The purity of man shall here be enforced through the instigation of cultural and social engineering. Thus be that any and all who live under the light of man shall worship the grace of only he who shall be priased, our Lord and Savior, the Kaiser.\n\n3. The purity of man shall here be enforced through the insitgation of cultural and social engineering. Thus be that any and all who live under the light of man shall worship the grace of only he who shall be praised, our Lord and Savior, the Kaiser.\n\n4. The fowl plague of Serenism and the elfen threat shall be eliminated through the systematic cleansing of the inferior races and the salvation of the Kaiser. Let our grand armies crush any and all militants against the glory and prowess of man.\n\n5. In the prescence of the impure, let us enter the cavities of all who have not been touched by the Kaiser. Let our seed flow into the chambers of darkness and let the Kaiser's grace guide our path into the horrors of the black worms.\n\n6. In address to our recent quarrels, we as a race, as a hope, as a dream, shall and must mold a new world free of the fetters of the lies of the individual and that of which is birthed from the valves of the individual.\n\n7. The counsel of Kingdoms shall henceforth be dissolved in exchange for the Grace and will of Holy theocracy and the divine right of the Rector.\n\n8. The economic might of man must be revitalized in response to the recent morbid and relentless inflation caused undoubtedly by the dwarvish conspiracy. Hence forth, all citizens of human heritage who are not of or associated directly with the blood\n\nof pure humanity shall be taxed at a rate of which must exceed 10% in proportion to the latter.\n\n9. All territory under the light of the Kaiser and the true realm of men shall be renovated to fit the amenities of the pure and centralized of three. Therefore, all roadways must not exceed but must hence thereby not precede the holy\n\ngirth of three metersin accord to our Lord's grand and superior highway system.\n\n10. In response to the elfen Serenist indoctrination of our pure culture, all architectural and aesthetic features under the light of man shall henceforth reflect the purity and holy national pride of our pious and superior culture.\n\n11. Above all else, shall each and every man under the glory of the Kaiser be blessed with the pious and ethereal zeal of white nationalism and forth be orgasmed by the exuberant passion of the autocratic fervor and the divine trinity of\n\nGod, King and Father.\n\nHeil to thee Kaiser, for my only true and mighty ubermensch, for thee may touch my heart and body through man's mighty thrust. Hail to thee my Kaiser, the true father of Man, the boiler of goblins and the cruncher of Elves. May your reign be felt in the\n\nviscera of all men, and may your pure prowess obliterate the tyranny of the impure and the steam of the lesser race. I love you, mein pious Lord, Heil to be thee, may the glory of Priorism, and may our mighty Vander Empire thrive until eternity!", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Guide V.1", "§bRilkor Niwarsay", "-------------------Field Guide to the\nImperium Army\n-------------------By: Rilkor Niwarsay\n((Arctic_Guard\n((Any concerns, contact me in game\n\nGuide to training\nRecruits or other\nSoldiers \n                   ---->\n\n-------------------- Chapter          1  -\n- What makes a       -\n- Good soldier       -\n-------------------There are many things that can be judged from a good soldier.\nDignity. Posture. Combat Skills. And most importantly the Quality standard soldier.\n\nIf ya wish to get anywhere in the Imperium, set a good\nexample of ya self, and act as a soldier should.\n\nThis means turning up to the standard of the best a soldier can preform. Forming bonds with others is key.\n\nThe Quality of a man judges what kind of a soldier he is. Make sure to straighten yourself out as much as possible, with your head held high to show you have dignity.\n\nCertainly showing good quality will show you are a good soldier.\nSo do that.    --->\n\n-------------------- Chapter  2          -\n- Simple Drills        -\n-------------------As a soldier you are expected to do drills.\nDuring drills showing good posture displays the quality of yourself and the army. This is important. Do not mess up.\n   --->\n\nYou will be expected to do these drills not just during intense training and formation demonstrations, but also out in the field. Wether it be traveling as a War Party, or a patrol. Your commanding officers, the Marshal, or even your superiors will\n----->\n\n-ask for you to display this as a group most likely, thus, if one messes up, you all mess up, and must suffer the pain as one. You do not question why or speak out unless spoken to. Failure to do so will result in disciplinary action.\n---------->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 3           -\n- The ABC's of the  -\n- Ranks and Your   -\n- Superiors           -\n------------------- Alright, so this Chapter, we're going to learn about who your Superiors are, and your position in the Imperium.\n--->\n\nFirst off, there is some what of a division between the Military, and the Nobility of Oren. Nobility will generally have more power over the military standard.\nLearning who what people are will help you a lot. \n\n------------>\n\nAt the top of the pyramid is the Emporer. Emporer Robert Chivay, of house Chivay. There are many different houses in Oren, with the Chivay's control firm of the throne.\nThen there is Empress Constance Chivay. They must both be shown the utmost respect. ->\n\nThe Emporer has his own personal guard.\nThey are considered superior to the Imperium Soldiers, for they are the finest.\nThere are, as I've said, other houses besides the Chivays, who also have members included within them.\n--->\n\nIn the Military, you have probably been put into one of two of the regiments of the Imperium. The First Regiment, consisting of burly front-line men, and the Second Regiment, consisting of the rest of the men who form the ranks, and carry out covert\n--->\n\n-missions. These men are considered to be more quick moving then the others. There are specifically chosen men who carry out the orders of these regiments, they are decurions. Not to be confused with Decanus. If ya be a footman, and require help, you --->\n\n-should report to them. They are your utmost importance, as they make or carry out the orders. These orders are given by most likely the Lord-Imperial Marshal. The Marshal will be leading the army into raids, or battles, and should be respected.\n-->\n\nBelow the Decurion, there is the Ensign, the Ensign doesn't have as much power as the Decurion, but can be seen as akin. They carry out the orders given by the Decurion.\nAs a footman, it is the bottom of the food chain, but very needed, for they are --->\n\n-the future soldiers of Orenia. And must be trained as such.\n*A diagram is shown*\nFootman < ManAtArms<\nRhoswenian < Lance\nDecanus < Decanus < QuarterMaster = Sergeant\n\nThat is a basic Diagram of the LOWER ranks.\nOnward ->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 4           -\n- Knowing People    -\n-------------------Getting to know as many people as you can will help you in the marathon. So do that. Form bonds with your human kins-man of the Imperium and of not. For you might find\n-->\n\n-Yourself in situations where you'd need help from your allies and such, this is why you make friends. Since when doesn't calling in your /home boys/ from the streets to help you kill bandit scum a crime? Never. Form strong bonds. You'll need em.\n-->\n\n-------------------- SECTION 2           -\n- COMBAT AND SUCH  -\n-------------------- Chapter 5           -\n- The Laws            -\n-------------------As being apart of the Imperium, you take an oath to server the Emporer, listen to your officers,\n-->\n\n-Fight for humanity and Oren, and uphold justice to the Humans. This means you will need to follow the laws, most of which are not to do anything daft. Conjurering, and magic is banned, this means druids and mages are outlaws. Also, Heretics should be -->\n\n-burned at the stake. ((Also follow the server's pvp rules, unless you want to get br'd and temp banned or perma banned))\nArresting without reason will result in penalties against you, such as de-ranking, or pyshical punishment. Killing enemies is ok. -->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 6           -\n- Raids                 -\n-------------------Occasionally the Marshal will call for a raid, when this happens, you are expected to wake from yur slumber ((get online)) and meet at a given place to prepare for -->\n\n-Battle, during battle you will be expected to identify yourself along-side your allies and bretheren. ((Set /status)) During a raid, you are supposed to be able to identify your enemy, and kill. If you're not sure if you can be the burly man you are\n--->\n\n-in a one versus five, then retreat to your allied company, and ask for assistance or tell of the enemies position. Surely you will be able to not get murdered and rather do the murdering.\nBe sure to be able to sustain yourself with LOTS OF FOOD.\n-->\n\nRemember to try not to die, or atleast die with your bretheren, and hopefully it's not in vain.\n\n\n\n\n((BLANK SPACE))\n\n\n-->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 7           -\n- Wars                 -\n-------------------There will come a time where Humanity will have to defend itself agaisnt the barbaric ways of the enemy. War is self explainatory. ((Server rules of wars))\n-->\n\n-------------------- Rules and such    -\n-------------------\n\n-------------------- Chapter 8           -\n- Arbalest What Is  -\n-------------------Every soldier should be able to cary and use an arbalest. It is the finest of Human made ranged weaponry. ((Rp weapon that is very deadly))\nTo learn to use an arbalest, ->\n\n-First one must aquire an arbalest and get proper training, not from the text I'm about to write. If you don't know who to ask to learn to use an Arbalest, then you probably should do some review. \nImmersive Instructions Follow.\n--->\n\nStep 1 : Pull out Arbalest in hand\n\nStep 2: Place Arbalest under foot\n\nStep 3: Pull back the mechanism till an audible *click* is heard\n\nStep 4: Load bolt\n-->\n\nStep 5: Put Arbalest to your shoulder\n\nStep 6: Comfortably and accurately aim\n\nStep 7: Fire and hope you hit ((Target and you both /roll 20, if shooter rolls higher, target is his))\n\n-->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 9           -\n- Patrolling           -\n-------------------Alright, Patrolling? -You ask, yes this is a thing you must be notified about.\nGenuinely, you are not supposed to wear any armor when patrolling. Why? Because a -->\n\n-man in full iron armor walking along the roads would seem scary to you wouldn't it? Yes it would. That's why you don't wear armor while patrolling, unless you spy some bandits or a criminal, then you gear up and arrest or kill them.\n\nEnough said. -->\n\n-------------------- Rilkor's Tips to    -\n- Combat              -\n-------------------Hopefully these tips will help make you better in combat ((MC PVP)). These secrets should not be told to anyone else, for they might end up in the enemy's hands.\n-->\n\nTip 1: When fighting, don't walk straight forward, that is the dumbest thing I see people do, and I take advantage of it. YOU NEED TO STRAFE. This will help you dodge attacks and position yourself more favorably.\n\n-->\n\nTip 2: Low ground means it's harder for the enemy to attack you as they need to reach down. YOU WANT THE LOW GROUND. If you have the low ground, it will be easier to hit.\n\n\n\n-->\n\nTip 3: When using a bow, contemplate where your enemy is going to be in the second the arrow you fire would hit. JUDGE THE DISTANCE AND SPEED. Shooting at a target far away means they have time to dodge the arrow.\n\n-->\n\nTip 4: For the love of everything, the more people you have on your side, the better the odds are you lot would win a fight, SO STICK TOGETHER. Unless you end up all to be very bad at combat, then I say to you, rest in peace.\n\n-->\n\nTip 5: Blocking is about as useless as bringing a knife to an arbalest fight. ((knife to a gun fight)). YOU SHOULD SWING AS MUCH AS POSSIBLE. Don't stop hitting the enemy! No regrets, no remorse, may only victory be upon you. ((That means spam hitting)\n->\n\n-------------------- End of the Field   -\n- Guide                 -\n-------------------Hopefully you learned something and became a better soldier. I wish ye luck out there.\n\n~Rilkor\n\nAve Chivay, Ave Orenia, Ave Humanity.", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis 5", "§bRalph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFifth Edition\n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Aesterwald united with Oren\n\n*Yakov’s Betrayal\n\n*A report from Kal’Agnar\n\n*And more!\n\nA deserved apology to our readers\nIt has been long enough since the previous edition was released, and I ask for your understanding. I, Ralph Riley, had caught a terrible illness, that medications could not really fight. Feverish and unable to work,\n\nJacob Chapel kept the bookstore working, but the paper could not continue without me. Now I have finally recovered from my illness and I am up to my feet, and this release marks the return of the paper.\n\nAesterwald united with Oren\nOn the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1477, Aesterwald finally joined Oren, uniting humanity once more. Voron Rovin I, König of Aesterwald, and Tuvya, our dear Emperor, signed the Act of Unification bringing together the two realms.\n\nFrom now on Aesterwald and all its vassals are part of our nation, and house Rovin is a Duke Elector in the Empire.\n\nHumanity should rejoice at this act of peace, kindness, and unity in this time of great peril.\n\nLet the united Oren be a strong force against the undead blight.\n\nThe unification act is visible in the public library of Petrus, and for sale at Books of Oren.\n\nPrince Yakov's Betrayal\nA great tragedy has unfolded in our dear capital city of Petrus, after our beloved Imperial Prince, Yakov of the royal house Carrion, was last seen leaving Petrus riding a horse heading towards the north.\n\nIt is unknown what happened on his voyage, but one thing is certain, he is no longer the cheerful man we knew. He is now part of the undead menace and we hope that it was against his will to join them.\n\nBut all of this was yet unknown when he-who-was-Yakov entered Petrus and requested a meeting with Tuvya, accompanied by two staff wielding fiends and an armoured dwarf. Our dear Emperor was attacked, and in a valiant battle he was able to slay\n\nthe evil monsters. Quickly the Wardens, Sonn Ander, and Airthorn came to his help. The battle was won, and he-who-was-Yakov was captured, but at great cost. Our dear Emperor was struck by Iblees’ lightning and gravely injured. To add insult to this,\n\nthe being that once was Yakov was able to escape, after a great explosion.\n\nOur feelings of safety and pride have been tarnished, and the wounds of this betrayal will never heal. It will take time, but Oren will rebuild and get stronger,\n\nand defeat the undead menace and get vengeance for the injustice and savagery.\n\nCarry on Carrion, and Creator bless our Emperor and nation!\n\nA report from Kal'Agnar\n“Upon my entrance into the former capital of the Dwarves, I see much has changed. A gruesome disfigured cultist stands upon the wall of dark stone, waiting to be called upon by his fellow cultists to raise the darkened gates.\n\n The once luscious and green rolling hills of this mountainland now bear the signs of darkness seeping into the soil and killing off all that lives. The city seems to be fighting against the evil that’s entangling it, and turning it into a hall of death.\n\nThe only witnesses of this being the cultists who slit the throats of the innocent, spilling blood upon the one life filled ground. A cavern to the left of the gates show signs of new inhabitants. The cavern called Asgol is watched over by the Doomforges.\n\nThey bear the marks of cultists, and I can only assume they live in this dark covered haven of death and despair. Along with death being strewn into the hills around the city, a substance of pure read laces through the hills, and a pillar stands near the\n\nentrance to the mountain hall, made of the same red substance. It is lit aflame and is perhaps a shrine to Iblees, or some deceptive pillar put up only to mock the once great capital. Fires burn in the hillsides, never wavering in the cold winds flowing\n\nthrough the mountains.\n\nIt seems as though the new residents of left large portions of the capital untouched, though. The mines seem to be sealed shut. As I wander about through the capital I come across a house built into the hillside.\n\n A steady stream of bloody water leaks out of a pipe heading out of the house. Limbs seem to be stuck in the drain, forcing spurts of bloody water out and onto the land. Dark ominous rain clouds float above, drearily drifting past,\n\nuntouched and unknowing of the evil and death that lays below. \n\nMy journey through the capital lead me to the gate once again, where a man stoop pleading for help to cross the deadly ravine between the mountains.\n\nWhile leaving a ghostly sight crossed before my eyes, a steed of pure bone, bearing no flesh, with a rider wearing the face of a pig and the body of a man. The city has been bearing the weight of this darkness for some time.\n\nIt is changing, growing in new ways that can define its path. These cultists prove to only kill viciously and with no defined reason and murder the innocent common folk who walk about.”\n\nReporter attacked by bandits\nAn eyewitness account from our reporter, Telperian Faroar\n“Just upon leaving Petrus my path seemed to be barred by two elven bandits. They seemed small, perhaps wood elves. Although I could not see much under their cover\n\nof darkness and the rusty chainmail that covered most of their bodies, leaving only hands and face exposed to the faint light of the moon through the rustling forest leaves. They held ferrum blades, with the lives of others before me stained upon the dull\n\nsurfaces of the blades. I was outnumbered and unarmed. I took my chance, seeing a narrow path, as I knew I could be killed if I’d stay and try to talk my way out of it.  I sprinted off through with fearless steps as my damp leather boots hit the ground.\n\nI hid behind a tree and waited. The two elves had been slow to notice my escape, but they pursued me nonetheless. From where I stood I could hear their heavy breaths. I took a risk and peered out from behind the trunk of the tree I was leaning against,\n\nnoticing the two men not far apart, one following a few paces behind the other. If only I had a weapon… Rummaging through my bag I located my bow. Removing it quietly, I notched a feathered arrow with ferrum tip. I drew the string up to my cheek,\n\nand all was silent except for the heavy breathing of the two elves. I leaned out from behind the tree, taking aim at the man in the back. As I released the bolt it whistled into the night, heading towards the man’s foot.  A scream pierced the darkness\n\nas the arrow struck the man into his calf. The next arrow found its target, and lodged itself into the elf’s chest. The screaming increased in volume, and his companion yelled out into the darkness “Show yourself and fight, you coward!”\n\nAt these words I began to whistle a merry tune. I released more arrows in their direction, and gave them a slight smile before running off, disappearing through the trees.”\n\nThe Karovian Column\nImperial marriage in peril?\nWhen first asked to write this week’s column on the quiet and peaceful town of Karovia, I of course asked myself… What would the people of Oren like to read?\n\nA thrilling piece on the construction of Prince Aleksandr’s newly erected fortress perhaps? A finely worded treatise on the governing institutions which keep Karovian society afloat? Or even a riveting article on how the good people of this town go about\n\n living their daily lives? No. For we all know the real reason why the people of Oren choose to read this great newspaper over the rest. Why, to indulge themselves in the latest gossip and hearsay of course!\n\nWord on the street has it told that the Imperial Prince Aleksandr and his newly wedded wife Lynn Rovin’s marriage is in danger! Sources on the ground have told us that the pair were heard to be partaking in a bitter argument, late into the hours\n\nof the night. Supposedly the subject of such feud regarded Lynn’s desire to have a child, a suggestion which Aleksandr has adamantly ruled out. It has even been suggested that he may be considering offloading his significant other in favour of\n\na new mistress! In the past the pair have not been unknown for their turbulent marital status, having been forced into partnership in a bid to create peace between the Holy Empire of Oren and the Königreich of Aesterwald.\n\nThankfully unification has succeeded, though as we know, the marriage itself has left much to be desired. Unfortunately our sources have reported that Aleksandr has so far refused to answer any of our questions on the matter!\n\nSo dear readers, what is next for our Imperial Prince? Will he succumb to his wife’s wishes? Or will he emerge a fighter after all? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Six!\n -An anonymous source from Karovia", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicine Vol. 1", "§bKale", "A Dose of Solace\nVolume 1\n\nWritten By: Dr. Kale\n\n\nIn this book you will find effortless remedies to common day sicknesses.\n\n1. Stomach Pain\n\n1 cup of hot chamomile tea\n3 peppermint leafs\n\nPlace the leafs on top of the hot steamy cup of tea and drink it twice a day to ease the churning pain.\n\n2. Flashes (Fever)\n\n4 rags\n1 big bucket of cold water\n\nSoak the rages with water and place each rag on the forehead, under each arm pit and behind the neck. Do so as needed until it subsides.\n\n3. Burning Throat\n\n1 hot cup of water\n5 drips of honey\n2 tsp. of sugar\n\nMix it all together thoroughly and sip until your throat begins to feel soothing.\n\n4. Coughing\n\n1 rag\n1 pot of boiling water\n\nPlace it rag over your mouth and bend your head close enough to the steam and breathe it in. Do this until your coughing has calmed itself.\n\n5. Ear Pain\n\n   Warm up oil until it is at a lukewarm feel and pour it into the ear. Lay on the opposite ear that isn't causing you pain. The pain should stop momentarily.\n\n6. Bruises \n\nThere's multiple remedies to heal a bruise quickly \n\n1st- Cold Herbal Tea Compress\n2nd- Ice Block compress\n3rd- Cold Poppy Tea Compress\n\n7. Rashes\n\nCacutus Paste\nHerbal Tea\n\nMash the two together until it become a thick like paste. Rub the paste on the rash until it drys or can be scraped off.\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make the rash paste*\n\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to apply a compress to a bruise*\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make different teas*\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to mix honey with tea* \n\n*Here would be a sketch of a person breathing in the steam with a rag covering their mouth*\n\n[!] The sketch would be drawn very well", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic First Aid", "§bGwyneviere de Savoie", "Basic First Aid\n\nGwyneviere de Savoie\n\n~                        ~\n          Vol 1\n\nIt is important for those who commonly engage in fighting or combat that the wound is more deadly than your enemies' weapon. Even the smallest cut can kill you. Tend to your wounds as soon as you can and ensure that your wound does not become infected.\n\nUnder the circumstance that the patient has been inflicted with a cut or puncture injury, there will be blood. Tourniqet the wound to stop the blood flow, or apply a moss to absorb and clot the wound.\n\nForeign material, such as cloth and dirt\n\nfor example, will need to be removed from the wound. Particularly if the wound is a puncture. Anything inside the wound can lead to infection and then death.\n\nEven the smallest injury can kill the strongest, and it is important to be aware\n\nof how deadly infection is. Animal urine is an efficient way to sterylise an injury of any infection. Cauterizing the wound is a painful method, but an efficient one, to reduce chances of external infection. If perhaps you do not have ready available\n\nanimal urine, or a brand (or a fire), or you do not have herbs or medical plants; wrap the injury as best you can and replace bandaging often. Reach a doctor, or a field medic immediately.\n\nAfter sterylising the injury, you may chose to apply a medic\n\nor herbal paste to the wound if you have it on hand. Otherwise, apply a clean bandage to the wound and seek proper medical aid. Again, change the dressing regularly.\n\nIf a wound is so severe that an internal organ is punctured\n\nor cut by sword or knife- there isn't much first aid can do. Organ damage will most likely lead to a painful death without proffesional care. It is unlikely that the correct attention will be gained if the wound was inflicted in battle. Use tea's or herbs\n\nto ease your pain, or your patients' pain as best you can. It is likely that the patient will be suffering from his or hers' injury.\n\nSide note: Alcohol is good way to sterylise a wound and act as a pain killer.\n\nSevere Head Injury:\n\nIt is likely that in battle a person will come across a head or skull injury. This may also occur after a fall or a slip. If the injury is small, reach an area where you can sit, and check yourself for obvious\n\ninjury. It is likely you will be dazed or nausious. If skin has split, apply a bandage and seek help as fast as possible to ensure that no long term damage is dealt.\n\nIf the injury is severe, such as the crushing of a skull, your\n\npatient is most likely unconcious, or in a coma. Either way, they're in a bad state- and hopefully you're there to save their life. Check their pulse first, they may appear to be dead. Swelling of the face, nose, and eyes is a sign that the patient\n\nhas undergone some serious damage to their head or skull. In this case, it is unlikely that basic first aid can save their life. Do not move them, and if possible, seek proper medical attention. The brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage\n\nor death. A hole will need to be drilled into the skull of the patient in order to allow the brain to swell. It is still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause nausia, headaches, dizzyness and physical sickness. Resting will heal\n\nBroken Bones:\n\nYou can check to see the severity of your patients injuries (or your own) by physical appearance. Your patient or yourself will most likely be in shock because of the injury. State of shock is a dangerous thing. Never\n\nunderestimate the severity of the situation. Broken bones often can be seen externally as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape or difference in your limbs, and the limb affected.\n\nYou can use sticks and straps from boots or clothes, or fabric from your clothes also, to create a splint to keep limbs straight. If your patient has a broken leg, it is likely they wont be able to walk. This is a no brainer to identifying a broken bone\n\nor fracture. Splinting or creating a stretcher out of sturdy sticks strapped together in a ladder shape can be used to transport the patient. A splint can be used to keep the injury straight and reduce movement to the affected area\n\nin the case of injuring yourself.\n\nYou can also pack mud around the limb to set the break. Seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be relocated with pressure to the\n\naffected area. It is painful. Your patient may need pain killers. If you do not feel comfortable tending to a dislocated bone, seek medical attention of another, or man up.\n\nSlings, made out of tied cloth, or a shirt is great for arm or shoulder brea\n\nA bone break can also break the skin. There may be blood. Apply a splint or use a stretcher to get the patient to proper medical attention if this is the case.\n\nWater Injuries:\n\nIf a person has found themselves floating face down in the water. The first thing you should do is turn them onto their back. It is important not to apply weight to their body, as you could force them under water.\n\nThere isnt much you can do out in the water, so bring them back to shore quickly, and remember to keep their head above the waters' surface.\n\nLay them on their back and check for a pulse. A persons pulse can be found under their neck or the under-\n\n-side of their wrist. Either way, there is a possibility of saving the patient. Place one hand, a fist, onto the chest of the patient above their heart. Place your second hand atop the other.\n\nPump their chest, with short breaks. Count thirty pumps b\n\nstopping. This can force water out of the lungs of the patient or restart the heart.\n\nOpen the airway of the patient by placing your palm on the persons forhead and gently tilting their head back. Check for normal breathing. If the patient is not bre\n\n-ng still, open the persons mouth and transfer air from your own lungs to the patients. Afterwards, continue pumping. Hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out of their lungs.\n\nArrow Wounds:\n\nIf your patient has an arrow injury, first be prepared to apply a lot of force to free the person of the arrow. They are very hard to get out safely. Pulling it out without care can sever arteries or break leave splinters\n\nor wood inside of the body. You could die of blood loss or infection. So long as the bolt or arrow is inside of the patient, the blood loss will be lower than without it.\n\nYou can remove the arrow by propulsion, where you force the arrow\n\nthrough the flesh and out the exit point of the wound. Reccomended for limb injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft, and leave it for a few days so that the wound becomes full of pus and can then be removed with ease. The pus signals infection.\n\nand would then need proper medical attention.\n\nStretch the wound by plugging it with probes of elder pith, soaked in honey and then using a pair of tongs, reach into the wound and slowly, carefully, tug the arrow/bolt free.\n\nWash the wound with wine or liquor, and apply a bandage securely or cauterize the wound. Reduce the amount of strain on the affected area and rest for a few days to prevent pains and quicken the rate of healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Herbs", "§bAndriel Elré Z'lorn", "In the field there are many ways to treat the wounded. From burns to cuts to scrapes to arrow wounds, there can be many different things that may need to be cared for. Here is a guide on Medical Uses of different Herbs during everyday life.\n\nBlissfoil:\nBlissfoil can be very useful for minor injuries or ailments. It can relieve pain and itchyness at the slightest of touch. The oil around it's stalks and petals can be used medically to relieve these symptoms.\n\nTippen's Root:\nThis herb is great for stopping the bleeding of a large wound once made into a Salve/Balm. This root is known for having an unpleasent smell, however, the medical uses outweight such factors.\n\nFlameTounge Root:\nThis Root is not to be used lightly, and is only to be used if out of Tippen's Root. It gives off an intense heat that can be used to seal and stop blood flow. NOTE: Make sure to wear gloves when handling this Root.\n\nSerpent's Stalk:\nThis herb is generally dangerous for consumption as a plant, however, once one crushes the upper stalk and mix it with water, it can be used to treat burns and minor pain.\n\nFrost Vine:\nIt is wise to crush this herb and mix it with water. This will produce a substance, somewhat sticky, which can be used to numb areas from pain.\n\nAqua Nymph:\nWARNING: Only use in extreme cases.\nThis plant can cause closing of the airway if taken orally. However, if one were to receive\na terrible burn. To use the plant correctly, boil the plant (Gently) in some water, strain the plant from the water\n\nAqua Nymph Cont.:\nand use the remaining oil on the affected skin.", ""),
