 be suffering from his or hers' injury.\n\nSide note: Alcohol is good way to sterylise a wound and act as a pain killer.\n\nSevere Head Injury:\n\nIt is likely that in battle a person will come across a head or skull injury. This may also occur after a fall or a slip. If the injury is small, reach an area where you can sit, and check yourself for obvious\n\ninjury. It is likely you will be dazed or nausious. If skin has split, apply a bandage and seek help as fast as possible to ensure that no long term damage is dealt.\n\nIf the injury is severe, such as the crushing of a skull, your\n\npatient is most likely unconcious, or in a coma. Either way, they're in a bad state- and hopefully you're there to save their life. Check their pulse first, they may appear to be dead. Swelling of the face, nose, and eyes is a sign that the patient\n\nhas undergone some serious damage to their head or skull. In this case, it is unlikely that basic first aid can save their life. Do not move them, and if possible, seek proper medical attention. The brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage\n\nor death. A hole will need to be drilled into the skull of the patient in order to allow the brain to swell. It is still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause nausia, headaches, dizzyness and physical sickness. Resting will heal these\n\nBroken Bones:\n\nYou can check to see the severity of your patients injuries (or your own) by physical appearance. Your patient or yourself will most likely be in shock because of the injury. State of shock is a dangerous thing. Never\n\nunderestimate the severity of the situation. Broken bones often can be seen externally as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape or difference in your limbs, and the limb affected.\n\nYou can use sticks and straps from boots or clothes, or fabric from your clothes also, to create a splint to keep limbs straight. If your patient has a broken leg, it is likely they wont be able to walk. This is a no brainer to identifying a broken bone\n\nor fracture. Splinting or creating a stretcher out of sturdy sticks strapped together in a ladder shape can be used to transport the patient. A splint can be used to keep the injury straight and reduce movement to the affected area\n\nin the case of injuring yourself.\n\nYou can also pack mud around the limb to set the break. Seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be relocated with pressure to the\n\naffected area. It is painful. Your patient may need pain killers. If you do not feel comfortable tending to a dislocated bone, seek medical attention of another, or man up.\n\nSlings, made out of tied cloth, or a shirt is great for arm or shoulder breaks.\n\nA bone break can also break the skin. There may be blood. Apply a splint or use a stretcher to get the patient to proper medical attention if this is the case.\n\nWater Injuries:\n\nIf a person has found themselves floating face down in the water. The first thing you should do is turn them onto their back. It is important not to apply weight to their body, as you could force them under water.\n\nThere isnt much you can do out in the water, so bring them back to shore quickly, and remember to keep their head above the waters' surface.\n\nLay them on their back and check for a pulse. A persons pulse can be found under their neck or the under-\n\n-side of their wrist. Either way, there is a possibility of saving the patient. Place one hand, a fist, onto the chest of the patient above their heart. Place your second hand atop the other.\n\nPump their chest, with short breaks. Count thirty pumps before\n\nstopping. This can force water out of the lungs of the patient or restart the heart.\n\nOpen the airway of the patient by placing your palm on the persons forhead and gently tilting their head back. Check for normal breathing. If the patient is not breathi-\n\n-ng still, open the persons mouth and transfer air from your own lungs to the patients. Afterwards, continue pumping. Hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out of their lungs.\n\nArrow Wounds:\n\nIf your patient has an arrow injury, first be prepared to apply a lot of force to free the person of the arrow. They are very hard to get out safely. Pulling it out without care can sever arteries or break leave splinters\n\nor wood inside of the body. You could die of blood loss or infection. So long as the bolt or arrow is inside of the patient, the blood loss will be lower than without it.\n\nYou can remove the arrow by propulsion, where you force the arrow\n\nthrough the flesh and out the exit point of the wound. Reccomended for limb injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft, and leave it for a few days so that the wound becomes full of pus and can then be removed with ease. The pus signals infection.\n\nand would then need proper medical attention.\n\nStretch the wound by plugging it with probes of elder pith, soaked in honey and then using a pair of tongs, reach into the wound and slowly, carefully, tug the arrow/bolt free.\n\nWash the wound with wine or liquor, and apply a bandage securely or cauterize the wound. Reduce the amount of strain on the affected area and rest for a few days to prevent pains and quicken the rate of healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Arganos", "§bMaladem Uuthlini", "To Arganos§0\n§0By Maladem Uuthlini§0\n§0\n§0Proud Uuthlini, raise the flagon!§0\n§0Set the table for the feast!§0\n§0Gather all by boat and wagon,§0\n§0All your kin from west to east!§0\n\nCall your fellow ker together!§0\n§0Let no beast nor Undead thrall,§0\n§0Nor any sort of fearsome weather,§0\n§0Keep them from the banquet hall!§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "§bLefkos Glowsbane", "Efficiency:\nEfficiency is one of the quickest and easiest of all of the enchantments to make. The purpose of this is to make any desired tool do its job faster. Using it, you may find that your pickaxe digs through stone like a knife through butter, or an\n\naxe may fell a tree in one or two swings. Even though it may be a cheap enchantment, it remains one of the most well known and used.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                ----x----                ---x-x---                ----x----\n\nUnbreaking:\nThis would probably be the second most used enchant, its purpose rather simple and self explanatory. I will review it anyway. Unbreaking is meant to make your tools harder and stronger. Tougher to break. Using it, you may notice that tools\n\nthat used to break after you use them for a while may still be functional. Its another easy enchantment that wouldnt cost to much to purchase.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                -x-x-x-x-                --x---x--                -x-x-x-x-\n\nSharpness:\nThis is a rather difficult enchantment, much to hard for a novice to make, and a rather expensive one as well. With this enchantment, you may find that your swords cut through bodys easier, making your opponents fall before your blade.\n\nThose that seek out an enchanter for this enchantment are normally guards, or people about to go to war.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        --x------                xxxxxxxx-                xxxxxxxxx                --x------\n\nPower:\nAn enchantment similar to sharpness, but for a different item. Power is made for bows, and when using it, you may find arrows you shoot from your bow hitting harder, enough to crack stone and injure your opponent more then a normal arrow. Only\n\nProffesional marksmen and archers will seak out this enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        xx----x--                --xxxxxx-                --xxxxxxx                xx----x--\n\nFire Aspect:\nOne of the oldest and harder enchantments to master. Many seek this enchantment on their blades for its usefullness. It is a must have for armies and a hard level enchantment. Adventurers and high ranking officers may seek out an enchanter\n\ncapable of this for their army. Fire aspect gives your blade an arcane power that, upon cutting any living creature, will set them aflame. Its thought of as a brutal but useful enchantment.\n\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -xxxxxxx-\n\nFlame:\nVery similar to Fire Aspect, Flame is another hard level enchantment. It lets your arrows catch fire, and burn whatever they hit.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        x--x--x-x                -xxxx-x-x                x--x--x-x                ------xxx\n\nKnockback:\nOne of the best enchantments in my opinion, knockback is sure to prove useful to anyone, no matter who they are fighting. This enchantment, rather then strengthening the actual blade, strengthens the arm holding the blade.\n\nIt is called \"Knockback\" because at that point, if you hit someone with your arm at full force, you possess the strength to send them flying back. Combine this with Fire aspect and you can shoot little fireballs called 'your opponent.'\n\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xx-----                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xx-----\n\nProtection:\nOne of the less common used enchantments, but more useful. Protection was made to make your armor harder, so an arrow that would once pierce your heart wouldnt even reach it. The only reason it isnt commonly used is because not many\n\npeople have the time to wait for their armor to be enchanted.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                ---xxx---\n\nFeather falling:\nA rarely used enchant. Infact, not a single person has asked me for it. I will put it here anyways. Feather falling increases the strength of your feet in terms of impact for the ground. Normally if you would barely survive after a 10\n\nmeter drop, you would be fine for this handy enchantment. Most people under value this enchantment, until they slip and fall!\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         -----xx--                ----xxx--                ----xx---                ---x-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "§bAmbros", "A Guide to Sorcery\n\n\n      By Ambros\n\nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage.\n\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the same power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often considered to be a more modern version\n\nof magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\n\nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic.\nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect of your spell to be.\n\nSome scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim that their powers are akin\n\nto keys-necessary to unlock the final effect of a spell-another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting that even the most learned of\n\narcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\n\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\n\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.\n\nAlthough they can often achieve a number of other magical feats that the other magical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then more often than not you will see a mage locking a door with\n\na spell, shooting fire from his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any form of \"spiritual\" attributes about it are gone.\n\nA healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is a form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire\n\nor easing pain with a numbing spell.  Whatever the case is arcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arcane Arts", "§bShariana", "-------------------The Arcane Arts\n    By Shariana TWW\n-------------------\n\nIntroduction.\n\nIn this book, you will get an understanding of the different areas around arcane void magic. This can be useful, if you practice these arts, or fight against an Evocationist, Thaumaturge or Conjurationist.\n\nChapter 1.\n\n     - Evocation -\n     The Sorcerer\n\nPerhaps the most well known of the four arch-types of magic.  Evocation involves evoking the elements of air, fire, earth, water, and lightning from the void.\n\n-Sorcerers cannot manipulate pre-existing elements, only summon them.\n\n-Each element is considered one arch-type of magic on its own.\n\n-The elements must follow the same laws as they do in nature.\n\n-Sorcerers must be ‘attuned’ to their element, spend time around their element, understand its scientific properties, how it feels etc…\n\n-Sorcerer’s must see the area they wish to summon their element in.\n\n-Sorcerers can only summon their element in its rawest form.\n\n-Hydromancers can also be Cryomancer (Ice Mage).\n\n-Sorcerers must imagine the element in their mind and bend it in their mind before evoking it.\n\nChapter 2.\n\n      - Alteration -\n    The Thaumaturge\n\nA true science of magic, Alteration involves altering the physical world around the mage.\n\n      * Enchanting *\n-------------------The art of imbuing magical effects upon an object.\n-------------------\n\n-Changes what the item does rather than what it is.\n\n-Thaumaturge must be touching the item to enchant it.\n\n-The enchantment cannot alter the object physically.\n\n-Enchantments only last as long as they have a mana source.\n\n-Thaumaturges must imagine the object they see, in great detail, with the enchantment on it in their mind.\n\n  * Transfiguration *\n-------------------The art of changing an object’s appearance.\n-------------------\n\n-Objects must keep their original mass.\n\n-Objects can only change their state, not their chemical makeup. (Ie. Ice to water, not water to wine.)\n\n-Thaumaturge must be touching and see  the object to transfigure it.\n\n-Thaumaturges must imagine the object altering,exactly how they want it, in their mind and the steps it would need to go through for the transfiguration to be possible.\n\n     * Abjuration *\n-------------------The art of protection.\n-------------------\n\n-Wards are barriers of mana which cancel out other, aggressive mana.\n\n-Wards only block spells which have less mana than the ward was made with.\n\n-Wards only last so long as they have a mana source.\n\n-The Thaumaturge must imagine their mana being released from their body and forming a barrier around them, in the shape they desire.\n\nChapter 3.\n\n   - Conjuration -\n    The Conjurer\n\nA highly complicated form of magic, Conjuration involves summoning organic beings from the Void.\n\n-Beings can only remain in existence so long as they have a mana source which would keep them alive in reality.\n\n-Conjurer’s need to understand the insides and outs, literally, of the creature they wish to summon lest they get something terribly wrong.\n\n-Primordial Conjurers can summon elemental beings, though they must have an understand of at least one evocation element.\n\n-Primordial Conjurers do not need to understand the biological structure of their being, only use their mana,  and an understanding of basic motor skills in creatures.\n\n-Conjurers must see where they wish to summon their creature.\n\nChapter 4.\n\n       - Illusion -\n      The Magician\n\nA dark form of magic which involves using mana to alter one’s senses.\n\n-Magicians can only alter the senses\n\n-Anything a magician does is not actually there, no matter how real it feels, looks, smells etc…\n\n-Magicians cannot read minds….or directly change one’s emotion.\n\n-This is often known as glamour magic.\n\n-A Magician must have experience with their illusion in real life. (ie. To make someone feel as if they are giving birth, the magician would have to understand what giving birth feels like)\n\n-Illusions only remain in existence so long as they have a source of mana.\n\n-Magician must be able to see where they wish to produce their illusion.\n\n-The Magician must (smell, taste, hear, touch etc…) the object before they can produce it, with accuracy.  This is why the Magician must have experienced the sense they wish to alter in reality.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n         The End\n         ~ ~ ~ ~", ""),
        StaticBook("Meditation", "§bThereon Ireheart", "Bardmancy Meditation\n\nTo become a Bardmancer you must first connect with \"The Void\" a magical force that gives a Mage their power.\n\nBardmancers at first need much \"Mana\" of magical energy to connect but once they have connected they\n\nneed far less \"Mana\" to use and sustain their magic.\n\nMeditating\n\nTo meditate with \"The Void\" they must first get three things Wax Candles, a copy of the Bardmancy Tome, and a Quiet place with a statue of a Godly figure.\n\nOnce someone has these three things they need only Knell or Sit facing the God/Goddess with the Candles lit and they must pray to the God or Goddess.\n\n((You must Pray 4 times with a /roll of 15 or higher))", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "§bLori Oathcast", "Long Range Translocation Device Investigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from Archmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockets within the void to place objects and a --->\n\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the void, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the original void translocationist present. The void translocationist must --->\n\n- then re-locate himself and in the area he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stay open when powered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation Basics", "§bGerald Elgan", "===================\n                                                                                                  The Basics\n             Of                       Evocation\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n==================\n\nIn order for sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as they must know how fire feels to touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\n\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\n\nEvocation is often quite physically and mentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The large the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast it. And just as any other magical branch of the\n\nArcane tree, the mage must be capable of envisioning where he is casting his spell, and at what - that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball\n\nbehind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of water to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight. Despite the seemingly passive nature\n\nthat any one mage may seem to possess, they however remain filthy abominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child-\n\nfor all who walk upon God's blessed earth.\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Dictionary", "PiercingDarkness", "The Magic Dictonary:\n\nYir'sari - True Wizard, powerful magic masters.\n\nAscended - The demi-god children of the aenguls.\n\nUndead - The evil fists of Iblees, they destroyed Aegis.\n\nArcane Transportation Pad - \n\nStaff - a tool used to conduct mana, as well as aid you in Void connections.\n\nWand - Akin to the staff, doesn't work as well.\n\nCleric - Powerful magicians based mostly in healing, they are fueled by aenguls.\n\nNecromancer - Users of Necromany, a deadly magic having to do with life drain.\n\nPyromancer - Fire evocationist, magician of fire.\n\nElectromancer - Users of electric magic, mostly evocationist of electricity, they are common in Anthos.\n\nEvocation - The use of summong elements from the Void.\n\nFire-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create fire.\n\nWater-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create water or other water related things.\n\nElectric-Evocation - The evoking of mana from the Void to form electricity.\n\nWind-Evocation - The use of void mana to create wind and it's similiar elements.\n\nEarth-Evocation - The evocation of mana to form earthen elements.\n\nShamanism - Magic having to do with the use of spirits.\n\nElemental control - A shaman magic having to do with spirits.\n\nMagic(k) - The use of mana to conjure things, and even to control things.\n\nMana - Life force and energies around us, used to form complex spells.\n\nNecromancy - The use of life drain to get mana to form complex\n\nspells.\n\nShade-Magic - Fueled by a gem, it's a shadow magic having to do with the art of tendrils, and other shadow elements.\n\nIllusion - A arcane magic, the use of mana to form false images and feelings, and project them upon others, it's impossible to illusion yourself.\n\nConjuration - The conjuring of living beings.\n\nWizard - Common term name for the Yir'sari, true wizards.\n\nArch-Mage - Ruler of the mage's guild.\n\nMage - Practicer of magic.\n\nMagician - Mage is it shortened.\n\nAscended Magic - Magic fueled by a patron aenguel, it is a light magic, and holy, it is akin to cleric.\n\nUndead-Magic - Fueled by Iblees, the Undead used their necromancy to begin their conquest of Aegis.\n\nThe Void - A place where mages draw power from to fuel their spells.\n\nDragon - A beast of huge size and intelligence, they roam Northern Anthos, hunting.\n\nYellow Stone Material ((Endstone))\n\nA heavily weird material, it spreads corruption of many kinds.\n\nDruidism - Magic over nature, has to do with the spirits known as the Aspects.\n\nAlteration - Magic that alters the properties, of real world things.\n\n-------------------\n\nMagic sayings:\n\n\"Magic seeks those who don't seek it.\"\n\n\"Magic is the path of ths scholar, not a insolent warrior of heavy brains and no mindset.\" \n\n\"Magic is the path of destruction, insolent mage!\" - Gavin the Druid\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\"Good and evil doesn't decide how magic works, only the acts of the user.\"\n\n- The Arcane Mage\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nWritten by, Mythras Ardere.\n\nSources:\n\n- history of magic\n- The Clerical Order\n- The Mage's Guild\n- Salamandra's spirit\n- Many assorted books on magic, and knowledge from other mages.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bloody Poetry", "§bAlan Marlsbush", "Eldre-home§0\n§0\n§0Hoilelio goiu holias§0\n§0\n§0Ana viev §0\n§0\n§0Del Dorini ec Eldre Enshu§0\n§0\n§0Hoilelio§0\n§0Be hoilelios hoilas\"§0\n§0\n§0ritiou\n\n Petals pooled in crimson red.§0\n§0Life flowing out and leaving him dead.§0\n§0So came the book man,§0\n§0with no ill intent.§0\n§0To the noble city full of discontent.§0\n§0He meant no trouble and caused no strife,§0\n§0but the city's guards§0\n§0chose to end\n\n Empty it lies, §0\n§0Asleep in the cold,§0\n§0Just another lost city, with a tale to be told.§0\n§0With high towers and statues so great,§0\n§0Yet silent it stands,§0\n§0Forever open it's gate. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Odo's Story", "§bOdo Komninus", "This is the story of a young boy named Odo. He is 12 years old and lives with his caretakers who are Helzya and Ioannis. He has lived a rough life his two parents put him in a orpanage before he could remember them. Odo and his sister Lilly were raised\n\nby human farmers. These farmers taught Odo how to farm which lead to his cooking intrest. The farmers sent him away at age 10 because of growing danger for him there. He dosent know why he was sent away but he was told it was for the best. Him and Lilly\n\nsoon found refuge in Kal'Karrad, Ironicly it was the mortal enemy of the Humans, but Helzya and Ioannis took him and Lilly in, they lived in a tarvern for a bit untill Ioannis let them move into his manor! What was really hard was Odo getting used to\n\naround people. Over the years he was taught to hate the dwarven race, not cherish them. Now he loves it and studys it. Odo wants to become a master Chef, but he is really good at fishing. \n\nWritin by Odo Komininus\nAge: 12", ""),
        StaticBook("A Carrot Poem", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "A Carrot Poem\n       By:\n          Franswaar\n\n\n    Based on true \n         events\n\nRotten Carrots serve as no treat, The Knight is very displeased at this feat\nDeath is his sentence, what a poor man, The Knight must cleanse the rotten carrot land\nA twist in the story, what is this! An outsider now comes into action from the mist\n\nFighting in the streets, blood on the walls oh my! Does everyone have to die because of this rotten carrot guy?\nBlood covers the ground, screams are heard all around. Someone please help kill these hounds.\n\nHow could carrots ever escalate to this. Canon would be displeased, these men will be given no bliss", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sonnet", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "A Sonnet\n    Written By:\n      Franswaar\n\n\n\n\n     Dedicated to:\nThe Memory of someone you have lost\n\nShe left me in a hurry without thought\nLeft alone mourning a memory\nCries from a sinner gave heaven no fraught\nEven the wisest oak men shall fade suddenly\n\nHonour shattered, respect lost, and heads turned\nStanding slightly ever straight though dwarfs looked upon\nTwo mountains over looking the edge of the world\nOne stands while the other crumbles toward the fading sun\n\nThe voice of the fallen echo through out\nVisions of haven through branches of the williow\nTombs sit empty while the bodies of the living prowl\nThough gone the sight of her to my life I owe\n\nJust one last glimmer I wish I could see\nRosalina, you were my queen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem", "§bBeluar the Botanist", "Kypris the beauty\nOh how I love thee so much\nWe have barely spoke\n\nWhat is wrong with me?\nLove with a female so soon?\nI am a failure\n\nOh but I would fail\nBut I would fail a thousand times a day so\n\nI could have her hand\n\nShe says I'll find love\nI wonder who it will be\nHopefully it's her\n\nThey call her evil\nI see her as a flower\nShe may be a witch", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lover's Day.", "§bKili Al-Deen", "they shine brightly in the moon lit gaze,i have traveled near and far yet seen not such beauty as this\nlike a diamond strong and proud yet pretty and pleasing to the eye.their touch is of a gentil flower on a warm sunny day,their voice is soft and\n\ngentil that fills the heart with a warm reassurance and a aw that makes you feel as thuo you have been touched and carryed away by a cloud,you get lost in their gaze as one gets lost in a sunset and your mood rises like the sun in the dawn. you yearn\n\nto be around them with and want to see their smile and happyness you feel as if its your duty to make them smile and joyfull.thy are my warm sunrise and Beautiful jem.to rise before you and make you your favorite dish and bring you roses of compasion is a\n\nhonnor and love that goes to no one but you,My dear love.\n___________________\n\n         By:Kili Al-Deen\n      (ibraheemc2000)\n\nnotes from writer:\nI made this for the enjoyment of the read and the warmth of the heart-Kili Al-Deen.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lion & Mouse", "§bKlaudia Crast", "-=-=-=-=--=-=-=-=-\n\nThe Lion & the Mouse\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n------------------\n\nOnce when a lion, the king of the jungle, was asleep, a little mouse began running up and down on him. This soon awakened the lion, who placed his huge paw on the mouse, and opened his big jaws to swallow him.\n\n\"Pardon, O King!\" cried the little mouse.\n\n\"Forgive me this time. I shall never repeat it and I shall never forget your kindness. And who knows, I may be able to do you a good turn one of these days!”\n\nThe lion was so tickled by the idea of the mouse -\n\nbeing able to help him that he lifted his paw and let him go.\n\nSometime later, a few hunters captured the lion, and tied him to a tree. After that they went in search of a wagon, to take him to the animal keep.\n\nJust then the little mouse happened to pass by. On seeing the lion’s plight, he ran up to him and gnawed away the ropes that bound him, the king of the jungle.\n\n\"Was I not right?\" said the little mouse, very happy to help the lion.\n\n-------------------\n\nMORAL: Small acts of kindness will be rewarded greatly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Moonlit Eyes", "§bKili Al-Deen", "In moon Lit Gaze I saw Her Eyes,in which made my heart fill with crys, if i would fall for you it would be my demise!\nbut can I live my life with out your eyes?\nin the nights i Lie adrift in thoughts of your silky hair,and in the days i have the\n\nstrangth to kill a bear! and when I see you my heart races like a hare. Yet I wish you can see me amongst the croud,I shall say hi,I shall not now,days go by i see her smile, if i say hi its like a mile! oh such agony if a day goes by it will feel like\n\napart of me will die.\nAlas Alas it canot be more i will do it tonight!\nwhere i saw her and her eyes i will walk that mile and spare the bear for this night! the moon lit glaze fills her eyes by the tree she stands on that night i make my walk up\n\nslowly feeling more and more alive,what will i say what will i do for years now and i have not thought it thruo. i stand with her face to face struck by her dazziling eyes and beautiful silky hair until she made a warm smile like none ive ever seen on her\n\nface,and to my amaze,\nher cheeks looked ablazed.she came closer,i didnt know what do to.then i told her\"I Love You.\"with a second of silence she smiles and turns around.I walk back home in the moon light with my head down until i hear a sound\n\nso I turn around as i hear a gentil voice say \"I Love you too.\"\n\n\n        By:Kili Al-Deen\n       (ibraheemc2000)\n-------------------\nI made this because I was bord,i hope you injoy it and one day say it to your love i also planed this\n\nto be a poem but toward the end of it i couldnt find ways i could make it rhyme Hehe.\n___________________", ""),
        StaticBook("The Frost Witch", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "An Encounter with Frost Witches\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\n\nRevised edition\n\nI first learned about the dreaded creatures, known as frost witches, from one of the tomes in the libraries of old Haelunor. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways.\n\nThough as an adult of more mature understanding and greater constitution, I revisited the subject of “monsters” and relearned the available details of the frost witch. They are exclusively women so far as any adventurer who has survived an encounter\n\nwith them can tell.\n\nThey are horrid to look upon in their natural state. Grey skinned with eyes like ice, but it is not so easy to spot one of these slippery creatures for an ice witch is a master of disguise.\n\nThey employ illusion to mask their true selves, that they may, with more subtlety, intrude upon our societies and seek out their prey.\n\nIn fact, as the story goes, a frost witch will adopt the guise of a young woman and sit, crying, in the midst of\n\nsnowy glade. This is done to attract young and hapless men. The clever frost witch will then transform into her hideous self and dispatch the unwitting male then and there, or she will lure him back to her coven to become a grisly meal for her sisters.\n\nThey are, without exception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a “Witch Mother” who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee, she will build her nest\n\nand gather workers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent.\n\nWhen another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience, she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or saddened.\n\nThe frost witch will then “mark” the woman with a curse. Should she succumb to her sorrow she will become a frost witch herself, and thus do their numbers swell.\nIt is reportedly a favorite tactic of the frost witches to seek out a married man\n\nand devour him, then they will curse his grieving widow. In this fashion do they gain both a meal and a prospective member of their coven.\nNot much is known about the curse, and there is no known way to remove it. It has been said, however,\n\nthat if the woman resists her sadness and sorrow that she may endure the curse and not become on of these fiends. Though she will likely live with the curse for the rest of her days.\n\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must seek out and destroy the witch mother. In some cases this is enough to cause the coven to wither and die. In others, however, if a witch who is powerful enough survives, she may assume the role\n\nof witch mother and allow the coven to limp on. In any case, the most foolproof method of destroying a coven is just that, destroy the coven. All of it.\n\nIf one seeks to harm a frost witch I would give them this advice. Strike fast and strike true for you shall not likely receive a second chance. Also, a sellsword of types once told me that gold is good for killing all kinds of unnatural monsters,\n\nperhaps it applies here as well, though I do not know for certain.\n\nIt is important to note that  a frost witch is not a rabid animal, and they can be reasoned with. They are also possessed of terrible cunning and one should not expect the blind fury of mindless monster when dealing with them.\n\nIt is possible to treat with them and in fact they could exist within your own city, your very neighborhood and most would be unaware. They humor of a frost witch is quite changeable and every moment you stand in their presence you are in grave danger.\n\nThe truth is that they are fickle creatures, and there is no telling what a frost witch might do.\n\nIt is said that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them on it that the witch will be bound by her curse to do the clever mortal one favor. Though this is only rumor and would prove both difficult and dangerous to study.\n\nIn closing, frost witches are a dangerous fascination and one should not seek them lightly. They are elusive and hide among the peoples of the world, it is for this reason that we must be ever watchful lest we become their next meal.\n\nI hope that this book has been useful to you, the reader. And that this information will help you, should you ever have….\n\nAn encounter, with frost witches.\n\nBy Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date 8th of Deep Cold, 1516\n\nRevised 18th of Amber Cold, 1520", ""),
        StaticBook("On Bryophites", "Toodles", "On Bryophites\nBy: Revion M. Tathron\n\nAt first site, Bryophites may appear incredibly strange-- entirely green figures, with various plants growing on their 'skin'. However, Bryophites were once normal people-- they were merely transformed by a parasitic plant dubbed 'Verdigris Moss', which\n\nreplaces the biological material of a person with the biological material of a plant. This, naturally, induces many changes in a person. These changes include:\n-An increased vulnerability to fire and cold.\n\n-The ability to subconsciously create a sedative that numbs a significant amount of pain.\n-Plants now grow in abundance on the skin, more bountiful than those found naturally.\n-Now experience the drawbacks of voidal magic more quickly\n\n-Cannot use dark magic without becoming physically ill.\n-They now photosynthesize, with a lack of sunlight inducing various negative effects until death.\n-A small, cordoned-off section of their mind is produced, which can be spotted by a\n\nmental mage, which is presumably the area of the brain which the parasite controls to maintain the plantlike functions of the Bryophite.\n\nThere are no behavioral changes in Bryophites-- they are not more inclined towards insanity, as said in other accounts. The Bryophite that the author spoke with seemed completely normal, in terms of psychological and behavioral traits.\n\nFor further information, 'Vertigris Moss' in the Plants and Farming section of the Library of Dragur is recommended, as it provides a more in-depth list of the physical changes in Bryophites.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary V1", "§bAdeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's Bestiary\n\nContents:\n1. Beasts of Nature\n2. Natural Monstrosities\n3. Sentient Supernaturals\n3. Supernatural Monstrosities\n4. Constructs\n\n-Beasts of Nature-\n\nThese creatures are the beasts commonly seen throughout the world and pose no real threat to the innocent mundane.\n\nCanines: Either intelligent pack hunters or less witty companion animals, the canine often possesses sharp teeth and fur- unlike their Ursidae cousins, they are not often large and do not possess significantly sharp claws. Canines are known to be tamable.\n\nRats: These creatures are the messengers of coming pestilence and death, they've the standard qualities expected of small rodents. Extended exposure to these creatures often leads to sickness, earning them the nickname \"Plague bearers\".\n\nBats: These creatures are physically quite similar to the common rat despite the fact that they have wings and do not possess a tail.\nThey're generally nocturnal and have an enhanced sense of hearing which makes up for their poor vision.\n\nBirds: Variations of these are seen far and wide. From the common pigeon to the barn owl. The creatures have near countless variations and are often used to carry messages over long distances. They are mostly harmless.\n\nSand Tortoise: These creatures are of staggering size. We've precious little information on the beasts and taking one down would require no less than a siege party. The creature grows in size rivaling a small keep. They are extremely rare.\n\nSand Lizard: A common sight within the Orcish deserts. These creatures are surprisingly fast and can topple a target with very little effort. Their hide is nothing worthy of note. Their bones are of decent density and genuinely sturdy.\n\n-Natural Monstrosities-\n\nThese are the creatures commonly found within nature but are considered perverse and diluted in purpose. They're to be hunted and their existence extinguished.\n\nThe Harpy: These monsters have the ability to fly and resemble ugly women- their skin is extremely oily and susceptible to fire. They're bones are quite brittle and will crack under pressure. Their feathers are fine for use in arrows and their pelts make-\n\n-for good middle class clothing. They've a cruel sense of humor. They are known to scoop up targets and drop them from lethal heights. If a Harpy nest is discovered it is suggested that it be burned immediately.\n\nKrummavisur: Resembling a Raven, though staggering in size. These beasts have awe-inspiring wing spans and considerable strength.\nThey scoop up their prey and toss them immeasurable distances. The beast is not to be fought alone. They can kick up dust-\n\n-with the density to block sight for yards. When effort is applied they can shove a man in full plate to his knees with the power of the air from their wings alone. It is suggested that the feet are struck, as they are quite thin and easy to amputate.\n\nCockatrice: An odd looking creature. Standing at the height of a small building with the width to match.\nThey are quite intimidating to fight up close and are able to fly, rendering close combat to be the inevitable result of an encounter.\n\nThe Cockatrice has the ability to exhale a thick gray smog that turns whoever comes in contact with it to stone. Being submerged in water will negate this effect.\nTheir skin is unholy in strength, steel will hardly damage it, an aurum blade is required\n\nThe Beast's bones are strong as stone and they've the strength to topple a building with ease.\n\nLeaf Apes: Fundamentally illusive creatures that have flesh as hard as rock and bones like fresh timber. They possess decent strength for their size but struggle to penetrate leather. They tend to rush a target and make an effort to climb atop its face.\n\nOnce atop the victim's face, the Leaf Ape will tear at the flesh. Bladed steel weapons are practically useless against these creatures and will often break upon contact with their skin- blunt weapons are suggested as well as aurum swords.\n\nCave Leeches: A beast that drops down on it's targets and spews acid onto them, it has the strength to render armor useless. They only attack in complete darkness. \n\nNo one has survived an encounter thus far.\n\nDrakes: Creatures with bat-like wings, the ability to breathe flame, scaly hides, complete with muscular legs and tail-- these truly majestic beasts have captured the awe of men for centuries. Despite this, magical perversion has lead to the Drake species\n\nundergoing various mutations and become near extinct. It is expected that combat with a Drake be avoided and alternative methods to killing be used to neutralise the threat such a beast poses. The Drake's main weaknesses are its wings, mouth and eyes,\n\n-however this beast will continue fighting until the last drop of blood runs from it's wound. Decapitation and siege weaponry is suggested.\n\nEnlarged Arachnid:\n\nThe average spider, though colossal in size and extremely venomous- they are susceptible to fire and relatively easy to defeat compared to other beasts in this compendium.\n\n-Sentient Naturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with if possible and relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane population.\n\nTroll: Usually found lurking under bridges, in caves or forests. These beasts can be at times helpful and friendly-- at other times they are forces to be reckoned with. Trolls are generally quite intelligent and are capable of speech, complex emotion and-\n\n-co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to use aurum and to disable it's method of movement, trolls are known to carry enormous amounts of weight in the form of fat around their waist and are unable to get up if any of their legs are damaged.\n\n-Sentient Supernaturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with and if possible relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane.\n\nSpecters: Spirits without bodies, these beings can be benevolent, neutral or malevolent, just like a living person. They can only be harmed by aurum as normal metals will pass straight through them.\nSpecters have the ability to wield enchanted weaponry\n\n-and don enchanted armor, some have the ability to fly and cast spells, those that have this ability use it to deadly effect. It is suggested that aurum weaponry be used combined with a high-guard stance.\nSpecters are vulnerable to salt and it is-\n\n-suggested that the perimeter in which the spirit is manifesting be surrounded by lines of pure sea salt.\n\n-Constructs-\n\nThese are the result of spells or golemmancy, they are able to fit into the supernatural sentient category as well as the monstrous supernatural category depending on what they are- constructs usually have a master and a purpose to foll\n\nHunters: \n\nSharing many traits with a specter, the Hunter has the ability to fly- it wears large, heavy armor but is not impeded in any way by this fact. The Hunters are apparently a sort of Golem gone rogue, they once served a holy order and sought\n\n-slay dangerous Magi. Now they slay any who wield magic, including Marked Men. Hunters explode when defeated and it is advised that those who have defeated it clear the area before it does so, as shrapnel is often projected.\nAurum seems to weaken the-§\n\n-creature considerably, though it is probably wise to use steel in order to damage the armor before an aurum weapon is presented.\nHalf swording is suggested due to the armored nature of this foe.\n\nGolems: The result of powerful runes and magic, Golems can take many forms- from colossal lumbering humanoid to slithering metal snake, all Golems have an 'Impera' who dictates their every action-- Golems will attempt to protect these individuals at all-\n\n-costs. These constructs are often the result of a soul being bound to the magegold core, destroying this would most likely neutralise the threat. \nWays to destroy the Golem depend on a number of things including environment and the material the Golem\n\n-made of. Golems made of stronger materials may need to be cast from great heights, thrown into watery depths or toppled into a substance hot enough to melt metal.\n\n-Supernatural Monstrosities-\n\nThese creatures defy all reason. They serve no purpose in this world and are to be slain.\n\nNecrophages: These creatures come in two variations; Fleshed and Skeletal.\n\nFleshed typically maintain a slumped posture, they've considerable strength and an immunity to pain.\n\nAurum weaponry is recommended for these types of creatures.\n\nAlone, their presence is a joke, but when amassed it's often best to simply route.\nThe method of reanimation is unknown, however it is to be noted that they appear more frequently around areas of frequent fighting or wickedness.\nFire is a weakness.\n\nLich: The ultimate product of an individual's greed for power or knowledge. Liches are beings that have made a transformation into entities powered purely on arcane energies and a deep seated hatred for those that get in the way of more power.\n\nTypes of Liches vary broadly and improvisation is to be expected. One recurring trait seems to be the presence of a crystal known as the phylactery- it is where the Lich's soul is rumoured to be kept, destroying this crystal will kill the creature.\n\nBloodsuckers/Sangbriseur:\nThese creatures take the form of an obscene lump of slimey acid. Depending on their environment, the creature can absorb it's surroundings and become deadlier-- there are such things as Bloodsuckers who have absorbed fire,\n\nbecoming thrice as dangerous as their acidic counterparts. To dispose of the creature, it is suggested that it be cut into smaller pieces and set alight-- be sure that every chunk is burnt or else it will regenerate over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Killin' a troll", "§bJentos", "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n     Killin' a troll\n\n\n  By Jentos Adam, last representant of the house of Blackwood.\n\n\n\n\n\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"Dear reader, in this book you shall learn to: recognize, flee and kill a troll.\"\n\nIntroduction\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"Troll. Nasty, cruel and stupid creatures capable of destroying whole towns, And fierce war-beasts.\"\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nWere to find a troll?\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nTroll's can be found about everywhere in these wild lands. From the frozen dwarven plains. To the heat of the Caliphate!\"\n\n\"Troll's like to live in unforested mountainous regions, dark caves in the\n\nmountains. Or in a big clearing in the forest.\"\n\nRecognizing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxWho has never pictured a troll? Big ugly figure walking in the forest? But the're are alot of different types of orcs and sub-trolls like half trolls half\n\nmen!\"\n\n\"Trolls can vary from 8 feet when young to a giant 20 feet tall!\nThey have a relative big orc like head with a few men-like features.\"\n\n\nFleeing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxRunning away from a\n\ntroll in a rather forested area is easier than in a mountainous or flat region.\"\n\nTactic's: \n\"If you find yourself in a forested or near a forested region, your best bet is to simply go we're the tree's are smaller so you can slow the troll\n\nand get out of its reach.\"\n\n\"Hiding in a cave isn't a good idea, a hungry troll is apt to wait a long time to be able to get his supper (especially if it's the trolls own cave!).\"\n\nKillin' a troll!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"In this final section, you will learn how to \n\n       Slay\n      -----\nThese mighty creatures!.\n\n\"The troll's weak spot, (like many other beats) are the eye!\nUnfortunatly it is easy to see that being able to get a good shot at them isn't easy.\"\n\n\"The trick is to, hack the legs until it falls, wait t'ill it reaches down or bend or simply atta\n\nfrom a good height!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"On this. I say to you! Have thy luck I never had!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Stoutchasms, V1", "§bMiscellus", "11th OF SUN'S SMILE, 1521\n\nA man came up to Dimlin Hammerfish, asking him if he knew of a (previously murdered) Dza the Old. After notifying the stranger that Dza was, in fact, dead, the man did not believe him: he repeated many times\n\nthat he had been 'out' for so long, then refused any evidence about Dza's murder. Dimlin told him that the murder took place a full 15 years ago before, annoyed, this man seemed to float out of the tavern he met the dwarf within. \n\nThis stranger was\n\nof a deep gray skin, a Cave dwarf not Doomforged but almost ethereal. His habit of... floating and coloration would suggest that he would be a ghost, but the only cases that I've heard of such were when a Dwarf met a Paragon himself! \n\nAfter a while, the\n\n'ghost,' as I will call him, entered the establishment once more. Dimlin asked him to leave and, when he went to put a hand on him to shove him out, his skin did not connect; the limb went straight through the translucent figure as it would with any kind\n\nof revenant. \nDimlin was confused. He asked the \"man\" to, if he was truly there, act upon a nearby torch; the torch proceeded to fall down, extinguished, almost at his command. \n\nThe ghost's name was Dunham Stoutchasm, which is a name that\n\nreminds me of.. something. The Stoutchasms are referenced at the statue of Hogarth, but I know not why. Something is in their midst, but I do not know what! I have heard that they are a clan of mystics and magicians, but not much more.\n\nThe spirit soon disappeared as Dimlin went to find me. As we have talked, many strange events have occurred: wind has blown in from all directions, even in the protected caverns of Kal'Akash, and a feeling of someone watching permeates my skull. It seems\n\nlike--\n\nIt just happened again.\n\nThe doors flew open! We now follow the events we see..\n\nAn arm protrudes around the corner.\n\nDear Dungrimm, it's a ghost.\n\nDunham has asked to find a Dzralen. Dimlin told him that Dzralen was dead, and so was he, but the ghost refused the answers, just asking if he could see the King. I awkwardly stumbled my words as he asked more and more confusing questions, talking to in-\n\nvisible beings outside of our sight... He asked for paper, said he could go for a drink, all out of nowhere... The torches in the alley go out. It becomes hard to write. The ghost disappears. \n\nDimlin managed to see the shadow of the ghost return to\n\nhis pub, and we have been following him. It's too fast to write much about. \n\nI have found out about the Stoutchasms from Hogarth Irongut himself. They were a clan of dwarves that lived here in Vailor before we came here-- they were\n\nan incredibly advanced race, with towering golems and amazing cities. They were quick to attack us Aegisian Dwedmar with what they thought was superior tech, but our numbers and strength held true: we fended them off for a long time before the Stoutchasms\n\nsimply faded away. They were not exterminated, but they did.. disappear. Dzralen was a higher-up in the clan, possible even the Clan Father. It is imperative that we find this ghost again and find out what happened to the rest of the Stoutchasms.", ""),
