        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "5th of Snow's Maiden,§0\n§0Sutica.§0\n§0\n§0The fresh wind from the Rivers of Sutica are ever-so remarkable, the Suticans are sure lucky to live in this breeze. I came to Sutica for trade but the quietness has taken me in shock.\n\nSutica always was that cold place, but recently it has been warmer then normal. Probably something with the gods that are kindly these Suticans believe, Interesting people they are. But the Guards can be annoying since my last engagement with them.\n\nThey seem to be afraid of my appearance, and dont really expect someone like me to be in a quiet place like Sutica, but you should always expect the unexpected.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I don't know how to support you, so this is my best way to go about it.§0\n§0\n§0It isn't much, but know that you have more friends than you think. We gotcha back covered.§0\n§0\n§0So don't waste time on grinding and be with others instead;\n\nlet them enjoy your company, you wonderful person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Myths", "§bWayward Druid Respiren", "* The Myth of the *           Great War\nMany moons ago a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards -one good and one evil- that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until  utterly triumphant\n\n Seeking to purge their rivals from the land. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning final victory . Through their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devastation on the world,\n\nForests blazed up, islands sank into the sea, entire races became extinct. Eventually, the the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict.\n\n Shocked by the destruction, the Goddess sent a vision to a single woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a druidic order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology.\n\n\n\nWith the guidance of her goddess, the  Order grew in strength Until finally it had the power to intervene in the wizard war...\n\nThe force of young druids pooled  their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\n\nOnce the former wizards now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the Order began to heal the lands.\n\nSince then, the druidic order  continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars of good  and evil no longer mar the precious land.\n\n But, the Order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the  guilds of warring wizards- those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows.\n\nEach guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered. \n\n-As recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons", ""),
        StaticBook("Aphidylytes", "Anonymous", "Scribed from the last words of Urangoi Ballenz, fifth descendant of Urguan’s generations-\n\nI am stuck. I ventured too deep into the coil of the Motley Ravine, and after a wrong turn in one of the\n\nabandoned mines I suppose I was knocked out. I’ve awoken to be affixed to a wall of some gooey, thick sludge. It binds me to the wall, but luckily I have my journal wedged beside me, and close enough to write on. Nearby I\n\nhear a woman, I can barely make out her lectures, but it sounds like she is preaching in a far off cavern… I fear for my life here.\n\nDeep underground, beneath the ridges of the Motley Ravine, lay a muddied labyrinth\n\nmarbled in stone and the hardened byproduct of ant-like construction. Riddling the maze of tunnels and crevices once scuttled swarms of uncountable hordes, writhing masses of legged, exoskeletal shells\n\nand tibia, clusters of wriggling bugs formed out of coxa and spinnerets. With thick armor of biomass from their antennas to their thoraxes, in the pitch abyss roamed the aphids, grand and gargantuan in both number and size.\n\n\nBut now, all have vanished. Not a single critter may be sought scuttling about in those barren halls, decrepit with time’s withering. That being due to collapse. The Deep now only consists of a chamber; the\n\npith. The lifeless bluff of the overworld resides without motion while all of the Aphidylytes are compacted into their own deposits and veins of sand and sediment. Except for one.\n\nIn the core of one\n\nmesa’s knoll, wedged down below in a sliver of openness, lies the central crux. It too lies in stillness, but not in death, but in concealed ambush. The ancient Hive Queen rests in unconscious slumber, awaiting the day for\n\nexcavation of a foolish kind before her automaticly reactive limbs may draw in the prey and feed upon it to revive her, and thus the Hive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gary's Adventure", "§bJeffwise Sadget", "The Adventures of\nGary Ironhammer.\n\nBy Jeffwise Sadget.\n\nGary Ironhammer was a very proud dwarf. He would always go around in his suit and he never left without a book and quill. He stood at 3.5ft tall with a long beard flowing down his breast, covering his tie with ginger hairs.\n\nGary's first big adventure began at a small town called Skandia, Gary's hometown. It all started when a friend of his, Erak Stormvogel, told him of a great leader, although neither knew the name of this man both were determined to meet him.\n\nThey started looking for him at the grand dwarven city. Although many people had heard of the leader no one knew his name or where abouts so the pair moved on to the elf city. The elf city was useful to the pair as they weren't even allowed in.\n\nHowever, they did meet an elf interested in finding the great leader. They allowed the elf to join the search. Soon, the trio arrived at the grandest city of all, Petrus, home of the Humans. The humans allowed the trio inside.\n\nSadly, not one soul from Petrus knew where to find the great leader so the trio decided to go exploring. On their journeys they met massive giants, hordes of the undead and bandit camps. They also met good things on their journey.\n\nThey came across other explorers and isolated military camps. The trio also stumbled upon vast canyons, great wizard towers and ruined castles.\n\nAfter many months of searching the trio found a small town called raev. The town was rather empty and peaceful. In this town they found an inn to sleep at overnight. The inn keeper, a young elf named Eregon was rather creepy but he did not disturb them.\n\nThe next morning the trio, Thialdir Nengeldir the elf, Erak Stormvogel the Dwarf and Gary Ironhammer the Dwarf went to ask if they could stay at the town for a while, and that's when they found him...\n\nAt the other end of the crowd stood a man. His voice was direct and clear, as the words came floating out of his mouth, the town fell silent. The great leader Tuvya addressed the town about small matters. But the trio knew.\n\nThey knew this was the man they had been looking for. The great leader Tuvya, a man who ran a rather small town, although that changed rather quickly. Within a few days of meeting the trio, the great Emperor Tuvya had his corination!\n\nThe End!\n\nThis book is not a true story although all the character did live in Raev before Tuvya became Emperor and all the characters were, and still are, loyal to Emperor Tuvya!", ""),
        StaticBook("Gardening Guide", "§b'Finek", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-          How to\n         Remove\n         Weeds\n         from\n         Crops\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nIt has long be tought that when you see a weed in your garden that you should pull it out at once.\n\nThis I say to you is not what you do, lest you rip up your crops with the weeds.\n\nWeeds at an early stage wrap themselves around the very roots of the crop for that is where they find a lot of water going, by doing so it takes away a little water from the crop though not very much.\n\nWhen the time of harvest comes you shall then harvest the crop along with the weeds. Place both the weeds and crops into a basket and throw them into the air, by doing the crops will fall down into the basket.\n\nThe weeds on the other hand are much lighter and would blow away even on a low wind.\n\nAfter repeating this for a good five minutes you should have mostly crops in your basket.\n\nIf you missed a couple you can simply go through it by hand.\n\n\nHere are the risks of what can happen if you do the opposite:\n\n1: The weed has wrapped itself mostly around the crops roots, so by pulling up the weed you risk pulling up the growing crop.\n\n2: Keep the crops well watered, if you don't the weeds will take almost all of it.\n\n3: You need at least a small wind blowing through the air for the weeds to be caried away on the wind, make sure it isn't very strong though or some of your crops might get away!\n\n\n\n          -=+=-\n        Written by\n\n          'Fenik\n     The Cervitaur\n          -=+=-", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bAeran", "A good luck charm!", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Proverbs", "§bMalog'Yar", "*As you open the book, you see in its pages a collection of proverbs written by the shaman, Malog'Yar. Each one is individually numbered for ease of memorization, it seems. They don't appear to have a particular order to them, but must\n\nhave been written as they came to the shaman's mind.\n((As in my other books, only those words which are actually different in the Blah are written in said language. The rest are in Common for ease of reading.))\n\n1. The lust for power is the beginning of shame. It concieves, agh brings forth arrogance. Arrogance, when it reaches maturity, brings forth humiliation.\n2. The path to honor is paved with sacrifice.\n\n3. Gold is a heavy thing, agh bub'hosh is the burden of he who hoards it. It will crush the heart, agh bring low the spirit.\n4.He who forgets his ancestors of the past will have nub future for his descendents.\n5.Food, water,\n\nshelter, praise; these things are wasted, when given to ash with nub honor.\n6.All is vanity for the whitewash, for he has abandoned his ancestors. He has departed from his purpose in life.\n7.Find that skill which lat are hosh\n\nat. Do it with honor, for even the lowly chicken farmer can glorify Krug.\n8.Do nub scorn simplicity. It is a chest of many treasures.\n9.Hosher is a small blarg with a mate agh cubs, than an empty palace.\n10.Integrity,\n\nuprightness, honor, discipline agh wisdom are the bones of the spirit. Without these, lat can nub stand.\n11.Hosher to be a blind man with wisdom, than a fool with many eyes.\n12.Luxury is an open gate to complacency.\n\n13.Complacency is a downhill path to the flatting of the spirit. It is an easy path to descend, but returning uphill is strenuous, requiring diligence.\n14.Bring up lats cubs in the way of honor, for they will take lats place in the future.\n\n15.This year's swineherd may be next year's Rex.\n16.Remember your brother, agh be quick to share his burden.\n17.The hardship of life is a refining furnace. It hurts for the time, but melts away that which would make\n\nlat weak.\n18.Lats body is a gift. Use it hoshly. Do nub abuse it, agh do nub let it wither.\n19.Life is work. Work hard or starve.\n20.The cactus lives in the dry sands, needing little nourishment. It is stronger for it.\n\n21.Hosher is a bag of rotten flesh, than a feast in the blarg of the dishonorable.\n22.He who lives with nub honor is like a fortress made of dry twigs or a zult made of still air: useless.\n23.Taking a title simply for the\n\nsake of taking a title is like eating sharp blades simply for the sake of eating.\n24.A wise blah is more precious than all the gems beneath the earth.\n25.Hosher to be flat for what is honorable, than to abandon lats\n\nintegrity simply to extend lats life.\n26.Honor is nub a currency to be traded. Do nub treat it as such.\n27.A life with nub honor is as meaningless as letters with nub order.\n28.Do nub tolerate weakness in body,\n\nmind or spirit.\n29.He who works hard will have his bread.\n30.Feeding the lazy is like planting the wind. It accomplishes nubthing.\n31.Be satisfied with food agh a cave. It may be all lat have ash day.\n\n32.Do nub envy the rich. Their decadence will make them soft.\n33.Do nub peep down on the poor. They are nub blinded by the glimmer of gold.\n34.Minas often do little more than disappear.\n35.Deceit agh\n\ntwisted words only clutter agh clog the mouth. Eventually, lat will choke on them.\n36.Blah what lat mean, nub what others want to hear.\n37.A slimy heart will slip, agh fall to its destruction.\n38.Rulers, do nub\n\nbe haughty. Ash day, lats reign will end, agh another will take lats place.\n39.He who is wise heeds the truthful rebuke.\n40.The fool surrounds himself with flatterers, agh is nub aware when ruin comes.\n41. Hosh is the\n\nfemale who bears strong cubs, agh works tirelessly to nourish their bodies agh spirits.\n42.Happy is the male who finds her, agh keeps her.\n43.Hosher is ash honorable lifemate, than ash hundred weak mates.\n44.As a blarg will\n\nnub stand on mist, cloud or vapor, neither will a family stand on weakness, foolishness of dishonor.\n45.Walk as Krug walked, agh honor the spirits. This will keep lats path straight.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Snelf's Greed", "§bJacob 'sharpblade' Jackstorm", "Once upon a time there was a snow elf prince. He wasn't a bit of a cunt; he was a massive cunt. As thus, he eyed Shreck's Swamp with some pretty cheeky greed, this is where the cunt crossed lines into being a bloody well idjit. You see, Shreck's might\n\nknows no ends, he's fucking tougher then me mum and she'll fucking bite your ear off for talking shit about her aweful onion pie. Anyways, Shreck found the fuck out, ork's connections are bloody everywhere, found one in me soup once. Tasted nice.\n\nSo, upon his majestic steed he set out from his swamp in the orkish desert until he got to his shoddy little wall. With a single leap he was over the walls. Killing the entire camp he moved to fucking RKO him, breaking his face, after a backflip drop\n\nkick. Then Shreck killed the snow elf prince and everyone lived okay. Except the snelves; snelves were fucking dead.\n\nAnd that, kids, is why you stay out of the blue cunt's fucking swamp.", ""),
        StaticBook("*A rotten note*", "§bThe Oogie Man", "Soon i will come~\n\nSoon you will be mine!\n\nI'm talking to you...the oogie man will come and he wants to play with you...\n\nLove,\nThe Oogie Boogie Man\n\n\nI talk to you...Arch Druid.\n\n      O           O\n.                          .\n .                        .\n   .                   .\n     .             .\n       .       .\n          . .", ""),
        StaticBook("CMask Guidebook", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\n\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\n\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\n\nSafety Tips\n1.) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people. \n\n2.) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness\n\nthe Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n\n3.) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of break or breaches in your mask's special\n\nprotective filtration and sealant systems.\n\n4.) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be\n\nresponsible for your life but to prove you have what it takes to survive in a hazardous world.\n\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place\n\nand secure along both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism\n\nthat make up the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are\n\nunsure as to how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also can along the main folds and seams of the\n\nmask to make sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for\n\nbreaches as a single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\n\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\n\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\n\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\n\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\n\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\n\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\n\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\n\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then\n\nurges you to remove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\n\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mr & Mrs Carrot!", "§bAylun'sae Tenna'tahu", "The Gallant Adventures of Mister and Missus Carrot!!\n\n  -Aylun'sae\n     Tenna'tahu\n\nDay One:\n The Carrot Patch\n\n The morning was a clear one, the season good for growing. Upon this fine morning, Mister Carrot stretched his roots and said to himself, \"Now isn't this a fine day!\" and with that he\n\nuprooted and went to start on his morning walk. \n  Upon this walk, he saw Mister Potato teaching his daughter how to starch. As a neighborly sort of fellow, Mister Potato called out, \"Hello Mister Potato! A fine day it is today!\"\n\n  To this, Mister Potato angrily replied, \"Yeah! A fine day to your skinny rooty self! Stay away from my daughter you orange fiend!\"\n  Mister Carrot didn't mind Mister Potato's angry outbursts. Usually they just meant he was being friendly. So on Mister\n\nCarrot went with his walk, and a fine walk it was.\n\nDay Two:\n  Mister Rabbit\n\n From time to time the garden patch would have visitors who would come from far and away to see the vegetables growing and raising their offshoots. Mister Rabbit was one of these fine fellows, and\n\nquite the self proclaimed vegetable afficionado he was!\n On one of the gallant mornings that Mister Carrot went for one of his delightful walks, lo and behold!! Mister Rabbit was meandering down his usual route of walking!\n Mister Carrot was quite beside\n\nhimself with emotion, \"What is this?? A Mister Rabbit?? In the gardens???\" It was quite the dilemma.\n Mister Carrot, being an unusually amiable fellow, of course, thought it best to give Mister Rabbit the appropriate welcome. And so, without further ado,\n\nMister Carrot found himself walking himself towards Mister Potato's usual garden bed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion On Truth", "Sofetios", "An Opinion On Truth\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        -By Sofetios\n\nBefore we begin, I just wanted to say that this book will shortly cover a variety of subjects regarding my opinion of fear, doubt, truth, belief, lies, and how I think they correlate with each other. This book is just my opinion.\n\nYou don’t need to believe it or not believe it. To begin we will start with fear.\n\n                    Fear\n\nWhat is Fear? Fear is when you are afraid of something. But what does it mean to be afraid of something?\n\nI think fear occurs most often in the absence of knowledge, when you aren’t sure about something. Fear of the unknown is a very common thing, as the unknown can possibly do anything.\n\nIf you had complete confidence that something will happen a certain way, then you likely will have little fear about it unless it is a bad thing that will occur.\n\nThough if something goes the wrong way when you are fully confident about something, That may cause the next subject to happen. Doubt.\n\n                   Doubt\n\nDoubt is something that can cause fear.\n\nAs I explained earlier it ties in with the lack of knowledge in something. Doubt can be a very powerful thing. It changes, or attempts to change your perspective on things, for better or worse, but usually worse.\n\nTo avoid both fear and doubt, I think it is best to find one of the things that defeats both. Truth.\n\n                  Truth\n\nTruth is a very simple thing, Though it can be very hard, or easy, to obtain.\n\nIf you know the truth of something, that means you have true knowledge in a certain part or all aspects of it.  This defeats both doubt and fear, because fear is caused mainly by doubt, and doubt requires uncertainty in something.\n\nThere is, however, something that increases doubt. Most all of us do it. Lie.\n\n                     Lie\n\nLies corrupt the truth, they make things harder to make out.\n\n In my perspective I think that the truth is a very simple thing to understand, it is lies that corrupt it and makes it more unnecessarily complicated.  In my opinion, lying causes most of doubt and fear.\n\nThe next and last subject I like to call absolute truth. \n\n           Absolute Truth\n\nThe thing with how doubt works is it tries to prevent us from getting to the truth.\n\n Lies and doubt have happened so much that sometimes even if we find the absolute truth, we still doubt it, Unless of course we believe it’s the truth. And finally, what to believe is the truth. Well, that’s for you to decide.\n\n(Please let me know if you like my philosophical writing by telling me in person or sending a bird! ((Sofetios)) )\n\n-Sofetios", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Balrog'", "§bArinislia", "'The Taint'\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1475\n\n       The day was calm and gentle. The sun was high, shining its rays down upon the Father Tree as the druids went about their day. One of the druid children suddenly runs up, gasping for breath as she appeared to have been running.\n\nShe looked panicked, saying that she ran into a Dread Lord summoning something in the nearby woods. Suddenly a loud shriek was heard. . All look up the natural carved stairs of the Father Tree to see the Dread Lord stand before them.\n\n. A ghoul standing next to him along with some followers, the Dread Lord unleashed the ghoul down upon the druids, commanded to kill them all. During this, the Dread Lord then turned and advanced up the tree,\n\n, telling his followers to block all that dare move up. The ghoul was quickly defeated, but not before spreading its taint on all that it bit along with ones that were near when it exploded.\n\nIt appeared that if something wasn’t done quickly to cleanse, they perished.\n\n       The druids now advancing further up the tree, the followers were quickly removed before advancing further up.\n\n. Again the druids were blocked and met with a horrible abomination. The Dread Lord cackled down at them, before unleashing a balrog upon the druids, charging down full force.\n\nSeveral that were in the way were easily knocked off the tree to their deaths.  The druids seemed unorganized, yet with some coordination from a few within the order, they quickly rooted the balrog and threw it off the tree.\n\nThe Dread Lord far gone by then yet the top of the tree tainted. The druids advance upward, circling around the taint and focused, using their healing magic to remove the corruption of the tree.\n\nBelow where the balrog  fell off the tree, several came from different nations and organizations and struck down the abomination where it stood.  With the Father Tree healed once more, the druids descended down and helped cleanse and heal the wounded.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Ring", "§b[Dedicant] Heroxis", "Fairy Ring\n\nby Heroxis\n\nSearching the night.\nNight quietly green.\nDeep in the forest.\nNo one has seen.\n\nThe circle of fungi.\nI enter you now.\nA force I sense.\nGreeting with a bow.\n\nTo sing in the rain.\nTo write in the sun.\nTo draw in the clouds.\nAttuned as one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Marrow", "§bUnknown", "I know that you have been visited by the Order of Youth, what have you been doing to get them to notice you? Surely you are not contesting what he has done, he found it that’s for sure, and you know how his followers become when you question him.\n\nIblees would be jealous of their rage. You know that humans fear for their short lives, trying to remove hope of extending it will make them mad. I hope you didn’t get hurt by them, the best of health to you, may Aeriel bless your body.\n\nAs for what you asked me to get, I convinced the town’s people that their death were diseased. You will have the corpses sent to you in a week’s time. I am glad to hear that you have traded those foul potions for the study of anatomy and healing.\n\nIf you ever require any more wisdom or help in the study, do not be scared to ask me. I have been your friend for many years, and your doctor for far more.\n\n\nSafe study,\n     Doctor Marrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Moot ((11/8/14))", "§bArinislia", "6th of The Grand Harvest, 1480\n\n        Two of the Arch druids appeared to have attended this meeting, Arch druid Gi’garun, and Arch druid Leyun. Guides were Sequoia Druid Lillith and Mist Druid Earendur. The Spirit of Nature also attended as well.\n\n First Topic :\n\nArch druid Gi’garun brought to attention was the path that all druids should be taking, the path of the Aspects. This is a path that all druids follow to help preserve and maintain the balance in nature.\n\nIt was unfortunate that two druids were un-attuned before this meeting, the Metal Druid Sharr and the Pumpkin Druid Aphoros. We understand the reasons why they stray from the path of druidism, We understand the reasons why they stray from\n\nthe path of druidism, but they cannot keep their attunement and title for their actions will not only hurt themselves, but the Order as a whole. \n\nSecond Topic:\n\nThe announcement of my own attunement\n\nand joining the order, I became known as the Owl Druid.\n\nThird topic:\n\nThe removal of non-active dedicants. There are lots of unaccounted for dedicants\n\nand the dedicants grotto is completely filled with non-active members.. It is recommended the removal of the non-active ones and to move ‘ALL’ druids to the upper housing so there are spaces for the new dedicants.\n\nGuides and Arch druids are moved to the new Guide grotto. . It was also mentioned that a new dedicant grotto could be made to accommodate all the new dedicants.\n\nFourth Topic :\n\nThe stepping down of Arch druid Gi’garun. In his place, he appointed Lillith to be the new Arch druid. Now a guide spot is empty and a new Arch druid stands up to watch over the Order.\n\nFifth topic :\n\nPine Druid Gi’garun being made a Hierophant. \n\nSixth topic:\n\nThe Spirit of Nature warning the Order of an old threat that seems to have come back to the world.\n\n. In the pass it threatened Luminaire and the grove. An unnatural tree that grew beneath the city and strangled the life out of the land and spread corruption. The Snow Arch Druid Zeremdos seemed to know more about it, yet he is no longer with us.\n\nThe Spirit of Nature stated that it was placed by the Black Scourge and feels there is a fully sized one now in this world, growing larger as it devours plants.. It was said that Solace Druid Callax exploded to destroy the threat last time,\n\nyet now this sounds like on a much larger scale. We were also warned it is guarded by something so killing it will prove to be more of a problem.A way of finding it is the feeling of death from trees. Do not shrug it\n\noff, for it may lead to the tree itself. Also there might be books on this matter and how to destroy it.\n\nSeventh Topic :\n\nUpon the Moot ending, a suddenly strange dark light appear above the disc ball.\n\n. It flew into it before forming into a figure below on the tree itself. The image was the spirit of Vardak, giving a warning. . The one that captured the grove in Asulon has returned to try and reclaim the grove once more.\n\n. A witch named Kyral, who is now undead and wishing to reclaim the grove once more. The spirit also stated that in order to talk to him again, we must seek out shamans to do so. And with that, the spirit departed back to the spirit world.\n\nEighth Topic :\n\nThe shunning and banishment of Evark. His crimes included of the burning the Frost Druid Dain to death and killing many others in his destruction.\n\n The After Story~\n\nThe Moot was then ended and everyone parted their own ways. Arch druid Lillith headed back down to the guide where I encountered her for a short time before departing.\n\nForgetting to inform Lillith of a detail, I came back to the grotto to come across the witch herself, Kyral. She found Lillith and cornered her in the Guide Grotto. Pine Druid Gi’garun came up behind me and quickly engaged as Kyral conjured fire\n\nfire at Lillith and shot it at her. During the encounter, Gi’garun was burned in the face, but Lillith and I quickly subdued the witch.. Angered form within Lillith’s thoughts and was shown in her rash actions.\n\n. Gi’garun and I made her see through her clouded mind and come back to reason and thus, correct justice was passed. Kyral sentenced to death and thus was ripped apart by the very vines and branches that Gi’garun and I provided from the encounter.\n\nThough our victory would be short-lived, for we assumed she is an undead and thus will be back for us again. And as of now, Kyral is now kill on sight. \n\nI put this story of what happened after the moot in here\n\nhere for this is a lesson to be taught to all druids. Do not let anger and impure emotions cloud your reasoning and judgment. To truly protect and guide others, never start conflict, only defend and end it.\n\n~Owl Druid Arinislia", ""),
        StaticBook("Pastries Anthos", "§bJistuma", "________________\n~                        ~\n\nPastries of Anthos\n\n\n~----------------~\n\nIn the mind of a child, there will always be a love for the sweet taste of cake. I have traveled the lands of Anthos after my love for pastries grew with my mother’s skill, and family’s bakery. Watching the children laugh and smile whenever they came and\n\nI served them a slice of cake, I decided that bakery would as well be my way of life. With the destruction of my home and bakery in Asulon, I had decided that I would search and try new recipes with the ingredients of all over the realm. I have collected\n\nsome to this recipe book, for others to bring a smile to other children.\n\nCheesecake of Salvus\nBefore the fall of Salvus I was able to try out their ingredients, and create a well rounded cheesecake. Sugar and wheat Dawn’s bakery, the eggs fresh from the farms, and the cheese came from a kind shepherd.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Two hand size goat cheeses\n-A glass full of goat milk cream\n-Three mugs of flour\n-Two soup spoon of refined sugar.\n-One fresh egg\n\nRemember to start heating the oven before you start mixing the ingredients. The Cheese and the cream first have to be added to the flour and mixed until fully clear. I advise that you slowly add the milk as the cheese is mixed with the flour. The sugar\n\nand eggs come after, or they would not mix very well. Mix well with the rest and Grease and flour a pan. The oven should be hot by now, so pour the mix inside the pan, and then the pan inside the oven. When you start smelling a sweet cheese aroma,\n\nthe cheesecake, and serve.\n\nHoney cookies\nI was quite amazed that the elves of Luminaire did not use sugar in their food, curious as that may be, their pastries were still quite sweet. The use of honey was their secret, very pleasant when used in cookies.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-One cup of Redbee honey\n-One duck egg\n-A bit of cinnamon\n-Two cups of forest wheat flour\n\nMakes 16 cookies.\n\nMore than difficult to make, the ingredients are quite hard to find, if you are not an elf yourself. Simply preheat the oven, and mix everything up. It will appear very hard, it is suppose to. With a spoon place on a mix in a pan, and place in the oven.\n\nKrill cake\nThe dwarves sure have some interesting tastes, the Krill cake being one of the most unique pastries I found. A pastry made of ingredients of the sea and eaten with a side mug of Ale.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Two mugs of Ale\n-A mug of Beer\n-Two mugs Whale Blubber\n-Krill, which is a paste of many small crustaceans\n\nThis recipe is quite hard to make. You will have to first preheat oil in a cauldron as you prepare the mix. In a bowl, mix half of the Krill, a mug and a half of the Whale Blubber, and the mug of Beer. Mix until even, it will appear to be a bit slimy. Mix\n\nthe rest of the Krill and Whale Blubber in another bowl, it will be able to hold its form. Place the slimy mix inside the other mix and close it. After making many of them, place inside a fishing net and deep fry in the hot oil. Let cool before you grab\n\na mug of Ale and drink another as you eat the Krill cakes.\n\nPine needle crackers\nEven those recipes that appear quite weird to ever be taught about, I have found. In the south snow mountains of the Urguan kingdom, I discovered the use of pine needles and seaweed in a result of hard crackers.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-A bowl of newborn pine needles\n-Five strips of dried seaweed\n-Two sweet potatoes\n-One cave cow mushroom\n-Two Owl eggs\n\nWithout any wheat in those cold lands, the residents of VaerHaven came up with using potatoes to create their dough. After removing the skin of the potato, cut it as small as you can before you add the egg. Let a few small mushrooms that were taken from\n\nthe back of cave cows, and pour everything into a frying pan. Mix everything up, and let it cook for a moment. When the red bits of the mushroom start turning brown, take the frying pan from the fire and let cool over snow. Not many pine needles are\n\nneeded, only a few newborns. Cut them very small as well and add to the dough. Mix everything up and place them seaweed around the dough. They need a few hours freezing outside, but to my surprise it came up quite sweet.\n\nCactus on a stick\nI would feel bad if I did not add anything about the orchish culture. They do not cook a lot, and it was quite hard to find this recipe, but it was the only one I found.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Long needle cactus\n-A stick\n\nNot a hard recipe, just find and cut a long needle cactus, they are the sweetest of them. You remove the needles and cut the cactus into bits, and stick them in a stick. Then you place over fire and let cook.\n\nCarrot bun\nThe Halflings are exceptional farmers, and what I enjoyed the most about them was the carrots, they were quite delicious. I created a simple recipe while using it.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Three hand sized carrots\n-A glass of milk\n-A few strips of sugarcanes\n-Two fresh chicken eggs\n\nPreheat the oven with Birch coal, which will give a mild aroma of the tree to the buns, but don’t let it heat too much. Skin and chop the carrots into a bowl, and add the milk. Crush some of the sugarcane juice as you stir, the eggs coming at the end.\n\nWith a soup spoon, take the dough and place over the leftover sugarcanes, which are now juiceless. Place everything in a long plate and place in the oven.\n\nCrab pie\nFor last, I present the Kha treats, made of the crabs caught in the waters around their island, and featuring cocoa from their jungle.\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Long Pincer crab\n-Five big Cocoa beans\n-Two mugs of Jungle wheat flour\n-Three parrot’s eggs\n-Blue silk seaweed\n\nA pie fully done with jungle ingredients, for a seafood pie, it is quite lovely. Pre-heating the oven is always a necessity. The Crab and the Blue silk seaweed are found at the shores of the island, the crab having a very long pincer, and the seaweed a\n\ndeep blue, with the texture like silk. The crab is hard to prepare, the shell needing removing so that the soggy meat can be taken. Cut to bits and mixed with the flour from the wheat that naturally grows in jungles. The eggs have to be taken from\n\nparrot’s nests, and they are what is added next. Then mix, it will be very hard. The seaweed needs to be made into the form of the pie, in the oven it will become crusty, so after the form is done, place the dough in it. While the pie is in the oven, pick\n\nup the Cocoa beans and start making it into powder. As soon as you take out the pie, place the cocoa powder over it, the smell will be wonderful.\n\nI hope that many smiles and giggles come while enjoying my recipes.\n\n          Mrs Ole\n\nPastries of Anthos\n\nWritten by Mrs. Ole\nCoppied by Rosso\nCloud Temple of Anthos", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive", "§bArtorius Thannius", "Missive to the People I - The Revolt\nThe Circle of Governance would like to inform all citizens of the Enlightened Caste that the city is now back under control: the revolt of the lesser castes has been suppressed. I would like to\n\nformally dispel the rumours that this revolt was led by one of the orc beasts. It is laughable that a beast of burden could conceive of a plan of revolt, instruct the lesser caste in the use of tools of labour as weapons, and lead the lesser caste up\n\nin arms against the Enlightened. It is obvious that this must be have been a coup attempt by one of the Enlightened, and we will spare no expense in hunting down the leader of this insurrection and reeducating them.\nI also wish to reassure the\n\nenlightened people of Rivel that the recent mass euthanasia of the orc beasts is to prevent the spread of disease amongst them, not, as some have had the lack of wisdom to suggest, to prevent further revolt. Orcs do not think, this is a clearly\n\nestablished fact. They are simple beasts possessing no capacity for higher thought nor magical skill. Likewise, the recent introduction of “reorientation” of members of the lesser caste via mental magic is simply to improve their\n\nefficiency and wellbeing. The idea that we are attempting to turn them into “drones” is equally unfounded, and I would request such rumours are ceased: we do not wish to agitate the Lesser Caste and reduce the efficiency of their\n\nservice to us.\n- Artorius Thannius, Exalted Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel", ""),
        StaticBook("Wrath's Clutch", "§bJacob Chapel", "Battle of Wrath's Clutch\nThis old tome has been transcribed by Jacob Chapel, High Scrivener of Oren, in 1478. The tome recounts the Battle of Wrath’s Clutch in Aegis, where an undead keep was sieged and destroyed, over a century ago.\n\nThe battle is nearing and an uneasy silence falls over the camp. There is no more continuous taunting by Kane and his ally Dusk. All is silent, the calm before the storm. I hear a call, \"All wardens to the outpost for a pre-battle meeting.\"\n\nWith my pulse pounding I enter into the Officer's building. I know while we are having our counsel of war, the other races are as well. Orcs, Men, and Dwarves alike, all planning the same massive assault on the undead keep of Wrath's Clutch.\n\nOur officers decide upon a plan, I am to assist in a flanking manoeuvre base with two other wardens. We set out from the base long before the battle is to begin. \n\nWe circle far around the enemy's fortress and reach the far side of Wrath's Clutch.\n\nFrom there I was separated from the other two wardens. Unsure of what to do I returned to the outpost and joined the main assault against the Clutch. I was uneasy and fearful, the Undead's thunder roared across the battlefield.\n\nThe battle cry sounds and we race across the open sands to the relative safety provided by the walls. The undead lightning was striking all around us, my head began to throb from the endless noise. The walls were breached and we flood into the Clutch.\n\nI was running through those dark and narrow passages searching for enemies, when I hear a shout and cry of death. It was an elf, I see the villain who killed my kin and give pursuit. He turned a moment too late,\n\nas I bring my iron sword crashing through his head, thus ending his corrupted life.\n\nThe thunder has lessened considerably as I make my way into the courtyard, where a great battle was underway. The foul undead had summoned ungodly amounts of skeletons,\n\nzombies and other abominable creatures. The dwarves were nowhere to be seen and the men and elves were losing strength. After the creatures had been vanquished we searched the keep looking for the undead necromancers.\n\nI descended into the lower levels of the keep which lead underground. I was attacked from behind and knocked unconscious. \n\nMy head throbbed mercilessly when I awoke, I had been stripped of all my armour and weaponry.\n\nI cautiously crept up the stairs and came upon a set of iron armour which I promptly put on. I had a set of armour but nothing to fight with except my hands. I returned to the ground level of the keep only to find the battle raging on.\n\nThe wardens had managed to corner the damned undead in their spires, but were unable to overcome them. I ran seeking shelter as lightning smote the ground all around me. I felt the intense heat burn my flesh and nearly cook me alive in the iron armour.\n\nMaking quick glance up the spire I see the undead spewing lightning and fire across the battlefield. I see Wrath himself laying waste to our troops with his magical golden staff and dark powers. I dive for cover as another blast of lightning and fire\n\nignites the battlefield of Wrath's Clutch. I see many bodies falling off the tall tower, as well as much weaponry and tools falling into the shallow waters. I dive into the water and gather as many tools and weapons as I can hold.\n\nIn the safety of the ruined clutch I examined what I had gathered. A few stone implements, chain armour, and a magical staff like I had seen Wrath using to destroy our men. I did not want the enemy to re-obtain one of these powerful staves,\n\nso I left for a short time while the battle continued, to ensure the safety of the magic staff. Upon arriving back at the forward walls of our base I see one of my superiors, Glade Guard Arthane Lazul.\n\nI showed him the staff and placed it into his care for the remainder of the battle.\n\nI then returned to the front lines, and could see that the battle had raged on while I was away. Through the noise of battle I faintly hear a lady shouting.\n\nI was unaware who she was, as I could not see her. I realized that she was in distress when she began shouting about how she was at the top of the spire held captive by the undead sorcerers. There was a large hole in the wall at the bottom of the spire,\n\nwhich opened to the ladder, which led to the top of the spire. Me and our allies fought our way to the floor below the roof only to find obsidian blocking further ascension. We were stalled for a while in this room before I dislodged some of\n\nthe cobblestone from the walls and created a way up to the roof of the spire. We leaped onto the rooftop and began destroying every evil creature in sight. The lady was screaming throughout the whole fight, which did not last long.\n\nWith the tower won and the fell creatures subdued, we began our descent with the lady. She was quickly escorted off of the battlefield whilst I returned to the ever raging battle.\n\nLighting poured down once again with renewed energy and I hear Ariel shout \"Flee my followers!\" All of the leaders began shouting \"Retreat! Back to the outpost!\" Our entire army ran through the gates as massive explosions began to shake\n\nthe entire outer wall. I hear a shout \"Put out those fires!\". I raced to the top of the wall with many others and we beat out the flames. It felt like a losing battle against the fires, as I would put one out ten more would spring up from the constant\n\ndownpour of lightning. I can see the flashes everywhere, the roaring of the thunder is almost unbearable now. \n\nI then hear a loud cheer arise from the ranks \"HUZZAH! The battle is won!\" Wrath had been defeated. I felt only sorrow at this moment.\n\nYes, Wrath had been defeated, but at what cost? I look out over the battlefield and tears sprang to my eyes. Fires still raged across the across the trees nearby and many brave souls bodies burned in the morning light. The undead necromancer must have\n\npaid close attention to the beautiful trees surrounding the battlefield as they were burning out of control. I could only watch in agony as they burned to the ground. I wept that day for all my fallen comrades many of whom I did not know their names.\n\nThe Clutch is being reclaimed by nature, grass springs up out of the scorched ground inside the courtyard. Trees and flowers were planted there as well. I wander aimlessly through the bloodied ruins. From the top of the wall I see Prince Mylas\n\nerecting a memorial for our fallen kin. The battle of Wrath's Clutch is over. We have won. I shall never forget the valiant soldiers who gave their lives to remove the foul undead from the land.\n\nHere I end my tale of the battle of Wrath's Clutch. \n\nWarden Initiate Amethain", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana Gem S/R-1", "§bTyrell Blavier", "Mana Gem Research:\n\n-A mana gem is part of enchanting, and supplies mana to an enchantment. It must be charged by an enchanter. \n-After awhile it loses it's charge, and needs to be charged with mana again.\n\nI talked to Mark Volaire xXMark123Xx about these gems and the theory of mana gems and being used for energy distribution back into us. He suspected this would not be possible, however suggested the idea of using them on Golems.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the\n\ntreatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with\n\nnothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\n-Minor Cut (Nienna)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\n-Stomach Ache (Nienna)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\n-Soreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n\n-Burns (Nienna)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about\n\nburns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check and clean the burn wound daily until the\n\nskin can finally reform.\n\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Saren's Journal", "§bTrintastic", "*The cover of the journal suggests it belongs to a young child.*\n\n    im tired.\n       \n       we have to \n           find new \n                 home\n\n i dont want him to hurt me agaim\n\nSaren\n    Saren\n                Sarem\n     Saren\n    \n *The name has been repeatedly written down, getting progressively less sloppy.*\n\n  im hurting.\n\n    my ears hurt\n          when i sleep \n      they hurt more\n\n   i love you ark.\n\n   need to get\n      mushroom\n       40\n        39\n       31 left\n\n\n*A trail of ink leads down the page.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Karma", "§bIsengar Brockfall", "The breeze flew into the deserted inn.\nThe doors slammed shut every minute, whilst the inn keeper kept his elbow onto the counter and his hand pushed onto his face people were looking in and running off.\n\n\"COM' 'N 'ERE\" he would shout.\nBut they got too scared and ran off into the distance.\n\nHe would glance out the dirty window, looking at the sky until it fades dark.\nHe would then blow out the candles, put on his brown coat and walk\n\nhome.\nHe would always hide the key under the inn mat.\n\n\"'Lo Isengar\" they would say when he stumbled into Gimblewood.\nIsengar was never the social person so he often grumbled or moaned and kept to\n\nhimself.\nAs he jammed in his silver key into his burrow he would sit down on his hand made wooden chair.\nYou could count his personal items in a matter of seconds.t\n\n1) 2 wooden spoons\none for eating and the other one for stiring stew.\n\n2) A small handmade wooden chair with a tied on cotton pillow.\n\n3) A dusty desk with old books on it stacked Alphebetically.\n\n4) An old mattress that has yellow stains on it.\n\n5) A bucket full of dirty water with old socks in it.\n\n6) A small wardrobe\n\n7) Knives and forks\n\nAs much as Isengar seemed like he was poor from the way his house was, he was actually very rich.\nHe was very tight with his money.\n\nHe always seemed to have money in his pockets or in the bank.\nPeople teased him saying \"Yer go' 'ny dust 'n t'em notes?\"\n\nHe would sit on his chair smoking a pipe looking out his window.\nHe would then prepare his favourite food:\n\nA roast pork stew with some seasoning.\nHe would stir the stew until it is brown, thick and gooey.\nWhere the meat is soft and tender.\nAfter his large meal he would wash it down with some Carrot juice that he squishes with a circular cutted log.\n\nThen he would go straight to his wardrobe and pull out his Light blue PJ's.\n\nThen he would go bed.\n\nOne day Isengar got up at about 5:30 which gives him time to prepare the meals for his inn.\n\nAs Isengar slowly got out his bed stretching his arms and yawning with a glum look on his face he would get changed into his coffe stained shirt.\n\nHe would then then put on his black trousers and head to work.\n\nIsengar glanced out\n\nhis window, and noticed it was pouring with rain.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled.\n\nHe would slip on his coat and wander outside.\nHe would take a right to head out of Gimblewood.\n\n\"Mornin' Mr Brockfall\" one of the Halflings smiled.\nIsengar gave him a fake smile and headed out.\n\"Feckin' humbug\" he whispered as he passed him.\n\nHe arrived at the inn at last the rain started to quieten down Isengar started to relax.\nHe made himself a mug of Vincenzo Ale slurping at every sip.\n\nSoon an odd man walked in with a red robe and had a strange look on his\n\nface.\n\n\"What ca' a'h get yer?\"\n\n\"Nothing\" he replied\n\nIsengar looked at him with a confused and solid look on his face.\n\n\"T'en ge' out yer stuped feck\" he shouted.\n\n\"Now. Now no need to get feisty little one\" he smirked.\n\nIsengar started to calm.\n\n\"Yer obviously 'ave a'h reason ter com' 'ere a'h s'pose?\"\n\n\"Aye\" the man said.\n\n\"T'en tell me'h or ah'll...\"\nIsengar threatened but was interupted by the man.\n\n\"You should learn to give your money away young man!\"\nhe smiled.\n\n\"A'h can do what a'h w'unt wit' me money yer cunt\" arthur growled.\n\n\"Aye, you can but perhaps you should learn to give some away to your fellow Halflings.\"\n\n\"'o do yer t'ink ye ar' tellin' me wot ter do wit' me mon'eh?\"\n\n\"I am Karma\" he smiles.\n\n\"Pfft, yer bullshites catchin' up wit' yer.\"\nHe grins an evil smile.\n\n\"Get ready Isengar for bad things to happen to you!\"\n\nIsengar ignored his pathetic speech, and carried on cleaning his counter with a ragged cloth.\n\nLater on when Isengar finished work he noticed a man sitting on the side of the road.\nWhen Isengar passed the man gripped his\n\ntrousers and asked for money, Isengar refused to give his money away to a peasant.\n\n\"Ge'h a'h job yer pesant\" he shouted.\n\nThe man looked down at the dirty pavement in sorrow.\n\nIsengar walked off to Gimblewood.\nAs he came in he noticed his house had a big sign out front, as he read the sign aloud it said:\n\n\"Dear Mr.Isengar, a'hm afrai' we'h kickin' yer out. Yer see Gimblewood 's a'h community, we'h shar'\n\nour stoof, so be packed by tomorro'.\"\n\nIsengar was furious, he kicked the sign over in rage.\nAnd went over to Milo's house.\n\"Yer feckin' cunt, yer can't kic' ma'h out!!!\"\n\nMilo chuckled \n\"Isengar calm dow'\" he said in a calm voice.\n\"CALM DOW' EY? YER FECKIN' KICKIN' MA'H OU'!!!!\"\n\"A'h can see why yer angr'eh, but unti' yer learn ter shar' yer shite t'en yer ain't comin' back!\"\n\nAs Isengar stomped back into his house grabbing and throwing things about.\nHe packed anything important like food etc.\n\nSo as Isengar was knocking things off the shelf into his small handmade bag he panicked of where he was going to stay.\n\n\"'n inn perhaps\" he muttered.\nIsengar peeked under his chair and grabbed his bag of 200 minas.\n\nIsengar opened his burrow door and slung his bag's over his shoulder.\nHe took the silver key out his pocket and looked at it for a\n\nmoment, then he extended his arm back and threw it forward letting go of the key it plopped into the lake and sunk into the soil.\n\nIsengar had his head down with a glum look on his face, the other Halflings giggled as he stumbled out of Gimblewood.\n\nIsengar walked down the road to Petrus.\nHe was blinded by the light when he was out of the trees.\nSquinting his eyes he made out a figure on the end of the bridge.\nIsengar Huffed realising who it was!\n\nIt was the Old man, he smiled at Isengar laughing.\nA sudden voice came to Isengar's head.\n\"Had enough yet, small one?\" The voice giggled.\nIsengar did not reply but instead shook his head.\n\nThe man smiled with an evil grin.\n\nSuddenly the rain started to fall from the clouds!\n\n\"'S t'is Karma too yer cunt!?\"\nThe man started to chuckle.\n\n\"No, That's just the weather\" he says politley.\n\n((PART 2 WILL COME OUT SOON))", ""),
        StaticBook("Digowen Part 1", "Jallentime", "One cold winters morning, upon the breast of new fallen snow, there stood a proud spruce forest of irrefutable infamy. There is nothing immediately discernible about these woods; the trees carried the same burdens of frost and insects as any other for\n\nmiles around. But what this forest did have, and that was quite unheard at the time, was a name. Digowen Woods was the name given to it, or at least that was the name etched into the sign just outside. If you decided to follow this sign you would find\n\nyourself upon the shambles of an old frontier road, long since buried under mounds upon mounds of soil and brown pine needles, only apparent from the trees whom still could not breach the stone laid so very long ago. It was peaceful here, in inherently\n\nominous. On this particular day a tattered huntsman trudged his way through the thicket, scattering leaves and pine-cones at his feet as he dragged a chain of cold, metal traps behind him. He stopped only a moment at a time, his eyes gazing at the\n\nlandscape around him and the ghostly breaths emanating from his throat, before he would lay down his trap and pull back the jagged teeth around it. The huntsman's pattern continued well on into the day, until the sun passed well over it's perch in the sky\n\nand began to refract it's light upon the forest floor. Golden brown sunshine danced throughout the canopy, signaling the forest creatures that night would soon belong to the predators, of whom Nature did not count it's intruder.\n\nThe huntsman, sadly, realized the error he had made too late, and found himself far from home, in a world not his own. He dragged his coarse leather boots through the rotting needles, clearing a small section of the forest floor to himself as the last\n\nbeams of light shone through the mist above him. He laid down on this small amount of luxury, and stared skyward at the cloudless midnight above him, his mind slowly counting each star and naming them off to himself. Soon his eyelids fell, and his dreams\n\novertook him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Losing a Hand", "§bHenry Winterleaf", "The following is the story of an injury that I have lived with for a long time and how it happened in the first place.\n\n\nIt all started back in Asulon as I was leaving the cloud temple one day. I had just left the borders of the temple lands where I stumbled across a band of pirates attempting to rob two young girls.\nTheir leader, a dark elf man, told me not\n\n\nto get involved or else. However, I stepped in anyway, hoping to see off these pirates. I found myself completely outmatched against these four pirates on my own. I managed to distract them enough for the girls to escape but I was\n\n\nseverly wounded in the fight. I had lost part of my left arm from just below the elbow down. I was unable to retrieve the cut-off piece so I was unable to heal it back together at the temple, as I have been told is possible. So, for many years I made\n\n\ndo the best I could.\nI wore a metal hand for many years as a replacement.\n\nHowever, recently I met an alchemist named Beros who made a potion that would regrow my arm. I have been using the potion for a while and it seems to be working.\n\nIt feels weird to me that, for the first time in years, I will have two working hands again.\n\nThe process is long and expensive but for me it says a lot about the powers of alchemy. So, if there's one lesson you take away from this book, make it this...\n\n\nDon't fuck with alchemists.\n\nOr pirates.", ""),
        StaticBook("UrUKz GuID", "§bBogrum'Lak", "Diz izh WeY tuH pEk uhp Da UruK Wumun.\n\nBai BOgRum.\n\ndIz IZH StUP AsH tuH Da WUMun GuDe.\n\nSTup Ash.\n\nfUInd dA wUmUN laT wUnd, UzE uR Lukz tUh pEEp ef Shi WuHNd LaT.\n\nWuRKz Un TwiGGEhZ.\n\nStUp DuB\n\nKlUmP dEm, Ef dEy sTel alIv, dEn KeP dem.\n\nEf Nub.\n\nFlaT dEm.\n\n\nStUp GaKH.\n\nMeK heeR uR zNaGA.\n\nNuW uH HAf a gRiL uF laTz Uwn.\n\n\nBud LaTZ Weel Neba bI leIk BoGRUm'LaK.\n\nUnLEZ LaTZ WUnD tuH BI BoGrUm'LaK ZnAGA.\n\nUKE GUG'YE.\n-BOgRuM'LAk", ""),
        StaticBook("Desc. Leaves", "§bCallax", "-=-=-=-=-=-\n          Descending\n              Leaves\n           =-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nAs the tree grows older, its roots wither and from the lack of nutrient the tree, too, withers. The tree, stiff and hollow, is parched and barren. Its leaves descend, becoming fewer and fewer. Like the leaf, I descend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Circle Fun", "§bAeran Winterleaf", "I have had conversations with different druids about Fairy Rings, and how attunement effects you. And I have been fairly terrified of it. Voices in my head sound awful, to be frank. But, I do know that they aren't just any voices: They are the voices of\n\nnature itself, of all the plants and all that.\n\nBut they are still fucking voices.\n\nSo, when I learned that I was to enter a fairy circle, I was... \n\nTimid.\n\nAs I stood on the edge, my mind was arace.\n\nThese are living things that I am about to commune with: I wonder if they think I smell? I wonder if--\n\nBut, when I was pushed into the Circle, I instantly not all control over my body. I fell on the ground, drooling all over myself, as I attempted to\n\ncomprehend my own morality in comparision to the blade of grass beside me. Well, my morality compared to all blades of grass, I suppose.\n\nIt was a bit overwhelming.\n\nSo, after drooling over myself, I was dragged out in the\n\nmost dignified way.\n\nNow, you ask yourself; Hey, this is clearly a feeling that is completely overwheling to this young dedicant, maybe we shou--\n\nOh, in again? Oh, ok.\n\nMy second time was\n\nslightly less traumatic: Instead of losing control of my body completely, I instead began to convulse and roll around.\n\nHow fun.\n\nBut, amid this torrent of pants-staining confusion, I did manage to focus. For a few moments, at least.\n\nA single mushroom, close to me. I was able to understand it completely, and, therefore, understand just how shallow mushrooms can get; Here I was, going through a defining experience,  and guess what this litle shit was thinking about?\n\nNo? I implore you.\n\nPlease.\n\nOk, I relent. All he could think of was growing! How selfish! Didn't even express any concern for my well being.\n\nBut, I wasn't able to connect for long. I\n\nwould compare the experience to a group of children bidding for your attention while you're trying to read a book: It's quite impossible to concentrate.\n\nThen I crawled out, nearly on my own. I believe that old coot said his staff had\n\nhelped me in some way, but I will go along with me crawling out under my own control.\n\nI suppose that is my first time under the effects of a Fairy Circle.\n\nOh, by the way: I crushed that prick mushroom on my way out.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Orphan.", "§bTyrell Blavier", "To Ante'ame.\n\nA curious and sweet\nlittle wood elven girl\nhas been around \nSalvus lately and I\nknow that i'd probably be better if I put her under your care than mine, considering you know more about female wood elven things...\n\n...and stuff. Do take care of the poor little thing, I'm sure you can turn her into more than I ever could.\n\nHer name is Alixera ((StariGamer)) and she's a mere 16 years old.\n\n~Signed your immortal not-lover Tyrell Blavier.", ""),
        StaticBook("Documentation", "§bDraoen", "Documentation- I found a Void Mage who says he is Fire Evocationist. His name is Cirimas Elendil. We went traveled next to the manor into an open field where he could use the magic safetly.\n\nHe begins to extend an arm with an open palm facing upward. He seems to be inhaling sharply. Cirimas looks like he is focusing, a pool of sweat begins to roll down his face. A small fire erupts just above his palms. It grows bigger as he breathes.\n\nThe flame grows in size, about the size of an apple. After he was done the fire fades and nothing was left. The man looks tired and has fallen into the grass. The man was very polite and I thank him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This page is filled with a wonderful sketch of Elvira the Cleirc Kneeling before lilyana offering an apology.§0\n§0\n§0the detail would be uncanny", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Coltaine Wick§0\n§0\"Kknotos godar'do gluska ygreht.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing", "§bThe March Ash", "I have entered this new place called the Far Glade for the first time. It is said to be a strange place, abandoned by everything but time and nature.\n\n It will heal me, the High Druids have said. I do not know if I want to be healed. Still, I will see what I can learn here, and then return as swiftly as I can.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Story", "§bThe March Ash", "The time I spend in the waking world seems only moments compared to my time in the Far Glade. How I wish it were the opposite. There is a feeling of inevitability about this place, that I fear will infect the rest of my life.\n\n The Far Glade tells a story, but it is one that is still being written. Despite it all, November, I know that our story is over.", ""),
        StaticBook("Captain's Log #1", "Finalhazard", "Captain's Log:\n\nAlas! Our galleon ran into a mighty storm that pushed us into some rocks, forcin' us t' abandon the 'Esmeralda' and take residence upon this here island. According to my first mate, we be not thee only ones here.\n\nMy first mate has reported that thee trees and bushes be always shufflin' about. I have reason to believe it's just thee wind. None of these islands be charted, meaning that no one else has visited them.\n\nDay 2: What I had previously said 'bout thee island havin' no inhabitants be false. 'tis land his home t' many tribal people. Many o' them have magical abilities.  Some o' them, be knowin' o' thee void's existence while others proclaim that\n\nthee gods bestow them thee abilities t' cast flames from their hands.\n\nDay Unknown:\n\nChapter 1:\n\nThee culture o' each tribe be extremely difference from thee next. Many o' them, if not a vast majority o' them hate each other as many o' them be at war with one another.\n\nSeein' as how our galleon has been completely destroyed, me men and I have decided t' try t' communicate with thee tribals in order t' figure out how t' survive here on thee isles they call 'Vailor'.\"\n\nTh' Ral'skas, th' Blind Bandits (who be all, actually blind one way or another), th' 'Kraskls, 'n th' Leafroots, among hundreds 'o others be all tribes within Vailor.\n\nSome 'o be here fer only a dozen or so years, while others have be here fer hundreds 'o years, or so they claim.\n\nMe First matey, Logan Proudwell, who be in his only in his early thirties has told me that th' crew be plannin' a mutiny. They feel me leadership isn't whar it be 'n that th' natives gunna murder them in their sliumber.\n\nUnfortunately, 'tis means that I must make a decision. As th' cap'n I decided that 'tis best if th' crew 'n I part ways. them that wish to help be rebuild th' Lusty Rose gunna stay wit' me, while th' others gunna have to find their own way,\n\nor join up wit' th' tribes.\n\nChapter 2:\n\n 'tis plan worked well, as I met wit' many 'o th' chieftains. They decided which 'o me former-crew 'n chose whom would fit in best wit' each tribe.  I then sent me own First matey, Logan to join th' Leafroots in order\n\nto act as a spy. ye spy wit' ye eye, th' Leafroots be currently th' strongest tribe.  They wield no magic, 'n they be also th' smallest in numbers. But they be th' eldest, which provides them wit' th' most wisdom, 'n wisdom be everythin' in their culture.\n\nChapter 4:\n\nConstruction on our newest ship, th' 'Lusty Rose II' has begun. 'tis be a year since th' crew split, 'n I haven't heard word from Logan, which leads me to believe that he's either in Davy Jones' treasure chest, or successful in his mission.\n\nChapter 5:\n\nSeven years later later 'n th' beautiful 'Lusty Rose II' can finally drop her sails. She's a fine vessel, much better than her predecessor, meanin' she'll brin' us back to th' cove in less than a a year.\n\nChapter 6: Departure\n\nTh' sun has just set 'n bin finally heart back from me first matey, Logan. He has befriended th' youngest Leafroot, a dark-skinned knife-eared fella' by th' moniker 'o Ri'va.\n\n It hadn't be brought to me attention that 'tis whole the hour their true family-moniker was T'sagari,  'n that Leafroot was th' common-moniker given to them by other common-speakin' people that landed on Vailor.\n\n So, Ri'vi T'sagari be his true title. Movin' on, at th' moment Ri'va be tied up 'n gunna be our trophy that we'll brin' home back to th' cove.  Seein' as how his family expects him to be off on a pilgrimage, they won't expect him to disappear.\n\nye spy wit' ye eye, every T'sagari leaves home to be off on a pilgrimage in order to discover their 'bond wit' nature', or somethin' to that notion. 'tis a comin' 'o age ceremony. They don't come back fer hundreds 'o years, if at all.\n\nLogan was goin' to take his sister, but th' females don't be off on pilgrimages like their male-counterparts.\n\nFinal Notes:\n\nIn case the hour takes me mind away, bin decided to keep a second cap'n's log in 'tis ship as a reminder that me treasure be still buried in 'tis island.\n\nRemember, ye don't trust ye own crew mates so ye hid it within a second journal. Chances be, th' savage animals (th' tribals) have that journal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         Travels of§0\n§0           a Scholar§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\nDay 1§0\n§0\n§0I had forgotten just how warm it was in Sutica, until I was half on the well-trodden, overgrown road. An icy chill blew with the wind, and I had forgotten to pack a cloak!§0\n§0\n§0Back to the city, I guess...\n\nDay 4 §0\n§0\n§0I have reached where I was before I turned back, after repacking and bringing along additional food. After a bit of thought, I put half my Minas in the bank, so I had something to return to when I went back to my home of Sutica.\n\nDay 7§0\n§0\n§0Received a splinter lighting a fire to write by. My fingers are cold, but I guess it's my fault for wearing fingerless gloves...? The bread I brought is slowly turning stale, and yet I hope it will not rot before I can arrange for more.\n\nDay 10§0\n§0\n§0I have encountered a large house on a hill, possibly an estate. It is tall, made of dark wood and stone bricking. The sun is setting, and I am to settle alongside the side of the house to ward off wind. Hopefully I am not persecuted for tresspass.\n\nDay 14 §0\n§0\n§0I have found a boat! For a book, they will take me to the mainland. That's a step closer to Oren! And they even said they'd give my book back at the end. I'm excited!\n\nDay 15§0\n§0\n§0I get seasick.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\nDay 18§0\n§0\n§0These trees are massive. I feel like an ant walking underneath them- their shadows are bigger than the road I live on. At least the weather's improved....\n\nDay 19 §0\n§0\n§0These ships are letting me on free of charge, but I'm not sure if I like how they're staring at my rucksack.\n\nDay 21 §0\n§0\n§0They tore my things apart while I slept, and dropped me somewhere. I have no idea where I am, and my bread is long past rotting. My stomach growls insistently.\n\nDay 23§0\n§0\n§0I seem to be on the road to a town called Haense. Maybe I could learn something on the way...?\n\nDay 25§0\n§0\n§0I am lost and hungry. Turning back to try the other path.\n\nDay 30§0\n§0\n§0The other path has led to Oren! I am pleased; it took long enough to get here and my calves ache like one wouldn't believe.\n\nDay 33 §0\n§0\n§0I have taken a cart to a town named Karlsburg. It is very cold, and my breath fogs in front of me here. I miss my home.\n\nDay 34 §0\n§0\n§0I have had two attempted muggings; my cheap dagger, purchased with my last coin, let me escape with my belongings and my life. Is this a town I should stay in, I wonder?\n\nDay 36§0\n§0\n§0Spoke with a small boy. The town itself is named St. Petersburg, and is owned by House Barbanov, the ruling family of Haense. They speak with Raevir accents, and use the Hanseti tongue. Or maybe it's the same language? Warrants further study", ""),
        StaticBook("November", "§bThe March Ash", "The bones weigh heavy on me, they break my body and my spirit. November. The name still stings. The memories are wasps in my mind. The pain brings tears to my eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Shí - I", "§bYíng Zhéng", "§0§l§nThe Book of Shí I§0\n§0 Fashion and Culture§0\n§0\n§0§lGarments§0\n§0Fashion in the Shíguó is quite uniform, with both commoners and government officials wearing similar styles of clothing, with the only distinguishable features being the colour and quality -\n\nof the garments. Silk is considered the material of choice by high ranking individuals, chosen for its smooth and slippery texture as well as its ability to stay cool to the touch in the warm Shí climate. Vividity and variety of colours used in a piece -\n\nof garment were used as indicators of wealth, as they showed that the wearer was able to afford for the greater array of dyes. Both male and female garments were adorned with emroidery, with wealthier individuals being able to afford for more detailed -\n\nand larger works on their garments.§0\n§0\n§0Male§0\n§0Traditional Shí clothing is referred to as ‘shífú’, for men it consists of a ‘shēnyī’ (a long coat or robe) and a ‘zhóngyí' (shirts and trousers). The Shényí is a robe-like garment that covers the entirety of the-\n\nwearer's arms, and reaches to their feet, it is generally worn in more formal confrontations. The zhōngyī is worn underneath the shifu and is mostly made of cotton or silk.§0\n§0\n§0Female§0\n§0The most common garment worn by women is a 'rúqún', -\n\nconsisting of a long skirt and an upper garment, decorations such as braids or ornaments may be worn with these.§0\n\n§lHairstyles and Headwear§0\n§0Both male and females refrain from cutting their hair once they have reached adulthood, between the ages of 15 to 20, allowing their hair to grow long. This follows the ideas and teachings that every inch o an individual is a -\n\ndebt to their parents and to God, that they are of their parent's flesh and blood; thus to cut your hair is to dishonour your family. The shaving of hair is a common punishment considered equivalent or worse than death.§0\n§0\n§0Male§0\n§0Men are allowed to tie their-\n\nhair into a knot (jí) - that is all. The fútóu, a cloth wrap around the hair is the most common headwear for men.§0\n§0\n§0Female§0\n§0With the changing of fashion throughout the ages, many different styles of hair have come and go, such as -\n\nthe xiáfá, sánfá, and yuánfá. These hairstyles would be accomodated with various hair accessories as ornaments for the hair, such as hair pins (jiá, which were also used by males) in order to hold their hair in place. It is also common for females -\n\nto leave their hair down before marriage.\n\n§lNames§0\n§0An individual’s name consists of their family name (xìng) and personal name (míng), in some circumstances it is seen as being disrespectful to use personal names. Family names originate from clan names and are patrilineal, passed from father to-\n\nchild. Sub-surnames are given to government officers in order to distinguish between ranks and seniority, this is known as a 'shi'. Personal names are given by parents to have a meaning, they are used as a blessing on their child.\n\nIn formal consultations, the xìng comes before the míng, which is followed by their shì and title.§0\n§0\n§0Example:§0\n§0Yíng (xìng) Zhēng (míng) Meng (shì) Taishi (grand historian), meaning 'to bring success'.\n\n§lLanguage§0\n§0The language of the Shí is known as 'Shíhuà', its can be found in two written forms: New Shíwén and Old Shíwén. New Shíwén was introduced 200 years ago bby linguist Qian Jiegang in order to improve communication with the outside world -\n\nand vastly improve literacy rates amongst the Shí people, it is a flexiosisation of the Shíhuà (Shí tongue). Despite Shíhuà being the official language of the Shí, the 'Common' tongue has become more widespread among the Shí people, and Old Shíwén has -\n\nvastly died out.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wúyuán", "§bQiù Chóngyáng", "Wùyuán\n  The Five Principles\n\nThe Five Elements\nThese elements are known as the Wùyuán (five principles) and are water (shuí), metal (jín), earth (tù), fire (huó), and wood (mù).\n\nThey are believed to be the source of all things in the realm, and are the undermining values in all concepts. The Wùyuán are present in almost all Eastern cultures, being established from perhaps the beginning of time.\n\nEarth represents balance, and is portrayed by the colour yellow. It is believed by the Shí people that life is a cycle and that people are born from the earth and return to the earth when they die.\n\nIt also represents the centre of all things in the universe, and a passage to the divine world.\n\nWater is an element of neutrality, but also represents the cold and winter climate. The black tortoise is used to depict the north in Distorian and Eastern folklore.\n\nWood is used to represent the beginning of life; thus used to characterise spring and used as a symbol in agriculture in order to bring good fortune to crops and yields.\n\nFire of course associates itself to heat and warmth, from this it is used to depict summer. The vermillion bird corresponds to the south, where the climate is generally far warmer.\n\nMetal is coupled with the colour of white, and used to represent divinity. This stems from the ancient use of meteoric iron, linking the Earth to the aether above. The Shí rulers also use it to represent their dominance on this realm.\n\n§§The Five Colours\nThe principle colours are concepts established from the five elements, they are:\n\nWhite (bái) is the colour of the Shí (quartz), representing brightness, purity and harmony.\n\nYellow (huáng) is the colour of the emperor (Huangdi). Distorian legends tell of the first men being moulded from the clay and silt in the yellow river (Huánghé).\n\nIt is said that only the emperor may use the colour yellow, as it represents his divine right over the Shí people.\n\nGreen (lù), the colour of the Cuì (emerald), representing wealth, strength and health.\n\nRed (hóng) is associated with fortune and happiness, it is used extensively in celebratory events like weddings and festivals.\n\nDoors are pasted with red papers with blessings, and red lanterns adorn streets in order to bless those who pass by.\n\nBlack (héi) is regarded as the colour of neutrality, some consider it as the colour of the heavens, as daylight is blue and the night sky is black.\n\nThe Five Stars\nIt is said that five stars guard our realm, the Black Tortoise to the North, the Vermillion Bird to the south, the Azure Dragon to the east, and the White Tiger to the west. The brightest star of them all, the Yellow Dragon of the Realm\n\nEach takes its roots from the Five Elements. The tortoise from water, the bird from fire, the azure dragon from wood, the tiger from metal, and the Yellow Dragon from earth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "aqua§0\n§03 earth -fortitue , power , resilence§0\n§0\n§0fire power§0\n§0\n§0-Dwarf Pumkin§0\n§0-\n\nGreater healing:§0\n§0\n§0-athin§0\n§0-frost vine§0\n§0-crouching feather§0\n§0-Tippen root§0\n§0-Alabaster Leaf\n\nAlch Fire§0\n§0\n§0- mandragora§0\n§0-serpents Stalk§0\n§0-Crimson Vase§0\n§0-Drale's tail§0\n§0-Flamountgue Root§0\n§0-Dwarf§0\n§0-Feather", ""),
        StaticBook("Resignation", "§bEdward Poeroes", "To Captain Ironsword§0\n§0and to whoever else§0\n§0who gives a fock.§0\n§0\n§0I've been working here for an elven week. In that time, I've seen 10 bandit attacks, 15 assassination attempts, 12 counts of robbery, and 2 buidings being burnt down. I've seen elven assassins\n\nwith knives up their bumhole, lords and ladies who don't give one flying fock about us, and knights who treat us like arse. I am quite tired of all the shit that has happened with us guards, and I am tired of the constant shortcomings of those that\n\nwho take us for granted.§0\n§0\n§0To be fair, I enjoy the company of you Captain, and the Chief. You are just people. You are kind people. I am sure that you have deeply and carefully thought about our city and what can be done to improve it.\n\nI do not blame you. Rather, I blame those that have constantly brought us more work, and more effort to extinguish the threat of Dreadlanders and assassins to our city. §0\n§0\n§0For example, the citizen gate has not been updated and people that should\n\nhave keys do not have keys for over 4 elven days. Others guards and me do not have access to the eastern gate, where Dreadlanders come from. I have not heard of any money coming to me pockets, and I fear that this pension system is not worth it\n\nfor the shit I have to deal with. We do not have the numbers to deal with mobs, nor do we have the equipment to deal with Dreadlanders and assassins. It is not a mark upon those in the force, but for those that should provide us the equipment and funds to\n\ndo our duty. As I write this, there is a mob inside the square. THe crows dealt with them. Fockin Crows. We have not the resources to help them. I am ashamed that I myself did not stop the riot, but what good can I do against 20 to 30 men and women\n\ninsenced and angry. I feel as if I do not matter to anyone, not even the citizen, nor the lords and ladies who hold our pursestrings. I saw these Crows round the rioters and later left, a satisfied look on their face. It is disgusting.\n\nI am writing this in the hopes that whoever comes after me, they hopefully receive more than what I have gotten and put in to the force. I have done patrols. I have helped quell dissenters. I have brought those who are guilty to court. I have beaten\n\nand administered injuries on those who would disturb the peace. Quite frankly, it seems as if the people are content to enjoy violence and murder. I do not know if it was my failing as a person, as a guard. I do not know if it was the failing of the guard\n\nas a whole. But I feel as if I can not control the tide of violence without help. I feel hopeless as good citizens are disiillusioned and go against us as if we can change things. Because we cannot change this.§0\n§0\n§0I have been to Sutica\n\nand it seems more peaceful there. Is it our people that are broken and michievous?§0\n§0\n§0As I write this, I am looking to other places for work. It has been an honor to work with you, to meet you, and to see the good that you have\n\ndone. To the Captain, that has always supported me and helped me work my way through reports. To me chaps and fellow privates who has patrolled with me. To the chief, who has been steadfast and firm to the code of the law.\n\nWith this, I will resign and work for work elsewhere. It has been a pleasure working with you all.§0\n§0\n§0I hope to see all of you again soon. Maybe not in Oren perhaps.§0\n§0\n§0Signed§0\n§0Edward Poesroe", ""),
        StaticBook("Sins of Alchemy", "§bSarrion", "Alchemy: Homunculus and Chimeras\n-------------------From: Tales of a Traveling Alchemist\n\nRe-Written by:\n Sarrion di' Pascali\n\nNow then, faithful student, a word on the dreaded Homunculus and grotesque Chimeras. If I were to speak to you, and I am sure you have picked this up quite easily, I would speaking in a grave tone about this subject, for it is one\n\n filled with torment and grief. The Homunculus, a cunning creature, is what one may refer to as a “man” but in fact, this is further from the truth than one could possibly imagine. It is the creation of the hands of man, hands that wish to pull the puppet\n\nstrings normally reserved for the gods and craft life. Chimeras are, in fact, an earlier form of this “flesh-crafting” in the fact that they are a combination of two, or more, animals. If this practice has disturbed\n\nyou, please remove your eyes from these pages and go on to the next chapter, but if you are one with a stout heart and strong constitution, then do persist.\n-------------------\n\n=[Homunculus:]=\nBred from the insane practice of creating life, these creatures show little fear and are as twisted as the ways to create them. The facts, or so I am told for it is more of a legend than factual truth, is that the first homunculus\n\nwas born through a failure to resurrect a person. Although I tend to reject “stories” that circulate around communites in which alchemy is present, since they tend to tell of silly fables such as an elixir of immortality\n\nand a “cure-all”, but this particular legend seems to hold quite a bit of truth. These “accidents”, as you may wish to call them, are often twisted in appearance at times and unlike a golem, they are quite alive. Whereas a golem tends\n\n to have a master and does not reason like the intelligent races, the homunculus is capable of acting out on its own accord, and is certainly capable of higher thinking. Further evidence to support this as a failure\n\nto make life, or “resurrect” a loved one, is that they are very limited in things such as conscience, and empathy. Truly these are apathetic, and sometimes even wicked, creatures that care not for a life and seem to\n\nseek purpose in the world. Those who cannot find purpose, make one in often outrageous and violent forms.\n\nIt should be noted, to any who desire a homunculus\n\n that their minds are often fractured and broken. They are bi-polar and spontaneous beings that seldom act in a favorable fashion. But fret-not, for if you desire one of these creatures, and you manage to make one,\n\nthere are ways to combat their insanity. There are numerous serums capable of soothing the mind, and almost any of the stronger will work on these beings. But do be warned, if you plan on fighting\n\na homunculus you had better have a blade handy.\n\nA homunculus, bred of magic and the folly of man, is naturally resistant to numerous forms of magic. Now if you desire to know why this is the fact,\n\nyou must simply compare its origins with ours. The Orcs are naturally less susceptible to the heat, for they have grown accustomed to the searing sands of their desert. The people of Hanseti are naturally capable of withstanding\n\nthe cold far better than; let’s say, a wood elf, for they have grown accustomed to their frigid homeland. Therefore, a homunculus, a creature born of magical means is naturally capable of withstanding magic.\n\nWith that said, they still bleed like anything else there is in Asulon and they do feel pain. Although their erratic behavior could prove to be quite troublesome, as their tactics could shift suddenly,\n\nand the pain will most likely have little effect on them, even if they feel it. Finally, as they are naturally resistant to magic some potions may have little to no effect on them.\n\nCrafting a homunculus is a difficult procedure for numerous reasons, the foremost being there’s multiple methods that all have their different dangers, but it is one that is possible with both determination and, perhaps, a touch of madness.\n\n If you are an alchemist seeking the fabled Elixir of Life or the Philosopher’s Stone then you, most likely, have already produced several, if not many, homunculus in your research. A homunculus can be produced\n\nby attempted to resurrect someone if the proper condition are met, such as powerful materials and a faulty Philosopher’s Stone, or perhaps attempting to create Takwin, artificial life. I cannot go into specific detail into how a homunculus\n\nis made exactly, for the methods that do not include the sacrifice of an individual, corpses, and drake hearts are few to none, I can on the other hand provide the last way,\n\nthat is known and has been seen by me, to craft a homunculus. Although this way is gruesome, and often accidental, I have seen men turned into these monsters by the ingesting of, what they believed to be,\n\nthe Elixir of Life. This potion, said to grant immortality, has been researched and sought after for centuries and centuries by skilled alchemists and it often ends with either their death, or the gruesome fate of transforming\n\n into a deformed homunculus. Truly a horror to watch, and it is a lovely thing that this topic is over with. Although I could do not provide exact information in how to create a homunculus, I do hope this information has aided you.\n\n=[Chimera:]=\nNow then, the Chimera, unlike the cunning homunculus, is a much simpler creature forged from the combination of two or more animals. With that said, it should be known that chimeras are often unstable creations, prone to decay\n\nand eventual death early on in their creation making their usefulness quite limited. An average chimera may only last a few months, but there have been whispers of some living for years on end, and even of ancient chimeras built by the\n\nancestors with only the most perfect specimens. Of course these are only rumor, and must be taken with several grains of salt. Now you might ask, how exactly does one combine many different forms of life into one and the simply answer is, you do not.\n\nThe reason I state that you do not, is simply because the chimera is proof that it is impossible and not meant for this world. The chimera, upon its creation, is a damned creature in which nature spits upon. The fact that it dies within the first few\n\nmonths of its creations, and its overall form is filled with decay and blemish, is proof enough that whatever creatures may make it are not meant to be put together in that fashion, or in any fashion to be exact.\n\n It is true that many believe the alchemical process that one must go through to craft these abominations is an unholy one, but I believe it to be a purely scientific one. The hypothesis being that if I were to fuse a wolf, a snake,\n\nand perhaps a sheep together, the product would be better than all three, but the fact of the matter is that this hypothesis is incorrect. Fusing these three animals together through the use of heavily earth and water\n\ncentered potions produced a monster of an animal that has little thought, obeys its master’s simplest commands, and falls apart at the seams within three months of its creation.\n\nWhich leads me to the creation of these strange, twisted beings, for the creation is not a matter of balance, but in-fact, imbalance. I say imbalance for the chimera, as far as I know, has never been crafted with the principle of Equivalent\n\nExchange being fully satisfied. Chimeras are often only created with partial satisfaction to this principle, causing them to become twisted and rot rather easily. Now one may ask themselves why exactly we are not capable of taking the animals\n\nof our desire, taking strong enough symbols of the elements, and fusing these animals together in perfect synergy and balance. The simple answer is, life was not ours to create and attempting to craft something that was not meant to be simply results\n\nin imbalance. This could be compared to introducing wolves to a forest that knows not of this animal. The rabbits, deer, and whatever have you would be thrown into disarray from this new predator. Much like this example,\n\nthe natural order is thrown into chaos when chimeras are crafted and therefore balance cannot be achieved. This is why some chimeras simply never come to be. But, as I have seen with my own eyes, if one’s\n\n ingredients and will are strong enough, a Chimera can be born, no matter how imperfect it is to the eyes of the natural world.\n\nIf one wished to craft one of these strange and disgusting monsters, they would require\n\nstrong symbols of the Earth and Water, for animals fall under the domain of earth and life under the domain of water. Using these symbols, you would have to craft a large quantity of this potion with a base\n\nas equally strong as these symbols so that their power is not diluted from not being able to reach their full potential in a weaker base. One would need pour this potion into a body of water big enough to submerge\n\n the two or more animals you wish to fuse and let sit for an hour so that everything may settle and balance. After allowing the potion to sit, simply dip the animals you wish to fuse into the body of water and after\n\na rather gorgeous lightshow you will either fill the body of water with gore, or produce a monster. Either way, you may have either shamed your colleges or produced a breakthrough, depending on your outlook.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XIV", "§bMarch Ash", "I am closer to the sky here than in any other place. I can feel the wind on my skin, through my hair. Its cold bites at me. I summon my strength, and I send it spilling out across all of Tahn, to bite at my foes.\n\nThe wind is but another natural thing, it only requires a gentle hand and a powerful set of lungs to guide it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of", "Anastasius", "Writ of deed:\n\nFor the services rendered to the crown of Oren, duchy of Savoy & etc, hereby grant the silver elf Delonna Aeléyèlsa an estate of land no greater than twenty square acres between the northern wetlands and western badlands of Kaedrin. Such a\n\nplot possesses no recognized title within the trappings of nobility and thusly is to be rendered as a private estate.\n\nSigned,\nHis majesty, Olivier of house de Savoie.\n\n*The document bears a weathered, waxen sun.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Resignation.", "§bRykov Tanet", "I, Rykov Tanet, hereby resign rank and uniform. I find myself unfit to deal with the ideology of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Welcoming Letter", "§bAnne Catherijne Hagelijn", "We would like to welcome you to our community of Batavians.§0\n§0If we can help you with anything please don't hesitate to ask.§0\n§0*Willem Hagelijn§0\n§0*Anne C. Hagelijn§0\n§0*Adriaan de Witt§0\n§0------------------- Here are some things you can find in our district.\n\n*Batavian Home Guard: If interested please contact W. Hagelijn or A. de Witt.§0\n§0*Oranjestraat's public garden.§0\n§0*Oranjestraat's library (Coming soon)§0\n§0*Batavian Shop at Sutica's Main Square§0\n§0*Leyunia's Arcane and Sub-arcane magic lessons.\n\n------------------- More information will be posted in our Community Noticeboard. Keep in touch for monthly updates.§0\n§0\n§0To show our hospitality the Welcoming Committe would like to gift you this rose bouquet along with a honey jar and mushroom soup.\n\n>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<§0\n§0\n§0- Anne Catherijne Hagelijn,", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Tavern Sales §0\n§0(DO NOT SIGN)§0\n§0(PLACE IN CHEST)§0\n§0\n§01. Vodka for 5 minas§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Duke was here", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Roopak Khalin's Recipe Book! §0\n§0\n§0~Taste of Roopak~§0\n§0\n§0Roopak's Spicy Chicken Curry! §0\n§0\n§0-Fry onions with chopped chillies and ginger.§0\n§0-Crush some garlic, and fry it with the other ingredients.\n\n-Then add chilli powder, turmeric and sugar.§0\n§0-Then, add in the tomato puree and stir it.§0\n§0-Then, add it all in a large bowl and stir ferociously!§0\n§0-Then, chop up small pieces of chicken and fry them too.§0\n§0-Then, add in the mixture and stir.\n\n-Then stir in yoghurt and add chopped coriander leaves.§0\n§0-Finally, add the mixture to rice or not, and eat!§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "General Goods§0 30§0\n§0A1§0\n§0\n§0The hungry sage 30§0\n§0F31§0\n§0\n§0Bartholomew's Bountiful Books 90§0\n§0D4§0\n§0K5§0\n§0D10§0\n§0\n\nSmoke and mirrors potion shop§0   80§0\n§0K17§0\n§0K12§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day One: §0\n§0Under the cover of the stars, I found the perfect spot, in the open near a large oak tree. I gently dug into the dirt, laying my new sapling in the hole. §0\n§0I pushed the earth around it, hugging it and saying a prayer in hopes that the aspects le\n\nit take root, and let it grow into a magnificent life. I laid my bedroll at the base of the great oak tree, my gaze upon my sapling until I was lulled to sleep by the sound of the nearby river.\n\nDay two: §0\n§0\n§0Today I wole up with the chirping of sparrows in the nearby oaktree. I lazily rose from my bedroll and sought out the fountain, where i filled my water skin, bringing it over to my sapling.\n\nCaringly, I shared my water with the small sapling, looking towards the base of my treasure to see how it took root. The leaves gently shook, already looking healthier than the day before.\n\nDay Three. §0\n§0I awoke with the breath of the breeze upon my cheek this morning, my eyes open set upon my sapling. It has grown, certainly the aspects have blessed me so this day.\n\nI do not wish to question the intentions of the aspects, yet i truly feel blessed by them. May they continue to guide me on my journey.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "§bRosso", "Water: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\n\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\n\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability\n\nto control \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is\n\ndifficult to put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\n\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties\n\nthat is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from the end of my\n\nstaff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nOne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice\n\nwater evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is,\n\nas it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming projectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing\n\nthem in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another\n\nmage must do something to break the ice (i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\n\nIntroduction to Hydromancy\n\nWritten by Ev Ar'ahern\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This is what happens when you war against Frostbeards, may it be a warning", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "§bKirrekith", "Arcane Evocation\n\nTranscribed by the Farseer Thurak, 19th of the Great Harvest, 1529.\n\nOne: What is Arcane Energy?\nTwo: Arcane Energy.\nThree: Aura.\nFour: Beginner steps.\n\nChapter One\nWhat is Arcane Evocation?\n-------------------\nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can be shaped as anything the mage can think of.\n\nThis is a creative form of magic with the mostly\n\nartistic uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to aquire a means of dealing damage, then this is not the magic for\n\nyou.\n\nChapter Two\nArcane Energy\n\nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\n\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn. As with all other types of evocation one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic. This\n\nmeans it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\n\nNow for those already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element  can be described as follows. \n\nIn its purest form,\n\narcane energu is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having similar composition to most gaseous substances. \n\nThose who have observed evocations my have noticed a fine, thin mist\n\nsurrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is, in fact, a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object. \n\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles arcane energy\n\nmost in our world. Studying its shapeless and erratic nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\n\nChapter Three\nAura\n-------------------\nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as\n\ndescendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura. \n\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour. This colour do\n\nchange, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad. Auras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular. \n\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mages\n\naura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocations manipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\n\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible. \n\nAura is a very personal thing, like your own soul.\n\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone else's or other types of evocation.\n\nChapter Four\nBeginner Steps\n-------------------After you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to do is to keep practicing. W\n\neach successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt. \n\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n\n[!] A Detailed Drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occuies most of this page.\n\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your ecovation, but must learn to control it properly.\n\nmoving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movements you wish it to make. \n\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good exercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in si\n\nAdding and removing the amount of energy is an evocation is a basic tool that is key for the later stages of learning.\n\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it.\n\nSimple geomertical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders are the easiest to achieve and you should start there. Imagine that arcane energy taking the desided shape wit has much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the\n\ndesired shape or it will become amorphous again.\n\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefully this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation. \n\nAs book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists\n\nbe written in the future. Thank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n\nWrote by Farseer, re-wrote by Kirrekith during the raid on the Orc Capital, on the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. \n\nSigned Kirrekith", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Sketchbook of Tekai§0\n§0-[!] The worn pages of the sketchbook would be crinkled from wear and tear as well as the elements, the earlier pages faded and clearly from days long gone, but the newer pages in sharper detail.\n\n-[!] The most early recognizable page in the sketchbook would be the work of a child's, depicting a Kha kitten between two human parents. The kitten would be smiling and happy, but the father's face would be obscured by a water mark.\n\n-[!] Several more pages of children's drawings would follow the first, gradually improving in quality over time, but many of them obscured from full view. Other human figures would be depicted, but never any other Kha.\n\n-[!] Some of the pages in this section of the sketchbook would be torn up or covered in heavy, angry scribbling, as if the owner had let out their frustrations about the subject matter upon the paper itself.\n\n-[!] Towards the middle of the sketchbook, a singular drawing of a human man would stand out. His form would be far better detailed than any image beforehand, but his face would appear as if it were sheltering some deep and foreboding secret.\n\n-[!] The only other standalone picture of note in the middle of the sketchbook would be that of a human woman, her face for the most part blurred out by the artist but with a distinctly melancholy feeling to the piece.\n\n-[!] Most of the pages following these would be smudged, dark, and altogether unreadable. Others would have notes scrawled upon them--recipes for simple dishes marked by water damage as if from tears, little poems and songs, and various other memories...\n\n-[!] The freshest pages, relatively crisp given the overall condition of the booklet, would feature rather detailed portraits of several different Kha, along with the outline of an island city and the faces of several other creatures of varying races\n\n-[!] Another entry would have several sketches of the moon and a pool in the depths of a hidden cave, the details sharp and clear on the water against the rocks. The image would give the viewer a sense of peace and warmth that the artist wished to convey\n\n-[!] Another page held various, lightly done sketches of different weapons and clothing, clearly a page meant to experiment on future use for such items and how they might look on the wearer--a first glance to the viewer of any form of self-portrait", ""),
        StaticBook("Citizen Passport", "§bFloris de Ruyter", "=-     PASSPORT    -=\n\nIssued by Floris de Ruyter of the Imperial Administration and given to Roo, whom is a class C1 citizen, on the 9th of the Amber Cold, 1588.\n   This passport is legal tender until the 9th of the Amber Cold, 1598. If found,\n\nplease return to the Imperial Administration in Johannesburg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Karin Faieya Vallei'onn, with my odd sleep hours and your regular ones as well as your travels to that second home of yours, we are having little interaction even tho we share this home. My sollution for such? We write to each other through this book.\n\nI do hope that the ability to reflect back might be something of use or interresting for you to do just as I hope a string of messages will be.§0\n§0I will allow you to find a topic of your choosing if you prefer, if not I will bring up one at the next\n\nrespond to your message. §0\n§0\n§0Yours truely, Seth Calith.\n\nKarin'ayla Seth, llir.§0\n§0Though, perhaps ayla is a tad strong, as I was just at a valah tourney. I doubt you need details on how dreadful it was, needless to say I distracted myself with sewing.\n\nReflection is certainly useful for self improvement, I can agree that much.§0\n§0\n§0Is such a thing of interest to you? I've never gotten such an impression.\n\nBy the time you read this, the garden we discussed should be in place, just outside of the front door.§0\n§0\n§0Take care of it as you will, I shall offer advice where needed.§0\n§0Regards, F.V.\n\nKarin llir.§0\n§0Your questioning about reflection, I used to do so and do it a lot, but now I already know the dreadful result which I would prefer not to be reminded of.\n\nI will try to take care of the garden, should we set up a small fence around it? Surely such defensive structures would make people notice our project.\n\nDays are still simply passing by, I do honestly hope that no harm will come by your way as you travel alone.§0\n§0Regards §0\n§0-S. C.\n\nKarin'ayla, llir.§0\n§0\n§0Bad memories can certainly leave a bad taste in one's mouth, I agree. Allowing them to stand in your way, however, is defeatist.§0\n§0\n§0A method to fix this can be replacing said memories with pleasant ones.\n\nDecisions about the garden I'll leave to you, it's sole guardian. If you require assistance with fencing however, I can offer some advice in defense against foxes and the like.\n\nI hope you have faith enough in my skills that your last comment was mere pleasantry, llir. For what it is worth, I've faith in your safety too.§0\n§0\n§0Regards, F.V.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The clerics:§0\n§0They are cunts.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=+=-§0\n§0-Potions-§0\n§0\n§0Alchemist Fire:§0\n§0\n§01. Water + Nether Wart = Aqua Vitae§0\n§0\n§02. Aqua Vitae + Mandragora = Greater Salve Of Mandragora§0\n§0\n§03. Greater Salve Of Mandragora + w\n\nSerpent's Stalk = Boggy Concotion§0\n§0\n§04. Boggy Concotion + Dwarves Pumpkin = Taste Of Sewers§0\n§0\n§05. Taste Of Sewers + Drake's Tail = Pungent Decoction§0\n§0\n§06. Pungent Decoction + Flametonhue Root = Molten Cure\n\n7. Molten Cure + Crimson Vase = Nether's Wrath§0\n§0\n§08. Nether's Wrath + Crouching Feather = Alchemist Fire", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Seth's feeling Journal, as according to Miss Asul Acosta's wishes.\n\n1'st of The First Seed, 1676.§0\n§0\n§0I feel empty, as I miss the sight of Amarie Calith, Alyn Alfakyn Calith, Aerion Alfakyn, Aiera Seregon, Elleyun Calith and lastly my kidnapped son my memory can't even recall his name.§0\n§0\n\nIt saddens me, knowing I must go on without them, that I can't see them, hear them or embrace them anymore. Forever gone for what is dead is no more. §0\n§0\n§0I raised most of the names but as every name died, so did parts of me, for I was the one to be -\n\nbe outlived. At least they all have the luxery of death. So they do not have to feel the pain of watching their loved one wither before them or embrace the corpse of the child you raised. §0\n§0\n§0A hint of gratitude and envy, that they do not\n\nfeel what I feel today. And worry not reader or observer. For no matter how tempting a quick cut with a dagger is or the chance to fly for but a second as the ground beneth gets closer, I do not wish to take my own life. Not only is it the curse of the\n\nliving, but we only live once. And while death is empty, the next generations of cursed people shouldn't be left with nothing.§0\n§0\n§0Even an elf with nothing remaining needs to continue. As Larihei said many years in the past. Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.\n\n1'st of The Grand Harvest, 1576.§0\n§0\n§0Today after waking up, I spent 4 hours of staying in bed, in the comfort of the soft pillows, I don't have anything to do, why leave? Hunger, that is why. After I had already been lured out of my bed and had breakfest, -\n\nintended to return to Haria, to breed and slay the cows. On my way I met Azorella, curiously bright considering she knows what darkness looms around her, after a small trip to the Library of Draguur, we returned to Kalenz'nor and I to my bed.\n\n1'st of the Suns Smile, 1576.§0\n§0\n§0Another day of nothing. No one to share it with. Another sour day as the sun shines bright as the shadows of Kalenz'nor roams the streets, library and homes.\n\n21'st of Sun's Smile.§0\n§0\n§0Almost lost my life recently, if I had, no one would had cried. No one but me would had been affected.§0\n§0\n§0Yet as Larihei's words degrees. I shall remain with the living. To walk as a cursed being.\n\n7'th of Malin's Welcome, 1577.§0\n§0\n§0So after recovering from the slug's poison, I am, as before, without purpose and lonely.\n\n10'th of The First Seed, 1577. §0\n§0\n§0I will try to travel to elmali'ame, maybe I will not be shot in the back as their praised \"Liberator\" Phaedrus the Second Betrayer would had done.§0\n§0\n§0First glance of the city's inside.\n\nIt is dissapointing at the first glance, just as the first time I visited this realm's Malinor, even if they will not accept the name, that is what they are.§0\n§0\n§0That said, no arrow has made it's mark yet.\n\nAn alcoholic has started a conversation with three mali'ame. Nothing good can come out of this Malinor, unless manipulation and decit is used that is or they amend for their actions of the past.\n\n9th of Sun's Smile, 1577§0\n§0\n§0I have returned to Kalenz'nor. Still empty and without a purpose. This is getting very dull.§0\n§0\n§0I wonder what Miss Asul's thoughts is about this, unless she takes joy in reading\n\nbland pages of the same text.§0\n§0\n§0I have also chosen to take distance to my former wife, Amarie. Just for this month, a poor time to get back into Kalenz'nor but such is the situation.§0\n§0\n§0I miss Amarie.\n\n9'th of The Amber Cold, 1578.§0\n§0\n§0So after being bored of repeating the past, I start a new course. To remind myself of the lost ones. The order which they are listed is not going to be in order they are missed, other than Ikur.\n\nFor if I had to make such a list, I would ruin myself on the idea itself that I had to pick one above the others.§0\n§0\n§0I will start out with Aerion Alfakyn Calith, my first born son.§0\n§0\n§0Born in Asulon's Haelun'or, he had a bright future had it\n\nnot been for my lax teaching of him and the allowance for him to hope that his loose uncaring haelun would return. Had I taught him properly, he would still be here, with wife and children.§0\n§0\n§0I never got enough time with Aerion, he moved out at the age -\n\nof 49 before getting married at the age of 50 and later the same year, becomming a father, partial my fault that it happened that early but the result, Anya is without a shadow of doubt, a joy to be near.§0\n§0Had I just one hour with him, I would embrace -\n\nhim and apology for my parentship. Ask him to forgive my flaws as I have forgiven his, for he is the creation of my actions and inactions. My blood and the blood of Aiera.§0\n§0\n§0Maln always remembers.\n\n8'th of The Deep Cold 1578.§0\n§0\n§0So today will the topic be Karmana, the first victim of mine.§0\n§0\n§0In deep depression while I was in a relationship with the fickle Lona, we found comfort in each others arms after my\n\nrelationship ended with Lona, altho I knew even back then it brought much joy to Karmana, she was quiet about it.§0\n§0\n§0After two years or so, we ware officialy in a relationship, while I was still hurt Karmana did the best to cheer me up and so I was.\n\nYears passed and one day Karmana left a letter. It read that she had taken to the human lands to do buissness, I became worried as it reminded me too much of Lona and even went out in attempts to find her yet with fruitless results.\n\nTwo and a half years later, an elfess spent much time with me and over time, convinced me that Karmana must be dead since I was unable to locate her, that was one of my largests mistakes, one that I still can't forgive myself for, even without Karmana's\n\nreaction then she returned home, a year and a half after. At least I told her the truth. No attempts to decive her, the truth hurts and it did more damage then expected, as the sun rose the next day, Karmana was no more.\n\nHad I but a minute with Karmana, I would beg for forgiveness, even if I do not deserve it. Explain that my greatest mistake has not been repeated and if death cheered her, that the seductress has suffered a slow death alone.\n\nEven as I think back, I also fear had I never been weak, I would never had been blessed by my limited time with Aerion Alfakyn Calith and Anya Alfakyn Calith.§0\n§0\n§0I am sorry Mayilu, for all the pain I have caused. For my weakness and betrail, which I\n\nwas victim of before and after my own mistake.§0\n§0She was not deserving of my heart and if it has not been that mine was tainted, I would offer mine to you but now I am only worthy to give you a chance to destroy it, as it destroyed you.§0\n§0\n§0-Seth C.\n\n5'th of Malin's Welcome 1579.§0\n§0\n§0I was told to write in my journal after my talk with Miss Asul but after I left her, my hand started to shake, for I see my dear Amarie in her, as well as the untimely death.\n\nThe small amount of wamrth was pleasent but my fears are growing for I will be the winner of a morbid bet between Asul and I.§0\n§0\n§0I write today with heavy heart as I fear of the future, not my life but the life of others.\n\n\"Hello,\"§0\n§0-Ignatius of Metz", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dreadknights", "§bThe Eternal Librarian", "On Dreadknights\n\n by Cir'dian Nymphea\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Annil’sul, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Eternal Librarian\n\nGenesis\nThe dreadknights are beings comprised of suits of armor bound together through the engraving of specific runes unique to the blood mages, of whom draw their magic from a deity presently unknown to me. They originated in the land of Asulon,\n\nas did their constructs (The dreadknights). As it stands however, it is somewhat of a mystery as to where the blood mages came from, and how their magic came to be. However it is known that the dreadknights are the tools of the blood mages. They are the\n\nstrength behind them.\n\nCreation\nThe dreadknights are created over the process of several months through a long and arduous ritual involving the removal of freedom and physical flesh. The process begins with the abduction of a\n\nspecific choice being. The selection is not bound to physical aspects (Which would be removed in the end anyway) but rather decided by the quality of those taken. Usually of whom are stubborn and loyal to whom they serve. In post of their abduction- the\n\npatron is taken to which ever stronghold the dreadknights would presently occupy. From there they would be bound. The dreadlord then begins the process with the destruction of both knee caps, as to prevent escape and standing. No sedatives are used in\n\nthis process. The patron is then fitted with a suit of armor usually comprised of a metal known as black iron (Known for being particularly dense, and durable). The leader then engraves several runic symbols into the armor of the victim. This can be done\n\nby both dreadlord, and blood mage. These runes bind the soul of said victim to the suit of armor. Once finished, the subject is cast into a cell, and left for several days before further work is done. For the next few weeks the victim is tortured, their\n\nrunes left open to rot. Flesh eventually gives way, leaving nothing but the victim’s skeletal form beneath. Alongside this, the will of the victim is broken, and they are taught to love pain. By two months, the process is complete, and the new dreadknight\n\nmay now set out to do the will of their dreadlord or blood mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basics of Runes", "§bBalorien \"Ien\" Navicula", "~Runesmithing~\n\nRunesmithing is a strange profession.\nFirst of all you need\nto obtaina runesmitihng table. After that you might notice that you have to make smybols using lapis, gold, or emerald.\n\nUnbreaking:\n\nUnbreaking enchantment is one of the easiest encant.\nto make it use 5 piece of lapis lazulit.\nPlace the lapis in this form\n \n        * *\n         *\n        * *\nYou have to form a X.\n\nSmite:\n\nThis enchantment is good againts unholy beasts. The symbol is the following.\n\n  **\n ****\n  **\n\nEfficieny:\n\nIt's a true help if you wish to mine faster or cut wood hastier.\nThe symbol is the following:\n\n  *\n   **\n  *\n\nLure:\n\nLure enchantment will help you cathc fish faster.\nThe Symbol is the following:\n\n *\n *\n * *\n\nLuck of the Sea\n\nThis enchantment helps to find treasure while fishing.\nThe symbol is the following.\n\n  ** *\n *  *\n  ** *\n\nAqua Affinity:\n\nThis enchantment helps you break blocks hastier under water.\n\n*\n**\n***\n **\n\nSilk Touch:\n\nThis enchantment helps you retrieving blocks witohut breaking them.\n\n*********\n\nFortune:\n\nIt' helps you to retrieve more valaubles while mining.\n\n**\n  *   *\n * * ***\n*  *  *\n\nLooting:\n\nIt' helps you gain more items form killing mobs.\n\n *      *\n***** ***\n *      *\n\nRespiration:\n\nHelps you breath underwater.\n\n****\n****\n ** \n*  *\n\nPunch:\n\nPunch works on bows and ot knock backs the enemies.\n\n ***\n****\n****\n ***\n\nKnockback\n\nIt works in meele weapons and knocks your enemies.\n\n**\n*****\n*****\n**\n\nBlast Protection:\n\nProtects you from explosions.\n\n      **\n ****\n******\n ****\n\nInfinity:\n\nIt allows you to shoot with a bow witohut losing arrows.\n\n *** ***\n*   *    *\n*   *    *\n *** ***\n\nProjectile Protection\n\nDefends you from arrows.\n\n*  *   ***\n **** ***\n*  *   ***\n         *\n\nSharpness:\n\nIt make your meele weapons to do more damage.\n\n  *\n********\n*********\n  *\n\nPower:\n\nIt make syour bow to do more damage.\n\n**     *\n  ******\n  *******\n**     *\n\nThorns:\n\nYou place it on your armor and if somebody hit you he will also be damaged.\n\n* * * * *\n* * * * *\n* * * * *\n* * * * *", ""),
        StaticBook("Informer Issue 2", "underwhereknight", "The Informer\n        Issue #2\n\n        Edited By:\n\n           Adam\n16th of the First Seed         Year 1564\n\nContents-\n--------\nThe Feslen Housing Scandal           pg3\n\nCannibals in Feslen? \n                      pg9\nThe Guard Moves into the Old Palace\n                     pg13\nUpdate on the Lorraine Killings\n                     pg15\nThe Grand Vailorian Tournament   \n                     pg19\nMurder Locations\npg25\n\n The Feslen Housing\n         Scandal\n\n   An anonymous source let me in on what is going on in Feslen behind the scenes, here it is. Past Feslen mayor Piero Gradic has been abusing his power as mayor for personal gain. To start the long list he\n\nhas been overturning houses in Feslen at an incredible rate to turn a profit at the expense of those being evicted. Gradic has also sold houses far under value to secure votes for mayor before. As well Gradic never paid his stewards for their hard work,\n\nowing over three thousand minas to one steward. Most astonishing of all he falsely tampered with the city ledger to do this and it has been years since taxes have actually been checked or logged! Many properties in Feslen are owned and unused by goverment\n\nofficals- likey from the corruption of Gradic. Feslen has three banks- only one open. My source claims Piero Gradic did not run for re election because he could not win and now that Gradic is head Steward he will likely keep overselling houses unless\n\nmayor Markese de Rolle sets prices for houses so they can't be overpriced.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Come Drink and Eat\nat the Cracked Tankard Inn! The best place to get a drink in Feslen!\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n Cannibals in Felsen?\n\n   From the Lorraine Cross murders we thought things in Feslen couldn't get much worse but an unamed source let me in on something the Guard is hiding. An unknown group of cannibals have been killing and eating their victims.\n\nSome of the victims of this unholy act are already dead victims of the lorraine killings and devoured anyways. Another though had their door chopped down and house broken into and has eaten. It was truly horrible I hear. Are these cannibals the cultist in\n\nthe sewers? In league with the lorraine killer? The work of the undead? Rebel practices? It is unknown as of now. Be safe Feslen.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   The Feslen Informer needs writers! Contact Adam by bird and turn in an Artical for a mina payment and have your work seen!\n\nFor articals that are excepted.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n The Guard Moves into      the Old Palace\n\n   The ever growing Feslen guard has claimed the old royal palace once untouched it is now for the guards use. Although commandant Markese said the old garrison for the guard may be sold with the approval of a\n\ncouncil it seem as it will remain under the guards control. The old palace was to be the site of the new guild halls, one a magic school after the end of the war. Where will the guilds of Feslen move into now is unknown.\n\n     Update on the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   The unknown lorraine killer is still on the loose and among Feslen. The killer carving the lorraine's cross into the victims chest's and has been known to kill guards who witness them. A couple was brought into\n\nquestioning from the guard about the killings. Thoramir, a dwarf and Sue a human women with a baby child, Daren. They at first claimed at doing it but then broke their statement saying they did it all for the baby. Neither could decide who did it both\n\ntaking full responsibility for the crimes. In the end the guard released them on probation, taking on all their weapons and book that could connect them with a cult. For all of the known locations of lorraine killings see the back of the paper. The only\n\nlead in who could be the true killer is a man in a light brown cloak ran from the scene of a murder.\n\n The Grand Vailorian \n      Tournament\n\n   On the 11th of the Grand Harvest 1563 a grand and mysterious tournament was held in the middle of a desert in a grand area. The fighters fought for glory and prizes. In the end there were three prizes. And the\n\nthree remaining fighters fought a free for all to see who could win the grand prize. It pitted an orc, dwarf and undead ghoul agaisnt each other. In a fury of blades the dwarf and orc fought. After a drawn out battle the orc left walking, but was soon\n\nambushed by the ghoul, falling to it. The ghoul named Valdren won the main prize of tourney. I interviewed a man who got fifth place in the tournament, besting an orc to get there. I asked this Maximillion Dwanstead, a rugged man with a scar down his eye\n\nhow he bested the orc. Growing up sparing as a child in his spare time while being in the Golden Crozier he learned the art of fighting. he says \"Besting an orc feels good, though challenging. One can find it simple. When you ue their length and weight\n\nagaisnt them. Time your movements and strikes and they should fall before you relatively easily.\" He also said \"Any Orenian like myself can do what I've done. Just trust your feelings it's not as hard as it seems.\" There you have a good honest man to lend\n\nhis wisdom.\n\n   Locations of the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   Here is the list of the location of known spots of the lorraine killings.\n\n-1 Garin Road\n-5 Ganford Road\n-Infront of the Feslen Garrison\n-Falling from the church ceiling\n\n-Ross Road\n-The courtyard by the back gate\n-By the Feslen Auction house\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Buy Ad Space in the Feslen Informer for\n        50 Minas\n      Contact Adam!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Lonly Man", "Wedgytarianism", "Siegfried Vallberg\n\nWun dae, dere wos a lonly man ande a lonly boy.\nThe boy sayved lonly man throm a Ork hoo wos abowt to kil hym. \nLonly man treeted boy lyke hiss litlle bruthur. Lonly man saived boy throm dieing wen boy wos fretened bye Gards.\n\nButt den boys mummey and daddey fownd owt abowt lonly man. Dey did nott lyke hym. So dey kikked hym out ovv howse.\n\nBut dey du nott no lonly man saived boy. Iff lonly man didd nott saive boy den boy wood bee ded.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keru Letter 1", "§bKeru", "Dear Zentora,\n    It's me, your brother, Keru. I have sent this letter to you for a major reason. I need you to come to Monterford. There is a mission here that you would greatly enjoy. If you can't find me, please contact Adam. He has a scar on his left\n\ncheek. He will tell you the rest.\n         Best Regards,\n              Keru", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flaming Bird", "§bJarrod Melton", "A bird flies, building it's nest. Four eggs lay atop it, Everything is peaceful, until the nest bursts into fire!\nThe eggs are burned, the twigs are being burned to ashes. Even more horrible, the bird flies into the fire! But out comes a burning bird,\n\nnot in pain, but rejoice and hapiness! The fire burns away all it's sorrows. The flaming bird flies into the sky, looking like a star until it is it out of view, not a trace of it in sight. And there you sleep, dreaming of the bird, how it's fire created\n\nand deystroyed. As you dream of it you become as joyful as the bird you saw, and you tell your family and friends of the wonderful flaming bird, and they too become joyful", ""),
        StaticBook("Interviews", "§bAeran Winterleaf", "Dedicant Task: Interview\n\nI was given the task to interview some Druids on what they do. I decided to also make this a bit of a candid interview series, so maybe someone in the future can read this and think 'Wow, that Aeran guy is a jerk.'\n\nMirabelle\n~~~~~~~\nA: Ok, specifically, as clear as you can say it, in less than three sentences, what do you do in the Order?\n\nM: One: I learn from Miss Izzy how the use my gifts of healing.\nM: Two: I use my gifts to purge the taint and hairy ticks.\n\nA: What are hairy ticks?\nM: Oh, uhm. Dey're, y'know, hairy ticks. They commit heresy and sacrilege against nature and the balance! Like necro-spooks and void slingers.\nA: I never got the spook meme. CONTINUE!\nM: Three: I do the sweeping and tend the\n\nthe shrines here in the Mama Grove.\n\nBarry\n~~~~~\nA: What do you do?\nB: The rank of druid has the duty to uphold the balance of nature and help wherever  needed. That's the most basic description.\nA: And you specifically?\nB: I myself as a druid, I travel, help people who may be injured,\n\nobserve others, and protect those in danger as well as helping within the grove.\nA: So just general helping, Barry?\nB: I also help with taint removal.\n\n*Many dumb jokes and angry sentences ommited.\n\nKefi\n~~~\nA: What does your rank do for the order, and what do you specifically do for the order?\nA: In the simplest way you can explain it, of course.\nK: Hmm...\nA: Hmm isn't acceptable, I think.\n\nK: I'm just a normal Druid. I got about daily business, making sure order is kept and help other Druids when needed. Like today I helped heal the tree.\nA: Affirmative. And, do you do anything special specifically?\nK: Nope!\nA: So, do you think I write down\n\n'lame as a mule' or...?\nK: I think that would be bad...\nA: Me too. Do you... I dunno, smuggle cactus green in from the orcs, or... Subvert Orenian power by slipping peasants with 'Praise the Aspects' fliers?\nK: Nope. I talk to flowers and grow\n\ntrees.\nA: Do you ever talk to flowers and grow trees, or specifically in that order?\nK: Both ways.\n\n*Kefi may or may not have been high, depending on who's asking.\n\nGi'Garun\n~~~~~~~\nA: So, uhm, what do Archdruids do, and what do you do specifically unique to other Archdruids.\nG: Well... Archdruids are considered head of the order, and head of the inner circle. They head teaching, upkeeping the grove,\n\nmaintaining relationships with other organisations yet always maintaining our neutrality. We deal punishments in the order where it is needed, which is rare, and are in charge of pushing the order forwards.\nA: Segwaying a bit, but is hanging Dedicants\n\nfrom vines acceptable punishment?\nG: Hmm? If the situation called for it...\nA: We'll assume it didn't and put that as a 'No.'\nG: Anywho, Archdruids are the only ones who may call moots or shuns, and are the only members of the order who may\n\ninterract with a shunned person.\nG: As for my specific role... I'm currently heading the upkeeping of the grove, as well as working on spreading the teachings of the Aspects about Athera. I'm also a Hierophant, although I am unsure if you want to hear\n\nabout that position from me as well.\nA: That answer was much better than Kefi's 'I dunno.' It's alright, I dunno if I could handle you talking for much longer anyways. Joking, joking.\nG: I could say the same about you. But anywho, that everything?\n\nA: Uhm, also, when was your last bowel movement? For the task of course.\nG: I'd say... About five decades ago.\n\nTaynuel\n~~~~~~\nA: What do Druids in general do, according to you, and what do you specifically do?\nT: Druids in general work to maintain and protect the delicate balance of nature.\nT: As a druid, as in my duty, I watch over the highly volatile\n\nbalance of the world that Cerridwen and Cernunnos have been gracious enough to provide us with, ensuring that it does not fall to such a state of disrepeair and pandemonium that the druids are unable to save it from destruction by the ill-advised or\n\nunknowing hands of the mortal races. Put simply, I keep people from fucking up nature.\nA: Eloquent.\n\n*Alcohol may have been involved a bit in this conversations.", ""),
        StaticBook("A White Tome", "§bAshanaak", "[!] The tome is bound in white leather, with only a silver diamond encircling a silver dot embossed on the front cover: the Clerical Eye. Its pages would be marblesque in color, with silver trim, and the writing a flowing font in black ink. [!]\n\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\nThe Utterings of Tahariae\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\n\n\n\nAssembled and Recorded by the Prophet Ashanaak in Vailor\n\n------=+=------\nThe Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recorded by the Prophet Braxis in early Anthos:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brethren.\n\n[II] Cannot stray from thy faith.\n\n[III] Shall guide the lost.\n\n[IV] Shall not kill, harm, or spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Abuse of thine gift and punishment shall fall to you.\n\nAs Interpreted by the High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae in late Athera:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae.\n\n[II] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae.\n\n[III] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure.\n\n[IV] Do not spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Four Revelations\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recited through the Prophet Ashanaak by the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, between the years 1436 and 1442:\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Judgment: The Apokalytiria\n---------------\n\nI am the Glory of the Rising Sun. I am the Bringer of Light. I am the Lord of Purity and the Archon of Justice. I am the Vehement Lord. I am Tahariae. Witness Me, My Chosen\n\nProphet. Witness Me.\n\nI, the Divine Stag, He Who Walks in Pure Light, the Great Purge, have merely watched My Servants for too long. You have Divided, and Divided you shall fall. You failed to Understand the Mission I had given you, and so you have\n\ndeteriorated into mere wandering healers and warriors who know only my Blessed Name. Your mockery of Faith and Piety offends Me, and so I return once more. Witness Me, Ashanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Wisdom: The Eight Woes\n---------------\n\nAnd now, my Chosen Prophet, recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:\n\n[I] Woe to those that turn against Me and My Mission, for they must be cast out of thy ranks.\n\n[II] Woe to those who only know Me for My Blessing, and not for My Mission, and do not recognize Me and My Glory in prayer except when My power is needed.\n\n[III] Woe to those who refuse to heal the Innocent, to return to Pure form what has been rendered Impure.\n\n[IV] Woe to those who let the Impure, the Beings of Darkness and Evil, and the Descendants who bring harm to the Innocents, walk free when they cross thy path.\n\n[V] Woe to those who cause harm to the Innocent, for they are those you are sworn to protect.\n\n[VI] Woe to those who are sexually immoral, who give themselves outside of the holy bed of marriage, who dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent.\n\n[VII] Woe to those who give themselves over to perpetual drunkenness and intoxication, for they dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent. Such is only acceptable in celebrations and festivities.\n\n[VIII] Woe to those who steal, cheat, and utter vulgarities, who abuse the Innocent with their tongues and hands.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Valor: The Eight Commands\n---------------\n\nAnd now, Ashanaak, I give you these Commands. Recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, that you may live a Pure life:\n\n[I] Go forth, and spread not just my Light among the Descendants, but My Words and the Truth of My Glory.\n\n[II] Go forth, and become true Clerics among the Descendants: scholars, protectors, and leaders, to guide the Innocent with words, justice, and wisdom.\n\n[III] Go forth, and guard yourself against marriage, for service to Me demands complete and total commitment. If you do marry, do not marry those who serve Darkness and Evil, for in doing so you taint the very nature of holy matrimony.\n\n[IV] Go forth, and kneel before Me in maniael: private prayer, gratitude, and submission before My Glory when you awake and before you sleep.\n\n[V] Go forth, and kneel before Me in manaakh: prayer, worship, and submission in fellowship with your Brothers and Sisters in Me once each Elven year.\n\n[VI] Go forth, and respect the fallen clerics who I have sent back to you, to listen and follow what they have returned to say. And when their wisdom has been imparted, that you will have the strength and courage to send them back to My Halls.\n\n[VII] Go forth, and follow My Chosen Prophet, for they shall be My Light in the darkness of the world for you.\n\n[VIII] Go forth, and in My Blessed Name, use any means necessary to bring Purity to the Taint and Darkness that has become the world. The realm must return to how it once was, when the Four once ruled in Peace and Taint had not yet manifested. Through the\n\nsuffering My Mission shall bring you, remember that it is not out of Moral Good that you must do these things, but out of Necessity.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Hope: The Anachorisi\n---------------\n\nDo all that I have commanded for you to do, and do not do all I have commanded you not to do, and you shall not perish. Nay; once suffering consume you and you leave thy mortal coil,\n\nI shall welcome you into My Sacred Halls, to forever be with Me in Purity, to forever be witness to My Sacred Light, forever and ever more.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Anamniseis\n------=+=------\n\nThe Interactions the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, has had with His Clerics, as Recorded and Collected by the Prophet Ashanaak:\n\nIt was in Aegis that the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, first came to mortalkind, but He did not reveal His blessed name. In mortal man’s wonder at His eternal and pure radiance, He was worshipped as the Creator, and only the most holy of clerics\n\ncould serve Him.\n\nIt was in Asulon, Aerial, the Arch-Aengul, lost the ability to grant power to Her servants, and the Aengul Gazardiael withdrew His blessing, thus why He is known as the Abandoner. Tahariae, in His infinite kindness, granted the clerics\n\nHis Blessing, so the holy work of healing and the purging of evil could be done still, yet He still did not reveal His blessed name, and the clerics believed their patrons to be Aerial and Gazardiael.\n\nIt was in early Anthos that He revealed Himself and\n\nHis Sacred Mission of Purity to the Prophet Braxis, that the bodies of Mankind be whole and protected from the forces of evil, and that taint be removed from the realm, and that the realm be returned to the Purity that existed when the Four Brothers first\n\nwalked the Earth.\n\nIt was in late Anthos, when the clerics were few and Setherien and the wraiths threatened the realm, that Tahariae chose four to be His champions, perfect representations of His four aspects: Judgment, Wisdom, Valor, and Hope.\n\nTogether, they fought the many threats to the purity of the realm.\n\nIt was in late Thales Tahariae summoned forth His clerics to investigate a portal, through which we were to enter. The Abandoner, Gazardiael, confronted Tahariae, and the two did battle\n\natop the mountain on which the portal was located. After the battle, and Gazardiael briefly pushed back, Tahariae manifested before the gathered clerics and their allies as a radiant white stag. He told us the portal required two keys to open, as well as\n\nthe Itharel of Wisdom Hosper, who had been captured by forces unknown. “O Lord, can you tell us where Hosper is?” I asked. “Nay,” He responded. “A dark force clouds My vision; I cannot see him.” So began the quest for the keys began, of which I was\nnot\n\ninvolved any further in.\n\nIt was in Athera that the Order of the White Lance, a union between the servants of Tahariae and Xan, Aengul of Gaurdianship and Order, was formed. Alas, it was not to last, and so began the Schism and the Conflict of Light. In\n\nlate Athera, Aldrik, Second Itharel of Hope, was given a vision by Tahariae commanding the Clerics and the Paladins to reunite, but such did not come to pass.\n\nIt was in Vailor that Tahariae commanded His followers to leap from high places and He would\n\nsave us. It was a test of faith to prepare us for His message: the realm was passing through a Great Cycle that must occur, lest the world be consumed by the Destroyer. However, in order for the Realm to be protected, four Harvesters wielding scythes must\n\ncut down many innocents. “For it is not out of Moral Good or Holiness that we do these things, but out of Necessity,” sayeth Tahariae unto us. So great was His insistence we trust in Him that two of us briefly lost connection to Him for not leaping\n\nenough, but they were forgiven, and His Blessing returned to their hearts.\n\nIt was many years later, amidst the assault of the clerics by the Being known as the Undying One, that Tahariae revealed His new commands by speaking through the cleric Ashanaak,\n\nchoosing him to be His next Prophet.\n\nSuch is the history of the actions of the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, in our realm. May our actions be a testament to the Glory of Tahariae, Blessed Be His Name.\n\n[!] An ornate picture of a stag facing the viewer is here. Its antlers are tall and winding, and a radiant halo surrounds his head. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruined Land Pt1", "§bEdward VonKrenol", "--------------------------------------§0\n§0\n§0           Nemisis§0\n§0           of the§0\n§0       Ruined Kingdom§0\n§0\n§0--------------------------------------§0\n§0\n§0\n\n The children who stand on the scorched plains continue to dig graves with their powerless hands.....§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Atop the scarred battlefield, they covered the bodies of nameless boys and the remaining corpses\n\n\n§0      Steal, be stolen §0\n§0from: What remains is§0\n§0          Despair§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0  The consequences§0\n§0  of mutual loathing...\n\n\n§0    As I embrace a§0\n§0      cold corpse,§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         Each Time§0\n§0      still-warm eyes§0\n§0      begin to shine....§0\n§0\n§0         I sobbed,§0\n§0    choked with tears\n\n       To greive for§0\n§0    those short-lived,§0\n§0         lost lives,§0\n§0     I can only mourn§0\n§0\n§0\n§0   Is there anything§0\n§0      I can protect§0\n§0    with my hands....\n\n       So we may§0\n§0    someday put a§0\n§0      stop to this§0\n§0    unending war,§0\n§0\n§0\n§0       So we will§0\n§0   no longer have§0\n§0     war as well..§0\n§0\n§0     We'll live on...\n\n         To be continued September 20th, 2016", ""),
        StaticBook("Soldierly Song 2", "§bChristopher d'Ibelin", "BALLADS of the SOLDIERY of the ARCHDUCHY of LORRAINE\n_____________________________\n\n\n\n\n_____________________________By Christopher d'Ibelin\n_____________________________\n\nLorraine's Rangers\n_____________________________In our army we’re the best, \nFrom the north, south, east and west, \nThe best of boys are following the drum!\nWe’re mighty hard to beat, \nI may say without conceit,\n\nFaith, the enemy, are welcome when they come!\n\nBe they Dwarves, Orcs or Elves, \nWhy, we’ll beat them ourselves!\nWe’re the boys to give them sugar in their tea!\n\nFor we’re Lorraine’s rangers, \nThe lad to face all dangers, \nGold in peace, steel in war, \nClear the way!\n\nYou may talk about your squires, boys, \nYour mercenaries to hire, boys, \nYour holy orders and brave Dwarves - without the forts!\n\nThe girls we drive ‘em crazy, \nThe foe, we beat them easy.\nThe rangers of Lorraine....Huzzah!\nThe land across the sea!\n\nTwas Barabanov who said, \nAs Adria he led,\n\n“My Crows, are them the rangers, do you know?”\n“Da” Says Crow “There’s no mistake! To our heels we better take!”\n“I think it’s time for you and I to go!”\nWhen friend or foe hears their step, \nIt makes their heart to leap,\n\n“Arrgh jewels, drink you to Edmond’s Day?”\n\nFor we’re Lorraine’s Rangers, \nThe boys to fear no dangers, \nAnd we’re the lads who always take the sway.\n\nYou may talk about your squires, boys, \nYour mercenaries to hire, boys, \nYour holy orders and brave Dwarves - without the forts!\nThe girls we drive ‘em crazy, \nThe foe, we beat them easy.\n\nThe rangers of Lorraine....Huzzah!\nThe land across the sea!\n\nNow there isn’t far to search for the lads who best can march, \nThe lads that never fear the longest day, \nFaith, you easily will know, their dashing step will show,\n\nTis Lorraine’s boys who always lead the way. \nIf me words perhaps ye doubt, come join ‘em on a route, \nI’m thinking you’ll not find it quite a treat!\nYou’ll see them in the van, you may catch them if you can,\n\nFaith, you’ll have to travel fast or you’ll be late!\n\nYou may talk about your squires, boys, \nYour mercenaries to hire, boys, \nYour kngiths and noble Dwarves - without the forts!\n\nThe girls we drive ‘em crazy, \nThe foe, we beat them easy.\nThe rangers of Lorraine....Huzzah!\nThe land across the sea!\n\nHearts of Oak - A Song of Chambery's Marines\n_____________________________Come, cheer up, my lads, 'tis to glory we steer,\nTo add something more to this wonderful year;\nTo honour, we call you, as free men, not slaves,\nfor who are so free as the sons of\n\nthe waves?\n\nHearts of oak are our ships,\nHearts of oak are our men, \nWe'll always be ready...\nSteady, boys, steady!\nWe'll fight and we'll conquer,\nAgain and again!\n\nWe ne'er see our foes but we wish them to stay,\nThey never see us but they wish us away;\nIf they run, why we follow, and run them ashore,\nFor if they won't fight us, what can we do more?\n\nHeart of Oak are our ships,\nJolly Tars are our men,\nWe always are ready: Steady, boys, Steady!\nWe'll fight and we'll conquer again and again!\n\nLorraine triumphant, her ships rule the seas, \nHer watchword is 'justice' and her password is 'free'\n\nChambery's docks heed our return, \nFor the foes that attacked them are ne'er to return!\n\nHearts of oak are our ships,\nSaints of old guard our men, \nWe'll always be ready...\nSteady, boys, steady!\nWe'll fight and we'll conquer again, and again!\n\nMy Bonny Light Horseman\n_____________________________O contemptible foe, You’re the cause of my woe,\nFor my bonny light horseman, to the wars he did go. \nBroken hearted I’ll wander, Broken hearted I’ll remain,\n\nSince my bonny light horseman, in the wars he was slain. \n\nWhen our foe commanded, his armies to stand, \nAnd proud waved his banners all gaily and grand.\nHe planted his sharp stakes, right over the plain,\n\nAnd my bonny light horseman, in the wars he was slain.\n\nO contemptible foe, You’re the cause of my woe,\nFor my bonny light horseman, to the wars he did go. \nBroken hearted I’ll wander, Broken hearted I’ll remain,\n\nSince my bonny light horseman, in the wars he was slain.\n\nAnd if I was some small bird and had wings and could fly,\nI would fly over the salt sea where my true love does lie.\nThree years and six months now, since he left this bright shore,\n\nOh, my bonny light horseman will I ne’er see you more?\n\nO contemptible foe, You’re the cause of my woe,\nFor my bonny light horseman, to the wars he did go. \nBroken hearted I’ll wander, Broken hearted I’ll remain,\n\nSince my bonny light horseman, in the wars he was slain.\n\nAnd the dove she laments for her mate as she flies\n\"Oh, where, tell me where is my true love?\" she sighs.\n\n\"And where in this wide world is there one to compare\nWith my bonny light horseman who was killed in the war?\"\n\nO contemptible foe, You’re the cause of my woe,\nFor my bonny light horseman, to the wars he did go.\n\nBroken hearted I’ll wander, Broken hearted I’ll remain,\nSince my bonny light horseman, in the wars he was slain.\n\nYe Madcaps of Lorraine\n_____________________________(The song is sarcastic, and made to mock.)\n\nYe madcaps of Lorraine, \nWho merry would make, \nCome over to Metz, \nAnd there you shall see, \nHow merry we'll make it, \nHow frolic we'll be.\n\nYour serjeants and officers are very kind,\nIf that you can flatter and speak to their mind,\nThey will free you from duty and all other trouble,\nYour money being gone, your duty comes double!\n\nAs soon as you've come to your enemies' land,\nWhere fat goose and capon you have at command,\nSing take them or eat them or let them alone,\nSing go out and fetch them or else you get none.\n\nAt last when you've come to your enemies' walls,\nWhere many a brave gallant and gentleman falls,\nAnd when you have done the best that you can,\nYour captain rewards you, \"There dies a brave man!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Advertisement!", "§bMylas", "CARRINGTON VENTURES\n\nMylas of Felsen is buying and selling everything! Buy iron, gold, diamonds, horses, land, or anything you can imagine!\n\nSell Mylas any of your goods for a fair price!", ""),
        StaticBook("Citizen Passport", "§bFloris de Ruyter", "=-     PASSPORT    -=\n\nIssued by FLORIS DE RUYTER of the Imperial Administration and given to ALTARON II of the HOUSE STAFYR, whom is a class B1 citizen, on the 6th of the DEEP COLD, 1586.\n   This passport is legal tender until the 6th of the DEE\n\nCOLD, 1596. If found, please return to the Imperial Administration in Johannesberg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Soldierly Songs", "§bChristopher d'Ibelin", "Ballads of the SOLDIERY of the ARCHDUCHY of LORRAINE.\n_____________________________\n\n\nBy Christopher d'Ibelin.\n\nOver the Hills and Far Away\n_____________________________Hark now the drums beat up again\nFor all true soldier gentlemen,\nThen let us list and march, I say,\nOver the Hills and far away.\n\nOver the hills and o'er the lands,\nFrom d’Amaury to the Marchands,\nDuke Lothaire commands and we'll obey,\nOver the hills and far away.\n\nAll gentlemen that have a mind,\nTo serve Lorraine, that's good and kind,\n\nCome list and enter into pay, \nThen over the hills and far away.\n\nOver the hills and o'er the lands,\nFrom d’Amaury to the Marchands,\nDuke Lothaire commands and we'll obey,\nOver the hills and far away.\n\nNo more from sound of drum retreat,\nWhile cavalry and footmen beat,\nBandits and Blackguards every day,\nWhen over the hills and far away.\n\nOver the hills and o'er the lands,\nFrom d’Amaury to the Marchands,\n\nDuke Lothaire commands and we'll obey,\nOver the hills and far away.\n\nOld Augustus e’up and scratched his bum,\nHe says ‘Dreadlands [or any other foe], lads, thee’s ‘ad thee fun\nMy men-at-arms will win the day\nWhen over the hills and far away.’\n\nOver the hills and o'er the lands,\nFrom d’Amaury to the Marchands,\nDuke Lothaire commands and we'll obey,\nOver the hills and far away.\n\nThere’s ‘fifty minas on the drum,\nFor those who volunteer to come,\n\nTo list and fight the foe to day, \nOver the hills and far away.\n\nOver the hills and o'er the lands,\nFrom d’Amaury to the Marchands,\nDuke Lothaire commands and we'll obey,\nOver the hills and far away.\n\nWhen Javelins are Whizzlin'\n_____________________________Soldiers with swords in hand, to the walls coming, \nHorsemen about the streets, riding and running, \nSentinels on the walls, \"Alarm!\" a-crying,\nCrossbowmen armed with bolts; enemy a-dying.\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nTrumpets on turrets high, they are a-sounding, \nDrums beating out aloud, echoes resounding,\n\nAlarm bells in each place, they are a-ringing, \nWomen with stones in laps, to the walls bringing.\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nTrumpets on turrets high, they are a-sounding, \nDrums beating out aloud, echoes resounding, \nAlarm bells in each place, they are a-ringing, \nWomen with stones in laps, to the walls bringing.\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nTrumpets on turrets high, they are a-sounding, \nDrums beating out aloud, echoes resounding,\n\nAlarm bells in each place, they are a-ringing, \nWomen with stones in laps, to the walls bringing.\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nCaptains in open fields, on their foes rushing, \nGentlemen second them with their bills pushing. \nEngineers in the trench, earth, earth uprearing, \nSoldiers in the mines, enemy a-facin!\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nPortcullis in the ports, they are downletting,\nBurghers come flocking by, to their hands setting,\n\nLadders against the walls, they are uprearing, \nWomen, great timber logs to the walls bearing.\n\nWhen javelins are whizzing,\nAnd bullets are flying, \nHe that would honour win, \nMust not fear dying!\n\nThe Plains of Lorraine\n_____________________________Come all you bold sportsmen, and listen to my story\nIt's about noble Stewball that gallant racing pony!\nArthur Marble was the man that first brought Stewball’s fame,\n\nAs he ran with Miss Griesel on the Plains of Lorraine.\nO the fame of his actions we've heard of before,\nBut now he is challenged by young Mrs. Gore,\nFor to run with a grey mare, called Champagne,\nFor a thousand gold minas on the Plains of Lorraine.\n\nAnd the cattle they were brought out with saddle whip and bridle,\nAnd the gentlemen did shout at the sight of the gallant riders,\nAnd in viewing the cattle just as they came there,\nO, they all laid their money on the Gore’s grey mare.\n\nAnd the order it was given and away they did fly,\nStewball like an arrow the grey mare passed by,\nAnd if you had've been there for to see them going round,\nYou'd've thought to your heart their feet ne'er touched the ground.\n\nAnd when at last they came to half way round the course,\nStewball and his rider began to discourse,\nSays Stewball to the rider \"Can you tell to me,\nHow far is that grey mare this moment from me?\"\n\nSays the rider to Stewball \"You run in great style,\nYou're ahead of the grey mare almost half a mile,\nAnd if you keep your running I vow and I swear,\nThat you never will be beaten by the Gore grey mare!\"\n\nThe last winning post, Stewball passed it quite handy,\nHorse and rider both called for sherry wine and brandy,\nAnd they drank up a health to the horse with the famous mane,\nFor she emptied their pockets on the Plains of Lorraine.\n\nMen of Metz\n_____________________________Hark I hear the foe advancing\nBarbed steeds are proudly prancing,\nHelmets in the sunbeams glancing\nFor God and my right!\nMen of Metz lie ye dreaming?\n\nSee ye not their falchions gleaming?\nWhile their penons gaily streaming\nFor God and my right!\nFrom the rocks rebounding\nLet the war cry sounding\nSummon all at Lorraine’s Call\nThe haughty for surrounding!\n\nMen of Metz on to glory\nSee your banner famed in story,\nWaves these burning words before ye,\nFor God and my right! \nMen ofMetz! In the Hollow,\nDo ye hear like rushing billow\nWave on wave that surging follow\nBattle's distant sound?\n\nTis the tramp of enemy foemen,\nEnemy spearmen, Enemy bowmen,\nBe they knights or hinds or yeomen,\nThey shall bite the ground!\nLoose the folds asunder,\nFlag we conquer under!\n\nThe placid sky now bright on high,\nShall launch its bolts in thunder!\n\nOnward! 'tis the country needs us,\nHe is bravest, he who leads us\nHonor's self now proudly heads us,\nFreedom, God and Right!\n\nWhy Soldiers, Why?\n_____________________________How stands the glass around?\nFor shame you take no care, my boys,\nHow stands the glass around?\nLet wine and mirth abound;\nThe trumpets sound,\nThe heraldry it flies my boys;\n\nTo fight, kill or wound;\nAs you would be found,\nContented with hard fare, my boys\nOn the cold, cold, ground.\n\nO why, soldiers why?\nO why should we be melancholy boys,\nO why soldiers why?\n\nWhose bus'ness is to die;\nWhat? sighing? Fye!\nDrink on, drown fear, be jolly boys;\n'Tis he, you or I, wet, hot, cold or dry;\nWe're always bound to follow boys,\nAnd scorn to fly.\n\n'Tis but in vain;\nI mean not to upbraid you boys,\n'Tis but vain;\nFor a soldier to complain;\nShould next campaign,\nSend us to him that made us boys;\nWe're free from pain,\nAnd if we remain,\nA bottle and kind landlady\nCures all again.\n\nThe Knights of Lorraine\n_____________________________Some talk of Saint Edmond, \nAnd some Prophet Godfrey, \nOf Ashfords and Horens, \nGallant in the Melee.\n\nBut of all the world’s brave heroes,\nThere’s none that can compare…\n\nTo the tow-row-row-row-row-row,\nOf the Knights of Lorraine!\n\nWhen’er we are commanded, \nTo storm the palisades, \nOur leaders march with halberds, \nAnd we with gleaming blades. \nWe charge for the breach, \nEver the foe’s bane,\n\nAnd sing tow-row-row-row-row-row to the Knights of Lorraine!\n\nThen let us fill a bumper, \nAnd drink a health to those, \nWho carry swords and shields, \nAnd wear our Archduke’s clothes, \nMay they and their commanders, \nLive happy and not slain…\n\nWith a tow-row-row-row-row-row to the Knights of Lorraine!\n\nThe Ramblin’ Soldier\n_____________________________I am a soldier, blythe and gay,\nThat’s rambled for promotion.\n\nI’ve laid the foe and blackguard low;\nSome miles I’ve crossed the ocean.\nI’ve travelled Lorraine and Crownlands, too,\nI’ve travelled bonny mountains through,\nI’ve caused some pretty girls to rue,\nI’m a roving, rambling soldier.\n\nWhen I was young and in me prime,\nTwelve years I went recruiting\nFrom crownlands to the Lorraine,\nWher’er there was no shooting.\nI led a gay and splendid life,\nIn every town a different wife;\n\nAnd seldom was there any strife\nWith the roving, rambling soldier.\n\nIn Johan’s town I courted Jane,\nHer sister and her mother;\nI mean to say, when I was there,\nThey were jealous of each other.\nOur orders came, I had to start.\n\nI left poor Jane with a broken heart.\nThen straight to Metz I did depart,\nThe roving, rambling soldier.\n\nWith the blooming lasses in each town,\nNo man was ever bolder;\nI thought that I was doing right,\n\nAs the Duke did want young soldiers.\nI told them tales of fond delight,\nI kept recruiting day and night,\nAnd when I had made all things right,\nOff went the rambling soldier.\n\nLothaire permission granted me\nTo range the country over,\nFrom the Library to the capital,\nFrom Metz down, and all over!\n\nAnd in whatever town I went,\nTo court all damsels I was bent,\nAnd to marry none was my intent,\nBut live a rambling soldier.\n\nAnd now the wars are at an end,\nI’m not ashamed to mention\nHis Grace will give me my discharge;\nMinai and a pension.\nNo doubt some lasses will me blame,\nBut never once they can me shame,\nAnd if you want to know my name,\nIt’s the Rambling’ Soldier.", ""),
        StaticBook("Informer Issue 1", "underwhereknight", "The Informer\n         Issue #1\n\n        Edited By:\n\n           Adam\n\n\nContents-\n-------\nCracked Tankard Killing\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nCultist in the sewers?\n\n     Several saint days ago I was in the Cracked Tankard Tavern with my Business associate Aldern Osgood when I noticed the barmaid, Oxana shouting in her basement. After leaving the tavern a lack of guards on the streets was\n\n obvious. From interviews with the Feslen guard and an eyewitness. The guard with Oxana searched for a dead body... of a guard dead for at least a year. The Feslen guard broke down every door in the sewers (including the ones under the\n\ninn) though they could not open the door holding the dead, unknown guard as the door was enforced with iron. After saying the Feslen guard would not return to the sewers Markese de Rolle commanded the guard to patrol the sewers after suspicions of cultist\n\nhiding in the sewers! The guard managed to get to the body this time and is still looking for cultist.\n\n<><><><><>/\\<><><><><>   Have you ever wanted to write?\n Do want your work to be seen and need minas?\n<><><><><>\\/<><><><><>\n\nContact Adam by bird or at The Osgood Smithy to get your artical in the Informer!\n\nCracked Tankard Killing!\n\n     Shortly after the first search through the sewers the guard found a wood elf stabbed to death lying a pool of blood on the third floor of the Cracked Tankard Inn. Editor of the Informer, myself was taken in as a suspect who\n\n with the help of Aldern Osgood was proven innocent. The Feslen guard responded quickly and sealed off the Inn. Sources from within the guard say the victim was in league with an elven anti-human group. The victim got on the wrong side of a business\n\n deal and was killed by the groups trained killer. The group also reportedly killed a young human child. The Elven killer was taken into the Palace and executed by a crossbow squad. But the group remains at large, who are they..?\nThey could be these\n\n cultist, mayhaps a trusted elven shop owner or even an elf sitting next to you. Be wary Feslen.\n\n>-----------------<\n\n    Are you looking for an exciting life style?\n\n           Join \n            <>\n           The\n            <>\n          Feslen\n            <>\n          Guard\n\nEnlist Today!\n\nInterview of Markese\n De Rolle-\n\n     During the midst of the Cracked Tankard Killing an interview on the Feslen guard Commandant was taken by Aldern Osgood it is as follows. \n\n     Born in Feslen both Markese's parents are passed\n\n away. His father fought and died in the Duke's war. He was trained by the Gold Corps before the civil war. After offering his services to Mayor Gradic he was made trial and then permanent Feslen guard Commandant.\n\n     On the topic of the Civil war he\n\n said \"I'd call the Civil war a tragedy. Orenian men killing Orenian men. Imagine, these men might be friends under differnt circumstances. One might like to fish, the other to hunt. A true tragedy.\"\n\n     This inspiring man is running for Mayor\n\nunopposed. But do not worry, he aims to help the average man in Feslen do better. From lowering taxes to encouraging business in Feslen.\n\nSo Vote for Markese!\n------------------\n\n}-----------------{\n\n     Do you have a business in feslen and need advertising?\n\n     Contact the Informer today about placing an Ad!\n\n     Send a bird to Adam or go to the Osgoog Smithy!\n}-----------------{\n\nThe Lorraine Murders!\n\n     Don't stay outside after dark! A string of murders in Feslen have been going. Victims have a lorraine's cross carved into their body. The Feslen guard advises everyone to follow a curfew starting at nightfall.\n\nLittle is known about the murderer. Could they perhaps be seeking vengeance agaisnt these anti-human elves? A sign of god? A crazed man? \n\n     No one knows as of now, but the guard is looking as you read if they've not already been caught.\n\nProfile Piece: \nThire Horen\n\n     While interviewing the people of Feslen I was lucky enough to meet Thire Horen. Thire is a man tasked to reform the Order of the lion by Emperor John II Sigismund himself! The reasoning behind this is Thire's blood.\n\nHe is the grandson of Ser Purnita the Pure, according to Thire \"The last true Holy kngiht.\" Thire even said the emperor had \"Odd tastes.\" But with no disrespect. Thire was a busy man, though very polite.\n\n[=================]\n\n   There will be more Issues of the Feslen Informer coming out soon!\n    Remember to Contact me for writing or Ad placement!\n   The Osgood Smithy can be found at the Feslen docks on the very edge to the north.", ""),
        StaticBook("Goodbye Family", "§bSiegfried Vallberg", "Dear, family§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By the time this book is held into your soft hands, I will be long gone. §0\n§0\n§0So though all you'll ever find of me is this note, know that it isn't all I left.\n\nMy love is in the very walls and foundation of our home, love for you to find.§0\n§0\n§0 I left every ounce, and while it remains, I live. I never left your side at all, abandonment isn't my style.\n\n As I turn to depart I feel part of my soul imprint onto the walls, a parting gift from me to this place. §0", ""),
        StaticBook("Orhan, Book 1.", "§bChristopher d'Ibelin", "THE CHRONICLES OF ORHAN SUNGUR\n_____________________________Written by Suleyman I Tarchi.\nTranslated by Suleyman II.\nCompiled and transcribed by Christopher d'Ibelin.\n\nIn which Orhan Sungur reaches the height of glory.\n\nI.The Prophecy of Ayaz Ata\n\nI, Suleyman, have served at the whim of my lord for decades. He was the Bey of Beys, a man without parallel in bravery and skill.He invaded upon distant tribes; many thousands lay their subdued or slain in his wake.\n\nHe was not a merciful man, but in the almost untenable situations he found himself in, little mercy could be found anywhere. When he was not merciful it was not without reason, not without just foundation, and when he could do so\n\nso he did act with an admirable mercy. It is for these reasons that we, the Turkins, so love and strive to be more like Orhan Sungur!\n\nFor, truly, who could be so worthless and apathetic as to not want to know, by what means, and under what system of\n\npolity, Orhan, in less that 50 years, went from a commoner to master of all the Turkins, an achievement without parallel in any people’s history?\n\nHis background was humble. He was born to simple craftsmen, his father living an honest life as a bowyer.\n\nHis mother would not give Orhan bread until he had first hit it with his sling; she exclaimed and lamented of his nature often. He was not destined for greatness at first, merely, Tigir and his spirits, in the wisdom of millennia, decided to make it so.\n\nmake it so. He was absent-minded, his head ‘in the clouds’ as they say, and was of a sickly disposition. His mother exclaimed, upon every evening:-\n\n‘Why, useless boy! Must you so constrain yourself within\n\nhe absence of your mind and the weakness of your body? You are dirt, and the weakest of your father’s blood. You are alike with the asses and goats, and, therefore, should be cast aside so that you may be with them, those who are your closest kin.’\n\nBut rather than taking up his father’s craft, he took up his uncle’s. This was to great disappointment and anger, yet Orhan wished to become a shieldmaker. It was on a seemingly uneventful night, in the dead of winter,\n\nhen he was making glue out of dairy, limewater, and vinegar, at age of 7, that the spirit of Ayaz Ata visited upon the ‘Orhan the Foolish’ as he was known. Orhan felt a sudden urge to go into the middle of the wilderness.\n\nThere he met the great spirit; he called out to him, with a voice undescribable in authority, yet at the same time, benevolence. Orhan needed no proof - the identity of the spirit had been etched into his heart - and he knew that for a purpose he was\n\nwas there. He was fearful, but did not allow the fear to rule him like an İmparator. He acted true to his heart, despite his fear.\n\n“Young Orhan!” The spirit cried out to him. “Tigir has willed something for you. He sees in you what no one else sees,\n\nthat you have the heart of a lion. In his infinite wisdom and mercy, he calls out for you to seek an audience with the Bey of your tribe. He shall raise you up to the heights of glory, and a fate as high as the heavens awaits you there, in which you shall\n\nbecome master of all.\"\n\n“But” Orhan countered “Why would a Bey be interested in the whim of the peasant son of a bowyer?\n\n“I shall instill in him my gift of benevolence towards you. Do not question the wisdom of our one and true God.”\n\nII.Household of a Bey\n\nOrhan did as Tigir willed the next morning, entering upon the magnificent resting place of the Bey. The guards felt compelled to allow him in, and Orhan found a tall, handsome man of a kindly\n\nappearance and manner, who immediately gave the boy hospitality. Orhan fell upon the feast set between them with the speed of an eagle; within minutes he had eaten great mountains of food. The Bey, who was called Alp, took a great liking to the boy.\n\nHe bestowed upon him rich silks and many a gift of sword, mount and a betrothal to his young daughter, who was called Aka. He offered to take him in and make him a noble of very high standing. \n\nOrhan returned to his household with mixed reactions.\n\nis mother, her heart made of ice, said: “If another man wishes to take away the parasite who infests our household, let it be. I shall be in favour of it.” His father was very proud to see his son favoured by a great man, ho was renowned across the land\n\nas a man of great fortitude and wisdom.\n\nOrhan spent his next years in training as an horse archer,, growing massively in stature, until he was the tallest man for 100 leagues in all directions.\n\nWhen he reached adulthood he was a man of youthful vigor. Many grew jealous of his upstart rising, suspecting he would be appointed heir to the Bey, who had no sons. A faction drew up against him. At Orhan’s 15th year, the leader of this faction was a\n\nmerchant called Suleyman, who was of such wealth that he regularly discarded gowns of silk encrusted with magnificent jewelry, and did likewise with cups of silver and even gold. Such was his desire to prove his wealth and power that he had managed\n\nto assemble in his train dozens of concubines, whom were all dressed in the finest Akritian silks as a display of wealth. Suleyman often spoke ill of Orhan and called him “Orhan the Upstart”, openly insulting him and saying onto him\n\nand saying onto him “Orhan, most unworthy, who sucks his mother’s clitoris.” He, one day, spoke against Aka, who was then Orhan’s wife, saying that she was lewd and should be disowned.\n\nOrhan was enraged. At dawn, he stormed from his bedchambers, wielding a woodcutting axe and completely naked, rothing from the mouth and biting the wood of his axe in anger. Suleyman had his sword drawn and was speaking\n\nto some of his fellow faction members atop a camel, when Orhan charged at him and cut off his camel’s head with a single, brutal cut. He then fell upon Suleyman, beating him senseless. Such was Orhan’s ferocity that none even spoke of him,\n\neven when not his presence, for fear that he might be listening, and he might unleash an unspeakable wroth onto them. “O, Orhan, whose lion’s heart is indestructible and whose strength causes the foe’s armour to sing the\n\nsong of terror!” Were the only words spoken, yet only by his wife.\n\nSuleyman lost all his teeth on that day, thus earning the nickname ‘The Toothless.’\n\nThe Bey formally announced Orhan as his successor, and denounced his detractors with words which thrusted at them, like the iron tip of a spear! He said unto those men:-\n\n“O, ye who doubt the greatness of Orhan!\n\nYou are the ones without urbanity or elegance, whose tongues are of the serpent, whose tone positively disgusts! Vile, inhuman, savage, inhuman creatures, that did knowst the key of the tribe, and sought to use it to full extent to destroy our most\n\nbeloved warrior!\" These words rung true, for those who spoke against Orhan were the masters of deceit and forgery, their petty intrigues threatening the Bey himself.\n\nIII.Heart of a Lion\n\nBut there was little time for reflection.\n\nBut there was little time for reflection. By his 16th year, Orhan was atop his most beloved mount, a beast which only he could ride with any kind of skill, whom he called ‘Mehmed.’  Mehmed was swifter than a winged chariot\n\nand had an unbreakable bravery ; as if pattern-welded steel of the ancients he rode forth, without a hint of shattering from exhaustion or fear.\n\nFor he was at war. The insufferable and villainous Beys\n\nof the tribes of the north, who arrived in unthinkable numbers, united against the just Alp, intending to strip him of his titles and throw him into the dust.\n\nThe ground trembled as an army of over 24,000 trudged rapidly against our territory,\n\nthe constant tremor of their march easily mistakable for an earthquake. Even the dead could feel their seemingly unending march. They terrorised our populace, forcing our Bey to fight in open battle.\n\nOur Bey met them at a field which they call the Field of Nightmares. rhan stood beside him, their force numbering but a few thousand. The cavalry were hidden beyond a hill, the levy spearmen in front to face the brunt of the attack.\n\nThe enemy pressed all their might against it, till a slinger ran beyond the hill, and loosed a lead bullet, which lodged itself into the fondly-remembered Alp’s eye. Alp collapsed instantly.\n\nHe was Alp, rich in wealth and promise, father to his people and protector of Orhan. He had married a woman whom they called Isim, for whom he had sacrificed much, and kept to her with love. Now, he was but distant; dead. A lifeless shell of a man,\n\nlying pitifully on the ground near his comrades whom he would risk his very mortal soul for; they in awe of him, even in death. Yet he was dead, and his steady hand was to be replaced by youthful promise, of which we relate most gloriously now.\n\nOrhan was Bey, and the situation was deteriorating. All around him, his fellow nobles were exclaiming at the Bey to abandon his infantry and withdraw from the field. But Orhan, his heart inflamed with a desire for revenge\n\nand his sympathy for his men overpowering his cowardly doubts, emerged from the hillside and smashed into the enemy right. Leaving his cavalry to charge and retreat, hammering at the enemy, Orhan rode with his most trustworthy soldier,\n\nBekir Aryal, and the two of them rushed after the enemy commanders.\n\nO, glorious God who spins the webs of fate! You made our noble Bey rush forth upon them with the fiery fury of battle,\n\nand allowed him and his companion to slay 8 Beys on their own! Surely enough, the enemy saw, and the rear ranks spread the word about that their commanders were dead. Panic shattered their line like a hammer breaking glass,\n\nand they dispersed into the wilderness, chanting of their doom like madmen. The battle, against all odds, was won. \n\nOrhan and his companions scanned the field with narrowed eyes. Little more than a third of their men remained.\n\nThe field was watered with blood, the red hue sickening to those men unaccustomed to war. They all unconditionally pledged their lives to Orhan - he was undisputed master of the tribe, and an undisputed master of the art of war.\n\nYet Orhan wept rivers into existence for the fate of the man who had been like a father, and who had elevated him far beyond what was expected of him by the cold tongue of his mother.\n\nIt was at this point that\n\nOrhan decided to relay to his tribe the prophecy of Ayaz Ata. None would have believed before, but he had arisen from nothing and scored a masterful victory; there could be little doubt now. But of course, foolish as they were,\n\ndissenters from other tribes remained. O, how foolish were they that disbelieved! There can be little doubt that by his sword he cut the enemy asunder, and surely these victories are proof of the favour of Tigir? Although no Prophet of Tigir -\n\nfor the last Prophet he sent is long dead - surely Tigir intended (as he intends all things) for his rise to greatness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Saying Farewell", "§bHäidår Qâdir", "-[]=-=[]-=-=-[]=-=[]-\n    Saying Farewell.\n\nWritten By Haidar Qadir.\n-[]=-=[]-=-=-[]=-=[]-\n\nAs I sit alone, in my quiet, humble abode. I begin to think off I've done, and what I have yet to do. I am known to some as Haidar, and to others. A nameless man, I sit here in deep thought..A quill in hand, and a book infront of me. My thoughts only\n\nthinking of a farewell, so as I sit alone, in my humble abode. With the silence breeze blowing through my window, I begin to think. What will come, and what will pass? Friends, or family? As I sit, I wonder. Who would miss me? Or who wouldn't?\n\nThe question that floods my thoughts every night, keeping me from a peaceful slumber. I must say farewell one day, perhaps soon. Or perhaps years from now...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Forest", "§bMayilu", "Come, take my hand\nFollow me into the forest.\nThe fallen leaves, drenched with rain, will guide our path\nThrough the shaded glade and up the moss covered hill\nDon’t be afraid to step in the mud\n\nListen, hear the crisp snap of twigs echo in the distance\nThe soft lull of trickling water, flowing in the creek\nWatch, catch a glimpse of the timid deer\nHiding in the thicket and the little squirrel\nLilting across the treetops, acorns in cheek\n\nTouch, stroke the rough bark beneath your fingertips\nCaress the summer leaves, immerse your hands\nIn the tranquility of soothing waters\nFeel, accept the dawn’s gentle kisses upon your face\nThe pure spirits that inhabit the trees\n\nFeel nature pulsing through your body with renewed vitality\nBreathe deeply; \nInfuse your lungs with the richness of life", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs Vol.3", "§bLaerean", "Chimera Weeds§0\n§0Poking up from the debris on forest floors, this twisting, black weed absorbs pieces of dead and decaying animals, insects, and other plants. Instead of digesting these pieces, it sustains them in a zombie-like\n\nstate and treats them as its own appendages. However, it cannot sustain anything much larger or complex than a human’s thumb. The weed is covered in small, hooked spines, and a dark, sticky mucus resembling motor oil. It is most common\n\n to see parts of insects stuck to the plant, like dragonfly wings or beetle legs, which may twitch slightly if touched. If a section of the plant that has been cut that has no parts of other organisms assimilated into it, it cannot successfully\n\nbe used as a reagent. Represents: Life and Death§0\n§0((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nNightglow§0\n§0A beautiful blue bioluminescent flower which is very flexible and small. If one were to go looking for this specific flower they would often find it next to a water source all by itself,  but it would look like any other blue\n\nflower in the day until it opens up and shows its bioluminescence at night. The flower requires a very specific environment to grow, such being a place where it can get quite a lot of water and shade, as it dies in sunlight very quickly.\n\nRepresents: Light§0\n§0((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nBiteit§0\n§0Biteit Is commonly found in marshes and areas with high amount of hidration, rainforests for instance. it's a small non-toxic greenish mushroom that may have brown dots on it's top. These Mushrooms are usually found growing under lilypads,\n\npossibly because they require protection from sun and heat. Biteit also seems to stick to lilypads so it can use them as reservoir, if it lacks water or any other nutrients.§0\n§0Represents: Life and Calmness§0\n§0((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nJailer's Moss§0\n§0A moss that grows in the caverns of the swamps, inside of the water or right next to streams of it, having the peculiar ability to make a durable, sticky substance. It has a yellowed white color in it's small pores, no longer than an inch\n\nA carnivorous plant that eats of the insects and fishes that get stuck to the substance that it creates. It's like a powerful glue, which means that either the animal or insect get stuck to the moss, or the fungus breaks and is carried\n\nby them to germinate in another place. §0\n§0Represents: Travel§0\n§0((Unable to be obtained mechanically§0\n\nMiner's Helmet§0\n§0A large mushroom spanning a meter of space when fully bloomed it enjoys damp corners and produces an earthy smell. Hence the name, as its chaotic nature of growth can often cause havoc for those working\n\nthe damp and cold mine shafts upon a daily basis. Like most mushrooms it is inedible and it is highly cautioned that one should not eat the mushroom under any circumstances. Known to stop one's nervous system in a matter of hours it goes\n\nalmost completely undetected and can only be identified in the early stages of its process. If it's boiled for over 15 minutes, the poison is diluted and the result is a fairly good mushroom soup.§0\n§0Represents:§0\n§0((Unable to be obtained mechanically§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancestors Riddle", "§bCheza", "I hear of my ancestors, beneath the stone, beneath the waves, and crack of the wind.\nI hear of my ancestors, I hear of their moans, as waves do buffet the fish and their fins.\n\nI hear the roar, of giants long past, their weapons in hand, their shoulders broad and vast.\nI heard the crying, of giants now dead, sleeping in slumber, t'horns on their head.\n\nThey cry for the sea, they cry for the land. And the Zh'thueal's will achieve so with all they have.\nTears of gratitude, or tears of sin? We can't hear you over the din.", ""),
        StaticBook("Babys First Wand", "Toxzero", "Baby's First Wand\n\nBy Sarrion Di'Pasali\n\nWhat is a wand?\n\nA wand is a tool made from a few simple materials but shaped together in an art and love for craftsmanship, then used as a focal point for any spell. They are used for users who find ease to use a point rather than one's palm,\n\nor users who use destructive magic and wish to have a distance between them and such. Advanced use for wands can be configured with external magic and crystals, allowing enchantments and the like to be added.\n\nSelecting your material:\n\nThe base for your wand has to be selected out of a material, one of the most common ones would be wood as it can be carved into one’s own design for originality and personality, easy to put a socket in for the focus crystal\n\nand any other gems, and very light to carry but easy to break. The next most popular type of material would be metal, harder to get designs engraved into and harder to get them forged, and much harder to get gems\n\nand the crystal socketed but much much more durable and will last longer.\n\nSelecting your Focus Crystal:\n\nThe tip of your wand is going to be tipped with a focus crystal, a crystal that naturally grows in the forest and used as a focus point for spells.\n\n They vary in color and length, but they can be incorporated simply on the tip or as a neat-o design such as in the mouth of a dragon’s head on the tip of a wand. Once your wand is fully put together, have fun casting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Study of Magic", "Toxzero", "Foreword:\nIt’s really no question that our world was forged in the ways of a greater ancient magic through voidal influence as we’re so tightly tethered to the void in which those who dedicate their lives to the study of the arcane draw their powers\n\nfrom can even feel any massive differences in the void. It is in my studies of recent times that everything was created and shaped by will, which brings life to the world with such an influx of mana,\n\nallowing people who study the arts of transfiguration to be able to shift the world as they please so long it follows equivalent exchange of course.\n\n“Voidal Tethering”\nOur world is so heavily influenced by the void that a lot of people don’t realize it, every action leaves a shift in the void. Our realm is tethered closely to the voidal realm, everything having dormant mana and the\n\ndescendants having the scar which acts as our gateway to the voidal influence goes to show such. Mana is simply our bridges to influence the void and summon forth powers that don’t even come close to match the ancient magic before our time,\n\nand all of this sums up to a fact of voidal tethering.\n\nMana’s Influence:\nEvery action from walking, to cooking, sword play and especially casting spells let them be voidal or deity, mana is consumed. Once we discovered how much influence we have over our mana we were able to create bridges\n\nto the void with them, and summon forth anything we could imagine, so long it followed equivalent exchange of course. Deity subjects summon the powers of the gods through a bridge created through the soul using mana,\n\nallowing them to summon forth the spell so long their bridge is held. Voidal users are able to summon forth arcane spells through the tear in their soul into the void rift, the bridge created and sustained by mana as they draw forth\n\n the endless powers of nothingness. This goes to show that anything and everything has mana that influences us, infact without such there would be no life.\n\nOn Deity Users:\nDeity users are people who devote their lives to the gods, or as many call them aungles or daemons. It is proven fact that these gods have direct influence on our realm, with powers unbelievable to very thought,\n\nand as every god is they are greedy for more. Subjects under these gods are considered Deity users, who summon forth the ability of their deity through a bond created by being synced to your deity,\n\nthis bond is embedded into the soul and becomes your gateway for summoning those powers. Like all spells there is a bridge formed through mana in which allows them to draw forth the powers to our realm, so long that bridge is held.\n\nOn Voidal Users:\nEvery descendant has a scar inside of their soul that tethers us to the void, once tapped into and synced with the void they gain the ability to see aura and the like. Voidal users are actually little to no different to those\n\nwho worship gods, only they summon forth power through self will and imagination, knowledge purely and it’s not handed down to them. They create a bridge from themselves to the voidal realm,\n\nin which they influence the power in that realm to create the spell they so wish to desire to summon dependent on the school of magic they study, and bring forth the spell to our realm to cast such spell.\n\nWritten by Sarrion Di'Pascali.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mana Anchors", "§bSarrion", "Notes on Mana Anchors\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThese notes are taken entirely from my experience with magic and entirely from my years of learning from other mages.\n\nEverything that pulls power outside of our realm is very generally called a “Spell”, and these Spells can draw from different “wells” such as the Void, or an Aungledaemon entity. Everything that’s a spell works the same progress.\n\nThe person uses their mana to connect to this well, and from the well a “Mana Anchor” is created between that realm and our realm to bring forth the power of the spell that’s being casted. Now Mana anchors are a physical thing, it’s been reported that\n\nsometimes when a mage fluctuates too much mana the air between their spell and them have been distorted. This distortion is the mana anchor that binds the spell to the mortal realms.\n\nDo note that because it’s physical thing that an Transfigurationist can cast an “Abjuration” which is a burst of mana that destroys the mana anchor, nullifying the spell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'hiiran'tanya", "Toodles", "Fi'hiiran'tanya\nOriginally written by\nValia'laure Faeifeth\n\nTranscribed for the Library of Dragur by\nRevion M. Tathron\n\nThe following is a transcript of a book found in the ruins of a house in Celein.\n\nThe Smile of Larihei Heals the Mind Like Milk Heals the Body.\nThe Lifting- Sacrifice\n\nThe Ritual of the Lifting is different from that of Untempered Fi, for it is the stringent conditions which make for the true, Tempered Fi's creation.\n\nThe ritual of the Elibar'acal follows, and yet it is sufficient but not necessary to create a Tempered soul.\n\nThe sacrifice is tied to the Altar, imbued with the magic of Fi. The room is lit only by the light of a Fi' orb in a specially made lamp.\n\nGold dust is scattered upon the sacrifice as the following is read. Each in attendance may bless themselves as they so desire.\n\n<Transcriber's note:\n\nBoth the Elvish and common versions of the Ritual have been removed, to deter those who seek to practice this vile art.>\n\n<Basically, it detailed how the Golden Owl is saving everyone from monsters. It wasn't worth reading, believe me.>\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nMilk is passed between those in attendance in a Silver Chalice. It is drunk by each in turn, symbolising they are worthy of the Milk of Larihei, and therefore her smile.\n\n\n\nYour body unfit for the milk, Your mind unfit for the smile of Larihei, \nYour very essence forfeit.\n\nThe Milk is refused to the sacrifice, symbolising they are unworthy of it. A blade imbued with Fi' energy (read: Fi'chant, just as the altar is)\n\nis used to cut the sacrifice's throat and as this is done droplets of blue will pool on the blade's tip.\n\nBlood is collected in a clay pot. The droplets will spin and form a blue light which will become stable (PK)\n\nor will explode in a flash of light (no PK, soul escapes). It is required an orb be present to power both the altar and the blade.\n\nFi'hiiran'seth\n\nThis subtype of the magic focuses on the negation of Arcane Magic. Whether Evocation, Conjuration, Illusion, Runes, or Alteration, if can either send a forming spell back to the void or eat away at a created spell.\n\nThe magic will also steal the aura needed for Shade magic, but has no affect on existing tendrils.\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele\n\nThe second subtype of the magic can stop all Deity Magic. (For example: Clerical, Druidism, Shamanism, Monk, Muun'Trivazja, and Ascended). Unlike its brother subtype, which funnels mana away into the void,\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele disrupts a connection, interfering with someone's ability to connect with their chosen deity. This can be small, when they cast a spell, or large, severing a connection for a time.\n\nStrangely, neither Fi'hiiran'acaele or Fi'hiiran'seth affect Necromancy.\n\nThe mage must be a first-time magic user, never having connected to anything, Deity, Void, or otherwise.\n\nThe mage must be of good condition. Fi'hiiran'tanya corrupts the body twice as much as a normal magic, and the mage's increased metabolism may wither them away without proper care.\n\nThe mage must perform the Ritual.\n\nThis Ritual, developed by the Elibar'acals, is the source of the mage's power. They much find a sacrifice (a character willing to be permanently killed) that they know well, and kill them on the altar.\n\nIt is in this moment, when the soul is leaving, that the mage will connect to the Void for the first time. The soul will be returning to The Cloud Temple,\n\nand the mage will grab it, trapping it in a state of Limbo. A state of half-death, forever caught in the mage's grasp. The soul will become a tool,\n\nand will eventually forget its old self, becoming more and more compliant. There is a small chance, in the beginning years, that the soul will attempt to wrest control, though no soul has ever gained full control.\n\nPhysical and mental strain\nLoss of weight and muscle mass\nIncredibly realistic lucid dreams and nightmares, leading to a confusion on what is real and what is imagined.\n\nEnchanted areas will leave a Fi'hiiran'tanya user fatigued if they stay in there for too long a time period.\nProblems with breathing, blood loss, internal bleeding, and the rate at which wounds heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Botany Guide", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "Sarrion's Pocket book of Botany\n\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nFire:\n\nCrimson Vase\nFound in: Woodland's and Plains\n((MC Blocks: Grass))\n\nDrake's Tail\nFound in: Savana's, aka Caliphate.\n((MC blocks: Shrub))\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nFound in: Swamps\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nBlood Lotus\nFound in: Woodlands / Plains / Savanas\n((MC Block: Grass / shrubs in Savanas))\n\nFlametongue root\nFound in: Woodlands / Planes\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nWater:\n\nMandragora\nFound in: Swamps\n((MC Block: Lily pad's))\n\nSerpent's Stalk\nFound in: Wood Lands\n((MC Block: Sugar Cane))\n\nFrost Vine\nFound in: Snowey Regions, Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\n\nBlissfoil\nFound In: Woodlands / Plains\n((Mc Block: Blue Orchard))\n\nAthin\nFound In: Snowey ice lands.\n((Mc Block: Ice))\n\nEarth:\n\nTippen's Roots\nFound in: Wood Lands / Plains\n((Mc block: Grass))\n\nAlabaster Leaf\nFound in: Wood Lands / Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nSaffvil\nFound in: Swamps\n((Mc Block: Grass))\n\nClutcher's Straw\nFound in: Savanas\n((MC block: Grass))\n\nMetzli'sTangle\nFound in: Jungles\n((MC Block: Grass or Vines))\n\nAir:\n\nLarihei's Fingers\nFound in: Snow/Mountains\n((Mc Block: Grass))\n\nElf's Hair Vine\nFound in: Snow/Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\n\nCrouching Feather\nFound in: Wood Land's / Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nHalfling's Grass\nFound in: Wood Land's / Plains\n((MC block: Grass))\n\nTips:\n-Alchemist Sheers can be imbued with Unbreaking Glyph to make them last longer and Fortune for better chances to find Herbs!\n\n-If you leave alchemist sheers at 20 Durability before breaking them you can repair them with iron!", ""),
        StaticBook("Tablet Riddles", "§bCheza", "\"The Breaking\" \n\nNow broken, once whole. 7 knots in a rope.\nThe children of sea, betrayed by their hope.\nUnfinished promises, an entente unbound,\nas both of our tribes, lay sleeping underground.\n\nA prophet, the ocean, master of none,\nMaster of nothing, fatherless son.\nFather of nothing but what has been done,\na rope now broken, leaving its sons.\n\n\"Grieving of brothers.\"\n\nMan of him does not trick us like them\nman of him will not slay us instead.\nFor men of stone fall not for his act.\nFor men of stone still remember our pact.\n\nWe care now for seven, sons of the ocean.\nBut even now, we lose all motion.\nTired we slumber beneath the dirt.\nAs we return to dwell in our mother's hearth.\n\n\"Tales of the fall\"\n\nLet it be known, the danger of words.\nDanger of silence, danger of herds.\nDangers of mouthless phrases unheard.\nDanger of trickers and mission spurred.\n\nRest now, for tricksters do trap us alive,\ntrap us for power, trap us and bind,\ntrap us in guilt, worry hindsight,\ntrap us in questions of why we were blind.\n\n\"A price paid\"\n\nPeople yearn for gold and silver,\ncoins of copper, bars and silver.\nSilvers of soul, shards of dust,\ncurrency of monsters, beings above.\n\nCurrency they pay, brothers in debt,\nto the trickster of faith as he marks them for death.\nMark them for harvest, a farmer that sows,\nReaping of lives come a second toll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn I", "§bMarch Ash", "The Forest is strong, here. In few other places is the land as untouched, by magic or by Men. A better weapon there is rarely ever forged. The yolk of the world will yield to us the end of civilization.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Star", "§bArnorian Elendil", "The Knights of§0\n§0           The§0\n§0     Silver Shields§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0            By§0\n§0        Arnorian§0\n§0         Elendil\n\nA Knight there was, and that a worthy man, That from the time he first began,§0\n§0To Riden out. . .§0\n§0\n\nA Knight must prove§0\n§0          Always§0\n§0\n§0To be true.§0\n§0To be brave.§0\n§0To be kind.§0\n§0To love his land.§0\n§0To be a gentleman.§0\n§0To fight for what is just and right.§0\n§0To do no wrong of which he must be ashamed.\n\nThere once was a great castle deep in the woods. The castle had big thick walls, a high gate and towers that were bigger than the tallest trees. The old woods that spread around it was dark and dangerous, and many fierce giants lived in it.§0\n§0\n§0In the castle\n\nwas a group of knights who were kept there by the King of the country. It was there job to help travelers who might be in the woods, and to make war on the giants whenever they could.§0\n§0\n§0Each of the knights in the castle carried a magic shield. These\n\nshields were not like those of other knights, but had been made by a great magician who had lived in the castle many years before. The shields were made of silver, and when a knight was brave and good, his shield shone beautifully in the sun.§0\n§0\n\nWhen a knight was first given his shield, it was dark and plain in colour. Then, as he showed himself to be brave and kind, the shield began to sparkle until he could see his face in it as if the shield were a mirror. However, if a knight were lazy and\n\nafraid, the shield grew so dark that he became ashamed to carry it. §0\n§0\n§0But this was not all. When any knight was a very fine man and did something very brave, a golden star appeared in the middle of his shield. This was the greatest thing\n\nthat could happen to any man. At the time this story begins, only the captain of the castle had a gold star on his shield. The stars were very difficult, indeed, to win.§0\n§0\n§0Now there came a time when the worst of the giants gathered in the woods to make war\n\non the knights. They made a camp not far away, and killed anyone who traveled along the road.§0\n§0\n§0The captain told his men that on the next day he would lead them agaisnt the giants. When they heard the news, the knights were very pleased.\n\nHere, perhaps, was a chance for them to earn a gold star for their shields.§0\n§0\n§0Among the men in the castle was a new knight called Sir Roland. He was a fine soldier, and already his silver shield showed he was brave and strong. Sir Roland was looking\n\nforward to meeting the ugly giants. He promised himself that he would do his best to chase them far away.§0\n§0\n§0The next morning the captain of the knights came to Sir Roland and said, \"One good man must stay here and keep watch on the gate to our\n\ncastle. I have decided that you are the one who must remain behind.\"§0\n§0\n§0Roland was sorry, very sorry to hear the captain's order, but he said nothing. Soon the knights rode away on their horses and he was left alone. An hour went by, then two hours, and\n\nnothing happened at the castle. A deer came out of the woods to eat grass in the shadow of the castle wall. But Roland saw no other living creature. §0\n§0\n§0Then, at last, the Knight saw a man coming along the road through the trees. Roland saw that it was one\n\nof his fellow knights from the castle. The man had been hit in the hand by an arrow. He was not a brave man, and the look in his eyes showed that we had frightened. \"Let me watch the gate for you, Sir Roland,\" he cried.§0\n§0\n§0Roland's heart jumped with joy.\n\nThen he remembered the captain's orders. Sadly he said, \"My place is at the gate. Your place is with our knights. Go back to them.\"§0\n§0\n§0The knight was ashamed when Sir Roland spoke. Slowly he walked back to the woods and disappeared\n\namong the trees.§0\n§0\n§0After a time an old woman came along the road to the castle. She came up to Sir Roland and asked for food. He told her no one could come into the castle that day. Then he sent a servant to bring her bread and cheese.\n\nWhile she was waiting, Sir Roland asked her if she had seen the Knights and the giants. \"I have seen them,\" she said, \"and things go badly for your friends. If you were a real man, you would go and give them help.\" Sir Roland felt so badly that he shut\n\nthe gate after the old woman had her food. He did not want to listen to her any longer. After while the Knight heard a knock at the gate. \"What do you want?\" he asked.§0\n§0\"Open the gate, Sir Roland,\" someone replied. The Knight opened the gate and saw an old\n\nman standing a few feet away. The old fellow wore a long black cloak and carried a very beautiful sword.§0\n§0\"You should not be here,\" the man said, \"when your friends are having such a hard struggle with the giants.\" §0\n§0\n§0\"I have my orders,\"\n\nsaid Roland. \"I must not leave this gate.\"§0\n§0\"Look here! Listen to me,\" the old man cried. \"I have brought you this magic sword. Nonthing can stand before it. Take it, my friend, and help your fellow knights beat the giants.\" Roland believed that the sword\n\nreally was a magic one. He reached out his hand as though he would take it. The old man came forward as if he were going to cross over to the castle. §0\n§0\n§0But again it came to Sir Roland's mind that he had been told to stay the gate. He called out to the man\n\n\"No! Stay where you are.\" The man stopped, but he waved the sword in the air and cried, \"This is your last chance, Sir Knight! If you do not take it, your friends will all be killed by the giants while you hide behind a castle wall!\"§0\n§0\n§0Roland feared that\n\nif he listened any longer, he could not make himself stay in the castle.§0\n§0\n§0\"Close the gate,\" he told the servant. \"I must follow the captain's orders, and remain here.\"§0\n§0\n§0As the knight said these words a strange and surprising\n\nchange came over the old man. He began to grow bigger and bigger. Soon he was as tall as any giant in the great dark woods. At first Roland could not believe his eyes. Then he realized that the old fellow was really one of the giants. By magic he had made\n\nhimself look like a little old man! The Knight trembled to think of what would have happened if he had taken the sword and left the gate!§0\n§0\n§0While Sir Roland watched, the giant angrily went off down the road and was lost to sight among the trees.\n\nSoon after the giant had left, Sir Roland heard the sound of horses and men coming. It was the captain and his men returning to the castle. Roland signaled the servants to open the big gate and then he ran out to meet his friends.§0\n§0\n§0The knights were\n\ntired and dusty, but they were full of joy because they had soundly beaten the giants. When they had all come into the castle, Sir Roland closed the gate once more. Then he hurried to follow them to the great hall.§0\n§0\n§0As Roland came into the hall, he found\n\nevery man's eye upon him. \"The Shield! Look at Sir Roland's shield!\" they cried.§0\n§0\n§0The Knight slowly looked down at the silver shield he carried. There, flaming in the middle of the shield was a star of gold!§0\n§0\n§0\"Tell us, Sir Knight,\n\nwhat happened here at the castle today?\" The captain asked as soon as he had gotten over his surprise. \"Did giants try to break down the gate? Did you drive them away alone?\"§0\n§0\n§0\"No, Sir,\" said Roland. \"Only one giant came here, and he went away quietly\n\nwhen he found that he could not enter the castle.\" Then he told of all that had happened throughout the long day. §0\n§0\n§0When Sir Roland had finished his tale, the captain spoke. §0\n§0\"Men may make mistakes,\" he said, \"But our magic silver shields are never\n\nwrong! You, Sir Knight, have been the greatest among us today because you would not leave the gate on which I had ordered you to keep watch. No matter how much you wanted to be with us, you stayed at your job!\"§0\n§0\n§0Then the knights jumped to their feet\n\nand cheered Sir Roland until the great hall rang with their cries.§0\n§0\n§0   \"Long Live the§0\n§0    New Knight of§0\n§0  The Golden Star!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A moldy journal", "§bBeltran", "[!]The script below is written in a shaky, but experienced hand. As you read through the journal, the letters slowly turn red as ink is replaced with blood.\n\n\"It grips me, this madness. It coils through my bones, the very sickness in my flesh. The holes have started to appear, symptoms of this unholy disease. I fear our time is at an end.\n\nBrother Grimsby has advised us to pray to our lord,\n\nso that the lord's water may sweep us away to peace, but what peace shall I know if these waters are the very root of our sickness? Even now, I ponder upon the legitimacy of our god.\"\n\n\n1570 Brother Hosei\n\n\"Brother Lackmin was the first to fall out of our congregation. We buried his screaming corpse in our first grave. The other's are no better. Even now, I see the rotted specks of black upon their eyelids, hint of the corruption within them.\n\nThe great serpent has made it's visit again. It seems to detest our diseased bodies. Though I write this entry by candlelight, I still remember it's yellow eyes.\"\n\n\n\n1570 - Brother Hosei\n\n\"Brother Grimsby was the last who fell, except for me. Else the hint of rot on my body, I do not seem to be sucumbing to the rot as my fellows. I call it blessed, but Grimsby named me foul. 'God's water does not wash you away to his embrace' he chortles-\n\nas he reanimates. I had no choice but to smash his skull open, less he does the same to me.\"\n\n\n\n\n1570 -Brother Hosei\n\n[!]The script below appears in a chaotic, loopy script, a noticeable difference from the previous pages.\n\n\"It is me. I am chosen. I kneel at the alter and he speaks to me. The crimson waters flow from my flesh but yet he demands more.\n\n'a sacrafice, a sacrafice' they whisper in my ears. My Brother's voices pester for life, but even stab after stab, slice after slice, they do not abide.\"\n\n\n\n\n1571- Brother Hosei\n\n[!]A picture of a snake fills the entire page, printed in crimson are the words 'It Watches, my time has come.'", ""),
        StaticBook("T.F. Notes I", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "As I had guessed the art of Transfiguration seems to be just as easy as telekinesis, though this time it requires thorough understanding of Equivalent Exchange and alteration. Every object, no matter how small or large, has dormant mana.\n\nThis mana controls the alchemical make up of every object and such is where alchemy gets its powers, by tapping such and creating elixirs of the likes. This time the idea is to tap this mana using your own,\n\nnot to just change the velocity of this object but to change the whole makeup in your own way.. to alter the material how /you/ choose, though the law of equivalent exchange must be followed, so no turning Ferrum to Aurum any time soon.\n\nMy first connection seemed to be more easy than when I had first connected to control an object’s velocity when I had learned about telekinetics, but this time instead of using my connection to the void\n\nto ‘grip’ an object by this dormant mana, I was actually using my own mana to tap into this mana, and activate it! It was incredible, it had felt like I was one with this object.\n\nEven at my fairly low training with this magic I understand vastly on how this whole concept can be used in the most complex scenarios. For now I am to stick to heating this ball up, or cool it down.\n\nA simple task as temperature is a mere thought, though because of how new I am to this spell It seems to take a toll on my body as if I was a student once more, an odd feeling.\n\nAvenel, after our first lesson, has provide me with this metal ball. I will be using such to practice my first and many attempts of Transmutation, as it’s one of the most easiest matters to understand, especially as a blacksmith such as myself,\n\nor rather ex-blacksmith. It was simple, I had understood the weight of the ball when I had first held it, and I knew the makeup of Ferrum. So it was merely just /thinking/ of the reaction.\n\n-Sarrion\n2nd of Snow's Maiden\n1547", ""),
        StaticBook("Water Evocation", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "Water, appearing to be possibly one of the most simplest of the elements, however, it’s more than such. It’s an incredibly complex element in which one must spend a large amount of time meditating and spending there time around water in general to be able\n\nto learn such an evocation such as itself. Water is a necessity of life, needed by generally all living things, for example; Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also plants, including beasts too. Water, also appearing as such a calm element is also\n\none of the most dangerous, out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments, one can never have full control over water that isn’t evocated, well, practically no control whatsoever unless you’re of course, a Shaman. Despite our\n\nattempts, we are mortal, we do not live forever nor do we have amazing powers unlike the Ascended and Undead back in Aegis; as said before, water can be a very dangerous element, a single flood can wipe out a town, contaminate food and destroy buildings\n\nwith ease. A harsh winter, such as the one's in the North of Anthos and around the Dwarven regions which could halt one's food supply for months on end. The element, water contains raw power, a power that all Water Evocationist's would wish to wield.\n\nA Water Evocationist’s training consists of learning about the void, being able to evocate from it and about the element one is learning. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the\n\nsame as the water we have around us, however, it is completely different. The water that us Water evocationist’s evocate can only be found in the void and some say it isn’t water at all. As all evocoationists know, their power comes from the ability to be\n\nable to control ‘mana’, mana is your life force in a way. If you use it to much then one would simply fall unconscious or they can even die from the overuse of course. After much dedication and training; such as spending time to learn about the void\n\nand about Water Evocation, a Water Evocationist is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however, once one has managed to learn about\n\nWater Evocation itself, then you should be able to understand about it and where we're coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained as a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and\n\nevoking said element becomes more and more simpler tasks. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff, however, it isn’t needed much, though, it’s easier to focus upon, usually the tip for most and you would be able to evoke water from the tip,\n\ntoo. When water has been evoked, it can be placed into many forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice and other things which I generally haven’t explored yet.\nWater Evocationist’s which have been learning for a long period of time will\n\nbe able to use more things and be able to explore other skills such as learning to control ice which is also evoked from the void. Ice is more suited for battle than defence, however, water evocation itself is mainly used for defence than anything.\n\nHowever, ice can be evoked and be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block incoming projectiles as a form of short-distance defence, and as a method of harming others too. Ice that we evoke isn't the same which can be found in our realm, it cannot\n\nbe melted by the heat of the sun nor a torch, however - it can be melted with the use of Fire Evocation. To break the ice, the Water Evocationist must either lose concentration, or as said before, a Fire Evocationist must melt the ice with their evoked\n\nfire. In the later stages of Water Evocation, one would be able to evoke wisps of steam, however, it's possibly too difficult for even the best of Water Evocationist's to do such. Water, being able to form any concievable shape, is only limited by the\n\nby the caster's imagination and fatigue, which the exception of finely detailed creatures of sort. Such is reserved for Elemental Conjurationists. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\n\nCopied by Haadi Mubdee, Instructor in the Mages' Guild. 1471", ""),
        StaticBook("Novice Booklet", "§bBeltran", "[!]A novice script, the leather bound journal seems to belong to a novice monk.\n\n\"I have fled my teachers, the plague has been wrought upon them but an even dangerous creature lurks in the crowd of those undead! It slithers, the scales it clashes against the cobblestones. I fear I am alone in my endevaour. My peers have gone blind to-\n\nmy cries. My stomach grumbles but not for food but for escape, for food is what the eye wants from me.\"\n\n\n\n\n1570 -Frair Towl\n\n[!]Scratch marks are present on the page. Several pages are ripped apart. Blood is splattered upon the sheets in a careful manner, resembling an eye.\n\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n\n[!]The rest of the pages are crusted, as if they have been soaked in water.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs Vol.2", "§bLaerean", "Murex Cactus\nAn odd little cactus with a squat, spiraled cone structure. It is named after the murex shell, a type of conch featuring long spines. The murex cactus is covered in small barbs, but features several larger spines positioned along the path\n\nof its spiral. The cactus is partially hollow, with walls in its interior that break up its spiral into thin pods. Each of which are filled with a clear sap that causes vivid, primarily positive and fun hallucinations if drank in large enough quantities.\n\nFumes from burning the sap can also cause hallucinations if inhaled. \nRepresents: Fluidity\n((Unable to be obtained mechanical\n\nDrilltongue\nThis extremely hardy plant has a green hue and looks like a tangle of roots. Sometimes referred to by its common name, vines, it's typically found within that of mountainous or tundra related scene. It has the ability to ingrain itself into\n\nrock and to take water and nutrients from the snow and sleet around it. It's ends give out purple flowers which give out some sap. \nRepresents: Hardiness\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nElrow Berries\nElrow Berries, or Hellfire Fruit as the locals enjoy calling it, are probably one of the only symbols of Fire you will find within the cold and one may even find the fact that there is a symbol of Fire within cold to be quite strange.\n\nThese berries grow red surrounded by the whiteness of the snow around, making their bushes easy to find. When lost in these parts of the realm, finding a bush like this might be the salvation from freezing. These berries have also been known to be used\n\nin a rather potent ale, and therefore you should be wary of taking strange drinks from a strange man within the kingdom of Hanseti.\nRepresents: Rage, Poison, and destruction\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nPhoenix' Teardrop\nAn herb that is rare to find in the wilderness, as it requires a very steady climate found in warm places such as jungles or near hot springs so that it can stay warm because it freezes to death in cooler temperatures found\n\nin most of the other parts of the world. \nAt first glance this flower looks like a lily, but upon closer inspection it would prove that to be false, as the petals glisten in sunlight. The flower grows in clumps of fours to fives, and each flower's size\n\ncontributes to its average height of a rose bush. The people who are able to obtain the knowledge of this herb's properties count it as an extremely useful herbs in the field of healing.\n\nRepresents: Life\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nFire Flower\nThe Fire Flower or Phoenix Flower, is a stout piece of flora, and is quite rare to see natural-bushes of this flower in particular. As the several explorers further sought out to entail secrets of Anthos, they caught sight of the Fire\n\nFlower's death, which is what gives it it’s name. The flower can grow in warm or damp environments, however, cooler valleys with Fire Flowers are not unheard of. Desert, Taiga  and other forms of frozen or extremely hot\n\nlandscape seems to lack, or over-exceed, the requirements for Fire Flowers to groom on them. If an ash-seed of the flower was to fall on one of these biomes,\nthe seed would not sprout. It's appearance shares little to no particularities,\n\nexcept it’s flame-shaped small leaves. Other than that, it seems like an oddly-shaped thorn-less rose. The flower, upon death combusts it’s entire organic mesh, engulfing the entire flower in a prancing death dance of flames.\n\nThe flower’s ashes usually are taken by the wind, and these are actually seen to form new fire-flowers sprouts upon days of falling onto the ground. This flower only lasts a few hours burning, however, it, on it’s normal state,\n\ncan live for about three years. \nRepresents: Fire\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nBlazing Fern\nUpon the forests of the realms a strange few trees and plants seem to have changed. Some may say that the trees are ablaze in a flame, but to those with the keener eye, it is a growing vine-like plant bright orange and red,\n\nseemingly changing colors simultaneously. It has fern leaves protruding from the vines, and they take over branches and leaves,  leaving the tree into a form of hybrid. The next step in the cycle of the plants life is its decay.\n\nThe ferns begin to become a fading orange, as if it were a dying flame. It then turns to an ashen grey, as the colors on the vines begin to fade. At this point you would see strange insects, the color of foggy water climb up the vines, and eat\n\nthe grey remains. The roots of the vines, unlike most plants, start from the top of the trees. They are originally seeds from another vine, as they grow small pellet-like seeds on the ferns, and are carried out in the wind.  They take rainwater and spread\n\ninto the leaves, then into the tree itself. It entwines into the bark, and grows vines.\nRepresents: Poison and Destruction\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nBlistering Toad\nA gnarled orange and red fungus it grows only in places of great humidity. Found commonly in rotting trees it is a rare sight even for the trained eye. At a first glance it looks like an ornamental toad that is stuck\n\nto the edge of a rotting oak log. There is no sap inside of the fungus instead there are spores which will begin to decay almost instantly unless they are transported quickly and smoothly from the inside of the fungus into an air-tight jar\n\n(This can be achieved with a wax seal). The fungus is practically odourless and so are the spores and this is one reason why it makes it so difficult to find. Very difficult to cultivate as there are no seeds just the spores and the conditions need\n\nto be almost perfect for it to grow. \nRepresents: Poison\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nKing's Ivy\nA delicate flower found mostly growing in ancient ruins around the world. It's named originates from it's royal look, with delicate golden petals protecting an almost gem looking center. In full bloom this flower almost seems to shine\n\nbright like a small star. This flower is very useful for adventurers due to it's effects. Some myths even tell of King's Ivy's growing where royal families used to live, so they can mark a place of royal tombstone.\n\nWhile some adventurers claim that this myth is true, it is still uncertain.\nRepresents: Vigor\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nFlash Fruit\nThe Flash Fruit is a fruit which grows on the tallest of trees usually where predators cannot reach them, soaring to grow on any branch. Their seeds are carried by the wind, and will only grow in a thin oxygen atmosphere\n\nusually found onto of the Elven elder Trees or on the cliff trees of the jungles. The fruit is not part of the tall trees, being of a plant which only grows on these particular conditions. There aren't any leaves, the plant creating nothing\n\nmore than vines around the branches, then creating the fruit. The fruit has a texture of yellow with orange streaks through it's body. The skin of the fruit has a rich sweet taste, and can satisfy someone's thirst for a day. The insides are filled with\n\na maroon ooze, which if consumed will slightly numb the muscles in the throat, however not enough to cause that of death or tremendous suffering.\nRepresents: Hydration\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nNightsap\nNight sap seems to be found in deformed growths (probably caused by some type of insect) on the trunks of sturdy oak trees. A thick, honey like substance, it is as golden as an afternoon sunrise and as mouth-watering\n\nto behold as any substance one can readily find. The taste and smell brings back memories of blue skied, worriless evenings on grassy plains, eating fine meals with finer company; unrivalled in texture and taste by any morsel yet to devourer.\n\n Night sap can be used as an average earth symbol in alchemy or a highly addictive drug by those who are truly troubled. It can also be used in dire situations to sedate a patient in an operation, or to poison some poor fellow\n\nwho wronged the wrong herbalist.\nRepresents: Calm and Poison\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nShadeleaf\nA small, short plant. The plant is very similar to a common weed which has quite plain leaves, yellow flowers when reproducing, and which is rather short and small as well. In addition, this weed grows in a large\n\nabundance, normally hiding Shadeleaf. In addition, the two greens of the plants are quite similar, Shadeleaf leaves being a tad darker. The only difference is that the veins on the bottom of the leaves of Shadeleaf plants are silver-colored.\n\nHowever, when looking at the plants from above both are practically identical. Because of this, searching for Shadeleaf plants is quite difficult since large amount of time is wasted lifting up leaves and looking at the veins underneath\n\nto see if they are silver. And to make it even worse, Shadeleaf plants are quite sparse. There is only one part of this plant that has been proven to be useful, the leaves. Shadeleaf leaves have a drug-like effect, hallucinogenic with large enough doses.\n\nThe leaves can be breathed in, eaten, or directly applied to the bloodstream, and the effect is the same due to the plant’s sustaining effects. In order to use the drug, most people grind the leaves up or extract the juices from the leaves by boiling\n\nthe leaves in water. Then the drug can be burned in incense trays or using pipes in order to inhale the substance.\nRepresents: Fluidity, Relaxation, and calmness\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nAnt Blight\nAn uncommon yet quite interesting plague on most types of fruit trees, (and primarily found in orchards where fruit trees are tightly packed,) the Ant Blight fungus appears as a swarm of tiny,  shiny black spots on the bark of a tree.\n\nHowever, its interconnected roots can run fairly deep, as it must be able to drink from its host’s water supply effectively. The ant-like spots range in scale from roughly the size of a mustard seed to the size\n\nof a pinto bean. They release their spores around the early spring months, but can also spread through the fruit of the trees they infect. Fruit from trees infected with Ant Blight develop tumor-like growths and other grotesquely mutated features,\n\nand taste rotten and disgusting if eaten, like the 'ants' themselves. The seeds from inside these fruits, if planted, are guaranteed to grow trees that are also contaminated by the blight. If farmers notice Ant Blight growing in their orchards,\n\nthey would do best to hastily cut off and dispose of any branches covered in the black spots before it spreads to other trees. One cannot remove the blight simply by scraping the ants off, for if the roots are still there, they will just grow back.\n\nRepresents: Plague\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically", ""),
        StaticBook("Workers Handbook", "§bBeltran", "[!]A list of buildings supplies are listed upon the page, including the curious entry of 'Frog Oil'\n\n[!]A list of excavations needed are listed upon the page, including the entry of 'Escape Tunnel'", ""),
        StaticBook("Stone Men Riddle", "§bCheza", "Stone men... §0\n§0Speak stone words...§0\n§0Eggs do not hatch.§0\n§0For face without mouth...§0\n§0Speak words that they lack.§0\n§0How do they speak?§0\n§0These stone men with none...§0\n§0Unmoving lips, eyes and ears sewn shut...§0\n§0What of our hands, what of our tools?\n\nIn a wordless whisper, they do nonetheless move...§0\n§0For such is the ode...§0\n§0Of brothers of fish.§0\n§0Mountains of madness, chisels and wish.§0\n§0Mountains of stone...§0\n§0Mountains of words.§0\n§0Standing in forrest...§0\n§0Message unheard.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Enchanting", "§bSarrion", "On Arcane Enchanting\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following are my own personal notes taken from my research from interviews with other Transfigurationists and my lessons from Avenel.\n\nIn Transfiguration there is a sub-classed spell base called Enchanting. Enchanting is the simple art of transmuting either a command for an object or a spell  to bind to an object with a medium\n\nground  that powers the spell. This medium ground is almost always a mana crystal, which is any gem though the rarer the gem the more mana it can hold. The transfigurationist is to first channel his/her mana into this gem and fill it entirely\n\nwith his mana, then transmute the spell or command into the gem and bind it to the object arcanely. This whole progress burns /a lot/ of mana in the mage's mana pool, and it a dangerous art that can either kill the mage\n\nor cause a mana fluctuation. This is why that sometimes a mage may set up an enchanting lab with a “Mana Obelisk”, for those who are ignorant in the topic a Mana Obelisk is a large gem pillar that has\n\nbeen enchanted to contain a large mass of mana, that way when it comes time to enchant the enchanter can pull the mana from the crystal to the gem, not having to use their own mana.\n\nDo note the creation of a Mana Obelisk is very intricate and will need to be activated by two or more Transfigurationists.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs Vol.1", "§bLaerean", "Mandragora\nUsed in Alchemy as a strong healing reagent, it can be found in pools of waters in swamps, spotted by their leaves on the surface.\nThe Mandragora's leaves are used sometimes as a garnish or for teas. The meat of the plant is what you are\n\nlooking for, and it is suspended by the leaves. Remember to wear gloves or other protection while harvesting this though, as it has spores that cause paralysis.\nRepresents: Life, Rebirth, Rejuvenation, Fluidity, and Regrowth\n((Block:Lilypad, Swamp\n\nSerpent's Stalk\nA common plant normally found growing near water in dry areas. It is most often mistaken for sugarcane or reeds, as it has a similar color to it and it grows in the same manner. It has excellent healing properties, mostly being used for\n\ntreating burns. The inside of the stalk is almost like a gel, when collected and mixed with water it has a cooling effect.\nRepresents: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, and Fluidity.\n((Block: Sugarcane, Plains\n\nFrost Vine\nA blue colored vine growing on snowy cliffs in mountainous regions. Frost Vine has healing properties like other water symbols do. It can be rubbed on the skin to cool burns or loosen stiff muscles. Prolongued use is not advised but will\n\nnot cause permanant numbness.\nRepresents: Life, Ice, and Calmness.\n((Block: Vine, snowy\n\nBlissfoil\nA plant with thin stems topped with blue flowers. Blissfoil is a plant that can help relieve pain and numb an area. Be cautious when using it though, as too much can cause permanant numbness.\nRepresents: Calmness, Peace, and Apathy.\n\n((Block: ???, ???\n\nAthin\nA blue colored algae\nthat grows in icy waters. Athin is only found in cold regions and one who is looking for it should come prepared so they don't sucumb to the elements. Fishing nets are often able to get Athin. Athin is also extremely\n\nresistant to heat, and one of the best reagents to use for a cold potion or oil.\nRepresents: Life, Ice, Freezing, and Balance.\n((Block: Packed Ice, Snowy\n\nCrimson Vase\nThe flower has deep red petals that curve upwards like a vase. Its petals are very delicate and harvesting it for use should be done with care or it will become ineffective. Touching the petals gives the person's skin a warm sensation\n\nthough not unpleasant. It is found in dry areas like forests or plains and is spotted in grass due to its red color.\nRepresents: Heat, Love, Passion, Compassion, and Warmth.\n((Block: Grass, Fores/Plains\n\nDrake's Tail\nA thorny plant growing in hot, humid areas such as deserts. It's fairly rare to find, often growing in shade near a water source such as an oasis. It has red hued, thorny stems and short roots beneath the sand. When harvesting be careful\n\nand wear thick leather gloves, because being pricked by the thorns can cause a high fever.\nRepresents: Chaos, Heat, and Destruction\n((Blocks: Dead Bush, Desert\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nAn orange-leafed shrub that is found in swamps. Dwarf's Pumpkin is short and stumpy with thick leaf stems and broad leaf blades. The leaves themselves are what you want to harvest but be prepared for a strong odor on your trip back to\n\nwhere ever you go back to. This plant is often used to brew a strong ale dwarves love. \nRepresents: Rage, Envy, Power, Strength, and Bitterness\n((Block: Grass/Lilypad\n, Swamp\n\nBlood Lotus\nA viny plant that crawls up the walls of sandstone caves and is well adapted to its hot climate. It has incredible nutritious properties and you could live off of a diet of it alone.\nRepresents: Hope, Courage.\n((Blocks:DeadBush,Des\n\nFlametongue Root\nThe plant appears almost like a rose in a forest or field, loving to live in sunny water abundant regions. Its thick stalks are covered in brambles and has bright red roots. The brambles, if allowed to prick the skin, will cause\n\nblistering pain, the likes of which will cause most to pass out. The use of thick leather gloves is recommended when harvesting. \nRepresents: Heat, Anger, and Destruction\n((Blocks: Grass, Forest/Plains\n\nLarihei's Fingers\nA plant with smooth burrowing roots and small, short leaves in the summer months.\nIt grows in snowy regions, and can often be hard to find amongst the snow. It has no immediate healing properties and isn't really edible but when\n\nused in the right mixture it can make you much more acute and aware.\nRepresents: Grace, Beauty, Steadiness, Focus, and Swiftness\n((Blocks: ???, ???\n\nElf's Hair Vine\nA strong white vine that is covered in dozens of small white flowers. It grows on cliffs out of the wind, as the flowers are very fragile and will blow away easily. Harvest the plant with great care, as the smallest touch can make the\n\nflowers float away in even the lightest breeze.\nRepresents: Grace, Speed, Flight, Travel\n((Block: Vine, Snowy\n\nCrouching Feather\nA plant that is a very rare sight. It has three white curved petals that flow downward from the top of the stem, looking like a feather. It only blooms at night, and usually grows beneath the shade of trees in forests. The petals are\n\nvery delicate and liable to break and float away with a strong gust of wind.\nRepresents: Speed, Travel, Grace, and Beauty\n((Block: Grass, Plains Forest\n\nHalfling's Grass\nA tall plant that grows in lit forests. The roots are soft and round, and are the part of the plant that an alchemist is looking for. The leaves can be smoked and have an effect similar to cactus green.\nIt can also be processed\n\ninto a potion which has even stronger effects. It is named for being able to grow the same height as a Halfling, and also for its uses by that race as pipeweed.\nRepresents: Calm, Joy, and Lifting.\n((Blocks: Grass, Forest\n\nTippen's Root\nA foul smelling weed of which is the bane of gardeners and farmers alike. It grows everywhere and is almost impossible to get rid of, because if even a single root remains it will simply grow back and spread. It has purple flowers above\n\nthe ground, and a reddish brown root with black spots below the ground. It is mainly used for healing potions and has blood clotting properties in the root. It can also be used directly on the wound if you can stand the awful stench of the root.\n\nRepresents: Regrowth, Resilience, Strength, Endurance, and Life.\n((Block: Grass, Plains and Forests\n\nAbalaster Leaf\nA small leafy plant found growing on fallen trees and up the trunks of those still standing. It can blend in with the leaves that the tree it resides on, and holds a residue that causes nausea, though it isn't particularly harmful\n\nuntil brewed into the right mix.\nRepresents: Immobility\nand Perseverance.\n((Blocks: Grass, Forest\n\nSaffvil\nA grass that spreads over the bodies of dead animals and rotting plants. It is extremely hard to get rid of, and smells like death. Its main use is in poisons.\nRepresents: Resilience, Endurance, and Death\n((Block: Grass, Swamp\n\nClutcher's Straw\nA plant that grows about as tall as your common grass, but has a brown color akin to that of a dead bush. The blades aren't as sharp as normal grass, but the roots beneath the ground are extremely sharp, so caution\n\nis advised. It grows in hot, dry regions such as deserts.\nRepresents: Brutality,\nImpairment, and Loss\n((Block: Dead Bush/Grass, Desert\n\nMetzli's Tangle\nA thick green vine found in jungles. It has a few leaves protruding from its main stalk, and relies on its host tree for water and nutrition.\nIt cannot survive on its own, and because of that it can only be found against a large\n§\n\ntrunk in humid, dark jungles.\nRepresents: Fear and\nDependency.\n((Block: ???, ???\n\nGoblin's Ivy\nA murky brown colored ivy that spreads like a weed in deserts. It is extremely hard to get rid of and loves growing up on the sides of buildings, ruins, any mountain it can latch onto. Though it doesn't get very tall and remains the bane o\n\nthe people who have to deal with it. It is a weak ingredient in poisons.\nRepresents: Poison, Life, and Resilience.\n((Block: Vines, Desert\n\nGijaklul\nAlso known as the \"Bloodflower\", it is a rare type of flower found in deserts, especially the ones orcs reside in. It is known for its crimson petals that create an odor similar to that of rotten flesh. The flower is mostly found\n\nnear the Gijakul trees in the deserts growing near the waters of a stream or oasis. Another thing to note; it gives off a faint glow after dusk. The flower only blooms during the blood moon, giving them the name \"Bloodflower\".\n\nRepresents: Life and Warmth\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically.\n\nJavens\nA plant most commonly found in deserts. Javens is a large sand spur with green colored stripes going along this green plant. Despite its thorns, it's quite soft and easy to chew. Due to its effects it is commonly used by doctors\n\nto help victims in pain.\nRepresents: Calm, Impairment, and Immobility.\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nZawabate\nThe Oasis Blossom of the Desert, Zawabate is as rare a sight to see as a lush and fertile Oasis is in the deserts. Zawabate has some of the most prominent hues of green and yellow, its petals short and curvy, and its stalk tall and proud.\n\nZawabate’s favored growing location is near the fertile waters of the Oasis it rests within, protected from the harsh realities of the desert in something of a dreamland of verdant life. This plant is known by the locals to possess\n\nmirage-inducing properties that are often used in a tea to grant hallucinations.\nRepresents: Life, Calmness, and Rebirth\n((Unable to be obtained mechanically\n\nWisp of Old\nThe first words directly spoken to this flower upon its blooming the Wisp of Old will repeat in a soft and whimsical tone, nearly incoherent unless being focused upon. This single quote will be repeated until the flower dies.\n\nWisp of Old flowers grow and bloom only once every 7 years upon a cactus, and only remains alive for a single night while attached to the cactus. Removing the flower would require very steady hands, for if one petal is damaged or lost, the flower\n\nwill die. Upon removal from the cactus, a Wisp of Old can remain alive indefinitely. However any damage upon the flower will still result in the flower dying, even after it’s safe removal from the cactus. \n((Unable to be obtained mechanically", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Fai, Zilas, Erwin, Cerilos, And A Kha of which I did not get the name.\n\nFai, Helped get a bucket, aided with other task.\n\nZilas, Helped with A spook problem.\n\nErwin, Took him in after nearly dying outside Sutica.\n\nThe Kha, Gave food, and helped with the Soul Pillar.\n\nCerilos, Gifted an Item he needed.", ""),
