        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Zilas,§0\n§0Helped with Some spooks, as well as had a friendly chat.§0\n§0*Most of the Task were Random, Maybe not task at all, but done non the less.*\n\nTrent, Gave Food to someone ineed, tried to have a friendly chat..\n\nErwin, Aided within Sutica,\n\nCerilos, Gave a needed Item to Cerilos.\n\nFai, (Half of the name was written.) §0\n§0Gifted her with a much needed Teapot, and Teapot Talk. As well as gave her a bucket.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Traveling Diary§0\n§0\n§0Page 1 Warhawks", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "A series of odd runes are either sketched here or seem to be a charcoal rubbing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bKristoff Herrick", "Wound healing\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet's start by steps\nStep 1- Cleaning the wound. \nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or\n\ndeeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. (ofcourse you need to take the dirt off first if it has dirt in it). \nStep 2- Suttering the wound. \nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread.Sounds easy\n\nright? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these...Let's called them sub steps.\nSub Step I Heat up the needle. You need to do that incase of the needle carring any illness.\nSub Step II Clean the thread.You need to do\n\nit beacause you don't want dirt on your wound.\n \nSun Step III-Suttering You start at well the start of the gash or deep wound (Warning this does NOT apply for small wounds.) \nYou'll then sutter like your sewing a rag, a messy and bloody rag\n\nthat screams like a little girl, non the less a rag. \n\nStep 3-Bandaging\nA bandage can be almost anything, a old rag (As long as it's clean) A bed sheet (As long as it's clean) etc. Then you just wrap it around the wound. Done\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection after or  before you done this process you'll be better off cuting off the leg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Will of §0\n§0Archrim Dominic Elmoran:§0\n§0\n§0In the event of my death be it natural or otherwise the items within this chest shall be divided between my family and loved ones as follows.\n\nRuby Ring: To my daughter Frieda as a token of my caring and love for her.§0\n§0Crystal Flower: To my daughter Arwen as to remember to appriciate the beauty and magic of nature.§0\n§0Ornate bracelet: To my wife Isabella and the woman whom I loved above all\n\nelse.§0\n§0\n§0Any mina left within my bank savings is to be divided into fourths and a quarter be given to each of my daughters and half to my wife Isabella§0\n§0\n§0wyvern tail: To my one of my greatest friends Karysmov Faroe\n\nas a token to remember the adventures we had and to know that life with out fun and adventure is no life at all.§0\n§0\n§0Anything not named within this chest is to be given to my family so they may give it to those who the deem deserve it or keep it\n\nMy Axe Service as well as my armor both iron and Carbarum sets and all other weapons and tools are also to be given to my family and kept by my family so they may see use and appriciation by my Posterity. Aswell as my home within the city and any land I\n\nmay own outside the city.§0\n§0\n§0Final thoughts: I suppose I will not be able to say any proper goodbyes upon my death and so within this document let me say I wish all of you my warmest and happiest farewells.\n\nI wish it to be known that I have a few requests upon my death §0\n§01. That I be laid to rest atop a Pyre and set ablaze §0\n§0\n§02. That a statue be Erected in my honor in my likeness to honor not only myself but the brave\n\nmen and women who protect us and the city we hold so dear.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0And with that Let it be known that I was an Honorable and brave man who did his best to serve others and be the best man he could be.\n\nAnd most importantly be known as a kind and loving husband and Father to the best family I have ever known§0\n§0\n§0-With Love§0\n§0First Knight of Sutica§0\n§0Archrim D. Elmoran", ""),
        StaticBook("Ysuldan", "§bBeranabus Seregon", "[!] Msg Booklight12 for more information and to interact with the book\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nAscended\nPaladins\nClerics\nOren\nDwarves\nOrcs\nWood Elves\nDark elves\nLibrary\nNorth\nEnchantry\nMisc", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "2 bodies, 1 male and 1 female.§0\n§0\n§0female was named \"Dawn\"§0\n§0\n§0Both bodies burnt by lightning and eyes were gouged out.\n\n2 attackes, one was elf, the other unknown, §0\n§0one said to have dark tendrils (shade magic), §0\n§0the unknown was hooded and had red robes with white trim", ""),
        StaticBook("Ethro's Report", "§bEthro Kellian II", "To Sentinel.§0\n§0\n§0You have a Disrespecful guard on your hands. §0\n§0The redhead known as 'Eve' Refuses to accept your orders about the Armored man, chooses to argue with me about how he shouldent have to take off his armor.\n\nEven though the Person in question was Cooperation and removing his arms and Armor.§0\n§0She then canceled the Class thing she was doing as she tried to use it as a threat towards me to listen to her orders.§0\n§0I did not have need for her class.§0\n§0-Lt.Ethro§0 Kellian", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy herb", "§bLlywellyn Oakleaf", "Fire symbols\n\n-Strong-\nBlistering toad\nDrakes tail\n\n-Moderate-\nFlame tongue root\nDwarfs Pumpkin\nSinged Kha\nElrow Berries\nBlood lotus\n\n-Normal-\nBlazing fern\nFire flower\nNight sap\n\n-Weak-\nDessert Bush (Berries)\nOrc's Braid\n\nEarth symbols\n\n-Moderate-\nAlabaster leaf\nFairie truffle\nTippens root\nSaffvil\nDrilltongue\nDesert berry bush (stalk)\nBronze dust\n\n-Weak-\nGoblins Ivy\nMiners Helmet\n\nWater Symbols\n\n-Strong-\nAqua nymph\nAthin\nSpirit of Magnolis\n\n-Moderate-\nSerpents stalk\nMandragora\nFrost vine\nZawabate\nJokers scum\n\nAir Symbols\n\n-Strong-\nCrouching feather\nElf's Hair Vine\nWisp's Breath\n\n-Moderate-\nSwamp blossom\n\n-Weak-\nJailer's Moss\n\nUnknown\n\n-King's Ivy\n-Shadeleaf\n-Biteit\n-Atheros (possibly a water symbol)\n-Gijaklul\n-Javens", ""),
        StaticBook("To slay a Ghoul", "§bWilliam Roswell", "Ghouls\n         =======\n\nBy Edward William Roswell\n*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*\n\nGhouls are strange creature, the work of a deranged necromancer they are deadly beasts, coming in many shapes and sizes, each-\n\n- a different set of skills, claws and teeth.\n\nGhouls are driven by their hunger, appearing to not feel any form of emotion, the only thing which can cause it to show a reaction is sudden and severe pain.\n\nGhouls often attack when you least expe-\n\n-ct it, often staling it's prey from afar before striking.\n\nGhouls stalk their prey at a distance to mask their smell, it being a similar smell to rotting corpses.\n\nOften before the attack, the victim can smell the ghoul, but only when it is-\n\n- very close to the house, the smell of ghouls being easier to smell when the creature is outside.\n\nAs the ghouls attack when you least expect it, it is hard to combat and every ghoul comes with it's own set of deadly surprises.\n\nBut the one thing the ghouls have all shown to have incommon is their weaknes to Aurum weaponry.\n\nAurum works effectively against the beasts, it being one of it's main weaknesses, it might be caused due to something similar to an allergic reaction to th-\n\n-e metal.\n\nAlthough aurum is effective against them, the one thing which can kill a ghoul instantly is a strike towards it's neck, sever the neck and the beast dies instantly.\n\nSome tend to explode after death, leaving-\n\n- a horrible smell and black muck covering the explosion radius.\n\nFerrum weapons are also effective against ghouls if, and only if you strike it's neck to kill it instantly, otherwise it is useless.\n\nFire is also highly effective against ghouls, either-\n\n- setting it on fire or using the fire to distract it works, as it causes the beast pain.\n\nAlways keep a broom handy to clean up the mess which a dead ghoul leaves, as slaying a ghoul is a truly messy ordeal.\n\n*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*", ""),
        StaticBook("Report", "§bAerith Oranor", "Report on the attack on 10th of Snow Maiden:\n\nDraoi attacks Sutica once again after the Ascended created a brazier to ward of dark beings and fight off corruption.\n\nFirst it was complete silence of the nature surrounding Sutica, followed by a slight tremor and nearby animals starting to act weird. Eventually the tremor grew worse as the buildings in the city started shaking and the animals became aggressive.\n\nFrom what I could observe-\n\nThis Draoi is capable of...\n\n-controlling most if not all animals\n-control of nature to some extent\n-weather especially, ex: rain, lightning", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Revolver?\"", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Idea- \"Elmoran Revolver\"§0\n§0\n§0I have heard rumors of evocationists with devices never before seen by man. devices that are when used with magic they launch projectiles out of the front ends. projectiles that of course are\n\nakin to the nature of the evocationists magic, such as a fire evocationist whom could launch a fireball out of it or a arcanist who fires a beam of sorts.§0\n§0But what would a telekinetic such as myself use since we use objects\n\nin the world around us as our weapon?§0\n§0I hypothosize a sort of ammunition, made of iron that would place within the chamber and using telekinesis on it launch it out of the front end or \"barrel\" at high speeds.\n\nproblem- wouldnt having to reload every shot be a waste of time?§0\n§0Why yes it would be but what it you could load more than one round into the device at once? I have thought on this for awhile and I think that perhaps a cylindrical\n\ncontainer for the ammunition would suffice, place holes within each end of the cylinder to be able to load the rounds into the device and on the handle near the thumb place a handle for when pulled it would rotate the cylinder of ammunition\n\ninto position to fire another shot. §0\n§0\n§0I have had another idea dealing with what I like to call the \"Elmoran Revolver.\"§0\n§0\n§0Why stop at iron rounds? Im a guardsman i fight just about everything\n\nso why not fight dark creatures with my new tool? perhaps I can start making arum rounds for my soon to be weapon as to be able to launch them into the waiting flesh of evil-doers\n\nMy project is nearlyt complete, within a month or two my weapon should be ready for its first test, I am excited to use it in combat soon, im sure it will throw off anyone who dares commit crime within sutica", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!] There'd be multiple sketches of various things rather unrelated to eachother§0\n§0\n§0You can piece together several written phrases...\n\n\"Nightmares, still present, if I'm lucky they stop for a few days\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Twitching is worse, thankfully it rarely happens with the others around\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Is painting still working? No idea...\"\n\n\"Should I take drinking up again? Maybe...? Maybe not...? Hm...\"§0\n§0\n§0\"It's like I'm slowly going §0mad...haha...\"§0\n§0\n§0\"How's Eris been?\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Could I really be forgiven...? Nah...\"\n\n\"Am I seeing things...?\"§0\n§0\n§0[!] There'd be more unreadable scribbles and such", ""),
        StaticBook("Passport B3", "§bFitonor de Fontaine-Elmpool", "Issued by Fitonor de Fontaine-Elmpool of the Imperial Administration * given to Ser Walter Marshall, whom is a class B2 citizen, On the 14th of the Sun's Smile, 1588. This passport is legal tender until 14th of the Sun's Smile, 1598. If found, please -\n\nreturn to the Imperial Administration in Johannesburg.§0\n§0\n§0~Fitonor de Fontaine-Elmpool, Auditor General ((Chorale_))", ""),
        StaticBook("Morality V:I", "§bTheon Mallister", "§0\n§0\n§0   Human Morality V:I\n\nIf the entire human species were a single individual, that person would long ago have been declared mad. The insanity would not lie in the anger and darkness of the human mind—though it can be a black and raging place indeed.\n\nAnd it certainly wouldn't lie in the transcendent goodness of that mind—one so sublime, we fold it into a larger \"soul\".  The madness would lie instead in the fact that both of those qualities, the savage and the splendid,\n\ncan exist in one creature, one person, often in one instant.§0\n§0\n§0We're a species that is capable of almost dumbfounding kindness. We nurse one another, romance one another, weep for one another.\n\nWe're the only species with language, we told ourselves—until gorillas and chimps mastered sign language. Until cats could walk and talk. Khas, they call themselves. We're the only one that uses tools then—but that's if you don't\n\ncount otters smashing mollusks with rocks or apes stripping leaves from twigs and using them to fish for termites.§0\n§0What does, or ought to, separate us then is our highly developed sense of morality, a primal understanding of good and bad\n\nof right and wrong, of what it means to suffer not only our own pain—something anything with a rudimentary nervous system can do—but also the pain of others. That quality is the distilled essence of what it means to be human.\n\nWhy it's an essence that so often spoils, no one can say.§0\n§0\n§0Morality may be a hard concept to grasp, but we acquire it fast. A preschooler will learn that it's not all right to eat in the classroom, because the teacher says it's not.\n\nIf the rule is lifted and eating is approved, the child will happily comply. But if the same teacher says it's also O.K. to push another student off a chair, the child hesitates. He'll respond, 'No, the teacher shouldn't say that.'\n\nIn both cases, somebody taught the child a rule, but the rule against pushing has a stickiness about it, one that resists coming unstuck even if someone in authority countenances it. That's the difference between a matter of morality and\n\none of mere social convention.§0\n§0Of course, the fact is, that child will sometimes hit and won't feel particularly bad about it either—unless he's caught. The same is true for people who steal or despots who slaughter.", ""),
        StaticBook("YOR MOTER STORY", "§bGu-Zhizhe", "YOU MOHTHER JOUREY§0\n§0\n§0SHE BIG HOR SHE COME FROM OEN SHE KOK MANY SOK SHE TAKE DHE BEK SHE MAKE DHE FEK SHE LEK DHE DEK SHE GE TE BET SHE NEK DHE GEK SHE FEK DHE SEK AND KEK A LEK§0\n§0\n§0HAAHHAHAH UR MOHER HOR FEK FER LEK", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I begin my task by travelling to the woodelf city. When I arrived, I looked around to see if someone could open up the gates but no one was around so I moved on. I travelled down the road and found the dark elf city.\n\n I was excited some given I haven’t really seen another dark elf or really remember seeing anyone of my kind. I was greeted by large and strong dark elf woman named Varasa. She made me nervous at first,but I followed her after she let me\n\nin and I offered her some bread. She refused and I asked her who she worships. Her reply was her Ancestors. I inquired more about that which turns out to be family Ancestors of dark elves such as myself. I felt embarrassed for not knowing or perhaps\n\nnot remembering that and she offered me to come live there and teach me about them. I am not sure if I should or not given I am afraid of my own past.§0\n\nMy journey then continues down the path towards Haria when I came across a small village off to the right side. It was there I met my second person. He was in full armor, but sounded like a human I think and his name was Robyn.\n\nI offered him some bread, but he declined then we talked about religion for awhile. He himself doesn’t believe in any because of the conflict that comes with it. Choosing one side and fighting with the other. I do agree with him on not liking conflict or\n\n someone pushing their views on another, but to me if someone wishes to follow and/or worship, I think that is alright.§0\n\nMy journey then continues on to the great city of Haria. It was still under construction, but still very beautiful. I wandered around for awhile, not finding anyone until I shouted and got a reply. After several minutes,\n\nI ran into a rather hairy looking woodelf male that went by the name of Rafiel. He was very kind and invited me inside his home to get out of the rain. I offered him some bread and he accepted it and ate while we chatted some.\n\nHe is an alchemist and spends most of his time with his own studies and doesn’t really socialize much. I ask him about what he worships and he replied with none. His reason was because of past experiences and finds those that worship silly.\n\nWhich I have seen some that are rather silly. He wished me luck on my journey on becoming an Adherent and said we should meet up again. I might if I travel there again.§0\n\nContinuing on my journey I end back up on the road heading towards the woodelf city. There on the road, I found female woodelf by the name of Mare. She was very kind, yet declined the bread when I offered it to her. When I asked her which religion\n\n she worshipped, she replied with Aspectism. I asked her what that was and she said it had something to do with a cycle and life and death. I thanked her for her explanation and continued on my way.§0\n\nMy last stop ended up at the woodelf city again and luckily there were people there this time. I was let in by a female woodelf by the name of  Arahaelth. She sat near the fountain afterwards and I walked over to chat with her.I offered her bread and she\n\n declined and when I asked about what religion she worship, she said she was a druid and worship the Aspects. It was then I realized Aspectism or these Aspects were deities and druids seem to be like Adherents and paladins except druids\n\nworship thier own deities. Ara confirmed that and also said her husband was an Adherent too, Katar Aureon. I hope I meet him along with any others I haven’t met yet.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem", "§bTorren", "Blue is the sky that envelopes our heavens.§0\n§0Red is the flames that can both give and take.§0\n§0Yellows the blessing us with life and beginning our day.§0\n§0Green is the grass that envelopes our earth.§0\n\nOrange is the sunset that brings end to our day.§0\n§0Purple is the twilight that brings forth the night.§0\n§0Brown is the dirt from which life springs.§0\n§0The aspects are our painters and nature their beloved masterpiece of art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic medicine", "§bRhova'dir", "-How to make a first aid kit-\n\n*You will need the following things*\n\n>Strips of Cloth for bandages and cleaning wounds.\n\n>A vial of Vodka to clean wounds, needles and hands.\n\n>Gauze to use for putting herbs on a bandage.\n\n>Suture needles and a spindle of thread for stitching deep cuts.\n\n>Water bottles for mixing herbs into a solution, cleaning eyes or even hydration.\n\n>Honey allows the medicine to go down easier and helps with colds and with the new borns-\n\n-to start feeding.\n\n>A mask for not allowing poisonous chemicals or body fluids enter your body.\n-----------------------------\n\nIf the patient has been cut or stabbed, quickly remove all the materials that can infect the wound like cloth, dirt and other things, proceed to apply some moss to absorb the blood, clot the wound or even tourqinet the wound.\nIf the wound is a-\n\n-puncture, anything inside it can infect the wound; and remember, even the smallest cut can kill the strongest;\nIts good to know how deadly the wound is, urine can be used as a streyliser for infections and injuries. Cauterizing is a painful method-\n\n-but its an efficient method and it reduces the chance of external infection.\nIf by chance you dont have animal urine or a fire or even some medicinal herbs, wrap the injury as best you can and replace the bandage often, reach a doctor or a field-\n\n-medic immediately. After sterylising the wound you can choose to apply an herb paste or apply a bandage, Again change the bandage often.\nIf the wound is so severe that first aid will not help like an organ damaged for any reason like a knife, there is-\n\n-nothing you can do without a professional medic, it will lead to a painful death if not treated. Use teas and herbs to ease the pain of your patients. (Alchohol can be used to sterylise and act as a pain killer)\n\nHead injuries:\nIts more likely that a person in a battle will get an injury on his skull, if this happens sit down for a moment and check for any wounds in your head. Its more likely you will nauseous or dizzy. If the skin has split apply a bandage-\n\n-and seek help to ensure no more damage. If a severe injury happens like skull crushing your patient is more likely unconscious or in a coma. Check their pulse, nose, eyes and the swelling of the face to ensure the patient has not undergone through-\n\n-severe brain or skull damage, in this case is unlikely that first aid can save their life.\nDont move them, and if possible seek proper medical attention.\nThe brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage or death. A hole will be drilled-\n\n-into the patient skull in order to the brain to swell, but its still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause dizzyness, nausea, headaches and physical sickness; resting will heal these.\n\nBroken bones:\nYou can check the severity of the wound by its physical appearance. Never understimate the severity of the wound!\nBroken bones can be often seen as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape in your limbs.\n\nUse sticks, cloth or fabric to make a splint to keep your limbs straight up. Using a splint keeps the limb straight up and reduces the movement of the area, you can also use mud to set the break, seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be healed by applying pressure on the affected area, it is very painful so your patient may need some pain killers.\n\nSlings are made out of cloth or fabric and they are perfect for broken arms.\n\nA broken bone can break the skin too so seek proper medical attention quickly if that happens.\n\nIf you find someone floating face down on water quickly put them onto their back. It is important to not apply weight on them, you can force them go-\n\n-underwater. There isnt much you can do on the water so bring them to dry land and check their pulse. First, put your hand in the patient chest above the heart and put the other hand atop of it. Pump thirty times with short breaks before stopping,\n\nthis can cause the water to come out of the lungs and restart the heart. \nFor opening an airway, gently place your hand on the patient forhead and tilt it back. Check for any normal breathing, if the patient is not breathing, open the mouth of the-\n\n-patient and transfer the air from your lungs to the patient's lungs, after this continue pumping, hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out the patient's lungs.\n\nArrow injuries:\nIf your patient has an arrow stuck on any part of their body, prepare to apply lots of force to get the arrow out of the patient body. It is very difficult to pull out an arrow safely, if not done correctly it can leave splinter wich-\n\n-will infect the wound.\nYou can remove the arrow by using propulsion, where you force the arrow through the flesh and out the exit point of the wood.\n\nThe next method is used for limb arrow injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft and leave it for a few days so it creates pus, after that it will be easier to get it out. \n(Pus is a signal of infection)\n\nWheatGrass Ingested, Dry, or tea: Helps with broken bones\n\nHorse tail, Comfrey root, Oat straw, Lobelia, Lavender, Chamomile, Mandagora: Ingested in teas\n*I dont know what it does yet*\n\nBergamot Oil, Comfrey root, Mandagora: When applied topically, cures bruises\n\nComfrey, Mandagora, Aloe Vera:\nWhen applied topically cures burns\n\nTippen's root, Yarrow: Cures Concussions\n\nEchinacea, Pot Marigold, Gumweed, Mullein, Chamomile, Lavender, Mandagora, Orchid, Strawberry, Orange peel, Shade leaf, Blissfoil: In a tea, works like a coagulant\n\nBlueberries, Raspberries, Strawberries, Blackberries, Blissfoil: When used in teas cures minor and major cuts\n\nJohn's Wort, Kanna flower: When used in teas works as a desinfectant\n\nYarrow, Witch's Hazel, Comfrey root, Tippen's root: Applied on scabs or around the wound when clean, it also causes depression\n\nDragur tongue, Yarrow: Applied topically to scabs, scars and internal wounds\n\nBeard weed oil, Yarrow, Tippen's root: Cures muscle fatigue\n\nCrampbark, Skullcap: Ingested in coffee: Helps with pregnancies\n\nGinger root, Red raspberry leaf, echinacea, Lavender, Skullcap, Crampbark: Cures scars with milk teas\n\nBromelian, Aloe vera, Gotu Kola: When applied topically cures stomach aches\n\nGinger root, Peppermint, Chamomile, Blissfoil: When ingested in teas cures sore throat\n\nBlackberry, Mullein, Blissfoil, Honey, Slippery elm bark, Marshmallow root: Ingested with honey-milk teas\n\nYou can add honey or licorice root to sweeten teas, the foul taste of the herbs will not disappear but it will be better\n\n*Side note* If you find someone who was punched hard, quickly apply some Athin in the affected area.\n\nAnd a quick life saving potion! Mix destilled water with Tippen's root, it will help a lot in your first aid kit.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kaedreni", "§bThe Bloody Baron", "22nd of Malin's Welcome,\n                              1519\n\n\n         THE STATE\n             OF THE\n           KAEDRENI\n\n\n       by Titus de Sola\n\nDust scatters on the horizon.  Hooves on valley upon valley thunder to a halt, beasts glaring across to the other, obeying their rider's whims.  Carrion birds dare defy the scorching heat and incandescence of the regal\nWhite Sun.  A scene is painted fo\n\nyou that will set the stage for generations to come. But no matter the turmoil nor the degeneracy of either side I find my conscience bothered greatly by the fact that the blood of Kaedrin and Rhoswen turns against eachother under both banners of the war.\n\nThe Kaedreni have opted to let their luster become a finely honed weapon, a greatsword, to be used at the whims of Savoie and Sarkozic alike, though disrespected moreso on behalf of the latter.\n\nBut only the Kaedreni allowance of such be at fault.\n\nAnd it is a weapon, forged inside the lungs of hell, wrought by tens of thousands of the strongest men of our Kaedreni race, that we do now let the others, who have forgotten their place as our vassals, use freely and improperly against eachother,\n\nlike children who can scarcely pick up a fork.  That weapon is our martial mastery and sheer superiority in waging conflicts, gained by our diligence in carrying out the will of God and His first, the line of Horen, and then of Chivay.  No other Race\n\namongst Men can maintain aggression nor offensive nor conviction in the way that the Kaedreni man can; it is simply impossible.  They cry as they attempt to emulate our finest military traditions that they have inherited our place as the finest amongst\n\nmankind, but like all others their walls crumble, their people degenerate, they turn to banditry and villainy, and they destroy themselves from the inside.\n\nThey frequently seek our service as their officers, but they will never be heirs to Kaedrin.\n\nThe free men of the Rose have turned on eachother, instead of their proper enemies: those who envy all we Kaedreni have done.\nPeter must weep, if the dead weep, at the state of our people, our Kaedreni race.\n\nI would weep in his place, bu\n\nwould also hope.\n\nI would not see the blood of Kaedrin wither into nothing in the same way that the Horens did.  Even the common Kaedreni man, at this stage, is more bloodworthy than your mainstay Orenian lord, and no doubt far more\n\nthan those savages of color out of the Duchy of Adria whom want to eat us alive. I would not see our people fall to that fate. I would endeavor to stop it.\n\nI, De Sola, would fight to the death if need be for our people, so long as it granted my\n\ncountrymen victory.\n\nAnd though when fighting we are naturally greater, fight, we must not always.\n\nWe need consolidation.  Ties of marriage between our Kaedreni Houses.  Living space, territories, slaves.  We cannot forget what it means to bea\n\nour name.  We were made to militarily administrate the world, and everyone else living in it are either ourselves, our allies, or they are rebels.  There is no other alternative.\n\nWhich of the three are you, friendo?\n\nMy love and my strongest wishes to those whom this letter concerns.  May it find you in good health, and in the mind for a change of the course of our history.  Hear out this message, brothers, hear out this message and bring Creeping Death to them all.\n\n\nBy Owyn's guidance, we will prevail.\n\nAve, true to Kaedrin!\n\n                         T.d.S", ""),
        StaticBook("Cadence's Diary", "§bCadence Tundrak", "Diary of Cadence Tundrak~\n\n10th The Deep Cold 1528\nDear Diary,\nHello! My husband's name is Lucien Dreden Tundrak. We live in the Princedom of Fenn.\nIf anyone is reading this, this is very personal and I prefer you didn't.\n\nI want to have children. If I were to have a boy, I would name him...I don't know. And if it's a girl...I don't know! All I know is that I want to have kids!\nO, how thy wind blow,\nhow thy snow collects, stay strong, Princedom.\n\nWhat would thy do, if I never existed? Probably live on life.\n\n14th The First Seed 1529\n\nDear Diary,\nToday I feel lonely. Part of me wants to run back to Lucien and spend the day with him, but he's busy. If that were an option, I would all over it. Right now I'm in this flowery area. HUGE flowers. The size\n\nof wood elven trees! I love it, but I think a young girl used to \"live\" here. She is dead. I grieve her death. I just know she's dead. I'm not sure how I know, but I do. I also know her ghost haunts places. I grieve her. I feel as if she was around eleven\n\nwhen she died. It's so sad. \nAnyway, I'm going to rap this up so you don't have to listen to my boredom and lonelyness.\n\n~Cadence L. Tundrak\n\n10th of Malin's Welcome, 1533\n\nDear Diary,\nI'm back again! Nothing much has happened. I slapped a thousand year old dark elf who was pregnant with Aelthir's son (who died before he was born). It was fun. She was teasing me saying she\n\nslept with Maloch (Lucien). She's never\nsaid anything since. Not that I've met her again. My son, Ilius, is healthy as ever, and my husband is doing fine. As for me...I'm really not sure. To be honest, I'm not really quite so well.\n\nMaloch has died. I'm not sure of what, all I know is that he is dead. So is my soul. This'll probably be my last entry. I know Maloch wanted to see my diary...but...I didn't get a chance to show him. I wish he didn't die. I'll probably die after writin\n\nthis. Either by my own hand, or by another's. I'm going to die. Goodbye.\n\n~Cadence L. Tundrak", ""),
        StaticBook("Prices", "§bJace Kellian", "Wheat- .1 Mina per\n\nBand of wheat- 7\n\nWheat bale- .5\nTower of bales- 32\n\nPotatos- 2 Mina per\nSac= 48\n\nCarrot/Beet 1mina per\nSac= 32\n\nSugar Cane 1 mina per\nWrap for 40\n\nWarts 2 mina per wart\nBag= 48\n\nPumpkin= 3 mina per\n\nMellon .5 a slice\nBag for 20\n\nCoco is 1 mina per\nBag = 40\n\nPlants 1-3 mina\nPots 2 mina\n\nCompost 5 mina a Bag\n\nSeeds- 3 mina per bag\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nwer", ""),
        StaticBook("65", "§bHamilton Huntley", "65 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\n\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\n\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\n\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\n\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\n\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowes\n\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\n\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\n\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\n\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\n\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\n\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity o\n\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\n\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\n\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\n\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\n\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\n\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\n\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\n\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\n\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvati\n\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\n\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\n\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\n\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\n\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for\n\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\n\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\n\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\n\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\n\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\n\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\n\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\n\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\n\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the gra\n\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\n\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\n\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\n\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\n\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\n\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\n\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\n\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repu\n\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sorrow", "§bThe Inquisitor", "The breastplate of another champion. His exact 'placing' in the Glade's timeline is unknown, but it's obvious that he cared about the place deeply. While not being a religious man by any-means, he had his morals.\n\nHe entered The Glade with a group of soldiers, although he was the only one to stay. He found peace within the Glade, and quietly becme it's guardian under the watchful eye of Aureus.\n\nThe sorrow he feels comes from having to kill the very fellow soldiers he entered the Glade with, in order to protect it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XI", "§bMarch Ash", "The void has touched the world, drenched it in its poison. I will suck it from the earth as a man sucks snake-venom from the bite. Despite all his power, Iblees and his legions are nothing compared to nature, and all that it consists of.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn X", "§bMarch Ash", "It is amazing that not a kilometer from here the world has been consumed by the void, yet in this place nature has recovered. Despite all of Iblees' machinations, the resilience of nature is more powerful.\n\nSo long as a single glade survives, the world might recover. I hope the Aspects are patient enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=*=-§0\n§0The Holy Book of the Seven§0\n§0              -=*=-§0\n§0\n§0\"Oh Seven, bless us and guide us. Teach us\n\nChapter One:§0\n§0     The Seven Gods§0\n§0•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•–•§0\n§0Grant, O Great Gods§0\n§0Thy Protection;§0\n§0And in protection, strength;§0\n§0And in strength, understanding;§0\n§0And in understanding, knowledge;\n\nAnd in knowledge, the knowledge of justice;§0\n§0And in the knowledge of justice, the love of it;§0\n§0And in that love, the love of all existences;§0\n§0And in the love of all existences, the love of the Gods, our protectors, and all goodness.\n\nTo Aeriel: Oh Goddess Mother, you are the mystery of the night. Your radiant shine is the day. Infinate realms cascade within you. Abundance is your essence of being. Blessings flow from you, limitlessly. Your universe is harmony and tension is balance.\n\nTo Malchediael:§0\n§0Make me strong in spirit, courageous in action, and gentle at heart. Let me act in wisdom, conquer my fear and doubt, and discover my own hidden gifts. Meet others with compassion, be a source of healing, and face each day with hope & j", ""),
        StaticBook("Menu", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Jaya Jayamen's House of Entertainment Menu\n§\n\n           Drinks\n\nCarrot Juice\nA fresh glass of Carrot Juice.\n4 Minas\n\nPumpkin Juice\nA fresh glass of pumpkin juice.\n4 Minas\n\nPine tea\nA relaxing tea made with Pine leaves.\n4 Minas\n\nBirch tea\nA good drink to wake up a bit.\n4 Minas\n\nRose Tea\nA sweet smelling tea.\n3 Minas\n\nPale ale\nA good hearty mug of Ale.\n5 Minas\n\nWine\nA good bottle of Wine\n10 Minas\n\nRum \nA big bottle of Rum.\n7 minas\n\nClean water\nA good glass of boiled then cooled water.\nFree\n\n          Meals\n\nBread\nA fresh loaf of bread, soft on the inside and crunchy on the outside.\n2 Minas\n\nSandwich\nRoasted beef in between two pieces of bread.\n7 Minas\n\nPumpkin Pie\nA hot, fresh pumpkin pie.\n8 Minas\n\nMelon Pie\nA fresh, sweet, melon pie.\n6 Minas\n\nPotato Chowder\nHot, ready Potato chowder\n4 Minas\n\nMashed potatoes with Cheese\nHot, well cooked mashed potatoes loaded with cheese.\n5 Minas\n\nChicken Stew\nStew with Fresh vegetables and Roast chicken.\n11 Minas\n\nPork Stew\nStew with Fresh vegetables and Roast Pork.\n8 Minas\n\nMutton Stew\nStew with Fresh vegetables and Roast Mutton.\n9 Minas\n\nBeef Stew\nStew with Fresh vegetables and Roast beef.\n7 Minas\n\nChicken noodle soup\nHot and filling Chicken noodle soup.\n6 Minas\n\nLasagna\nA hot square of lasagna.\n10 Minas\n\nFried Chicken\nCrispy fried chicken breast.\n5 Minas\n\nPrime Rib\nA well cooked and seasoned piece of beef.\n3 minas\n\nPork Cuts\nA plate of large, cooked, pork cuts.\n4 Minas\n\nLamb Chops\nGood Cuts of cooked lamb\n4 Minas\n\nPizza Pie\nA fresh Pizza with sausage.\n9 Minas\n\n        Desserts\n\nCaramel bread\nA cooked soft bread with caramel cooked in it.\n5 Minas\n\nCake\nA fresh baked cake with icing.\n25 Minas\n\nCheesecake\nA Thick, rich, cheesecake.\n20 Minas\n\nChocolate Pie\nA rich, chocolaty Pie.\n7 Minas\n\nCream Pie\nA creamy, rich pie.\n6 Minas\n\nPlain cookies\nA plain doughey cookie.\n4 Minas\n\nButter biscuits\nA good smelling butter buiscut.\n6 Minas\n\nTriple Chocolate Cookies\nA chocolate filled Cookie.\n7 minas\n\nCaremel cookies\nA Sweet caramel cookie.\n3 Minas\n\nThank you for dining here and please return your menu!\n\n~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Isabella Contrac", "§bHareven Lorenthus", "Drafted Contract For§0\n§0\n§0Isabella Wood§0\n§0\n§0For§0\n§0\n§0Honorary Guild Member Work§0\n§0\n§0Written By§0\n§0\n§0Guild Head Hareven Lorenthus\n\nProposed Wage: Anywhere between 200 to 250 Minas a week, plus in the event of stalls opening up under the Guild Banner and selling Isabella Woods wares, she shall receive 50% of the total profits seperate from her wage.\n\nThis page is to clarify that all persons related to the Guild and its Allies will not harm her during her work and will also do their upmost to defend her from harm should the risks of working with The Guild fall onto her.\n\nFinally, if said worker wishes to leave her post, she shall be properly granted the pay she was to get for the Elven Year(IRL Week) in which she left. §0\n§0Isabelle Wood\n\nSigned§0\n§0\n§0Hareven Lorenthus§0\n§0", ""),
