        StaticBook("Base Drinks", "§bLuna Nevermore", "Juices (Apple, Carrot, Orange, Lemon, Melon slice, Pumpkin)\n\nTeas (Birch, Pine, Rose bush (Rose Tea), Cactus green, Grass (Herb Tea), Oxeye Daisy (Chamomile Tea), Dandelion, Poppy, Orchid, Brown Mushroom)§0\n\nVodka (poisoness potato)\n\nCoffee (cocoa beans)\n\nMushroom Poison (Red Mushroom)§0\n\nPale Ale (wheat)\n\nEggnog (egg)\n\nMulled Wine (Dark Resin)\n\nBlood (Rotten flesh)\n\nSweet Ale (Melon juice + Wheat)\n\nRum (sugarcane)\n\nMead (Honey)\n\nDistilled Water (Coal, GlowStone)\n\nAqua Vitae (Neather Warts)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Advanced potions. Constantly update! These notes where taken from multiple sources as well as your own testing. Dont forget.\n\nAlchchemist Fire: §0\n§0Mandragora§0\n§0Serpents Stalk§0\n§0Dwarf Pumpkin§0\n§0Drakes Tail§0\n§0Flame tounge Root§0\n§0Crimsion Vase§0\n§0Crouching Feather§0\n§0\n§0Aqua§0\n§0\n§0Effective Potion, No further testing required.\n\nStone Skin:§0\n§0Mandragora§0\n§0Serpents Stalk§0\n§0Dwarf Pumpkin§0\n§0Drakes Tail§0\n§0Flame tounge§0\n§0Crouching Feather§0\n§0Alabaster leaf§0\n§0Clutchers Straw§0\n§0Metzils Tangle§0\n§0???§0\n§0\n§0Ingredients to complete unknown.\n\nGreater Healing§0\n§0Athin§0\n§0Frost Vine§0\n§0Crouching Feather§0\n§0???§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Assumed recipe for it. Might end up being some frost potions. Testing required.\n\nVirulent Slime§0\n§0Mandragora§0\n§0Serpents Stalk§0\n§0Dwarf Pumpkin§0\n§0Crimsion Vase§0\n§0\n§0Unknown Base§0\n§0Assumed Aqua. Preform test in spare time.\n\nPosoned Inferno:§0\n§0Mandragora§0\n§0Serpents Stalk§0\n§0Dwarf Pumpkin§0\n§0Flame Tounge§0\n§0Crimson Vase§0\n§0\n§0Aqua§0\n§0\n§0Effective potions. Can be brewed further, testing required, test in spare time and with spare resources.\n\nFrost Oil:§0\n§0Serpents Stalk§0\n§0Athiun§0\n§0Frost Vine§0\n§0Crouching Feather§0\n§0Elf's hair Vine§0\n§0Tippen§0\n§0\n§0Unknown Base, assumed Aqua. Athuin required, test when possible.§0\n§0\n§0Fire Oil also possible? Test at later date.\n\nMinor Healing:§0\n§0Tippen§0\n§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Can be pushed further. Further testing required preform on spare time and resources.\n\nSmoke Whispers:§0\n§0Blood Lotus§0\n§0Drakes Tail§0\n§0larihei's Fingers§0\n§0Crouching Feathers§0\n§0\n§0Aqua§0\n§0\n§0Effective Smoke bomb. No further testing needed.\n\nParalising Venom:§0\n§0Clutches§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Effective Potion. No further testing required.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Daitan Padaryns Journal§0\n§0Malins welcome 1600§0\n§0\n§0My first action as Tilruir'tir was to ally us with Linandria.§0\n§0It went well, as long as we are in Peace with Haelun'or we will be allowed to stay in Linandria.§0\n§0A wonderful girl, Melethre, offere\n\nus a place to stay, an expansion in her house, she renovated it,put in some beds and we now officially have a Linandria expansion to the Vigil, we are making progress.§0\n§0\n§0A Priestess died in fornt of my eyes, Melethre seemed absolutely distroguht at th\n\nshe said something about a mother figure, then went to to the shrine.§0\n§0The priestess returned to great suprise of everyone, and happiness for most.§0\n§0\n§0Elrith somehow managed to get me drunk, i barely remember anything\n\nfrom that night, i think i wasnt too impacted by the alcohol, head hurts too much to remember\n\nspent most of the night trying to look after Mel so she didnt get in trouble, didnt go well, she mostly ran away and stole alcohol, then i attempted to lock elrith in whilst i found Gen, went much better. i then slept awaythe most of the next day, now my\n\nhead is exploding, why dont i have herbs for this sort of situatuion?\n\nThe First Seed 1600§0\n§0Only fun stuff this month, first my plan with the flowers failed, trying to distract myself from that failure , then i managed to lose one of our sets of armor, good job Daitan, you truly outdid yourself.\n\nThe grand Harvest 1600§0\n§0\n§0At least i didnt get kicked out and she doesnt hate me, i will just accept the situation and back down i guess.§0\n§0Then i failed with a recruit, a recruiting trip with Mele helped out a bit, turns out im still known in\n\nHaelun'or, they still hate me, remember me by name even without my uniform on, and apparently Mels father lives there, just more reasons for me to avoid the place i the future\n\n*The next two pages are written with a very shaky hand, slmost unreadable*§0\n§0\n§0Banished.§0\n§0Banished to be killed on sight.§0\n§0Lost it.§0\n§0Almost Killed Gen.§0\n§0Left Vigil.§0\n§0No longer Leader.§0\n§0Lost it.\n\nI will move to live with Gen.§0\n§0safer that way.§0\n§0Need treatment.§0\n§0Need family.§0\n§0Lost friends.§0\n§0Melethre.§0\n§0Varen.§0\n§0Lost.§0\n\nThe Deep Cold 1600§0\n§0I once again have no home, a wanderer once again, i have left the Vigil, the Vigil who has been my family for years, the Vigil who has saved my life so many times, but we have a plan.§0\n§0\n§0I have a plan.\n\nThe deep cold 1601§0\n§0I have started to try and join the Vigil again, my brothers and sisters, i have found them a recruit, Amara.§0\n§0She is a curious one, i like her, she has a noble goal and a potential it seems.§0\n§0I do not know how she will fare i\n\nmilitary, but i can only hope she at least stays in the Vigil, we need someone like her, hell, I need someone like that\n\nThe amber cold 1602§0\n§0I again serve the Vigil, or Llythiran as we know are called.§0\n§0\"Those who strike\", i like that name.§0\n§0\n§0So, i have been put in command of an elite group of Rangers, supposed to start recruiting soon, this is exiting.\n\nSuns smile, 1607§0\n§0War.§0\n§0War with the dwarves.§0\n§0War with the undead.§0\n§0Steward.§0\n§0Steward of Norland.§0\n§0At the same time my loyalty lies with the Llythiran.§0\n§0i think.\n\nSun smile 1617§0\n§0I have decided to go back to write in my journal again. might help me sort everything out and keep  reality for itself.§0\n§0Im soon to be married.§0\n§0Rini, a almost blind girl i met a few years ago, wonderful woman, i am undescribably happy i met\n\nher.§0\n§0In other news, i have finally left the Vigil, the faction that held me as a willing slave for years.§0\n§0Im in the Sirame, i have not made any advancements in the ranks but i have managed to prove my loyalty to the state.§0\n§0Im studying to become a druid.\n\nEverything seems to be going right for once.\n\nMalins welcome 1617§0\n§0Bad news first :§0\n§0Im forbidden from seeing Liah, so thats fun.§0\n§0In other news Rini is acting strange, i suspect shes either sick, or maybe pregnant considering a thing that happened.§0\n\nThe first seed 1618§0\n§0The new high prince, Aenor, officialy had his coronation today.§0\n§0A lot of standing around, but i managed to speak to him whilst relatively alone and get what i wanted to get said, said.§0\n§0\n§0i once again swore my loyalty to him, but this\n\ntime directly to him instead of a brazier.§0\n\nThe Amber Cold 1618§0\n§0So, Rini is going to give birth within a few months.§0\n§0I will have a child to take care of, We will have a child to take care of.§0\n§0We are planning to have our marriage sometime, im not sure when we have not yet spoken to Awaiti about it.\n\nI have oficially dropped my position as a steward of Norland and they have threatened to start a war with us since we have a deserter of the ashguard in our city, luckily the high prince decided to hand her over so that should not be a problem.\n\nMalins welcome 1621.§0\n§0\n§0So, whats new? Nuvae got born, a child Elleonora offered to carry for me and rini after the miscarriage with Lieren.§0\n§0My bronze meditations are going better than expected, the fire inside is still there, but its less of a wildfire and\n\nmore like a controlled flame, within a furnace.§0\n§0still a strong flame but one i can control.§0\n§0The business wtih Varen should finally be over after all these years, my past should finally bbe behind me. I couldnt be happier about the current situation, i\n\nhave a family, i have found a home, i have finally found peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerics", "§bSer Duncan Lefay", "I believe that a Cleric's purpose is to be a light in the darkness. I believe that they are to protect the innocent and shine Taharie's light to all. §0\n§0\n§0They need to be strong in their faith, and able to be empathetic. They also need to know when\n\nit's time to fight and when it's time to talk.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task #5", "§bSer Duncan Lefay", "1. The Sutican Government-- I donated several sets of armor and weapons to the army. (If you want to pick them up, it's by the palace gate)§0\n§0\n§02. Atturi Silversteed§0\n§0(Askuzai) My friend asked me if I could watch his horse for a few minutes while\n\nhe shopped in Jornheim.§0\n§0\n§03. Daxx Vorhees (DaxxGamer_) --§0\n§0This friend of mine asked me if I had any alchemy ingredients. I gave him all I had (Which was actually quite a bit).§0\n\n4. Unknown woman (Torkoal_Tom)--§0\n§0This lady in Adelburg was wounded. I offered to patch her up, but she declined. So, I left her with the proper medical equipment and left.§0\n§0\n§05. Augustus Windsor (Fnik) This friend of mine asked for some\n\ncounicl on a personal matter. I believe I eased his mind significantly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Welcoming Letter", "§bAnne Catherijne Hagelijn", "We would like to welcome you to our community of batavians.\nIf we can help you with anything please don't hesitate to ask.\n*Willem Hagelijn\n*Anne C. Hagelijn\n*Adriaan de Witt\n-------------------Here are some things that you can find in our district:\n\n*Batavian Home Guard: If interested contact W. Hagelijn or A. de Witt.\n*Oranjestraat's public garden.\n*Oranjestraat's Library (coming soon)\n*Batavian Shop at Sutica's Main Square.\n\n*More projects coming soon.\n\n-------------------More information will be posted in our Community Noticeboard\n-------------------Keep in touch for monthly updates.\n-------------------To show our hospitality the Welcoming Committe would like to gift you a rose bouquet along with some\n\nmushroom soup and a honey jar.\n>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<\n\n-Anne Catherijne Hagelijn", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Kaelerelle's Contact Book.§0\n§0__________________§0\n§0*Willem Hagelijn§0\n§0*Annie Hagelijn§0\n§0*Grytros (Nurbo_)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This diary belongs to§0\n§0Anne Catherijne H.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sutica Codex", "§bJace Kellian", "Codex Of Sutica§0\n§0\n§0 I. Laws of the Realm§0\n§0\n§0II. Laws of the Capital§0\n§0\n§0III. Pertaining Vassals§0\n§0\n§0IV. Rights of Citizens§0\n§0\n§0V. Punishments\n\n I. Laws of the Realm§0\n§0\n§0Laws to be followed in all Sutican territory §0\n§0\n§0 I. Pertaining Acts of Theft§0\n§0 1) Burglary; defined as the stealing of goods from one’s property.§0\n§0\n§0a) Minor Burglary (Class D)\n\n The theft of lesser than 300 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.§0\n§0\n§0b) Burglary (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0The theft of lesser than 750 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.§0\n§0\n§0c) Grand Burglary (Class B)\n\n The Theft of greater than 750 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.§0\n§0\n§0 §0\n§0\n§02) Robbery; defined as the stealing of goods from one’s person.§0\n§0\n§0a) Minor Robbery (Class D)\n\n The theft of lesser than 300 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.§0\n§0\n§0b) Robbery (Class C) Brandishing a weapon or threatening violence to achieve the theft of lesser than 300 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.\n\n c) Grand Robbery (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0Brandishing a weapon or threatening violence to achieve the theft of greater than 300 minas, in equivalent goods or coin.\n\n 3) Other§0\n§0\n§0a) Swindling (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Using deception or feminine whims in order to deprive one of goods, minas, and/or property.\n\n b) Breaking Deals (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Breaking an agreed upon contract between one and another, in order to boost profits or deprive the other of their labors.§0\n\n c) Animal Theft (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0The theft or slaughter of any animal(s) belonging to another.\n\nII. Pertaining Acts of Violence§0\n§0 1) Assault; defined as unwarranted physical attack upon another.§0\n§0\n§0a) Third-degree (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0An unplanned attack upon another causing minor injury, such as drunken brawls or bouts of passion.\n\n b) Second-degree (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0A planned attack upon another causing minor injury.§0\n§0\n§0c) First-degree (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0A planned attack upon another causing grievous or debilitating injury.\n\n 2) Murder ; defined as the unlawful killing of one.§0\n§0\n§0a) Attempted Murder (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0The unplanned attempt of taking another’s life and failing in doing so.\n\n b) Third-degree (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0The unplanned killing of another, citizen or otherwise. §0\n§0 c) First-degree (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0The planned killing of another, citizen or otherwise.\n\nIII. Pertaining Acts of Malicious Intent§0\n§0 1) Fraud; defined as deception for unlawful gain.§0\n§0\n§0a) Impersonation (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Impersonating another, guard, noble, or otherwise.\n\n b) General Fraud (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Deceiving another for unlawful gain. §0\n§0\n§02) Espionage; defined as the unwarranted spying upon another.§0\n\n a) Minor Espionage (Class D)§0\n§0\n§0Spying upon a citizen to achieve unlawful gain or knowledge. §0\n§0 b) State Espionage (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Spying upon an official to achieve unlawful gain or knowledge.\n\n c) Trade Espionage (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0The unlawful gain of Sutican trade secrets.§0\n§0\n§0 3) Vandalism; the unlawful destruction of property.§0\n§0\n§0a) Minor Vandalism (Class D)\n\n Destruction of property totalling no more than 250 minas in damages.§0\n§0\n§0b) Major Vandalism (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Destruction of property totalling more than 250 minas in damages.\n\n 4) Kidnapping; the unlawful seizure or holding of another in one’s custody.§0\n§0\n§0a) Petty Kidnapping (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Holding one against their will unlawfully as in cases of child custody or etc.\n\n b) Kidnapping (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0Holding one against their will unlawfully in order to extract profit or gain. §0\n§0 c) Grand Napping (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0Holding an official or noble against their will unlawfully for any purpose.\n\n 5) Aiding an Outlaw; defined as granting aid or shelter to a fugitive of any nation.§0\n§0\n§0a) Petty Aid (Class C)§0\n§0\n§0Providing a fugitive sustenance or any means to escape capture.\n\n b) Aiding (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0Providing a fugitive shelter or knowingly aiding them in escaping capture. §0\n§0\n§0 IV. Pertaining Acts of Illegality§0\n\n 1) Whaling; defined as the hunting of whales or other life in the Sutican waters§0\n§0\n§0a) Petty Whaling (Class C) §0\n§0Unlawfully hunting & slaughtering any animal of the oceans in amounts no more than 250 minas.\n\n b) Grand Whaling (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0Unlawfully hunting & slaughtering any whale or animal totalling more than 250 minas. §0\n§0\n§02) Iblees Worship; defined as the unlawful worship of Iblees or Daemons\n\n a) Worship (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0Worshipping Iblees or any Daemon, providing aid to any worshipper. §0\n§03) Undermining Authority & Defenses; defined as knowingly acting against the Sutican interest\n\n a) Circumventing defenses (Class B)§0\n§0\n§0Digging tunnels or otherwise circumventing Sutican defenses to provide unlawful entry to the city\n\n b) Undermining Authority (Class A)§0\n§0\n§0Undermining the authority of the Sutican government through malicious acts or words.\n\n II. Laws of the Capital§0\n§0\n§0Laws pertaining to the City§0\n§0I. Guards§0\n§0 a) Guards reserve the right to remove from the city any mal-contents.§0\n§0\n§0b) Guards reserve the right to levy fines for crimes committed in the city.\n\n c) Guards reserve the right to arrest any criminal.§0\n§0\n§0d) Guards reserve the right to don armor and arms within the city.§0\n§0\n§0e) Guards reserve the right to search any home suspected of affiliation with a criminal.\n\nf) Guards reserve the right to seize any goods suspected of affiliation with a criminal.§0\n§0\n§0II. Taxes§0\n§0a) Taxes will be levied at discretion of the Trade Princess.§0\n§0b) Taxes must be paid  as specified, or seizure of property & goods may occur.\n\n c) Materials may be used in place of minas at discretion of the Trade Princess.§0\n§0\n§0d) Tax fraud shall be punished at a Class B level. §0\n§0\n§0III. Pertaining Vassals§0\n\n a) Vassals must follow all laws of Section I of the Codex of Sutica within their territories.§0\n§0\n§0b) Vassals are entrusted by the Trade Princess to govern their people.§0\n§0\n§0c) Vassals thusly may use their own laws in governance.\n\n d) Vassals are expected to levy taxes or manpower in times of  dire need, at discretion of the Trade Princess.§0\n§0\n§0e) Vassals reserve the right for their designated leader to sit upon the Advisory Council of Sutica.\n\nf) Vassals reserve the right to pick their own leader in the manner they see fit.§0\n§0\n§0IV. Rights of Citizens§0\n§0a) A citizen of Sutica is defined as any landholder within the territories of Sutica.§0\n§0b) Citizens reserve the right to fair trial.\n\n c) Citizens reserve the right to privacy.§0\n§0\n§0d) Citizens reserve the right to free trade & enterprise.§0\n§0\n§0e) Law-abiding citizens reserve the right to live unmolested by law enforcement. §0\n\nf) Citizens reserve the right to voice their complaints to the Trade Princess.§0\n§0\n§0V. Punishments§0\n§0Punishments for crimes are levied on the following scale:\n\n Class D (Petty Crime): 100 minas fine, or 20 elven minutes jail time.§0\n§0\n§0Class C (Minor Crime): 250 minas fine, or 35 elven minutes jail time.§0\n§0\n§0Class B (General Crime): 500 minas fine, or 1 elven hour jail time.\n\nClass A (Major Crime): 2,000 minas fine, or execution via sea creatures.§0\n\n To be convicted of a Class A crime, the criminal must face trial and be found guilty.§0\n§0\n§0Jail time consists of sitting in a small cell with little or no interaction to think on your sins.\n\n Example of Use:§0\n§0\n§0Accused has been charged under the Sutican Codex, section I, subsection II.1.c; attempted murder", ""),
        StaticBook("Welcoming Letter", "§bKaelerelle Taetharen Avalon", "We would like to welcome you to our community of Batavians. \nIf we can help you with anything please do not hesitate to ask.\n*Willem Hagelijn\n*Anne C. Hagelijn\n*Adriaan de Witt\n------------------\nHere are some things you can find in our\n\ndistrict that you may want to check out:\n\n*Batavian Home Guard: If interested contact A. de Witt or W. Hagelijn.\n*Oranjestraat's public garden\n*Oranjestraat's Library (Coming soon)\n*Batavian Shop located in Sutica's main square.\n\n*Leyunia's Arcane and sub-arcane magic lessons.\n------------------\nMore information will be shared in the Community Noticeboard.\nKeep in touch for Monthly updates.\n\nTo express our hospitality we would like to gift you this\n\nrose bouquet along with a jar of honey.\n\n      *Anne C. Hagelijn", ""),
        StaticBook("The All-Theory", "§bArchibald", "The Theory of Everything, by Archibald Vallero\n-------------------\n\n    In this tome, I wish to explain to all my beliefs on why things exist with direct connection to the realm known as the Void. At times, you might be confused. This is entirely\n\nunderstandable given just how abstract this idea of mine might be.\nIf any of this offends you, I will let you know right now that I did not intend to offend or undermine anyone's religious beliefs. If that is what you believe I intended to do by the\n\ntime you've finished reading this book, then sorry. \n\nNow, let's begin.\n\n       The Void\n-------------------\n\n    Many readers probably have no idea what the Void is, which is why I've decided to begin this with an explanation so that non-mages can be at the same level of understanding with mages as to what the Void i\n\n     The Void, in short is a dimension where everything exists simultaneously along with nothing. It is all that is and all that will ever be, but at the same time there is nothing there. One point I should emphasize while explaining this is that the Void\n\nIS another dimension. Implant this into your mind: the Void is a completely separate dimension to ours. Now, the use of the Void to mages is simply to draw the ability to create from it. Another keyword I'd like for you to remember is 'creation.' It will\n\nbe mentioned continually throughout this tome. As said before, voidal mages are able to create an array of elements and entities by exhausting their mana, which is essentially every living being's life force. Mana flows through our veins, and with it we\n\nare able to connect to the Void and bring about lightning, flesh, fire, water, air, earth, 'raw' energy (arcane energy), and the ability to alter the world or the people around us through different types of illusion or alteration. We use the Void to bring\n\nabout the CREATION of something or another that would otherwise be inaccessible to non-mages. Now, all of us have a mana anchor in the void, which is what it sounds like. Our mana, while in our bodies, is also connected to the Void, and this is what\n\nallows all non-mages to become mages. Now, with this explanation, I wish to bring up my theory.\n\n    The All-Theory \n-------------------\n\n    So, now you understand what the Void basically is. Good. Now, what if I told you that, since the Void is a dimension where anything is possible and, while it is in a constant state of balance and\n\nunbalance, it was still able to create /everything/. What if the dimension is the epicenter of ALL creations? What if it was even the creator of /our/ Creator? Think about it like this . . .  Mana can be found in all living, organic beings. This means\n\neven grass, trees, all abundances of animals, and us. This mana is what allows for there to be a mana anchor, weak or strong, to the Void for all beings. While the grass you stand on might have an extremely weak mana anchor, there is mana there\n\nnonetheless. Necromancers can drain the life from anything with mana in order to power themselves, meaning that, indeed, all things have mana. Even the stone of castles or the earth beneath us might have mana, though it might be in such an insignificant\n\namount that nothing can really be done with it. If we move up the chain and start with trees, there's more than likely more mana in them than both grass and stone, since Graven's are capable of manipulating their own mana to creator a connection or bond\n\nwith the tree that allows it to stay there. The tree is also involved in this process, though, by allowing for their to be a connection in the first place. Perhaps they have enough mana to have such a thing be done. Next is us Descendant races.\n\nWe are able to cast spells that closely resemble elements we can observe in modern day life, but with more manipulation involved. I won't go into specifics, but it requires the touch of our minds to create ice sculptures, fiery animals, and other such\n\nabnormal things. \n\n    Now, I did say that mana flows through our veins, but what if, just like stone, our skin, bones, and other bodily particles also contained mana? We are beings of mana, from the bottom up. All other things are made of mana,\n\neven if it is difficult for mages to tell. This leads me to believe that we were all created by the Void, but with middle-men inbetween the process of our creation. \n\n    Let's delve further into the nature of the Void for just a moment. We can use i\n\nto create a myriad of things. Here comes the confusing part of this theory, but I will try to summarize it as such first before explaining.\n\nInanimate materials have low mana, not able to create anything. We are animate along with animals, and some\n\nanimals are capable of being magical while us Descendant races can connect with the Void to create. Aengudaemons are powerful, capable of creating amazing and wondrous things, an example being the Arch-aengul Aeriel creating the Ascended, or Metzli\n\ncreating the entire race known as the Kharajyr. This type of creation is far beyond the Descendant races' abilities. Then there is the Creator, which many believe has created the aengudaemons and all of us. This could be true. But now, answer this for\n\nme: what created the Creator? The answer to this, I have deduced, is the only dimension capable of bringing about everything material and animate, or the Void itself. It is to my belief that the Creator is simply a powerful entity that has a immensely\n\npowerful connection to the void, allowing for this being to acquire a massive amount of mana and the ability to create the aengudaemons and us all. Essentially, the Void brought about the powerful being known to us as the Creator, which had a greater,\n\nintense mana anchor and mana pool, that this creator of ours was able to use everything available to it in the Void (which is everything conceivable) to create this world, and the aengudaemons. \n\n    There's also a pecking order, I've noticed. The\n\n Void is the creator of all, it is a dimension/entity/being capable of granting power and creating any and everything, and as it had created our Creator, since the Creator has such a close connection to this dimension, this being's powers closely\n\nresembled the Void's. Then there are the Aengudaemons, some ranking higher than others. They have an immense amount of power, but have physical restrictions. An example would be the fact that they can only shape our realm through us lower beings, as\n\nthe paladins resemble Xan's hand, or the clerics resemble Tahariae's hand, or the cultists of Ikuras resemble Ikuras's hand. Then there is us. We do have a connection to the Void, but at only at a great cost. The more we master arts that allow us to\n\ncreate wards, elements, or bring things back to life or even drain mana from other living beings, the more our muscle mass and sanity disappears. We are thinning out. We are losing ourselves as we continue. This leads me to my next theory.\n\n    The All-Pure\n-------------------\n\n    As said before, the more one attempts to bring something into this realm, the more mass, or particles of themselves, they lose. I've lost around twenty pounds while still maintaining a healthy diet as I\n\nattempted to master conjuration, but if I were to try and learn even more evocations or magicks of another kind, I would be even far more thin. Weak. Decrepit. We lose our corporeal selves as we delve into the power that allows us to create. This leads me\n\nto the other observation that the more closely connected one entity is to the almighty Void, the more of 'themselves' they lose, or, rather, the more they lose their body, the greater their ability to manipulate elements and, naturally, everthing else.\n\nWhy this occurs I'm not /entirely/ sure, but an idea that's come to my mind is that it's the cost, as everything has a cost. The cost for becoming more god-like in being is that you lose what we know as ourselves. We lose our body and our 'mind.' This can\n\npotentially explain why Aengudaemons are able to have such great power in their own realm, creating what they want at their own whim, but as soon as they enter an earthly vessel to interact with us, they only become the equivalent of a powerful mage,\n\nrather than some being with the capabilities to destroy and create. The cost for having a body like ours is that they lose some of the powers that makes them 'them.' At the same time, once they are killed in this world, they are still able to ascend back\n\nto their own and retain their original powers. All very interesting, indeed.\n\n    The real aspect of the All-Pure theory involves 'purity.' In my belief, the closer one is to obtaining the ultimate power that the Void grants, creation, the more\n\n'pure' they are. In this sense, non-mages are not as pure as voidal mages. Inanimate objects aren't entirely as pure either, and are on the bottom of the order. This does not mean that one being deserves to live and one to die. It is simply my outlook on\n\nthings. Now, with this new theory, it is fact that mages who are granted their power from an aengudaemonic force, such as paladins, clerics, and cultists, are not as pure as voidal mages. The purest one can be is when they are able to siphon\n\ntheir spells of creation from the Void, the dimension where, believe, all life truly originates! The reason why paladins and clerics are not as pure as voidal mages is due to the fact that they are drawing their power from a being lower than the Void,\n\nand rather from an aengudaemon which had been created by the Void. They are drawing their power from a weaker source. The Void is the most powerful, truly. This could also explain why they, the aengudaemonic siphoners, are able to retain some muscle\n\nmass and weight while us voidal mages are weakened. We're closer to reaching the nature of the 'nothing-yet-everything' Void, while they are granted their power from a lower and less powerful being which takes its power from the Void. If they were to cut\n\nout the middle-man in their magicks, they would end up being like the voidal sorcerers: able to create more elements and manipulate this world further, yet at the cost of them losing more and more of their bodily matter. \n\n    With this in considerat\n\nI do believe that there is a Creator. I believe, though, that our Creator is, frankly, a being who has such a powerful connection with the Void that it was capable of bringing our kind about along with the aengudaemons. But the true Creator is the voidal\n\ndimension. \n\n    With this, I conclude my novel. I hope you, brave scholar, found this piece of literature interesting and profound in its content. Thank you.\n\n         -Archibald V.", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Healing", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "A guide to Creator Clerical healing\n\nby Lady Sarah Hightower.\n\n\nDedicated to my dutiful students.\n\nAssessment.\n\nThe first step in treating a patient is to assess his or her injuries. Ask yourself the following questions before you attempt to treat the injury.\n\n1 Where is the wound located?\n\n2 What is the severity of the wound.\n\n3 Am I able to treat this wound.\n\nStart by locating the wound, sometimes you'll have to cut away clothing to properly access it.\n\nThen classify the\n\nwound using the following scale\n\nI Light cuts and bruises, no severe bleeding.\n\nII Cuts with bleeding, at risk of infection, no internal damage. Burns that leave skin intact.\n\nIII Broken bones in the limbs. Major burns and arrow wounds in the limbs or ones that did not damage major organs.\n\nIV Broken ribs, Internal injuries, broken skulls arrow and crossbow bolt wounds that pierced major organs.\n\nV Loss of limb, defects in the lungs or heart.\n\n\nAttempt the find the classification that fits the scale best and then decide if Your clerical abilities are prudent to use, or perhaps the patient can be better treated with\n\nmundane healing. In the early stages of your clerical career you will often have to combine both Clerical and mundane healing.\n\nConnecting\n\nThe second step one must take to heal a patient through clerical magic is to connect to the Creator, this must be done through prayer.\n\nYou begin by clearing your mind of all woes\n\ntry and think of a place or memory that fills you with joy, then you will have to say or think of a prayer, asking the creator to bestow his Holy gifts upon you. for the newer clerics this is an exhausting process, but the more talented can summon\n\nHoly light in a matter of seconds.\n\nYou must be a devout follower of the creator to use his holy light, one who kills or injures without good cause will not be able to do so.\n\nGuiding the light\n\nThe next step is to bring the holy light onto the injury, staves may be used although using your hands is most likely the more practical solution. \n\nIf you concentrate enough you will find\n\nthat the light will obey your commands and goes where you want it, in theory you could heal a patient without using your hands, but this will be severely exhausting and even Class I wounds will prove a challenge to fix for the advanced cleric.\n\nHealing\n\nWhen you've guided the light to the injury, you may start the healing, this is not done automatically, you must know how the injury works before you are able to heal it. \nFor instance if you cannot set a bone\n\nproperly, you cannot use the holy light to do it, the results will most likely be unpleasant, so educate yourself in mundane healing before attempting to treat the more difficult wounds. \n\nTo heal the wound you simply imagine how the\n\nwound mends, think of the procedure and guide the light so that it does thus, you will find that the light will mend the injury you are faced with, granted it is within your abilities to heal it.\n\nProgressing your abilities.\n\n§ § Clerical magic differs from other schools of magic in one aspect. A cleric can draw on more power than he or she can handle this is fairly common and in light doses harmless\nhowever there are\nside effects\n\nI Fatigue\nII Light shaking.\nIII Headache.\nIV Light coughing.\nV Danger of falling in an unconscious state.\nVI Coughing up of blood.\nVII Long term weakness, damage to the lungs.\nVIII Death.\n\nYou will often have to push yourself to stage V or even VI\nto advance your abilities. this will mean you advance faster, but comes at risk of long term weakness, if you treat wounds that are at your level of experience you will also grow\n\nin power, but you will rarely find wounds that match your experience exactly.\n\nMindsoothing.\n\nA cleric also has the ability to calm the minds of others, to achieve this you must be in a calm state yourself. If you are not then you will not be able to succeed, however you can calm yourself through a quick prayer\n\nor a short meditation session.\n\n§PDistress Scale.\n\nA: Normal state of mind.\n\nB: Light panic, nervous eye movement, soft speech, cautious movement.\n\nC: Total panic, crying, heavy shaking, difficulty speaking.\n\nD: Catatonic state, generally inable to move or speak, will sit or remain still, as if frozen. Some patients may repeat phrases or motions until treated.\n\nAs with the healing of wounds, you must first assess the condition of the patient, if there is a physical injury as well you must decide which to treat first. \n\nThen you must clear your mind of woes and connect to the creator.\n\nThen you must guide the light to either your eyes or your hands. and look at the patient directly, or in the latter case, move your hands to touch his body, then you simply project your own calmness unto the patient.\n\nLimb regereneration.\n\nIn the final stages of your abilities you will be able to regrow limbs using the creator's blessing, however this is not to be taken lightly and will take a great physical cost and depending on the severity\n\nmay require several Clerics. However fingers and hands can be regrown over multiple sessions at a lesser physical cost.\n\nYou MUST § do the proper research before attempting this procedure, every vein, bone and muscle must be regrown\n\nperfectly or the limb will not be of much use, or worse the patient may suffer internal bleeding and die.\n\nIn theory one could regenerate a vital organ such as a lung or liver, but this will leave you at a severe risk of dying.\n\nNever attempt to regrow a heart or brain, you will most likely die of the side effects before you generate a working heart, the brain is simply impossible.\n\nI hope that this guide has helped you in understanding Holy magic.\n\nMay you heal many people.\n\n~Sarah Hightower\n\n10th of Sun's Smile\n                  1456", ""),
        StaticBook("2 V III I", "§bOracle", "Koigan and the Dungeon\n((Written by Huuki for the Asulon Novella Competition))\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nKoigan Opened His Eyes and Yawned, he scratched his head...\nStill dazzed by his earliness of Awakeness, he tried to look around and re-rubbed his eyes.\nKoigan's Mouth\n\nfell below his chin, he re-rubbed his eyes for the third time, he was being carried on his own bed!\nHe hung of the bed clinging on tightly to see what wa carrieing him it was three large Endermen. Koigan went to shout but reliased that It would\n\nprobably end badly.\nKoigan let them keep walking getting slightly more paroniod at every step the Endermen took, suddenly Koigan seen a Dungeon enterance in the side of a mountain and looked shocked, he started shouting, but the Endermen\n\nignored him.\nThey carried on walking, through the enterance. Koigan lay down his face could be scraping the rock of the ceiling right now, so he kept as low as possible.\nKoigan lifted his head a little, He now had lots of head space, but was in a\n\nrandom room. Koigan was carried down some stairs and then the bed tipped, and Koigan fell through a Black Hole, surrounded with Ugly Green Circles.\nKoigan screamed as he fell through and closed his eyes, but he opened them in a very unusual\n\nplace. He looked around there were massive Dark Pillars.\nThe Endermen suddenly came up behind Koigan and lifted him High In the Air. They then teleported several times forward, Koigans stomach churned as he was teleported\n\nforward, everytime he felt like he would vomit.\nThe Endermen stopped their were more stairs dark and cold on Koigan's Feet.\nThey pushed him up the stairs and Koigan allowed them to, there was many Endermen around, all looking\n\nat him then disapearing to go behind him.\nKoigan panted, and wiped his head as he reached the top of the Pillar he had to climb, suddenly a Dragon landed Next to Koigan!\nThe Dragon then Turned Around, and set alight\n\nsomething!\nThen it turned back to Koigan...\nAnd handed him some cooked Chicken?\nThe Endermen laughed, Koigan Looked confused, but chicken was his favourite so he quickly ate it and then looked around as the Endermen\n\nshrank.\nLoads of Men, Dwarves and Elves got out of their Endermen costumes and Started laughing and Pointing at Koigan, The Dragon's stomach opened and out stepped several Dwarves who to had been wearing a Large Costume.\n\n\nKoigan Gasped In Confusing, one Elf Moved forward showed him a Strange Dark Ball, which had a small bit of green light,\nThe Elf chucked it and suddenly he teleported, to where the ball landed...\nKoigan still looked confused, then\n\nsuddenly something fell over and Koigan was in normal day light sky and normal grass, and everything was light again.\nKoigan looked even more confused and looked around, their were large cardboard rectangles lieing\n\non the floor.\nA Man walked up to Koigan and Laughed,\n\"Koigan You have been pranked... Wha... You Dont know who I Am? Ah...\"\nThe Man pulled at his hair and his whole face came off, he too was wearing another mask.\nIt was Brevius!\n\nKoigan's Goblin Friend, but then he pulled his Hair again...\nAnd his face came off again, another mask? He was know a Dwarf, he pulled it off again, now he was an Elf, he pulled it off again he was a Orc.\nThen he pulled of his shoes and melted\n\ninto the soil, so did everyone else as they laughed.\nKoigan looked around in alarm, as people melted into the soil, a tree apeared were everyone was standing, then it died straight away and fell to the floor.\nThen Stood up pulled off its twigs and\n\ndissapeared.\nKoigan screamed, as He woke up in his bed... It was just a dream.\nhe scratched his head...\nStill dazzed by his earliness of Awakeness, he tried to look around and re-rubbed his eyes.\nKoigan's Mouth\n\nfell below his chin, he re-rubbed his eyes for the third time, he was being carried on his own bed!\nKoigan screamed again, He looked under his bed he was being carried by Endermen!\nKoigan Fainted and Re-Awoke loads of people were\n\nstanding around him, Koigan had been sweating badly, and was shaking Wildy.\n\"Wow You Must of had a Horrible Dream Koigan\"\nBrevius Said!\nKoigan Closed his Eye's...", ""),
        StaticBook("2 I II I", "§bOracle", "Quacktopia\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n4th of Malin's Welcome -1443\n\nThere once was a man named Jack, he was the most coolest and best person in alllll of Aegis . He was the kings most trusted advisor and warrior, one day the king told him to go on A adventure to Quackatopia, the\n\nduck ruled kingdom of the sea, Jack eagarly accepted. : He traveled through the blazing deserts, the freezing forests, and the mean ocean fianlly making it to Quacktopia, he celebrated, drinking till drunk then flirting with allll the pret ty duck\n\nladies. When he awoke he got to business and was tasked with eliminating the meany head wolf people to the south of Quacktopia. Jack arrived at wolftopia and beat up alllll the wolves . After arriving back at Quacktopia he found out he\n\nimpregnated the duckling, later he was killed by the ducklings dad, THE END Quacktopia", ""),
        StaticBook("Whitestorm Ck.Bk", "§bRosso", "Baking with the\n      Whitestorms\n  Some of\nThe family’s\n    Favorite recipes.\n             James\n\n       Whitestorm\n\n\n\nVolume One:\n               Cakes\n\nBasic Cake\n----------\nServes an entire party. Prepare long in advance, and douse in brandy to prevent mold.\n\nIngredients\n----------\n1 lb Oat Flour\n1 lb Egg\n1 lb Sugar\n1 lb butter\n½ cup Candied OrangePeel\n½ cup Candied Lemon Peel\n½ cup Candied Citron\n1/3 Cup Currants\n\nIngredients Contd.\n----------\n½ Cup Almond Flour\n1 Tsp Nutmeg\n1 Tsp Mace\n1 ½ Tsp Cinnamon\n1 Tsp Ginger\n1 Tsp Cloves\n¼ Cup Sherry\n¼ Cup Brandy\n\nDirections\n----------\n1. Heat stove to adequate temperature. Grease a 10 inch pan in preparation.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n2. Beat the butter in a bowl until creamy. Add sugar and beat until fluffy. Stir at a medium speed while gradually adding in egg, until thoroughly combined.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n3. Sift the Oat Flour in a separate bowl. Add the spices and almond flour. Add the mixture gradually to the butter, sugar, and eggs, while stirring. Continue stirring until thoroughly mixed.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n4. Add the brandy and sherry to the batter and mix.\n5. Pour the batter into the pan, and spread it evenly. Bake until a knife can come out clean. Allow cooling for half an hour.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n6- Invert the pan onto a plate, then onto a cooling rack. Allow even more cooling.\n\nWhitestorm cook book\n\nWritten by James Whitestorm\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("On \"Racism\"", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "On \"Racism\"\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nDuring my initial days of Haelun'or, I took great care in writing a treatise upon the more common questions critical of Mali'aheral society. This book contained rebuttals to these questions for the sake of education, and the sake of the ignorant\n\npeoples beyond our community. This is a reprint of sorts (though not truly, as the original manuscript was lost in Asulon) that contains more ignorant questions, extended arguments, and superior literacy. That said, this introduction is long enough.\n\nLet us begin.\n\nA human once told me,\n\"Purity is of the heart, not of the mind and body.\"\n\nLet us ignore the obvious conclusion that a heart is merely a muscle that pumps blood through the body, with no importance to purity other than filling its\n\nmandatory biological role. The human presumably refers to the heart as the beholder of an abstract concept of \"goodness,\" so we shall argue that point. \n\n\"Goodness,\" the act of being \"good,\" is a fundamentally flawed concept. There are\n\nthings that are innately evil, such as the dread-demon Iblees, profligates of Dark Magics, and other varying monsters who tout goals of domination and destruction. These are certainly cruel. But what can truly be considered \"good?\". Good (and at times\n\n\"evil\") are subjective in their very nature. Even the words of the much-revered Aenguls are only a matter of perspective. Let us say that in a Valah village, a family is taxed heavily by their local Lord. This lord treats them the same as any other\n\nfamily, but this one is particularly poor, and can barely survive the long winters. One day, the father in desperation robs a nobleman, and kills him. The pauper did not take pleasure in the act, and had not intended the nobleman to die. This allows him\n\nto feed his long-suffering children. Would this act be good, or evil? If one situation can be skewed in such a way, then, logically, others must also be flawed. \n\nThe maehr'sae hiylun'ehya teaches that purity is a combination of mind,\n\nand body. It is something only mali'aheral are capable of, and can never be allowed to fester beneath the guidance of the ignorant. To advance our people, Mali'aheral must enhance and strengthen their minds. To understand nature's workings is\n\nto understand our existence and its natural place in the true-world. To this end, our people are gifted with extraordinary intelligence, and it allows us a greater capacity to absorb information, and create our own.\n\nIn advancing our people, we complete the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. The heart has no purpose in true purity.\n\nA wood elf once asked me, \n\"If you are not racist, why do you not allow intermarriage between your people and other races?\"\n\nThe other races are, as commonly said, \"lesser\" than true, pure mali'aheral. This is not a malicious slur\n\naimed at them for amusement or as an emotion-fueled outburst of hatred. This is simply observable fact. Traits that commonly bring the ruin of other societies, for example; greed and violence, are barely prevalent within our community. Furthermore, our\n\naforementioned heightened mental faculties make such traits almost non-existent. Our blood ensures this superiority, and every muddying of our family lines with inferior specimens dulls preferred Mali'aheral traits. This makes the completion of the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya more difficult with every corrupted generation. Were we to allow rampant, foolish breeding, then the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya would never be completed, and our kind would languish in the mediocrity of the other Mali.\n\nA Dwarf once asked me,\n\"If you have no prejudices, why do you allow so few outsiders within your society?\"\n\nOutsiders are difficult to trust. There are a worthy few of them accepted into our numbers, but these have proven their\n\ncompliance and worthiness to our people. To why we bar outsiders in general, will be answered in an allegory--one that will be far simpler to grasp for those not of our people. \n\nImagine yourself the owner of a fabulous dwelling, filled with\n\ndelights unknown to your envious neighbours. You enjoy your life amongst the trinkets and comfort items that you gathered, and rest in a fine wicker chair in the sitting room. Suddenly, a person you have never met walks through your door, without so much\n\nas a knock, and begins to walk about \"Ooh\"ing and \"Ahh\"ing at the many delights and placing her dirty fingers upon your property. Confused and concerned, you ask the obvious question of \"What are you doing?\" The stranger, with a smile, explains that she\n\nthinks your home beautiful, and is looking around. You, in turn, explain to her that you don't want unannounced people in your home. With that, she becomes angered, and declares that you're \"greedy\" for keeping your property to yourself. Such things\n\nshould be for everyone to see! You explain to her that she is free to do as she pleases with her own home, but that you prefer your privacy, thank you very much. \n\nThe stranger disappears, and begins spreading  rumours amongst your fellow\n\nneigbours of your greed, and how you \"hate people.\" Suddenly these neighbours also begin to barge their way in, and look about. Sometimes, things go missing. You in turn build a high wall around your home, and though they continue to voice their anger\n\nat your actions, they are no longer a nuisance. It should not be a necessity to do this, but the nature of your neighbours makes it so.\n\nA dark elf once asked me, \n\"Your people insult ours so viciously! Why would you be so cruel?\"\n\nMisinterpretation on the part of those whom we \"insult.\" If this occurs so commonly, why have these victims not re-evaluated the\n\nreasons behind our words? What we say always has merit. This is what they do not understand. They choose defensiveness over recognising their faults, and therefore never adapt and improve themselves. Thusly, our people will \"insult\" them again, and will\n\nlikely continue to do so until their missteps are recognised. Such is only befitting a proper Mali, and for their own good.\n\nA Goblin once asked me (version interpreted from orcish babble),\n\"If you are superior, how is it we orcs have slaughtered you in battle countless times?\"\n\nActs of combat and physical strength do not imply superiority. Violence is one of the\n\nbasest and most simplistic natural urges that any animal is capable. It can stem from any dark emotional outburst, and those that practice them commonly cannot be fully trusted. To use yet another example -- were a giant spider to attack and kill an Uruk,\n\nwould the spider therefore be superior to the orc?\n\nSuch as it is, these questions irk me so, especially when my associates cannot answer them. May you be further enlightened, my reader.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("°~.First Aid.~°", "Timelord_Lalve", "The use of Healthy\nPlants in the \nmountains.\n\n~.First Aid.~\n\nby\n\nRadagast Aiwendil Ernest Swampstone.\n\n°~.Chapter One.~°\n  ~Sickness~\n\nThe following plants can heal normal diseases.\n\n~.Pine Juice.~\n\nYou need:\n- Pine Leafs\n- Water\n- A place where you can heat the water.\n\nThe sick patient must drink the juice completely.\nIt heals the lung from aches.\n\n~.Mushroom Tea.~\n\nYou need:\n- One Mushroom\n- Hot Water\n- A mug\n\nThe patient must drink the tea to cure headaches.\n\n~.Mushroom.~\n\nThe patient need to smoke the mushroom, he will get a feeling of happiness and relaxing.\n\nGood use for those, that losed someone important.\n\n°~.Chapter Two.~°\n  ~Healing Wounds~\n\nThe following chapter will explain to heal wounds without the help of a healer.\n\n~.Scratches.~\n\nScratches can be dangerous, a infection can lead to death.\n\n1. Clean the Scar with fresh and clean water.\n2. Lay Grass on the scar.\n\nIn a few seconds, the scar will be gone.\n\n~.Wounds.~\n\nIt is important to got bandages.\n\nFor bigger wounds, it is needed to clean them with fresh water to avoid a infection. \nTake a look, if the wound got no splinters.\n\n~.Stop the Bleeding.~\n\nTo stop the bleeding with plants from the mountains you should find the following:\n- Pine Leafs\n- Grass\nThe patient must chew the plants and then gulb them down.\nThis will stop the bleeding.\n\n~. Bandages.~\n\nUse the bandage only if the wound is cleaned from any blood and other materials.\n\nTipp:\nRub some grass on the bandage, but clean it before. It will heal faster.\n\n~. Burnings .~\n\nIf someone got burnings, get some snow and cool it. The wound will now stop hurting the patient and the wound will compost.\n\nThe healing procedure won't be a problem.\n\n~.Important.~\n\nA injured person is a weak one. Fighting and heavy movements can open the wounds on the patient.\n\nThis will result in the losing of blood.\nIt is recommended to get the patient to a healer.\n\n~. Warmly .~\n\nYou are in the terran, without a bed or a tent? \nBuild a tiny shack with snow. It is warm in the inside.\n\n~.Last Words.~\n\nYou should got everytime two bandages and clean water with you.\n\n\n\"The tiny things can heal the biggest.\"\n\n--.Ernest.--", ""),
        StaticBook("Da Brathmordakin", "§b[Masked] [High Prophet] Indago Stormhammer", "*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*Join Our Brotherhood\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\n  Have you've done your duty to please\n   Yemekar?  It's           important that we       praise and worship\nour creator for giving us the land we stand         upon today.\n\nYemekar created the lands of Aegis using       his great forge.\nFrom the power of his Great Anvil, it created the Brathmordakin.  The Brathmordakin the     seven gods of\ncreation and they are vital to our faith in            many ways.\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n  The Brathmordakin\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-* Us brothers follow the Brathmordakin so that we can secure a place  for our souls in the\nafterlife.  When we die our souls travel to Dungrim's keep on the             moon.\n\nThere, our souls are auctioned off to the god that bids highest for it.  A dwarf that has faithfully served    their god in life will have a much greater chance to be bought and serve that god in        the afterlife\n\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\nThe Brathmordakin consists of:\n*Yemekar\n*Anbella\n*Belka\n*Dungrim\n*Ogradhad\n*Grimdugan\n*Armakak\n\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*Join Our Brotherhood\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*If you wish to study and worship to secure a promosing afterlife, join the clergy be filling out the form and giving it to a Prophet         High Prophet.\n((\nForum>DwarvenRolplay >DwarfClergy)\n\nInitiate Application\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\nYour Name:\n\nWhat God You wish to follow:\n\n\n\n    May We Always \nCommemorate Yemekar!\n\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\n    If you have any\n questions about our\nfaith.  Ask a clergyman to assist you & guide    while you seek the            spirit of our             Brathmordakin.\n\n  (Forums>DwarfRP\n  >Dwarven Clergy)", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge Members", "§bUnsigned", "There is a cult in Anthos that has the purpose of following the commands of the Black Scourge. In a way, they are considered part of it.\n\nIn this book there is information on their past members, and some of their current ones.\n\nVithquar\n\nAn experiment created by some of the members of the Scourge, particularly the Judge and the Shadowed alchemist, with aid of one of the Harbinger, Shae'Tan. Physically strong, and slightly sexy, she is not really that smart.\n\nTo identify her is easy, she has horns, a tail, black wings, and black and yellow eyes. She also wears very little slothing.\nShe believes she is a goddess that has lost her powers, and that she should be treated as such. If you actually treat her like\n\nshe wants to be treated, you get on her good side.\nWhile she is part of the cult, she does not worship Setherien. She is only in it because she was created by them, and because she has received power from them.\n\nThe Listener\n\nLeader of the cult, not much is known about him. A warrior, always armored when meeting the cultists. He is in direct contact with the Harbingers, and takes orders from them.\nHe is one of those who recruits.\n\nThe Judge\n\nOne of the higher ups in the cult, a more calm person. He hides his identity through black robes and a skull mask, having a straight posture and speaking in an unnatural voice. Not a fighter himself, he used to stand behind others he\n\ncommanded, or make more use of tricks.\nFrom those captured he would be normally the cause for it to happen. He would interegate them, question them, before deciding what to be done. Some he releaced, some only after torture, some he killed fast, but when\n\nhe didn't like the answers or the person, he usually did something else. It would be a sort of ritual, before he carved symbols into someone's back and skinned them. Why he did so was never known.\nHe was a true believer of the word of Setherien,\n\nmostly the part about adquiring peace by force, yet this soon turned out to be false when he betrayed the Scourge, and destroyed a Harbinger.\nHe is wanted by the Scourge, and as such, he is in hiding.\n\nQa'darath\n\nBefore a higher up of the cult, he too betrayed it, the reasons for the betrayal known. An elf which had quite a few powers. He could tap into the mind of people, and he was a necromancer. If you have not known until\n\nnow, the Scourge and the necromancers are against eachother. The reason for his betrayal is simple, he sided with the necromancers instead of the cult.\nHis description is as simply described as white haired high elf, thin, and with purple robes.\n\nBurzumkil\n\nOne of the stronger warriors in the Scourge. A human with a thick accent. Very powerful in war. Merciless as well, he was one of those who lead raids against towns and villages. He has not been seen for a while.\n\nPrince Ebs\n\nOne of the best spies in the cult, prince Ebs is said to be the one responsible for the information required to access the lands of Old Malinor with the power corruption. He would also keep the Scourge updated with movements of the\n\nelves, and information about politics of Anthos.\nA Prince of Malinor, he has the perfect cover, and would only meet with the Scourge in designated times and places. He would bring great information that would keep the Scourge up to date. While as a spy,\n\nHe never really attacked anyone, and he has great skill in lying. He was commanded to never show himself as a cultist, even to those of the cult, nor to help them. He is a pure spy, one which has not even been given much information on the Scourge, as for\n\nhim to do his job as best he could. If captured, he has nothing to tell, even if tortured. Giving away his position as spy, would only result in his execution, he knows that if he says he worships Setherien, even in torture, he will lose his life, be it\n\nby those who captured him, or by those under Setherien’s will.\n\nThe Oogie Boogie Man\n\nA twisted being, corrupted so much that neither his mind or body is anything good. Black robes and skull mask like the Judge, but the way he behaves is quite different.\nBugs of various kinds seem to be what he is\n\nmade of. Spiders crall from his eyes, ears, and hands.\nOne that enjoys te pain of others, and the bringing of destruction. If he does worship Setherien, it would be because Setherien brings those things. Knowledged in the arts of weird dark magics,\n\nhe was the one that was able to bring a strong ghost into the rule of the Scourge, and he was the one which discovered a way to destroy Old Malinor.\nPowerful in knowledge… weak physically. He is one of those weaker in the Scourge, using tricks and dark\n\nmagic to capture and torment the people of Anthos.\nHe likes to tell stories, and normally just walks unprotected through the lands, with his black robes and skill mask.\n\nThe Shadow Alchemist\n\nAnother one to take intellect over power, this old man is an alchemist that focuses on the dark and twisted sides of it. Experimenting and taking to the Judge were some of the things he did best. Also a great friend of the\n\nOogie Boogie Man, for the same reasons, knowledge.\nExtremelly smart, and twisted to the point of not caring of the life of those he experiments on.\nUnlike the other two, this one can still swing an axe once or twice before he gets tired.\n\nThe Mistress\n\nA twisted elf, which collects heads. Only in the cult to gain more power.\nA fighter and a spy, she also collected relics and information when not killing.\nNothing much is known about her appearance, as she wore masks.\n\nKaos\n\nA human or elf, not known. He is another powerful warrior, leading charges and raids with Burzumkil.\nHe made good use of armor, and hid his identity quite well.\n\nThere are more but I do not know enough details to write about them. This information has been given from a member on the inside, so the informer will remain anonymous as well.\n\n*The book is left unsigned.*", ""),
        StaticBook("1 VII I I", "§bOracle", "Zevandir's Newbie Guide by Zevandir\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of The Grand Harvest -1443\n\nHello new traveller of Aegis! Aegis is a vast and wonderful world, with much to explore. This book is a wonderful investment, as it will teach you the basics and help you get started. ::You have probably already chosen a name\n\nand race. If you havn't, lets do that now. ::All the commands in Aegis are preceeded by / so we type /setname &lt;RP Name. &lt;Race&gt; remember not to include the '&lt;' and '&gt;' symbols. Well done! Now, lets go over some rules.\n\nThe main rule of Aegis is RolePlaying. One definition of RolePlaying from the Oxford dictionary is 'The changing of one' behaviour to fulfill a social role.' RP'ing generally means acting a certain way to play a certain role. This is the main rule of\n\nAegis, and failing to comply will probably get you banned. Please note that the World of Aegis is patrolled by multiple military groups, you can join one of these military groups, a great way to earn Minas and have fun. Minas is the in game currency,\n\nand is used to buy houses, shops and goods. Minas is also what bandits want when they attack, and they will RP holding you up. A Bandit role is very carefully monitored, you MUST RP banditing someone. Random PVP and killing will get you banned, and\n\nBandits prefer to loot and steal before fighting. ::Races. Races are the main factions of Aegis. Dwarves, Elves, Orcs and Humans. Each faction has its own Kingdom, and each faction is rather different from the others. For example, the Elves are rule\n\nby an Elven Council and a High Prince, with tree-like architectur e. The Orcs live in the desert and use sand and sandstone, ruled by a dictator-like Rex. Aegis is a wonderful land, full of diverse cultures and people. However, Aegis is also inhabited\n\nby the Spawn of Iblees [Read the History of Aegis for more]. These evil beings are exactly that, evil. They will try to kill you on sight, and are very strong. The spawn of Iblees are also different from regular monsters. ::Zombies hit\n\nharder, reach further and are very resilient to your attacks. ::Creepers do not damage the land, do slightly less damage, but have far more health. Meaning they cang et closer and explode before you can kill them. ::Spiders are best avoided unless\n\nbehind a fence, these demons of the night fall onto your head and rip out your brains, they are faster, stronger and have more health than you, but you have skill, cunning and a will to survive, making you far more dangerous if properly trained.\n\nYou are probably thinking, I guess I'll just make a dirt shelter for the night. Well, in Aegis, you can't. You must buy some form of house in a protected city, or venture into the dangerous, unrpotected wilds, where no guards patrol and your\n\nstuff isnt safe. Houses cost anything from 1,000 to 30,000 Minas, and until then you will have to risk living in the wilds or someone elses house. There are also Inns along the main roads that service travellers, and you could pay a small fee to live\n\nthere until you own your own home. Well, you are now ready for the World of Aegis! ::Look out for the new series, Races! ::All written and transcribed by Zevandir. All rights registered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mathic Code", "§bRosso", "From a note written by a friend in code, of many pages, she had no memory of writing it, or what it did mean.\n\nI decided to try and decipher it as if it were a secret note between armies, and I came with results. The code is copied first, then the meaning of the code is told, then the translation.\n\nCode\n\n{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\n\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.*,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\n\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\n\n{t, ƒ‘“ªt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t,:ª i.û :º t, ö‘û,ª ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[ºi‘ûiü t, i:øe£º .ª, ,æª.u,ô û:t t, ºüñd‘iº ‘ƒ t, ,nº,ñdi,º ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[t, º:øe£º ‘ƒ n,û ç.:nº .ª, ƒ.ñ:i:.ª]\n\n{t, ƒ:ƒt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.øñ,n£º .ª, ñ.ô, .º £‘ø,t,ª .º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n[t, ñ.nü ç‘‘º, t,:ª ö.t| £‘ t, ª,ö,£:£:‘n .º t, º“n ª:º,º .nô ƒ.iiº ‘ª £‘ t, dª,.*:æ ‘ƒ :£| t.£ t, º“n ê.ii º£.nô º£:ii]\n\n{t, º:xt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ñ.nü d,c‘ñ, .º ‘n, .º û.º t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n\n{t, º,u,nt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º ñ.nü ñ.ô, .ø.:n]\n\nMeaning\n\n. - a\n, - e\n: - i\n‘ - o\n“ - u\n\nt - th\nƒ - f\nª - r\nº - s\n£ - t\nñ - m\nc - c\n\nø - g\nû - w\ne - h\nç - ch\nô - d\nn - n\nü - y\nu - v\nö - p\nd - b\ni - l\nê - sh\n* - k\n\næ - ng\n\n| - ,\n\n[] - sentance\n{} - title\n\nTranslation\n\nThe first mathic age.\n\nThat which is He made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were His to command.\nThey were dust and He was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape.\n\nAs was before, that which is He made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea.\nSuch directionless is anathema to Him, who is linear.\n\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over.\n\nThe second Mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry.\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate.\n\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight.\nThe way is shut.\n\nThe third Mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts.\nIt is as it was.\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others.\n\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows.\nAll wielding their law.\n\nThe Fourth Mathic Age\n\nTheir law is the power of the many.\nSlowly the lights are engraved with the symbols of the ensembles of the many.\nThe sights of new chains are familiar.\n\nThe Fifth Mathic Age\n\nThe fragments are made as together as was before, that which is he\nThe many choose their path, to the repetition as the sun rises and falls or to the breaking of it, the sun shall stand still.\n\nThe Sixth Mathic Age\n\nThe many become as one as was that which is he.\n\nThe Seventh Mathic Age\n\nAs was before, that which is he many made again.\n\nMathic Code\n\nCoppied and Decoded by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry", "§bSofetios", "Poetry\n\n          ~ By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n\n        The Lake\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\n\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\n\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven thought it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\n\n        The Dreamer\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\n\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\n\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\n\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\n\n        The Cobbler\n             and\n         The Crow\n\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\n\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\n\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\n\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\n\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\n\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\n\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\n\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\n\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\n\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\n\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\n\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\n\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\n\n         Friend\n           or\n         Enemy?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\n\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\n\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\n\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\n\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\n\n         Imprint\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\n\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\n\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\n\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.\n\n   An Uncommon Sight\n\nI go about my day,\nDoing the same things as before,\nThe same old road,\nFrom my humble abode,\nNot realizing it is a bore.\n\nI walk ever onward,\nKnowing all my tasks by heart,\nA straight narrow trail,\nWith nothing new to avail,\nAll I do is my part.\n\nThen one day as I'm going past,\nA park once again,\nI see a boy,\nwithout even a toy,\nwho couldn't be past ten.\n\nThe boy was doing something abnormal,\nsomething I hadn't seen before,\nHe was looking in the sky,\nNot even blinking an eye,\nthey didn't even seem sore.\n\nI wondered if there was a hawk,\nOr something in the sky,\nI didn't hear a thing,\nOnly the birds that always sing,\nSo I did wonder why.\n\nI looked over,\nto the boy sitting by,\nHe was being bullied by his peers,\nAnd was starting to go in tears,\nJust for looking in the sky.\n\nI was about to go over,\nTo try to help if I could,\nbut the parents went first,\nBefore I feared the worst,\nTo help as they should.\n\nI walked on my way home,\nWondering why what I saw came to pass,\nI had a thought why,\nso I looked to the sky,\nand saw it in it's great mass,\n\nAs I looked to the sky,\nI was transfixed,\nI hadn't done this in a while,\nAnd it did make me smile,\nAs past and current memories mixed.\n\nI saw the vast expanse,\nIn all its mystery,\nI watched the clouds in the sky,\nAs they changed shape and passed by,\nAs they had for all of history.\n\nSuddenly someone laughed to my left,\nEven thought it was mild,\nSomeone looking at me,\nLaughing at what I appeared to be,\nJust as the others had done to the child.\n\n         Courage\n\nIt is a thing you use\nWhen you can't go to the end,\nWhen all seems lost\nAnd you can't defend.\n\nYou use it as\nIt combines with your will,\nAll you need to do is\nLet it give its fill.\n\nThe choice is yours,\nGive in or go,\nThough in the end\nOnly you will know.\n\nSee with your spirit\nAnd not with fear,\nfor then you will know\nThat courage is here.\n\nThe End\n\nThank you for taking the time to read my poetry. I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing let me know! By Bird or in person.\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\n\"Everything you think you know all has to do with what you believe.\" ~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("The Servants'...", "§bMonk Scribe", "The Servants' Conflict\n\n...the female Aengul proceeded to leave, Aeriel and the Wizard were indeed distraught. The system collapsing before their own eyes... Odion was called for guidance. It is reported that the Daemon's stone halls spat flames like a\n\nbaneslither when he heard of this dissent. They rushed to find that the portal had already closed, making it impossible to trace the followers of the Dark Lady, as Monk John was apt to call her.\n\nAeriel decreed that the ethereal spirits\n\nmust refrain from the constant contact with the Descendent Races as to avoid further mishaps such as this. Some of the Daemons who had befri...d mortals were angered and left the realm as well, while the remaining Daemons and the majority of Aenguls\n\ndecided to abide by thi..., each in their own way.\n\nIt did seem that Aeriel, as well as the Wiz... which some did not... and throughout Aegis, the monks destroyed all tomes other than... much to his dismay. The Wizard was quite upset with the actio...\n\nthough it was all for a grand cause, indeed. He later came to be glad for Aeriel's decision, for... efforts were certainly successful for the most part, as is apparent in society, and the account o... nut fully untrue, naturally, yet th... only to be\n\npreserved within this room by the Scarlet Monks.\n\n- Written by the Third Elder Monk in year 109 in Aegis. Part of the Hidden Scrolls. The document is badly damaged and pages are missing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hello.", "§bAudrey Caillot", "Hello\nWhen her face turned to me,\nI saw stars.\nStars in her eyes.\nGlittering at me,\nShimmering at me,\nAwash in life, she was,\nAnd she did not hide it.\nA single smiling face,\nIn the sea of many.\n\nEntire worlds thriving within those starry eyes.\nHer ivory cheeks moons.\nAnd her lively, smiling eyes,\nPearly white skin,\nAll adorned with the sky.\nA tumbling mess of curls and waves,\n\nWild and free.\nReckless.\nIt casts who she is undeniably well,\nFrom the upwards twitch of her smile,\nTo the way she breathes.\nWild, free.\nWithout boundary.\n\nIt is with all of this in my mind that I swallow,\n\nLips forming words,\nWords bubbling up,\nAnd I say:\nHello.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Healing", "§bmaynard66", "The human body is suseptable to many various deseases and injuries. Through my studies I have learned that clerics are more efficient in their healing but can not help teach the common person how to heal without converting them to their face. This book\n\nwill contain all my notes about healing others using simple herbs and the help of minor arcane magic. The magical spells I have learned from my books should help me save many lives without losing my faith in him.\n\nTable of Contents\n\nTools of the Trade...pg 4\n- This will cover the basic tools required to heal patients.\n\nHealing the Wounds...pg 12\n- This will cover basic wound healing and treatments.\n\nTools of the Trade\n\nSutures : Simply called a needle and thread. The better the thread, the better the stitching will be. Stitches take care and patience and even simple wounds take at least three emotes to do. Threading the needle, carefully\n\nstitching the injury, tying off the thread. There are more steps to this and can easily be made into a more in-depth roleplay should you wish. Stitching a wound is very similar to stitching clothes. You tie off an end and slowly slide the needle through.\n\nFor stitches it is important to make them closer together to insure there is no seepage and to keep the wound closed. If you use regular thread, it can break and after some rough movement, the stitches can pop. It’s always best to keep the stitches close\n\ntogether and using high quality thread.\n\nBandages : Bandages can be as simple as a torn rag or as complex as a roll of gauze. A healer always has enough bandages on hand to tend to any emergency.\n\nWhen in a pickle, one can easily use a torn shirt or a strip of dress to create a bandage. The purpose of bandages is to stop bleeding and to prevent a wound from becoming dirty and infected. In order to apply bandages\n\nproperly, you need to follow the blood flow and remember not to make it too tight or too loose. Too tight and the patient will lose feeling and eventually the limb, too loose and the bandages can fall off, leading to other complications.\n\nHerbs : Anthos is full of herbs that many can use to heal with. A healer must be adept in the most basic of herbs in order to heal properly. Many herbs can be used to heal but the most common is Dragurstongue, Frostvine, Blissfoil, and Tippensroot.\n\nFire : Cauterizing a wound can be benificial to sealing a wound quickly. HOWEVER, keep in mind, you need to close the wound with your hands first before attempting to. Do not throw alcohol on the patient then a torch! You may end up killing them.\n\nHealing the Wounds\n\nHealing wounds takes knowledge of herbs and practices. This should clear up a lot more when it comes to healing even the most injured.\n\nMinor Scrapes and Cuts\nMinor cuts and scrapes are easy to tend to as they take little effort. First you must clean the wound with water and then disinfect the wound with Dragurstongue. Once you have\n\ndone this, you can apply a clean bandage and send the patient off. Minor injuries don’t always require bandaging, so its safe to save the bandaging for more serious wounds.\n\nGashes\nDepending on the location and the severity of gashes is whether or not you will need to stitch it. Always disinfect the wound first. Clean it well before assessing if it needs stitching. If it does, stitch the wound\n\nclosed with simple cross stitching. Keep the stitches close and make sure your take your time. Once you are done, apply blissfoil for pain and carefully bandage the wound.\n\nBroken Bones\nBroken bones are tricky. There are several things to look for. Is the bone sticking out? Then you will need to set it and then treat it like a gash. Most bones you will need to set back into place, which is generally\n\nvery painful for the patient. Its a good idea to apply blissfoil to help a bit with the pain. After treating any wounds the broken bone may have caused, you will need to stabilize the bone. Splinting it usually helps.\n\nTake two sticks and then stabilize the wound. For arms, make a sling also. For broken ribs, you just need to wrap the chest, DO NOT add sticks, it can do more harm than good.\n\nBurns\nThe severity of burns can vary. First degree burns are the easiest to tend to. All they are is pain and slight redness. Take a cool, wet rag and frostvine, let the patient sit till the pain passes. Second degree\n\nburns are blistering of the skin. Take a cool rag and clean the burn, gently, before applying dragurstongue, frostvine, and blissfoil. Wrap and send them on their way. Third degree burns is charred\n\nskin. Do the same with second degrees but be extra careful. With second and third degree burns, make sure there is nothing stuck to the skin, if there is, be as gentle as possible in removing the item.\n\nChild Birth\nMake sure the mother is truly comfortable and fetch water, warm towels, and some herbs. Many mothers go through labor well and have healthy children. However there are the few that need help. If one begins to lose too much blood it is\n\nimportant to stay calm and not allow the mother to panic. Try to stop the bleeding with tippensroot. Know that some mothers or infants will not survive and this is not your fault. All you can do is help slow the process. Make the mother as comfortable as\n\npossible. When the infant is born, make sure they are  breathing and crying. Once you are sure both are healthy and able to be left alone, you can let them rest.\n\nLoss of AppendageLoss of an appendage usually means death for the patient. However, if you use a tourniquet you can save them. A tourniquet requires a strip of fabric and a stick. Wrap the fabric around the amputated limb\n\nand tighten it with a stick. As the blood flow stops, slowly take a torch and burn the wound. It is best for the patient to be unconscious for this. Once the wound has been cauterized, place blissfoil and a\n\nbandage on the wound before releasing the tourniquet. If the wound begins to bleed again, you have not done it correctly.", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_CERU_4(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Speaking Blah", "§bBuluk", "Speaking Blah\n----------------------------\nAlbai - Elf\n\nMi nuud tu klomp dat Albai.\n\nBlah - Talk or Speak\n\nDat Albai cun blah?!\n\nBlarg - Home\n\nGu blarg luttle one!\n\nBubhosh - Great\n\nDat bruddah iz eh bubhosh Olog!\n\nBuurz - Dark\n\nDis ruum iz buurz!\n\nDabu - Yes or My Pleasure\n\nDabu, dat ork iz luukin fur pinkzkin tu klomp.\n\nFlat - Dead\n\nDat ork iz flat!?\n\nGazat - Dwarf\n\nGazat iz luukin tu klomp.\n\nGlob - Fool\n\nDat whitewash iz a glob!\n\nGoi - City\n\nTuk eh luft an gu tu da goi.\n\nGruk - Understand\n\nMi gruk wut latz iz blahin'.\n\nGug'ye - Goodbye\n\nGug'ye Bruddah!\n\nHowlur - Wolf\n\nDat Howlur iz sturin eht uz.\n\nKlomp - Fight\n\nPINKZKIN! WUNT TU KLOMP?!\n\nKrimp - Control\n\nMi krimpd da pinkzkin!\n\nLat - You\n\nLat nuud tu run!\n\nLigz - Arrow\n\nDat buw shut ehn ligz.\n\nLusk - Axe\n\nGut da limbz of dat tree with lat'z lusk.\n\nMi - Me\n\nMi nuud eh ligz fur meh buw.\n\nMojo - Magic\n\nDat shamun duz mojo.\n\nNub - No\n\nNub zult ehn mi.\n\nNubded - Undead\n\nDa Nubded ehr cumin'!\n\nNubhosh - Bad\n\nNubhosh bruddah!\n\nNuutshara - Ascended\n\nDa Nuutshara iz luukin' fur nuw nuutshara.\n\nO'lig - Bow\n\nDat ligz iz fur lat'z O'lig.\n\nPinkzkin - Non Orc\n\nDat Pinkzkin iz smurt.\n\nPushdug - Stinky\n\nUgh! Dat Pinkzkin iz pushdug!\n\nQuikspawn or Breedurs - Human\n\nDat Breedur duz nut liv lung.\n\nRulg - Thank you.\n\nRulg bruddah fur da zult.\n\nShara - Human\n\nSharas are lookin' fur klompin'.\n\nSnaak - Halfling\n\nDa Snaak liv en eh hul?\n\nSnaga - Slave\n\nSnagas ar nub tu beh uzd!\n\nSqueals - Halflings\n\nDuz squeals wunt tu KLOMP?!\n\nSteemiez - Redstone tech.\n\nDuz tinkurz ar gud wit steemiez.\n\nStik - Staff\n\nDa Albai curriez eh stik!\n\nStowt - Dwarf\n\nDa Stowt iz shurt.\n\nThrom'ka - Formal Greeting.\n\nThrom'ka Drudz.\n\nTwiggies - Elves\n\nDa twiggies ar buin'\nklompd!\n\nUg - Hi/Hey/Hello\n\nUzg - World/Lands\n\nDa Uzg of Vailor iz buin'\nwurd...\n\nWub - What\n\nWub latz wunt?\n\nWruten beh Buluk.\n-Buluk", ""),
        StaticBook("Play Orc", "§bBuubHozh Hefner", "PlayOrc\n\n\n*The cover page features a caricature of a bunny with rows and rows of teeth*\n\nZlutz Uv De Munth\n\n*The following ten pages feature women with disfiguring scars in extremely high quality armor.*\n\nPruper Tuzk Care\n\n*Listed here is a long and suprisingly informed article about polishing tusks to shine. According to the article, \"Bitchez Luv Shinee Tuzkz\" *\n\n BuubHozh Hefner\n\n*This article, accompanied by a drawing of an old uruk wrestling two female uruk and a Lur Wolf at once, depicts the life of a fictitious Uruk mating tychoon named BuubHozh Hefner.*\n\nMojo ztrength, Real ur Fayke?\n\n*Depected in a picture for the article is a battle-scarred, armored elven woman lifting an entire boulder above her head.*\n*The rest of the article is about telekinetics.*\n\n  De Bear Flattin\n     Ztandurd\n*Below is a drawing of a scarred, scantily clad orc woman snapping a bear's neck with her bare hands. It folds out into 4 pages.*\n\"If Zhe can nub flat a bear wid hur bare handz, zhe iz nub Hozh Mayte!\"\n\n      Flat - Ztickz\n      Agh Lat!\n*The featured weapon this issue seems to be the famous White Rose Arbelest, accompanied by a picture of a scarred human woman firing it.*\n*To one side of it is a column comparing serrated and normal battleaxes.*\n\n Lettur Frum De           Zlutz\n *There's a long (and likely fictional) letter below from a (presumably) female author about how she cant stand an uruk who doesn't smell like the blood of their enemies.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Journal", "§bUnknown", "2nd of Sun's Smile, 1500\nKuro has begun teaching me magic, as he had agreed to do back in Kaphro, Guarger also seems much more stable, and it seems he would like to rekindle our old relationship...I'm not sure if I have the heart to tell him...\n\n15th of The Amber Cold, 1500\nThings are becoming incredibly uncomfortable between Guarger and I...I have to tell him soon, this can't keep going on.\n\n5th of Snow's Maiden, 1501\nI told Guarger, he took it well, I also met a nice elf named Sana, we spoke for a while and then had tea, I quite enjoyed talking to her, I think I'll invite her around again soon.\n\n16th of Snow Maiden, 1501\nSana has moved in with me, and Kuro has explained The Void to me, he also gave me a flower and asked me to love him, which confused me, but it's Kuro, so I'll just roll with it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Painting", "§bImmortal of Soth", "--------------------------------------------____--------------/      \\-------- ----/         \\------- ----| ~     ~  |------- ----| O /  O   |3------ ----|  /_       | ------ ----|            | ------ ----\\  \\__/   |------ -----\\______/------", ""),
        StaticBook("2 II III I", "§bOracle", "A Tale of Family\n((Written by Kido122 for the Asulon Novella Competition))\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nIt was noon in the city of Salvus and a young girl no more than thirteen was standing in a ally next to a bakery, it was a small little bakery with a nice artistic sign\n\nwaving in the wind and people crowded together in line and at tables, but this girl had no interest in the people, he interest were focused on the nice aroma of the fresh baked bread and how she was going to get it. “Ok, remember don’t get caught this\n\ntime and I might get something in this stomach of mine tonight’ she said to herself. She sat there for little over an hour watching the movement of the guards and the people, timing was everything when it came to stealing. When the girl saw that\n\nthe man at the counter was getting bread out for a customer she decided it was her best chance to go for it, she sprang to her feet, grabbed the bread was off, but a guard soon followed. She ran through ally way after ally way but the guard\n\nstilled followed. She was going around another corner when, as her luck would have it, she ran into another guard. “Hey” the guard shouted as he grabbed the girl by the arm. “What the hurr….Gabby? What did you do this time?”. “Hey Lorantine,\n\nsorry about running into you an all but I really got to go.” The girl said nervously. “Not so fast Gabby, where’d you get that loaf of bread in your hand there?” Lorantine said with an n humorous nut serious look. “Would you believe me if I said I\n\nfound it on the street?” Gabby said trying to avoid Lorantine’s stare. “No I wouldn’t. This is the second time this week I caught you stealing, how would your parents feel if they…”. “My parents left me on my own when I was six, If they didn’t care\n\nenough to keep me then, they wouldn’t care about me taking a bread loaf to keep myself from starving!” Gabby said interrupting Loranantine. “Hey! What did I say before, I talk , then you talk and that’s not the point I was trying to get\n\nacross, the point is stealing is stealing even if your dirt poor, now give me the bread an run off, if your caught stealing again you are going to be staying in a cell for a while.” Lorantine said letting go off Gabby’s arm. Gabby gave Lorantine a\n\nsincere look then ran off. Gabby was often in trouble since her parents abandoned her in the old land of Agies, after she came to this new land she lived in area of Salvus and watched the city grow, then she met Lorantine when she was running away from\n\nthe guard after stealing a apple from one of the merchants, Lorantine saw that she was just a child trying to survive in the world, he helped her out a lot through the years and he was her only real parent figure, he tried his best to be a good parent\n\nfigure to Gabby, but she was too much of a free spirit. Later that day Gabby was sitting upon a roof watching the sun set as she often did, tying to remember anything about her parents, but there memories slowly died out and vanished through the\n\nyears.\nThe next morning Gabby awoke to a strange noise below her, she looked down at a boy that just ran into a can of trash. She climbed down the roof and went to the boy, “Are you ok?” she asked. “Um yea, listen I really have to go because….”.\n\n“HEY, THERE HE IS” a man shouted pointing to the boy, “He’s the one that just stole my chicken!”. Gabby looked at the boy and saw the worry in his eyes and reluctantly said “Listen, Fallow me” and then they ran off. They ran through the market crashing\n\nthrough stalls like a wild animal trying to find a way of a town. They ran through an open door and into some ones house, they ran to the roof and Gabby jumped to the roof of the house next door and looked behind her to see the boy standing there. “What\n\nare you doing? Come on they’ll catch us!” she said screaming at the boy. “I’m afraid of heights, I can’t jump that!” he said staring at the gap between the roofs. “You’re either jumping it or coming with me, or you’re going to jail alone!” she shouted\n\nangered at the boy. The boy backed up, and ran for it just making the jump. “Was that so hard?” Gabby said sarcastically, “now let’s go!” and with those words they were off. They kept running for hours and eventually scaled over the wall and ran into\n\nthe forest, as they were running off they heard a guard yell “Next time we see you two here it will be your heads!”. They kept wondering through the woods for hours until they finally made camp in a clearing. After a few hours she finally ask they boy\n\n“What is your name?”. “Eragorn, yours?’ he asked. “I’m Gabby, so where do you come from?” asked Gabby. “I’m not Shure, I lost my parents when I was five or six and just been going where the world takes me, I been fending for myself for quite some\n\ntime”, “Well I Shure wouldn’t have noticed with what happened in the city” said Gabby in a rude tone. “Hey I didn’t say I was good at fending for myself” Eragorn said jokingly. “Well get some sleep we need to head off in the morning”. In the morning\n\nwhen Gabby and Eragorn where getting ready to leave Gabby noticed something fall from the neck of Eragorn’s shirt. “Hey what is that?” Gabby asked. “What is what?” replied Eragorn, “That thing dangling from your shirt.” Eragorn looked\n\ndown and held up a silver necklace inscribed with two large letters G an E. “Oh this, it’s the only thing I have left of my parents, helps me remember them, why?”. “It looks so… never mind, forget about it” said Gabby awkwardly. “Ok. Whatever” said\n\nEragorn with a little smirk. They spent the next three years together traveling from city to city and town to town, but on the fourth year something happened that changed both their lives. They were in the city of Hanseti, planning on robing a rather\n\nlarge home. “Ok, you go in through the roof and I’ll go in through back, we get as much as we can and we leave.” Said Eragorn. “Right” replied Gabby. Soon they went on with their plan. Gabby went in through the roof and started to clear out the attic\n\nwhen suddenly there was a loud bang from downstairs, Gabby went downstairs and hid behind a door looking at a man staring at Eragorn and his wife on the stair well. Eragorn tried to run for it but the man caught him by the arm, “Wait!” he shouted. “Let\n\ngo off me I’m not planning on going to jail!” Eragorn yelled. “I’ll let you go after you answer my question, agreed?”. “Agreed” said Eragorn hesitantly. “where’d you get that necklace?” asked the man. “Why, what is it to you?” replied Eragorn\n\nconfused. “Just answer my question and you can go” said the man staring at Eragorn. “It was my parents long ago, I kept it with me ever since they abandoned me” Eragorn said still looking quite confused. “Kasey, we found him” he said\n\nnearly in tears. “what do you mean?” asked Eragorn. “We gave that to you when you were little, and we gave an identical one to your sister”. Eragorn just looked at the man and women confused. Then Gabby stepped out and said “I knew that was familiar, I\n\nhad one when I was little but lost it in the ship on was on when it crashed” Gabby said nearly in tears. “My daughter and my son have returned? I can die right know a happy man” said the man with a tear falling from his cheek. “Why did you leave us?”\n\nasked Gabby. “My daughter, my son, forgive us for not finding you before, but we did not leave you” said the man. “Then what happened” said Eragorn. “It was right before we all moved to this land, Agies was in great turmoil, but you\n\nwere children and wouldn’t have noticed, I was drafted into the military in the final battle for Agies, so I had to leave with the thought of my death coming soon, I told your mother to bring you two to the ships and to leave without me, When I found\n\nyour mother again as she could do was weep, there was a crowd rushing aboard the boats and she lost you among the people, I tried searching for you two for two years, spent all my money trying to find you, but I had to give up wondering if you\n\neven still alive, but as fate would have it you found us instead and now where together” said the man in tears. “and that’s all that matters, that we are together and we shall never leave again” said the women. They all embraced each other, tears\n\nrunning down their faces, tears of joy and happiness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "§bRosso", "__Orichalcum__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: I found this little gem off of a dead spy named Devin Ryder. Yes, he was a bard and a spy, and he had quite a few things in-between. I’m pretty sure he stole this book. Actually, I’m sure of it.\n\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as staves, swords, and magical Tiaras.\n\nIt is used by mages to store spells so that they can release those at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don’t mess around with it - it can become dangerous at the wrong moments.\n\n==How to make==\n\n==Orichalcum==\n\n1- Melt the white gold and silver.\n\n2- Let flow energies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n\n3-Make one metal bar of the combined metals\n\n4- Bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\n\n5- Power the rune\n\n6- Reshape the rune to the symbol of resistance\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n7- Reshape the rune to the symbol of capacity\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n8- Now create the object you want to make\n\n9-Bury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies of nature, such as a forest or grove\n\n10- After 5 days your  metal is ready and you can recover it.\n\nThe process is complete now, but don’t expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a process that needs experience.\n\n-Contact Aurea in Haelun’or if you have questions-\n\nOrichalcum\n\nWritten by Nienna\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepy Tales V1", "§b[Teen] Mikazuki Mantisuku", "~The Cursed Doll~\n\nThe story begins back in Elysium. A young woman found a doll laying in the dirt. Believing it to be a sign of good fortune she picked it up and took it home.  It was a small beat up porcelain doll with beautiful blue eyes.\n\nThe hair on the doll was something of an oddity. It was filled with strands that were slightly different shade of color and there were some bald patches. Not thinking much of it, she took it home and cleaned its face.\n\nRestoring the doll back to beauty. She sewed new dresses for it and cleaned it thoroughly. That night, she left the doll on a shelf. She went to bed happy and content. The moon slowly rose over the sky and a loud crash was heard.\n\nStartled, the woman bolted up. The wail of her infant daughter in the room brought her attention to the child. Slowly she lit a candle and made her way to the crib. To her shock, she spotted the doll next to the crib on the floor.\n\nShaking the strange feeling she got, she picked up her child and began singing a lullaby. After the child was asleep, she picked up the doll and headed back to the main room. She frowned seeing a vase that had been next to the doll was shattered.\n\nSetting the doll back up, she began cleaning up the shards. Tired and a bit on edge, she took it outside to dispose of later. It was then she looked up, seeing a very ominous red crescent moon.\n\nA cry broke the silence and the woman turned. Hurrying inside she froze in her tracks when the crying stopped. Straining to hear she heard no crying or cooing from her room. Candle in hand, she moved to the crib.\n\nHer scream of terror pierced the air when she looked upon the thing in her crib. Blood stained its clothes and a new patch of hair had been added.\n\nThe doll sat in the crib, no child in sight. Its blue eyes stained with blood as it stared into the eyes of the woman. Slowly they seemed to glow orange and a sinister look fell upon the doll as the room soon lit aflame.\n\nThe woman, too paralyzed to move, went up with the house. The neighbors heard her screams of pain and sorrow, tried to get in the house to save her but to no avail.\n\nWhen the blaze finally died out, the only thing found was bones of the mother, cradling the broken bones of an infant. The doll was found untouched on the shelf where the mother had originally placed it, its clothes singed slightly\n\nand its head of hair nearly full. Blood still stained the clothes. When the people returned to collect the things, the doll was no longer in the home.\n\nRumors are spread that a similar doll was found in the home of the duchess, not long before the orcs claimed her head. Through out the history since that first recorded event, the doll has appeared over and over, death and bloodshed following its wake.\n\nWhen the Fringe opened, the doll seemed to have disappeared, but who knows how long until it resurfaces.", ""),
        StaticBook("Liches.", "§bJakir Axem", "[ In eloquent writing the word Liches, is spelled out on the front cover of the book. The words striking and glowing a faint golden. Under it are the words. By Jakir Axem. It seems the writing glows brighter as you get closer to it. Inviting you in.]\n\n[What seems to be a man shrouded in black, and clad in a dark robe. Staring out at you, watching from under his hood. The hands of the man seem to be skeletal and he is flanked by two undead zombie like figures. The words under it.] \"A Lich.\"\n\n[For the rest of the book, the writing seems to return to normal black ink, with less time spent on the style of writing to help the reader to clearly see the writing and understand the lessons in the tome.]\n\nChapter one: Introduction.\n\nFor many years Liches have roamed the earth, we do not know where they first come from. But we do know they have been around for a very long time. I myself have killed a few, but they are not to be taken lightly.\n\nI was gifted with the power of gods, many who read this will not be, so I decided to make this guide so you may be able to fight them without the help of others. In this book you will find the information one might need as well as my own personal.\n\nexperience with these dark beings so you may better survive the next encounter you may have with them. It will only have the basic knowledge for we do not know it all, and do not wish others to try to copy in their dark arts.\n\nChapter two: The Lich.\n\nThe Lich is a creature made of dark magic, usually necromancy. At first they were thought  to of come from the dark power of Iblees. This is true, but those Liches are long passed, today Liches are made\n\nfrom necromancy and many a necromancer has tried to transcend into Lichdom. But you may wonder why there is not hundreds running around. It’s because the process is deadly and requires a lot of time and effort, and also the knowledge\n\non creation which has been lost to most. They use the power of necromancy to move a large portion of their life-force into an object referred to as a phylactery, this is their power supply, for it connects directly to the Lich in question.\n\nThe only problem being it could be hidden anywhere, so the permanent death of a Lich is unlikely but it also has a time it can live, due to the removal of life-force and the tether. The Lich will die in the end and it can’t stop it.\n\nChapter three: Combat.\n\nAs undead creatures, the main weakness of a Lich is gold. Gold is the bane of all known undead and as such. One should use golden weaponry over all else. Liches are unable to use necromancy due\n\nto the lost of most of their life-force and are also unable to access voidal or divine magic. But they are strong and smart. Bound to the will of the necromancer that created them but also free to do as they please otherwise.\n\nThey know fear and they will target the most dangerous person first. I myself have killed only a few, and they all have tried to kill me first. Only by me being ready was I able to stop them killing me and becoming their next victim.\n\nA few Liches are known for ranged weapons. Due to the lack of magic they use alchemy and bows. They are the cause of the Fringe Plague for it attacked me directly with a stronger version of the plague I was only just able to bat away in time.\n\nSome even wear armour, but they are made of bone and dead skin, so non golden or divine weapons are almost useless when fighting them. So be careful when facing them, they are not something one should take lightly and even more so if you are alone.\n\nChapter four: Personal experience \n\nI am a user of divine magic, and as such I have had to face them at their most deadly and worse. They tend to enlist the help of necromancers for extra help. As such I have\n\nI have had to fight the beasts of the necromancers and Liches. One being a monster made of young Mali children sewn together and made alive again with the vile magics. The lich that caused the Fringe Plague\n\nI had to remove after it infected most of Alras killing many and infecting many others. To which I had to remove the plague from. They are deadly creatures and some of the worst beings you can find, I hope you\n\nnever have to use the information found within this tome, for it is a true horror what these dark beasts will do to those who mealy get in it’s way, or if it feels like having fun.\n\nEpilogue: \n\nI Jakir Axem made this book to help others in fighting Liches, this book will no doubt be one of many, you can tell it is of my own design by the cover. . If it does not glow, then the book is just a copy.\n\nThank you for taking the time and reading this tome, I hope it helps you should the worse come to pass, and I hope that you never have to use it. This is part of the collection I shall be making on this subject,\n\nranging from as many dark beings I have come to fight, and find within the world. Thank you once again, and if we do meet out in the world, understand that what I do, I did by choice, and that even if you do face these things\n\n, you can move on and you are not alone.\n\n[Once again the fancy writing returns, the small signature of Jakir Axem written in golden glowing ink pulsing lightly at the end of the book.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Navitas II", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees.\n\nMalin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\n\n the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\n\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\n\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\n\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Meat Cuts", "§bJistuma", "Beef cuts:\n\nChunk (lower Neck)- Chuck Beef is located in the lower neck region of the animal. It is by far the best cut to be used in a stew or to be ground due  to its large amount of connective tissue\n\nBeef Rib (Ribs) – The Beef rib is part of the rib cage of the animal. It contains prime cuts such as the prime rib, as well as rib-eye. So far the best cooking methods I have found are cooking it on a grill or in an oven because of its tender nature.\n\nBrisket (lower front, underneath Chunk) – Brisket is another tough cut of beed, it is located directly under Chuck. It is best prepared as a pot roast, or covered in spices and smoked.\n\nPlate (Short Ribs) –The Plate is the part where both Short Ribs and Skirt Steak are made. Usually good for braising, they are also great if marinated and grilled. This cut also contains a lot of cartilage and care needs to be made cutting it.\n\nShank (Legs) – Shanks derive from the upper left portion of the animal. It is tough and not very edible unless braised and slow cooked.\n\nShort Loin (behind the Ribs)  – The Short Loin is a piece that is usually cut into steaks. It contains the Porterhouse, Tenderloin, and Strip Steak. All of them seem to be really tender and are derived from the rear part of the ribs.\n\nFlank (Utter Area)  – Flank is usually marinated before cooking and its preparation usually includes marinating and careful cooking. This cut is found near the utter and usually best when ground.\n\nRound (Rear end)  – Round is usually a tougher, but leaner piece of meat. It is best using moist heating methods such as stewing or pot roast. This part of the animal is where cubed meat traditionally derives from.\n\n\n\nPork Cuts\n\nPork Butt (shoulder)  – Despite the /unfortunate/ name, the Pork Butt is actually the upper shoulder. Although it is great for braising, it can also be made into sausages. Right above this is a fatty layer great for making lard.\n\nShoulder (Above the legs)  – The Shoulder is a pretty self explanatory name. This is another tough cut of meat however I find it good in making sausages as well. However it is usually cured or smoked.\n\nPork Loin (Ribcage)  – This part of the pig is mostly ribcage. It can be cut into Tenderloin located in the back and the whole Loin can be roasted or chopped into individual pieces. Like the Butt the Loin also has a fatty layer above for making lard.\n\nHam (actual Butt)  – The Ham is the part of the pig which is a deceptive name. This cut comes from the back of the pig and is saved for salted meats, and smoked ham. In addition the bottom portion, the Ham hock can be braised as opposed to curing.\n\nSide (Bottom)  – The side of a pig is where many can enjoy the simple breakfast treat of bacon. As well this part can be cut into steaks o made into pancetta, this is by far one of the tastiest parts of a pig and it takes much effort to avoid eating.\n\nSpare Rib (Under the Loin)  – The Spare rib is located where the breast connects to the ribs, it can be prepared by braising, slow cooking, or even grilling.\n\nJowl (Head)  – The Jowl is mostly used for sausages, as with any area this part is located. However it is not uncommon to see this part cured. Although not common it has been done.\n\nMeat Cuts\n\nUnknown author\nCoppied by Rosso\nCloud Temple of Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frosty Base Map", "§bZeliek", "[!] Within the book rests a rather detailed drawing of a map. Upon one side of the map is drawn a large city of sorts with the name \"Vanaheim.\" wrote across it. The other side has a large ruins of sorts ontop of a snowy mountain, with the words-\n\n\"Frost Witch Coven.\" writen across it. Between the two drawings is a path detailing the way in order to head to the ruins.\n\n((Coords X 129 Z -3742 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("2 VII II I", "§bOracle", "The Fall of Vormroth\n((Written by Spamshok for the Asulon Novella))\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n4th of Malin's Welcome -1443\n\nA thousand leagues from Aegis, and many hundred more from Asulon, over deserts ere great forests and across deep seas. Through old ruins, and great cities...You may\n\nfind what was once the great duchy of Vormroth, a powerful land, under the control of the ruthless Til'Esof dukes for hundreds of years.\nNow forty-three years ago, the duke and duchess had a child, a boy. Whom they called Issbaner,\n\nafter one of the great heroes of Vormroth. At the age of five, he had become a strong, vigorous and energetic child. He had dirty blond hair, and deep brown, almost red eyes. with a skin tanned by the blasting suns of his lands. He was soon\n\nput to private tutoring, and while being reticent about it. He learned quickly, and well. Even if he preffered watching the Zlàraks, or Warriors of his fathers armies train. Or even taking long awalks escorted by his guardian, enjoying the\n\nfeeling of freedom.\nOnce Issbaner turned ten, he had become a bright, intelligent boy, already possessing the ruthlessness needed, if you were to become a duke in these unforgiving lands. He was put to training with weapons, also\n\nkeeping on with his educations, and learning the duties of a duke. And yet, his parents worried, for they saw that he carried little intrest in learning and finding out about the duties of a duke, preferring to talk to war veterans about distant lands,\n\nwhen he was not training with his now favourite weapon; the saber. While he possesssed neither the technique, nor the strength to defeat a warrior, he could easily beat any of his companions in his training. And his parents were relieved, for a\n\nchild who was so skilled with the sword, coud only become a great duke, could he not?\nAnd yet, when Issbaner turned fifteen, disease stuck down his father, prematurely naming him duke, to replace his dying father. And to add\n\nto the problems, unrest shook the lands in these days, and talk of rebellion was heard, talk of uprising agaisnt the harsh dukes. And yet, Issbaner ignored these signs, preffering to spend his time on long hunting trips with his friends, or\n\nparties, where he shamelessly flirted with the young ladies of the court. For rare was the lady who would claim she did not find him unnatractive, with his semi-long blond hair, and muscular body.\n\nCHAPTER 2: REBELLION AND EXILE\n\nAnd when our young duke turned seventeen, the inevetible happened, following his uncaring and selfish leading of Vormroth, the citiens rebeled. Overhtrowing the\n\narmies in a matter of weeks by sheer weight of numbers, and marching on the capital, and the citadel where Issbaner, and the remains of the army still stood. Yet, Issbaner feared not, for this city was strong, and the rebels would\n\nsmash themselves agaisnt the walls. Of course, this was not counting the massive defection of the army, who opened the gates, letting the rebels through them, and into the city, leaving the city ripe for pillage. And pillage they did, raping, killing\n\nand burning at will. But it was not to be the end of Issbaner, no, for with his closest friend, and his mother, they fought their way through an ancient tunnel, towards the outside of the city. Alas, on their way out, he and his mother got seperated,\n\nand he was never to see her again.\nAfter an arduous and dangerous trip through old and abandonned taunnels, he escaped. But only three of his six friends came out with him...As he turned to look on last time upon the ruins of his\n\nbeloved city, he felt, mixed with sadness, relief....for a weight had left his shoulders, and he was free...Suddenly, a black crow landed on his shoulder, it looked at him mournfully, and his heart filled with dread. For it was the omen, the\n\nlegend...the black crow with hellish red eyes, the punisher of kings. Atlanar. The crow's claws dug deep into his shoulder, as it eyes seemed to glow brighter, \"You have been judges guilty...Duke of Vormroth, you have failed your task\"\n\nit's voice echoed in Issbaner's head. It gave a last cry, and flew off suddenly, leaving Issbaner staring at it with unseeing eyes, as his body slowly fell to the ground, soulless, his spirit taken by the punisher. He had failed hsi task, and Atlanar\n\nhad seen him as not fit to continue living, as such.", ""),
        StaticBook("°~Personal ~°", "Timelord_Lalve", "~.Personal Log.~\n\nLog of the Beard of Nature.\n\nRadagast Aiwendil Ernest Swampstone.\n\n-Greenbeard Ernest-\n\n~.Beards.~\n\nThe Order of the beard is in this world, to keep the balance between the living.\n- Elderbeard\n- Shadowbeard\n- Greybeard\n- Greenbeard\n- Redbeard\n- Whitebeard\n\n~.Elderbeard.~\n\nThe Elderbeard is the Father of the Order. \nThe most powerfull of us and the wisest.\n\nHis words are everytime the true.\n\n=Missing=\n\n~.Shadowbeard.~\n\nThe Shadowbeard represents the darkness. His task is, to keep the balance between the light and the darkness.\n\n=Dead=\n\n~.Greybeard.~\n\nThe great mage of the order. He represents the magic.\n\n=Dead=\n\n~.Greenbeard.~\n\nThe Greenbeard is the master of nature and represents it. His task is to keep balance in the nature.\n\n=Alive=\n\n~.Redbeard.~\n\nThe Keeper of the war. He supports the wars, he is the Beard of war.\n\n=Dead=\n\n~.Whitebeard.~\n\nThe oldest of us, he is the wisest. It is unknown where he is currently.\n\n=Missing/Dead=\n\n~.Nature.~\n\nI can't join the Druids, i can support them. There is no need for me to become a druid as i'm allready know the nature and how it's working.\n\n~.Time to move.~\n\nThe Order made there choice. We are moving into the mountains.\n\nA new place awaits us.\n\n~.Secret.~\n\nThe order made there choice. Our Order will be a secret. No one should know about our excistence.\nWe are going undercover...no one should know our tasks.\n\n~.Good Bye.~\n\nWe made the choice to move out, into the world. Every Beard will go to there chossen land. Our Grove is locked, the grove is no more.\nNo one knows, where it hides and that is good.\n\n~.New live.~\n\nIt's time for me to go undercover and hide my real personality under my third name.\nI'm Ernest...Ernest Swampstone.\n\n~.Alchemy.~\n\nAfter almost 10 years, we meet again. The order is still alive, everybody got a lot to tell. The Grand Elderbeard choosed me, to learn the Natural Alchemy.\n\n~.Alive.~\n\nThe Order is not dead, everybody moved under a new name. But we are still alive. We choosed, to meet every year in the mountains.\n\n~.Hunters.~\n\nSomeone found the informations about our Order. We need to move into a secret place to hide.\n\n~.The Death.~\n\nA sad day for the Order.\nWhitebeard is dead...killed by the Hunters...\n\nMay the nature be with you, Whitebeard.\n\n~.The Last Meeting.~\n\nOur Order is in danger, we are hunted. The Elderbeard decided about the Last Meeting.\nAfter it, we will never see again.\n\n~.Return.~\n\nThe Elderbeard returned to me and we got a conversation. I'm glad to see him again. It was a long time.\n\n~.No more.~\n\nGreybeard, Whitebeard, Shadowbeard, Redbeard...everybody is dead...everybody got killed...\n\nThe Elderbeard is missing...where is he? I feel alone. My plants are brown.\n\n~.The Last.~\n\nI...Greenbeard Aiwendil is the last of our Order. I will take the Order with me and i will still finish my task.\nI'm the Last one.\nThe Order is no more, but i will still be a Beard!\n\n~.Reborn.~\n\nMy name is Ernest, i'm not Aiwendil. I will work as a Healer and i will secretly help the nature. No one should know about my Real name. No one should know about the Beards. No one should ever destroy the nature.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNo one should damage the balance in the nature...\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe World is damaged...even if the Druids are trying...", ""),
        StaticBook("Grizzly Legend", "§bRyn Powell", "Legend of the Grizzly\n\nLong, long ago there were only creatures on the earth. There were birds, bears, deer, mice, everything but people. In this long ago time, all the animals spoke the same language.\n\nAnd just like some people nowadays, they played tricks on one another and made each other laugh. They also helped each other. So it was with all the animals.\n\nOne day in the winter when the lakes had frozen, but before the winter sleep, Bear was walking along the lakeshore. As he was walking, he came upon Otter sitting near a hole on the ice with a pile of fish.\n\n\"You've got a mighty big pile of fish there,\" Bear said. \"How did you get them fish?\"\n\nInstead of telling how he dove down into the water and caught the fish, Otter decided to trick Bear.\n\nYou see, back then Bear had a very long bushy tail. He was very proud of his tail, and all the animals knew it.\n\n\"The way I catch my fish is by putting my tail in this ice hole,\"\n\nOtter explained. \"I wiggle it around once in a while so the fish see it. When a fish bites onto my tail, I quickly pull it up and out of the water.\"\n\n\"That sure is an easy way to catch fish,\" Bear said. \"Do you mind if I use your fishing hole?\"\n\nOtter, laughing behind the Bear's back, said, \"I have enough fish. Use my fishing hole as long as you like.\"\n\nThen Otter picked up his fish and walked away. Bear carefully poked his tail into the ice hole and waited. He waited and waited. Once in a while he'd wiggle his tail so the fish could see it.\n\nBear waited until the sun began to set, but not one fish even nibbled at his tail. At last, he decided to go home, but when he tried to stand up, his tail had frozen into the ice! He couldn't move!\n\nHe pulled and pulled at his tail, but it was stuck tight. Finally, he pulled with all of his strength and ripped off half his tail!\n\nNow you know why the Bear has a short tail, and remember . . .\n\nDon't always believe what people tell you!\n\n((Adapted from a real Native American legend.))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bards Ellis", "§bDread Knight Verin", "The Bards\n              Of \n             Ellis \n\n\n\nBy Verin Etitlan\n    Edemah Etitlan\n    Eiheiu Darky\n\n\"There once was a bard,\nDashing and daring,\nThe queens pants he did start to mangle, and they found him, and threw him to shambles.\n\nOut on the floor, cold as ice, his hair scratched and withered like lice --\n\nThat lonely bard, he did song. Of a place to the east, where no men could ying.\n\nThe druids, his home he did fine, and once more did this lonely bard find; \n\nHe took the archdruids pants and threw them a mangle,--\n\nAnd there they found him, and threw him to shambles!\"\n- Verin Etitlan.\n   Kalos/Anthos\n\nThe Will of God:\n\"The man looked down in fond reminiscance at the man he once knew. His dagger upraised in firm defiance, astrew its' blades handle, and he spoke, like the angry vassal of the messiah. \"You. Are. Done.\" The blade plunged down, slamming int\n\no the mans heart, and the ether came for him.\"\n  Edemah Etitlan\n     Kalos\n\nThe End:\n\"The armored man looked down to his creation, to its' mangled body. Its' child of any other, and it worked. Its' firm machinations elliciting no response, the ether calling out, trying as it would to grasp the man, to give him the end..unable.\n\nHe became his son, in all but name. His father his lord, forever in vein. His own son gone, lost to the ether he hoped for each day, he wishes he could go there, one day.\"\n   Unknown.\n     Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. Notice", "§bRobrecht \"Umbridge\" Crast", "Introduction Notice:\nBecoming familiar with your comrades is essential. \n\nIntroduce yourself to three other Brigade Members.\n\nReport back to Robrecht upon completion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human Babies", "§bRosso", "Where do human babies come from?\n\nThe mother and father or the soon to be parents, shag a lot until the woman is pregnant. Human shag so much, sometimes the father is not even the husband of the mother. They shag everywhere they can, in a bar, on their home, in other’s home, in a brothel,\n\noutside, and so forth.\n\nWhen a woman gets pregnant, it takes 9 seeds for the baby to be born in the most VILE of experiences for the woman, where it seems like the Nether has been opened in their wombs, and rivers of blood and slime\n\nflow from it, until a bloody crying newborn comes out.\n\nEven those men that have been in the Nether itself, get disgusted by the sight that is the human birth.\n\nWhere do Human babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Pricing", "§bAudrey Caillot", "~Arcana & Oddities!~\n       ~Pricing~\n*Leather Wine Skin; 50 Mina\n*Crystal Flower; 75 Mina\n*Runic Key; 75 Mina\n*Ivory Tusk; 125 Mina\n*Wooden Cane; 125 Mina\n*Elven Music Box; 150 Mina\n\n*Druidic Flute; 150 Mina\n*Wyvern's Pocketwatch; 300 Mina\n*Maiden's Reprieve; 400 Mina", ""),
        StaticBook("1 III III I", "§bOracle", "The Ancient Elves by Aedan\nIrba 12th of the Second Seed, 1314 Aegis\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nOnce upon a time, long before the beginning of written history, the lands of the wilderness were inhabited by a single race: The Ancient Elves. This race was the first to live in the lands of Aegis. They built incredible structures in the\n\nlands of The Niben bay, and it's sorroundings. :: :: The Niben bay was a large body of water lying in The Niben Basin, largely east of the city of Hawkhaven. It lies across the Niben River, splitting it into two parts, and so is technically a lake\n\nrather than a bay. :: :: :: The Niben was once ocuppied by their capital: Garlas Malathar, also known as Nirn Weye vas Cyrod: The White Gold City. :: :: ::This city was, according to the ancient books, the biggest capital in Aegis. The city was filled\n\nwith complex tunnels and districts, each district with different ambience. They say you could feel one with the city, it was filled with statues of nature, exotic birds and wonderful animals... Including...Dragons. :: :: ::The Ancient Elves learned how\n\nto befriend a Dragon, instead of taming them like most races did. They knew that friendship was stronger than any force in the world. This Dragons shared their knowledge with them, they showed them the basics of energy manipulation that are still used\n\nnow-a-days. :: :: ::They soon found how to store energy in crystals and use them for many things. They used them to power their entire civilization, giving power and light to their cities. :: :: :: One day, a new Dragonlord took power of the\n\nempire. His name was Akron. He was foolish and always wished to have more power. He hated other races and considered them inferior. He soon tried to power stronger crystals for war. The Dragons refused and prevented him from doing so. :: :: ::\n\nAkron then called upon the forces of Iblees to drain the dragons' power. The dragons, foreseeing their end, created the varla stone and powered it with The Dragonfires, sealing the gates to The Nether, and killing themselves... :: :: ::Some dragons\n\nremained as statues, petrified, and waiting to be awakened. They will wake up when the right time comes. :: :: ::After the beginning of the First Era, Akron began to damage nature and attempted to enslave other races. This marked the beginning of the\n\nGreat War wich lasted decades. :: :: :: Akron was finally defeated. To the fall of their Empire, humans took the power of the crystals. Their power turned them blind and foolish. They began to kill all survivors of The Ancient Elves and burned their\n\ncities to the ground. Some of them managed to escape and survived. :: :: ::Many kings tried to restore their old glory but failed. Without the power of The Dragonfires, they weren't able to do such thing. :: :: ::They say that if you look closely to the\n\nsunrise, you can still see the ruins of Garlas Malathar, waiting to be discovered, and raised once again... :: :: ::-Aedan, Dragonlord of The Last Ancient Elves. :: :: Irba, 12th of the Second Seed, 1314.", ""),
        StaticBook("1 IV I I", "§bOracle", "Through The Teeth of Hell\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of The Grand Harvest -1443\n\nHarold Fergensun, and Orc, was walking down a stone road. Pretending he was innocent. You see, Harold was a robber, rapist, murderer, just to name a few. Then...... he was shot by gaurds. Arrow in his back, Harold dropped to his knees, and died.\n\nSwirling shapes and figures rushed around him. He landed, in the stone of Hell. Crying, yelling, death, all 'round. He saw above him the teeth of hell. He started climbing, and saw his friend Lucas, burning , pleading for him to help. But he said \"I\n\ncannot help\". He climbed further. He then saw his father, begging for salvation. Harold again says, I cannot help. He climbs almost to the top. ALMOST THERE AND- his wife. His dead wife. \"Help me Harold, I love you!\" Harold couldnt resis t. \"I love you\n\ntoo but.....\" he looked down. \"I must help you all\" He drags all the earlier mentioned friends through the teeth of hell. He asks them, \"Why were you there?\" They said \"Because of you....\". He told them he was sorry, and knew what to do. He jumped back\n\nin. He saved his friends from hell, and sacrificed himself. He the heard the voice of God calling him up while he was grinding in the teeth of Hell. God said \"You have sacrificed yourself for others. You are redeemed\" He was saved from the Nether and\n\nbrought up to heaven. There he saw the people he just rescued, and many more. The Cathaldus family the Harronis family, and many more. He was at peace with God, and Aegis. THE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("Horen's 'Swamp'", "§bDaniel 'Vince' Ward", "There once was a wee lil' lass named Emporer Horen! His demease was rather petty so he stooped low, low, low. He set his eyes upon the jewel of the world, Shreck's Swamp. With a bold strut he rapped upon Duloc's gates, Shreck's castle, and demanded he\n\nopen the gates and swear fealty. Shreck peered down, offering him a 'bro you crazy af' look before descending. Huffing and puffing, he blew his own gates right off then kicked Horen's head right off. Literally. Before it hit the ground his corpse had been\n\nmutilated with Shreck's strong orkish hands to such a degree it looked like a heap of onions. That is the story of how Horen the swamp thief lost his life to Swampgoth Shreck'Lak.\n\n\n\n\ns w a m p", ""),
        StaticBook("Dornishman's Wif", "§bDirk Novokain", "The Dornishman's wife was as fair as the sun,\nand her kisses were warmer than spring.\n\nBut the Dornishman's blade was made of black steel,\nand its kiss was a terrible thing.\n\nThe Dornishman's wife would sing as she bathed,\nin a voice that was sweet as a peach.\n\nBut the Dornishman's blade had a song of its own,\nand a bite sharp and cold as a leech.\n\nAs he lay on the ground with the darkness around,\nand the taste of his blood on his tongue.\n\nHis brothers knelt by him and prayed him a prayer,\nand he smiled and he laughed and he sung.\n\n\"Brothers, oh brothers, my days here are done,\nthe Dornishman's taken my life,\n\nBut what does it matter, for all men must die,\nand I've tasted the Dornishman's wife!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Ciw Lenniel", "§bLelien", "Ciw Lenniel\n\n      by Unknown\n\nNarn ito ciw kae Malii’leh\nNarn ito ciw kae Malii’leh\n\nEl’asul karinah marn’oem\nNarn ito ciw kae Malii’leh\n\nKer ito par’karinah\nNarn ito ciw kae Malii’leh\n\nCiw’sulier hileia’ehya wyn\nCiw’sulier ayla’marn lye\n\nCiw Malii", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oussana", "§bSeraphine Drake-Flormai", "The Dark Elves have been born an enigma, since their very first steps into this realm. They’re various and varied in both body and mindset. In them is the potential of the most tenacious warrior or wisest of seers.\n\nTheir eyes can be of crimson fire, or sapphire water. Among these dark skinned sons and daughters of Malin are the Oussanas.\n\nThe Oussana family describe the birth of the dark elves as part of the first insurrection against Iblees. Their tale of their origin provides an in-depth insight into their beliefs and mannerism, even though the tale is left as simply a myth or\n\nstory among themselves  During this first war between benevolence and a absolute evil, Malin needed children who would have more will and might than his first group of children, the wood elves, in order to decimate the servants of iblees.\n\nHe needed children who can handle the atrocities of war and the evils Iblees could deal. To create this chidl, he reached up into the night sky and took parts of the darkness itself, leaving stars and celestial bodies in place of the darkness he took.\n\nHe then reached into the ground and took a strong, sturdy root from a tree. He then cut the palm of his hand, allowing blood to pool in the center. When he combined himself, nature, and darkness he created the first Dark Elf, a creature born for conflict.\n\nAfter the war, the Dark Elves began to look for where they would dwell. Some sought refuge with their wood elven brothers in what would be malinor while others looked to the roots of trees for their home, far from other elves.\n\nAmong the ones who sought their own destiny aside from their brothers were the Oussanas.\n\nAppearance\n\nAt the adulthood of an Oussana their eyes are typically solid black; however, at birth their eyes are a lighter blue-red color. As they age, the dual blue-red eye color begins to darken until their body fully matures at twenty.\n\nlthough in youth it usually starts off as the dual color, it's possible to see a set of red or blue eyes to begin with At twenty years old, their eyes stop darkening and remain black while the whites of their eyes turn into a light grey color.\n\nHowever, the eye color can take more than twenty years to darken, although it is rare. The typical skin color of an Oussana is a Darker Grey, a shale color. However, if they diverge from the typical, they tend to be paler than more charcoal.\n\nTheir hair is always of long, straight, and white\n\nCustoms\n \nGender Roles\n\nAmong the Oussanas there is no such thing as a gender role. The females are taught the exact same things as any male in the family. A child, if raised by an Oussana, will experience\n\nno gender socialisation that distinguishes male and female. They are both expected to meet the same expectations throughout their life and will not held back because of gender.\n\nClothing\n\nTo express strength, family members will wear less clothing. Like most elves, they do not see a lack of clothing being extremely strange or scandelous. This is only to express physical dominance and prowess.\n\nA family member will believe that both clothing and armor are for individuals who are hiding a particular weakness.  However, they’re not running around in underwear either. They will wear what an environment requires them to wear.\n\nYet when an Oussana shows skin, it’s not meant to be a means of attracting others, it’s how they express their strength.\n\nTattoos\n \nOften times, accomplishments and achievements throughout a family member’s life are marked on their skin in the form of a tattoo. Before in Aegis, this tradition was required,\n\nyet since the disunion of the Oussana it’s a more of a choice, although strongly suggested. To represent these events, a symbol should be designed by  the one desiring the tattoo that would provide insight to the event. If a tattoo is\n\ngiven yet it carries no meaning, it’s often celtic in design. At the age of ten, an Oussana is required to get a tattoo on their skin. It’s often given given by one of the parents. The child however, chooses who gives them the tattoo and where the\n\ntattoo will go. Consciousness at the time of the marking is not required, given that it’s fairly painful.  This tattoo is of the family seal which is a  triquetra(celtic knot) with a moon in the center. One way an Oussana shows true devotion\n\nto a lover is marking themselves with a tattoo. This is only for an individual that has been decided to spend the rest of their near-immortal elfen life with. If there is any doubt, an Oussana raised by their traditions\n\nwill not mark themselves to the other. Symbols engraved onto their body can only be the truth, they will not willingly write a lie on their chest.\n\nValues\n \nDominance and strength:\n\nOussana both male and female are raised to believe they were created to be the strongest . They do not fear flaunting their strength and if given\n\nthe chance they will go to extreme lengths to show dominace. At a very young age, children are taught to fight, usually with swords, to achieve this strength. They are raised to believe the only way to be successful in life is to be feared.\n\nA good example of this would be how animals act when asserting dominance. If challenged they try to prove themselves better. Nearly at all times they would be flaunting their strength, which is the reason for them often having less\n\nlothing when compared to your average elf. Since they enforce strength so adamantly, the exact opposite, weakness, is despised. Oussana were raised to surround themselves around strong individuals and cast away the weak. In the past,\n\nthose that were weak among the family were cast out to malinor to live among the weaker elves. An Oussana will go to any  lengths to not appear weak.\n\nBeauty:\n\nThe idea of perfection is engraved into every child’s mind; however, it’s not just the perfection of physical strength that is sought after. Beauty and maintaining beauty is almost as highly pressed as ones ability in combat.\n\nTechniques and secrets in beautifying both the male and female body is passed down, generation by generation. In the past, if an Oussana did not at least try to maintain physical beauty they would of been deemed lazy and\n\ncould've been cast out from the family because they’re lazy.\n\nOussana Code of Honor\n\n*Oussana protect the weak and do not bring harm to them.\n*The Oussana value family, loyal to the members of their clan above others.\n*The Oussana do not bow to those inferior, but bend.\n\n*The Oussana do not allow Pride to be destroyed by minor things.\n*The Oussana are proud, strong and honorable at all times.\n*The Oussana do not tolerate weakness in the family.\n\n*To show emotion is not weakness, but to control it shows strength.", ""),
        StaticBook("Refugee's Legacy", "§bAeran", "With each day it becomes increasingly clear that the packed ice and snow between us and the world will not be passed. \n\nTo think, we escaped the claws and teeth of a million monsters only to die in the halls of our refuge, with nothing to blame but\n\nthe freezing winds.\n\nTal'ei is preparing the last of our supplies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bElluna Koortova", "Treating Wounds\n  \n    By Anonymous\n\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet’s start using steps,\n\n\nStep I - Cleaning the Wound\n\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. Of course you need to wash the dirt out\n\nfirst should it have dirt in it. Remember to clean thoroughly!\n\n\nStep II -  Suturing the Wound\n\nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread. Sounds easy right? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these.. Let’s call them sub steps.\n\n\nSub Step I - Heating the Needle\n\nYou need to do that to burn away any remaining illness covering the needle, should it have had any.\n\nSub Step II - Clean the Thread\n\nYou surely need to do so, as you do not want a single speck dirt in your wound!\n\nSub Step III - Starting the Suture\n\nYou start at, well, the start of the gash or deep wound. (Warning! this does NOT apply for small wounds!)\n\nYou then sew it closed like you’re sewing a tear in a rag, a messy and bloody rag that screams like a little girl. Nonetheless, a rag. \n\nSub Step IV - Bandaging the Wound\n\nA bandage could be just about anything,\n\nan old rag (As long as it's clean, obviously!), bed sheets, anything of cloth material. Then you simply wrap it around the wound. Done!\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection before or after you’ve gone through this process you'll be\n\nbetter off cutting off the leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("Betraying God", "§bGeoboy66", "His children are unruly.\n\nThe creator, our binder, our conciever. The tales of the creator are not ones false, for it is him that radiates power.  Some see it as a boon, and others see it as a plague.  But one group of thieves see it as a\n\ngem to be stolen.\n\nThey call themselves the 'clerics'.  It is this myth in which you have been guided astray.  For a cleric is not what you think it is, it is not a vanquisher of evil and slayer of foul beasts.  It is a thief, a thief of the highest tier.\n\nThere are many things that this could mean, however only one rings true.  The creator does not grant these 'clerics' his holy might as a boon to bask in, or a tool to use.  No, they take it from him, from his open palms the grasp.  They steal from god.\n\nThe common eye does not percieve this.  It goes on with its life without suspecting a thing.  Exactly what they wish.  The are the essence of corruption, wielding a weapon of purity.    This act of defiance to their creator angered him, infuriated him.\n\nYet god was powerless.\nHe had been sapped and drained of his power from clerics around the world for hundreds of years, if not thousands and this weakened him.  The creator could not retaliate personally.\nHe could not fight back.\n\nThen he did what the creator did best.  He created.  Minions on the battlefield, chess pieces on the board.  Pawns for his use.\nHe created a new power to gift to his subjects, one that would free him from the corrupting shackles of foul clerics.\n\nHe created necromancy.\nThe touch of life and death was brought upon the world, the ability to weave the forces of life at ones will.  They were to be done responsibly, and not in a terroristic fashion.  These new fighters were peacekeepers.\n\nThey held the secrets of the dead and were sworn to protect them from those that would misuse them.  Most importantly though, they were created to vanquish the thieves that put thorns in the creators side.  Though legend portrays them as being villains...\n\nThose that keep the secrets of the dead once acted heroicly to purge the blight of our god.  They would do so again, and some still do.   \n\nToday's views are terribly twisted indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("1 IV III I", "§bOracle", "Paragon Lefor\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nLefor was born into a normal dwarven family. His Father worked in the mines, His mother at home. Lefor Was raised in the mines as he helped his father there from a young age. When he came of age Lefor told his father he wanted\n\nto be more than a miner ,he wanted to server his king by joining the army. Lefor's father was stubborn but eventually let Lefor join a training camp, sending him off with the family armor and axe. Lefor had a hard time at the camp, he was smaller than\n\nmany of the others but he strived to be the best, and so he did after much hard work he finished training and was made sergeant of the new battalion. :: Before the beginning of the Great War between the Orcs and Dwarves tensions where high and\n\nthere where many skirmishes between both races. The Orcs where bloodthirsty and hungry for land and the Dwarves had expanded very close to the orcish border. Neither the Warlords of the Orcs or the High council of the Dwarves could maintain peace\n\nand so the war began. In the early stages of the war dwarven losses where high and they slowly retreated. It was at the small village of Kas-Grit that Lefor and his men were stationed to protect the villages whilst they gathered their items in\n\npreparation to seek refuge in the Capital. On the final day before they where to head to the capital a great horde of orcs attacked, the villages fled in panic and Lefor and his men fought their best to contain the great horde but the orcs where to many\n\nand lefor gave orders to retreat and protect the villagers. Lefor however did not leave he told his men that he was going to hold back the orcs as long as he was able. The orcs attacked again and again but Lefor kept them at bay and so he slew many\n\norcs fighting them in the narrow alley ways of the village. However Lefor finally tired and was cut down by the orcs and his head put apon a spike. :: That day Lefor saved many dwarves and because of his bravery the king and council made him a\n\nparagon. To be worshipped along with the stones of the earth. Lefor's family were made nobles and his bloodline still survives in many dwarves. Lefor is seen as the incartation of bravery, sacrafice and warrior-hood . :: Even today many\n\nwarriors pray to Lefor before battle . So is the story of Paragon Lefor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gay shit", "§bGiovanni 'Gino' Giordano", "12/29:§0\n§0-1 set iron armor§0\n§0-320 arrows§0\n§0-32 coal§0\n§0-2 swords§0\n§0-1 battleaxe§0\n§0-128 oak logs§0\n§0\n§0Estimate: ~400 minas total, 280 minas to you§0\n§0\n§0Karl Klargus", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic The Basics", "ventus2", "Magic The basics\n\nMagic is the art of using magical energies from the void and bringing them to life, forming them into what most people call spells or magic. Now this book shall state the very basics of magic. What the energy is and some other facts\n\n     Magical Energy\n\nMagical energy or in other words “Mana” is what mages use to perform their spells, How mana is found is through the void, the void is the realm that supports all mana inside, There is a everlasting amount of mana inside the void,\n\n         The Void\n\nThe void is everything and nothing at the same time, An everlasting is inside the void and is where mages connect to perform their spells, Connecting to the void is a process that is easy in a sense but at the –\n\nSame time extremely dangerous, and the reason for this is being that the mana inside the void is what we call stamina, or in other words life energy, The main way of connecting to the void is through one’s mind, And how to do this? One must find out for-\n\nThemselves, Also considering that mana is life energy there may or not be a way for a mage to use this in order to grant themselves eternal life, But I leave that to you as well as how to perform spells and use mana.\n\n-Corvo", ""),
        StaticBook("1 II I I", "§bOracle", "The Legend of Lady Sophia\nDiscovered and Recovered by Talithia\nProtected by the Monks of Asulon\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of The Grand Harvest -1443\n\nOn the island called Silva Insula*, there is a legend** of a Sainted woman named Sophie...and a dark evil.\nIt all began when people who lived small societies near the Lucky Goblin Inn began to go missing.\n\nThey would leave the inn, or step out of their homes for a minute and just vanish, never to be seen again. Then people noticed that some of the others were slowly changing, becoming wilder and more aggressive, or just insane.\n\nPeople became frightened and began to withdraw from each other, joining with their neighbors in an effort to stay safe. Lady Sophie and her son Trevor were among those who sought shelter and safety at the inn.\n\nAround that time creatures began to appear around the town. No two descriptions were ever the same, but most could agree on their glowing eyes and how they seemed to fade into the darkness around them when you looked at them.\n\nThen Trevor went insane overnight. He began to kill his friends and neighbors. People from the small societies banded together and tried many ways to stop him, but, alas, the only way for his terror to end was by his death.\n\nOn the day he was buried, the Lady Sophie sat all day by her beloved son's grave, neither eating nor speaking to any who came by to offer her their condolences. The remaining people gathered at the Inn to wait for her return.\n\nBy the time night fell, a dwarf named Brokk became concerned for her and went to the grave to check on her. As he approached the grave, Lady Sophie stood up and walked out into the misty forest. Brokk tried to follow her but quickly lost\n\nher and turned to go back to the inn. That's when the scream pierced through the fog and darkness. No one could find the words to describe that unearthly, chill inducing scream. Many recalled grabbing their heads from the pain as the scream ripped\n\nthroughout their brains. When the scream ended, Brokk went in the direction Lady Sophie went in, and found her unconscious on the ground. He picked her up in his arms and took her back to the inn.\nAs the sun banished the darkness,\n\nLady Sophie woke once and tried to tell Brokk what happened. She had found the source of the evil plaguing them and went to confront it. The scream that had rent the air had come from this evil as she defeated it. **** She only had time to\n\nmention that it would never return before she closed her eyes and passed into that unknown realm we call death. As she died, all the others who had been slipping into madness, became whole once more. No one else disappeared after that. Life went\n\nback to normal for the people of Silva Insula. They moved closer to the inn and resurrected a church in her honor; it still stands to this day watching over her beloved town.\nAlthough none knew what actually happened that night, there is\n\none theory that many in the town seemed accept as fact. They said that Lady Sophie, after grieving for her loss so deeply, became determined that no one else should suffer her fate. It is whispered that her will and determinations\n\nwas so strong, that she defeated the evil with her mind alone. And some even whisper that the evil that she faced was somehow connected to the enders that plague Asulon now.\nBut perhaps the most disturbing thing of all is the rumors of\n\nnoises coming from the graveyard late at night and the shadow that rises from Trevor's grave and prowls around the town looking for a new victim.\n\n-footnotes-\n*Silva Insula is known for the Lucky Goblin's Inn and it's delicious Red Rum, which is no longer made. There are several abandoned villages near Silva Insula that date back to the events described in this legend\n\n**The tale has been passed from a local Dwarf named Brokk Wayland MacGowan to his brother Ferron Andvare MacGowan and the townspeople who were left by the end.\n*** Brokk Wayland MacGowan is the builder and original owner of the\n\nLucky Goblin Inn.He is considered to be the founder of Silva Insula and all it stands for.\n****The means to defeating this unknown evil was either lost or Lady Sophie never said\nwhat she did to defeat it.", ""),
        StaticBook("1 III II I", "§bOracle", "The Dark Brotherhood\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nIntroduction :: Many Aegeans now are sheltered. They know nothing of this world and what is happening. For instance,today I saw the Temple of Aegis in trouble. Slimes had started a siege on recently\n\nressurected players,and sending them back to the Crypt. It was mayhem. And what troubles me even more,as a traveler,is that very few people know about the Dark Brotherhood. :: This evil guild is intent on the destruction of this world's\n\ninhabitants. And needs to be stopped at all costs. This is why I write this book,so that you may learn to defend yourself against this,this taint... Let me begin on the history of this guild. :: The History of the Brotherhood :: It is said they started\n\noff as...well...assasins with perfectly harmless intentions. This soon changed with the arrival of one known only as \"The Stranger\" . This \"Stranger\" as he is known,is responsible for the deaths of many,and is rumored to be the Grand Master of the\n\nguild. It has been this way for many years now. If his true identity is found,report it to me immediately! It must be shared! :: The Guild Itself :: The Guild is mostly assasins,with a few bandits mixed in. This makes it hard to track down\n\nmembers,commonly referred to as \"Danalus'\". These apear to be the average rank,with half the guild seemingly comprised of it.. . There is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached\n\nthis rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank.Only higher is the \"unique\" ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who have proven their worth to the Grand Master, lesser councel and High Councillor. This is the Silencer rank. This\n\nrank is only availible to those select few,and it is limited space. How it works is each high ranking member has one or two silencers,who carry out personal contracts for the high ranking members. There is one more rank within the\n\nBrotherhood,and it is by far the most terrifying of the assasin ranks.It is \"Iblees Champion\",a seemingly obscure term used to describe the best member. It terrifies me,but thankfully,there is not a Champion yet. :: High Ranks :: The\n\nhighest ranks availible are now closed it seems. These are namely the Lesser councel,High Councillor and Grand Master.", ""),
        StaticBook("2 V II I", "§bOracle", "Journal of a Philosopher I; Elindor's Travels\nI'm leaving Laurelin. I've spent my life amidst these majestical trees in uninterrupted solitude, but I sense a yearning that I don't understand. There's trouble in Aegis\n\nand in all my years Iremain barely aware of it. Tomorrow I shall embark on a journey of discovery. I'm not sure whyI'll be keeping a journal, perhaps I'll meet an untimely end and my head will end up on a pike outside Krugmar.\n\nThis way someone might know who I was.\nJournal of a Philosopher II; Elindor's Travels\nI journeyed towards Oren and come upon a small city outside Alras. It was here in Kramoroe that I spent days absorbed in the dusty old pages of a towering\n\nlibrary. I never saw a warden, but I'm sure that there would be one, for the place was well kept and the books, vast in numbers though they were, were organised. I felt a presence. For the first time since leaving Malinor I forgot\n\nabout my desire to learn my own history and sensed the forthcoming of something bigger. We were too sheltered in Laurelin to realise how far Iblees had spread. We were too foolish. I read journals that made me shiver and old\n\nparchments that illustrated the same heinous shadow which brought back my undercooked porkchop sandwich. The fate of Aegis hangs in the balance of a war that only days ago I wasn't even fully aware of. I've no idea the role I have to\n\nplay, but I know I must do something.\nJournal of a Philosopher III; Elindor's Travels\nI met an ascended in the gates of Alkhazar. She was well learned and spoke with a gentle tongue, yet went to great measure to\n\nanswer my queries. Of course I was delighted to siphon a bounty of knowledge and wisdom, but I am just an Elf, and a wanderer at that. I had no idea of her importance until I entered the Followers of Aeriel library and read\n\nof her holy bloodline. This meeting has got me thinking more about God. His servant's presence is here in Aegis, both Good and Evil, as is their power.\nJournal of a Philosopher IV; Elindor's Travels\nI sit in Oren's castle library\n\nsurrounded by magnificent rows of books. There's floor after floor of ancient tomes, kingdom records and glimpses of history. I could spend a year here, but I know that I must not. For whatever purpose the Creator God sent me on this mission\n\nI must be moving forward. There is more to be discovered! I'm beginning to wonder if I have been called to be a messenger. Surely far be it from me for such an important mission, for who would be MY audience? The elves wouldn't\n\nheed my word, and men seem disinterested in the sayings of an elf, now that they have the ascended walking among them. The orcs seem ready to fight, for what cause they couldn't care less, and I haven't met the acquaintance of\n\nmany dwarves, but as I understand it they aren't on the friendliest of terms with us 'tall ears'. Still, there is a bigger picture in all this, I just cannot fathom it.\nJournal of a Philosopher V; Elindor's Travels\nThis entry may\n\nconsist entirely of my thoughts, but I've been wondering... The Ascended do the\nwork of Aeriel, who is an Aengul and an immortal creature that serves God. So in balance the Undead do the work of Iblees, who is a Daemon and likewise immortal subject\n\nof God. With the assumption that Aegis is a trial period for us mortals to pick a side before our lives end, then we would be taken out of our mortal bodies to be made another form. Does this mean that the Undead, who are in a sense immortal,\n\nhave chosen their side and moved on? Given the choice of being Undead for an eternity or absolutely anything else, I don't think any amount of tempting power could have me settle for wandering around Aegis slowly disintegrating. But what if\n\nI'm seeing it wrong? Perhaos they have received an enlightenment that they desire to share with us mortals. An enlightenment that stinks of rotting flesh and hungers to tear muscles from bone and\n\nbe drenched in warm blood. I think I should seek a druid.\nJournal of a Philosopher VI; Elindor's Travels\nThe modern druids were of little assistance. They seem now to be a reflection of their ancient power. They\n\ndesire to protect this world but harbor little soncern that it may all burn in a\nNether fire. They also don't beleive that God formed Aegis but that it was the work of wizards and druids. I came with questions of spirituality and our theologies were\n\nfar too disconnected to formulate any answers.\nJournal of a Philosopher VII; Elindor's Travels\nThe Imperial Coalition will be another indepent force fighting valiantly on our frontlines. I spoke with their\n\ncommander, a strong man who seems weary of battle but honourable enough to lead the charge again. I realise from our conversation that there are few who are attempting to understand this battle in a deeper sense, and fewer\n\nstill who have considered God's perspective. They are but men and they will more hastily pick sides than come to diplomatic reasoning with something they deem a threat. The preservation of Aegis needs them, just as it needs\n\nthe Druids, just as it needs the rain. It troubles me that so many good people are lost against a struggle that we don't comprehend.\nJournal of a Philosopher VIII; Elindor's Travels\nWhile praying today something dawned\n\non me. It is so simple to question God in all this, but what if the knowledge that we lack is in our understanding of suffering? I haven't seen the devastation of the North through my own eyes, so I should probably hold my tongue; however, what if\n\nsuffering is just another mortal emotion, like content or anguish. It is nothing more than our response which we bare for just a time and then continue along towards our purpose. I fear that there is no question that I\n\nwould not want to discover the answer to more than 'what is suffering?' But I know that I will find an answer, and it will shatter my heart.\nJournal of a Philosopher IX; Elindor's Travels\nMy insides churn at this Evil that pits brother against\n\nbrother, harbors such hatred of love and shatters friendhsips. A father having to drive a sword into his own son. How can this be in the name of God? If this is an end on the path that is our lives, what God could be in\n\nsuch a thing? I saw a strong and compassionate elf turn on his lifelong friend and his lover at the hand of the corruption of a tormented soul from Nether. But the turned one did show a weakness. Not as far as compassion, but he\n\nwas not the bloodthirsty animal I expected. The Tainted have purpose and drive, each seeming to follow their own will but still under Iblees' command. It revealed to me many things, but above all that I am not ready to face the horrors\n\nthat make their way across Aegis.\nJournal of a Philosopher X; Elindor's Travels\nToday I am beginning my journey through the North. In search of what, I know not. I expect that when I find my answer it will be staring me in the face. I have\n\nstopped for the night in Al'Khazar. I thought it wise to get off these roads while the sun was hid, but inside Oren's walls is more dangerous than the open road. Lightning crashes down within the city igniting thatch rooves, and even\n\npeople, ablaze. All the while they fight between themselves. The old King\nSheffield's followers may start a revolt against Ponpao's son, all the while the Undead army encamps the nation's walls. A seperate Aegis is a doomed one.\n\nJournal of a Philosopher XI; Elindor's Travels\nI journeyed to Crimson Vale only to find an abandoned town. As I made my way back to the road I was stopped by an Ascended with maroon stripes. This came as a confusion as the Ascended\n\nfort lies outside of Crimson Vale and I had heard tale that the town was under Iblees' control. The man was willing to speak with me and was willing to speak with me and answered many of my queries about the war. But as he illustrated the\n\nimpending doom of Aegis his voice grew deeper and I noticed a horrible stink of rotting burnt flesh. Realising that he could no longer remain hidden, the man removed his robes and I saw that he carried no\n\nAengul blood but the stain of the Nether. He introduced himself as Wargoth and I saw that he was once a man, now only a fowl and corrupted worshipper of Iblees. Wargoth lead me to some kind of dungeon under Crimson Vale with a\n\nfew rooms intentionally constructed in the art of killing a man. After much heated conversation about God, power and liberated knowledge that resulted in a philosophical stalemate, he commanded me to\n\npick a room. I knew that his promised 'path to enlightenment' harbored dire consequences for my ability to share this knowledge, so tempted though I was to learn the secrets of the Nether and Iblees'\n\ntrue form, I lowered my head to accept my death. There are many ways to discover the universe and all its knowledge, but none of those paths can be forced into an immediate instance. Except death. I will not bow down to him. May knowledge\n\nremain liberated forever.\nJournal of a Philosopher XII; Elindor's Travels\nThe undead attacked. Right upon the gates of Laurelin. The voice of Iblees boomed through the trees about imminent destruction and bowing before his\n\npower. Not denying, the display of might was tremendous, but still found its match against our united strength. I won't stop trying to understand the Undead, but I won't let Iblees take control of Aegis either. All noble paths need a path of less\n\nnobility to reap recognition; the truly noble path is unseen by others. The presence of such evil makes it easy to pick the righteous side, but our paths should not be so easily chosen for us. Has God taken away the choice so that all\n\nmight come to him or suffer? If so, Iblees was formed by God, because there is a little bit of Iblees even in Him. I must go, the thunder has returned.\nJournal of a Philosopher XIII; Elindor's Travels\nThe ascended are\n\ngone. The sages left and the remaining followers of Ariel are scattered among the races they once left to discover Haven. It serves as the desperate wake-up call that the war involuntarily concerns everyone. That is isn't happening in some\n\ndistant land being taken care of by the holy kin. Now we're all required.Finally we're going to see the prophecies fulfilled and the descendants of Horen, Malin, Krug and Urguan will come together again to defeat Iblees.\n\nAriel guided us this far, but another will rise as a shining light to lead Aegis to victory. That light could be someone as unexpected as myself; but it would never be me.There is great suffering still to come. This war's violent crescendo\n\nhas only just begun. We, including myself, still have much to learn of pain. Dark days ahead.\nJournal of a Philosopher XIV; Elindor's Travels\nA pungent aroma of ale and an untunefully recited dwarven drinking song shroud the\n\nbusily cleaning barmaid as she removes blood from the counter after yet another drunken brawl. I do enjoy Dawn's Bakery in Al'Khazar. A female follower of Aeriel came in yesterday and a brute of a man, who I had\n\nseen only days earlier terrorizing a woman for the fun of it, placed a blade against her throat. A long and hideous fight followed in which I got my fair share of blows in defending her. After the assailant was zapped with a ball of light and\n\ndissappeared I went with the Priestess to listen to Aeriel's guidance. The remaining ascended, and consequently the Followers of Aeriel Guild, seem\nfutile without their Sages. I likened her efforts in recruiting me to Wargoth and his", ""),
        StaticBook("1 I III I", "§bOracle", "The Legend of Shiranui\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nAct one: scene opens on the small town of Kamui :: narrator: This is the small town of Kamui, home of the great warrior Nagi :: Nagi comes and begins training :: ::Narrator: unlike most small towns, this was not a\n\npeaceful one ::Narrator: Every year a maiden would be selected from the town to be sacrificed to Orochi, a horrible beast ::::Narrator: the day of the selection was drawing close, and Nagi was worried that :: Nami, his love, would be chosen :: Old man\n\nOrange approaches Nagi :: Old Man Orange: Nagi! Great warrior of Kamui ! As you know, the day of the selection draws near, and there is a fearsome white wolf-beast who roams the town at night. We fear he is a servant of Orochi. He must be slain! ::\n\nNagi: Of course, Old Man Orange, I shall slay the beast tonight! He shall not see the light of tomorrow! :: Old Man Orange: Good. Good. I know that the beast will be no match for you! :: Old Man Orange leaves Nagi to his training :: Nami approaches Nagi\n\n:: Nami: Nagi, my love, the night of the selection approaches! I am concerned about being sacrificed to that horrible beast. ::Nagi: do not worry, Nami. All the maidens concern themselves with this every year. You will not be chosen. :: Nami: I\n\nthink you are right. Farewell my love. :: leaves Nagi to his training, while Nagi goes in his home :: Night falls over Kamui, and Shiranui comes out and paces the road :: Nagi appears and stands before Shiranui :: Nagi: Foul beast! I shall slay you\n\ntonight! :: Shiranui growls and bares his fangs at Nagi :: the two fight, with Shiranui eventually defeating Nagi :: Nagi: urgh..... your power... where does it come from? :: Shiranui disapears into the night, and Nagi drags himself to his home :: The\n\nsun rises over Kamui ::Old Man Orange approaches Nagi :: Old Man Orange: Nagi! I trust that you slayed the beast last night. :: Nagi: No... he defeated me.. :: Old Man Orange: What?? The great warrior defeated? What has happened to the world? It has\n\ndescended into madness! :: Nagi: Do not worry. I shall fight the beast every night until it is slain! :: ::Narrator: Nagi fought the beast ever night until the night of the selection came . The white arrow marking the home of the maiden to be sacrificed\n\nflew into Nami's home. :: Nagi runs to Nami :: Nagi: No! My love! Do not go! :: Nami: I must, lest the beast lay ruin to the town :: Nami puts on the sacrificial gowns and leaves for Orochi's lair :: Nagi comes after her and enters the beast's lair ::\n\nNagi slowly approaches a great stone circle with a bell in the center :: Orochi (unseen): Mortal! Who are you? You are not my sacrifice! :: Nagi: I am Nagi! The great warrior of Kamui! You shall not have Nami, my love! :: Orochi: Fool! You shall\n\nfeel my wrath for interrupting my sacrifice :: Oroch shows himself, with all his heads looking threateningly at Nagi :: Orochi and Nagi fight, Orochii knocks Nagi to the ground :: Orochi: Hah, mortal! You are no match for me! :: as Orochi is about to\n\ndeal the final blow, Shiranui attacks his head, saving Nagi :: Shiranui stands before Nagi, protecting him from Orochi's attacks :: Nagi stands up :: Nagi: Orochi! We shall slay you! (raises sword into the air) :: the three of them fight, with Shiranui\n\nand Nagi winning :: as Nagi and Shiranui are about to deal the final blow, Orochi wounds Shiranui, and knocks him to the ground, while Nagi delivers the final blow, slicing off all 8 of Orochi's heads :: Nami is brought into the chamber to be\n\nsacrificed, and sees Nagi and Orochi's body She runs to Nagi :: Nami: Nagi! You defeated him! :: Nagi: It was not just me, my love. The wolf- (sees Shiranui on ground) :: Nagi runs to Shiranui with Nami coming behind :: Nagi carries the wolf back to\n\nKamui :: Nagi, Nami and Old man Orange are gathered around Shiranui :: Old Man Orange: We distrusted this wolf... and he was our only ally. We shall erect a temple and a statue to honor his sacrifice! :: Shiranui licks Nagi's and Old Man Orange's feet\n\nbefore closing his eyes :: last scene shows the statue of Shiranui", ""),
        StaticBook("Vydra: Vol I", "§bAndrik Vydra", "7th day of Malin's Welcome, 1491\n\nThe war is over.\nI sit here, in this empty hall, upon the seat of Humanity. The Lord's seat in Petrus, once grand capital of the Empire. \n\nI cannot help but feel utterl unaccomplished and empty as I write.\n\nOur once proud people are splintered into pieces, this farce of unity nothing but that - a facade. Petty squabbles and ambitious Lords litter my new Kingdom, but it was their swords and banners which placed me upon this throne.\n\nI have won a crown,\n\nbut now I find myself shackled to it, unable to act as a true monarch of men.\n\nWhat should happen when I pass? Who will follow? And if they succeed in keeping the Kingdom intact, what then shall come after? Our destiny as a people lies in the hands of -\n\n- indivduals who rise through whatever methods possible, no matter how incompetend, or cruel, or undeserving they may be. The reigns of Varon Kovachev in Akovia and Aleksandr who sat where I do now is testament to this. \n\nI fight now not just\n\nfor my homeland Akovia, but for all of Humanity. I must ensure that there is always someone to take up the mantle, even when I am but ash and memory.\n\nThere is much to do.\n\n12th day of The First Seed, 1491\n\nI have heard whisperings of discontent in my realm. In every corner, I see enemies. If only there were some way to purge these blinded fools in one fell sweep.\n\nDo they not understand?\n\nI AM Humanity. When I sleep, I see the destiny of our flock. Our people, MY people, shall reign supreme over all the lands from sea to sea. And then I wake to see the despicable state of things, the idiocy that has permeated itself throughout the very air\n\nthat we breath. The shortsightedness of my court is enough to make me sick. \n\nThe other races, even my own subjects - are not fit to rule themselves, squabbling as children do over toys.\n\nTo even attempt such a feat is monumental\n\nin itself, impossible in the current state that once proud Orenia finds itself. Personal armies and retinues dominate the nature of our marital strength. We must consolidate so that we may conquer.\n\nOne King. One Kingdom. One iron fist to smite down my -\n\n- my enemies in the form of the unwavering ranks of those who will see my vision into reality. My children, my Sons of Vydra - the Zealots of Man.\n\nMy legacy.\n\n20th day of The Grand Harvest, 1491\n\nUnfaltering strength is the only way to make others see reason, I have decided.\n\nThe weak are the easiest to manipulate, and any man can be made weak through force - A man cannot make a stand if\n\nhe has no legs with which to raise himself. \n\nMen mistake my silence for those very things I despise. Lethargy, indecision, weakness. How I pity the fools. Wisdom is patience. I sit and listen to them prattle and say nothing but simply nod. I watch on -\n\n- as they sneer and scheme, wringing their filthy hands with malice as they conspire against what I have build - what is yet to be built.\n\nBut one day, I will strike. \n\nWithout mercy and without remorse.\n\nI will gut them from head to toe, boil their children before their very eyes, let them watch on in terror as I skin their women alive. Their screams and pleas for death will do nothing for them.\n\nWho then, will have the will to oppose me? My vision?\n\nBut until that day - I sit and wait, and not like the buffoon they take me for.\n\n3rd day of Malin's Welcome, 1493\n\nObstacles do not exist to be surrendered to, but only to be broken.\n\nToday I walked past a great pasture field, full of grazing livestock. The grass within the field was dry - a field of nothingness.\n\nBut without...beyond the pitiful fences, that constituted the barrier between these feeding cows and freedom - was lush greenery, far as the eye could see.\n\nAnd yet they continued to roam aimlessly, picking at the dirt and dry patches of weeds.\n\nWhen the greater good is at hand, there is no length one should not go, no number of taboos taken up, traditions and expectations trod upon. I take the lesson those mindless creatures taught me to heart.\n\nOnly when every single possible -\n\n- option is exhausted, every terrible - deplorable - path explored, will I consider conceding. But only for the time being, for there is always another opportunity. Another man to kill. Another idiot to fool and bend like the branches of a tree in summer\n\nor if need be - break, like those in times of winter.\n\n17th day of The First Seed, 1493\n\nI am ashamed by my countrymen. They war seems to have given every human able to draw breath a bloodlust equal to that of even the savage Orcs to the west. There is no reason to it, no logic.\n\nThey cry for more and more with each battle, victory or defeat. What has happened to the versatility of Humanity? We are not weapons forged for war, a people with a purpose so singular and barbaric as simple slaughter.\n\nWar is raged for a purpose, and the day that purpose is for the simple slaughter of others and razing of homes is the day I set down my crown and relinquish any notion that Humanity is truly superior.\n\nYou cannot rule the dead.", ""),
        StaticBook("2 II II I", "§bOracle", "What The Druids Know About The Battle Mages\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n4th of Malin's Welcome -1443\n\nPart One Purpose: They protect people using wepons and armour. If they see a person being attacked by bandits or monsters they must try to help unless it would certanly kill them.\n\nPart Two Ranks So Far: Master:Makes decisions. The master is Mavrick.\nScribe:Writes things regarding the battle mages down.\nApothacary:Is in charge of potions and healing:Apothacary is:Timothy Varius\nBattle Mage: Main", ""),
        StaticBook("2 III II I", "§bOracle", "A Blind Man's Inspirational Sayings\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nHope is the thing with feathers-\nThat perches in the soul-\nAnd sings the tune without words-\nAnd never stops-at all-\nNever loose Hope,\n~The Blind Man", ""),
        StaticBook("1 IV II I", "§bOracle", "Druidism\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nIs this what the druid college is like...? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I'm a druid for some reason... It's as if they're brainwashed.\n\nThey think I'm an elf, too! I'm a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She's also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe...? I'm just jotting down notes... And my thoughts... And why is htis\n\nhappening!? So, what do write now. I don't even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I've been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact... It's a magical artifact from\n\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it's in the hands of one, named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It's from the Kar'Lani tribe, and is hidden in the \"fake father of Al'Khazaar\". It's cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\n\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact. :: :: I've been living in Al'Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al'Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went\n\nto Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while. But then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of\n\ncourse. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me enough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us\n\nor something. He kept on saying we were elves and druids, which neither of us were. Bell's human and I'm a dwarf. And I don't think either of us would want to study druidism after this.... Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it. Er, not it. us. He tried\n\nto break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house . We found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I'll go back to Al'Khazaar... but I'll write about the next\n\nadventure . :: :: I went to go to Al'Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell's help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell dissapeared. I still don't know where she is. We continued on\n\nthe path, along with an orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and\n\ndied. :: :: A while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fun at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits . The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil\n\nbandit. It's obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al'Khazaar didn't even notice. He, along with the rest of human\n\nroyalty, is just STUPID. There's no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn't even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point...no. Untrue. Just untrue.\n\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. veryone thought he was a pale orc, even though he's admitted to be undead many times . The fools... the idiots, the fools... I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead\n\ncame. He even used the same teqnique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponets. The fools.. no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on... :: :: I would write\n\nmore about my life, but I realize I just don't know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can't let people know of my feelings or all of my thoughts. That's pretty much all of my life so far that I care to\n\nshare.", ""),
        StaticBook("2 I I I", "§bOracle", "On Orcs\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nNo race is more adapted to the harsh deserts and its predators than the muscular Orcs. Masters o f combat and wrestling these 7ft high Goliaths can destroy most prey with their bare hands. To an Orc the most important\n\nthing is the hunt and the protection of his tribe and clan. For that reason, t they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred and respect for the Dwarves of they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred\n\nand respect for the Dwarves of Kal'Urguan because of their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because because of their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because because\n\nof their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because they're not big enough. Where other races establish cities and build monuments to their predecessors, Orcs establish tribes and build strong clans around the\n\nmythic figures of their ancestors. Orcs tend toward nomadic life, but what villages they do choose to establish are usually built from the ruins of other cities, swallowed and spat forth again by the drifting dunes of the desert. :: Although Orcs can\n\nnaturally live longer than humans, this rarely becomes a point of debate. The oldest Orc to ever live was Karugk of Clan Pyrathon, who died in glourious battle on the turning of his two hundredth year (Eight Hundred Orcish Seasons). Orcs are just as\n\nprolific as Dwarves and Humans, but their children have the shortest period of puberty, somestimes reaching full adulthood in only fifteen years. Orcs are also the race in Aegis most likely to cull their own, whether purposefully\n\nleaving the incapable behind in the desert, or removing the weak through ritual trials. However, the strength of the clan is paramount in an Orc's eyes, and they will defend their young and wise to their very last breath - even if it is only to give\n\nenough time for the wise to show the young how to best attack after their elder clansmen have fallen. :: Orcs are usually brownskinned with green tints, varying from sandy to dark green and rarely black, and their hair is usually very dark, with\n\nbrown and black the most common. Most Orcs follow the practice of coloring their hair with the blood of their enemies. Because their hair is so dark, this coloring rarely shows until many dousings, and it is considered a sign of a great warrior\n\nfor your hair to glow red with the blood of your enemies. Orcs of the Shaman bloodline tend more toward green skin and black hair, usually distinguished from other Orcs by :: Size and musculature set them apart from all other races on Aegis, sometimes\n\nconsidered giants at two and a half meters tall. Orcs of the goblin bloodline, are most notably smaller most notably smaller than other Orcs, usually only reaching a meter and a half. Goblins are the most likely of all Orcs to have black skin and fairer\n\nhair. Orc eyes are usually brown or black, with a rare few blessed with blood-red.", ""),
        StaticBook("2 I III I", "§bOracle", "Mist's Adventure\n((Written by Mist for the Asulon Novella Competition))\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n4th of Malin's Welcome -1443\n\nMist awoke at the sound of screaming, Mist sprant out of bed, quickly opening the door,\nHe sprant outside of his room and outside, only to find Alys, Voak, Aylir and\n\nAdeon sprinting for their lives out of the inn, Mist tried to yell out but he couldn't, he tried to move, but he couldn't, his feet started to bind with dark magic, he looked at his feet and he made a barrier around them, it\n\nforced the magic away and he quickly thought to himself and he sprant off the edge of the inn, he fell at the ground and he shed a tear, he\npainfully got up and saw that destruction was all around him, Mist then notcied something\n\nat the corner of his eye, a Ghast, he sprant away from it, a magma bomb exploded behind him, it propelled him 3 meters away, he got up and collapsed again, he had sprained his ankle, he got up and ignored the sharp pain, the limped away, trying\n\nto get away from the ghast, another magma bomb hurtled at his legs, this time he was blown 8 meters, he started bleeding all over he got up only to see a slime creeping towards him, a lone traveller then wandered up to the slime and punched\n\nit, the slime got angry and it swallowed him up in a gulp, blood exploded\nfrom the slime, Mist started to limp weakly away from the slime, the slime soon got to Mist and the slime jumped, the slime was falling right towards Mist, Mist catapulted\n\nhimself as far away as he could from the slime, he sprant and sprant, ignoring all pain and sound, an arrow then hit into his leg, it started to grow numb, he saw the portal, he looked all around him, Mist's vision started to grow dark, he\n\ngot up and limped to the portal, he swayed heavily, he stumbled, so close, he thought, he then got a sudden boost of small energy, he ran with a sway, and he then tumbled into the portal. Mist awoke to see an endermen, it was\n\ncarrying him, he didn't dared to look into it's eyes, the endermen glared it's eyes and teeth at Mist with a menacing look, Mist looked down, the endermen\nteleported away up in the air and dropped down again, he repeated this until it was knocked\n\nout \"Stupid Endermen\" Mist said, he saw that it had an Ender Pearl next to it, he picked it up and threw it as far away as he could, \"Stupid Pearls, they don't to sh-\" He was then flung away, he then smashed into the\n\nwall and lost all his teeth, then a slime appeared, it came up to him and Mist threw another Ender Pearl at it absent mindedly , the slime just ate it and then Mist was dissolved into the slimes stomach", ""),
        StaticBook("Azog Scrolls", "§bGrool", "The rhythmic beating of hammers can be heard throughout the village. Azog’s mother is grunting in beat with the hammering as she is giving birth to a sandy colored orc.  You can see pain in her eyes but she refuses to cry. Gorkil is the father,\n\n she can not fail to give him a healthy cub. Her water had broken earlier while she was making Gorkil a hunting dagger as a gift. Azog plumps out quickly without any problems. She looks down onto his sandy face and smiles.\n\n-------Azog-------\nAzog, the sand colored orc, can not remember his mother. He has been living in the smithy or in the mine since birth and Gorkil has forgotten him.\n\nBurns and scars from stray embers lay across his body and his eyes are black as the coal he helps carry.\n\nThe head smith, Bruul, has been letting Azog try to lift his hammer. Azog’s goal is to be seen by Gorkil as a worthy heir to the clan.\n\nHis small scrap metal sword, more like a toothpick then weapon, is always strapped to his loincloth.\n\nClothes are something undesired by Azog and are often neglected. The soles of his feet are black from his constant hours in the smithy.\n\n------Gorkil------\nGorkil is seated in the arena at his throne with his choice of mates laid out in front of him on multi-color carpets. Klomps to honor him and to gain standings among the clan are happening in the arena below.\n\nOccasionally, between klomps, Gorkil vanishes along with a mate to indulge himself.\nAzog, now 8, is chewing on a bone in the stands. Bruul said that he would get to klomp another orc today, he just did not say who.\n\nAzog’s tusks are starting to become more prominent. Bruul grunts and points to Azog’s younger half-brother Ugluk. “Dat iz whu lats wel klomp.” Ugluk is bigger then Azog by about 5 inches and has bigger tusks.\n\nAzog, standing in the arena, facing Ugluk, is going through internal strife. He is scared to flat of losing and Gorkil seeing his own son get beaten. Gorkil is attentively watch two of his sons get ready. \n“KLOMP VUR DE HUNUR OV KRUG!”\n\nUgluk is charging and Azog was zoned out thinking. Ugluk full on tackles him, trying to use his weight against him. Azog has the breath knocked out of him but pushes up with his large biceps, extending their use to the fullest.\n\nUgluk stumbles back and snarls. He swings a large, lumbering arm at Azog. He is too quick and small for such a slow attack. Azog dodges and kicks Ugluk in the gut. Ugluk bends over and Azog uses both elbows to smash\n\nthe back of his head toward the ground. Ugluk falls to the ground but gets up, his nose bleeding from the impact. He uses his tusks to stab Azog in the side. Azog grunts but then pummels Ugluk in the neck and upper back.\n\nUgluk having suffered a concussion, slowly passes out. Azog is bleeding from his side quite badly but raises his hands in triumph.\nGorkil grunts, “Hosh klomp”. Then he goes off with two females to his tent behind the arena.\n\n-------Mines-------\nHe can barely breathe, he feels like the life is being crushed out of him, Azog is all alone. A recent mine collapse has trapped Azog in a vein of coal that was recently discovered.\n\nAll around him is the darkness of underground. Only, off in the far distance, is a slight glow of a fallen torch.\n\n2 days later, a rescue operation brings Azog out of the caves, but his fair skin is turned black from the exposure to coal dust. He was coughing up black soot for days, not even strong enough to get out of bed.\n\nAt one point, it was said he coughed out a gold nugget that was hidden inside the coal. Azog’s skin would always be black or sandy colored from then on, even the adopted one were forced to undergo the same experience,\n\nhaving coal beaten into their skin in patterns.", ""),
        StaticBook("2 V I I", "§bOracle", "Immortal Blood\nOriginally Written in Aegis\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n4th of Malin's Welcome -1443\n\nThe moons and stars were hidden from sight, making that particular quiet night especially dark.\n\nThe town guard had to carry torchlight to make their rounds ; but the man who came to my chapel that night carried no light with him. I came to learn that Movarth Piquine co uld see just as well in the night as in the day - an excellent talent,\n\nconsidering his int erests were exclusively nocturnal. One of my acolytes brought him to me, and from the look of him, I at first thought he was in need of healing. He was pale to the point of opalescence with a face that looked like it had once been\n\nvery handsome before some unspeakable suffering. The dark circles under his eyes bespoke exhaustion, but the yes themselves were alert, intense , almost insane. He quickly dismissed my notion that he himself was ill, though he did\n\nwant to discuss a specific disease. \"Vampirism\" he said, and then paused at my quizzical look, \"I was told that you were someone I should seek for help understanding it.\" \"Who told you that?\" I asked with a smile. \"Tissina Gray\", I immediately\n\nremembered her. A brave, beautiful knight who needed my assistance on the subject of Vampirism. It had been two years, and I had not heard from her since. \"You;ve spoken to her? How is her ladyship?\" I asked. \"Dead\" Movarth replied coldly. And\n\nthen, responding to my shock, he added, perhaps to soften the blow. \"She said your advice was invaluable. She was tracking a Vampire\" a pause, \"It killed her.\" \"Then my advice was not enough\" I sighed. \"Who says it would be enough for you?\" \"I know\n\nthat if a student doesn't ask the right questions, the teacher cannot be responsible for his failure. I intend to ask you the right questions.\" And that he did. For hours, he asked questions and I answered. but he never volunteered any information\n\nabout himself. He never smiled. He only studied me with those intense eyes of his, commiting every word I said to memory. Finally, I could detect some weariness in his eyes. I would like to commit this tomorrow night. I must sleep and absorb this. \"You\n\nsleep during the day\" I smiled. To my surprise, he returned the smile, though it was more of a grimace. \"When tracking your prey, you adapt their habits.\" The next day he returned, with more questions. I told him of the Vampires of Eastern Malinor,\n\nthe Volkihar, paranoid and cruel, whose very breath could freeze their victim's blood in their very veins. I explained to them how they lived amongst the tree trunks, never venturing into the world of men except to feed. He left, and returned\n\nwithin a few days. True to his word, the man returned to my chapel. There was a fresh scar on his cheek, but he was smiling that grim but satisfied smile of his. \"Your advice helped me very much\" he said. \"But you should know that the Volkihar have an\n\nability you did not mention. They can reach through the bark of their trees without breaking it. It was a nasty surprise, being grabbed from behind.\" \"Terrifying\", I said, \"You were lucky you survived\", \"I don't believe in luck\" he replied, \"I\n\ncan land a thousand blows without losing my balance, providing I get the first strike\" \"So you must never be surprised\", \"That is why I came to you. Again, I answered his questions, they taxed my knowledge. There was much to cover. The Bonsamu, who\n\nwere indistuingishable from men except when seen by candelight. The Keerilth who could disintegrate into mist. The Yekef who swallowed men whole. The dread Telboth who preyed on children, eventually taking their place in the family, waiting\n\npatiently for years before murdering them all in their unnatural hunger. Once again, he bade me farewell. Promising to return in a few weeks. I nodded, knowing then that this man was on an eternal quest. He wouldn't be satisfied but with the\n\nbarest hint of how things were. He needed to know it all. He did not return for a month, and on the night that he did, I could see his frustration and despar, though there were no lights burning in my chapel. \"I failed\" he said as I lit a candle. \"You\n\nwere right. I could not find a single one.\" \"I brought the light up to my face and smiled. He was surprised, even stunned by the pallor of my flesh, the dark hunger in my ageless eyes, and the teeth. Oh, yes, I think the teeth definitely surprised the\n\nman who could not afford to be surprised. \"I haven't fed in seventy-two hours\" I explained, as I fell on him. ::He did not land the first blow or the last.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "e", ""),
        StaticBook("Log-Staff Ritual", "§bElrune Presna", "Elrune's Staff Task\n--------------------------------------\nLog and Diary\n-------------------By Elrune Presna-Currently a Dedicant of the Old Hunt Circle\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLog 1-Deciding on what sapling to plant. Meditated in the grove to see if my mind could find what sapling would be best, though it hadn't led to any developments. Stopped meditation and decided to walk through nature outside of the grove, to possibly find\n\na sapling.\n\nLog 2-First area of exploration is Sutica. Haven't found much, saw a quite lard Oak Tree, impressed by it though I didn't feel a connection to it, I continued to the Snow Elves. No trees of significance to be found, though it was very\n\ncold. Went back to the grove for some more rest and meditation. The proper tree wont be found in a day.\n\nLog 3-Stayed in the grove for another day, meditating and trying to see if anything would come to me. Once completed I decided I would make\n\nhaste to the islands of Asul.\n\nLog 4-Visited Veric. The city was quite lush with nature, leaves covered the houses and streets, felt comfortable here explored further to find a sapling. While walking I studied several tree types, what would make the\n\nbest staff as well as what I felt a connection toward. The connections were faint so I decided to not use any of them, I continued to other places.\n\nLog 5-Visiting the Deadlands of Golin'Dar. Was unable to enter the town, instead i decided to take a\n\nwalk around the walls, exploring the surrounding bushes. Most of the surrounding area was devoid of nature, most of it full of dead trees, though upon further investigation I discovered vasts expanses of quite large trees. I managed to climb on top of the\n\ncanopy, it allowed me to have quite a good rest, but I was no closer to finding a tree.\n\nLog 6- Visited Calethia, explored the forests there, helped me feel more intune with nature, I believe this was a major step in me finding the proper sapling.\n\nThough the final decision hasn't been made. Same day I decided to visit Asterleigh, again no steps in going further towards completing the task.\n\nLog 7- Visited Carasca. Saw insanely large trees, made everything around them seem insignificant\n\nSat around the stumps for a while, used this to help out my connection toward something greater, wasn't much help.\n\nLog 8-Rested some more at the grove, used this time to study up on druidism.\n\nLog 9-Went around various small areas\n\naround major cities, visiting smaller towns. Nothing really happened.\n\nLog 10-I had almost given up today so I decided to take a walk around the coast, the water always makes me feel better. While on my calming walk I noticed something floating on\n\nthe waves, slowing edging itself closer to the land. I went closer to it and waited for it to make it. While it got closer I noticed it happened to look like a sapling, something i've been trying to find for a while. When I finally grabbed it I felt\n\nsomething, something I don't think I can fully explain, maybe connected to nature, at least I hope, but whatever it was, it was something important. I grabbed the sapling and hoped that it would actually grow. Once I made it back to the grove I decided to\n\ndry the sapling out, after some time of drying I needed to ensure that the salt was gone to, so of course I washed some fresh water over it. I left it to dry for a while over night.\n\nLog 11-I woke up today and felt like this was the one. I decided\n\nto plant it in an open spot within the druid grove. I'll leave it to grow for a while.\n\nLog 12-I spent a while watching over the sapling as it eventually became a mighty (actually pretty small) Oak tree. I spent my days sitting by it, reading as it grew\n\nbeside me. Once it was fully grown I felt connected to it, and it felt right to continue towards the creation of the staff.\n\nLog 13-I took off a part of the tree and created a staff for myself, once it was done I went to the carving process of it, trying\n\nto find something that felt a part of me.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-------------------\nStaff Desc. Next Page\n\n-------------------xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX            STAFF                  DESCRIPTION\nXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx-------------------On the top lies the body of a Kraken with two dark purple eyes. Its tentacles wrapping\n\naround the staff in a spiral pattern, going downwards. At a closer look the tentacles have small veins of blue, this is seen around all of the tentacles as well as the body of the Kraken. The tentacles end in a connection at the bottom of the staff, the\n\ntips if its tentacles being dipped in gold. The exact bottom of the staff is also capped with gold, you're able to hear the distinct heaviness of the staff tapping along the floor. The wood itself is stained oak, slightly darker than usual oak wood.\n\n-Elrune Presna-\n-Staff Ritual Log-\n(BloodSaint)", ""),
        StaticBook("Ashton to Riley", "§bAshton", "*This unsigned letter appears haphazardly written. The handwriting is hard to make out in some spots.*\n\n\"You stupid bitch. You just had to come back here. You've ruined my life. I hate you.\"\n\n\"You've taken everything from me. You've destroyed everything I cared for. Why couldn't you just stay gone?\n\nNo one asked you to come back. You shouldn't of come back. I hate you so much. You destroyed me.\"\n\n\"GO AWAY!\"\n\n*The words are smeared, as if something wet dropped on them while the person wrote.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Song of Despair", "§bKira Winterleaf", "The sky was a crimson sash.\n\nA golden place where trees touch sky.\n\nMany fluffy clouds roll by.\n\nMany think they have seen it all.\n\nThrough summer and through fall.\n\nThe unliftable veil of ignorance settles upon the races.\n\nYet despair and depression etch into faces.\n\nLove isn't a present drapped in pink laces.\n\nBut I don't see a reason to cry.\n\nDesperately trying to find\n\nout why. \"Why me? Why everyone I love?\" \n\nBut life'll always give you a shove in the right direction.\n\nBut not through love and affection.\n\nAn unliftable irration irrevocable veil of ignorance.\n\nThere's no reason to be sad.\n\nTo shed tears.\nDo do bad.\nTo be depressed for years.\nYou might wonder the reason for this song, and I'll tell you now.\n\nIf nature is always here, always here to live and keep living eternally,\n\nthen why do some take their own lives?\n\nNature is lovely, but it can not live for a thousand bees in a large hive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mistakes", "§bAeran", "Mistakes I've made\n(post Dedicancy)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSo I don't forget.\n\nRejecting Anarane\n\nI loved her and don't know why I thought we shouldn't be together. I used her when she was vulnerable and then tossed her aside, and wish I could go back and fix that more than anything else.\n\nDisrespectful to Arin\n\nCalled her Arinibitch, called her many things for no reason, ever though she was the most supportive Archdruid for me. I've apologized to her about this, but still can't forget it.\n\nReading Endvani's Journal\n\nWas a stupid thing. Led to me being kicked out of Dedicancy the first time. I think she forgave me, but it was still incredibly juvenile and pathetic. Sorta led to her and Nivndil being together, though.\n\nArguing with Terreni\n\nWasn't arguing as much as me calling her names for no real reason. Got kicked out a second time for it. I think it might have made her leave her Dedicancy, in which case it's pretty unforgivable.\n\nNot Going With Them\n\nArin and Lillith were taken by something, kidnapped and tortured. When they went to rescue her, I didn't come. I wish I had. Maybe that's why, maybe she thinks I abandoned her so she should do it to me.\n\nNot Visiting Lillith in the Infirmary\n\nAfter the kidnapping she was hurt and scarred. Wish I would have went down and saw her. Didn't want to, didn't want to see her like that.\n\nTold Chirr How I Felt\n\nShe was married, but he was gone for a long time. I think we could have been happy together, maybe would have made her stay around. I think she felt the same way about me. Miss her.\n\nDidn't Give Meiala the Golden Apple\n\nI don't know if she ate it or not. I never talked to her after that. I gave her the wrong type of support when she needed support. Don't know if we could have ever been together.\n\nPunching Marcy\n\nLed to me being kicked out for the third time. I was upset about the Meiala stuff, and took it out on someone else, for no reason. Led to her being kicked out too, even, which led to her fucked up life. I'm sorry.\n\nLetting Myself be Destroyed\n\nI went to a very dark place. Lots of people offered help, but I didn't accept it. For no reason. Don't know why. Life was awful. Hate to think about it too much. Don't want to go back to that.\n\nTelling Oliver I Hated Him\n\nHe was my only real friend for a long time. The only person who came and talked to me. And as we got closer I got worried that he'd become broken hearted because I killed myself. I didn't want that, so I tried to make him not\n\nwant to talk to me, by telling him I didn't like him. Worked for a bit, but he came back. And then I broke his heart, but he came back again. Because he's Oliver.\n\nDenying Erin's Help\n\nShe offered to make me her Dedicant, to help me along. But I just said no. I don't know why.\n\nNot Doing Aeras' Tasks\n\nTold me to do three things to prove I was worthy of being a Druid. Would have been easy, but... I didn't do them. Don't know why. Made life a lot worse.\n\nNot Doing Arik's Tasks\n\nHe basically forced me to become a Dedicant again. Which is what I needed. But then I stopped, for no reason. And I think that hurt him.\n\nLeaving Without Saying Bye\n\nI tried my best, but when I moved out of the Grove, I didn't say bye to Wendy. And she was quickly becoming as close to me as me and Oliver were. I had that happen to me enough to know how awful it feels.\n\nTrying to be a Bandit\n\nI was hungry, I guess. I wanted to die, too. So I tried robbing a few people at knife-point. Didn't work, I got hurt or humiliated. But I had no right to do that, even if I was how I was. Idiotic.\n\nNot Telling Wendy How I Felt Sooner\n\nShe was the one that came to me, told me she loved me. I loved her too. We were great together.\n\nBreaking up with Wendy\n\nI shouldn't have. She was perfect, we were good together. She gave me support in a dark time, helped me, and in turn I abandoned her. I think it destroyed her. I haven't seen her in a long time. Miss her.\n\nLetting me and Riley be Together\n\nShouldn't have happened. She's younger than me, she's my second cousin (even if by adoption), she's my closests friend's sister and aunt. Our relationship destroyed Ashton, and it could have been avoided. I wanted to\n\nhelp someone who was feeling bad. Maybe I did. But she could have found someone else. I would have been fine. Maybe Gwendlyn would-- will come back sometime. I don't know. I don't regret marrying Riley, though.\n\nHelping the Ash Druid get Poppy/Aislinn\n\nI sent a bird to Poppy to get her to the Grove. Thought Aurojia would just talk to her. She had other plans, but I stopped that and let Poppy go as quick as I could. And I helped her get Aislinn, hit him when he\n\nwalked into the Grove, beat him up. Helped her hide it. That's not justice. That's not how you fix things.\n\nDidn't Stop Riley Being Stabbed\n\nI could have stopped it. Could have got an Archdruid back, tried to pull Riley away stronger. But I didn't. So she got hurt. Aurojia shouldn't have done what she did, I know, I don't blame Riley.\n\nNemiisae Stuff\n\nI should have let things be how they should be. I learned the consequences of my actions, almost got the whole Order killed because I couldn't keep my mouth shut. Arik and Ouity are going to be killed because of me.\n\nAttacked Kyral\n\nI got emotional and lashed out. Lillith and her abandoned me, when I was kicked out, when I needed it most. Kyral lied to me, said that they were trying to get my back into the Order. Lied and abandoned me. I cried ever night for years\n\nbecause the person who is supposed to stay with you no matter what, your mother, thought I didn't deserve that common thing. Destroyed me. But eventually I got over it. But then Kyral came back. And that made me more upset about it than I ever had been.\n\nLied to Ashton\n\nPromised her things I shouldn't have, manipulated her. I should have tried to make her feel better in other ways. Shouln't have lied and manipulated. She shouldn't ever forgive me for that.\n\nHow I Treated Riley\n\nShould have been better. Not lied. Not been an asshole. Not done the things people have done to me that have destroyed me. I don't deserve her love, I know that now. So we can't be together.\n\nAsshole to Taynuel\n\nThere's no reason for it. He doesn't even like me, yet he's given me support many times when I've needed it. Because he's a great Druid, and I'm not. And I guess I lash out or something.\n\nSelfish\n\nTrying to get myself killed. Leave people I love behind. Kira would be devastated, so would Ashton, Oliver. Maybe Riley would feel sad, think she was the cause. I was the cause of that, I know. But I've got to be better.\n\nI forgot so many things. If I remember more, I'll try to add them. I know there is more.\n\nOn that topic\n\nFairy Ring\n\nIt messed me up, abusing it like I did. My memory is bad, I used to see things. Attunement helped. If I was unattuned I'd go mental, I know. Maybe worse than death. I don't want that. Please.", ""),
        StaticBook("Birthday", "§bKira Winterleaf", "A feeling of warmth floods by body.\n\nI feel like I've grown a foot! \n\nI wouldn't care if I was covered in soot on this very special day.\n\nI want to run and jump and play! \n\nGo lots of places but\n\nnever stay!\n\nIt only comes once a year.\n\nIs yours finally coming near? \n\nKeep your heart close and never jeer on this very special day.\n\nI lay down my head tonight, thinking of happiness and not blight.\n\nI see the stars--so beautiful they are!--alined as they were thirteen years ago on my birthday. \n\n\n1556 10th of The Snow's Maiden (my birthday) \n\nBy: Kira Raine Winterleaf, recently age thirteen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunes Of Time", "§bSaeed Ibn Malek", "The Dunes Of Time\n------------------- A poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------Thru the sands I walk, the dunes always the same yet always different\nMy heart seeks but always turns to the gust of sand that sprays my face and wounding my e\n\nI yearn for the warmth of one I could trust upon my cheek Yet the sun Burns me when the thought arises\nLost I am in thoughts that burn my every being! Tell me, is there a end of this sorrow?\n\nWill the sky of mine give me a cloud of rain to wash my grief? \nor am I to drift deeper into the sands of sorrow becoming lost to my own desolation!\nTell me! why have the thoughts of happiness hurt me!\n\nTell me! When will you utter a word and then leave me to my own destruction!\noh why does my mind persecute my heart's yearn and turn everything to the sand that loses me to time!\nTell me...Will I be lost in the dunes of time never to be rescued\n\n--------------------------------------\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n  (Ibraheemc2000)", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Rose", "§bSaeed Ibn Malek", "Desert Rose\n-------------------A Poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\n\nI dream of fire,\nThose dreams are tied to a horse that will never tire,\nAnd in the flames,\nHer shadows play in the shape of a man's desire,\nThis desert rose,Each of her veils, a secret promise,\n\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nAnd as she turns,\nThis way she moves in the logic of all my dreams,\nThis fire burns,\nI realize that nothing's as it seems,\nI lift my gaze to empty skies above,\n\nThis rare perfume is the sweet intoxication of her love,\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\nSweet desert rose,\nEach of her veils, a secret promise,\n\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nSweet desert rose,\nThis memory of Peace haunts us all,\nThis desert flower,\nThis rare perfume, is the sweet intoxication of the fall.\n----------------------------\n\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n(I did not make this my self irl <3 thanks for reading)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         Rowan's§0\n§0        Journal\n\n18th MW 1603§0\n§0\n§0I am frightened. I want to die, and that scares me. Everything is going well for once, I have a family, I suppose I'm just waiting for everything to go wrong. Everything always goes wrong. Something bad will happen soon. It has to.\n\nThat is the pattern. I want to die, but why? Why am I still unhappy? Why am I still like this? Why am I so pathetic?§0\n§0I'm sorry. I'm so so sorry. Everything will be alright. I just need to think positively. Everything will be alright. No one will die.\n\n13 FS 1602§0\n§0\n§0Dear Rowan,§0\n§0\n§0That's my name. That's me. I'm real, I am Rowan. I need to remember that. I am here. I got the date wrong last entry. It is 1602, not 1603. Time.. I'm here though. I'm here. I am Rowan. It is 1602. No one can read\n\nthis. No one should ever read this. I'm sorry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Once upon a time there was a young elf. It was a small elf even for one it's age. Part of it knew that it had something to do with how often it was sick.§0\n§0\n§0  One day, the elf's father brought the child to the Cloud Temple and promised to return sho\n\nHe never did.§0\n§0\n§0  The elf waited as it was supposed to and decided to play in the snow. A woman soon came along who took the child in.\n\n\n§0\n§0   The next story is one of just plain crude behavior", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0      Please do not read this, its private.\n\nDear Kaari,§0\n§0\n§0With all luck you will not awaken and require this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Once upon a time there was a lovely young maiden. However while on the outside she was beautiful, she had a wicked temper and was very unkind. One day she came across a man who had accidentally fallen into a hunter's trap. Instead of helping him, she\n\nmerely laughed at the man's misfortune.§0\n§0So he placed a curse on her. By day she would be cursed to be ugly, by night she would transform into a goose. Only at that time between the day and night would she regain her original beauty. When she returned\n\nhome, she was driven out, for no one recognized her. So, she ran away into the woods all the way to a quiet pond. She immediately flew into a rage. She threw things, kicked whatever she could kick, and even slashing at a tree with the hunting knife she\n\ncarried. She didn't stop until she had collapsed with exhaustion, and even then she was seething with rage. She sat there until despair finally hit her. She was alone, with nothing of her own aside from the clothes she was wearing and an old hunting\n\nknife.§0\n§0\"Oh what am I going to do?\" She wailed. It was far too humiliating to show her face anywhere, what with how ugly she was. She concluded she would attempt to live as a goose for a while. However it only took one night for her to abandon that\n\nplan. She was hungry, and even though she had transformed into a goose, grass and pond weeds were not appetizing at all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I have seen a most spectacular thing this day! A dragon if you could believe! I was on one of my routine visits to Haelun'or when it approached. A large being, shining black and charcoal gray. I was awestruck the moment I saw him. It's pink eyes glowed\n\nvery bright, and it even breathed fire! It was snowing, and for those unaware, Haelun'or is a city of white and blue. The visual contrast was absolutely stunning!§0\n§0The guards dutifully fought and through one of their cries I learned the creature's name. An\n\nelf adressed the dragon as Satar, and I must assume this is his name. What a beautiful majestic and elegant creature. I would have loved to get a closer look, and maybe attempt conversation should it not have been my enemy at the time. Truly though, I am\n\nno fighter, and all I could do was stand and watch as the citizens and visitors to Haelun'or battled against this fantastical being. Still, as and observer I found the whole thing almost underwhelming. The dragon did relatively little damage to the city\n\nand its occupants. I'd always expected a dragon to have the capacity to cause immense amounts of destruction should one chose to fight. I am thoroughly confused as to the purpose of the conflict today. 8th of the Snow's Maiden, 1565.\n\n In the aftermath of this event I have learned numerous things. The first is that this encounter was with a drake. From what I have read, a drake is a corrupted form of a lesser dragon", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Diel'Koigh§0\n§0Eldrec§0\n§0Daa-no§0\n§0Alayac- hello§0\n§0Joiu ec al- Good, and you?§0\n§0Fai- sprite/fairy§0\n§0ona- one§0\n§0un-two§0\n§0Ana- I§0\n§0boic§0\n§0Ana kwa kjo rtiau§0\n§0I would like that (close enough)\n\nAshe bev al -how are you?§0\n§0Bev- are§0\n§0me- am§0\n§0Vela- walk§0\n§0aniu-yes§0\n§0Hwova§0\n§0Hwe-he§0\n§0Quel-Dorei- high elf\n\nShe smiles softly§0\n§0Circled by blue roses, they sing together.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lover's Day.", "§bKili Al-Deen", "they shine brightly in the moon lit gaze,i have traveled near and far yet seen not such beauty as this\nlike a diamond strong and proud yet pretty and pleasing to the eye.their touch is of a gentil flower on a warm sunny day,their voice is soft and\n\ngentil that fills the heart with a warm reassurance and a aw that makes you feel as thuo you have been touched and carryed away by a cloud,you get lost in their gaze as one gets lost in a sunset and your mood rises like the sun in the dawn. you yearn\n\nto be around them with and want to see their smile and happyness you feel as if its your duty to make them smile and joyfull.thy are my warm sunrise and Beautiful jem.to rise before you and make you your favorite dish and bring you roses of compasi\n\nhonnor and love that goes to no one but you,My dear love.\n___________________\n\n         By:Kili Al-Deen\n      (ibraheemc2000)\n\nnotes from writer:\nI made this for the enjoyment of the read and the warmth of the heart-Kili Al-Deen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Last Will", "§bRaine", "The Last Will and Testament of Raine Arsden Vonleibrand Aidan Winterleaf\n\nI don't think this needs to be too lengthy. I've already said my goodbyes to those I could bear to say goodbye to. Kira, Mia, Nora, Avelon, my dearest mother whose name escapes me, and the same goes for my father, I love you all.\n\nAll of my belongings go to Avelon Granel Winterleaf, to distribute to the rest of the family as she sees fit. My home at 8 Saldin Street goes to her. The parental guardianship of Kira, Mia, and Nora Winterleaf goes to her, as well. Essentially, everything\n\nof mine is hers.\n\nIf Illern Winterleaf ever returns, and requests to take on the role of parental guardian of Kira, Mia, and Nora Winterleaf, she and Avelon will share the privelige.\n\nI go now to the north of the Oasis Grove.\n\nAvelon, please do not try to find me.\n\nI know you will anyway, so when you do find me, have me cremated and spread my ashes in the swamp that was once Aeroch Nor.\n\nI'm sorry that I have to leave you like this, but I would rather die than forget you all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XV", "§bMarch Ash", "The winds converge in this place, splitting and merging between the stone like rivers. I hear on it a thousand conversations, from a thousand places all across Axios. It speaks to me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VIII", "§bMarch Ash", "The canyon is wild. The fossils tell a story. A history. When I trace my palms down the rocks I can feel what remains of so many creatures. So many lives, now embedded in rock. Their lives give me will. Their passions are my power.\n\nI feed on them. Their hungers, and loves, and hates.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Commandments", "§bSchreck'Lak", "The\nCommandments ᛋᛋ\n\n\nA comprehensive list of how to avoid degeneracy and please the spirits\n\n\nWritten by Schreck'Lak\n*Written in Blah*\n\n1. It is the avowed duty and responsibility of all orks to secure and assure the existence of the orkish race upon the mortal plane. To do elsewise is a direct insult to Krug and his blood which you bear.\n\n2. Be fruitful and multiply. Do your part in increasing the proportion of Krug's sons among the mortal plane.\n\n3. The guiding principle of all your actions shall be: \"What is best for the orkish race? What is best for Laklul? For Krug?\"\n\n4. Remember that the inferior inferior races are our enemies, and that the most dangerous of all is the human race. It is our immediate objective to relentlessly expand the orkish race, and keep shrinking our enemies.\n\n5. Show preferential treatment in business dealings with members of our race, the orkish race. Phase out all dealings with the kin of Malin, Horen, Urguan and those cat things.\n\n6. The offspring of interracial mates are infertile, pathetic creatures. While recieving all the curses of their lineage they recieve nothing. Do not mix your blood.\n\n7. Might makes right. Orks are to strive consistently towards physical, mental and martial excellence. Weakness is a disgrace to your racial comrades and ancestors: avoid it.\n\n8. Remain loyal to the spirits, and the spirits shall remain loyal to you.\n\n\n\nPraise Krug", ""),
        StaticBook("My Return", "§bWargoth Malog'Yar", "These past several years mi have been on pilgrimage. It was nub a pilgrimage to any particular holy place or shrine, but was rather a sacred wandering of sorts. Mi explored wild and uninhabited places, and further hardened mi already thick hide.\n Mi\n\nhave meditated atop the highest peaks of frozen mountains. Mi have trod the scorched earth of volcanic regions where the air is clouded with smoke agh ash. Mi have stalked through the underbrush of mi people's jungles, braving the dangers of the many\n\npredators thereof.\n In mi travels, mi have observed the skies by morning, listened to the voice of the wind by day, gazed into fires by evening, agh dreamed both wonderous agh terrible dreams by night. All of existence, both waking agh sleepeing, blah to\n\nmi. The spirits guide mi through the stars agh moon, agh drive mi on through the sun. They whisper in the grass of the fields agh murmur in the caves. The waves of the sea shout to they who listen.\n Mi return this day from mi pilgrimage to find mi people\n\nscattered, agh their blargs empty. The streets are silent. The walls have been thrown down. Just as well though. I hated that goi. The orcs have done far hosher. San'Orca; San'Vitar; Kodar'goi; San'Thraka. These were gois worthy of Krug!\n Still though, mi\n\nbrothers agh sisters are left without a land. The sharas mouth boastful things in their perpetual arrogance, agh their wood albai whores have spat on the shadow of Enrohk  by stretching their hands out against his shrines. Darûkûrz bûbri, afar angathfark\n\nagh vadokanuk, ashdautus vrasubatlat! All who read this, heed those words. Let them be the words of all the Orcish people. Gruk them agh lock them in lats spirit.\n Meanwhile, the spirit realm screams, agh the bub'hosh powers of the universe shift. Mi\n\nhear the moaning agh creaking of all reality in mi sleep. The h'ash arms have fallen. Such is the price of betrayal, though mi blah it with a heavy soul. Those arms could have upheld us for all eternity, had carelessness nub taken hold of our Rex. Kharak\n\nwas a fine Rex, but his ambition outgrew his wisdom. Now, that which brought us such power has been layed low, agh we suffer for it. The powers with which he played are not toys, agh Orgon is nub a howler on a leesh. Had he gruk'd that sooner, things\n\nwould still be as they ought to be. Let all living shamans learn from his error, agh excercize due caution when wielding such power.\n Now, Kinul stands where mi old master agh the giver of mi sight once stood. These days weigh heavily on mi bones. Now,\n\nhowever, is nub a time to mourn. Now is the time to steel ourselves. We are nub as the sharas, who live on through their gois agh land. Wi are nub as the albai, who grow fat at the trough of comfort agh luxury. We are nub as the gazat, who hole up in\n\ncaves, agh find their security in riches. We are the orcs, the cubs of Krug. Our strength is to be found in hardship agh trial. \n Since the days of the Ancients, our kind has fought for every morsel of food; every cup of water; every inch of land;\n\nevery breath of air; agh every second of existence. These days are nub to be lamented, but rather let us stand tall as ever. Let us remember who we are. These days are not a grave to lie down in. They are a crucible to purify us. They are a fire to harden\n\nour skins.\n We are the uruk, the goblins, agh the ologs. We are the cubs of Krug. We are the orcs. Look upon lats ancestors, brothers agh sisters, agh shout proudly. Raise lats lusks, lats zults, lats o'ligs, agh lats fists. Bare lats tusks, stand atop\n\nthe bloody agh broken heaps of lats enemies, agh roar. For the spirits. For the Ancestors. For Krug!\n -Malog, Wargoth of the Yar Clan.\n 7th of The Grand Harvest, 1583.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn IV", "§bMarch Ash", "Mesa is dry. Not far from here are the salt flats of Dangier. Will reach them by nightfall. Nature is loving, but is also cruel.", ""),
