        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Mana is within all living things, it is our life force. And such is why when connecting to the void earlier on can be fatal. When a mage with very little experience connects for his first few times he risks being unable to withdraw or disconnect,\n\nthus having the void consume his life force. A most painful death. There is several observable ways in which mages express connecting and showing the strain of establishing and maintaining a voidal connection. They will often turn pale, and sweat\n\nprofusely upon their foreheads or arms. And some mages even have a habitual twitch which occurs upon he or she connecting to the void.§0\n§0\n§0These effects lessen in time as your mana pool grows through meditating, but as an intitiate they are felt ten fold.\n\nSo you may throw up, or pass out your first few times connecting. Such is common, but heed this warning i will not permit you to meditate less you be with a partner who knows to break your connection if you succeed in connecting but unable to withdraw it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*the text seemed rather nicely written despite who did it* I've broke down the library's door. I'm too big to fit myself, what about you? Could you fit?", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVII", "§bMarch Ash", "And in the sand, respite.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 1", "Catarrh", "The Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHear what mi blah, young one, for mi blah lat h’dub honors by which the orc lives, agh h’dub pillars on which he stands.\n\nSTRENGTH\nVALOR\nBOLDNESS\nCONTENTMENT\n\nWISDOM\nFORTHRIGHTNESS\nDISCIPLINE\n\nStrength is the simplest honor. It is by nub means easy to attain, but very easy to lose. It comes with the weight of earth, yet drifts away on the currents of the river from the unwary. Yet, for he who keeps watch, it\n\nstands firm as iron. By it, the body stands strong. Without it, the bones fall as dry reeds. By the strong outer self, the strong inner self is protected.\n\nValor is that which compels us to stand. By it, we face our enemies agh conquer our fears. Turn nub\n\nfrom the challenges of life. Cower nub before latz foes. Stand agh face those who oppose lat.\n\nBoldness is that energy by which we charge into the flames. Be unafraid of risk. It is the gate to many rewards. As valor makes us stand our ground,\n\nboldness commands us to press forward.\n\nContentment is the key to satisfaction. Trust nub in wealth, for gold flees as the sands on the night winds. Trust nub in land, for many lands agh whole continents have been lost before this ash. Be content with\n\nlatz lusk agh latz bread. If you have a blarg, a mate, agh cubs, lat be truly blessed beyond measure.\n\nWisdom is born of a strong mind. It is more practical than philosophy, agh goes beyond mere knowledge. It is the ability for right living, common sense,\n\nwit, resolution of life’s problems, agh success beyond material gain. Gruk for latself, but heed the blahings of those more experienced with the respect agh consideration due them. Learn from life, agh apply latz learning in a way that means something.\n\nForthrightness is honesty agh directness. It is intentional clarity of blahing, agh the absence of deception. Blah truth. Blah to blah, nub to flatter. Do as lat blah, agh let latz blah be latz bond. If lat blah it, mean it. Live it\n\nDiscipline is that\n\nwhich keeps latz life in order. Without it, all other honors forsake lat, for honor demands that the honorable governs his life with the will of iron. Hard work agh control of the self hold body agh mind together.\n\nStand firm in all these things, agh lat\n\nwill stand indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary: Slave", "§bHileia'elr", "Kivessin got his payback for me getting him banished, I suppose... He kidnapped me, and sold me to an Uruk. Roklah'Braduk, a blacksmith. So far, he's kicked, scarred, and branded me with a big 'B' on my back.\n\nIt hasn't been too bad so far... By comparison. Although, when Roklah isn't around, the other Uruk throw food at me and make fun of me.\n\nAside from Kivessin being pissed, Kale isn't that happy, either.\n\nI understand why she's mad, though. I don't think she has a right to be, but... I understand. Kale and Kivessin were an item, so it must pain her to not be able to run the clinic and see him at the same time. I'm not mad at her, though.\n\nAlthough, Kivessin is going to pay when I escape from this prison of a city... I don't care how far I have to go. He ruined every aspect of my life... My career, my love lift, and my own body.\n\nOf course, I won't kill him... I can find a punishment even worse than death for good ol' Kivessin. He told me that, \"I'll only make you go through what I did,\" and, \"I hope you've learned your lesson, Hileia.\"\n\nWhat Kivessin doesn't realize is that I'M the good guy here, HE'S the criminal. He killed a noble, and since he was a guard, I had to tell someone... I was the good citizen, he was the murderer. I swear, he'll suffer once I escape...\n\n-------------------Today, I was kicked by three other Uruk whilst Roklah was out. I wanted to communicate with them, so I attempted to speak 'Blah.' They didn't appreciate it. I was thrown onto the ground by one of them, the beaten.\n\nOne kicked me in the eye so hard, I need an eyepatch now... This is why I hate Uruk.\n\nAfter chopping down wood, Roklah took me to the Caliphate to auction me off. Someone tried buying me, but when the bid was too low,\n\nmy master just dragged me back to the Iron Uzg. Now, I'm sitting here writing, while he makes some sword.\n\n-------------------Kale... Actually visited me. She heard about the auction, and she tried to buy me back.\n\nI am a bit... in shock. I thought she didn't care about me anymore. She offered my master 100 minas, far more than at the auction. He decided he wanted to keep me though, simply to show me off to, 'The Rex.'\n\nKale wished to speak to me, but... I don't think I'm quite ready for that, yet.\n\nRecently, I've been picking up on the so called 'Language' called Blah. It's easy to do that if you stay in one place long enough...\n\n\"Too bad I can't use it, though... A non-Uruk speaking Blah is like... I'm not even sure. It's just disrespectful. It's alright, though. They're disgusting creatures, anyhow. I don't care to speak their language.\n-------------------\n\nWhilst I was cutting down more trees, Roklah and his crew joined me to get more wood for some project... I dropped the axe on the ground, then ran for the docks. Instantly, I went to the Caliphate.\n\nRunning away was sure to get me a beating, but I didn't care. I  wanted to visit the Caliphate... The place I hadn't visited in months. \n\nWhen I arrived, Kale was treating a patient in her clinic.\n\nShe instantly stopped what she was doing to greet me with open arms. Now, she's finishing up in the surgical room, and then she's going to serve us some tea.\n\nOh wow... That was, uh... Surprising. Not much happened, but Kale told me that she was never a 'Thing' with Kivessin in the first place! It was just to get him out of some arranged marriage... The nerve.\n\nWhile I am slightly upset that they lied to me about that, I also don't mind... After all, this should mean that Kale won't mind when I cast Kivessin into a living nightmare.\n-------------------I suppose I haven't learned my lesson.\n\nAfter returning to the Iron Uzg, I got a punch to the forehead. That was it, though. Nothing serious... Although, now I'm in Laureh'lin. And I just lost 60 mina from gambling...\n\nSome geezer named Lornengoth or something. Green eyes, long white beard, no shirt. Whatever, though. He won it fair and square through gambling with me all night. Lucky him.\n-------------------\n\nBack in the Iron Uzg... After another week of work, there's some... Tournament happening. Something the Uruk call 'Klomping.' I heard a horn sound while I was on the road, so I came to watch.\n\nSome people from the Caliphate were coming in to fight, so the Uruk already there needed to warm up... And guess who they used as their training dummy? That's right, the only non-Uruk there. I was just a punching bag for 10 minutes.\n\nWhen the arena was full of fighters and spectators, the fighting began. So many Uruk were there, but plenty of Valah, Mali, and Kah. One fight after the next, it came down to the final two: The Rex himself, and some guy named Rilkor.\n\nThe first match was won by the Rex. He beat Rilkor to the ground... I was surprised he was alright to keep on going! Although, in the second round, The Rex took quite a beating. In the final round, Rilkor came out on top.\n\nNow, he received some sword as his prize, and he's, 'Champion of the Iron Uzg.' I didn't pay too much attention... I don't care much for this type of entertainment.\n-------------------\n\nLooking through my bag today, while Roklah was busy repairing some tools, I found an old book written by Nienna. It was her dark arts book... I had never read it before, so I decided to give it a read.\n\nIt's all very fascinating. Puppets bound by darkness, mages rising dead bodies from their graves; However, one particular article caught my eye...\n\nSoul contractors... The idea of binding your soul to a physical document is quite... scary. Scary, but interesting. And I was wondering- Is this a possible option for revenge on Kivessin?\n\nNo, revenge is the wrong word... I don't want revenge. I simply want to rid him from this world to protect everyone else from his evil presence. Maybe send him into a deep sleep, where he has the most wonderful dreams.\n\nEither way, I wouldn't mind sacraficing something of mine to keep him from harming others... If a contract is what it takes, then that's what I'll do. I would just need to actually FIND someone with the ability to make a contract, first...\n\nHa, hell, I'd do it myself if I had to! Wait, no... That wouldn't work. I would still have to carry out the process myself, even if I did know soul contracting magic. And I really have no way to do that, besides kill him...\n\nBut who am I kidding? He's an assasin, and I'm a Mali'aheral from Haelun'or that writes romance novels for a living- Well, used to, anyways... But still, becoming a soul contractor... I wonder what that's like for them.\n\nI bet it's fun for them, but I couldn't imagine skinning someone alive. It must be an awful process that would drive one to insanity. And for something so trivial as a contract? Well, actually, I can see why it'd be important...\n\n-------------------Do I even have anything else to live for? Those gates are wide open, and I could just run out, but... What would be the point? I suppose I should learn how the world has been changed since I've been gone...\n\nBut what if it's changed for the worse? Maybe there's nothing left for me out there, but... If there isn't, staying in this hell hole isn't going to solve anything. I just have to run for it, if Roklah comes for my head, so be it.\n\n-------------------About to enter the Caliphate again... With no clothes. I'm done with this diary. After almost a year of writing, I think it'd be best to leave it as it is. Although, that just means that I can start a new chapter to my life.\n\n~Hileia'elr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir", "§bUnknown", "She walked onwards, onwards through the darkness. She had walked for so long, so far. The shadows around her seemed like hands, hands that wanted to grab her and drag her into the abyss below. She was unable to recall when she began her trek.\n\nHer memories were a blur. No matter how hard she tried to remember, she only found that she couldn't. The empty shadows devoured her name and soul. Who was I, why am I walking? Questions plagued her mind everyday.\n\nThough. she couldn't tell if it was day or not. She couldn't remember what sunlight was like. What the warm essence of day was like on her skin had left her mind long ago. The shadows had drained her life away many centuries, at least she assumed she...\n\nhad been there for that long. Time was irrelevant in the darkness. All of the pain, all of the loneliness, and all of the despair beat her down every second that passed by. Yet, there was one thing that kept her mind intact...\n\nOne simple thought that kept the infernal darkness at bay...§0\n§0\n§0\"I must keep going...\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VIII", "§bMarch Ash", "The jungle is a wild place. There is more life -- more biodiversity here -- than most other places in Axios. Only the shrublands match it in the number of species. Survival is an art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic & You", "§bNienna Calm", "Dark Magic\n      And You!\n-------------------  A Guard's Guide to\n  Identifying Dark \n          Mages\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\n\n      ForeWord\n-------------------This book was written with the intent to educate the guardmen and women of the Caliphate of Khalestine. However, should you find this book in your possession, I would suggest reading it anyways. It is a good\n\nguide for identifying Dark mages.\n\n     What is a\n    Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including Pacts with dark gods, Rituals set forth by\n\nIblees, and other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\n\n    Necromancy\n-------------------\nNecromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. It's age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\n\nthis world today. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state. Since Necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life, or reports of people feeling drained after\n\ntouching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\n\n   Frost Witches\n-------------------Frost Witches are monsters of Ice and Snow who disguise themselves as women and prey upon the libido of Men. The Frost Witch is an easy threat to counter in the hot weather of the Caliphate, but requires constant\n\nvigilance to identify. A Frost Witch's true form is bright blue, but using her curse's magic, she is able to take any form she pleases, so long as that form is female. Frost Witches use these disguises to trick men into a false sense of security,\n\nwhereupon they will take their true form, and devour the unsuspecting male.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe easiest way to identify a Frost Witch is by touching their skin. A frost witch's body temperature is colder than anything one could imagine.\n\nThere is no way for them to disguise this. Also, because of this impairment, any disguised frost Witch will show signs of great fatigue under the Caliphate sun. Any women demonstrating a severe aversion to high temperatures and regular food should have\n\nthe temperature of their skin checked immediately.\n\n       Shades\n-------------------\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, second personality that desires for only chaos and\n\ndestruction. Shades are capable of corrupting every form of Arcane magic, empowering their spells with the dark powers of Iblees himself.\n\nHow to Identify:\nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only\n\nrevealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air. Their ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of\n\nbeing a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics, and these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a Shade.\n\n Soul Puppeteers\n-------------------\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), They are able to bring sickness, pain, and even death to a\n\nperson from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify:\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer\n\nstraight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies. If you suspect someone of Soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it's the\n\nonly way to confirm for sure.\n\n Soul Contractors\n-------------------Soul Contractors are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word. This would be potentially useful, if not for the material they must fashion these\n\ndocuments on. Soul Contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken whilst they were still alive. It is a brutal and horrifying process, that speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nHow to Identify:\nLike Soul Puppeteers,\n\nit is hard to identify a Soul Contractor. The only way to tell for sure is to either catch them in the act, or discover their flaying equipment, which may not even be on their person.\n\n   Black-Dragon\n     Parasites\n-------------------A more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its hosts and causes\n\ncauses them to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how is parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you keep any suspected carrier of this foul creature far away from\n\none's person at all times. It is unknown at this time if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they be either expelled from the city on sight, or, in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify:\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\n\nare easy to identify. All carriers of the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area. If you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full-body search immediately.\n\n General Warning\n    Signs Of A\n    Dark Mage\n-------------------\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general. These are by no means\n\ndeciding factors in a suspect's ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nBe Suspicious Of Any Persons you see that:\n\n-Wear Primarily Black Robes.\n\n-Are Hooded at all times\n\n-Possess bright red eyes.\n\n-Project a magical Aura that Black, Gray, or Red in color.\n\nAs a guard of the Caliphate, it is up to YOU to root out these psychopathic evildoers wherever they might rise their ugly heads. For the sake of our grand city, do your duty well.", ""),
        StaticBook("God Dream Theory", "§bDaniel 'Vince' Ward", "\"In the beginning there was nothing, only the Void, and from this Void came a light, although in truth it wasn't a light, but that is the closest one may come to describing the existence of such a thing, and this light was the Creator, whom spoke the -\n\n- world into existence.\"§0\n§0\n§0   Look upon the world around you and how do you see it? Is it a thing of many colors, yet totally separate from you? \"There is a window, a chair, a cup\", I hear you say, but in truth they are all the same, including yourself.\n\n   Existence is that of an illusion, a perception brought about by a paradoxical knowing between all beings. A dream of sorts, that is ever-changing and fluid, yet we remain unaware as a dreamer does his unconscious ventures. Except we are not the only -\n\n- dreamer, we are all a fragment of the single dreamer, that of a single being that encompasses the hemisphere of realms. It is an unknowing, unconscious god in an eternal sleep, resistant to the unending nothingness around it. In this way, one may call -\n\n- it the 'god dream'. Who this eternal slumbering god may be is up to you to decide. Is it the Creator? Willingly and consciously directing the flow of change? Or is it everything, and the Creator is but another fragment, an infinity within a being -\n\nbeyond infinity?§0\n§0\n§0By the power of the conduits, some have come to realize the truth that we are all souls connected, creating a network of unending ethereal glow unseen by our physical eyes, but a truth nonetheless. What this truly means may have -\n\n- several answers, as does many things in this existence. It is because we are all just a single part of this dreaming entity, unknowing to the eternal truth. The truth being that there is none. What you make of this is up to your own perception, but -\n\nknow that because we are all one, each answer is correct, even if they are entirely contradicting, such is the nature of existing: contradicting and paradoxical.§0\n§0\n§0   The implications of such a revelation is vast, and staggering. Because of this, -\n\nperhaps one may come to understand what 'magic' truly means, and the nature of existence. When a person realigns their mind into the state of nothingness such as the Void, they pull their minds closer to the ultimate truth, much as a dreaming mind may -\n\n- start to realize it is dreaming, and may thus become lucid. This revelation does not always come to us in full, as many act instinctively, bending the realm without fully knowing what it means, acting by a spreadsheet of pre-conceived notions.\n\n   Regardless, when a mind realigns itself to the ultimate truth, and connects with the Void, the true existence beyond the pre-mentioned 'light', one can realize that the world around them is apt to be changed from their will, much as a dreamer may -\n\n- alter their dreamscape by the force of their will. The difference here is that we are but fragments, and not the whole known as the sleeping god, and thus do not hold ultimate sway over the world. We are limited, and cannot change the fundamental -\n\n- illusions of law placed upon the world. Although in truth these fundamental existential laws of the universe too may be changed with enough force, force that cannot be contained within we mortals, nor even the gods. Yet, together, perhaps...\n\nAnd so we are often forced to follow such pre-established law, but they are loose and malleable, capable of stepping around in many instances. With this, a fragment with limited power, gaining lucidity towards the external existence such as the Void, one-\n\n- may come to realize their ability in altering the world around them much as a dreamer does when becoming lucid in their unconscious ventures. §0\n§0We are all one sleeping entity, but perhaps one day we may realize that existence is but an illusion, a -\n\npeaceful dream we are all having together. What we do with such a dream is up to us. Will it be nightmarish and harsh, or calming and free-flowing like a river? With the revelation that is 'magic', we come to lucidity and enlightenment, and realize the -\n\n- power that holds. To contemplate such things is the way of a wizard, understanding that things are not so regimented as one may hope to believe. But regardless, one day we may all discover lucidity. What this means is yet to be explored, but perhaps in-\n\n- such a way we may reconvene as an awakened slumbering god.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 2", "Catarrh", "The second book of the Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka, agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHeed mi warning, all who are wise, for mi blah lat h’dub dishonors by which an orc is ruined, agh h’dub shames which may befall him.\n\nWEAKNESS\nIRRESOLUTION\n\nCOWARDICE\nAVARICE\nTHOUGHTLESSNESS\nDUPLICITY\nCOMPLACENCY\n\nWeakness, blah’d plainly, is the absence of strength. Be nub frail, agh neglect nub the body. He who can-nub defend himself, how can he defend that for which he stands? To give place to weakness is\n\nto keep latz bub’hoshest treasure in a fortress of straw.\n\nIrresolution is the way of he who falters in the presence of adversity. Do nub quail when the storm thunders. Do nub turn away when latz enemies roar. Be nub like the rabbit, who, when he is\n\nfrightened but a little, flees to his hole for safety. The rabbit is prey, agh the orc must never be prey.\n\nCowardice halts the feet, agh binds the spirit. Nub hosh thing comes to the coward, for the coward takes nub risk. The coward never takes the\n\ndifficult path. There is no success for such an ash. All his ways are worthless, agh his life profitless.\n\nAvarice is the heart of the empty spirit. Lust for gold blinds the eyes to truth, agh numbs the mind to wisdom. It makes the senses dull, such that\n\nhe whose life is governed by the mina can-nub perceive honor, agh hears nub the call of Krug.\n\nThoughtlessness is to the mind as weakness is to the body. The ash who gruks nub is nub’hosher than the blind or the deaf, for he chooses himself nub to gruk\n\nthe way to live rightly. He is blind to the way in which he should walk, agh the advice of the wise enters nub his ear. All his workings are senseless, agh his feet lead him to shame.\n\nDuplicity is the forked tongue of the dishonorable. The duplicitous\n\nash blahs “yub” with his mouth, but “nub” in his spirit. His blah can-nub be trusted, for he is a serpent agh a companion to serpents. With his face he grins agh flatters, but behind his back he bears a double-edged dagger to betray lat. Do nub be like\n\nsuch an ash, for the number of those who will hear him dwindles by the hour.\n\nComplacency is the quicksand upon which the glob builds a blarg. It is a hosh-smelling poison, agh a smooth road which leads to ruin. Complacency lulls lat to sleep with a soft\n\ntouch agh sweet songs, but, when lat have awoken, it has stolen latz strength, latz mate, agh all latz bread.\n\nThe ash who falls into any of these falls surely agh quickly to his destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancers V I", "§bFreyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into Necromancers Volume I\n\nA picture of a man in dark robes standing over dying man a stream of dark green is slowing from the dying man into the robed man hand, two decaying zombies stand behind the dark robed man awaiting his orders*\n\n\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront Necromancers unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\n\n\nA Short Introduction\nNecromancy is the defined pragmatically as the utilisation of Life-Force. Necromancers usually have tell-tale signs of their necromancy,\n\n It is like poking a hole in a bucket they can take others life force with the imbalance but their own life force is slowly drained.\n Necromancy is the draining of life-force for nefarious purposes commonly, it’s an art shunned by many.\n\nAppearance\nThey look like us, For all you know one could be next to you they are very hard to find the only true tell is that many will have a very pale look and are extremely sensitive\n\nand weak but this does not go for all necromancers. Basically, signs of decay on their bodies would be a significant give-away.\n\nBehavior\nDue to the extreme difficulty of actually picking one out in a crowded this second cant be added in details.\n\nStrengths\nThey have the power to resurrect the dead and use them as Minions.\nThey can drain the life force of living things leading to a quick death.\n\nWeakness.\nLike all mages they are physically weak and can be killed easily..\nSome instances, holy magic can effect them but it's not always the case. \nThey also have the ability to curse other by modifying life force.\n\nOrigins and Additional details\nHow mortals found this magic is unknown, but it's safe to conclude that the undead under Iblees was instrumental to the art during Aegis\n\nIt’s likely that they drain life-force whilst using their own bodies to draw it, whether through physical means or through other ways such as mists.\n\n\nA note of warning. \nLearning Necromancy is a taboo and would lead to severe repercussions on one’s own wellbeing and health.\n\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))Further Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking", "§bLillian", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   A Guide To Basic\n         Cooking\n     \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    <><><><><><><><><>\n\n  <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Dough~~~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo binds of wheat.\nCooking Pot.\n\nFind the granules of wheat and remove them, before grindng them and mixing them with a small amount of water. You now have a basic dough.\n\n  <><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Bread~~~~~~Ingredients:\nOne lump of dough\n\nCut off a small amount of the dough made previously, and form it into a ball. Place it in your cooking pot over your hot water, and wait for it to cook.\n\n  <><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pan-Cakes~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo portions of dough.\nCut your dough into two portions, and then go to flatten them out, and place them in your cooking pot side by side over heated water.\n\n  <><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Fish~~~~~~~\n\nIngredients:\nRaw fish of your choice.\n\nRemove the bones of the fish, and peel off one layer of scales, placing it in the cooking pot with the small amount of seasoning.\n\n  <><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Meats~~~~~~\nIngredients: Your choice of raw meat.\n\nSeason the meat with your choice of herb or salt, and then place it in your cooking pot, with a small amount of fat, or water.", ""),
        StaticBook("EWOROENLETEA", "§bThurak'Yar", "Entities within our realm of Existence no Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\nOr, Void Translocation\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1'st of Snow's Maiden, 1488\n\n1. Introduction\n\n2. Study\n\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n\n4. Destruction\n\n5. Re-Creation\n\nIt does no take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, winin and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\n\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull real matter from The Void.\n\nBut what is a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\n\nStudy\n\nTake within your hands something that exists. \nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing \nan 'Entity'. Begins your examination in the simplest of interests:\nForm.\n\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n \nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\n\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily inclined\n\ntowards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\n\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\n\nSensory Overhaul\n\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective\n\nwith the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not a single thing\n\nbut the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not.\n\nCertainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\ndown, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you muse measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this\n\nworld but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently\n\nexisting within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of\n\nglass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\n\nNo Longer Existing\n\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangiable\n\njust stops and is no more. \nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and therefore able\n\nto return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something\n\nfor that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The\n\nVoid that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the\n\npotential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\n\nTo Return Again\n\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only\n\nthing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work) will assign the potential\n\nwith its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood Job,\nYou Meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Daniel", "§bNemir", "It had grown heavy, my soul§0\n§0Sinking down, just as my heart§0\n§0Down, slowly, into the depths of mourning.§0\n§0\n§0There was no sun, my beloved;§0\n§0Down here, there was no you.\n\nI could not feel whole§0\n§0My love had been torn apart§0\n§0Down more, there was only sobbing.§0\n§0\n§0O' a kiss had suddenly removed my dread§0\n§0A light had suddenly taken away the cold dew.\n\nYour return, my sun, had arisen§0\n§0Spreading your loving warmth to me§0\n§0I broke free from despair's grip§0\n§0And unto your arms I smiled.§0\n§0\n§0I love you.§0\n§0\n§0- Nemir", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Study the properties of glass.§0\n§0\n§0Speak with Armin on the melted ferrum ball.§0\n§0\n§0Bring jewlery that I'd like to be enchanted.§0\n§0\n§0Study arcanism", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Strange white, magical pillar. - 3180/128/1757§0\n§0\n§0Found Katherine and Vargen, they've set up their tents with the humans.  I've decided to set up mine there before looking for the others.§0\n\nFound another strange obelisk, looks somewhat like the other near the wood elves.  This looks to be made of stone.  It's right next to the dwarven camp, 1154/88/-1917§0\n§0\n§0Frozen tree, 468/71/-2201\n\nWorld just.. ends.  It leads to a seemingly endless pit. -723/107/-3152§0\n§0\n§0Another weird obelisk is near Haria, no one knows what these are for.§0\n§0\n§0Other obelisk near druids at -\n\n2730 68 -288§0\n§0\n§0Another obelisk in the middle of no where, XYZ: -1975 98 -2270§0\n§0\n§0Portal to the Sunless Sanctum is also near here, -2149 98 -1924§0\n§0\n§0Large ruined building is also near the previously -\n\n- two mentioned. -1894 146 -2309§0\n§0\n§0Another obelisk near Ker'nor, lilacs surround it. 3237 111 1697§0\n§0\n§0In the north, near the Library I've come across some ruins.  A crumbled building, and\n\na few bridges, another in the area seems to've completely collapsed.  Beneath it, was some sort of hole along the freezing river.  Inside it I've discovered a mural, showing what looks to be elves bowing to some white orb in the sky. -1504 62 -1200\n\nRuined city with dragon statues.  It's called The Fell City of Dreinloch. 3638 72 -1863§0\n§0\n§0Remember \"Benny Black\"§0\n§0\n§0Strange building in the mountains. -823 227 -1510\n\nStrange mountain with.. black shit on the top. 656 129 -1742 - Volcano§0\n§0\n§0Another obelisk stands within a forest north east of the Orenian capital. 1283 85 -580§0\n§0\n§0There are 10 obelisks, says a kha, i have 7\n\nI hear there's another obelisk around the orcs, that makes eight.§0\n§0\n§0Odd cave entrance on the isle of Sutica, -107 43 -935  Another entrance similar to this one, leading to a HUGE underground, glowing cave. 245 43 -560\n\nSome strange.. altar?  Is within one of this large glowing caves beneath the Sutican mountains.  912 26 -303§0\n§0\n§0The ninth obelisk that I've discovered is on the isles of Sutica, the land surrounding it is.. rotted or just dead.\n\nThere are lakes of lava, this one is in the middle of one. -862 85 250§0\n§0\n§0Final obelisk discovered is at the high elves, -2739 207 -192§0\n§0\n§0The obelisk at the orcs is 2547 48 1856\n\nit's bigger than the rest.  And stands in the middle or near the middle of a lake§0\n§0\n§0Nice place in the north, small pond and beautiful waterfalls between two mountains. 1327 135 -1538\n\nA beautiful lake hidden within the mountains, a little waterfall leads into it.  It's so secluded and gives off of a tranquil feeling. -83 70 -1166§0\n§0\n§0Strange, eldritch, old man classfied as a spook was spotted in Johannaseburg -\n\n- it was standing over a woman who as unconscious.  Seemed as if it were in a trance while doing this, this was broken when Richard stabbed it.  He used a ferrum weapon and it caused it pain, there was no aurum or salt.  Weapon was clean.  The creature -\n\n- had a strange, light blue ooze seep out from the wound.  Its name is Sephtis?§0\n§0\n§0Obelisk near warhawkes§0\n§0\n§0Volcano south of Sergei's barony§0\n§0135 249 -1584§0\n\nHauxir has returned, find John§0\n§0\n§0Found another mural, looks just like the one I found on the riverside north of the library.  Elves bow to a white orb in the sky. It's located within a cave, south of the barony. -21 127 -1554\n\nAnother mural of elves bowing to a white orb is actually under the large tree everyone woke up in at the docks.§0\n§0\n§0Somewhat odd and hidden cave, a waterfall comes out of it.  It's between Oren and the Wood elves, 3592 144 140\n\n-try to find anything on a fountain of youth§0\n§0- find lori ireheart§0\n§0-ask sarrion about merit pasqual? pascal?§0\n§0\n§0\n§0[!]A sketch is here, it shows a few short birch trees.  Giant mushrooms tower over them.  Written --\n\nbeneath the drawing is a poor scrawling of the map to Axios.  A northern island is circled near the dwarves. ((2132 100 -2951))§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Sephtis update: ---\n\nIt's been a while since I've been exploring, started to exlpore the Harian island again.  Decided to look past the obelisk looking over the old warhawke camp and came across these peculiar ruins.  The stone seems crumbled, but I've made the shape of --\n\na bird-like head sticking out of the mountain.  It's huge.  It's long, stone arm lifts up from the ground and clutches what looks to be a sword with its blade stuck into the earth. 1128 109 1791\n\nLook for some place that just looks magical for Armin.§0\n§0\n§0[!] The handwriting in this entry looks rushed[!] The ice cavern near Haria or whatever, the maze.. those --\n\njaws(?) all of that blood... West of 740 107 1867", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "It was a normal, quiet day for me.  I was at the Library of Dragur, sitting alone behind the front desk.§0\n§0\n§0My friend, Tara, rode in on her horse, I believe she named it Pinecone?  Anyways, we greeted each other and I told her\n\nof the stables we've got for travellers near the entrance to the garden.  She tied up her steed there and returned, asking if we had any books on medicines.§0\n§0\n§0I was in the middle of telling her our variety of books fitting that general section\n\nwhen an elf walked in.  It was another friend of mine, but I suppose friend is a rather strong word to use since it had been years since I've seen him.  It was Ibar, a rather goofy and clumsy paladin.§0\n§0\n§0I was quite surprised to see him, especially\n\nat the library.  I had tried asking him where he had been and whatnot before some young man charged into the building, shouting that his friend needed help.  He looked as if he was a resident to Haria due to his robes and the fact that he\n\nkept thanking \"Allah\" about us being there. He said his friend Chet needed help and that he had gone into some large keep.  The young man seemed to've been in a state of panic and was out of breath so I sorta understood about half of what he said.\n\nThe three of us decided to help the poor man and Chet so he gave us a key saying that it'd be needed in order to enter the castle.  So the three of us went on, the young man staying behind.§0\n§0\n§0Took us about a half\n\na day walk or so until we reached the large castle, good thing Tara knew where it was exactly otherwise I got a feeling we would've been wandering around longer.§0\n§0\n§0As we approached the gigantic keep I felt uneasy.  Something\n\nabout it seemed off to me, something dark.§0\n§0\n§0It didn't take too long for us to find a small ferrum door on the side, the key unlocked it and we entered a dark room connected to a hallway lit by a dim candle.  I took the candle so I could at least get\n\nan idea of where I was going.§0\n§0\n§0The hallway led into what looked like a cave?  There was another candle which was taken by Ibar.  The small cavern-like tunnel lead upwards, into an overgrown garden.  A harsh wind put out our candles, but we had the\n\nsun now so it didn't matter too much.  The garen seemed to've been singing with little critters.  It was the only thing which I found calming within the place.  Tara ended up finding another door hidden away, Ibar seemed eager to see what was behind it\n\nbut I wanted to continue searching around the garden before going through more doors.  Tara agreed after unlocking it, but Ibar was a bit of a piece of shit and bolted through it.  So we just decided to follow, not wanting for us to get split up.\n\nThe room we entered a few peculiar doors.  Were they doors?  No idea, but that's what I'm calling them.  The metal they were made of had a red tone to it, there was an odd seal on the door as well.  We couldn't get past it so we moved on to this hallway.\n\nIt lead into a room with a hole in the roof and a pit in the center of the floor.  Something clearly happened here.  Tara and Ibar quickly climbed down into the pit, if one were to look closer there was something at the bottom, laying on the ground.\n\nThe creature twitched here and there, as if it were alive.  And it was, but barely.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Lesson 1 Notes.§0\n§0\n§0-Wards are not inheritly put into objects.  WArds are a separate spell that you can cast that is a part of transfiguration that you can also enchant into an item.§0\n§0-The enchantment you make is not putting\n\ninto the gem.  Rather, it is putting into the item itself.  The gem merely stores the mana used for the spell§0\n§0-Transmuation is the manipulation of mana that is stored into every single object of existance.§0\n§0-In order to do anything with transmutation\n\none must know about the material and it's properties at its desired state. The process of it is pooling your mana into an object to tap it's mana to change certain aspects of it.§0\n§0-Enchanting is weaving a spell into an item so that the spell can be\n\ncasted from that object.  The mana used for it is stored in a mana gem on the object.§0\n§0-There are two types of enchantings. The 'regular' version is just simple enchanting.  Where the transfigurationist casts and uses their own spell for enchanting.\n\nThe other version is known as Entrapment.  More will be learned about this at a later time.§0\n§0-Abjurations are the 'anti-magic' of transfiguration.  Their bases of them is to disrupt the mana anchor of the targetted spell.§0\n§0-A mana anchor is\n\nthe location in the world that you create what is essentially a tear in the void in which you funnel your mana into. §0\n§0-There are two types of abjurations.  One is the abjuration, the next is a ward. An abjuration is more of a projectile.  It may only\n\ndisrupt one type of magic as a ward can disrupt several.  A ward is more like a barrier.  But in order to disrupt any sort of magic with either of these, the transfigurationist must have good knowledge of the magic. (By having knowledge of the magic, you\n\nneed to have someone describe and show it to you.) §0\n§0-Abjurations are swifter to cast than wards.§0\n§0\n§0Homework: Study the iron ball, sapphire gem, and list uses of transmutation.§0\n§0\n§0-Final note. Transmuation can\n\nbe done at most of an arm's length away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "What can transmutation be helpful for?§0\n§0\n§0Heating up water for cooking, drinking, or perhaps for alchemy.  Other liquids as well, with enough study and understanding of them.§0\n§0\n§0Cooling beverages for refreshing drinks.\n\nI wonder if it could be used to warm or cool the air around one's self just as Daniel did for the first and a half date.§0\n§0\n§0If an enemy threatens you with a dagger, keeping it still but pointed at you, and you know -\n\n- of the material is made out of, perhaps you could heat it up enough to melt the blade?  It'd be an odd situation, but could possible work.§0\n§0\n§0Heat clothing in cool temperatures.§0\n§0\n§0Cool clothing in warm temperatures.\n\nCould be used to repair clothing§0\n§0\n§0Dying clothing§0\n§0\n§0Changing the color(s) of things", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 3", "§bAnthron", "Curious words as a continuation from part 2. 1 - 4\n-------------------Elven Grammar 5 - 41\n------------------\nElven counting 42 - 45\n-------------------more on part 3\n-------------------\nAgain, more thanks to Sporadic for making the post!\n\nan*h- (a/o/i/e/u):\n\nBy adding one these five vowels into the place of the asterisk the prefix takes on a new usage. This prefix gains many new meanings when combined with other affixes and relies heavily on context.\n\nSentence order is especially important when using this prefix multiple times.\nElan*h [a/o/i/e]: North, South, East and West respectively.\n\nanh'sae: expanding, stretching - replacing the apostrophe with a vowel specifies in which direction.\n\nan*h il'an*h: - refers to a diagonal path, defined by the vowel used.\n-------------------\n\nElven Grammar.\n-------------------Sentence Order: The common order of elvish sentences is Subject-object-verb.\n\nPlural nouns: indicated by the suffix -an.\n\nThe apostrophe: Used in certain cases and possibly dictates a certain pronunciation.\nCurrent known uses are:\n\n*Denoting certain honorifics (such as sainted)\n*Between a modifier and a verb\n\n*Between a word and its suffixes (more on this below).\n*With the word 'eyha' (and) to connect sentences and and in terms of a list.\n\nUse of affixes: This has shown to be a very important factor in Elven language. Elves, tend to use multiple affixes to further define their nouns and verbs, rather than using separate words. For these, the following rules exist:\n\n*Most affixes seems to have two forms, depending on wether or not the word it relates to ends or begins with a vowel\n*Suffixes often get added with an apostrophe between it and the word.\n\n*If a word has multiple suffixes, there will only be an apostrophe between the full word and its last suffix. The priority in ordering the suffixes remains unknown.\n\n*If a suffix is seperated by the apostrophe, it inflects as if the last letter of the word it relates to was a consonant.\n\nRecombination of words:\nWhen one understands the heavy use of affixes and their combining to forge words,\n\n it is not surprising that the elves relied on a dictionary where this recombination was prevalent in creating new words. \nTheir core words were little, but their abundant use of affixes and linking words still allowed them to describe nearly anything\n\nunder the sun.\nExamples of this are:\nnarn'vallei: travel'water -> swim\nnarn'acaele: travel'sky -> fly\nathrinarn'acaele: serpenttraveling'sky -> Dragon.\npar'karinah: Before the sunrise -> Dawn\n\npar'ker: Before the sunset -> Dusk.\nuvul'igne: Firepowder -> Ash\nuvul'thrurn: Explosive powder -> Gunpowder\n\nWe also see this occuring a lot when the word tali is involved.\n\nMany more examples may be discovered by the studious scholar soon. Take heed, however, that any particular combination, while perhaps comprehensible, may not be correct. The language of nature seems very particular on what words may coexist in harmony.\n\n-------------------Affiliation: The suffix 'leh (note the apostrophe) designates affiliation, the possession of the object by the subject.\nNote: If no object is present, the suffix is implied to mean something similar to 'lives' or 'spirit'. However,\n\nit is not placed in translation\nEx: part of a common farewell 'kaean'leh evareh', means 'may (it) protect our spirit' literally, but is translated to 'may (it) protect us'.\n-------------------\n\nKnown inflections of the elven verbs:\n\nIn this section, the dash indicates the stem of the word.\n\n*-e: First person singular\n\n*-a: Second person singular\n\n*-e: Third person singular\n*-ae: First person plural\n*-an: second person plural\n*-eyae: Third person plural\n*-eh: Optative singular\n*-erih: Optative plural The optative inflection changes slightly depending on the ending letters of a\n\nverb. Most verbs end in -er, but if one ends in -ar the plural inflection of the optative becomes -arih ( the -ar- syllable is not repeated!). A verb ending in -h will have the -h- replaced by the full inflection of the optative (thus eth becoming eteh\n\nand eterih. Other irregular verbs have the inflection simply added to the end.\n\n*The stem of a verb functions as a singular imperative.\n*The stem of a verb used as a suffix to a noun (apostrophe where required) is a modifier\n\n*The optative serves as a wish ('may' + verb) in most cases. However, adding the negative (-ne) affix after the verb indicates the lack of permission.\n-------------------Pronouns as a subject:\n\nA pronoun is usually not used to denote the subject of a word, as the inflection of the verb itself would usually denote in which person the verb is denoted. However, on occasion a rather critical ambiguity may arise, like in the following example:\n\name ignere: The forest burns.\nShould we 'assume' a pronoun here, we can suggest that this sentence may also be translated as 'I burn the forest' or even 'he burns the forest'. This ambiguity is too serious to ignore, and therefore we are expected\n\nto place another pronoun here as the subject if we wish to denote an action like such:\n\nkae ame ignere: I burn the forest.\n\nKnow that a pronoun used as a subject alone never gains the suffix 'leh' (this is possible when it is an object, making the implied translation \"spirit\".)\n-------------------Infinitive:\n\nAn infinitive can be made by tying two verbs together with an apostrophe and adding an 'o' ('or-') prefix to the second verb (the infinitive). The first verb is usually the assisting verb (possibilities include can, must, will) and needs to be the only\n\nstem.\nThe infinitive verb receives the inflections similar to the way to a simple, single verbed sentence would.\nBy Example:\nito ame ern'onarna: You can travel to the woods\n\nAn infinitve can also occur without an assisting verb. In this case, you shall add an o prefix to the verb, but no inflection. An example of this:\nito ame onarn: to travel to the woods.\n\nTake note that the infinitive must not be used to express a wish, as only the optative form may serve this purpose.\n\nPast and future tense:\n\nTo create a past or future tense, we first need to take notice to the time of day. The words an elf uses for tenses depends on whether it's day or night at the time of speaking.\n\nFor a past or future tense, we add one of these four words at the very end of a sentence:\nkarin'ento: next sunrise\nkarin'ante: last sunrise\nker'ento: next sunset\nker'ante: last sunset\n\nThough elves have taken to shortening this to karinto, karinte, kento and kente in more casual speech.\nIf it is night, we use ker'ante for past, and karin'ento for future tense.\n\nIf it is day, we use karin'ante for past, and ker'ento for future tense.\n\nThis remains true even if the time period one wishes to denote is more than one sunset or sunrise from the time of speaking.\n-------------------\n\nThe verbs 'to be' and 'to have'\nBefore reading this, you might find it beneficial to have read about the word 'ito' in the 'CURIOUS WORDS' section.\nNote that:\nito kae: To him / on him\nito kae'leh: To his spirit / on his spirit ('spirit' being implied)\n\nNow, should we place a noun in front of this:\nmali ito kae: An elf to him. -In elvish, this is the equivalent of 'He has an elf'.\nmali ito kae'leh: An elf to his spirit. The equivalent of 'He is an elf'.\n\n\nIt becomes easy to mix these meanings up. After all, kae'leh is the possessive form and seems the logical candidate for the verb 'to have'.\nHowever, the implied addition of 'spirit' is very important here. Elves speak of their spirit, or essence, as\n\nsomething deeply intimate. When something belongs to you as a person, you have it. But when something belongs to your essence, you are it.\n-------------------\n\nCAPITALIZATION\n\nElves do not capitalize the word at the beginning of a sentence the way we do in common. Instead, only on a select few occasions are words capitalized, namely:\n\n*Names (of persons, places, titles)\n\n*Races (Mali, Valah, etc.)\n*Objects of worship (Usul, Velulaei), even when the word's not used to denote the divine being tied to the object\n*When denoting aspects of nature (such as Vuln being the aspect fox.)\n\n*Words of significant concepts are sometimes capitalized, such as 'lye', 'talar', 'acaele' and 'tuva'\n-------------------\n\nELVEN COUNTING\n\nElves, while their numerical system remains a subject of discussion, were able to write numbers 'in full' like we are. That is to say, they could name numbers of any size in regular conversation.\n\nAn Elven number, when expressed in full, consists of multiple words. Each word represents an order of magnitude. They were written in descending order, meaning the largest part of the number came first.\n\nElves had words for the numbers one to ten, and words for a hundred, a thousand, and so on. To denote multiples of hundred,\nhey would take a number from one to ten, and put it in front of a word denoting an order of magnitude, linking the two with an\n\naprostrophe\nDiscovered words for elven numbers are as follows:\n1: oem\n2: niut\n3: hael\n4: vailu\n5: kulin\n6: banih\n7: laier\n8: esun\n9: moiel\n\n10: telu\n100: matelu [ma-(mar-) a preffix for 'very']\n1000: marmatelu\n-------------------CONVENTIONS OF THE ELVEN LANGUAGE \n-continues to part 4-", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bDela Vaik", "My time in the Oder of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. Lets start by steps.\n\nstep 1- Cleaning the wound\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something\n\nwith alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sort. (Of course you need to take the dirt out if there is any in the wound first.) \n\nStep 2- Suttering the wound.\nFor that you will need a needle and some thread. sounds easy right? well not\n\nreally, you need a steady hand and you also so need to do it by theese... Lets call them sub types.\n Sub type 1\nheat up the needle incase it holds any illnesses.\nSub type 2 clean the thread\nYou need to do it because you do not want dirt in\n\nthe wound.\nSub type 3 shuttering\nYou startat well the start of the wound or gash.(warning this does not include small wounds.) you'll then shutter it like you are sewing a rag, a messy, bloody rag that screams like a little girl, a rag non of the\n\nless.\nStep 3- bandaging\nA bandage can be almost any thing, a old rag (as long as its clean.) A bed sheet (as long as its clean.) etc. then you just wrap it up. Done.\n\nBy: Kristoff Herrick", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "§bDiane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\n\n       Foreword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\n\n      The Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usually be\n\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\n\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller blobs.\n\n     The Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a staggering 5\n\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\n\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\n\n  The Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They are like\n\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\n\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\n\n  The Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent boring\n\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\n\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this, they\n\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\n\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\n\n   The Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shapes and sizes,\n\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\n\n The Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\n\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: Alchemy\n\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\n\n    The Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will begin\n\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\n\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\n\n  The Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\n\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\n\n    The Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance constantly.\n\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\n\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\n\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\n\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres are\n\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\n\n    The Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the lands,\n\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\n\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\n\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\n\n   The Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous to fight.\n\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\n\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\n\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\n\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\n\n  The Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. Based on\n\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\n\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle and size,\n\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\n\n    Conclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Stay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat: Volume I", "§bGerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nMarked Combat:\nVolume I\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\n\nThe Magical Versus the Mundane- The Knight's Way of Defense Against the Supernatural:\n===================Through the ages, mankind has faced countless threats, both mundane and magical. The wars against the undead have taught us techniques and-\n\n\n===================countermeasures that can be- with ample experience, skill and prayer- successfully utilized against the unholy and the profane.\n\n\n===================What is Recommended:\n-Numbers\n-Ranged Weaponry\n-Light Armor\n\nExcerpt taken from \"The Guide to Hunting Mages\"\n\nMarked Combat\n===================Combat Basics:\n------------\nThe 3 Stances\nHigh- Form is leaned in, knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward.\nReferred to as the \"Counter\" stance. Used in an effort to -\n\n\n===================counter-act movements from mid-guard and stanceless efforts.\nMid- Form is relaxed, blade pommel is parallel to one's waistline. Knees bent and arms relaxed. Known as the \"Assaulting\" stance.\n\n\n===================Attacks vary on situation, be in Arc or thrust. Used to counter low stance and when assaulting shielded or untrained foes.\nLow- Form is lowered, knees bent, body leaned in. The arms are left in a -\n\n\n===================half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as, \"Wounding\", stance. Used to counteract High-guard, spearmen and is only used to hinder movement or knock a foe off balance. This stance is used with two handed.\n\nMovement\n===================When in combat, keep the foe in your direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps taken forward or backward, instead side-step in.\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================When Assaulting, nature may say rush the target head on, instead, aim to the target's right or left with movements. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Should the target-\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================continue to stand after the inital blow, aim for immediate execution, striking to either the neck or lower-spine.\n\nMovement, cont.\n==================\nWhen countering, side-step, parry or retaliate. Know the range of the Foe's weapon, if the range of your own counter-acts that of the enemy's, retaliate with side-step, aiming to either cleave limb or behead the foe.-\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================Should the weapon be lesser or equivalent, parry and close the gap. The strike won't likely be lethal. Instead, aim to disarm or hinder.\n\nCombat Stance\n===================So, think of the three stances as a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. When on even grounds, and not taking situation at hand, the three stances are as such\nHigh-Rock\nMid- Scissors\nLow-Paper\n\nCombat Stance, cont.\n===================When starting combat, take stance. Do not suddenly switch stance, since it exposes yourself, parry or sidestep while shifting. Shifting to counter will result in a half stance, which is a stance of valuable parries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V1", "§bMage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be a copy*\n\n\nThere were no planes of existance. There was nothing. Just the void. And a birght shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\n\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is in-fact, herecy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\n\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\n\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and\n\nhow clean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and The Daemon, the\n\ntwo spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and the Man\n\nlived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings\n\ncould not talk, nor did thay know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was\n\nthe father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 2", "§bAnthron", "Continuation of Seed words from part 1\n1 - 27\n-------------------\nCurious Words 28- and on to part 3\n-------------------The credit for this dictionary goes to the maker, Sporadic whom made the post to make this book possible on the forums.\n\nnae: you\n-------------------naeri: devout one, cleric\n-------------------narn: to walk, travel through\n-------------------nealu: to teach\n-------------------nor: land - nor'sae: farming\n-------------------\n\no: why\n-------------------ohn: like - Either a prefix or stand-alone\n-------------------oment: to meet\n-------------------okar: to safeguard\n-------------------okarn: oasis\n-------------------orrar: to hunt\n-------------------\n\nothelu: sharp\n-------------------parir: harbinger\n-------------------pern: potato\n-------------------parsaer: to conceive, to kindle. \"to have an idea\". \n-------------------perith: to remember\n-------------------puer: to write, to draw, to scribble.\n\n-------------------puerith: to write down (of books), to memorize. to record (more formal than 'puer')\n-------------------riv: claw \n-------------------riurn: swamp\n-------------------\n\nraell: carrot, root, herb. (refers to subterranean parts of plants possessing healing or nourishing properties)\n-------------------san: word, news - saner: to speak\n-------------------saneyr: to debate, discuss. - saneyir: debater, public speaker, orator.\n\n-------------------salum: to feel, to sense\n-------------------seth: void\n-------------------sew: soup, stew\n-------------------siimah: tower\n-------------------sil: sword\n-------------------siol: lone, lonely\n-------------------\n\nsirame: Honor; connection to the forest. - Has no plural\n-------------------siru: mushroom -siruonn: bitter\n-------------------siyuer: to play\n-------------------\n\nsohae: devout one, cleric - In a militant or executive sense. sohaer: ruler (through teachings, more positive than uthir.)\n-------------------suika: sugar -\n-------------------sul: light - strictly a noun.\n-------------------sulier: to see\n-------\n\nsulii: eye\n-------------------sulirrin: glowstone\n-------------------taeleh: mind\n-------------------taelu: to learn\n-------------------tahorran: hawk\n-------------------tahu: high\n-------------------tahn: peak, height\n------------------\n\ntalar: horizon - considered a place between the heavens and earth;\n-------------------talareh: stone - evolved from the words tali and lareh.\n-------------------\n\ntaliyna: body, living being, aspect -'taliiyna' can be used to denoted the physical parts that allow the body to live, i.e. organ, heart, mind and blood\n-------------------taliiyh: to bleed\n-------------------taliyu: secret\n-------------------\n\nTalonnii: family, blood(line) - always capped\n-------------------tarem: Elven week -Equivalent to 7 'karim'\n-------------------tayna: life, energy of living\n-------------------taynei: green\n-------------------\n\ntaynuel: vitality, energetic, alive (noun or adverb dependent on positioning)\n-------------------tenna: until\n-------------------tennallar: ocean\n-------------------\n\nterh: to grind, process, churn - wehn'tehral: bread; valein'tehral: cheese; raell'tehral: salve, potion), luci'terhal: wine\n-------------------\n\ntiuth: triangle - the triangular shape is found as a symbol for oppression, unlike the circle, which is used to describe (just) councils; - taliuth: oppressor\n-------------------thruer: to explode\n-------------------thrur: explosive, volatile\n------------\n\nthrurn: explosive, dynamite\n-------------------thill: pure, refined, delicate\n-------------------thilln: silver\n-------------------thul: raw, unrefined, brusque\n-------------------thulith: metal\n-------------------thuln: ore, raw material\n\n-------------------tilru: serving, submissive\n-------------------tir: law\n-------------------tos: desert, wasteland, barren ground - tos'sae: razing\n-------------------tufer: to construct, to prop\n-------------------\n\ntur: bone\n-------------------turr: sheep\n-------------------tuva: everything, all\n-------------------\ntuveh: wool, something soft\n-------------------ueth: nether\n-------------------uhier: to seek\n-------------------\n\nulln: rot, withering - strictly a noun.\n-------------------ullr: rot, decay, wither - Often of dead flora.\n-------------------ullral: monster, undead -lit: decayed. Used for living beings that have severed themselves from the natural way.\n----------------\n\nuradh: to scowl.\n-------------------uradir: naysayer\n-------------------uriar: to shout\n-------------------urth: to rule - negative connotation to this word.\n-------------------urthir: ruler\n-------------------maruthir: tyrant\n------------------\n\nUruk: Orc\n-------------------ut: because\n-------------------uvul: powder\n-------------------Valah: human\n-------------------vallei: water\n-------------------valein: milk\n-------------------vallel: blue\n------------------\n\nvallum: crying, griefing\n-------------------valmir: artist - from purple, the color of art.\n-------------------valmuel: purple\n-------------------van: to fare\n-------------------Velulaei: moon - Named after the moon goddess worshiped by the dark elves.\n\n-------------------vihai: whisper\n-------------------vilut: cow\n-------------------vira: vigilant, mournful - Traditionally used for attending the wake of vigil for a deceased Elf.\n-------------------vularale: bat\n-------------------\n\nvull: to deceive, to trick\n-------------------vuln: fox\n-------------------waleh: to heal\n-------------------wehn:  grass, grain.\n-------------------welier: to listen, to hear - rewelier: to repeat, to echo\n-------------------\n\nwy: appendage - more useful are the words that can be formed in combination with 'an*h': anah'wy: head; anoh'wy: foot, anih'wy: left hand, aneh'wy: right hand; anuh'wy: hand (either)\n-------------------wyl: while\n-------------------wyn: happy\n------------\n\ny: upon\n-------------------yallr: to live.\n-------------------yuln: gemstone - Used as the seed for many words, including maleyuln: diamond\n-------------------\n\nCURIOUS WORDS\nNo doubt you are left with many questions as you skim through the Elven wordlist. Indeed, their mystique and unique language has many intricacies which are not readily understood by those who did not take ample time studying them.\n\nFor perusal at your leniency, I have taken apart the words with most reason to spark confusion, and gave them the special attention they require in this section.\n-------------------\n\nito:\nThis particle is a means to denote location. However, it has many different meanings, depending on its location and accompanying words in a sentence.\nThe simplest case:\nito narne: I/he walk(s) here / I/he walk(s) within.\n\nNo ambiguity arises here. However, when we add a noun to this:\name ito narne: The forests walks here\nito ame narne: I/he walk(s) to the forest.\name'ito narne: I/He walk(s) within the forest\n\nameto'eyha narne: And I/he walk(s) within the forest\name'eyha ito narne: And the forest walks here.\nNote that the location of ito becomes crucial here. Putting it on the place of a subject aligns it to the meaning 'to'. On the object's location\n\n(to understand this, educate yourself on the elven sentence order), the noun 'ame' becomes the subject instead, and ito regains the meaning 'within' or 'here'.\nIto can also be used as a suffix, which is demonstrated by the last examples. In this case, the\n\naddition of ito restricts the noun to an object.\nThis word is also used to create the elvish equivalent to the words 'to be' and 'to have'. This particularly might confuse a novice to the language. to read upon this, I refer you to the grammar section of\n\nthis tome.\n-------------------tali-:\nThis word can do two very different things to the word it is connected to. In the simplest case, it adds the modifier 'part of' to the linked noun. But sometimes, the addition of this prefix creates a whole new word:\n\ntalibortu: Part dwarf -> Halfling\ntalivalah: Part human -> Halfling\ntal'uruk: Part Orc -> Goblin.\n\nHowever, sometimes ambiguity can abound from this word. For example:\n\ntaliame: Tree\ntal'ame: Part of the forest.\n\nIt would seem that in confusing cases, elves add an apostrophe between to denote they mean multiple words rather than a single noun. However, this is not always a safe rule,\n\nas it may clash with other rules for using apostrophes. Caution is urged, and ambiguity may indeed arise.\n--------------------sae:\nThis word, meaning the development, spreading or management of something, can be used to create many new words in elvish\n\nSome of these may not seem obvious. Examples include:\n\nnor'sae: development of land -> farming\ntos'sae: spreading of desert -> pillaging\nThe combinations grow even more numerous when we consider that sae can be combined with\n\n ir to create sair, lending a word for, exemplum gratia, 'farmer' and 'pillager'. It can also be turned to saean to create a \nplural (where applicable) and saer, turning the word into the stem of a verb, effectively giving us the words 'to farm' and\n\n'to pillage'.\nThese further combinations exist almost always wherever a word was created from the suffix sae. Knowledge of this fact will allow the reader much more affluency in this language.\n-------------------\n\nma-:\nApart from being an intensifier, used at your leisure, the prefix ma- often finds its home in places where the intense use of affix would cause the same affix to start. An example of this is found in the word 'log': The elves would consider a log\n\n'part of tree' thus 'part of a part of the forest'. However, talitaliame is NOT a correct word to use in Elven.\nInstead, the second tali is implied by the use of the intesifier. Thus:\nmataliame: Log\n\nIf used in an event where a repeated suffix is used, ma- is placed after the seed word, but before the suffix one wishes to repeat.\nInterestingly enough, ma- is one of the rare affixes that does stack on certain occasions, as seen in the word marmatelu.\n\n-------------------onn:\n\nThis word is much like tali, in that it can be used to further define a certain word, as well as be used to create a noun of it's own. Also like tali, he inclusion of an apostrophe in a confusing case will imply the speaker is\n\nmeaning to talk of multiple words\nAn example:\n\name'onn: Born of the Forest, from the forest.\namonn: wood\nThe suffix will create a myriad of new words for the advanced speaker. Study of its usage will surely be beneficial.\n\n-------------------fer:\n\ngrammatically, nothing is strange about this word. However, its uses in combinations are so numerous that a separate section may be devoted to it.\nfer'ame: Axe\nfer'thuln: Pickaxe\nfer'nor: shovel\nfer'sul: torch\n\nfer'bilok: hammer\nfer'norsae: hoe\nfer'puer: quill. Pen. A tool for writing.\nOther uses can be thought up by the cunning mind. However, bear in mind that the word fer is mostly used to speak of handheld tools, not of crafting tables, anvils or furnaces.\n--", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Passages", "§bMysterious Author", "*This book's cover is entirely black. The material used to craft it seems to be leather, though it's thicker then usual. Whatever it's made out of. It's obvious it's not that of an animals hide.*\n\n-As you open the book. You'd take notice on how each and every page is made of a thin leather as well. The coloring of each being a light shading. The words written are thinnly laced along too. Diffrent from a regular quills.-\n\n Greetings ot whom ever reads these words incribed.\nYou now have the chance to learn and take in things that I've experianced on my adventures throughout the diffrent lands we've traversed.\n\nI've seen many things, though I'll speak of few in these pages. One competely corporal. Though, the other. Not so much.\nThe first I'll speak on is that of those whom once held breath. Once lived as you and I do.\n\nTasted, laughed. And possibly loved. Though, for such beings. These things matter none to their broken minds. They exist on, after death to carry out one goal. To feast on the warm flesh of the living. To taste the life that runs in\n\nthe blood that flows through every vein in your body. If you, who reads has such.\nThese creatures that crawl, creep and continue to come after being hit, even after losing limbs. For physical pain is nothing to them.\n\nThey only feel the lust to feed. To devour all life that harbors in every fiber of a living things body.  Though, I've also witnessed them gnaw on a corpse, long dead as it's dried skin cracked between it's jagged teeth.\n\nThey seem to be in a constant setting of pain. Though only from their shattered minds trying to cope with realities harsh lessons of how tampering with nature. Can have\nunexpected repercussions. Even in creating\n\nsuch a being. As few truely take to heart. That monsters do, what monsters are capible of. And that they should be feared by all the living.\n\n*A detailed picture is penciled in. That showing of three Ghouls. One being a human with a cut neck. The second, an Uruk who's head is half caved in. And the third, a Ghoul Kha that's missing a right arm. All three are reaching out.\n\nTheir faces all posed in a sorrow-filled expressoin. Though they seem to be clawing.. At the reader, as if to make a point.*\n\nAs for the second being of darkness I shall decribe, is one that has found a way to ascend in their own sense. Through warping the ways of a certain dart art. They're are to unbind themselves from this realm, though partially\n\nto say. As their spirit is in a constant struggle. Caught between both the land of the living. And that of the dead. Something anyone would. nd should dread even the thought. Though, from my seeings. I've taken note\n\nthat some have lost their minds partially. Forgetting and rambling on. Those they knew. Nothing stuck to this one. But others. Are as they were in their mortal shell. Calm for the most part. Though brash all the same when\n\nspeaking for them in anycase.  For they are in a state of undeath. Damnation that rids them of mortal needs. But a thirst for life still. As I've witnessed them suck the land dry around them. Leaving nothing of a husk of flora\n\nand trees. Fueling them along in whatever their twisted minds compel them with. Though, if one is wise. And hopefully fast on their feet if not. Then if running into one of these unholy creatures. You could have a talk.\n\nFor those whom do so. Would say that they hold many secrets. Some willing to share. Others, they keep for only the most trustworthy. Living or otherwise.\n\nRemember. Do not make enemies with a Wight. For death\n\nis only a setback in their burning, though hollow eyes.\n\n*On the next page is a penciled drawing of two Wights. Each being vastly diffrent looking. The first, being a hooded figure of a man at first. Though when squinting at the small drawing. You'd then be able to make out\n\nthe skeletal outline on it's facial features. It's would be hands that of a skeletal appearance as it's eyes give a faint illumnination of a red glow coloured in with some type of dye. The second figure stands to resemble that\n\nof a Lich. It's would be head missing any trace of flesh at all as it's hollowed out eyesockets glow with nonshaded dots of flames that seem to harbor nothing to burn to. It holds a large staff in both hands. Cradling it to one\n\nside as it leans towards that angle. Both skeletal figures stand to stare directly outward at the reader.*\n\nI leave you now to ponder on what's been taught. But remember this. The next time you hear something slam in an alleyway. Or shuffling noises permeate the darkness ahead of you. Think twice on traveling forth. For the\n\nshadows hold many secrets. Some harmless. Others not so much.\n\n((No signs of whom wrote the book are given. Only the knowledge provided is set within these pages.))", ""),
        StaticBook("How to be succes", "§bCroesus Letholdus", "How to the hearts of the people \n\n\n william karduin didnt take out the trash becaues he was overencumbered with the sewing table he was repairing for a quick buck to spend at epicot studios where he would meet rap star drake aubrey graham and\n\n\n\n\n   exch ange bodily \nfluids via saline solution as i write in this book abou t  an adventure i never went on william karduin sits in front of the fireplace trying to turn it on but he will not turn it on\n\ntabletop tucker is unaware of the obliging comrade that waits patiently for him to park his horse in the nearby oven water is vital and much needed for survival \n\n\n   y  e  s  t  e  r  d  a  y\n\ni \nwent for a walk acros\n\nfelsen \n         looking\n                   for\n                        a \n                          chap  \n                            his \n                         name\n                       was \n                      nelson\n\nnelson had just gotten in\n\na slimy predicament with a man noone would ever dare cross \n\nhe did it for a quick buck so he can take his shoe laces to the cobbler adam sandles richard shoelace ties shoelaces he is the ologmeister he   plays the game the game of life he walks line\n\non \n    \n\n\n\n\n           no \n   \n  \n\n                      mans\n\n                                  time\n\nthinking hes hip, thinking hes that thinking i dont make flapjacks in the morning along with some maple oat meal and six eggs with a banana and four strips of bacon for about 1,100 calories to start my day \n\nthen later i'll go the gym so i can train my\n\nphysique and not be ugly this way i can find a soulmate and settle down\n\nbuild a house\n\n       kill some orphans\n\nand worship chin chin\n\n16.9 fl oz (500 ml)\nofficial yogurt of the halflings", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 1", "§bAnthron", "Table of contents\n------------------\nAffixes: 1-13\n-------------------Seed words: 14-part 2\n-------------------\nContent provided by\nSporadic:\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/19254-recovering-the-ancient-tongue-of-the-elves/\n\nAFFIXES\nAffixes  served a very important purpose in the Elven language. You are recommended to learn of them and their purpose before anything else,  for many words are formed by the addition of affixes to the so- called 'seed words', which are listed\n\nbelow.\nWe further discuss our findings on affixes in the grammatical section of this volume. Furthermore, words deserving extra explanation will be handled in the 'curious words' section.\nNote: The dash indicates the location of the seed word to the affix\n\nac- (aca-) Honorific for an accursed.\n-------------------ah- (ahe-): Honorific for reverence. Often used in front of names to denote sainthood.\n-------------------ael-: Vile, unnatural, beastly.\n--------------------al: -Designates the completion\n\nof an action.\n------------------\n-an: many, full of -Mostly designates plurality.\n------------------\nan*h- (a/o/i/e/u): To direct (up/down/left/right/rotate) (more on this in 'curious words').\n-------------------\n\nav-: wandering.\n-------------------ay: for.\n-------------------\n-ante (-nte): Last.\n-------------------div-: Empty, devoid of (antecendent to -an).\n--------------------ento (-nto): next.\n-------------------\n\n-ehya: and - used at the beginning of a sentence for 'but...'\n-------------------\nel- (ele-): - Changes a noun into a pronoun, making it a title of someone, or possibly something.\n-------------------\n\nfi-: new, anew - Often used as prefix, but not exclusively.\n-------------------heya- (hey-): what, how, who.\n-------------------\nil- (ilu-): with\n--------------------ii: little Designated the diminutive form. Plural: iian.\n-------------------\n\n-ir: - Designates the purpose of someone.\n-------------------iyl-: this usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\n-------------------iyul-: that usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\n--------------------leh: -Designates affiliation.\n------------------\n\nma- (mar-): very -Intensifier. More on this in 'curious words'\n--------------------n: - Sometimes put behind an adjective or verb to create a noun.\n--------------------ne (-ane): not - A suffix used to indicate the negative.\n-------------------\n\n-onn: from, born, kin - Often a suffix, but not always. More on this in 'curious words'.\n-------------------par- (pra-): before, pre-\n-------------------res- (re-): wayward, capricious, unpredictable.\n-------------------\n\n-sae: Spreading, development management. - More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------tal- (tali-): Part (of) - More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------u-: or - Always a prefix and always used with apostrophe.\n-------------------\n\n-yem (-hyem): again -Can be used to make a 're-' family of verbs\n-------------------vul- (vule-): clever, intuitive, deceptive.\n-------------------\n\nSEED WORDS\nThese words make up the brunt of the Elven language, and may be modified by various affixes to create new words.\n\nacal: valuable, golden, cursed - From ac-al: Completion of the word\nac: Cursed. Beware of this double meaning. Because of this double meaning,  Elves of old may give those they wish ill a nugget of gold to declare their hostility.\n\nThe gesture was often wasted on other races, who considered the gold a tribute.\n-------------------acalin: shop\n-------------------acaln: gold\n-------------------\n\n(a)chikr: (without the a:) ***** - denotes a woman who murders her children (or neglects them to death), which is considered a horrible crime due to the value of fertility and the rarity of Elf children. Without the 'a', the word degenerates\n\ninto a grave insult. Know that intentional cursing in Elven attracts ill-willing aspects.\n-------------------(a)dil: needy, desiring, wanton - When one forfeits the 'a' it becomes as of a vice.\n-------------------\n\n(a)dont: requesting, awaiting - Without the 'a' it becomes 'demanding', -er makes verb as always.\n-------------------adri: evil, immoral, hate.\n-------------------(a)elor: abomination, faithless, demon. -Denotes any non-humanoid of intelligence.\n\nWithout the 'a' the word becomes an insult to call someone disfigured. Know that intentional cursing in Elven attracts ill-willing aspects.\n-------------------Aengul: Aengul - race of semi-divine beings affiliated with light.\n-------------------aetah: age\n\n-------------------aeth: aether\n-------------------aher: to bless.\n-------------------ahern: blessing.\n-------------------akal: valuable, golden - less ominous.\n-------------------akaleh: wealth, money, valuable.\n-------------------akalin: shop\n\n-------------------\nakaln: gold - less ominous way to speak of gold.\n-------------------allim: sin  - allimar: to sin; alliman: sinful.\n-------------------andria: hope\n-------------------annyer: to dance\n-------------------Asul: Sun\n------------------\n\nata: ugly, tainted\n-------------------athri: serpent, snake\n-------------------a)iler: Wizard, conjurer, heretic -Any wizard or spiritual humanoid that's not a druid. When one forfeits the 'a' in the word it becomes an insult.\n\nIt should be noted that the word 'Ailer' is not used for your everyday magic user, but reserved for a powerful, exclusive brand of spellcasters.\n-------------------alor: salmon -aloronn/alonn: salty\n-------------------ame: forest\n-------------------\n\nannil: guiding -anniler: to guide, direct\n-------------------ante: Last\n-------------------arche: infrequent, sporadic, rare.\n-------------------(a)rhil: just fair (without the a:) vengeful, scorned.\n-------------------\n\nasimulum: sanctuary, glade, asylum, dedicated place (esp. one of nature).\n-------------------aver: to wander, to roam around aimlessly, to be confused.\n-------------------avern: wanderer, confused person.\n-------------------ayal: yellow\n------------------\n\nay(i)lu: liked, likable - may(i)lu: loved. The 'i' is optional, but may not be used if the object is not a person.\n-------------------ayla: good\n-------------------barbu: dark, black, hedgehog\n-------------------bilok: to create, to make.\n----\n\nBortu: dwarf\n-------------------(a)caele: sky. - The plural, caelan, is used to reference to the Seven skies and with that, God. The lack of an 'a' in front makes the word disrespectful or insulting.\n-------------------celia: star\n-------------------\n\nceru: strong, mighty\n-------------------chirr: wolf\n-------------------chul: to must\n-------------------cihi: city\n-------------------cinh: to stop, to cease\n-------------------ciw: to sleep\n-------------------\n\ncrua: hurting, suffering - which makes cruan: pain\n-------------------Daemon: Daemon - race of semi-divines affiliated with smoke and fire.\n-------------------dion: long - dionne: short\n-------------------divu: empty\n------------------\n\ndrui: Druid\n-------------------draoi: Evil/corrupted druid. Warlock. Sorcerer.\n-------------------ehier: to find\n-------------------enaer: guest\n-------------------ento: next\n-------------------ern: to can, to be able to\n\n-------------------eth: end, to end, to die -word can be a noun, passive verb and active verb depending on usage.\n-------------------evar: to protect, preserve\n-------------------eyr: to use, apply\n-------------------faesu: horse\n------------------\n\nfer: tool - This word creates a wide array of words for various tools, such as torches and pickaxes. They are discussed further in 'curious words'.\n-------------------fenn: ice\n-------------------feta: cold\n-------------------fih: to eat, to feed\n--------\n\nfin: region\n-------------------fiyem: reborn, renewed, revitalized\n-------------------fyu: full\n-------------------hae: her\n-------------------haelun: mother\n-------------------haler: to promise, to pledge\n------------------\n\nharriel: square\n-------------------heial: circle, council\n-------------------hier: near\n-------------------hileia: Peace. - Has no plural\n-------------------hiuw: to twitch, to move\n-------------------hiylu: Healthy / spirited\n------------------\n\nibar: white, owl\n-------------------igne: flame, fire - igne'sae: destruction, war\n-------------------iheiuh: wind\n-------------------iheiuhii: voice, breath\n-------------------ihn: stick\n-------------------ihnsil: spear\n------------------\n\nikur: wrought, cold, gray\n-------------------ikurn: iron\n-------------------ikru: foolish\n-------------------iller: to give, to grand\n-------------------ilum: glowing - when something only reflects light. ilumr: to glow.\n------------------\n\ninder: to read\n-------------------indor: book\n-------------------irrin: glass\n-------------------ito: to, here, within - Can also be a suffix. More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------iyat: thought\n-------------------iyath: to think\n\n-------------------iylanh: to place\n-------------------kae: me\n-------------------kalem: Malin's year, - Roughly 26 Anthos years, denotes the length of a High Prince's reign.\n-------------------kaliri: Event, party\n-------------------\n\nkarim: Fortday, - The measure of time from one Dwarven sleeping cycle to the next, roughly 24 Anthos days.\n------------------\nkarin(ah): sunrise, - Also used to speak of day\n-------------------kathir: foe\n-------------------\n\nker: dark, sunset - Also used to speak of night\n-------------------khel: darkness - Strictly a noun\n-------------------kina: murdered, killed, death, in mortal danger-a noun used for someone who is marked for death by someone or something.\n---------------\n\nkrafeh: corpse\n-------------------krey: single. kreyn - pair.\n-------------------lae: him\n-------------------lar: sturdy, steadfast.\n-------------------lareh: boulder, mountain, rock\n-------------------larebil: anvil\n------------------\n\nlarueth: netherrack\n-------------------laureh: chosen, favored, noble\n-------------------laurir: Noble\n-------------------len: song\n-------------------lenaern: inn\n-------------------lenniel: melody\n-------------------lent: to (over)grow\n\n-------------------\nlenti: growth, moss.\n-------------------lentos: brown\n-------------------leyu: graceful, beautiful.\n-------------------liewyn: smile - liewynh: to smile, liewyn'saer: to entertain, to amuse; maliewynh: to laugh\n-------------------\n\nlle: kindness, good intention\n-------------------lie: dishonest, untrue, false, deceitful -lien: lie , liear: to lie; maliear: to betray (malieir: traitor)\n-------------------llir: friend\n-------------------lin: home, place -linan'sae: town\n--------------\n\nllum: sorrowful, mourning - llum'saer: to sadden\n-------------------llyt: aggressive, intimidating, -llyth: to strike\n-------------------lom: to fragment, to splinter\n-------------------lomi: fragment, splinter, pebble\n------------------\n\nlomal: flint\n-------------------luci: grape - lucionn: sour\n-------------------luer:  to imprison, to cage \n-------------------luerlent: flowerpot\n-------------------lye: we - Used to speak of elves, a people, or even the world as a whole. Often misused.\n\n-------------------lyu: silent - leads to the words lyun: silence; lyuer: to silence and lyu'saer: to censor \n-------------------maehr: wisdom, knowledge\n-------------------maelu: to know\n-------------------mahnih: wall\n-------------------\n\nMali: elf/elven - Word is both singular and plural, noun and adjective.\n-------------------maln: father\n-------------------marn: more\n-------------------marenne: less\n-------------------masuleh: anvil\n-------------------medi: helping, helpful\n\n-------------------meracahe: balance\n-------------------miar: lava miar'sae: griefing, harming, spiting\n-------------------mira: warm\n-------------------miruel: red\n-------------------myumier: to carry, to bring\n------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("30 Strictures", "§bYpres Signus", ";-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;\n        The Holy\n     Strictures of\n      Yeu Rthulu\n\n    As according to\nthe cannon which has been confirmed and past down by all servants of Yeu Rthulu. Blessings upon you.\n\nStricture 1: One must never find joy in the death of any man, woman, or child. \n\nStricture 2: It is right for one to be bound in matrimony as to create lifemates, but one must never force such a sacred act on another.\n\n \nStricture 3: One must never make love outside of marriage.\n\nStricture 4: One must restrict themselves from gluttony and drunkenness.\n\n \nStricture 5: One must restrict themselves from un-marital lust and intercourse.\n\nStricture 6: One must restrict themselves from taking what is not theirs.\n\nStricture 7: One must find peace and tolerance to deal with those whom're not enlightened, for they follow their own path.\n\nStricture 8: One must restrict themselves from needlessly striking out against someone.\n\nStricture 9: One must not allow one's lust for revenge overtake them. Just retribution may be needed, but vengeance is reserved for the Gods.\n\nStricture 10: One must not deceive or harm one another with words.\n\n \nStricture 11: One must not abandon those whom trust one for support.\n\n \nStricture 12: One must allow their hearts to not be apathetic to their brother's burdens.\n \nStricture 13: One must respect their family, for they're of same blood.\n\n \nStricture 14: One must not show hatred to anyone due to their race, their age, or gender.\n \nStricture 15: One must restrict from the use of substances which muffle and cloud the emotions as to use to deal with their pain.\n\n \nStricture 16: One must support all whom are widowed, lame, or otherwise unable to support themselves. \n\n \nStricture 16: One must support all whom are widowed, lame, or otherwise unable to support themselves.\n\nStricture 18: One must be submit under the discernment of others as to have a understanding of what is brought by justice, and what is brought by anger.\n\nStricture 19: One must keep themselves accountable to their spouses. And likewise hold their spouses accountable.\n\nStricture 20: One must not allow one's anger to provoke trouble, and pain.\n\nStricture 21: One must allow themselves to be counted as equal unless proven otherwise by content of character.\n\nStricture 22: One must not challenge or disobey those whom are appointed to authority.\n\nStricture 23: One must find mercy within themselves to be patient with the mistakes of others.\n\nStricture 24: One must find joy in whatever he has, whether little, or great.\n\nStricture 25: One must find the purest of joys from their spouse.\n\nStricture 26: It is in due right, and in way of nature that those bound in marriage should enjoy the privileges of sexual intercourse and relations. Yet, it is to be kept between the 2 lifemates,-\n\nnot extending to others and creating such things as orgies or brothels, for they are detestable and disgusting.\n\nStricture 27: One must support and nurture their spouse as they would themselves.\n\nStricture 28: One must love their spouse more than any worldly thing, or person.\n\nStricture 29: One must not hide their true nature from their spouse. For it is the true nature of lifemates that must be bound together.\n\nStricture 30: One must honor and follow the strictures if they wish to live a pure life, contented, and compassionately.\n\n\n-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;", ""),
        StaticBook("Blah Dictionary", "§bShreck", "Diz buuk tranzlatez wurds in blah tew kommon, writtun bi Shreck.\n\n-Ug ¦ Hello, Hi, Hail\n-Throm'ka ¦ Formal greeting\n-Yub ¦ Yes\n-Nub ¦ No\n-Gug'ye ¦ Goodbye\n-Lat ¦ You\n-Mi ¦ Me, I\n\n-Wi ¦ We, Us\n-Hi ¦ He\n-Rulg ¦ Thanks\n-Blah ¦ Talk, Speak, Orchish Language\n-Blah'er ¦ Mouth\n-Peepers ¦ Eyes\n-Skah'er ¦ Male Reproductive Organ\n-Gruk ¦ Think, Know, Understand\n-Dabu ¦ Yes, My Pleasure\n\n-Bubhosh ¦ Great, Big\n-Nubhosh ¦ Bad, Small\n-Snaga ¦ Slave\n-Buub ¦ Pig\n-Pushdug ¦ Stinky\n-Glob ¦ Fool, Shit, Poop\n-Klomp ¦ Fight, Attack\n-Flat ¦ Dead, Kill\n-Blarg ¦ Home\n-Brudda ¦ War Uzg Orc\n-Stout ¦ Dwarf\n-Twiggeh, Treehugger ¦ elf\n\n-Darkie ¦ Farfolk, Dark elf\n-Squeals, Snaaks ¦ Halflings\n-Quickspawn, Breeder, Shara, Pinkii ¦ Human\n-Nuutshara ¦ Ascended\n-Nubded ¦ Undead\n-Howlur ¦ Dog, Wolf\n-Skah ¦ Fuck\n-Agh ¦ And\n-Buurz ¦ Dark\n-Mojo ¦ Magic\n\n-Bi ¦ By\n-Krimp ¦ Stun, Capture\n-Uzg ¦ World\n-Goi ¦ City\n-Lusk ¦ Axe\n-O'lig ¦ Bow\n-Ligz ¦ Arrow\n-Zult ¦ Sword\n-Stik ¦ Staff\n-Steemiez ¦ Redstone\n\n   Numburz!\n\nAsh ¦ One\nDub ¦ Two\nGakh ¦ Three\nFuth ¦ Four\nH' ¦ Five\nH'ash ¦ Six\nAshety ¦ Ten\nAshty ¦ Eleven\nDubty ¦ Twelve\nDubty ¦ Twenty", ""),
        StaticBook("Poison", "§bAriana Herenden", "The softness of touch\nThe warmth of breath\nWith airs the cobra strikes\n\nBreathing hope\nBreathing love\nAnd always breathing light\n\nThe bitten knows not\nWhat happened then\nFor days and days she's numb\n\nBut in time\nThe poison sinks\nAnd she will at last succumb", ""),
        StaticBook("Ghashn Baltbrodh", "Travista", "The Lak Mindset\n\n\n      Praise Laklul\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*The book would be\nwritten in Blah*\n\n1. Laklul First\n\nYou must act to further Laklul's influence. When you fight, do so in Laklul's name, when you triumph over you foe, do so in Laklul's name; lead your life in Laklul's name. Currently, Laklul is in battle with his\n\ntyrannical master, Freygoth, spirit of nature, in the immortal plane. This means that you must hinder the influence of Freygoth and those who follow him be they spiritual or mortal. Druids, although they worship nature and not Freygoth directly, are a\n\nquintessential example of our mortal foes. Drive them from their homes, burn their lives yet spare the ones who dedicate themselves to spirits loyal to Laklul such as swamp and jungle druids. Additionally, destroy all shrines dedicated to Freygoth and\n\nreplace them with ones in Laklul's esteemed honour for such is the will of Laklul. Aside from Freygoth, his followers and other dishonourable spirits such as Tukki and Ixli, you should praise them for they too are great and worthy, Krug especially.\n\n2. Orkish Supremacy \n\nThe Ork is the only race which has worshiped the astute \nspirits; the ork is the only race which can defy all others mentally and physically. Although humility is acceptable while treading on ill, foreign lands do no\n\nsuch thing when they dare to take on the privilege of treading our lands. Especially the swamplands which Laklul deems his home; they must be free of foreign filth unless they pay grand spiritual reparations.\nIn addition, do not lay amongst foreigners or\n\nallow them to lay among you for their weakness shall diffuse into you. A strong people who can serve the spirits must have the slaves squabble far from equal. All clans which are weak in terms of the individual have issues with this just command.\n\n3. Strive Selfwards\n\nThe most useful servant is the most skilled one. As a servant to Laklul and most spirits we must view the world with such a lense. The two main aspects of a mortal, the mind and body, must be toiled and trialed consistently into\n\nimprovement. One cannot forsake one in the name of another; a Lak must be as formidable with wit as he is in the fields of war. Every Lak must be bulked to their limit, every Lak must be trained in craft and  weapon to their limit; every Lak must be\n\nat their peaked for this is the best way to serve Laklul. This is the will of Laklul.\n\n4. Lakkish Loyalty\n\nAll Laks are to be utterly devoted to the clan; to the Swampgoth. As the Swampgoth and the clan in extension act on behalf of the mighty and rightous Laklul any severing of dedication severs Laklul's positive view. It likewise\n\ndictates the spirits to view you with an unfavourable lense due to forsaking the oath you took before the spirits which was sealed in the blood of your initial trial. Furthermore, do not fear death if it's in the name of Laklul. Welcome it. The greatest\n\nof Krug's kin transcend to the ancestral plane to live gloriously as Krug does himself. If the enemy takes you captive hold sensitive details to death; if the enemy drive forth, unless the spirit of hope himself would proclaim it suicidal, fight.\n\nConclusive Notes:\n\n-Avoid degeneracy\n\n-Respect swampland\n\n-Respect ALL spirits bar the ones detailed previously\n\nPunishments:\n\nFirst Offense:\n\nThe offender is beaten\n\nSecond Offense:\n\nThe offender is beaten, a finger taken\n\nAnymore results in death", ""),
        StaticBook("Sannleikurinn", "§bHeshakomeu", "The Sannleikurinn\n\n\nHere lies the Truth, the Way, and the Path.\n\nMay Yahweh watch over you.\n\nBOOK OF MALIV\n\nI. There was never a Dawn of the world. Before the Earth was Void, and in this Void lay Yahweh. Yahweh Dreamed, and so the world existed.\nII. This Vision came upon the eyes of Maliv, the First Prophet, so that he would Understand and\n\nspread the Truth among the Mortals.\nIII. Maliv did not Understand, however, and so, frightened by the Vision, fled his home with his wife and children.\nIV. Yahweh’s eye had not left him. As Maliv slept, the Second Vision appeared before him: Creation is\n\na Dream. From the subconscious of Yahweh came the Aenguls and the Daemons; the Mortal Races of the Earth; the Sun and Moon and Stars; the trees and the rocks; the seas and the mountains.\nV. Still Maliv was filled with fear. He fled to the mountains,\n\nin the hopes he would find peace.\nVI. Yahweh then bestowed the Third Vision: There is no end to the soul. The soul wanders from body to body after each body dies, assuming new forms and making new journeys, but it is eternal.\nVII. Once Maliv awoke from\n\nthe Third Vision, he stood and spoke the First Words to Yahweh: “Bugger off, ya daemon.”\nVIII. The Greatness and Glory of Yahweh then descended upon Maliv. The mountains on which his home stood upon shook, the wind pushed down the forests that\n\nsurrounded him, and the sky was filled with fire and lightning and rain. For Six Days, the storm tormented Maliv, destroying his home, his animals, and the very clothes on his back.\nIX. On the Seventh Day, Maliv cried out to Yahweh in fear and anguish\n\nthe Second Words: “What do you want from me?” Immediately, the mountains ceased to shake, the wind disappeared, and the fire and lightning and rain vanished from the sky.\nX. The Voice of Yahweh was not heard. It was not in any Mortal tongue. It appeared\n\nin the very Heart of Maliv. The Utterance is best understood as: “To make you Understand.”\nXI. Yahweh then bestowed upon Maliv the Mission. Maliv embarked from the mountain to fulfill his Mission and tell the Races of Aegis the Truth of Yahweh,\nknown as\n\nthe Sannleikurinn.\nXII. So endeth the Truth of the First Prophet.\n\nBOOK OF SHUL’TAK\n\n\nI. Maliv began his journey in the sands of the Uruk. He was soon captured and enslaved by a roving band of Uruks. The Uruk warriors forced him to build, mine, dig, and toil in the smithy. At the end of each day of labor, Maliv would\n\ncall out to Yahweh to free him.\nII. After one year, Yahweh heard his cry. The apprentice witchdoctor Shul’Tak heard Maliv’s nightly prayer for rescue while passing by the slave tent, and, intrigued, entered the tent to question Maliv about his faith.\n\nMaliv shared the Truth of Yahweh to Shul’Tak, and they Discussed for many hours this Truth.\nIII. Shul’Tak became tired from the talking, and hit Maliv over the head with his club, knocking Maliv unconscious. Shul’Tak then went to rest, and a Vision of\n\nYahweh came upon him in his sleep:\nIV. Creation is the Endless Dream of Yahweh. The Imagination of Yahweh creates and destroys mountains, forests, oceans, villages, and life. It has been Said by the First Prophet, and is True.\nV. Shul’Tak awoke and\n\nimmediately went to see Maliv. Shul’Tak shared with him his vision, and asked Maliv what he must do to serve Yahweh. Maliv told Shul’Tak to go into the wilderness alone and Pray to Yahweh for Divine Revelation.\nVI. The next day, Shul’Tak took bread and\n\nwater with him deep into the desert. He walked until the sun disappeared behind the horizon. Shul’Tak then lay upon a sandstone rock and began to call up to the stars for Yahweh to receive him. He did this for many hours until he was struck by\n\nexhaustion and fell asleep.\nVII. That night, the Second Vision came upon him: Receive the Path of Yahweh and share it with the Peoples of Aegis.\nVIII. When Shul’Tak awoke,a stone tablet lay in the sands beside him. Here is what was written:\n\ni. Thou shalt acknowledge the Truth of Yahweh as the One and Only Truth. When in times of Great Strife, call out to Yahweh so you may been Seen and rescued.\nii. Thou shalt follow the Path of Yahweh, as written here, so as to not be distracted from the\n\nTruth and focus on Creation, which is not Real, rather than Yahweh, who is Real.\niii. Do not concern thyself with Material Wealth, for it shall not go with the Soul to the next Form in Its Existence. Instead, pursue Peace within thyself and Knowledge\n\nof Creation, so as to teach thy Soul Patience and Dedication.\niv. While you walk in this World, surround thyself with the Natural Beauty of Creation, and take part in the Natural Pleasures Yahweh has Created you to have.\nv. When the sun sets every\n\nSeventh Elven Day, go to a place of Natural Beauty and Meditate on the Truth of Yahweh. Remember who hath given thee this Beauty and take pleasure in Yahweh’s Creation.\nvi. Show Kindness, Humbleness, and Compassion to others, but remember their Forms\n\nwill disappear. Do not bind thyself to these temporary Hosts, for they shall return to dust but Yahweh shall always exist.\n\nIX. Shul’Tak thanked Yahweh, and bowed down to praise the Glory. Half-buried in the sand, he found a slate, upon which was carved the symbol of Yahweh: an infinity symbol.\nX. Shul’Tak had one last question for Yahweh. That night, he lay upon the rock\n\nand begged Yahweh to explain how he could give up the Spirits of the Uruk.\nXI. After many hours, Shul’Tak fell asleep, and the Third Vision was bestowed upon Shul’Tak: If presented with a Higher Power, be it king, ancestor, or Divine, pay homage to it.\n\nDivine or mortal beings were set above you for a reason; you are right to follow them, so long as you recognize Yahweh as the Highest Power.\nXII. Shul’Tak awoke reassured and returned to his village. He told his master he must travel, and took Maliv\n\nwith him as his servant. Together, they traveled Aegis, exploring Creation and deepening their Understanding of the Truth.\nXIII. So endeth the Path of the Second Prophet.\n\nBOOK OF VISKA\n\nI. The Path of Yahweh, although clear, did not detail the Conduct a Follower should have when certain Occasions Arise. I, Maliv, and Shul’Tak have seen fit to prepare a Guide for the Follower in a world of those who know not the Truth.\n\nII. On the subject of killing: Do not kill. This violates the Sixth Commandment of Yahweh calling for Kindness. The only time it is Forgivable is when it is done in the Defense of your Life or that of Others.\nIII. On stealing: Do not steal. This too\n\nviolates the Sixth Commandment of Yahweh by depriving the victim of the Property they earned. The only time it is Forgivable is when the object is needed to protect your Life or that of Others.\nIV. On lying: Do not lie. It distorts the Truth and\n\ncompromises the Integrity and Reliability of your character, so that when you share the Truth of Yahweh, the Truth is not Accepted. The only time it is Forgivable is when the Lie protects your Life or that of Others.\nV. On sexual relations: As a\n\nNatural Pleasure Yahweh has given us, it is Allowable. Do not, however, place your Partner above Yahweh and the Truth in Importance, or Bind thyself to them so you could not Live without their presence. This is in violation of the Sixth Commandment of\n\nYahweh.\nVI. On marriage: It is advised not to if it will Distort your view of Cosmic Truth, but is Permissible should both members of the marriage be Followers. The Two have accepted they are Dust, but they wish to enjoy Creation together.\nVII. On\n\nbusiness, trade, and all things economic: Do not invest in Creation and its Money, which would be in violation of the Third Commandment of Yahweh. It is Permissible if the Wealth acquired is given to those who need it, not Hoarded and kept for its\n\nowner’s Pleasure and Satisfaction.\nVIII. On destruction of nature: Treat Creation with Respect. Cut down trees, not forests; dig tunnels, not mountains; hunt animals, not herds. Reserve areas for Nature to Survive and Flourish. To do otherwise \nviolates\n\nthe Fifth Commandment of Yahweh.\nIX. On relations with those who do not Know the Truth: Treat them with Respect and Kindness. It is not their fault they are Ignorant, for the World is Ignorant, and they are of the World.\nX. In conclusion: The Follower\n\nshould not anchor themselves to one part of Creation. Rather, they should travel throughout the World, experiencing and witnessing all they can of the growth and passing of History.\nXI. May Yahweh watch over and bless you, Follower.\n\nBOOK OF NEZNAKOMETZ\n\nI. I, Heshakomeu de Campari Shidari, a mali’aheral Follower, have seen fit to record the unwritten teachings of the Second Prophet Shul’Tak that he spoke of in the years before his passing:\nII. The First Vision of Yahweh bestowed\n\non the First Prophet, Tilur, revealed that our world never truly began, in the same way there is never truly a beginning to a dream.\nIII. Nothing can truly destroy the soul. There are magics that can trap and control souls, but never can one destroy the\n\nsoul. The soul is, therefore, eternal.\nIV. The Third Vision of the First Prophet and the Third and Sixth Commandments of Yahweh speak of souls as temporary guests of the Mortal body. When our bodies are finally spent, the soul moves on to occupy a new\n\nbody. We shall be reincarnated for eternity, until Yahweh finally awakes and our world ends.\nV. The soul cannot escape this world. Copies of a soul may find their way to realms beyond Mortal perception by performing great deeds or through deities, such\n\nas the legendary Hall of Heroes or the ancestral plane. However, this is not the soul; it is merely a memory of the Mortal that shall be remembered by Yahweh and in the lore of our world.\nVI. Divine beings, such as the Aenguls, the Spirits, and the\n\nAspects, were set above you for a reason. To serve them is permissible, if not encouraged, so long as their commandments do not violate Yahweh’s commandments.\nVII. Orange and red represent the dawn that shall come when Yahweh awakes and true creation\n\nbegins. Followers should wear something of these colors. It is to remind us that we are temporary beings in a temporary world.\nVIII. Yahweh is not omnipresent. It is impossible for a being to be omnipresent. His Eye wanders the world, working in events\n\nhe happens to see. When one prays to Yahweh, go deep into nature, lay down upon rocks or tree or grass, and chant your prayer. Weeks must be spent in this way, so that if Yahweh’s gaze falls upon you, Yahweh may hear and answer your prayer.\nIX. Shul'Tak\n\nonce said this to me: “You are Utterly Insignificant in the Universe.”\nX. When Yahweh touches you, you will receive visions. Yahweh does not speak in mortal tongues. Yahweh uses images, emotions, and memories to communicate. They last only for a moment;\n\nthe being of Yahweh is so great and so wondrous that the mortal mind cannot comprehend it.\nXI. Meditation is key to achieving inner peace, contentedness, and self-awareness so one can fully experience Yahweh’s glorious creation.\nXI. May Yahweh watch\n\nover you and may you walk in the Light of the Truth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "§bUnknown", "[!] The handwriting looks rather messy, though the words are still readable.[!]\n\n*Get herbs!\nElf's Hair Vine\nDrake's Tail\nAthin\nMetzli's Tangle\n\nAsk Ibar or Rose if they have Alabaster leaf.\n\n[!] On this page there is a sketch of a rather short tower made of stone, a little pond shimmers in the sunlight next to it.  Some tulips peak out through a light layer of snow near the water.[!]\n\n[!]In the same handwriting as page before reads, --\n\n-- \"Couldn't sleep, this dream was about him again.  It was the same night when he returned, though I wasn't able to do what I wanted.  Instead of me fleeing like I did when it was real I froze in fear as the door bursted open.  I couldn't do anything --\n\n-- but watch as he came closer.  Before he got into the doorway I woke up.\"[!]\n\n[!]The rest of the page is just sketches of several different types of herbs and flowers.  A few of the lower sketches looked a little smudged, thought you can still point --\n\n-- them out.[!]  [!]On this page you see a sketch of a mountain, what looks like a cave is on the side.  On the bottom of the slope there's a giant figure that looks frozen.[!] [!] Next is a sketch of a frozen lake below a steep slope, a giant ice --\n\n-- pillar sticks up from the ground near the slope and lake.  At the top of the slope it looks like there's some platform, below it, in the lake, there's a hole in the ice.\nWritten near the sketch reads, \"Weird place near tall mountain with ice and --\n\ngiant ruins with thanium and a tower\"[!] [!]Another sketch has been scribbled down, this one is of a pudgy, grey bird with a flower held in its beak, another sketch besides it shows the bird fluttering with a bunch of white peonies clutched in its feet[!]\n\n\"Had another dream, this time the tower burnt down with me in it.  Another dream-- #//.... ##// \\\\\" The rest of the entry is scribbled out.[!] [!]A few sketches of several designs of a strange mask are on the next few pages, one of them --\n\n-- is a blue mask with red hood, a steel mask with a red hood, and a few more.  They all go with a red hood.  Signed below them reads, \"Barnak designs\"[!] Here is a note that sits between the pages, looks a bit worn but still --\n\n-- readable.  The note first starts with a scribbled out name, \"B-/#/--,  I found something you might want to see... This thing reads, 'Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment.  We are born by the dark; Made men by the Dark; Undone by the --\n\n-- Dark; We fear the Old Dark.'  *Next on the note is a scribble of what looks like a map, in the south there seems to be a little settlement, it's labeled Carnatia.  To the north in the mountains is labeled 'Ruins' just before the ruins --\n\n-- there's an area that's circled.* Signed, N-#..-\"[!]\n[!]\"Get soft relaxant for Kale.[!] [!] \"These dreams still continue even though H#//.- is gone.  A part of me thinks he will somehow come back like he did before, and when he does come back, it'd\n\n-- be the death of me.  This thing that I do with #o--+/n Taskan kinda helps take my mind off of it, plus I enjoy helping others.[!] [!] The rest of the page is just a rather detailed sketch of a peach plant, there's small white flowers around them.[!]\n--\n\n[!] Another note rests between the pages, this reads, \"Leave this land before I claim it myself.\"[!] [!]A sketch at the bottom of the page is scribbled out rather harshly.[!]\n\n-- [!]A sketch is on this page, it's of a narrow clawed figure with antlers.  Written below it is, \"Drawing from wendigo\"[!] [!]Here is a detailed sketch of ruins, snow rests atop of the cold bricks as the arches loom over the steps, leading to a tower --\n\n-- on the side of a mountain.  The tower looks over the ruins that sit at the bottom of steep, snowy mountains.  Labeled near the drawing reads, \"Sketchy plance north of Carnatia\"[!] [!] \"Continue to have trouble sleeping, nightmares --\n\n-- aren't as often as they were when they started.  They come about every other night or so, still about him.  I've sort of gotten use to being tired all the time, I don't really go out alone as much anymore unless it's on one of my walks.  We continue --\n\n-- to visit those ruins north of Carnatia, something is really off about that place.  Other than that, life is quiet.  I like it.[!] Another sketch is here, this one of a few potions and vials with flowers and herbs neard their bases, the soft --\n\n-- flowers are like a soft cushion for the small vials.[!] [!]\"Get mandragora, serpents stalk, dwarf's pumpkin, flametounge root, drake's tail, alabaster leaf, metzli's tangle, saffvil, and clutchers straw.\"[!] [!]A few houses --\n\n-- made of stone are sketched onto the page, one looks rather round and neat.  Another tall and ragged, though still nice.  Another, the stone looks oddly shaped, it looks elegant.[!] [!]\"Day one: 38 minas. Day two: 171 [!]\n\n[!]In messy, yet readable, handwriting reads a message,[!] \"Robe designs for Kelian.\" Below the scribble are a few sketches of an elf in dark robes, each sketch's robe design is different than the other.[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Hollowed Umbrage", "UnBaed", "[!] The pages in this book are filled with neat, ink writing.\n\n\n\n\n                 Hallowed\n                 Umbrage\n[A copy from the original]\n\nI write the following epitaph with dire haste so much that the winds part my words.  My account of these events may not be entirely accurate, something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have left in.\n\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded wit a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\n\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite  every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\n\nIt is the weakness of Man to succum to the allure of power, riches, and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain.  Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\n\nFor the corrupting mind of Men ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls, Harpies, and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\n\nLegends tell of the Abyss ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.  I would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\n\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it.  North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\n\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.  For I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\n\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've evered thought to measure.  I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\n\nI dare not write about the countless demonds that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\n\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn my back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\n\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.Radiated in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflamed beside him.\n\nHe worse armor, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armor, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armor, heavy as it appeard did not hinder him.\n\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\n\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with.  This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\n\nDripping with the hollowing souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\n\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage.  King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\n\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\nR A D I A N T\nI S  T H E  B L A C K\nS U N", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheet Music: 433", "§bHeruza", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Soul Puppetry", "Fury_Fire", "The following pages in this book cover a sparsely known Dark Magic known as Soul Puppetry. If this book is found by anyone, it is likely stolen and should be placed somewhere safe and where none will find it.\n\nSoul Puppetry, unlike common belief, is not used to control people in any way, sense, or form. There are no set list of spells, and there are drawbacks on the user. The closest control goes is forcing emotions upon people to the point that they may act\n\nupon such. Mages who practice this will notice a percentage of what they cause coming back upon them in return.\n\nA Soul Puppeteer begins by first learning how to make basic puppets, mimicking the race of the target they wish to inflict their magic upon. These puppets would begin by the molding of clay, making the basic shape of the person. Normal humanoid for\n\nhumans, larger puppets for Orcs. Kharajyr would have ears and a tail. Elves just having ears. Once the clay is shaped, the Puppeteer wraps a layer of moss around it. These signify the 'veins' of the target. After, a layer of hay is wrapped around it all\n\nto both act as the 'skin', and keep it from falling apart. The next bit is when it gets tricky though. The Puppeteer must find a way to extract the blood of the person who they wish to inflict. Such can be done however the puppeteer wants to do such.\n\nWhen the blood is got, even so much as a drop, the puppeteer would push eye sockets in and place the blood in each. They would take hold of the puppet and take a breath, holding it into their chest. They would invision the person that the puppet will be\n\ntied to, imagining him or her as the puppet, before letting the breath escape them and imagine it flowing into the puppet. The connection would be made, and the target would feel a dark presence awakening within them.\n\nThe next step would be complicated. In the end, it would also be similar to the first bit. The Puppeteer would imagine either an emotion or feeling- likely starting with something along the lines of anger. They would take a breath and hold it, imagining\n\nthe very concept of the emotion, before releasing it and willing it into the puppet, likely holding and squeezing its head whilst doing such. Holding the head allows for ease when doing mental curses. As a begginer, the Puppeteer would only make the\n\ntarget mildly annoyed, whilst recieving about half of said anger back upon themselves. Other emotions are easily practiced and learned even without the teachers guidance. Later in learning, the Puppeteer may learn how to inflict pain upon their targets as\n\nwell as horrible curses. Anything the puppeteer can think of can be done, and the more skilled they get the less drawback they recieve. Lower skilled Puppeteers would only hold the connection for twenty elven minutes. Higher skilled could hold them for\n\ndays on end, casting different curses upon someone, although only one at a time. Eventually, the Puppeteer is taught how to create new curses, which is when it is harder to tell what is happening with their victims.", ""),
        StaticBook("[AMC] Flyer", "§bFrancois d'Aumont", "Aumont Mercantile\n         Company\n    -=- -=- -=- -=-\n\nHiring Now! Looking for miners, farmers, lumberjacks, chefs, leatherworkers, breeders, and merchants.\n\nWeekly wages!\nLocation: Felsen\n(Msg: Aumont)", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\n\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\n\n       Lesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\n\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\n\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\n\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\n\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallness of\n\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\n\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treated\n\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\n\n        Lesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\n\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the city,\n\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\n\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\n\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\n\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\n\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\n\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\n\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\n\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\n\n      Lesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\n\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\n\n      Lesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and you\n\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\n\n you can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\n\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\n\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\n\n       Lesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers of\n\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate the\n\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and may\n\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\n\ntaken with all seriousness.\n\n       Lesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\n\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\n\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\n\n     Lesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf impure\n\n this offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\n\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\n\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\n\n        Conclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\n\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\n\n         A Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfling\nLlir/Lliran-Friend(s)\n\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "§bVenator", "Liriel's Book of\n    Alchemy Recipes\n==================\n\nBasic Teas using one ingredient and water:\nRose\nPoppy\nDandelion\nCactus\nBlue Orchid\n\nJuices, brewed with one ingredient and water:\nPumpkin\nCarrot\nMelon\n\nAlcohols:\nPale ale - made with wheat\nMulled Wine - Dark Resin\nEggnog - Egg\n\nPoisons: To be added", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Notes", "§bNemir", "Entry one, 9th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nIt's another cool day here in Kovagrad, there's a nip in the air.  The cold won't be good for the crops.  Never is.  But I hardly need to worry about that.  I'm no farmer, just a simple herbalist.\n\nNotes of lesser accuity potions.\n-----------\nI've prepared a couple of bottles of aqua vitae, just had to soak this red root in warm water for a few hours.  It's pure alcohol, perfect for greater potions.  Along with the aqua vitae, I've prepared a couple\n\nof bottles of distilled water.  These are for lesser potions.  Gonna need some more coal or perhaps some charcoal soon if I want more of these lesser bases.\n\n\nAlright.  Now that I've got my bases all set up, I'm gonna put some larihei's fingers\n\ninto the aqua vitae.  I ended up getting a salve of larihei.  Upon using it I've noticed my movements were more... delicate for a short amount of time.  Perhaps an agility potion could come out of this.\nI added halflings grass and got something I like to\n\ncall a soft relxant.  It pretty much soothes muscle pain for a short amount of time.  Perfect for sore muscles!  I believe this should be enough notes for the day.  I shall continue tomorrow or perhaps sometime later on this week.\n\nEntry two, 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nToday I've decided to mess around with the distilled water as the base.  I will do as I did the other day, use larihei's fingers.  The outcome of this was a potion that, when drunken, I felt like my mind was\n\nclearer.  I was more aware of my movements, could be useful.  Upon adding halfings grass to the potion I got a liquid that was thinner than water, and it swirled nonstop within the bottle.  Upon testing it, my vision was blurred greatly, though I felt\n\nmore agile.  I guess it'd be helpful.\n\nEntry three, 11th of The Deep Cold, 1569.\nSimple poisons.\nRed Mushroom Poison, makes the user have an upset stomach and feel nauseated.  Good for telling someone to fuck off when they ask for wine.\n\nPotion of Alabaster Leaf, about the same effects as the last poison, but looks more like tea than wine.  Plus it doesn't have white particles floating around in it.  Potion could also be used as an antidote to other poisons.  If used as one, it'd still\n\nmake the user's stomach upset.\nPotion of Saffvil, if this is consumed in large amounts the user will die due to its poison.  If consumed in smaller amounts the user will just vomit.\nPotion of Clutcher's Straw, if this potion is taken in large amounts\n\nthe user's muscles will lock up, paralyzing them.  They will remain conscious.\nParalyzing Toxin, this seems to be one of the most deadly poisons I've ever made.  Any amount taken makes the user paralyzed, keeping them from seeking out an antidote.\n\nAnother effect is that the user will struggle to breath, eventually suffocating them.\nParalyzing Tonic, another helpful poison.  If the user takes any amount of this poison they will become paralyzed and blind for a short amount of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("prophets trials1", "§bFaiz Ibn Qhuhafah", "Trials of the prophets Part 1\n\nby Faiz Ibn Qhuhafah\n\nThe prophets (peace be upon them all) have things in common and things seperating them. One thing in common is the common faith in Allah.\n\nThe first prophet (Allahs peace be upon him) lived and breathed for Allah. He was the first to bring us out of the time of many heads of religion where humanity worshipped the many faced god of barbery and savagry.\n\nthey believed him weak as a caravan found him by a burned down bush in the desert thirsty and almost starved to death. They laughed at him and asked him \"which god?\" as he said that allah had shown himself to him in the bush.\n\nThey believed him weak as he refused to join the savage rituals where you drank the blood of your fellow man... \n\nAs his words spread and the first believers of the Iman al-Rashidun began to gather they where scared.\n\nAllah had put his fear in them but the ïblis convinced them to do the unforgiveable. In the middle of the night guided by ïblis they dragged him out his bed in the middle of the night and dragged them to their camp.\n\nin their camp they bound him to a pike and roasted him alive above the flames of ïblis. THEY tried to get him to resign the Iman al-Rashidun... the only words he said was \"Subhanallah!\" in disbelief they kept roasting him... not a scream was let out.\n\nIn the morning however a broad scare of men screamt on top of their lungs as the wrath of Allah was released on the men and all where dead except one soldier to tell the tale of Allahs wrath.\n\nThe second prophet of Allah was once a brave warrior whom had killed countless people in battle untill he met the first prophet (Allahs peace be upon him). The first prophet inspired him to a life in peace trying to achieve the greatest of all jihads.\n\n“To fight against the infidels is Jihad; but to fight against your evil self is greater Jihad.” said the first prophet (Peace be upon him) to our second as our second raised his sword to defend our first. Our dear first prophet was lead off to die.\n\nThe second prophet gathered support from the commoners and support of Allah was spread trueout the camp. As the protests came to the cheifs tent our second prophet stepped forward towards the cheifs guards whom had swords drawn\n\nOur second prophet stepped forward towards the guards taking the sword from his belt dropping it in front of the guardsmen calling out their leader: \"If you want to fight come forth and kill me. If you do not let us pass.\" Seized by the compassion\n\nof Allah their leader surrendered and the men rejoiced in the glory of allah pronouncing: \"There is no god but allah and the prophets are his messengers.\"\n\nThis wave of peaceful protests swept a second camp but in the third camp something changed...\n\nThe third camp the garrison went amock leaving our prophet slain upon the field together with thousands of civilians. However Allahs plan was not over for the second prophet as he seven days later in a miracle rose from the grave for the world to behold.\n\nWhile dead he had spoken with Allah and in his wisdom Allah knew that the infidels would not surrender their many faced god without force but stubborn our second prophet carried on.\n\nHe gathered more people and led them back to the city in a peacefull wave... once more him and his companions where slain and Allah urged him to use violence but no. Thrice he was slain and thrice he was ressurected in total for Allahs plan.\n\nAfter his third resurection our prophet saw the damage it had done to his camp as they came together around him he asked for his sword with the words: \"We fight because He – the Glorified – commanded us with fighting\" when asked why he now suddently\n\nhave decided to fight.\n\nHe conqoured all the tribes and left men of the Iman al-Rashidun  to rule them independantly untill Caliph Faiz united the clans.\n\nAllah have plans for all of us both prophets, laymen and infidels. We may try to reject our plan but Allah will always steer us onto the path.\nInsha'Allah\n\nSubhanallah", ""),
        StaticBook("We come as crows", "§bUnknown", "------------------- -------------------   We come as crows\n-------------------\n \n\n      _IIII\n     --IIIII\n         IIIIII\n         IIIIIIIII\n          IIIIIIIIIIII=-\n             IIIII\n              _I.\n\nIt was a quiet night in the city of Kralta. The never-ending, calming trickle of the murky riverwater was one of the few sounds that were heard through the night. Occasional caws of the crows echoed through the muddy pathways and alleywas of the city, as\n\na single woman walked in the night. Slutinyova, the most beautiful woman in the city, though, she hadn't managed to find any work in the city yet. On her way towards the inn, she heard an odd sound in the night. She gazed upwards to the sign.. \"Smithery\"\n\nThe name was carved on the sign. A quiet, steady banging could be heard inside. Her curiosity took over, and she snuck inside in quiet steps. The planks creaked under her foot as she was fully inside, and she attracted the smith's attention. He had been\n\nhammering a sword all alone in the night.\nThe smith quickly put the unfinished sword away as he noticed Slutinyova, ashamed of his work. Slutinyova, however, didn't mind. In fact, she thought the sword looked mighty.\nSurely the sword had thrusted through\n\nmany challenges and stretched even more wounds. \n\n\"Make leave, customer, smithery am closed!\"\nThe smith said.\n\n\"Worry not, am here to help! Sword looked like needs many grinding and polish.\" She claimed.\n\nThe blacksmith allowed a sigh escape his lips as he presented the his sword to her. She gently took the sword in her hands, examining it with a curious eyes.\nThe blade was great in size, yet it had its faults, it was curved to the side slightly.\n\nSlutinyova held the sword for a bit, before starting to work on it.\n\n\"I'm sure I know what I'm doing.\" Slutinyova said, as she brought the sword to the grindstone. The blade began getting in better shape with each swipe against the\n\ngrindstone. It would soon be finished. The sword started to look like it was done. The smith seemed very happy of the outcome, though she wasn't completely done with the sword.\n\n\"Slutinyova must make polish of sword!\" She said enthusiastically.\n\nShe took the banner in the colours of Carrion in her hand, rolling it around her palm before she rested it against the mighty fine blade. The unladylike manner she polished it was astonishing, furiosly she swiped against the sword up and down. Across the\n\nblade, until finally it looked like it was ready.\n\n\"Am done.\" she said, when she finished and the blade was finally done and it gleamed with victory and glory.\nThe smith smiled, as the most tedious part of creating merchandise was made\n\nin his stead.\n\n\"Many thanks, woman.\"\nhe said, continuing;\n\"But now must make way to fix creak-plank on floor, da?\"\nThe smith said, as he rested his sword. He moved over to the plank Slutinyova had stepped on, that let out a nasty creak\n\nas she stepped over it. He took the hammer he had been using earlier, beginning to nail the plank back to its place. It was unheard of to bang this loud in the night of Kralta, yet the plank was soon as good as new. \"Now all am ready for business, make\n\nstay for assistance?\"\nThe smith said.\n\"Da, da, da!\" She nodded in reply hastily, happy to finally find work..\n\nand so they made many swords together for the glory of Raevir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 4", "§bAnthron", "Continuarion of part 3!\n-------------------CONVENTIONS OF THE ELVEN LANGUAGE 1 - 7\n-------------------\nThis is the last book, so final thanks to Sporadic for making these books possible on the forums!\n\nThe elven tongue was almost exclusively spoken. Evidence for this is found in the ruins of Inwe, where the writings of early Dark Elves were in an ancient dialect of the common tongue. The most often used elven words in writing are names\n\nsuch as Mali'nor (now Malinor) and Velulaei.\n\nWhatever caused the language to change so drastically through the ages is not known, but is especially remarkable due to the long lives of elves, which would presumably make evolution of a language go much slower.\n\nIt is suggested that a taboo on elvish was enforced, though why and by who remains unknown.\n\nIt has been rumored that elvish was also the language of nature, which the elves either learned through study or was taught to them by certain deities.\nThey then had the power to converse with nature directly, allowing\n\nthem to guide the growth of trees and migration of animals as if by magic. If this were true, elvish, assuming someone was capable of mastering the long-forgotten cadence of the words, would be a very potent language indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Homunculi", "§bBelegar", "The Homunculi\nBy Belegar Tunnelsmasher\n\nMalin’s Welcome, 1551\n\nPreface\nI, Belegar Tunnelsmasher, brother of Beros Oathcast whose body was made into a homunculi, am writing this to serve as a warning against dangers the homunculi pose and how to take on out if the situation comes to it.\n\nHomunculi 101\n\nThere are currently four tiers of homunculi being: fiend, deviant, aberrant and doppleganger. \n\nFiends\n- looks like a fiend\n- weak, very short lvied\n- not sentient\n\nDeviants \n- look similar to the race of the descendant whose body they are created from\n- slight disfigurements\n- odd skin colours\n- short lived\n\nAberrants\n- very similar look to descendants\n- unnatural skin colour\n- very small disfigurements\n- greater strength than descendants\n- average lifespan\n\nDopplegangers\n- extremely intellignet\n- very strong, to the point of being able to lift items such as entire iron gates\n- bodies are almost perfect\n- cannot be killed by natural means (will be explained later)\n- does not have blood, instead has a\n\nsubstance related to the element they were created with\n- look identical to the descendant they are made from\n\nHomunculi have no morals or regard for life. They only look to extend their own lives and further their own goal to achieve ‘ascendancy’. In other words, they seek to become a god. This is the fifth tier of homunculi, and the tier that has yet to be\n\nachieved. It is imperative that they do not achieve this.\n\nAdditionally, most homunculi do not have souls. \n\nThe process to create a homunculi will not be detailed in this book, but let it be known that in order to make one a corpse is required,\n\nand the homunculi will not hesitate to murder to get their hands on one.\n\nHow to Kill a Doppleganger\n\nIn order to kill a Doppleganger, one cannot use normal means. Simply cutting off their heads will not end their existence, as if their body is left alone, it will slowly regenerate until fully formed once again.\n\nThe only way to completely kill a Doppleganger is to inject their bodies with a ‘Potion of Unmaking’. \n\nThe process to create this potion requires an experienced alchemist. The reagents needed are: Metzil’s Tangle, Flame Tongue Root, Serpent's Stalk,\n\nLarihei’s Fingers and two lodestones. A lodestone is a rock that exhibits magnetic properties. Once this potion is made, the Doppleganger must be incapacitated and every piece of their body injected with this potion. The potion will then tear the\n\nhomunculi apart and end their existence.\n\nKnown Dopplegangers\n\nAt the time of writing, there are two know Dopplegangers. They are Prohan and Lotho. They are extremely dangerous, do NOT approach them voluntarily. \n\nBoth have air as their element of creation.\n\nProhan:\n\n- human\n- tan skin\n- black hair\n- looks like Daniel Nodal\n- Member of the Dawn Strider Voyagers, often seen wearing the uniform\n\nLotho:\n\n- dwarf\n- white skin\n- blonde hair\n- looks like Beros Oathcast\n- no accent\n- usually seen dressed in white robes with a set of goggles atop his head\n\nWeaknesses of Homunculi\n\nHomunculi are damaged by aurum and Holy Magic much like the undead are. If confronting a homunculi, especially a Doppleganger, it is highly recommended to wield an aurum blade and wear aurum armor.\n\nAlso, if possible, assistance of one versed in the arts of Holy Magic is highly recommended.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\n\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\n\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\n\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\n\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\n\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowess\n\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\n\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\n\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\n\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\n\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\n\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity of\n\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\n\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\n\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\n\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\n\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\n\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\n\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\n\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\n\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvation\n\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\n\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\n\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\n\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\n\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for in\n\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\n\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\n\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\n\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\n\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\n\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\n\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\n\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\n\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the grace of love\n\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\n\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\n\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\n\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\n\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\n\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\n\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\n\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repugnant\n\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electricity", "Fury_Fire", "12th of the Deep Cold\n((6:30))\nLightning struck some distance away. After searching for some time, it was found to be the root of a tree that had been struck. Upon examination, it was charred, a slight stench coming from it. By all appearences, the tree\n\nlooked to have been burned. The only thing that told me otherwise was the static electricity still in the air for a short time around it.\n\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n((12:40pm))\nSanctuary\nLightning had struck only a short distance away, in the nearby forest. After searching, the path of earth that was struck had been found. Being even near the strike that had happened moments before left\n\nthe taste of metal in my mouth, and the smell of burning grass. The ground looked as if it had caught aflame for some time, yet the downpour had put it out. Other then that, the lightning strike itself was caught in full view. It had shot down\n\ndiagonally from the sky, other minor areas branching off from the strike. It had been followed by a loud clap of thunder.\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:44 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, a Telekenisis user.\nShe mentioned tha\n*The rest of the page is ripped out*\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:45 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, telekenisis user.\nStated that every time one connects to the void, they get a tad weaker as their magic grows a tad stronger. Explained that they would clear their mind, much as done in\n\nnormal meditation, and then one would imagine said element in their mind, along with their target. As they did this, they would envision a connection with the void. Often, one would twitch someplace when they connected, and their bodies would be put under\n\ngreat stress.\n\n5th of the grand harvest, 1554.\n((11:25 AM))\nI sat in my home, having connected with the void. The spark I summoned remained there for some second, before I would aim to brighten it, as shown before. As this happened I would grow tired almost immediatly,\n\nthe spark vanishing and I fell over, exhausted. I had felt something different then the normal rate of mana consumption, however. As I forced myself to use the mana required to make the spark brighter, I felt something that could only be described as a\n\na portion of 'life force' being withdrawn. I couldn't quite tell the amount, but I assumed this was my mana. All I could learn from this attempt was that it used up more mana then a normal spark.\n\nSometime in the Amber Cold, 1554\n((1-2 am-ish?))\nI allowed myself to be struck by electricity in my Augur form. Almost all feeling left me side pain, my entire body feeling as if it had become static. Side that, I could not tell much else about it.\n\n15th of the Amber Cold.\n((9 PM))\nI had now grown familiar with telling the amount of mana being used. As I would brighten my spark, I now fully felt the mana leave me. I had over time grown accustomed to how much Mana I had anyways, which\n\nis a major help as I determine the usage. I remain aware that my mana pool will end up growing eventually through meditation anyways, yet I would imagine it would be slow enough that I would grow used to it as such happened.\n\n11th of the First Seed, 1556.\n((5:44 PM))\n\n[!]Page has been torn out angrily!\n\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1557.\n((10:39 PM))\nI sat upon an altar in a forest with Nemir, preparing to shoot a bolt of electricity. It began with normal meditation, and the summoning of several sparks. I would concentrate them within the center of\n\nmy palm, forming a 'bolt', of sorts. After this I would hold my hand out and release it forward.\nThe bolt would hit the ground, leaving the air with a light feel of static for some moments before it would vanish and the brunt of fatigue hit me.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1559\n((3:30 PM))\nAt this point, not much had changed side my bolts growing steadily stronger as well as my ability to cast more. At this point I can cast three before I run out of mana, and the chance of me forgetting to\n\ncut the connection with the void before firing is minimal. I have finally noticed to conductive affects of metal, having cast near an iron rod once. My bolt had veered in midair, hitting the rod instead of continuing to go straight.\n\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1559\n((6:50 PM))\nA Kharajyr female was attacking a group of elves as I stood back and raised my hand, curious on how powerful my bolts had truely grown. Sparks began to form as well as sweat upon my brow, soon collecting\n\nwithin the center of my palm to form a bolt. It was obviously weak in power compared to Locke's, yet still okay in my eyes. Soon I let it fly towards the Kha, and the effects were surprising. The Kha fell over, stunned for some moments as the elves took\n\nthat chance to grab the Kha and bind it. Upon further inspection, the Kha bore a charred burn mark where the bolt had hit- although likely only caused due to her fur temporarily catching aflame.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1562\nThis hasn't been written in for some time, but it's about time to continue it. Since my last entry, my bolts have grown to full power and I'm able to cast three in a row before being unable to cast another. A full powered bolt\n\nwill easily leave burns on someones skin and make them paralyzed for some while. Alternatively, I can call a bolt down from the sky.. Such is done as a normal bolt is made within the hand. The difference would be that you're treating a point in the sky as\n\nthough it would be what you were summoning with instead of your hands. This alone would cause much more mana, and you'd also need a view of your target. It would take as much mana as though you summoned a normal bolt and shot it to that point in the sky.w\n\nPast that, you would pour much more mana than a normal bolt of electricity into it, soon to the point where it would be a full powered bolt of lightning ready to be launched. At first it would remain very hard to aim, and almost every  shot would miss.\n\nThese would not grow more powerful, and the reason you summon it in the sky is simple: Controlling that amount of mana close to you is stupid and dangerous. Even if you controlled it, the amount of electricity would harm you even if you are the creator.\n\nAs you continue doing such, it will become much easier to aim and not stress you as much.\n\nFinal words:\nThis book was originally aimed as a record of my learning, yet eventually I decided that it could be used to help any aspiring Electric Evocationists learn. It does not cover everything about the magic, although it still does with a lot of\n\nit. And I urge any who would use it to be cautious and find another electric evocationist to assist them in learning, be it as a teacher or mentor. This magic is dangerous to learn and at times I nearly killed myself with it.\n-Lefkos Glowsbane", ""),
        StaticBook("((hobbits song))", "§bGeedin Jayamen", "2 6 9 6 \n2 6 9\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 4 3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3 2 3 2", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Story Vol. 1", "§bNemir", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0       Chronicles of§0\n§0           Nemir§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0        The Orcish§0\n§0          Deserts\n\nWay back in my youth, I had spent a year of my life living within the golden deserts of the orcs.  I was around the age of fifteen and had just fled from the high walls of the Silver City of Haelun'or.  I didn't agree with their ways of purity and was\n\nstill sepparated from my Father at the time, so had no connection with anyone from the city.§0\n§0\n§0I had met an impure high elf named Kelian Dawnstrider who offered me to go to the deserts and became his apprentice in smithing after I\n\nhad told him of my troubles with the Silver City.§0\n§0\n§0It may seemed foolish of me accept his offer so quickly, but I felt as if I had no where else to go and no way to support myself.  I was lucky that his words were true, and my new home became\n\na shabby wooden shack in the back of the Raguk's camp on the edge of the Orcish Desert.  There is where my journey began.§0\n§0\n\nThe work was harder than how I anticipated it to be, and the scorching sun was of no help with the heat of the forge.  All of the orcs seemed to respect Kelian, he was apparently a friend of the clan's leader.  I wish I could remember his name, but time\n\nhas blurred it from my memory.§0\n§0\n§0Not all of the orcs seemed pleased with my arrival to the clan, but most of them were welcoming.  It had taken me a few months to get used to their tongue, and I eventually didn't need Kelian or one of the\n\nslaves to help me with translating.  My clothes had also becomed stained with sweat and dirtied with dust, my hair was a little more tangled, and I noticed how tan I was becoming due to almost constant exposure to the sun's rays.  I truly looked out of\n\nplace when I visited some of the major cities, or maybe I just began to look like an average peasant; however, there were the occasional few who questioned why a young high elven girl was running about in dirty and tattered clothing.\n\nTo be truthful, I looked more like a sun elf than a high elf, but just shorter and thinner.§0\n§0\n§0Kelian had been teaching me how to make chainmail armor since I was too scrawny to use the hammer or other heavy equipment.  Over time, I was getting\n\nbetter with my work and began to feel more at home and at peace.§0\n§0\n§0After spending a few months with the Raguks, I was woken one night by Kelian saying that we needed to pack our things quickly and leave.  I was in a stupor and took a moment before\n\nasking what was going on.  He said that the clan leader had lost a honor klomp [klomp = fight in Blah] and thus lost his position.  His opponent turned out to be one of the orcs who disliked Kelian and I's presence in the camp and was rumored to be a\n\ntyrant leader by a few other orcs who were leaving with us.§0\n§0\n§0We left under the cover of night, unnoticed, as we trekked out into the wastes, our footsteps being drunken by the drifting sands.  All night we walked, lugging all that we had taken from t\n\ncamp.  It wasn't until dawn that we came across a gargantuan rock that loomed over the sands and a cacti forest.  We had discovered our destination: The Lur Clan.§0\n§0\n§0They accepted us, all of us, agreeing with our opinions of the new Raguk leader.\n\nKelian and I were out of work since the orcs in the Lur clan already had a smith, but we were still allowed a tent to sleep in.  We didn't plan to rest there for long and began seeking out new work.\n\nLuck was with us and we met a human family named the Malinovs.  They were lovely people, and over time of me knowing them, I felt as if I was a part of them.§0\n§0\n§0Kelian and I moved out of the deserts and into dwarven lands.  A human who owned a manor\n\nallowed us to live in a smaller building by his home, the Malinovs included, and together we planned to  create The Blackwood Company.§0\n§0\n§0My time with the orcs ended there, and I began my next beautiful journey with the dwed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comming of age", "§bHigh Consul Samsung II Irongrinder", "A comming of age story.§0\n§0-------------------------------§0\n§0\n§0Twas a gloomy day within the darkening halls of Dragur, a sojourn to learn with an elf, another elf, and surprisingly yet another elf. Such was uncommon company for our hero, for to converse with\n\nsuch sizeable beings, as one so short himself was rather intimidating, a slight on his stone-born honour. Yet nontheless they conversed, on topics taboo to those of the everyday. Untill much to his supprise, events took a turn for the worse, a lack of\n\nappreciation for one's particular choice of rhetoric, a face turning from joy to anger, and he was taken down. The remaining two turned to our chosen, displeased with his lack of empathy for their ways, one melded into shadow, and we saw naught but night\n\nfor many an unnaturally long hour. And so we walked, out of such a scholarly place, far through the woodlands, accross raging rivers and grassy plains, past sleeping elk and ignorant hunters. Stopping beside a rather naturally appealing area, a small\n\nspring and waterfall tucked beside a gargantuan mountain within a thick fir forest. The socially inept elf was thrown aside, and all eyes turned upon our hero, laying unaware upon the ground. The shadow walked forth, and planted life within him, delving\n\ninto a stygian pool, arising§0\n§0free, reborn. Such is the sad. . . sad. . .is such a poor choice of wording, for to call something poor merely because it is commonplace within society is a farce itself, for such is subjective, always a choice! One must\n\nnever limit their opinion based upon what is deemed natural! For the unnatural is a learning expierence itself, indubitably so. So let us return to our tale, and resume where we have left off. . .Our hero awoke a great deal of time later, days after the\n\neternal darkness had left the world, within a cell much like the ones within your own home's dungeon, beside him the socially inept elf, bloodied, and asleep. Our father was present, watching over us with an ever-loving gaze, he would ensure our rebirth\n\nexisted without interferance, a plesant birth, unlike those of years past, we would find ourselves not tormented, but knowing of our gift, not agressive to our kin, but warm, a true family.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pirate Insults", "§bNemir", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         How to§0\n§0          Insult§0\n§0           Like a§0\n§0             Pirate§0\n§0-------------------          Written by:§0\n§0   Nemir Valnelis Ward\n\nSo you want to talk like a pirate?  Well you've found the right book!  After reading this, you'll surely knock your enemies down wish just your tongue.§0\n§0\n\nStarter words:§0\n§0- Idiotic§0\n§0- Parrot-loving§0\n§0- Mumbling§0\n§0 - Blathering§0\n§0- Bleating§0\n§0- Sheep-brained§0\n§0- Pin-headed§0\n§0- Pig-breathed§0\n§0- Cricket-sized§0\n\nMiddle words:§0\n§0- Seaweed-slurping§0\n§0- Duck-billed§0\n§0- Pus-faced§0\n§0- Toothless§0\n§0- Knuckle-dragging§0\n§0- Cross-eyed§0\n§0- Scurvy-ridden§0\n§0- Clam-tongued§0\n§0- Yellow-bellied§0\n\nLast words:§0\n§0- Whale-fart§0\n§0- Cow-pie§0\n§0- Sack o’maggots§0\n§0- Cabin boy§0\n§0- Swabber§0\n§0- Waste of skin§0\n§0- Bag of vomit§0\n§0- Anchor-head§0\n§0- Piece of filth§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn II", "§bMarch Ash", "The valleys are beautiful. The soil is rich, game is plenty. It is an oasis among a world defiled by the city. I think I will rest here, for a while, and commune with the land. My journey has been harsh, and my wounds still need to heal.\n\nI will tend to them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!]In elvish the words read, \"Be warned those who enter here, you cannot kill what you do not know, and we did not know.\"§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0othelutal'ame?§0\n§0-------------------[!]The phrase above is translated into common.\n\n\"Do not take this warning as a challenge; Only the spirits can protect you here, and even then, only just barely.   It was cowardice to run from a fight, but not cowardice to avoid what is only death.\"\n\nLearn what Mali'ii means§0\n§0-----------------§0\n§0urthir'lari metta'igne = The Phoenix Queen", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "To his Grace High Prince Aenor Calithil and the Assembled Princely Council of the Dominion of Malin,§0\n§0\n§0We the Undersigned officers and enlisted Elves of the Order of Sirame humbly petition that a certain Writ of Commandment issued by his Grace the High\n\nPrince on the 10th of The Grand Harvest 1618 of Aegis be rescinded or Countermanded by action of the High Prince of the Assembled Princely Council, for such cause as follows:§0\n§0 §0\n§0We find that the exercise of Command§0\n\n over the armies or fleets of any Nation is best made by those experienced in command and chosen for their Place by virtue of martial skill and Experience; thus it is our humble Opinion that, considering the office of el'tilurirvahai is, to our Knowledge,\n\non the main administrative and scrivenal in nature, and that Persons who may in future hold this office will be elevated thereto on the basis of their ability to discharge these particular clerical or diplomatic responsibilities, giving this Office any\n\nsubstantial place in the hierarchy of fighting Elves is, respectfully, ill-advised and potentially catastrophic.§0\n§0\n§0We additionally find the Writ of Commandment aforementioned applies only to the Order of Sirame and not to\n\nthose divers Armies of the Dominion of Malin; considering el'tilurirvahai is considered a representative and surrogate of the High Prince and not the leader of the Principality of Laureh'lin we first would care to know why the Order has\n\nbeen singley targeted by this Writ, and second we find the imposition of additional Princely authority upon the Order alone is, in no small measure, unfair. §0\n§0\n§0We finally find that, though the Writ makes some provision for the maintenence of the\n\nprudent chain of command in event of combat, this reservation is insufficient to avoid the danger outlined in the first paragraph of this humble Petition; further, it is our humble Opinion any Circumstance in which the Command of fighting Elves shall\n\nbe decided by the precise State of affairs facing these Elves is one which shall beget only confusions and the dangerous potential of accusations of mutiny, for in such a situation questions shall inevitably arise, to writ:  When shall combat exist,\n\nbefore the law?  At what precise moment does the general command of fighting Elves revert to the officer of the Order of Sirame?  In our humble Opinion, these questions present the opportunity for harm to the Elves of the Order of Sirame, both by means of\n\nunlawfully issued orders, a difference of opinion between el'tilurirvahai and the officer of the Order of Sirame in a time when the existance or non-existance of combat shall be, before the present law, inconclusive, or in misunderstood instruction,\n\nthe execution of which will place officers or enlisted Elves of the Order of Sirame in legal peril.§0\n§0\n§0For these reasons we humbly request to your Grace and the Assembled Princely Council to rescind or countermand the Writ of Commandment,\n\nissued 10th of The Grand Harvest, 1618.  In testimony of our agreement to the views herein expounded and in order to illustrate the extent of support they enjoy, we have below signed our Names, as follows:§0\n§0\n§0§oE. Delsaran~§0\n§0§oD. Padaryn §0\n\n§oGuy. Willow§0\n§0§oK. Aureon§0\n§0§oGlee of Torena§0\n§0§oAmaris Onnekina", ""),
        StaticBook("Moonlight Dance", "§bKlaudia Crast", "[!] The story was given by a anonymous man. Though if one must know- he roams the streets of Oren daily.\n-------------------\n\n    Moonlight Dance\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n------------------\n\n~ 1.\n\nThe sun submerged itself beneath the dimming salmon mountaintop to the sight of a harmonic moonlight beginning its climb from the darkened Earth.\n\nThe air was amongst a thinning moisture that\n\n~ 2\n\ntingled the aromatic smell of lingering fern.\nPerfectly placed fingers were present among the warmth of the grass pressed palm. \n\nHer teal eyes pierced the skin to which she glanced, lustfully.\n\n~ 3\n\nEnticing my very being.\nThe charming aura surrounding such a woman pulled me closer to her ever so slightly.\n\nReturning the gaze I then pulled my lips closer to hers, watching the dimming sight of her illuminated -\n\n~ 4\n\nlips under the moonlight.\n\nI found my eyes closing, furthering my body towards hers. The warming sensation of her lips became that of a snug hearth\nbeneath a wood burning stove top.\n\n~ 5\n\nHis mind soon became detained in cadence of her soft lips against his. A joyful ache overtook me as her arms found home upon my shoulders.\n\nNow they were wrapped around my neck.\n\n~ 6\n\nThe slight tug of her arms took me onto the ground alongside her torso. The swing of her affection brought me amongst a trance of cherishment.\n\nThe trance, this trance was soon broken by the inevitable. Pulling my\n\n~ 7\n\nfrom my lips. My adoring eyes opened in a graceful haste to look upon a warming smile within her eyes.\n\nAlmost as if it was a pleasant virus; I too felt a smile manifesting at my mouth.\n\n~ 8\n\nThe beating of our breath was only so slightly shadowed by the delicate rushing water of the creek.\n\nI could only take a moment of admiration towards her before I felt the forward pulling of her weakend hands against my -\n\n~ 9\n\nshirt. The scene fading into an aengulic light as I was pulled down against her chest.\n-------------------\n\nThis story hides the identity of the pair. Although there is more and more descretion upon us.", ""),
        StaticBook("Death of Availer", "§bJosef Timothee", "THE DEATH OF THE\n WANDERING WIZARD\n\n\nOn Ahad, the 8th of the Deep Cold, 1336, the world of Aegis was struck by a terrible tragedy. I, Josef Timothee, record here my own experience during these events.\n\n\nI was in Al'Khazar when a voice rang out, filling all of Aegis. It identified itself as the Wandering Wizard. He said that he had three relics that needed to be taken to the Cloud Temple. If they were to fall into Undead hands, he claimed, terrible\n\ntrouble would result for the people of Aegis. He sent forth a cry over all the lands, asking for support on the journey from Al'Khazar to the Cloud Temple on the King's Road. A large crowd assembled with him in Al'Khazar, mostly humans but\n\nrepresentatives from other races there as well.\n\nThe procession headed down the King's Road and was immediately attacked. Lightning rained down from the skies, and monsters appeared out of thin air. But those in the crowd were ready, and struck back against Iblees minions. The monsters were defeated\n\nthrough sheer numbers of those opposing them, as well as the powerful magic of the Wandering Wizard. All along the journey, he kept up words of encouragement and urged the crowd onwards. The lightning and monsters were relentless, delaying\n\nthe journey terribly.\n\nBy the time the procession reached the Cloud Temple many had died trying to protect the Wizard en route. It was there that the Undead suddenly struck the most violently I have ever witnessed, not only casting lightning powerful enough\n\nto damage the Cloud Temple, but also changing the landscape around it to look like the Nether. Among this, explosions and lightning were striking everywhere, causing great suffering. The Wizard urged all present to take shelter in the Cloud Temple.\n\nI took this advice, having been clipped by lightning and set ablaze. Once inside, the extent of the damage was clear. Hundreds entered the Temple, many wounded by burns or monsters. The Temple shook as explosions rocked it from outside and pieces of it\n\nbroke off. Then...\n\nA new voice rang out, saying that the Wizard had been slain by the Undead. The outpouring of grief was immediate, and the attacks on the Temple ceased.\n\nSomeone shouted that the Undead had taken three objects from the Wizard that looked like eggs. The skies lightened, the landscape changed back, and the crowd left the Temple. But the world was altered permanently with the death of the\n\nWandering Wizard. It remains to be seen what the Undead will do with the stolen relics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Fundamentals of Xionism\n\nThe fundamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V3", "§bMage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be a copy*\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of\n\nthe Void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of\n\nthe Descendants were too weak of blood to stand infront of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood infront of the terror.\n\nIn Ibleeses right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself\n\nagainst the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from pores of his skin, he\n\nroared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krugs Axe and strong was Horens heart as\n\n they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malins sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor thirty years The Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their\n\ngraves to follow Ibleeses mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Ibleeses armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children\n\nmassacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his\n\nchildren and did not leave his forest sanctuary. Horen was too ambitious, too weak of a leader, many of his people fought for Iblees and many of them died of recklessness. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and\n\nThe Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\n\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the Seven Skys had\n\nappeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the\n\nskies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIbleeses soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of Skeletons and Zombies burst aflames and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by The Aengul and\n\nDaemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majest and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed,\n\nsentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut..\n\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunai : Rangers", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Origins ~*~\n\nDuring the reign of Braen Elendil, the Adunian Lord came to see that with the ever rising population of their race, he would soon need a military to keep order instead of relying on the good will of his citizens. And so, he asked his\n\nbrother Cirimas to gather the most elite and loyal soldiers he could find, and bring them before him. The names of these four men were never recorded, but it is known that one was of house Lorsmor, and another of house Loyola. The five men stood before\n\nBraen, all were well trained in the arts of stealth, the longsword, shortsword, dagger and longbow, learning from their fathers and their father's fathers who had to outrun and hide from the Rhodir and other men of Owyn Godwinson during their exodus from\n\nIdunia. Braen decided that based on their traits these five men wouldbe known as the Adunian Rangers, and they would serve as their race's first personal military force. Over time, Cirimas and the four rangers slowly built traditions and organization\n\nthroughout the order, and gained more men along the way.\n\n~*~ Uniform ~*~\n\nTraditionally the rangers had no official uniform, but they were told to stick to a certain code to do with what items of clothing they wore;\n\nthe rangers would wear leather boots, fingerless leather gloves, a leather belt, a large coat and a cloak over the top. The coat of Cirimas was passed from Captain to Captain in the rangers, as was occasionally his cloak. All of this would be over the top\n\nof whatever other clothes they wished to wear.\n\n~*~ Fort Arendil ~*~\n\nThe rangers lived in a large cave system under the hill which Al'Ildic stood upon, though the caves had been renovated to be more like an underground\n\nfortress. Said fortress was named after Arendil, the last King of Idunia, and was meant to be used as a fallback point if Ildon ever came under a siege that it was unable to hold off. Sadly, in the final battle of Ildon in which it fell to the undead, few\n\nmanaged to get inside the fortress before it's gates had to be shut to save those inside.\n\n~*~ Watchtowers ~*~\n\nAs the Adunian Kingdom spread over the land, the ranger's decided that they could only keep order in Ildon itself from\n\nfort Arendil, and would have to find a way to do so in the towns, farms and estates that surrounded it. And so the watchtowers were built all over the kingdom. In each watchtower, a single ranger would live along with up to 15 other initiates whom he\n\nwould use to keep order in the surrounding area. The Garrison of each watchtower was rotated every fortnight.\n\n~*~ Traditions ~*~\n\n-The Final initiation for a ranger was for him to be taken out into\n\nthe woods where he would swear an oath of service to the Adunian Race.\n\n-No women or men of non-Adunian blood were permitted to join the rangers.\n\n-An heir to the Adunian throne would have to spend five years in service\n\nto the rangers before he could become lord.\n\nIt is often thought that it was tradition that all young men joined the rangers for several years after they turned seventeen, though in reality seventeen was simply the age where one was permitted entrance\n\ninto the order, and over time it became a popular trend to join the rangers as soon as one was allowed.\n\n~*~ Ranks ~*~\n\nRanger Captain: Supreme commander over the Rangers.\n\nFirst Ranger: The Captain's most\n\ntrusted ranger, and therefor second in command.\n\nRanger: The primary rank of the Adunian rangers, and only the most elite warriors in Adunian society were offered this position.\n\nInitiate: The recruit rank of Rangers, most never made it\n\npast this rank. \n\nAuthor's note:\n\nI myself attained the rank of First Ranger, in the time of Elysium.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul III", "§bMarch Ash", "Underneath the mushroom-caps, the smell of the spores fresh in my nose, it feels easier to breathe. It reminds me so much of the Great Rot. Miles of mycelium, stretching all the way to the horizon. A ground alive with ten trillion hyphae,\n\nsplitting and merging like living rivers, a chaotic order. The memory is as sweet as slime mold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XII", "§bMarch Ash", "The air is cool, but even this deep in the wood I smell on the air the scent of burning coals, and the acrid smoke of furnaces. Even the far north is not free of colonization. Axios has suffered so much, in such little time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepy Tales V2", "§b[Teen] Mikazuki Mantisuku", "~The Girl in the Mask~\n\nNo one can be sure where she started. One thing was sure, she had long raven colored hair, deep sapphire eyes, a small form, fair skin, and a beautiful mask. The rumors that were spread\n\ncould never fully tell the story about this young girl who only seemed to appear at night. All they did tell was she was not something to be trusted or desire to see. Only one rumor seemed to be most agreed upon.\n\nThe story goes that a young girl lived happily in the lap of luxury with her human parents. She was of noble birth and to be wed to one of the princes. She had everything she wanted.\n\nThere was a masquerade ball made in her honor at her home, everyone was asked to wear masks and she was to see if she could find her \"prince\" among the men that attended.\n\nThe ball went well and the girl was excited. Still being just a young maiden, she was already prideful. She donned a beautiful royal blue velvet gown and lovely powder blue mask. She entered the room, excited and happy.\n\nDancing with glee she soon found a taller boy with a dark mask on his face. \"My prince~\" she whispered silkenly to him as she curtsied. Without a word he bowed and the two began to dance. Dizzy and joyous, she announced she found her prince.\n\nWhen he removed his mask, she was startled to realize it was a serving boy. Terrified, she called her guards and her father had him executed. Months passed and the girl lay in her bed soundly asleep. Her wedding gown near the bed,\n\nready for the next day's ceremony. A shadow fell across the room and a figure moved closer to the girl. Before she had time to scream he covered her face with the mask the serving boy wore to the ball.\n\nA scream ripped through the manor as the shadow vanished. Two guards broke into her room and ripped the mask from her face, only to find it had been laced with a powerful poison that ate at flesh. Horrified and fully maimed, they bandaged her face\n\nand tried to find a healer. Even monks could not reverse the damage that had been done and she was forced to wear a mask to cover her scars. With her fiance leaving her, she was locked away in the manor with only a few things to keep her company.\n\nOne night, she crept out and stole the dress away that she was to wear to her wedding. Donning the dress, she hung herself in her room, no one aware of her death till the next morning.\n\nWhen they went to bury her, the mother opened the coffin to find the body gone. Since that day, the young woman had been seen only at night wailing as she wandered.\n\nThe rumors say, if you were to see her, she would beg you to help her. If you try to remove her mask, you would be found brutally murdered with a pale plain mask on your face. But this is just a horror story meant to scare people at night. Or is it?", ""),
        StaticBook("Orcish Plague", "riverfyre", "The Orcish Plague has become a serious and debilitating disease that can kill those infected. With several having perished from the disease, new information has been given. While the information is not complete nor fully understood, what can be pieced\n\ntogether is ways to prevent further spread of this infectious disease. As such it is important to know how the disease is spread, what the symptoms are, and how to be treated. If this plague continues to spread at its\n\npace, entire cities could be wiped away within days of initial contact.\n\nHow it is Spread\n\nThe Orcish Plague has been know to spread in many various ways. How one becomes infected can be done through contact. Any contact with an infected person, creature, food, or area are at high risk of infection.\n\nThose with weaker immunities, children, and elderly are more prone to the disease. With just vicinity being an issue, the spread is far more concerning. The disease seems to be spread through air, consumption,\n\nand contact with poisoned areas. The disease seems to enter through the mouth and nose when exposed to the spores or infected air expelled from an infected individual.\n\nThe disease then spreads in the body from the lungs into the kidneys and other organs. When consumed, it starts with the stomach, spreading into the lungs and other organs. It is unknown what the plague does to the epidermal\n\nwhen touched, but the disease does pose serious health concerns. Bodies that have been infected risk infecting those that touch them. Avoid burying the dead as it can spread through the ground\n\nand can lead to infection of the water supply. Cremation seems to be the best solution for the dead, but take precautions with the smoke.\n\nSymptoms\n\nThe plague slowly devours the body internally. The organs fall one by one until the body can no longer sustain itself. As the body slowly decomposes inside, the pain becomes unbearable and the infected dies slowly and painfully.\n\n- Coughing within the first day\n- Lungs begin to inflame and fill with fluid\n- Lethargy\n- Eyes and flesh begin to turn yellow\n- Kidneys fail\n- Stomach rots\n- Internal organs slowly eaten away by the acid and rot\n- Death\n\nEven after treatment, the infected is left weak and in pain. If you see any sign of a cough or lethargy in children, immediately seek help.\n\nTreatment\n\nThere seems to be no normal way of treatment to spare one from this plague. However, it does appear that holy magic can be used to remove the taint from the bodies. While the plague can do severe damage, only powerful healers can\n\naccomplish the task on the more severe cases. Once healed, the infected can return to their normal duties after they have rested. The infection takes much of their strength and energy, leaving them exhausted\n\nfor several days. It appears even after treatment, one can become infected again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hugh & Humbert", "§bBeelzebub", "There once lived two boys within the great streets and slums of Felsen, one named Hugh and the other named Humbert. One boy lived in the south west of the city, while the other lived in the north east. The two boys were remarkably similar.\n\nThey shared facial features and physical traits, they lived in identical homes, with identical families, with identical pets and identical living circumstances. While identical in all forms, there was one key difference: one boy enjoyed his Scriptures, -\n\n- and the other did not. \n\nIt was Sunday, and both the boy's parents had great meals laid out upon the tables of their homes, to celebrate as any other Orenian families would a successful week. Remarkably, both meals were the same -\n\na big pot pie full with vegetables and meats of all assortments. Hugh sat and had his entree laid before him, and waited for his family to sit as well. He recited Grace, and when his family was ready, he enjoyed his meal with them. He finished his meal -\n\n- and did not pester his mother for dessert. On the other side of the city, Humbert sat and had his entree laid before him. Before his family was sat, Humbert, without Grace, dug into his entree, and feasted like a pig on slop, making a big mess of -\n\n- himself. He sucked down his pot pie, and immediately thereafter demanded dessert from his poor mother. \"Gluttony today, temperance tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he licked his fingers.\n\nAfter their meals, each boy was given free time to do what as -\n\n- they will. Both journeyed, as usual, to the market square before the Imperial Palace. There, Hugh in the south west and Humbert in the north east, the boys encountered similar situations. Beggars often did their works in the market, and both boys met -\n\n- an individual beggar. An old lady, clearly sickened with age, pleaded to each boy for a nickel to purchase some bread. Hugh, while only having just earned the nickel yesterday, was quick to hand over his change - Hugh knew, after all, that he could -\n\n- easily make his nickel back. Humbert, however, refused. Humbert had as well only just earned his nickel, and felt that he had a right to it, a right that the old lady did not have. Humbert told the lady that, once he makes for himself more change, he -\n\n- will come back and give her a nickel, and kept his nickel for himself. \"Greed today, charity tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he walked away from the old lady.\n\nAfter encountering an old lady each, each boy set out to buy a toy from the local toymaker.\n\nDibley's Den was situated on the south west of the market square, and Bungo's Bunk was situated in the north east. As it was a little later in the day, the lines at each shop were quite long, filled with eager children to buy something to play with.\n\nHugh entered the line to Dibley's Den and waited his turn like a good boy, understanding that the others got there first, and that waiting in line was not the biggest problem Hugh faced. He waited politely, until he could finally get his toy from Dibley.\n\nHumbert entered the line to Bungo's Bunk, and immediately became upset with how long the line was. He stomped and stomped, whining like an upset girl, and sniffled and snarled impolitely. Finally, Humbert smacked the boy in front of him in line in the -\n\n- head, knocking the boy out of line and taking his spot. Humbert finally bought his toy from Bungo. \"Wrath today, patience tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he exited Bungo's Bunk with a new teddy.\n\nAfter leaving each respective toy shoppe, each boy -\n\n- encountered another similar situation. Waiting outside both shops were two boys: one with a very nice and expensive toy, and the other with no toy at all, sniffling due to his inability to buy one. Hugh looked upon the boy without a toy, and sighed, -\n\n- for he knew down-below the misfortune of the child. Hugh approached the child, and offered him his teddybear, which the child eagerly accepted. Hugh smiled to the boy and waved him off, knowing that some day he could buy the teddybear again.\n\nHumbert, however, looked upon the boy with an expensive toy, and grew jealous. He desired the other boy's toy, because he knew it was more valuable than his own. He approached the boy, and smacked him upside the head. He took from the boy his expensive -\n\n- toy, a wooden knight, and walked away. \"Envy today, kindness tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he played with the wooden knight.\n\nFinally, it was time to return home. Each boy made his way back, Hugh in the south west and Humbert in the north east. They -\n\n- entered their homes, did as they would, and finally slipped into their beds. They both reflected upon their day. Hugh ate his meal modestly, and Humbert like a pig. Hugh gave to the old lady a Nickel, Humbert a nasty glare. Hugh waited in line -\n\n- patiently, while Humbert cut. Hugh gave away his toy, while Humbert stole a more valuable one. You see - Hugh lives each day like it is his last, and takes each action like the Lord is with him. Humbert tells himself every night that he would make up -\n\n- for his sins the next day. Humbert is a procrastinator when it comes to virtue, and always thinks that he will have a chance to redeem himself. \"Sin today, virtue tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he fell to sleep.\n\nNeither boy knew that this night would -\n\n- be their last. Each boy mysteriously passed away in their sleep, and both were sent before the Lord to recieve judgement. The Lord reviewed Hugh. A good boy Hugh was, diligent when it came to virtue, and a Boy of the Scripture. Of course, Hugh was -\n\n- granted eternal paradise in the Seven Skies above. The Lord reviewed Humbert. A bad boy Humbert was, lazy when it came to virtue, a boy who did not listen to his Scriptures. Because of Humbert's procrastination, his constant vows of \"...tomorrow,\" -\n\n- Humbert was cast down to the pits of Hell, to spend the rest of eternity sitting alone, muttering the following words:\n\n \"Heaven today, or              Hell tomorrow!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Adam", "§bBeelzebub", "There once was a boy, he was named Adam.\n\nAdam loved to sit on his chair.\n\nAdam's mother warned him.\n\n\"Stop! The more you sloth upon that chair, the more you shall become but a potato!\"\n\nAdam said \"No!\" and continued to sit upon his chair.\n\nHe cried and cried, and whined and whined. He would not move.\n\nAdam loved to sit on his chair.\n\n\"Why should I move?,\" Adam asked.\n\nAdam grew fatter and fatter.\n\nHe began to bald.\n\nAdam grew larger.\n\nHe sat upon his chair and all night.\n\nAdam's mother warned him once again.\n\n\"You shall become a chair-potato, Adam!\"\n\n\"That is what happens to boys who idle upon chairs!\"\n\nHe did not move.\n\nAdam grew spotty.\n\nHe became very pudgy.\n\nHe slumped to the side and released a large sigh.\n\nHe was a big chair-potato.\n\nAdam's mother found him upon the chair.\n\n\"Now, he is more useful!\"\n\nAdam's mother brought him into the kitchen, and he was cooked.\n\nAnd his family feasted for many days!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "15th of The First Seed, 1601§0\n§0\n§0*the following would be written in very childish handwriting.*§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary,§0\n§0Eja. My name is Shannara Sarr. I live in a manor by the Druuds. It smells like salt water. I have a Mamie Lila and Mama\n\nKat. §0\n§0\n§0I share a room with my sister, who is named Eloettah. I am seven years old.§0\n§0\n§0Mamie Lila and Mama Kat are out, and Eloettah is not here either, so I am alone. But I am not sad. When I make trouble, Mama Kat and Mamie Lila\n\nshow they care by making me punished. Like climbing over the wall, or riding the chickens (they don't know about that one). I pinky promise what I do is harmless, except the time I got a little boo-boo from climbing.§0\n§0\n§0I have two friends. One named Vivec,\n\nwho will be my Mental Magic teacher when I am twenty, and one named Kayden, who is just a bit older then me. He gave me a sphere of aurum. My friends are Elves, and so am I.§0\n§0\n§0I like to enchant books. Mamie Lila and Mama Kat say that it's useful, and I\n\nbelieve them. But I don't want to be an enchanter--I want to be a Mental Mage!§0\n§0\n§0I don't have any secrets. Secrets are hard to keep, and they get boring enough to share after a while. My deepest secrets I tell Mama Kat and Mamie Lila, because they are\n\ntrustworthy.§0\n§0\n§0My hands are getting sore, so I have to keep switching between them, which is hard. Writing with my right hand is easier, and the letters look prettier. But my left hand works, too, especially for eating with forks and spoons and butter\n\nknives. §0\n§0\n§0Mama Kat gave me something my Aunt Ashana had as a child. It's a little lion stuffed animal. I've never seen a lion. I hope they're friendly. I named my lion Ash. But she is a girl, so I don't think I call her a lion...§0\n§0\n§0Mama Kat and Mamie\n\nLila keep animals near the house, in a very nice pen. Sometimes, when it gets very cold, I help bring them in to the storage and skills room (which is separate from the main house), so the frost doesn't get them. §0\n§0It's getting late, and now my head is\n\ntired and both my hands are getting sore from holding the quill. I want to keep writing, but I don't know what else to write about.§0\n§0\n§0I hope I don't lose this,§0\n§0~Shannara Sarr\n\n14th of The Grand Harvest, 1601§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary,§0\n§0\n§0I'm really hot, and I want a cold treat. No one is around today, and I'm bored and have nothing to do. The walk to Sutica is hot and sweaty, so I don't want to go.\n\n\n§0I want my Mama Kat and Mamie Lila, but they aren't here. Eloettah isn't here, either, so I'm lonely. Vivec isn't around, and Kayden isn't either. Woe is me.§0\n§0\n§0Enchanting is still boring, and still takes up too much time and I hate it. Glyphs are hard, and\n\nmake my head hurt. I will not disappoint Mama Kat by quitting, because it will make her sad, and she will not like me for it.§0\n§0\n§0I hate beds. I hate sleeping. I hate sheets and blankets. When it gets hot, it's hard to sleep, and sometimes it's so bad I have\n\nto sleep in the cellar (because I sneak downstairs), and it's really damp and dark down there. At least it keeps out the heat.§0\n§0\n§0Luckily, because of where the Sarrs live, we are safe from intense heat, because when the sun sets by the ocean, the land cools\n\noff, and it gets really cold.§0\n§0\n§0I hate Mama Kat's horsie. It won't let me ride on it. It silently complained that it was Mama Kat's horse, and her horse only, so I couldn't ride it! AND it wouldn't let me take its saddle! I will tell Mama Kat and Mamie\n\nLila when they get home.§0\n§0\n§0I hate being bored. I hate not having anyone to play with, and I hate not having friends around, and I HATE being seven! I will never turn eight, therefore Vivec will never be able to teach me Mental Magic, because I'll never\n\nturn twenty! Being bored is so awful because it gives you that feeling that, if you don't do anything fun soon, you just might cry! Or resort to swimming in the ocean, which is cool, but salty and I'm not allowed to without Mama Kat and Mamie Lila.§0\n\nI think I'm done writing now. It felt good, and at least I chased the boredom away for a few minutes. I really want a friend to stop by, or get a bird, or Mama Kat and Mamie Lila to get home. I think I'll go to Sutica.§0\n§0\n§0I'm really bored,§0\n§0~Shannara Sarr\n\n13th of The Deep Cold, 1601§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary,§0\n§0An Elven day ago, I was grounded! Like actually grounded! And I did nothing wrong, either. I invited Miss Marzipan over for desert, and Mami Kat yells at me because \"we don't know her.\" I'm absolutely furious!\n\n\n§0Mami Kat was able to get me to apologize so easily, by questioning my love for her--preposterous! I won't allow it!§0\n§0\n§0Other than being grounded, it's been great around here. Eloet (my aforementioned sister) is doing well, and I've\n\nseen her again. I've got Ash under my arm, and I couldn't be happier. I've gotten to making my letters look really pretty, and I'm pleased with the results. §0\n§0\n§0I haven't seen Vivec or Kayden around, which makes me sad. I want to see them again, truly. I\n\nneed friendships. §0\n§0\n§0I guess that's all for now. Nothing more is interesting enough to make a diary entry about. It's not like I have any secrets--except for that I think I'm developing a \"crush\" on Kayden. I get only tingly and happy and awkward when I\n\nsee him on the street. Is that normal?§0\n§0\n§0I'm super embarrassed to document that,§0\n§0~Shannara Sarr\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1602§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary,§0\n§0A few days ago my sister Eloet and I got grounded.§0\n§0\n§0We were at the Wood Elves, and we met a pretty lady named Maeve, who was very pale and had white hair. Her lipstick was\n\ndark, and it contrasted nicely with the rest of her. §0\n§0\n§0And then we met Eris, a nice, seven-year-old girl with red hair like rubies, and green eyes like moss and emeralds. She played with us. §0\n§0\n§0Eris picked the lock to the gatehouse, and we\n\nsnuck in. Eloet was a little hesitant, and I shouldn't have made her do it. I'm really sorry I did. Either way, she forgave me. §0\n§0\n§0We were caught by guards, as Eris was messing with the gates. We jumped from the guard tower into the lake below. Eris was\n\ncaught, we were not. I'm not sure how Eris got away, but she did, and we hid behind a tree for a while, until Mami Kat and Mamie Lila found us. Then we were grounded, and a lot of worse punishments.§0\n§0\n§0I caused Mamis to fight, and I'm guilty, but they\n\nforgave me. It's hard not to backchat, or else I feel my opinion is invalid, and if I don't say something, I'll be figuratively walked all over. §0\n§0\n§0I said sorry, and now things are back to normal, but I think I'll be grounded until I'm ten (I am currently\n\nnine). That's all for today, considering that I am exchanging letters with Eris.§0\n§0\n§0Eris is my illegal friend,§0\n§0~Shannara Sarr", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Skygods and You.§0\n§0=================§0\n§0By a Stranger.§0\n§0\n§0\\\\\\§0\n§0 \\\\§0\n§0   \\§0\n§0    O§0\n§0  -|||||-§0\n§0   /\\§0\n§0\n§0A study on how not to be sent to Skyprison.\n\nPage one, the bad words§0\n§0=================§0\n§0It is true, that in all of this world there are words which can 'offend' even the Gods, forcing them to send you into a temporary stage of Purgatory, this usually follows with a small note saying why.\n\nI shall list all the known words of 'Badness'§0\n§0\n§0Manhood§0\n§0Cock§0\n§0Dick§0\n§0Bulge (Probably)§0\n§0Rape§0\n§0Sex§0\n§0Penetrate (Probably)§0\n§0C*nt", "")
    )

    val AXIOS_CERU: List<StaticBook> by lazy { _AXIOS_CERU_0() + _AXIOS_CERU_1() + _AXIOS_CERU_2() + _AXIOS_CERU_3() + _AXIOS_CERU_4() }
}
